// Generated from bank/merged.json by tools/make_bank_data.py (3205 questions, 3205 with explanation_zh)
window.CSCS_BANK={"generated_utc":"2026-09-08","note":"Merged+deduped from bank source files. See SOURCES.md for provenance.","counts":{"total":3205,"mcq":1604,"flashcard":1601},"questions":[{"id":"q0001","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sprinter is doing repeated maximal 5-second efforts. According to the sliding-filament theory, which two substances must be present inside the muscle fiber for crossbridge cycling to keep occurring?","options":["Sodium and inorganic phosphate","Calcium and ATP","ADP and iron"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Calcium and ATP","explanation_en":"Calcium released from the sarcoplasmic reticulum binds troponin to expose actin binding sites, and ATP hydrolysis by myosin ATPase powers the power stroke and crossbridge detachment. Without both, crossbridge cycling stops.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌絲滑行理論要求兩個條件缺一不可:肌漿網釋放的鈣離子結合肌鈣蛋白(troponin),暴露肌動蛋白上的結合位;ATP 經肌球蛋白 ATP 酶水解,同時供應動力衝程與橫橋脫附所需的能量。缺少鈣或 ATP,橫橋迴圈即停止。"},{"id":"q0002","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are explaining a motor unit to a new intern. Which description is accurate?","options":["A single muscle fiber and all of the motor neurons that innervate it","A motor neuron and all of the muscle fibers it innervates","An upper motor neuron paired with a lower motor neuron"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A motor neuron and all of the muscle fibers it innervates","explanation_en":"A motor unit is one motor neuron plus all the muscle fibers it innervates. Because of the all-or-none principle, when the neuron fires, all of those fibers contract together.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動單位的正確定義是一個運動神經元加上它所支配的全部肌纖維。依全或無(all-or-none)原則,該神經元一放電,其下所有肌纖維就一起收縮。錯誤選項把支配方向反過來(一條肌纖維在正常情形只由一個運動神經元支配)。"},{"id":"q0003","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two untrained athletes perform the same submaximal arm curl. As the load gets heavier and more force is needed, what is the body's main strategy for increasing the muscle's force output?","options":["Partially activating a larger fraction of fibers within each already-active motor unit","Recruiting additional, higher-threshold motor units and increasing firing frequency","Slowing the conduction velocity along the active motor neurons"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recruiting additional, higher-threshold motor units and increasing firing frequency","explanation_en":"Force is graded by recruiting more motor units (size principle, low- then high-threshold) and by increasing firing frequency so twitches summate. Individual fibers within an active unit cannot be partially activated.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增大出力有兩條途徑:依尺寸原則(size principle)由低閾值到高閾值續徵收更多運動單位,並提高放電頻率使單收縮總和加成強直收縮。已活化運動單位內部的單條肌纖維沒有「部分收縮」這回事,因為全或無原則。"},{"id":"q0004","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An endurance runner has a high proportion of Type I fibers in the working muscles. Compared to Type IIx fibers, those Type I fibers would be expected to have:","options":["Higher fatigue resistance and higher mitochondrial and capillary density","Higher force production and a faster contraction speed","A higher recruitment threshold and larger fiber diameter"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Higher fatigue resistance and higher mitochondrial and capillary density","explanation_en":"Type I fibers have more mitochondria, more capillary contacts, more myoglobin, and high fatigue resistance, favoring aerobic metabolism. Type II fibers produce more force, contract faster, and have higher recruitment thresholds.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第一型(慢縮肌)纖維粒線體與微血管密度高、肌紅蛋白多,耐疲勞性強,以有氧代謝為主。產力大、收縮速度快、纖維直徑粗、徵收閾值高都是第二型纖維的特性,不能安在第一型身上。"},{"id":"q0005","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a heavy biceps curl, the elbow acts as a third-class lever. Because the muscle's moment arm is much shorter than the resistance's moment arm, what does this mean for the biceps?","options":["The muscle force needed is much greater than the resistive (external) force","The muscle operates at a mechanical advantage greater than 1.0","The muscle force needed is much less than the external resistance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The muscle force needed is much greater than the resistive (external) force","explanation_en":"In a third-class lever the muscle moment arm is shorter than the resistance moment arm, so mechanical advantage is below 1.0 and the internal muscle force must exceed the external load. This is why internal muscle and tendon forces are so high.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肘關節屈曲是第三類槓桿:力臂(肌肉力臂)短於阻力臂,機械優勢小於 1,因此肱二頭肌必須產生遠大於外在負重的內部力量才能平衡。這也解釋了為什麼肌肉與肌腱承受的內部力往往遠高於舉起的重量。"},{"id":"q0006","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants an athlete to jump 40 cm, which requires a fixed takeoff impulse. The athlete can hit that impulse either with a big force over a short time or a smaller force over a longer time. Which biomechanical relationship explains why the SAME jump height can be reached either way?","options":["The force-velocity relationship","The impulse-momentum relationship (force x time = change in momentum)","The Frank-Starling mechanism"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The impulse-momentum relationship (force x time = change in momentum)","explanation_en":"Impulse equals force times time and equals the change in momentum. Since the required change in velocity (and thus impulse) is fixed for a given jump height, the athlete can trade off force against time to achieve it.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"衝量—動量關係:衝量(力×時間)等於動量改變數。固定跳高所需的起跳速度一定,因此所需衝量一定;大力量×短時間或小力量×長時間都能湊出同一個衝量,所以兩種方式可達到同樣的起跳高度。"},{"id":"q0007","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A lifter performs a barbell overhead press, then lowers it under control. During the lowering (eccentric) phase, how is the work classified?","options":["Positive work, because force is still being applied","Zero work, because the muscle is not shortening","Negative work, because the displacement is downward"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Negative work, because the displacement is downward","explanation_en":"Work is force times displacement. During lowering the force stays positive (controlling the bar) but displacement is negative (downward), so the work performed is negative.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力學上功等於力×位移。下放槓鈴時肌肉仍施加向上的力量控制,但位移方向向下(為負),正負相乘即為負功。肌肉沒有縮短不等於不做功,離心收縮同樣在做功。"},{"id":"q0008","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A pennate muscle and a non-pennate (longitudinal) muscle have the same overall size. Which statement about the pennate muscle is correct?","options":["It packs more sarcomeres in parallel, so it generates more force but has a lower maximal shortening velocity","It has more sarcomeres in series, giving it a higher maximal shortening velocity","Its angle of pennation is fixed and cannot change with training"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It packs more sarcomeres in parallel, so it generates more force but has a lower maximal shortening velocity","explanation_en":"Greater pennation means more sarcomeres in parallel and fewer in series, which boosts force capability but lowers maximal shortening velocity. Pennation angle also increases as the muscle shortens and is modifiable with training.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"羽狀(pennate)排列讓同等體積內以並聯方式塞進更多肌節,最大等長收縮力量提高;但串聯肌節數變少,最大縮短速度下降。羽狀角會隨肌肉長度改變,也會隨訓練增加,說它固定不變是錯的。"},{"id":"q0009","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete does a maximal 6-second effort, like a short sprint or a single heavy set. Which energy system is the primary supplier of ATP for that effort?","options":["The oxidative (aerobic) system","Fast glycolysis","The phosphagen system"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The phosphagen system","explanation_en":"For extremely high-intensity efforts of about 0 to 6 seconds, the phosphagen system (ATP stores plus the creatine kinase reaction with creatine phosphate) is the primary energy source because it produces ATP at the highest rate.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"0 到 6 秒的極高強度努力由磷酸原系統(phosphagen system)主導:肌肉儲存的 ATP 加上肌酸激酶反應分解磷酸肌酸(CP),ATP 再合成速率在所有系統中最快。"},{"id":"q0010","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete reports a burning sensation during high-intensity exercise and blames lactic acid. Based on current bioenergetics, what is the most accurate correction?","options":["Lactate is not the cause of fatigue; proton (H+) accumulation, largely from ATP hydrolysis, drives the drop in pH (metabolic acidosis)","Lactic acid dissociates immediately and is the direct cause of the acidosis and fatigue","Lactate accumulation accelerates metabolic acidosis by adding protons to the cell"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Lactate is not the cause of fatigue; proton (H+) accumulation, largely from ATP hydrolysis, drives the drop in pH (metabolic acidosis)","explanation_en":"The lactate dehydrogenase reaction actually consumes a proton; the term is metabolic acidosis, not lactic acidosis. The H+ accumulation comes mainly from ATP hydrolysis, and lactate is itself used as a fuel and even helps buffer acidosis.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"灼燒感與疲勞不是乳酸造成的。乳酸脫氫酶反應其實消耗 H+;pH 下降(應稱代謝性酸中毒,而非乳酸酸中毒)的 H+ 主要來自大量 ATP 水解。乳酸還可被當作燃料利用,甚至對緩衝酸中毒有幫助。"},{"id":"q0011","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When glycolysis starts from a molecule of MUSCLE GLYCOGEN rather than blood glucose, why is the net ATP yield from substrate-level phosphorylation in glycolysis higher (3 vs 2)?","options":["Glycogen produces an extra pyruvate molecule","Glycogen-derived glucose is already phosphorylated, so it bypasses the first ATP-consuming step","Glycogen breakdown directly produces an extra ATP in the electron transport chain"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Glycogen-derived glucose is already phosphorylated, so it bypasses the first ATP-consuming step","explanation_en":"Blood glucose must be phosphorylated on entry (costing 1 ATP), but glucose freed from glycogen by glycogen phosphorylase is already phosphorylated. So glycogen uses only 1 ATP and nets 3, while blood glucose uses 2 and nets 2.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"血糖進入細胞時須由己糖激酶消耗 1 個 ATP 磷酸化;而糖原磷酸化酶從肌糖原釋放的葡萄糖已帶磷酸基,省掉這一步。所以糖原起算的糖解淨得 3 個 ATP,血糖起算只有 2 個。"},{"id":"q0012","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is programming interval work to develop the phosphagen system using roughly 5-10 second high-power efforts. Which work-to-rest ratio range best fits that goal?","options":["1:1 to 1:3","1:3 to 1:5","1:12 to 1:20"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:12 to 1:20","explanation_en":"Phosphagen-focused intervals (about 90-100% of max power, 5-10 s of work) use long rest, roughly 1:12 to 1:20, because full creatine phosphate resynthesis is aerobic and can take 3-5 minutes (up to 8). Shorter rest ratios target glycolytic or oxidative systems.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"針對磷酸原系統的間歇訓練(約 90 到 100% 最大功率、5 到 10 秒)工休比約 1:12 到 1:20,因為 CP 完全再合成屬有氧過程、可長至 3 到 5 分鐘甚至 8 分鐘。較短的 1:3 到 1:5 針對糖解系統,1:1 到 1:3 則針對氧化系統。"},{"id":"q0013","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach wants to maximize the acute anabolic hormone response of a workout. Which design pattern is most consistently linked to the largest acute increases in serum testosterone and the 22 kD GH isoform?","options":["Large muscle-group, high-volume work with short rest periods","Single-joint isolation moves with very long (5+ min) rest periods","Low-volume, low-intensity work that avoids glycolytic stress"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Large muscle-group, high-volume work with short rest periods","explanation_en":"The acute hormonal response tracks the total work and metabolic demand. Protocols using large muscle groups, high volume, and short rest drive the glycolytic system and H+ production, which is associated with the largest acute testosterone, GH, and cortisol responses.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"急性激素反應的大小追蹤總訓練量與代謝壓力:大肌群、高訓練量、短休息會驅動糖解系統與 H+ 堆積,伴隨最大幅度的急性睪固酮、生長激素(含 22 kD 異型)與皮質醇上升。單關孤立動作加超長休息則幾乎沒有這個效果。"},{"id":"q0014","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hormones such as testosterone and cortisol are carried in the blood by binding proteins (e.g., sex hormone-binding globulin, albumin). What is the primary functional role these binding proteins play?","options":["They permanently block the hormone from ever reaching a receptor","They serve as temporary storage and protect the hormone from degradation, extending its half-life","They convert steroid hormones into peptide hormones for faster signaling"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"They serve as temporary storage and protect the hormone from degradation, extending its half-life","explanation_en":"Binding proteins act as a temporary reservoir and shield hormones from breakdown, lengthening their half-life and regulating how much free, bioactive hormone is available to tissues.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"性激素結合球蛋白、白蛋白等載體蛋白是暫時的儲庫:它們保護激素不被分解、延長半衰期,並調控可供組織利用的自由(未結合)激素量,不是把激素永久封死。"},{"id":"q0015","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete chronically overtrains with very high-volume heavy resistance work and poor recovery, leading to downregulation of beta-2 receptors. What does this specifically impair?","options":["Insulin's ability to clear blood glucose, causing hyperglycemia","Thyroid hormone's permissive effect on metabolic rate","The interaction with epinephrine, reducing muscle contractile force"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The interaction with epinephrine, reducing muscle contractile force","explanation_en":"When a hormone stays chronically elevated, receptors can desensitize or downregulate. Heavy resistance overtraining can downregulate beta-2 receptors, blunting their response to epinephrine and reducing the catecholamine-driven contractile force.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"激素長期過高會使受體去敏感或向下調節。beta-2 受體下調後,腎上腺素(epinephrine)與受體的互動作用被鈍化,兒茶酚胺本來能增強的肌肉收縮力量因此下降。"},{"id":"q0016","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cortisol is labeled a 'catabolic' hormone, yet acute increases after a hard session are not purely harmful. What beneficial acute role does cortisol play in muscle remodeling?","options":["It directly stimulates actin and myosin synthesis","It helps clear damaged proteins and helps maintain blood glucose","It upregulates androgen receptor content for 48-72 hours"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It helps clear damaged proteins and helps maintain blood glucose","explanation_en":"Although chronically high cortisol is detrimental and catabolic, acute post-exercise increases contribute to tissue remodeling by helping clear damaged proteins and maintaining blood glucose during the stress of training.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮質醇雖然被標為分解代謝激素,急性上升仍有正面功能:協助清除受損蛋白、參與組織重塑,並在訓練壓力下維持血糖穩定。只有長期慢性偏高的皮質醇才是純粹有害的。"},{"id":"q0017","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In untrained people the ability to maximally recruit motor units is limited. Where does the increased motor unit activation that drives early strength gains primarily originate?","options":["At the neuromuscular junction with increased acetylcholine release","In the higher brain centers (motor cortex) with the intent to produce maximal force","In the Golgi tendon organs through reduced inhibition only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"In the higher brain centers (motor cortex) with the intent to produce maximal force","explanation_en":"Increased motor unit activation begins in the higher brain centers: the intent to produce maximal force raises primary motor cortex activity, with adaptations then reflected down the descending corticospinal tracts and improved recruitment of high-threshold motor units.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"初學者力量快速增長的運動單位動員改善源自中樞:嘗試產生最大力量的意圖會提高初級運動皮質活性,相關適應再經皮質脊髓束表現出來,並改善高閾值單位的徵收,不是發生在神經肌肉接點或單靠腱器抑制改變。"},{"id":"q0018","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As a muscle hypertrophies with resistance (anaerobic) training, what happens to its mitochondrial density and capillary density?","options":["Both increase in proportion to the fiber size gain","Mitochondrial density increases while capillary density stays exactly constant","Both tend to decrease (no change or decrease), because fiber CSA grows disproportionately to them"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Both tend to decrease (no change or decrease), because fiber CSA grows disproportionately to them","explanation_en":"Density is expressed relative to muscle area. Because cross-sectional area grows faster than mitochondria or capillaries proliferate, both mitochondrial density and capillary density show no change or a decrease with heavy resistance training hypertrophy.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"密度以肌肉橫斷面積為分母。肥大時纖維橫斷面積的成長快於粒線體與微血管的增生,所以重量訓練後粒線體密度與微血管密度兩者皆不變或下降,不會與纖維面積等比例上升。"},{"id":"q0019","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is told that resistance training shifts muscle fiber type. Which transition along the fiber-type continuum does heavy resistance/anaerobic training typically produce?","options":["Type IIx shifting toward Type IIa (more fatigue-resistant)","Type IIa shifting toward Type IIx (more glycolytic)","Type I shifting toward Type IIx (more powerful)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Type IIx shifting toward Type IIa (more fatigue-resistant)","explanation_en":"Consistent activation moves fibers along the continuum from IIx toward the intermediate IIax and then to IIa. This positive shift reflects greater fatigue resistance at similar absolute force output, along with hypertrophy.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"持續的阻力/無氧訓練使纖維沿 IIx 到 IIax 再到 IIa 的連續體位移,即 IIx 轉向更耐疲勞的 IIa,同時絕對力量輸出維持。方向反過來(IIa 轉 IIx)或 I 直接轉 IIx 都不是訓練的典型結果。"},{"id":"q0020","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two weeks (14 days) after a competitive weightlifter stops training entirely, what does the detraining research describe as the earliest muscular change?","options":["An immediate, large decline in slow-twitch (Type I) fiber cross-sectional area","A measurable decline specifically in fast-twitch fiber cross-sectional area, with slow-twitch initially unchanged","A complete reversal of fiber type distribution back to untrained values"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A measurable decline specifically in fast-twitch fiber cross-sectional area, with slow-twitch initially unchanged","explanation_en":"In strength/sprint athletes, fast-twitch fiber CSA declines rapidly; one study found about a 6.4% drop in fast-twitch CSA in 14 days, while slow-twitch fibers showed no significant immediate change. Fiber-type distribution itself was unaffected at 14 days.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"去訓練研究顯示:力量與速度型運動員停訓 14 天內,快縮肌纖維橫斷面積即明顯下降(一項研究約 6.4%),慢縮纖維初期無顯著變化,纖維型別分佈在 14 天時也未被改變。"},{"id":"q0021","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The single most significant cardiovascular adaptation to long-term aerobic endurance training is an increase in maximal cardiac output. What primarily drives that increase?","options":["A large increase in maximal heart rate","An increase in resting heart rate","An increase in stroke volume (via larger left ventricle and greater contractility)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"An increase in stroke volume (via larger left ventricle and greater contractility)","explanation_en":"Maximal heart rate stays unchanged or even decreases slightly with training, so the rise in maximal cardiac output comes from improved stroke volume, driven by a larger left ventricle (chamber volume and wall thickness) and stronger contractions.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期有氧訓練最重要的心血管適應是最大心輸出量上升,而最大心率不變甚至略降,所以這個提升幾乎全由最大心搏量(stroke volume)增加貢獻:左心室腔室與壁厚增大、收縮力增強。"},{"id":"q0022","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A well-trained endurance runner can sustain a high percentage of VO2max before blood lactate accumulates. In a trained athlete, the onset of blood lactate accumulation (OBLA) occurs at roughly what percentage of aerobic capacity?","options":["About 40%-50% of aerobic capacity","About 60%-65% of aerobic capacity","Up to about 80%-90% of aerobic capacity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Up to about 80%-90% of aerobic capacity","explanation_en":"Aerobic training raises the lactate threshold so that lactate production matches clearance up to a higher relative intensity. In trained athletes OBLA can occur at up to 80%-90% of aerobic capacity, allowing harder sustained efforts.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練使乳酸閾值右移,乳酸生成與清除的平衡可維持到更高強度;受訓運動員的血中乳酸開始堆積點(OBLA)可高達約 80% 到 90% 有氧能力,得以用更高強度持續運動。"},{"id":"q0023","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two distance runners have identical VO2max and lactate threshold values, yet one consistently races faster. This difference is best attributed to which factor?","options":["Better exercise economy","A higher maximal heart rate","A larger arteriovenous oxygen difference at rest"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Better exercise economy","explanation_en":"Exercise economy, largely a function of biomechanics and technique plus metabolic, cardiovascular, and neuromuscular efficiency, lets one athlete hold a higher pace for the same energy cost even when VO2max and lactate threshold are equal.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"VO2max 與乳酸閾值相同而成績不同,差異要歸因於運動經濟性(exercise economy):生物力學與技術、代謝、心血管及神經肌肉效率更好的人,同樣的耗氧量下能維持更快配速。最大心率和安靜時的 a-vO2 差不是主要解釋。"},{"id":"q0024","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An endurance coach is comparing altitude training and heat acclimation. What is the principal physiological adaptation each one targets?","options":["Both primarily increase maximal heart rate","Altitude increases hemoglobin/red cell volume (via EPO); heat acclimation expands plasma volume","Altitude expands plasma volume; heat acclimation primarily raises VO2max by reducing core temperature"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Altitude increases hemoglobin/red cell volume (via EPO); heat acclimation expands plasma volume","explanation_en":"Altitude raises EPO, increasing hemoglobin mass and red cell volume to boost oxygen-carrying capacity, while heat acclimation produces a large expansion of plasma volume that raises stroke volume. They improve aerobic performance through different mechanisms.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩種環境暴露的機制不同:高原低氧刺激提高紅血球生成素(EPO)→血紅素總量與紅血球容積增加,提升帶氧能力;熱適應(heat acclimation)的主要適應是血漿量大舉擴張,從而提高心搏量。兩者都不靠提高最大心率。"},{"id":"q0025","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A youth coach is told muscle mass increases substantially during puberty in boys. This pubertal increase in muscle mass is due primarily to what?","options":["Hyperplasia (an increase in the number of muscle fibers)","A decrease in body fat being reclassified as muscle","Hypertrophy of individual muscle fibers driven by rising hormones"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hypertrophy of individual muscle fibers driven by rising hormones","explanation_en":"In both sexes the pubertal increase in muscle mass comes from hypertrophy of individual fibers, not hyperplasia. In boys, rising testosterone, GH, and IGF drive a marked gain in muscle mass.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"青春期男性肌肉量大幅增加來自個別肌纖維肥大(hypertrophy),由上升的睪固酮、生長激素與 IGF 驅動;人類並未證實纖維數量增加(增生,hyperplasia)是成長機制。"},{"id":"q0026","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A preadolescent boy completes a well-designed resistance program and gets noticeably stronger but shows little muscle size change. What best explains the strength gains in young children?","options":["Large hypertrophy driven by high circulating testosterone","Neuromuscular (motor development) adaptations, since circulating anabolic hormones are low before puberty","Hyperplasia stimulated by the resistance stimulus"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Neuromuscular (motor development) adaptations, since circulating anabolic hormones are low before puberty","explanation_en":"Preadolescents have low circulating testosterone, GH, and IGF, so they struggle to add muscle mass. Their strength gains come predominantly from neuromuscular adaptations and motor development rather than hypertrophy.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"青春期前兒童血中睪固酮、GH、IGF 都低,難以增加肌肉量;兒童阻力訓練帶來的力量增長主要來自神經肌肉適應與動作發展,所以變強但圍度幾乎不變。"},{"id":"q0027","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An S&C professional designing resistance training for older adults (over 65) should generally do which of the following for safety?","options":["Encourage the Valsalva maneuver to maximize trunk stiffness","Avoid all aerobic work and train the same muscles daily","Discourage the Valsalva maneuver and allow 48 to 72 hours of recovery between sessions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Discourage the Valsalva maneuver and allow 48 to 72 hours of recovery between sessions","explanation_en":"The Valsalva maneuver is generally discouraged in seniors because of the sharp rise in blood pressure, especially with cardiovascular contraindications. Recommendations include 48-72 hours of recovery between sessions and concurrent aerobic, resistance, and balance work.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"65 歲以上訓練者應避免 Valsalva 閉氣用力,因為它使血壓急升、伴頭暈,有心血管禁忌者風險更高;建議兩次訓練間隔 48 到 72 小時恢復,並搭配有氧、阻力與平衡訓練。"},{"id":"q0028","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Female athletes have a higher rate of noncontact ACL injuries. What is believed to be the single most significant contributing factor?","options":["A neuromuscular deficiency leading to abnormal biomechanics such as increased dynamic knee valgus","A smaller femoral notch size alone","Greater absolute upper-body strength"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A neuromuscular deficiency leading to abnormal biomechanics such as increased dynamic knee valgus","explanation_en":"While anatomical factors (femoral notch size, tibial slope, ligament laxity) contribute, the text identifies neuromuscular deficiency as the most significant factor, producing abnormal biomechanics like increased dynamic knee valgus on landing. This makes neuromuscular/plyometric training key for prevention.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書認定女性非接觸性 ACL 傷害最重要的因素是神經肌肉控制不足,造成落地時動態膝外翻(dynamic knee valgus)等異常力學;解剖因素(股骨窩大小、脛骨坡度、韌帶鬆弛度)只是次要。所以預防重點是神經肌肉與增強式訓練。"},{"id":"q0029","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When comparing strength between the sexes, the gap shrinks dramatically under one condition. Which statement reflects this?","options":["Females are stronger than males in absolute upper-body strength","When strength is normalized to muscle volume (relative basis), sex differences are greatly reduced","Absolute upper-body strength of females is closer to male values than lower-body strength is"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"When strength is normalized to muscle volume (relative basis), sex differences are greatly reduced","explanation_en":"Females have a similar number of muscle fibers as males, and when strength is expressed relative to muscle volume the values are similar. Absolute differences (driven by larger fiber size in males) are largest in the upper body; lower-body absolute strength is closer to male values.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"男女肌纖維數量相近,把力量除以肌肉體積(相對力量)後兩性差異大為縮小。絕對力量的差距以上身最大,下肢絕對力量反而較接近;說女性上身絕對力量較接近男性是弄反了。"},{"id":"q0030","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female endurance athlete shows greater fatigue resistance in long events despite a lower VO2max relative to body size than her male counterparts. Which sex difference best explains this fatigue resistance?","options":["A greater proportion of Type I oxidative fibers and higher fat oxidation","A higher absolute testosterone concentration driving more hypertrophy","A greater reliance on carbohydrate and protein during prolonged exercise"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A greater proportion of Type I oxidative fibers and higher fat oxidation","explanation_en":"Females tend to have a greater proportion of Type I oxidative fibers and higher mitochondrial respiration, so they oxidize more fat and less carbohydrate/protein during prolonged work, supporting greater fatigue resistance even with a lower relative VO2max.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性第一型氧化型纖維比例較高、粒線體呼吸能力較高,長時間運動中氧化較多脂肪、較少醣類與蛋白,因此即使相對 VO2max 較低,仍表現出較高的耐疲勞性。"},{"id":"q0031","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is described as having a general physiological and psychological activation that varies on a continuum from deep sleep to intense excitement. Which construct does this describe?","options":["State anxiety","Arousal","Trait anxiety"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Arousal","explanation_en":"Arousal is simply a blend of physiological and psychological activation that ranges from comatose to highly excited, and by itself is neither pleasant nor unpleasant. Anxiety is a negatively perceived subcategory of arousal.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"這是喚醒(arousal)的定義:生理與心理啟用的混合狀態,在從深睡到極度興奮的連續帶上移動,本身無善惡;焦慮只是其中被解讀為負面的次類。"},{"id":"q0032","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A lifter shows up to a meet with a fast heart rate, an upset stomach, and visibly tense muscles. These physical symptoms are best classified as which component of anxiety?","options":["Cognitive anxiety","Trait anxiety","Somatic anxiety"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Somatic anxiety","explanation_en":"Somatic anxiety is the physical reaction component, shown through symptoms like tachycardia, upset stomach, and muscle tension. Cognitive anxiety is the mental piece (worry, negative thoughts).","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"心跳加快、胃部不適、肌肉緊繃是焦慮的軀體(somatic)成分,即身體層面的反應;擔心與負面想法屬於認知(cognitive)焦慮,特質焦慮則指穩定的人格傾向。"},{"id":"q0033","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach insists that the more psyched up an athlete gets, the better they will perform, in a straight linear fashion. Which theory is the coach relying on, and what is its main limitation?","options":["Inverted-U theory; it ignores cognitive anxiety","Drive theory; performers can be too pumped up to perform well","Catastrophe theory; it predicts only gradual declines"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Drive theory; performers can be too pumped up to perform well","explanation_en":"Hull's drive theory proposes arousal and performance rise together linearly, but this breaks down because performers can clearly be too aroused to perform, especially on complex or poorly learned skills.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教練用的是赫爾(Hull)的驅力理論(drive theory):假設喚醒與表現線性同升。它的缺陷是明顯的—運動員可以被喚醒過度而表現變差,特別是複雜或未熟練的動作。"},{"id":"q0034","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does the individual zones of optimal functioning (IZOF) theory differ from the basic inverted-U hypothesis?","options":["Optimal performance always occurs at the midpoint of the arousal continuum","Best performance occurs within a small range of arousal that varies by individual, not at a single fixed midpoint","Only somatic arousal matters; cognitive anxiety is irrelevant"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Best performance occurs within a small range of arousal that varies by individual, not at a single fixed midpoint","explanation_en":"Hanin's IZOF holds that ideal performance does not always sit at the midpoint and that each athlete has an individual bandwidth of optimal arousal, rather than one universal optimal point.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Hanin 的個人最佳功能區(IZOF)理論主張最佳表現落在各人專屬的狹窄範圍內,不一定在喚醒連續帶的中點,也不是所有人共用同一個最佳點;這是它與基本倒U 假說的不同處。"},{"id":"q0035","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to catastrophe theory, what happens when high physiological arousal occurs together with high cognitive anxiety?","options":["A gradual, proportionate decline in performance","A sudden, sharp drop in performance rather than a gradual decline","An immediate boost in performance from the combined activation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A sudden, sharp drop in performance rather than a gradual decline","explanation_en":"Catastrophe theory says that under high cognitive anxiety, once arousal passes a point, performance can drop catastrophically and suddenly, and simply restoring calm does not automatically return prior performance levels.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"災難理論預言:高認知焦慮之下,生理喚醒越過某點後表現不是漸降而是突然大幅崩跌;而且事後恢復平靜並不會自動把表現沿原路帶回來。"},{"id":"q0036","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two athletes feel the exact same level of pre-game arousal. One reads it as excitement and anticipation; the other reads it as scary and worrisome. Which theory best explains why the same arousal helps one and hurts the other?","options":["Drive theory","Inverted-U theory","Reversal theory"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Reversal theory","explanation_en":"Kerr's reversal theory emphasizes that it is the individual's interpretation of arousal, not just the amount, that determines whether it helps or hurts, and athletes can choose to reverse that interpretation.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"反轉理論(reversal theory)認為決定喚醒是好是壞的是個人對它的解讀,而非數量本身;同樣的賽前喚醒,一方視為興奮期待、一方視為威脅恐懼,結果因此相反。"},{"id":"q0037","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete who is dominated by the motive to achieve success (MAS) is most drawn to which kind of challenge?","options":["Tasks that are nearly impossible, so failure carries no shame","Tasks that are very easy, guaranteeing success","Uncertain or challenging tasks with roughly a 50% probability of success"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Uncertain or challenging tasks with roughly a 50% probability of success","explanation_en":"MAS-dominated athletes seek challenging or uncertain situations (about 50% chance of success) because these best let them test and take pride in their abilities. MAF-dominated athletes prefer very easy or very hard tasks to avoid shame.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成就動機(MAS)導向的人偏好成功率約五成、帶有不確定性的挑戰任務,因為那最能考驗能力並帶來自豪;規避失敗動機(MAF)導向的人才挑極容易或極難的任務以避開羞恥感。"},{"id":"q0038","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach wants to boost a young lifter's intrinsic motivation. Based on self-determination, which approach fits best?","options":["Give the athlete some latitude in decision making and set process goals that build perceived competence","Rely heavily on cash bonuses for every personal record","Remove all athlete input and issue strict authoritarian directives at all times"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Give the athlete some latitude in decision making and set process goals that build perceived competence","explanation_en":"Deci's view ties intrinsic motivation to competence and self-determination, so allowing decision-making latitude raises perceived self-determination and appropriate process goals raise perceived competence; a total lack of delegated responsibility can kill drive.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"依 Deci 的自我決定觀,內在動機植基於能力知覺與自我決定:給運動員參與決策的空間可提高自我決定感,設定可達的過程目標可提高能力知覺;完全不放手、事事獨裁反而摧毀動機,現金獎金這類外在獎勵也不是首選。"},{"id":"q0039","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bandura lists several sources of self-efficacy. Which one consists of past experiences of success or failure, and is considered especially influential?","options":["Verbal persuasion","Performance accomplishments","Vicarious experiences"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Performance accomplishments","explanation_en":"Per Bandura, performance accomplishments (past experiences of success or failure) are one of the key sources of self-efficacy; others include vicarious experiences, verbal persuasion, imaginal experiences, and physiological and emotional states.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Bandura 所列來源中,過去實際的成敗經驗(performance accomplishments)是最有影響力的自我效能來源;其他還有替代經驗、言語勸說、想像經驗與生理情緒狀態。"},{"id":"q0040","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach tells a wrestler trying to cut weight to focus on the daily actions he controls, such as completing his aerobic work and hitting his dietary plan, rather than on the number on the scale at weigh-in. What type of goal is the coach emphasizing?","options":["Outcome goal","Process goal","Subjective goal"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Process goal","explanation_en":"Process goals focus on the controllable actions an athlete performs to execute the skill well, so success is strongly tied to effort. Outcome goals (like the final weight or winning) depend partly on factors outside the athlete's control.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教練強調的是過程目標(process goal):專注在運動員能控制的日常作為(完成有氧、執行飲食計畫),成功與努力高度掛鉤;體重計上的數字是結果目標,部分操之不在自己。"},{"id":"q0041","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach notices a high school athlete who, over the past six weeks, has a worsening mood, is missing practices and school, has stopped self-care, and reports no longer caring about the sport. Following the textbook's three-step approach, what is the most appropriate action?","options":["Treat it as a normal subclinical dip and wait a few days for it to pass","Refer the athlete to a qualified mental health professional such as a counselor or psychologist","Increase the athlete's training load to rebuild motivation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Refer the athlete to a qualified mental health professional such as a counselor or psychologist","explanation_en":"Persistent distress (greater than 2-3 weeks) that disrupts sleep, self-care, and social or academic functioning warrants referral to a qualified mental health professional, not self-reflection alone or training changes.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"情緒困擾持續超過 2 到 3 週、波及睡眠、自我照顧與學業社交功能時,已屬需轉介的層次:應轉給合格的心理健康專業(諮商師或心理師),而不是等它自過或加量訓練。"},{"id":"q0042","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which feature most distinguishes depression from anxiety, given that the two share signs like agitation, somatic complaints, and rumination?","options":["Worry and circular thinking","Rapid heart rate and sweating","Anhedonia, hopelessness or helplessness, and low energy"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Anhedonia, hopelessness or helplessness, and low energy","explanation_en":"Depression and anxiety overlap on agitation, somatic complaints, and rumination, but what sets depression apart is anhedonia (lack of emotion), feelings of hopelessness or helplessness, and low energy.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"憂鬱與焦慮共有躁動、軀體不適、反覆思考等徵兆,但鑑別關鍵是憂鬱特有的快感缺失(anhedonia)、無望感或無助感與精力低落。心跳快、流汗偏向焦慮的生理喚醒。"},{"id":"q0043","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete on your team has been diagnosed with diabetes and needs help managing his diet around his medication and training. As the strength and conditioning professional, what is the most appropriate action?","options":["Build the meal plan yourself, since you already act as his sports nutrition coach","Refer him to a sports dietitian (registered dietitian), since this requires medical nutrition therapy","Tell him to just follow MyPlate, since it is the standard guideline for everyone"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Refer him to a sports dietitian (registered dietitian), since this requires medical nutrition therapy","explanation_en":"More complex situations in which food or nutrition is used to treat or manage a medical condition (such as diabetes or a nutrient deficiency) require medical nutrition therapy, which falls under the role of the sports dietitian (a registered dietitian). An S&C professional can act as a sports nutrition coach for basic education only.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"用飲食處理疾病(如糖尿病)屬於醫療營養治療,是運動營養師(註冊營養師 RD)的專業範圍;體能教練只適合擔任基本教育性質的運動營養教練,不該自己開食譜。"},{"id":"q0044","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 90 kg strength athlete wants to build muscle mass. Using the textbook's recommended protein range for strength athletes, which daily protein intake falls within the appropriate target?","options":["About 270 g/day (3.0 g/kg)","About 72 g/day (0.8 g/kg)","About 150 g/day (1.7 g/kg)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 150 g/day (1.7 g/kg)","explanation_en":"Strength athletes should consume 1.4 to 2.0 g of protein per kg of body weight per day. At 90 kg that is roughly 126-180 g/day, so 150 g (1.7 g/kg) fits. The 0.8 g/kg figure is the RDA for the general adult population, not athletes.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量型運動員建議蛋白質攝取為每日 1.4 到 2.0 g/kg;90 公斤即約 126 到 180 g/日,150 g(1.7 g/kg)落在此範圍。0.8 g/kg 是一般成年人的 RDA,對力量運動員不夠。"},{"id":"q0045","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which statement best describes a low-glycemic-index food and how an athlete might use it?","options":["Low-GI foods are digested and absorbed slowly, causing a smaller rise in blood glucose; athletes can base their everyday choices on them while saving high-GI foods for around training","Low-GI foods spike blood glucose rapidly, making them the best choice immediately before competition","Low-GI foods contain no carbohydrate, so they have no effect on insulin release"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Low-GI foods are digested and absorbed slowly, causing a smaller rise in blood glucose; athletes can base their everyday choices on them while saving high-GI foods for around training","explanation_en":"Low-GI foods (vegetables, legumes, whole grains) are digested slowly, producing a smaller rise in blood glucose and insulin. Athletes can use low-GI foods as the base of their diet for health while reserving high-GI foods in and around exercise for rapid energy and glycogen replenishment.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"低 GI 食物消化與吸收慢,血糖與胰島素上升幅度較小;建議日常飲食以低 GI 為基礎兼顧健康,把高 GI 食物留給訓練前後使用,以求快速能量與肝糖回填。"},{"id":"q0046","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An aerobic endurance athlete is in her most demanding training phase. Roughly how much carbohydrate should she aim to consume to support that training?","options":["0.8 to 1.0 g/kg body weight per day","8 to 10 g/kg body weight per day","20 to 25 g/kg body weight per day"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"8 to 10 g/kg body weight per day","explanation_en":"Aerobic endurance athletes should aim for 8 to 10 g of carbohydrate per kg body weight per day during their most demanding training phases or competition, alongside 1.4 to 2.0 g/kg/day of protein. The other ranges are far too low or implausibly high.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力運動員在最艱辛的訓練期或賽期應攝取約每日 8 到 10 g/kg 的碳水化合物(蛋白質另計 1.4 到 2.0 g/kg);0.8 到 1.0 g/kg 太低,20 到 25 g/kg 則不合常理。"},{"id":"q0047","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A marathoner finishes a glycogen-depleting race and has another hard session in under 12 hours. To replenish glycogen, what is the recommended approach for carbohydrate intake immediately after exercise?","options":["Consume about 1.0 to 1.85 g of carbohydrate per kg body weight per hour, starting right after exercise and at regular intervals for up to 5 hours","Avoid carbohydrate for at least 5 hours so the muscle can recover before refueling","Consume only protein, since carbohydrate timing has no effect on glycogen resynthesis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Consume about 1.0 to 1.85 g of carbohydrate per kg body weight per hour, starting right after exercise and at regular intervals for up to 5 hours","explanation_en":"For rapid glycogen replenishment, athletes should consume roughly 1.0 to 1.85 g of carbohydrate per kg body weight per hour immediately after exercise and at regular intervals (every 15-60 min) for up to 5 hours. This matters most when recovery time before the next bout is short.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"距離下一次高強度課表不到 12 小時時,運動後應立刻攝取約每小時 1.0 到 1.85 g/kg 的碳水化合物,並每 15 到 60 分鐘補充一次、持續最多 5 小時,以最大化肝糖再合成。"},{"id":"q0048","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 68 kg distance cyclist plans to carbohydrate load before a long road race. Which scenario best reflects a use of carbohydrate loading consistent with the textbook?","options":["He loads carbohydrate before a 30-minute sprint workout to maximize power output","He follows several days of high carbohydrate intake (e.g., 8-12 g/kg/day) with tapered training before an event lasting more than 90 minutes","He cuts carbohydrate to near zero the day before to force his body to burn fat during the race"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"He follows several days of high carbohydrate intake (e.g., 8-12 g/kg/day) with tapered training before an event lasting more than 90 minutes","explanation_en":"Carbohydrate loading uses high carbohydrate intake (commonly 8-12 g/kg/day) in the days before competition, paired with tapering, to maximize muscle glycogen. It benefits athletes training or competing for more than 90 minutes, such as distance cyclists and runners, not short high-power efforts.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肝糖超補積載(carbohydrate loading)的正確用法:賽前數天攝取高量碳水(約 8 到 12 g/kg/日)並配合訓練減量,用於超過 90 分鐘的專案(如長距離公路賽);30 分鐘的短課表用不著它。"},{"id":"q0049","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 70 kg athlete wants to use creatine monohydrate and asks about a body-weight-based loading and maintenance protocol. Which dosing scheme matches the textbook recommendation?","options":["Load with 0.3 g/kg/day for about 5 days, then maintain with 0.03 g/kg/day","Load with 3.0 g/kg/day for about 5 days, then maintain with 0.3 g/kg/day","Load with 0.03 g/kg/day for about 5 days, then maintain with 0.3 g/kg/day"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Load with 0.3 g/kg/day for about 5 days, then maintain with 0.03 g/kg/day","explanation_en":"A typical creatine regimen is a loading dose of about 20-25 g/day (or 0.3 g/kg body mass) for 5 days, followed by a maintenance dose of about 2 g/day (or 0.03 g/kg body mass per day). Creatine reliably increases maximal strength, power, and lean body mass.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書的肌酸劑量:loading 約 20 到 25 g/日(或每公斤體重 0.3 g)約 5 天,之後 maintenance 約 2 g/日(或 0.03 g/kg/日)。3.0 g/kg 的 loading 高得不切實際,先低後高則是把順序弄反。"},{"id":"q0050","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An endurance athlete asks about erythropoietin (EPO) as a way to boost performance. What is the major health risk that makes EPO dangerous for athletes?","options":["It lowers red blood cell count, causing anemia and reduced oxygen delivery","It has no meaningful physiological effect and is banned purely on ethical grounds","It increases hematocrit and blood viscosity, raising the risk of clotting, elevated blood pressure, stroke, and embolism"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It increases hematocrit and blood viscosity, raising the risk of clotting, elevated blood pressure, stroke, and embolism","explanation_en":"EPO increases red blood cell mass, which raises hematocrit and blood viscosity (thicker blood). This increases the risk of clotting, elevated systolic blood pressure, stroke, and cerebral or pulmonary embolism, and deaths of competitive cyclists have been linked to EPO use.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"EPO 增加紅血球質量,使血比容上升、血液黏稠度提高,因而增加凝血、收縮壓升高、中風與腦或肺栓塞的風險;選手死亡案曾被連結到 EPO 使用。它不會減少紅血球,也不是無效藥物。"},{"id":"q0051","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two athletes have biceps of identical fiber type and pennation, but one has a larger physiological cross-sectional area. A coach wants to explain, in sliding-filament terms, the single most direct determinant of the force either muscle can express at a given instant. Which statement is correct?","options":["The instantaneous number of attached actin-myosin cross-bridges, which the larger cross-section can support in greater number","The tensile stiffness of the epimysium and surrounding connective tissue that transmits the pull to the tendon","The concentration of stored sarcoplasmic glycogen available to fuel the contraction"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The instantaneous number of attached actin-myosin cross-bridges, which the larger cross-section can support in greater number","explanation_en":"Force production is dictated by the number of actin and myosin cross-bridges attached at a given moment. A larger physiological cross-sectional area holds more parallel contractile filaments, so more potential cross-bridges and greater force. Connective tissue and stored glycogen do not set the instantaneous force ceiling.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌絲滑行理論下,瞬時能表現的力量由當時附著的肌動蛋白—肌球蛋白橫橋數量決定;生理橫斷面積大的肌肉含更多並聯收縮肌絲,橫橋上限更高。肌外膜的剛性和儲存的肝糖都不決定瞬時力量上限。"},{"id":"q0052","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An intern watches an athlete grind out a maximal lift and concludes that the nervous system must be sending a 'stronger' signal that makes each recruited motor unit's fibers contract harder. Applying the all-or-none principle, how should you correct this?","options":["A stronger central drive selectively activates a fraction of a unit's fibers with more force, sparing the rest","Once a motor unit fires, all its fibers contract together and one action potential cannot grade that twitch; whole-muscle force is graded by recruiting more units and by rate coding","The action potential itself can be amplified so that a single motor unit twitch produces more force"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Once a motor unit fires, all its fibers contract together and one action potential cannot grade that twitch; whole-muscle force is graded by recruiting more units and by rate coding","explanation_en":"By the all-or-none principle, every fiber in a motor unit contracts fully or not at all, and a single action potential cannot partially activate the unit or vary one twitch's force. Whole-muscle force is graded instead by recruiting additional motor units and by increasing firing rate (rate coding).","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"全或無原則:運動單位一旦放電,其全部纖維就一起全力收縮,單一動作電位無法調整單次抽動的力度。整塊肌肉的力量分級只能靠續徵收更多運動單位與提高放電頻率(rate coding),所以「每個單位收得更用力」的說法是錯的。"},{"id":"q0053","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach describes two receptors: receptor A lies parallel to the working fibers and fires when the muscle is stretched quickly, while receptor B lies in series with the fibers and fires as the muscle-tendon unit builds tension. Which pairing correctly names A and B and what each primarily senses?","options":["Both A and B are tension sensors; they differ only in how fast they respond","A is the Golgi tendon organ sensing tension; B is the muscle spindle sensing length and rate of stretch","A is the muscle spindle sensing muscle length and rate of stretch; B is the Golgi tendon organ sensing muscle-tendon tension"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A is the muscle spindle sensing muscle length and rate of stretch; B is the Golgi tendon organ sensing muscle-tendon tension","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles lie parallel to extrafusal fibers and sense muscle length and the rate of length change, triggering the stretch reflex. Golgi tendon organs sit in series within the tendon and respond to muscle tension, reflexively inhibiting the agonist when tension is high. The parallel/quick-stretch receptor is the spindle; the in-series/tension receptor is the GTO.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"與工作纖維並列、快速拉長時放電的是肌梭(muscle spindle),它感知肌肉長度與拉長速率、觸發伸展反射;與纖維串聯、張力上升時放電的是高氏腱器(Golgi tendon organ),感知肌肉肌腱張力。"},{"id":"q0054","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Mid-rep on a maximal back squat the load exceeds what the athlete can control, and a reflex acts to reduce agonist tension to protect the muscle-tendon unit. Which receptor drives this protective inhibition, and where does it sit?","options":["The Golgi tendon organ, positioned in series near the myotendinous junction","The muscle spindle, which reflexively raises agonist activation via the stretch reflex","The Pacinian corpuscle in the joint capsule, signaling deep pressure"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The Golgi tendon organ, positioned in series near the myotendinous junction","explanation_en":"Golgi tendon organs sit in series near the myotendinous junction and respond to high tension by reflexively inhibiting the agonist, a protective response. Muscle spindles do the opposite, exciting the agonist via the stretch reflex; Pacinian corpuscles detect pressure/vibration and do not provide this protective inhibition.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過大張力時反射性抑制agonist(主動肌)、保護肌肉肌腱單位的是高氏腱器,它串聯位在肌腱、靠近肌腱肌肉接合處。肌梭的作用相反(透過伸展反射興奮主動肌), Pacinian 小體只管深壓覺。"},{"id":"q0055","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A triceps pushdown is modeled as a lever in which the triceps inserts about 5 cm from the elbow axis while the resistance acts about 40 cm from that axis. Working from the moment arms, what does this arrangement require of the muscle?","options":["It gives a mechanical advantage above 1.0, so the muscle can use less force than the external resistance","It gives a mechanical advantage of about 0.125, so the muscle must generate force roughly eight times the resistance","It gives a mechanical advantage of about 1.0, so muscle force equals the resistance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It gives a mechanical advantage of about 0.125, so the muscle must generate force roughly eight times the resistance","explanation_en":"Mechanical advantage equals the muscle (force) moment arm divided by the resistance moment arm, here 5/40 = 0.125. Being well below 1.0, the muscle must generate force about eight times larger than the external resistance to balance the torques.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"機械優勢=肌肉力臂/阻力臂=5/40=0.125,遠小於 1;要平衡力矩,三頭肌必須輸出約為外在阻力 8 倍的力量。第三類槓桿永遠是力 disadvantage,不可能優勢大於 1 或等於 1。"},{"id":"q0056","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A weightlifter and a bodybuilder have similar muscle volume, but the bodybuilder's biceps has a markedly greater pennation angle. Compared with the more longitudinally arranged muscle, what is the most likely functional consequence of that higher pennation angle?","options":["A higher maximal shortening velocity measured along the muscle's line of pull","Fewer total contractile fibers in the muscle and therefore lower maximal force output","More fibers packed into a given cross-section, favoring force production at the expense of shortening velocity along the line of pull"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"More fibers packed into a given cross-section, favoring force production at the expense of shortening velocity along the line of pull","explanation_en":"A pennate arrangement packs more fibers into a given cross-sectional area, raising force potential, but because the fibers pull at an oblique angle to the tendon, shortening velocity along the line of pull is reduced. So higher pennation trades velocity for force, not the reverse.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"羽狀角大代表同一橫斷面積內塞進更多纖維,力量潛力提高;但纖維以斜角拉拽肌腱,沿拉力方向的縮短速度打折扣。所以高羽狀角是用速度換力量,不是提升縮短速度。"},{"id":"q0057","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two athletes have geometrically similar builds, but one is considerably smaller and lighter. In tasks like sprinting and vertical jumping that require moving one's own body, which athlete tends to have the edge, and why?","options":["The smaller athlete, because with similar proportions body mass grows faster than strength, yielding a higher strength-to-mass ratio","The larger athlete, because muscular strength scales in direct proportion to body mass, preserving performance","Neither, because in geometrically similar athletes the strength-to-mass ratio is constant across body sizes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The smaller athlete, because with similar proportions body mass grows faster than strength, yielding a higher strength-to-mass ratio","explanation_en":"As body size increases with constant proportions, body mass (a volume, roughly length cubed) rises faster than muscular strength (tied to cross-sectional area, roughly length squared). The smaller athlete therefore has the higher strength-to-mass ratio, which directly reflects the ability to accelerate one's own body.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"幾何相似的個體中,體重隨長度三次方成長,肌力只隨橫斷面積約二次方成長,所以較小者力量/體重比較高,在需要移動自身體重的專案(衝刺、垂直跳)比較吃香。"},{"id":"q0058","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A shot-putter explodes through a single all-out throw that lasts roughly 4 seconds. Which energy system supplies the majority of the ATP for that effort, and why is it the primary contributor here?","options":["The oxidative system, because it produces the most ATP per substrate molecule","The phosphagen system, because it supplies ATP at the highest rate for very brief maximal efforts","Fast glycolysis, because it dominates from the first second of any high-intensity work"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The phosphagen system, because it supplies ATP at the highest rate for very brief maximal efforts","explanation_en":"Very short maximal efforts of roughly 0 to 6 seconds rely primarily on the phosphagen system (stored ATP and creatine phosphate), which supplies ATP at the highest rate but for the shortest duration. The oxidative system is high-yield but slow, and fast glycolysis becomes dominant only as the effort extends beyond a few seconds.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"約 4 秒的單發全力投擲落在 0 到 6 秒區間,ATP 主要由磷酸原系統(儲存 ATP 與磷酸肌酸)供應—它的再合成速率最高、持續時間最短。氧化系統量大但供能慢,快速糖解要等超過數秒後才居主導。"},{"id":"q0059","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a heavy lift an athlete slowly lowers the bar (lengthening under load), presses it back up (shortening), and then holds it motionless. Ranking these three actions for a given muscle, during which one can the muscle develop the greatest force?","options":["The concentric (shortening) action, because active shortening recruits the most cross-bridges","The isometric (static) hold, because zero velocity maximizes cross-bridge attachment time","The eccentric (lengthening) action, which along the force-velocity relationship allows the greatest force"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The eccentric (lengthening) action, which along the force-velocity relationship allows the greatest force","explanation_en":"Along the force-velocity relationship a muscle produces its greatest force during an eccentric (lengthening) action, more than during an isometric hold, and least during a concentric (shortening) action. This is why an athlete can lower more weight than they can lift.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量速度關係上,肌肉產力為離心(慢放)大於等長、大於向心,所以運動員能控制的下降重量可以超過他能舉起的重量。等長不是產力最大的動作。"},{"id":"q0060","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach programs 5- to 10-second maximal sprints to tax the phosphagen system and asks how long rest should allow for near-complete creatine phosphate recovery. After a maximal effort that heavily depletes creatine phosphate, roughly how long does full CP resynthesis take?","options":["About 8 minutes, with roughly half restored in the first 30 seconds or so","About 24 hours, similar to the time course for muscle glycogen repletion","About 30 seconds, at which point creatine phosphate is essentially fully restored"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 8 minutes, with roughly half restored in the first 30 seconds or so","explanation_en":"Full ATP resynthesis takes about 3 to 5 minutes, but full creatine phosphate resynthesis can take up to about 8 minutes, with roughly half restored in the first 30 seconds. The 30-second mark reflects only partial recovery, and 24 hours describes glycogen, not CP.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"ATP 完全再合成約需 3 到 5 分鐘,磷酸肌酸完全再合成可長至約 8 分鐘,前 30 秒左右只回復約一半。30 秒就「滿血」是高估,24 小時講的是肝糖不是 CP。"},{"id":"q0061","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A well-trained distance runner can hold a high fraction of her aerobic capacity before blood lactate climbs sharply. In aerobically trained athletes, the onset of blood lactate accumulation (OBLA) typically occurs at approximately what percentage of VO2max, and how does that compare with an untrained person?","options":["Around 30% to 40% of VO2max, lower than the untrained value because trained athletes accumulate lactate sooner","Around 70% to 80% of VO2max, pushed higher than the roughly 50% to 60% seen in untrained people","Around 50% to 60% of VO2max, essentially the same threshold seen in untrained people"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Around 70% to 80% of VO2max, pushed higher than the roughly 50% to 60% seen in untrained people","explanation_en":"The lactate threshold begins around 50% to 60% of VO2max in untrained people but is pushed out to roughly 70% to 80% of VO2max in aerobically trained athletes, letting them sustain a higher intensity before lactate accumulates. Training raises, not lowers, this percentage.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"未受訓者的乳酸閾值約在 50% 到 60% VO2max;有氧訓練把它推高到約 70% 到 80% VO2max,使運動員能在更高強度下不堆積乳酸。訓練是右移這個百分比,不是左移。"},{"id":"q0062","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A triathlete finishes a glycogen-depleting race and must train hard again in under 12 hours, so maximizing muscle glycogen resynthesis is the priority. Which carbohydrate feeding strategy best matches the recommendation for rapid repletion?","options":["Withhold carbohydrate until the next full meal so the muscle can rest before refueling","Provide about 0.1 gram of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight once for the day","Provide about 0.7 to 3.0 grams of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight every 2 hours after exercise"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Provide about 0.7 to 3.0 grams of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight every 2 hours after exercise","explanation_en":"Glycogen repletion is optimized when about 0.7 to 3.0 grams of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight are ingested every 2 hours after exercise, which matters most when a hard session follows soon after. Delaying intake or feeding a trivial dose blunts resynthesis.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"快速回填肝糖的建議是運動後每 2 小時攝取約 0.7 到 3.0 g/kg 的碳水化合物;延到下餐才吃或一天只給 0.1 g/kg 都會明顯打折。"},{"id":"q0063","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach wants a single session designed to produce the largest acute rise in serum testosterone. Which set of program variables best fits that objective?","options":["Large-muscle-group, multijoint exercises at heavy loads (about 85% to 95% of 1RM) with moderate-to-high volume and short rest intervals","Single-joint isolation exercises at light loads with very long rest periods between sets","Low-intensity steady-state aerobic work sustained for about 60 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Large-muscle-group, multijoint exercises at heavy loads (about 85% to 95% of 1RM) with moderate-to-high volume and short rest intervals","explanation_en":"Acute testosterone elevations are most associated with large-muscle-group, multijoint exercises performed with heavy loads (about 85% to 95% of 1RM), moderate-to-high volume, and short rest intervals. Isolation work with long rests or prolonged low-intensity aerobic exercise does not maximize this acute response.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"急性睪固酮上升最大化的組合:大肌群多關節動作、大強度約 85% 到 95% 1RM、中到高訓練量、短休息。輕負荷單關加長休息或長時間低強度有氧都觸發不了這個反應。"},{"id":"q0064","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach notices an athlete can generate the most force at a mid-range joint angle rather than at full stretch or full shortening. Which mechanism best explains why maximal force capability occurs near the muscle's resting length?","options":["At resting length the actin and myosin overlap so little that only a few cross-bridges can form, minimizing internal drag","At resting length the actin-myosin overlap is optimal, allowing the greatest number of cross-bridges to form","Force capability actually peaks when the muscle is maximally shortened, and mid-range is only a testing artifact"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At resting length the actin-myosin overlap is optimal, allowing the greatest number of cross-bridges to form","explanation_en":"The length-tension relationship shows force capability is greatest near resting length because that length provides optimal actin-myosin overlap and thus the most cross-bridge formation. Force falls off when the muscle is overly shortened (filaments overlap excessively) or overly stretched (too little overlap).","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長度張力關係:肌肉處於靜息長度時肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白重疊最適,能形成的橫橋數最多,產力能力最高;過度縮短(絲絲過度重疊)或過度拉長(重疊不足)產力都下降。"},{"id":"q0065","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Under prolonged stress, cortisol behaves as a catabolic and anti-anabolic hormone in skeletal muscle. Which description captures its primary catabolic action?","options":["It drives protein synthesis and promotes glycogen storage within the muscle","It stimulates erythropoiesis, increasing red blood cell production in the bone marrow","It promotes protein breakdown and shunts amino acids toward glucose formation while suppressing protein synthesis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It promotes protein breakdown and shunts amino acids toward glucose formation while suppressing protein synthesis","explanation_en":"Cortisol exerts catabolic and anti-anabolic effects: it promotes protein breakdown, directs amino acids toward gluconeogenesis, and inhibits the incorporation of amino acids into protein. Stimulating synthesis or driving red blood cell production are not among its catabolic actions.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期壓力下皮質醇的分解代謝作用:促進蛋白分解、把胺基酸分流去醣質新生、同時抑制胺基酸合成蛋白質。促進合成與刺激紅血球生成都不是它的分解面作用。"},{"id":"q0066","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An untrained athlete gains strength rapidly in the first few weeks of lifting with little measurable change in muscle size, implicating neural adaptation. Assuming a normal recruitment pattern, in what order are that athlete's motor units brought into play as force demand rises?","options":["In order of increasing size and threshold, so lower-threshold units are recruited before higher-threshold ones (Henneman's size principle)","In a random order, though in beginners the largest, highest-threshold units tend to fire first","All of the muscle's motor units at once, following the all-or-none principle applied to the whole muscle"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"In order of increasing size and threshold, so lower-threshold units are recruited before higher-threshold ones (Henneman's size principle)","explanation_en":"Early strength gains are largely neural, and motor units are normally recruited in order of increasing size and threshold per Henneman's size principle, with smaller, lower-threshold units activated first. Recruitment is orderly, not random, and the all-or-none principle applies to a single motor unit, not the whole muscle at once.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"初期力量增長多為神經適應,而徵收順序依 Henneman 尺寸原則:由小而低閾值的運動單位開始,隨力量需求提高依序加入大而高閾值的單位;順序既非隨機,全部一次放火也不對—全或無只適用於單一運動單位。"},{"id":"q0067","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At the start of a hard run, oxygen uptake rises slowly and cannot immediately meet the energy demand, so anaerobic sources fill the gap until VO2 catches up. What is the correct term for this early shortfall between the oxygen required and the oxygen actually consumed?","options":["Excess postexercise oxygen consumption, reflecting elevated oxygen use after the effort ends","The oxygen deficit, reflecting the early lag before aerobic supply matches demand","The lactate threshold, the intensity at which blood lactate begins to accumulate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The oxygen deficit, reflecting the early lag before aerobic supply matches demand","explanation_en":"At exercise onset the aerobic system responds slowly, so anaerobic mechanisms supply much of the early energy; the gap between oxygen required and oxygen consumed during this lag is the oxygen deficit. Elevated oxygen use during recovery is EPOC, and the lactate threshold is an intensity marker, not this early shortfall.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動開始時需氧量與實際攝氧量之間的落差稱氧欠債(oxygen deficit):有氧系統供不上,由無氧機制先補。運動後升高的攝氧量是 EPOC,乳酸閾值則是一個強度指標。"},{"id":"q0068","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete asks whether resistance training can increase the actual number of muscle fibers rather than just their size. Based on what has been directly demonstrated in humans, what is the most accurate answer?","options":["Yes; hyperplasia through longitudinal fiber splitting is the principal growth mechanism in trained humans","Neither hypertrophy nor hyperplasia has been shown to occur in humans","Only hypertrophy has been directly confirmed in humans; hyperplasia has been shown in some animal models but not confirmed in humans"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Only hypertrophy has been directly confirmed in humans; hyperplasia has been shown in some animal models but not confirmed in humans","explanation_en":"Hyperplasia (an increase in fiber number via longitudinal splitting) has been demonstrated in some animal models but not directly confirmed in humans. Hypertrophy, the enlargement of existing fibers, is the established mechanism of resistance-training growth in humans.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"人類身上直接證實的只有肥大(既有纖維變粗);纖維縱向分裂式的增生(hyperplasia)只在部分動物模型出現過,人類尚未證實。說增生是人類主要生長機制是錯的。"},{"id":"q0069","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants lower-body loading heavy enough to trigger new bone formation. Under the minimal essential strain (MES) concept, the imposed force must exceed roughly what fraction of the bone's fracture force to stimulate osteoblasts?","options":["About one-tenth of the force required to fracture the bone","About one-fifth of the force required to fracture the bone","About one-half of the force required to fracture the bone"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About one-tenth of the force required to fracture the bone","explanation_en":"The minimal essential strain is thought to be approximately one-tenth (1/10) of the force required to fracture the bone; loads at or above that threshold stimulate osteoblasts to lay down new bone. One-fifth or one-half overstate the threshold.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最小必要應變(minimal essential strain, MES)約為骨折所需力量的十分之一;負荷達到此閾值以上才能刺激成骨細胞沉積新骨。五分之一、二分之一都把閾值講高了。"},{"id":"q0070","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants resistance training that produces the greatest net growth of tendon and ligament tissue. Which loading approach best achieves that, and why do lighter approaches fall short?","options":["Low- to moderate-intensity exercise, because that intensity markedly raises collagen content in connective tissue","High-intensity loading applied through the full range of motion of the joint","Prolonged low-force aerobic exercise such as easy jogging, because sustained loading time drives collagen turnover"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"High-intensity loading applied through the full range of motion of the joint","explanation_en":"Low- to moderate-intensity exercise does not markedly change collagen content, and low-force endurance work does not drive net connective tissue growth. It is high-intensity loading applied through the full joint range of motion that stimulates net growth of tendons and ligaments.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌腱與韌帶的淨成長需要高強度負荷且動作貫穿完整關節活動度;低到中強度對膠原蛋白含量影響不大,低力量的長時間有氧也驅動不了結締組織成長。"},{"id":"q0071","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After several months of aerobic training, testing shows the athlete's tissues remove more oxygen from each unit of blood that reaches the working muscles. Which specific adaptation does this reflect, and how does it feed into VO2max?","options":["A decreased maximal stroke volume, lowering delivery so extraction appears higher","A reduced muscle capillary density, concentrating oxygen extraction into fewer vessels","An increased arteriovenous oxygen (a-vO2) difference, reflecting greater oxygen extraction that, with higher cardiac output, raises VO2max"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"An increased arteriovenous oxygen (a-vO2) difference, reflecting greater oxygen extraction that, with higher cardiac output, raises VO2max","explanation_en":"Aerobic training widens the arteriovenous oxygen (a-vO2) difference, meaning tissues extract more oxygen from the blood. Combined with greater maximal cardiac output, this contributes to a higher VO2max. Stroke volume and capillary density actually increase with training, not decrease.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"組織從流經的血液中提取更多氧,反映在有氧訓練後動脈—靜脈氧差(a-vO2 difference)增大;它與最大心輸出量提高共同抬升 VO2max。訓練後心搏量與微血管密度其實是增加的,選項反了。"},{"id":"q0072","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After a year of aerobic endurance training a distance runner's maximal cardiac output rises substantially. Given how maximal heart rate behaves with training, which change is chiefly responsible for the higher maximal cardiac output?","options":["A rise in maximal stroke volume, while maximal heart rate stays essentially unchanged or drifts slightly lower","A simultaneous fall in both maximal heart rate and maximal stroke volume","A sharp rise in maximal heart rate, while maximal stroke volume stays essentially unchanged"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A rise in maximal stroke volume, while maximal heart rate stays essentially unchanged or drifts slightly lower","explanation_en":"The most significant cardiovascular adaptation to long-term aerobic training is an increased maximal cardiac output, driven primarily by a higher maximal stroke volume. Maximal heart rate generally remains unaltered or may even decrease slightly, so it is not the driver of the rise.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大心輸出量=最大心率×最大心搏量;訓練後最大心率大致不變甚至略降,所以提升幾乎全部來自最大心搏量上升,不是心率急升。"},{"id":"q0073","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength-trained athlete takes an unplanned two-week layoff and worries that fiber-type characteristics will shift. Based on the reported effects of about 14 days of inactivity in strength athletes, what should you tell him?","options":["Expect a complete reversal of his strength gains within those 14 days","Expect no significant change in muscle fiber type distribution over 14 days, with minimal loss of maximal strength","Expect a rapid conversion of his Type II fibers to Type I within 14 days"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Expect no significant change in muscle fiber type distribution over 14 days, with minimal loss of maximal strength","explanation_en":"In strength-trained athletes, about 14 days of inactivity has been reported to have no effect on muscle fiber type distribution, and short layoffs have minimal effect on maximal strength. Neither a full loss of strength nor a fast Type II to Type I conversion occurs over that span.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"停訓約 14 天對肌纖維型別分佈沒有顯著影響,最大力量也只輕微流失;不需要擔心 II 型快速轉換成 I 型或力量全盤歸零。"},{"id":"q0074","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An exercise physiologist explains why aging adults lose muscle power faster than they lose low-intensity endurance. Age-related muscle atrophy is attributed largely to inactivity plus a gradual, selective denervation of which fiber type?","options":["All fiber types about equally, with no preferential loss","Type I (slow-twitch) fibers, explaining the early decline in endurance","Type II (fast-twitch) fibers, explaining the disproportionate decline in power"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Type II (fast-twitch) fibers, explaining the disproportionate decline in power","explanation_en":"Sarcopenia involves atrophy driven by inactivity and a gradual, selective denervation of Type II (fast-twitch) fibers. This preferential loss of fast-twitch tissue explains the disproportionate decline in muscle power with aging, rather than an equal or Type I-selective loss.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"老化相關的肌肉萎縮(肌少症)主要歸因於活動量不足加上第二型(快縮)纖維逐漸選擇性去神經支配,因此功率下滑比低強度耐力明顯;不是各型平均流失,也不是挑慢縮纖維。"},{"id":"q0075","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Because NADH and FADH2 hand off their electrons at different entry points along the electron transport chain, they do not pump the same number of protons and so yield different amounts of ATP. Using the current biochemistry values, how do their per-molecule ATP yields compare?","options":["One NADH yields about 2.5 ATP and one FADH2 about 1.5 ATP","One NADH yields about 1.5 ATP and one FADH2 about 2.5 ATP","One NADH and one FADH2 yield the same amount of ATP because both ultimately reduce oxygen"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"One NADH yields about 2.5 ATP and one FADH2 about 1.5 ATP","explanation_en":"Because NADH enters earlier in the electron transport chain than FADH2, one NADH produces about 2.5 ATP while one FADH2 produces about 1.5 ATP. Complete oxidation of one molecule of blood glucose yields roughly 32 ATP. The yields are not equal, and FADH2 does not exceed NADH.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"以現行生化值,NADH 經電子傳遞鏈約產 2.5 ATP,FADH2 約產 1.5 ATP(因為兩者進入鏈的位點不同、幫浦質子數不同);兩者並不相等,FADH2 也不會比 NADH 高。"},{"id":"q0076","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach tells a parent that an 11-year-old with no prior lifting experience should see meaningful strength improvement over a 12-week supervised program, but wants to set a realistic expectation rather than overpromising. Based on typical findings for untrained preadolescents completing an 8- to 20-week program, which gain should the coach quote?","options":["About 70% to 90%, driven mostly by muscle hypertrophy at this age","About 30% to 40%","About 5% to 10%, similar to what a well-trained adult would expect"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 30% to 40%","explanation_en":"Strength gains of roughly 30% to 40% are typically observed in untrained preadolescent children after short-term (8 to 20 week) resistance training programs. These early gains are driven largely by neural adaptations rather than hypertrophy, and 5% to 10% is closer to what a trained adult sees.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"未受訓的青春期前兒童完成 8 到 20 週的阻力訓練,典型力量增幅約 30% 到 40%,主要來自神經適應;70% 到 90% 是過度承諾,5% 到 10% 比較像已受訓成人能有的進步。"},{"id":"q0077","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach progresses loads for a 12-year-old and is warned that one skeletal site, unique to the still-growing athlete, must be protected because injury there could disrupt long-bone growth. Which site is the concern, and where is it found?","options":["The diaphysis, the mineralized central shaft of long bones","The mature lamellar bone lining the joint capsule","The epiphyseal plate, the growth cartilage near the ends of long bones"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The epiphyseal plate, the growth cartilage near the ends of long bones","explanation_en":"Growth cartilage in children is located at the epiphyseal (growth) plate near the ends of long bones, at the joint surface, and at the apophyseal insertions; damage to it can impair bone growth. The diaphysis is the already-ossified shaft and is not the growth-related concern. This risk is minimized with proper technique, sensible load progression, and qualified instruction.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兒童的成長軟骨位於長骨兩端的骨骺板(epiphyseal plate)、關節面與骨突附著處,其中骨骺板受損可能幹擾長骨生長,是重量訓練要保護的點;已骨化的骨幹不是疑慮所在。"},{"id":"q0078","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach comparing average strength between male and female athletes notices the sex-related gap is not uniform across the body. When designing a female athlete's program to offset this, which region generally warrants the most added emphasis because the relative deficit versus males is largest there?","options":["The upper body","The lower body, where the relative deficit versus males is greatest","Grip strength specifically, with the rest of the body essentially equal"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The upper body","explanation_en":"Sex-related strength differences are most apparent in the upper body; the lower-body gap is comparatively smaller, especially when strength is expressed relative to body mass or lean mass. Program design for female athletes therefore often emphasizes upper body strength development.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"男女力量差距以上身最懸殊,下肢差距較小(以體重或瘦體重表現在相對時更小);所以女性選手的課表通常要額外強化上身力量。"},{"id":"q0079","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A cyclist finishing a long, low-intensity ride is drawing an increasing share of ATP from stored fat. Before the triglycerides in her fat cells can be oxidized, they must first be cleaved into free fatty acids and glycerol. Which enzyme catalyzes that initial breakdown?","options":["Phosphofructokinase, the rate-limiting enzyme that mobilizes stored fat","Hormone-sensitive lipase","Pyruvate dehydrogenase, which prepares the fatty acids to enter the Krebs cycle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Hormone-sensitive lipase","explanation_en":"Triglycerides stored in fat cells are broken down by hormone-sensitive lipase into free fatty acids and glycerol; the free fatty acids then travel to muscle and undergo oxidation to resynthesize ATP. Pyruvate dehydrogenase acts on pyruvate (a carbohydrate-pathway intermediate), and phosphofructokinase is the rate-limiting enzyme of glycolysis, not fat mobilization.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"脂肪細胞內的三酸甘油酯要先由荷爾蒙敏感脂肪酶(hormone-sensitive lipase)水解為遊離脂肪酸與甘油,遊離脂肪酸才能運往組織氧化供能。PFK 是糖解的限速酶,丙酮酸去氫酶作用於丙酮酸,都不負責脂肪動員。"},{"id":"q0080","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An S and C professional is setting safety guidelines for a healthy, resistance-training adult over 65. Which single recommendation best fits the guidance for this population?","options":["Cue a sustained Valsalva maneuver on every working set to maximize trunk stability","Test a true 1RM every session so progress can be tracked precisely","Generally avoid the Valsalva maneuver, since the blood pressure spike and dizziness it produces raise fall risk"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Generally avoid the Valsalva maneuver, since the blood pressure spike and dizziness it produces raise fall risk","explanation_en":"For older adults, the Valsalva maneuver should generally be avoided because it spikes blood pressure and can cause dizziness, raising fall risk; training should also use pain-free ranges and allow longer recovery. Routine maximal 1RM testing every session is inappropriate given the added risk and recovery demands.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"健康但年逾 65 的訓練者,建議一般避免 Valsalva,因為血壓驟升伴隨頭暈會提高跌倒風險;同時應使用無痛活動度、給較長恢復,每堂都測真正 1RM 也不恰當。"},{"id":"q0081","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A novice must consciously talk himself through each part of a new clean, while a veteran executes it automatically with a quiet mind and spare attention for the environment. In Fitts and Posner's model, these two performers sit at which ends of the learning sequence, first to last?","options":["Cognitive stage (early) and autonomous stage (late)","Associative stage (early) and cognitive stage (late)","Autonomous stage (early) and associative stage (late)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Cognitive stage (early) and autonomous stage (late)","explanation_en":"Fitts and Posner describe three stages in order: the cognitive stage (effortful, conscious regulation of movement), then the associative stage (refinement), then the autonomous stage (automatic performance with a relaxed mind). The novice is in the cognitive stage and the veteran in the autonomous stage.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Fitts 與 Posner 三階段順序為認知期(cognitive,有意識逐節自我指令、費力)→聯結期(associative,精修)→自動化期(autonomous,動作自動執行、心思放空還能兼顧環境)。新手在前段,老手在末段。"},{"id":"q0082","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sport psychologist maps an athlete's focus on two crossed dimensions, one running internal to external and the other running broad to narrow, and argues performance depends on matching the right focus to the task. This two-dimensional framework is best identified as:","options":["Catastrophe theory, describing a sudden performance collapse","Attentional styles, defined by direction (internal-external) and width (broad-narrow)","The inverted-U model, relating arousal to performance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Attentional styles, defined by direction (internal-external) and width (broad-narrow)","explanation_en":"The concept of attentional styles holds that focus varies along two dimensions, direction (internal versus external) and width (broad versus narrow), and that matching style to task demands is key. The inverted-U model and catastrophe theory both concern arousal-performance relationships, not attentional direction and width.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"這是 Nideffer 的注意風格(attentional styles)框架:注意力的方向(內向/外向)與廣度(廣闊/狹窄)兩個垂直維度,表現取決於風格是否匹配任務需求,與喚醒理論無關。"},{"id":"q0083","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach separates two things in a lifter: a stable personality tendency to read many situations as threatening, versus the specific apprehension the lifter feels in the moments before a max attempt. The stable, dispositional tendency is termed:","options":["State anxiety","Eustress","Trait anxiety"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Trait anxiety","explanation_en":"Trait anxiety is a personality variable, the disposition to perceive a wide range of situations as threatening. State anxiety is the moment-to-moment apprehension felt in a specific situation, and eustress is a positive stress response, not the stable dispositional trait.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"穩定的人格傾向—習慣性把各種情境解讀為威脅—稱特質焦慮(trait anxiety);當下具體情境的不安是狀態焦慮(state anxiety),eustress 則是正面的壓力反應。"},{"id":"q0084","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two lifters walk into a meet: one is nearly asleep and flat, the other is frantically over-hyped and shaky. According to the inverted-U theory, how does arousal relate to their expected performance?","options":["Performance improves as arousal rises to an optimal level, then declines with any further increase","Performance climbs continuously and linearly the more aroused an athlete becomes","Arousal and performance have no consistent relationship"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Performance improves as arousal rises to an optimal level, then declines with any further increase","explanation_en":"The inverted-U theory holds that arousal facilitates performance up to an optimal point, beyond which additional arousal is associated with declining performance. Both under-arousal (flat) and over-arousal (frantic) sit below the peak of the curve.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"倒U(inverted-U)理論:喚醒上升到最佳點前表現隨之改善,越過最佳點後再升反而下滑。「幾乎睡著」和「過度亢奮發抖」都落在曲線的兩側低谷。"},{"id":"q0085","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach must psych up an athlete before a simple, well-drilled max deadlift, but calm a different athlete who is still learning a complex, attention-heavy new skill. Regarding the optimal arousal point for each, which statement is correct?","options":["Optimal arousal is the same regardless of skill complexity or the athlete's experience","The optimal arousal point is lower for the complex skill and for the less-skilled performer","The optimal arousal point is higher for the complex skill and for the less-skilled performer"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The optimal arousal point is lower for the complex skill and for the less-skilled performer","explanation_en":"The optimal arousal point is lower for less-skilled athletes and for complex skills, because worrisome thoughts compete for the limited attentional capacity already occupied by movement details. Coaches should lower arousal for novices and complex tasks and may raise it for simple, well-learned skills.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最佳喚醒點對複雜動作與不熟練者較低—擔心雜念會與動作細節搶有限的注意力;簡單且高度熟練的最大重量硬拉反而適合較高喚醒。"},{"id":"q0086","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a heavy pull, a lifter silently repeats \"chest up, drive the floor\" to himself to hold a key technical point of the lift. Classifying self-talk as positive, negative, or instructional, this cue is best labeled as:","options":["Positive (motivational) self-talk","Negative self-talk","Instructional self-talk"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Instructional self-talk","explanation_en":"Self-talk is generally categorized as positive, negative, or instructional. Instructional self-talk directs attention to the technical, task-relevant elements of the skill (\"chest up, drive the floor\"), whereas positive (motivational) self-talk is encouraging (\"I can do this\") and negative self-talk is self-critical.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「挺胸、踩地」這類把注意力導向技術重點的自我對話屬指令型(instructional)self-talk;「我可以」屬正向/動機型,自責嘅屬負向。"},{"id":"q0087","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sidelined athlete who cannot physically train is guided to vividly rehearse flawless performances of her event using all her senses. Which of the following is a genuine advantage that this imagery offers over real practice?","options":["The outcome is fully under her control, so she can repeatedly experience success","It reproduces the same outcome uncertainty she would face in real competition","It lets her rehearse without engaging any of the senses"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The outcome is fully under her control, so she can repeatedly experience success","explanation_en":"Imagery is a cognitive skill in which the athlete creates or re-creates an experience using all the senses. A key advantage is that successful performance is entirely under the athlete's control during imaging, whereas reality always carries uncertainty of outcome. Imagery deliberately uses the senses rather than removing them.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"表象練習(imagery)相對於真實練習的一個真正優勢是結果完全由自己掌控,可以反覆「經歷」完美成功;真實比賽永遠有結果不確定性。表象刻意動用各種感官,不是不靠感官。"},{"id":"q0088","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Before competition, an athlete works through her body one muscle group at a time, deliberately tensing then releasing each, to regulate both mental and physical arousal via control of skeletal muscle tension. This technique is:","options":["Systematic desensitization to a feared stimulus","Progressive muscle relaxation","Autogenic training, which uses self-suggestions of warmth and heaviness"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Progressive muscle relaxation","explanation_en":"Progressive muscle relaxation self-regulates psychological and physical arousal through deliberate tensing and releasing of skeletal muscle, and can be paired with diaphragmatic breathing. Autogenic training instead relies on self-statements of warmth and heaviness, and systematic desensitization is a fear-reduction procedure, not tension cycling.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"逐組肌肉刻意收緊再釋放、藉控制骨骼肌張力來調節身心喚醒的技術是漸進式肌肉放鬆(progressive muscle relaxation),可搭配腹式呼吸;自我暗示溫熱與沉重的是自律訓練,系統減敏感則針對恐懼刺激。"},{"id":"q0089","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After a change-of-direction drill, a coach gives one athlete only her stopwatch time, and gives another a breakdown of how her hips and torso collapsed during the cut. The stopwatch time is knowledge of results; the description of the movement pattern is best termed:","options":["Knowledge of results","Intrinsic feedback that the athlete senses on her own","Knowledge of performance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Knowledge of performance","explanation_en":"Augmented feedback splits into knowledge of results, information about the outcome relative to the goal (the drill time), and knowledge of performance, information about the movement pattern itself (hip and torso position during the cut). Intrinsic feedback is what the athlete perceives directly, not information the coach supplies.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"跑表時間告訴的是結果與目標的差距,屬結果知識(knowledge of results, KR);分析髖與軀幹如何塌陷屬動作模式本身的資訊,稱表現知識(knowledge of performance, KP);運動員自己感覺到的才是內在回饋。"},{"id":"q0090","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Rather than having athletes finish all reps of one jump before starting the next, a coach shuffles several different jump skills into an unpredictable order within a single session. This arrangement is called:","options":["Random practice","Blocked practice","Massed practice"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Random practice","explanation_en":"In random practice, multiple skills are practiced in an interleaved, unpredictable order within a session, in contrast to blocked practice, in which one skill is repeated many times before moving on. Massed practice refers to short or absent rest between attempts (a work-to-rest dimension), not the ordering of skills.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多個動作交錯、順序不可預期地安排在同一課表是隨機練習(random practice);先練熟一個再換下個是區塊練習(blocked);集中練習(massed)講的是試次間休息短暫,與順序無關。"},{"id":"q0091","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While teaching a complex new skill, a coach tells the athlete after each rep only whether the attempt met the goal (correct or not correct), without describing how the movement looked. This augmented feedback is:","options":["Intrinsic feedback","Knowledge of results","Knowledge of performance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Knowledge of results","explanation_en":"Knowledge of results gives information about the outcome of the movement relative to the goal (whether it was correct), whereas knowledge of performance describes how the movement pattern was carried out. Intrinsic feedback is sensed by the athlete directly rather than provided by the coach.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每一下只回報「達標/未達標」而不描述動作,是典型的結果知識(KR);描述動作如何做出來的是表現知識(KP);教練提供的屬外加回饋,不是內在回饋。"},{"id":"q0092","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach debates whether to correct errors mainly by punishing mistakes or by reinforcing correct actions. Per sport psychology guidance, what is the primary reason reinforcement is generally preferred over punishment?","options":["Punishment builds skills faster than reinforcement and carries no meaningful downside","Reinforcement is effective only with elite athletes, so it is the safer default","Punishment floods limited attention with task-irrelevant thoughts like fear of failure, while reinforcement directs attention to task-relevant cues and what to do correctly"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Punishment floods limited attention with task-irrelevant thoughts like fear of failure, while reinforcement directs attention to task-relevant cues and what to do correctly","explanation_en":"Reinforcement helps athletes attend to task-relevant cues and what to do correctly, whereas punishment tends to flood limited attentional capacity with task-irrelevant cognitions such as fear of failure. Reinforcement is therefore generally preferred, and it is effective across skill levels, not only with elite athletes.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"優先使用增強(reinforcement)的理由:它把注意力引導到與任務相關的線索與「該怎麼做對」;懲罰則讓「怕失敗」這類任務無關的念頭塞滿有限的注意力容量。增強對各程度運動員都有效。"},{"id":"q0093","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete training in the heat is told to drink enough during exercise that his body weight loss stays below the threshold at which performance suffers and heat illness risk climbs. Fluid-related body weight loss during exercise should not exceed roughly:","options":["2% of body weight","5% of body weight","8% of body weight"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"2% of body weight","explanation_en":"Athletes should drink enough during exercise to keep water weight losses under about 2% of body weight, which helps prevent overheating, dehydration, and heat illness while protecting performance. Losses of 5% or more represent substantial dehydration well beyond the recommended limit.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動中體重流失應控制在約 2% 以內;超過這個閾值表現開始受損,中暑與熱疾病風險也上升。5%、8% 早已是明顯脫水的範疇。"},{"id":"q0094","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete asks about a widely studied, legal ergogenic aid found in coffee and tea that helps both endurance and resistance athletes, but is regulated in a category distinct from most dietary supplements. Which substance fits, and how is it classified?","options":["Sodium chloride, classified as a stimulant drug","Caffeine, which is classified as a drug rather than a dietary supplement","Creatine monohydrate, classified as a drug rather than a dietary supplement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Caffeine, which is classified as a drug rather than a dietary supplement","explanation_en":"Caffeine is a central nervous system stimulant found in coffee, tea, soft drinks, and chocolate and is popular with both aerobic endurance and resistance athletes; unlike most dietary supplements, it is categorized as a drug. Creatine is regulated as a dietary supplement, and sodium chloride is a dietary mineral, not a stimulant drug.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"咖啡因存在於咖啡、茶、飲料與巧克力,受有氧耐力與力量選手廣泛使用,在監管分類上被歸為藥物(drug)而非膳食補充劑—這正是它與肌酸(歸膳食補充劑)不同的地方。"},{"id":"q0095","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete tracking intake wants to convert grams of each macronutrient into calories. Which set of energy values is correct?","options":["Carbohydrate 4, protein 9, fat 9 kcal per gram","Carbohydrate 7, protein 4, fat 4 kcal per gram","Carbohydrate 4, protein 4, fat 9 kcal per gram"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Carbohydrate 4, protein 4, fat 9 kcal per gram","explanation_en":"Carbohydrate and protein each provide approximately 4 kcal per gram, while fat provides approximately 9 kcal per gram because fats carry more carbon and hydrogen relative to oxygen. Protein is 4, not 9, kcal per gram (the 7 kcal/g figure belongs to alcohol, not a macronutrient here).","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱量數值:碳水與蛋白質各約 4 kcal/g,脂肪約 9 kcal/g(脂肪的碳氫相對含氧比例高,所以能量密度大)。7 kcal/g 是酒精,不是三大營養素。"},{"id":"q0096","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants a nutritional strategy that raises the muscle's capacity to buffer or neutralize the hydrogen ions that accumulate during repeated high-intensity efforts. Which pairing works primarily through that buffering mechanism?","options":["Beta-alanine and sodium bicarbonate","Caffeine and creatine monohydrate","Vitamin C and iron"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Beta-alanine and sodium bicarbonate","explanation_en":"Improving buffering capacity through beta-alanine (which raises intramuscular carnosine) and sodium bicarbonate (an alkalinizing agent) can aid performance in activities limited by hydrogen ion buildup. Caffeine acts as a CNS stimulant and creatine works through the phosphagen system, while vitamin C and iron have no primary acid-buffering role.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸(beta-alanine)提升肌肉肌肽(carnosine)含量、碳酸氫鈉(sodium bicarbonate)屬鹼化劑,兩者都以緩衝 H+ 為機制,幫助反覆高強度、受酸中毒限制表現的專案;咖啡因是中樞刺激,肌酸走磷酸原途徑。"},{"id":"q0097","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Three athletes ask whether carbohydrate loading is worth it: a marathoner, a 100 m sprinter, and a powerlifter. Carbohydrate loading is most likely to improve performance for which one?","options":["The powerlifter, performing single maximal-strength attempts","The marathoner, whose continuous event runs well beyond about 90 minutes","The 100 m sprinter, whose maximal effort lasts under about 10 seconds"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The marathoner, whose continuous event runs well beyond about 90 minutes","explanation_en":"Carbohydrate loading raises pre-event muscle glycogen and benefits continuous aerobic endurance events lasting longer than about 90 minutes (distance running, road cycling, cross-country skiing), where glycogen depletion would otherwise limit late-event performance. It does little for brief, high-power efforts like sprints or maximal lifts, which rely on the phosphagen system.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肝糖超補積載只對超過約 90 分鐘的連續有氧專案(馬拉松、公路單車、越野滑雪)有證據支援—它提高起始肝糖、延後後段耗盡;100 米與舉重這類數秒的全力專案靠磷酸原,補充肝糖幫助不大。"},{"id":"q0098","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is selecting a sports drink for an athlete training in the heat and wants the electrolyte and carbohydrate content to match the recommended composition. Which option fits?","options":["60 mEq sodium and 30 mEq potassium per liter, with about 1% carbohydrate","No added sodium or potassium, with about 25% carbohydrate","20 to 30 mEq sodium and 2 to 5 mEq potassium per liter, with 5% to 10% carbohydrate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"20 to 30 mEq sodium and 2 to 5 mEq potassium per liter, with 5% to 10% carbohydrate","explanation_en":"The optimal sport drink contains 20 to 30 mEq of sodium and 2 to 5 mEq of potassium per liter, with carbohydrate at a 5% to 10% concentration. Very high electrolyte loads or a 25% carbohydrate concentration slow gastric emptying and can worsen, not aid, hydration.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動飲料的建議組成:每升含鈉 20 到 30 mEq、鉀 2 到 5 mEq,碳水化合物濃度 5% 到 10%;電解質太濃或碳水濃到 25% 會拖慢胃排空,反而妨礙補水。"},{"id":"q0099","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete weighing anabolic-androgenic steroid use asks you to state the documented health risks accurately. Which option correctly describes adverse effects associated with anabolic steroid abuse?","options":["Increased risk of liver tumors and liver damage, unfavorable blood lipid changes, and elevated blood pressure","An improved cholesterol profile alongside lowered blood pressure","No documented effect on either the liver or the cardiovascular system"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increased risk of liver tumors and liver damage, unfavorable blood lipid changes, and elevated blood pressure","explanation_en":"Documented adverse effects of anabolic steroid abuse include hepatic effects such as increased risk of liver tumors and liver damage, plus cardiovascular effects including unfavorable lipid profile changes and elevated blood pressure, along with endocrine and psychological effects. Steroids worsen, not improve, the lipid profile and blood pressure.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"合成代謝類固醇濫用的文獻風險:肝腫瘤與肝損傷風險提高、血脂譜惡化(HDL 降、LDL 升)、血壓上升,另有內分泌與心理效應;它不會改善膽固醇、也不會對肝與心血管毫無影響。"},{"id":"q0100","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Immediately after a heavy resistance session, a healthy younger adult wants the post-training feeding that best drives muscle protein synthesis. Which recommendation fits that acute window?","options":["At least 100 grams of protein, regardless of the source","About 20 to 50 grams of a high-quality, high-leucine protein","About 3 to 5 grams of protein from any source"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 20 to 50 grams of a high-quality, high-leucine protein","explanation_en":"After resistance training, younger individuals should consume about 20 to 50 grams (roughly 8.5 to 20 grams of essential amino acids) of a high-quality, high-leucine protein to maximally stimulate muscle protein synthesis; older adults may need 40 grams or more. A few grams is too little to maximize the response, and 100+ grams offers no added synthesis benefit for a single feeding.","tags":["Scientific Foundations - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"年輕人在阻力訓練後攝取約 20 到 50 g(約含必需胺基酸 8.5 到 20 g)高品質、富含白胺酸(leucine)的蛋白,即可最大化刺激肌蛋白合成;老年人可能要 40 g 以上,單餐 100 g 以上並無額外好處。"},{"id":"q0101","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are profiling a Division I athlete for the off-season and decide her primary resistance training goal is strength/power. Why should you commit to ONE primary training outcome per training block rather than chasing strength and muscular endurance at the same time?","options":["Concentrating on one outcome per block (emphasis/de-emphasis) lets you give a sufficient, focused stimulus while still maintaining other qualities, instead of diluting the adaptation","Training two qualities at once is biomechanically impossible because the load-repetition relationship only allows a single rep range","Insurance and liability rules prohibit programming more than one fitness characteristic in a block"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Concentrating on one outcome per block (emphasis/de-emphasis) lets you give a sufficient, focused stimulus while still maintaining other qualities, instead of diluting the adaptation","explanation_en":"The book recommends concentrating on only one training outcome per block using an emphasis/de-emphasis approach, while still providing enough stimulus to maintain other qualities for later blocks.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書主張每個中週期只聚焦一個訓練成果,用 emphasis/de-emphasis 方式給它足夠且集中的刺激,其他素質只用最小劑量維持;同時追力量與肌耐力會稀釋彼此的特異性適應。不是生理上不可能並存,而是不經濟。"},{"id":"q0102","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A beginner client just started training and you are choosing which exercises to prioritize. Why do CORE exercises receive priority over assistance exercises when selecting exercises?","options":["Because assistance exercises are unsafe for beginners and must be removed entirely","Because core exercises recruit large muscle areas, involve two or more primary joints, and have greater dynamic correspondence (transfer) to sport movements","Because core exercises always use lighter loads, making them easier to coach first"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Because core exercises recruit large muscle areas, involve two or more primary joints, and have greater dynamic correspondence (transfer) to sport movements","explanation_en":"Core exercises recruit one or more large muscle areas and involve multiple primary joints, giving them direct application and dynamic correspondence to sport; that's why they're prioritized.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"核心練習(core exercise, NSCA 分類用語)動員一個或多個大肌群、涉及兩個以上主要關節,與專項動作的動態對應性(轉移效果)較高,因此選動作時優先;輔助動作並非對新手不安全,只是層級較低。"},{"id":"q0103","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete's session includes a power clean, a back squat, a barbell row, and biceps curls. Following the recommended exercise order, where should the power clean go and why?","options":["Last, so accumulated fatigue forces greater motor-unit recruitment","First, because power exercises place a large neuromuscular and skill demand and are prone to fatigue, so the athlete should perform them while metabolically fresh","It doesn't matter; exercise order has no documented effect on adaptation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"First, because power exercises place a large neuromuscular and skill demand and are prone to fatigue, so the athlete should perform them while metabolically fresh","explanation_en":"Power exercises are performed first because of their high neuromuscular and skill demand and proneness to fatigue; doing them fresh protects technique and reduces injury risk.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"功率型動作(power clean)排最前:神經與技術需求高、最容易受疲勞破壞,要在體力充沛時做以守住技術並降低受傷風險。排在最後讓疲勞「逼出」徵收是倒果為因。"},{"id":"q0104","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You program a core exercise for a trained athlete with a goal of maximal muscular strength. Which load-and-rep prescription fits?","options":["About 67-80% of 1RM for 8-12 reps","Less than or equal to 67% of 1RM for 12 or more reps","Greater than or equal to 85% of 1RM for 6 or fewer reps"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Greater than or equal to 85% of 1RM for 6 or fewer reps","explanation_en":"Per table 18.11, strength training in core exercises uses loads of >=85% 1RM for <=6 goal reps; the heavier the load, the fewer reps possible.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"表 18.11 的核心動作最大肌力處方:強度≥85% 1RM、目標次數≤6;負荷越重可做的次數越少。67 到 80%×8 到 12 是肥大區,≤67%×12+ 是肌耐力區。"},{"id":"q0105","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A hypertrophy-focused athlete is doing a multijoint exercise (e.g., back squat) and a single-joint assistance exercise (e.g., lateral raise) in the same session. How should rest periods differ between the two?","options":["Both get the same 30-second rest because they share the hypertrophy goal","The multijoint exercise gets ~2-3 min while the single-joint exercise gets ~60-90 s, because rest is set by relative load and muscle mass involved","The single-joint exercise needs longer rest (3-5 min) because isolation work is more fatiguing"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The multijoint exercise gets ~2-3 min while the single-joint exercise gets ~60-90 s, because rest is set by relative load and muscle mass involved","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy rest is ~2-3 min for multijoint and 60-90 s for single-joint work; rest is allocated by relative load and amount of muscle mass, not just the overall training goal.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"組間休息依各動作的相對負荷與動員肌量分配,不單看訓練目標:肥大期多關節深蹲約 2 到 3 分鐘,單關側平舉約 60 到 90 秒。孤立動作不會比多關節動作更累到需要更長休息。"},{"id":"q0106","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You assigned 3 sets of 6 reps in the bench press. After a few weeks the athlete completes 8 reps in the last set on two consecutive workouts. Per the 2-for-2 rule, what should you do?","options":["Increase the load for that exercise at the next training session","Keep the load the same but add two more sets","Drop the load by 10% to manage accumulated fatigue"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increase the load for that exercise at the next training session","explanation_en":"The 2-for-2 rule: if the athlete can perform 2 or more reps over the goal in the last set for two consecutive workouts, add weight to that exercise next session.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"2-for-2 規則:連續兩次訓練的最後一組都能超出目標次數 2 次或以上,就表示現有負荷已夠輕—下次課直接為該動作增加重量,而不是加組或降重量。"},{"id":"q0107","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a depth jump, an athlete pauses noticeably on the ground between landing and the next jump. What happens to the stretch-shortening cycle if this amortization (coupling) phase lasts too long?","options":["More elastic energy is stored, making the subsequent jump higher","The stored elastic energy dissipates as heat and the stretch reflex won't enhance concentric force","The Golgi tendon organ is desensitized, increasing force output"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The stored elastic energy dissipates as heat and the stretch reflex won't enhance concentric force","explanation_en":"If the amortization phase is too long, the elastic energy stored during the eccentric phase is lost as heat and the stretch reflex no longer augments the concentric muscle action.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"伸展—縮短迴圈(SSC)的效益取決於短 amortization(緩衝)期:落地停留過久,離心期儲存的彈性勢能轉為熱散掉,伸展反射也錯過了增強後續向心收縮的時間窗,跳躍表現因此下降。"},{"id":"q0108","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"On the continuum of plyometric drills, which of the following is correctly ordered from LOWEST to HIGHEST intensity?","options":["Depth jumps, box jumps, jumps in place, skips","Skips (jumps in place), standing jumps, box jumps, depth jumps","Box jumps, depth jumps, multiple hops, standing jumps"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Skips (jumps in place), standing jumps, box jumps, depth jumps","explanation_en":"The intensity continuum runs from low-intensity drills like skips/jumps in place up through standing jumps and box jumps to depth jumps (highest); as intensity rises, volume should fall.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式動作強度由低到高:skip/原地跳→站姿跳(standing jumps)→跳箱→深跳(depth jump,最高);強度上升時訓練量應對應下降。"},{"id":"q0109","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are prescribing lower-body plyometric volume for a beginner (no experience) doing low-intensity drills. Volume is counted in foot contacts per session. Which range is appropriate for that beginner?","options":["Around 80 to 100 foot contacts","Around 120 to 200 foot contacts","Around 100 to 120 foot contacts"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Around 80 to 100 foot contacts","explanation_en":"Per table 19.6, a beginner at low intensity is prescribed roughly 80-100 foot contacts; higher experience and intensity levels permit different volumes, and beginners are not recommended at high intensity.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"初學者(無經驗)做低強度增強式的建議量約 80 到 100 次腳部觸地(foot contacts)/堂;初學者不建議上高強度,120 以上已超出新手建議。"},{"id":"q0110","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 235-pound athlete wants to add high-box depth jumps. What is the appropriate caution, and what is the maximal practical depth-jump box height for effective, safe performance?","options":["No cautions apply to heavier athletes; depth jumps up to 60 in. (152 cm) are recommended for everyone","Athletes over 220 lb (100 kg) should approach high-intensity plyometrics and depth jumps from heights >18 in. (46 cm) with caution; a box of about 48 in. (122 cm) is roughly the upper effective limit","Athletes over 220 lb should only ever use boxes taller than 48 in. (122 cm) to overload the tissues"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Athletes over 220 lb (100 kg) should approach high-intensity plyometrics and depth jumps from heights >18 in. (46 cm) with caution; a box of about 48 in. (122 cm) is roughly the upper effective limit","explanation_en":"Athletes weighing over 220 lb (100 kg) should be cautious with high-intensity plyometrics and depth jumps from boxes higher than 18 in.; about 48 in. (122 cm) is near the maximal effective/safe depth-jump height before technique breaks down.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"體重超過 220 磅(100 公斤)的運動員對高強度增強式與高度超過 18 吋(46 公分)的深跳要謹慎;深跳箱高約 48 吋(122 公分)已接近技術會垮掉的有效上限,再高只是多風險。"},{"id":"q0111","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to improve an athlete's maximal sprinting speed. Sprint speed is the product of which two variables, and what ultimately underpins maximizing both?","options":["Stride length and stride (step) frequency, both underpinned by rapid force production into the ground","Reaction time and arm-swing amplitude, underpinned by flexibility","Ground contact time and body mass, underpinned by aerobic capacity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Stride length and stride (step) frequency, both underpinned by rapid force production into the ground","explanation_en":"Running velocity is a product of step length and step frequency, and the underlying component to maximizing both is rapid force production applied to the ground.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"跑步速度=步幅×步頻,兩者共同的根基是短暫接地時間內快速輸出對地的力量(rapid force production);不是反應時間加擺臂,也不是靠有氧能力。"},{"id":"q0112","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete tries to run faster by deliberately reaching out and overstriding. Why does overstriding HURT sprint performance?","options":["It increases ground contact time, which dampens the stretch-shortening cycle and lowers step frequency","It shortens ground contact time so much that the athlete can't produce force","It increases step frequency but reduces stride length below optimal"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It increases ground contact time, which dampens the stretch-shortening cycle and lowers step frequency","explanation_en":"Overstriding attempts to gain speed via larger ground contact times, which dampens the SSC and lowers step frequency; success comes from high vertical force in a short contact time.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"跨步(overstriding)企圖用加大接地時間換取步幅,結果反而抑制伸展—縮短迴圈的利用並拖慢步頻;速度來自短接觸時間內的高豎直力量,不是把腿往前伸。"},{"id":"q0113","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You add overspeed (assisted) sprint training such as towing or downhill running for an advanced athlete. What is the recommended ceiling on the speed increase, and a key drawback?","options":["Increases should be limited to <=10%; assisted sprinting can cause chop steps and undesirable braking/overstriding mechanics","Increases should reach 25-30%; there are no documented technique drawbacks","There is no recommended limit; assisted work always improves propulsive force"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increases should be limited to <=10%; assisted sprinting can cause chop steps and undesirable braking/overstriding mechanics","explanation_en":"Assisted/overspeed increases should be limited to <=10%; pushing beyond can prematurely rush the stance phase, reduce muscle activation/propulsive force, and produce chop steps, leaning back, and overstriding.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"超速訓練(拖曳、下坡)的速度增幅建議控制在 10% 以內;超過會迫使預擺提前、肌肉活化與推進力下降,出現碎步、身體後傾、跨步等壞機制—加速反而變慢。"},{"id":"q0114","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Agility differs from simple change-of-direction (COD) ability. What added component defines AGILITY?","options":["A predetermined movement pattern executed at maximal speed","A perceptual-cognitive component (responding to a stimulus) combined with change-of-direction ability","Purely greater eccentric strength with no cognitive demand"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A perceptual-cognitive component (responding to a stimulus) combined with change-of-direction ability","explanation_en":"COD is a planned change of direction; agility additionally requires perceptual-cognitive ability, changing direction/velocity/mode in response to a stimulus.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"敏捷(agility)=變向能力(change of direction)+知覺認知成分:必須針對刺激(對手、訊號)改變方向、速度或動作模式;預先規劃好的變向只有 COD 成分。"},{"id":"q0115","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An advanced runner needs work just at race pace to improve lactate threshold and the maximal lactate steady state. Which aerobic endurance method is built around an intensity at or slightly above race pace, corresponding roughly to MLSS?","options":["Long, slow (extensive endurance) training","Pace/tempo (threshold) training","Fartlek training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Pace/tempo (threshold) training","explanation_en":"Pace/tempo (threshold) training uses an intensity at or slightly higher than race pace, corresponding approximately to MLSS, to improve running economy, LT, and MLSS.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"配速/節奏閾值訓練(pace/tempo, threshold training)的強度設在比賽配速或略高,約對應最大乳酸穩定狀態(MLSS),用來改善跑步經濟性、乳酸閾值與 MLSS;長慢跑與 fartlek 都不是這個定位。"},{"id":"q0116","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You program classic interval training for a runner. Work intervals close to VO2max typically last 3-5 minutes; what work-to-rest ratio is recommended for those intervals?","options":["About 1:3, with rest three times the work duration","About 1:1, with the rest interval equal to the work interval","About 3:1, with work three times the rest duration"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 1:1, with the rest interval equal to the work interval","explanation_en":"For 3- to 5-minute interval work bouts near VO2max, the rest interval should equal the work interval, keeping a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"經典間歇訓練:接近 VO2max 的 3 到 5 分鐘工作段,休息時間與工作段相同,工休比約 1:1,目的是累積接近 VO2max 的時間。"},{"id":"q0117","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A swimmer's coach wants variety and asks you to describe Fartlek training. Fartlek is best characterized as which of the following?","options":["A combination of extensive endurance, pace/tempo, and interval-type efforts (speed play) that challenges all body systems","Continuous training at a single fixed intensity below the lactate threshold","Maximal sprints with full passive recovery and no aerobic component"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A combination of extensive endurance, pace/tempo, and interval-type efforts (speed play) that challenges all body systems","explanation_en":"Fartlek ('speed play') blends extensive endurance with bursts of pace/tempo and interval-type efforts, challenging all systems and helping raise VO2max, LT, economy, and fuel use.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Fartlek(「速度遊戲」)是把持續性耐力、配速/閾值與間歇式努力自由混合的訓練,同時挑戰多個能量系統,有助於提升 VO2max、乳酸閾值、經濟性與燃料利用;它既非單一強度,也非純無氧衝刺。"},{"id":"q0118","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete under heavy psychoemotional and occupational stress keeps getting more intense training. Per Selye's General Adaptation Syndrome, prolonged excessive stress pushes the athlete toward which phase, associated with overreaching/overtraining?","options":["The alarm phase","The resistance (adaptation) phase","The exhaustion phase"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The exhaustion phase","explanation_en":"If stress persists too long, the athlete moves into the exhaustion phase of the GAS, where they fail to adapt and most likely experience overreaching or overtraining.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Selye 一般適應症候群(GAS)分驚覺、抵抗、衰竭三期;壓力長期過大而恢復不足時進入衰竭期(exhaustion),無法再適應,表現出過度負荷(overreaching)或過度訓練(overtraining)。"},{"id":"q0119","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are planning a training block that is several weeks long. On the periodization hierarchy, what is the cycle that typically lasts two to six weeks, with four weeks being the most common duration?","options":["Microcycle","Mesocycle","Macrocycle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Mesocycle","explanation_en":"A mesocycle lasts several weeks to months (typically 2-6 weeks, most commonly 4); microcycles are usually about a week, and a macrocycle spans months to a year.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"中週期(mesocycle)通常 2 到 6 週、以 4 週最常見;微週期約一週,大週期數月到一年。數週長的訓練區塊就是中週期。"},{"id":"q0120","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are designing the general preparatory (off-season) phase for a strength athlete. In the traditional periodization model, what are the intensity/volume characteristics and primary goals of the hypertrophy/strength-endurance phase?","options":["Low-to-moderate intensity, high volume; goals are to build work capacity and muscle mass as a foundation","Very high intensity (50% to >=93% 1RM), very low volume; goal is to peak performance","Maximal intensity (>=85% 1RM), low volume; goal is maximal strength"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Low-to-moderate intensity, high volume; goals are to build work capacity and muscle mass as a foundation","explanation_en":"The hypertrophy/strength-endurance phase sits early in the preparatory period with low-to-moderate intensity and high volume, building work capacity and muscle mass for later higher-intensity phases.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統週期化的準備期早期是肥大/肌力耐力階段:低到中強度、高訓練量,目的是建立工作容量與肌肉量,作為後續高強度階段的基礎;高強度低量屬後期的高峰化安排。"},{"id":"q0121","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two programs are compared: Program A keeps reps fixed but rotates heavy/medium/light loads day to day within a week; Program B gradually raises intensity and lowers volume across successive multi-week blocks. What are these two models called?","options":["A is the traditional (so-called linear) model; B is daily undulating periodization","A is daily undulating periodization; B is the traditional (so-called linear) model","Both are parallel models with no meaningful difference"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A is daily undulating periodization; B is the traditional (so-called linear) model","explanation_en":"Daily undulating periodization varies the load (and thus volume-load) across days within the week, while the traditional ('linear') model progressively shifts toward higher intensity and lower volume across blocks.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"A 在固定次數下於一週內逐日輪替重/中/輕負荷,是每日波動週期化(daily undulating periodization);B 隨區塊推進漸升強度、漸降量,是傳統(所謂線性)模式。兩者對應別弄反。"},{"id":"q0122","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach builds a warm-up using the RAMP model. In the 'Activate and Mobilize' phase, what is the primary focus that distinguishes it from a traditional static-stretching warm-up?","options":["Holding end-range positions statically to lengthen individual muscles","Developing movement competency through key patterns like squats and lunges (mobility, not static flexibility)","Maximally raising heart rate before any skill work"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Developing movement competency through key patterns like squats and lunges (mobility, not static flexibility)","explanation_en":"The 5th edition stresses that the Activate/Mobilize phase targets mobility, the capacity to move actively and effectively through movement patterns, not static flexibility of individual muscles.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RAMP 的 Activate and Mobilize 階段重點是發展行動能力與活動度(mobility):用深蹲、弓步等關鍵動作模式讓身體主動有效地通過動作幅度,不是像傳統熱身那樣靜態拉長個別肌肉。"},{"id":"q0123","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete needs maximal force and speed output in the activity that immediately follows the warm-up. Which RAMP phase is specifically designed to ramp activity intensity up to competition level and exploit the postactivation effect (treppe/staircase)?","options":["Raise","Activate and Mobilize","Potentiate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Potentiate","explanation_en":"The Potentiate phase uses sport- or capacity-specific activities of progressively increasing intensity; the contractile history (treppe/staircase effect) makes the motor neuron more sensitive, improving subsequent high-force, high-speed performance.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Potentiate(增能)階段:以專項或能力導向、強度漸增的活動把熱身推到比賽強度,並利用收縮歷史造成的 treppe/階梯效應(運動神經元敏感度提高)增強隨後的高力量高速度表現。"},{"id":"q0124","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a hold-relax PNF hamstring stretch, the athlete performs an isometric contraction of the hamstrings against the partner, then relaxes as the partner increases the stretch. The improved ROM after the isometric is primarily attributed to:","options":["Autogenic inhibition","Reciprocal inhibition of the quadriceps","Triggering of the stretch reflex"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Autogenic inhibition","explanation_en":"Contracting the muscle being stretched (the hamstrings) and then relaxing produces autogenic inhibition, allowing a greater subsequent passive stretch. The stretch reflex is something you avoid, not trigger, during stretching.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"hold-relax PNF 中,被伸展的膕繩肌做等長收縮會興奮高氏腱器,產生自生抑制(autogenic inhibition),放鬆後可進行更大的被動伸展。不是股四頭肌的互動抑制,也不是刻意觸發伸展反射。"},{"id":"q0125","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete uses a fast, bouncing sitting toe-touch where each rep pushes farther than the last. Why does the 5th edition caution that this ballistic approach may limit ROM gains compared with dynamic stretching?","options":["It cannot raise muscle temperature","It usually triggers the stretch reflex, which keeps the muscle from relaxing","It only works on the upper body"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It usually triggers the stretch reflex, which keeps the muscle from relaxing","explanation_en":"Ballistic stretching typically triggers the stretch reflex, preventing the muscle from relaxing, which can limit ROM. Dynamic stretching is controlled and moderate-paced, avoiding the negative effects associated with ballistic work.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"彈震式(ballistic)伸展快速的反彈通常會觸發伸展反射,肌肉不放鬆,限制 ROM 的進展;動態伸展則受控、中速,避開這個缺點。它不是不能升溫,也不只作用上身。"},{"id":"q0126","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A spotter is asked to spot a flat barbell bench press (an over-the-face exercise). Which grip should the spotter use on the bar?","options":["A closed pronated grip wider than the lifter's grip","A supinated grip matching the lifter's grip width","An alternated grip, usually narrower than the athlete's grip"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"An alternated grip, usually narrower than the athlete's grip","explanation_en":"For over-the-face barbell exercises the spotter grasps the bar with an alternated grip, usually narrower than the athlete's grip, to safely catch or assist with the load from a higher vantage point.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"保護位於臉部上方的槓鈴動作(平板臥推)時,保護者用交錯握(alternated grip,一手正一手反),通常略窄於選手的握距,才能在較高的位置安全接住或協助。"},{"id":"q0127","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An experienced lifter asks when breath holding (the Valsalva-type strategy) is acceptable rather than the standard exhale-through-the-sticking-point cue. The 5th edition's general breathing guidance is to:","options":["Always hold the breath through every set for spinal support","Exhale through the sticking point and inhale during the less stressful phase for most exercises","Inhale during the concentric phase and exhale during the eccentric phase"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Exhale through the sticking point and inhale during the less stressful phase for most exercises","explanation_en":"For most resistance exercises the athlete should exhale through the sticking point (the hardest part, just after the eccentric-to-concentric transition) and inhale during the less stressful phase. Breath holding is reserved for experienced lifters doing heavy structural exercises.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一般呼吸守則:在最費力的黏著點(sticking point)呼氣,在壓力較小的階段吸氣;閉氣(Valsalva 式)只保留給經驗豐富者做大重量結構性動作,不是每組都憋。"},{"id":"q0128","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following correctly lists the five points of the 'five-point body contact' position for a supine bench exercise?","options":["Head, shoulders/upper back, buttocks, right foot, left foot","Head, both hands, buttocks, both feet","Shoulders, hips, both knees, both feet"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Head, shoulders/upper back, buttocks, right foot, left foot","explanation_en":"The five-point body contact position is head, shoulders/upper back, and buttocks firmly on the bench, plus both feet flat on the floor. Maintaining it throughout the lift promotes maximal stability and spinal support.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"五點接觸位置=頭、肩/上背、臀部貼在凳面上,加兩腳踩實地面;全程維持它才能取得最大穩定與脊椎支撐。手不屬於接觸點之一。"},{"id":"q0129","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A new lifter wears a weight belt for every exercise, including biceps curls and lat pulldowns. What is the best coaching guidance?","options":["A belt is warranted only for exercises that stress the lower back done with near-maximal or maximal loads; overuse limits trunk-muscle training","Belts are appropriate for all exercises to build the habit","A belt should be worn only for upper-body pressing"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A belt is warranted only for exercises that stress the lower back done with near-maximal or maximal loads; overuse limits trunk-muscle training","explanation_en":"A belt is recommended for exercises stressing the lower back during near-maximal or maximal sets. It is not needed for exercises that do not stress the lower back, and wearing it too often reduces training of the abdominal and lower-back muscles.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"舉重皮帶只建議在會壓迫下背的動作(深蹲、硬拉等)於接近最大或最大重量時使用;舉啞鈴彎舉也繫帶只會讓腹部與下背肌肉失去自主穩定訓練的機會。"},{"id":"q0130","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are coaching a power clean. A trainee asks why you will not have a teammate stand by to 'catch' the bar like on the bench press. The best explanation is:","options":["One spotter is always enough for a power clean","The spotter should grasp the athlete's wrists during the catch","Power exercises are not spotted; athletes are instead taught how to miss the lift properly"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Power exercises are not spotted; athletes are instead taught how to miss the lift properly","explanation_en":"Power exercises (e.g., power clean, snatch, jerk) are not spotted because of the safety risk to both athlete and spotter; instead athletes are taught how to miss the lift safely.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"功率動作(power clean、snatch、jerk)不安排保護者:動作速度快,保護者來不及介入、反而危險對雙方;教法是教會運動員安全「棄槓」—向前丟槓掉槓。"},{"id":"q0131","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While watching a deadlift, you see the lifter's hips shoot up faster than the shoulders as the bar leaves the floor. The correct execution is to:","options":["Let the hips rise first to protect the knees","Keep the torso-to-floor angle constant so the hips and shoulders rise together, maintaining a neutral spine","Round the upper back to keep the bar closer"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Keep the torso-to-floor angle constant so the hips and shoulders rise together, maintaining a neutral spine","explanation_en":"In the deadlift the lifter extends the hips and knees while keeping the torso-to-floor angle constant; the hips should not rise before the shoulders, and a neutral spine is maintained with the bar kept close to the shins.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"硬拉的正確執行:髖與肩同步上升,軀幹對地面角度保持固定,脊椎中立,槓貼脛前上拉;臀部比肩部先竄起是典型錯誤,不是保護膝蓋的對策。"},{"id":"q0132","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is performing a two-arm kettlebell swing. Where should the hips and the back be at the bottom of the backswing?","options":["Hips flexed with the torso nearly parallel to the floor, back in a neutral spine, elbows extended","Hips fully extended with the back rounded to load the lats","Deep squat with the knees fully flexed and torso vertical"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hips flexed with the torso nearly parallel to the floor, back in a neutral spine, elbows extended","explanation_en":"The kettlebell swing is hip-hinge driven: at the backswing the hips flex until the torso is nearly parallel to the floor with the back neutral and elbows extended; hip extension then propels the bell forward and up to about eye level.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"雙臂壺鈴擺盪的後擺最低點是髖鉸鏈位置:髖關節屈曲至軀幹接近與地面平行、脊椎保持中立、手肘伸直;接著爆發性伸髖把壺鈴向前盪到約眼高。不是深蹲,也不是直背站直。"},{"id":"q0133","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach watches an athlete flipping a heavy tire and notices the athlete pulling the tire up with the arms (a lifting motion) instead of driving it. Why is this a dangerous flaw the coach should correct?","options":["It overloads the hamstrings and stalls the tire at the floor","It is unsafe only because it raises heart rate too quickly","It places greater load on the biceps (risking biceps injury) and the tire can lose momentum and fall back onto the athlete"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It places greater load on the biceps (risking biceps injury) and the tire can lose momentum and fall back onto the athlete","explanation_en":"Using a lifting rather than pushing motion makes the lifter muscle the tire over, loading the biceps and increasing biceps-injury risk, and the tire can lose momentum and fall backward. The cue is to keep hips low and drive the tire forward, moving with it.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"翻輪胎時用手「撈起來」而不是「推出去」,會讓肱二頭肌去扛輪胎重量(二頭肌受傷風險),且輪胎失去前進動量可能回落到人身上;口令是低髖、往前驅動、跟著輪胎走。"},{"id":"q0134","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When setting up a reverse sled drag (or forward sled pull), what foot position does the 5th edition recommend to maximize horizontal propulsive force?","options":["Feet positioned behind the knees with a vertical trunk","The front foot kept in front of the knees while leaning back with a relatively extended hip","Feet together directly under the hips throughout"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The front foot kept in front of the knees while leaning back with a relatively extended hip","explanation_en":"For the reverse sled drag the athlete leans back, keeps a relatively extended hip, and keeps the front foot in front of the knees throughout the pull to increase the ability to apply propulsive horizontal forces and accelerate the sled.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"反向雪橇拖行(與正向雪橇拉)的腳位建議:身體後傾、髖保持較大角度,前腳全程置於膝蓋前方,才最能對雪橇施加水平推進力並加速它。"},{"id":"q0135","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach builds a new body-fat assessment device and checks how well its readings line up with same-day DXA scans on the same athletes. What type of validity is being established?","options":["Concurrent validity","Predictive validity","Face validity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Concurrent validity","explanation_en":"Concurrent validity: a new test's scores are correlated with an already-accepted test of the same ability, measured at the same time (this new-body-fat-device-vs-DXA comparison is the textbook's own example of concurrent validity, and 'same-day' is the tell). It is not predictive (that links a score to FUTURE performance). And although DXA is a gold standard, the textbook still classifies validating a new practical test against an accepted test this way as concurrent (criterion validity), not convergent.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新裝置與已受認同的基準測試(同日的 DXA)同時測量並求相關,建立的是同時效度(concurrent validity,屬準則效度);預測效度看的是分數與未來表現的關聯。"},{"id":"q0136","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two different testers time the same group of athletes in the 40-yard sprint and consistently disagree with each other's recorded times. Which testing quality is lacking?","options":["Objectivity (interrater reliability)","Content validity","Intrasubject variability"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Objectivity (interrater reliability)","explanation_en":"Objectivity, also called interrater reliability or interrater agreement, is the degree to which different raters get the same result on repeated occasions. Disagreement between testers points to poor objectivity, often fixed with a clear scoring system and trained scorers.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩名測試者量同一批人卻拿不到一致成績,缺的是客觀性(objectivity),也稱評測者間信度(interrater reliability);改善方法是明確的計分標準與訓練過的計分者。"},{"id":"q0137","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You're sequencing a full test battery for a single session. Following the textbook's logical order, which group of tests should be administered FIRST?","options":["Maximum power and strength tests (1RM)","Agility tests like the T-test","Nonfatiguing tests like height, vertical jump, and flexibility"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Nonfatiguing tests like height, vertical jump, and flexibility","explanation_en":"The principle is that one test must not impair a later one. Nonfatiguing tests (anthropometry, flexibility, vertical jump) come first, then agility, then max power/strength, sprints, muscular endurance, anaerobic capacity, and finally aerobic capacity.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"測驗順序的第一原則是前一項不能影響後一項:先做不致疲勞的專案(身高體重、垂直跳、柔軟度),再敏捷、最大功率/肌力、衝刺、肌耐力、無氧容量,最後有氧耐力。"},{"id":"q0138","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete completes the T-test by sprinting forward, then shuffling left, right, and back without crossing the feet, touching cone bases by hand. What ability is this test primarily measuring?","options":["Maximal aerobic capacity","Lower-body maximal strength","Change of direction / agility"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Change of direction / agility","explanation_en":"The T-test is a change-of-direction (agility) test combining a forward sprint with lateral shuffles in a T-shaped pattern. The best of two trials is recorded to the nearest 0.1 second.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"T-test 的前衝、左側滑、右側滑、倒退走構成 T 字路線,測量的是變向能力/敏捷;取兩次嘗試中較佳一次,記到 0.1 秒。它不測有氧容量或最大肌力。"},{"id":"q0139","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to estimate an athlete's back squat 1RM from a load-velocity profile instead of testing it directly. What is the recommendation?","options":["The load-velocity profile reliably replaces a direct 1RM test","Directly test the 1RM; the load-velocity estimate tends to overestimate the true 1RM","Use the load-velocity profile only for the bench press, never the squat"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Directly test the 1RM; the load-velocity estimate tends to overestimate the true 1RM","explanation_en":"When the back-squat 1RM is estimated from a load-velocity profile it is highly variable and consistently OVERestimates the athlete's 1RM, so it should not be used for prediction. Direct testing remains the recommended way to determine maximal strength.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"以負荷—速度曲線推估Back Squat 1RM 變異大且一致高估真實 1RM,不建議拿它替代;教科書立場是直接測 1RM。"},{"id":"q0140","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A male NCAA Division I athlete's 1RM bench press falls at the 50th percentile on the normative table. How should you interpret this score?","options":["Well above average for his group","Average for his group","Well below average for his group"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Average for his group","explanation_en":"On the textbook's percentile descriptors, 90 = well above average, 70 = above average, 50 = average, 30 = below average, and 10 = well below average. A 50th-percentile score is simply average relative to the reference group.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"百分位對照:90 遠高於平均、70 高於平均、50 平均、30 低於平均、10 遠低於平均。50 百分位就是該對照組的平均值,沒有其他含義。"},{"id":"q0141","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During rehab from an anterior shoulder dislocation, the athletic trainer asks the S&C coach to begin upper-body strengthening, but notes the bench press should be avoided because it can place the shoulder in a vulnerable position. The bench press is best described as what for this athlete?","options":["An indication","A contraindication","A closed kinetic chain exercise"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A contraindication","explanation_en":"A contraindication is an activity that is inadvisable or prohibited given the injury. With anterior shoulder instability, the bench press can place the joint in a vulnerable position, making it contraindicated even while other upper-body work is indicated.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對前向肩關節不穩定的選手,臥推可能把肩置於危險姿勢,屬於該員的禁忌(contraindication);其他上肢強化則是被建議(indication)的,兩者不能混為一談。"},{"id":"q0142","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete reports that the pain from a muscle strain has resolved and wants to return to full play. Based on the tissue-healing model, why should the S&C professional be cautious?","options":["Pain often resolves well before tissue healing is complete, so reduced pain does not confirm it's safe to resume","Pain resolution always means the maturation-remodeling phase is finished","Once the inflammatory phase ends, full healing has occurred"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Pain often resolves well before tissue healing is complete, so reduced pain does not confirm it's safe to resume","explanation_en":"Pain levels typically decrease well before tissue healing reaches the adequate threshold. Athletes may wrongly assume that pain-free means healed, so return-to-play must be judged by healing and objective metrics, not pain alone.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"組織癒合的模型指出:疼痛往往遠早於組織癒合完成就消失;不痛不等於已癒合,復出與否要用癒合階段與客觀功能指標判斷,不能只問痛不痛。"},{"id":"q0143","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A preseason camp deliberately spikes training volume, causing a short-term performance dip, but after a few days to weeks of recovery the athletes supercompensate and perform better than before. This planned process is best termed what?","options":["Nonfunctional overreaching","Overtraining syndrome","Functional overreaching"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Functional overreaching","explanation_en":"Functional overreaching is purposely planned overload causing a brief performance decrement that, after short-term recovery (days to weeks), leads to supercompensation and improved performance. Nonfunctional overreaching only returns to baseline, and overtraining requires long-term impairment.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"刻意安排的短期超載、成績下滑、經數天到數週恢復後超補償反彈超過原水平—這是功能性過度負荷(functional overreaching);非功能性過度負荷恢復後大概只回原點,過度訓練症候群則要更久。"},{"id":"q0144","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When choosing tests for a daily athlete-monitoring program to catch impending overtraining, which category of assessment is most appropriate for everyday use?","options":["Category I: easy to administer, inexpensive, rapid turnaround, convenient daily","Category III: occasional, intrusive, expensive, long turnaround","Lab-based endocrine panels run weekly"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Category I: easy to administer, inexpensive, rapid turnaround, convenient daily","explanation_en":"Category I tests are daily, easy, inexpensive, and give rapid turnaround (e.g., RPE, resting/recovery HR, HRV, vertical jump), making them suited for routine monitoring. Category III tests are occasional, more intrusive, and slower, so they aren't practical day-to-day.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每日監測應選第一類(Category I)測驗:容易施測、便宜、出結果快,如 RPE、休息心率、HRV、垂直跳高度;第三類侵入性高、昂貴、出報錶慢,只適合偶爾使用。"},{"id":"q0145","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A new strength and conditioning facility is being built. During which phase of the design process is a reputable architect typically hired, usually through a bid process?","options":["The predesign phase","The design phase","The construction phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The predesign phase","explanation_en":"The predesign phase consists of a needs analysis, feasibility study, and master plan formation; hiring the architect (often via a low-bid process) is the final step of this phase, before the design phase begins.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"建館流程中,設計前階段(predesign)包含需求分析、可行性研究與整體計畫;聘請合格的建築師(常透過招標)是這一階段的最後一步,之後才進入設計階段。"},{"id":"q0146","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When planning the total area of a strength and conditioning facility, what is the recommended minimum amount of floor space per individual, counting all athletes, staff, and other persons present?","options":["50 square feet (4.6 m2) per person","100 square feet (9.3 m2) per person","200 square feet (18.6 m2) per person"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"100 square feet (9.3 m2) per person","explanation_en":"The recommended minimum is 100 square feet (9.3 m2) per individual, including all athletes, strength and conditioning professionals, and any additional staff present. Having enough space matters more for the training environment than having extra specialized equipment.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"場地面積規劃建議每人至少 100 平方英尺(9.3 平方公尺),物件包括所有選手、教練與在場人員;空間足夠比多買幾臺特殊器械更重要。"},{"id":"q0147","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is laying out a weight room and wants main walkways that allow safe traffic flow and ADA wheelchair access. What is the recommended width for these main walkways?","options":["2 to 3 feet (0.6-0.9 m)","5 to 7 feet (1.5-2.1 m)","10 to 12 feet (3.0-3.7 m)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"5 to 7 feet (1.5-2.1 m)","explanation_en":"Racks and machines are best lined up in rows running the length of the facility, creating two or three main walkways that should be 5 to 7 feet (1.5-2.1 m) wide. This supports safety, clear access to exits, and ADA-required wheelchair access. (Note: a separate minimum of 3 feet, 0.9 m, applies between individual pieces of equipment.)","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"器械與深蹲架成排沿場館長邊排列,留出兩到三條寬 5 到 7 英尺(1.5 到 2.1 公尺)的主要動線,兼顧安全、逃生與 ADA 輪椅通行;個別器械間另設至少 3 英尺的最小間距,兩者是不同規定。"},{"id":"q0148","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A facility will program box jumps, vertical jumps, and weightlifting. What ceiling height is recommended to give athletes enough clearance to comfortably perform most of these activities?","options":["8 to 10 feet (2.4-3.0 m)","12 to 14 feet (3.7-4.3 m)","16 to 18 feet (4.9-5.5 m)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"12 to 14 feet (3.7-4.3 m)","explanation_en":"A recommended ceiling height of 12 to 14 feet (3.7-4.3 m) accommodates the athlete plus the space needed for jumping and explosive lifting. Some exercises, like overhead medicine ball throws, may need additional clearance or an alternate space.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"場館淨高建議 12 到 14 英尺(3.7 到 4.3 公尺),讓跳躍與爆發性舉舉的動作有足夠 clearance;過頭藥球投擲這類動作可能要額外高度或另找空間。"},{"id":"q0149","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In the law of negligence, how is the standard of care for a strength and conditioning professional best described?","options":["The degree of caution and prudence a reasonable person would exercise in similar situations","The highest level of skill possessed by any expert in the field","Whatever level of care the athlete agrees to in a signed waiver"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The degree of caution and prudence a reasonable person would exercise in similar situations","explanation_en":"Standard of care is the degree of caution and prudence a reasonable person would exercise in similar situations. The strength and conditioning professional is expected to act according to their education, training, and certification.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"注意義務標準(standard of care)指合理之人在相同情況下會展現的謹慎與留意程度;體能教練被期待依其學歷、訓練與認證水準行事,而不是要求領域專家的最高技術。"},{"id":"q0150","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is recovering from a knee injury and asks the strength coach whether she is medically cleared to resume training. According to scope of practice, who is responsible for providing that medical clearance?","options":["The strength and conditioning professional, based on a movement screen","The sports medicine staff (e.g., athletic trainer, physician, or physical therapist)","The athletic director after reviewing the athlete's file"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The sports medicine staff (e.g., athletic trainer, physician, or physical therapist)","explanation_en":"It is not within the strength and conditioning professional's scope of practice to diagnose or evaluate a medical condition. Only the sports medicine staff can grant medical clearance; the coach then collaborates with them to modify workouts as needed.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"診斷與判定醫學狀況不在體能教練的執業範圍內;醫療放行(medical clearance)只能由運動醫療團隊(運動防護員、醫師、物理治療師)簽署,教練再據此配合調整課表。"},{"id":"q0151","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Per NSCA Strength and Conditioning Professional Standards and Guidelines (Guideline 3.1), which set of recommended professional-to-participant supervision ratios is correct?","options":["1:10 junior high school, 1:15 high school, 1:20 college","1:5 junior high school, 1:10 high school, 1:15 college","1:15 junior high school, 1:20 high school, 1:25 college"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1:10 junior high school, 1:15 high school, 1:20 college","explanation_en":"Guideline 3.1 recommends professional-to-participant ratios of 1:10 (junior high school), 1:15 (high school), and 1:20 (college), along with at least 100 ft2 of floor space per participant. Ratios should be increased (more supervision) for complex movements or low-training-age athletes.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"NSCA 準則 3.1:國中生 1:10、高中生 1:15、大專生 1:20,且每人至少 100 平方英尺;動作越複雜或年資越淺,監督比還應更緊(數字更小)。"},{"id":"q0152","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach notices a frayed cable on a machine, makes a mental note of it, but does not post an 'Out of Order' sign or remove it; an athlete is later injured using it. This scenario most directly illustrates which legal concept?","options":["Assumption of risk","Sovereign immunity","Negligence"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Negligence","explanation_en":"This is the textbook's example of negligence: the coach had a duty to fix the cable or post a sign, breached that duty by failing to act, and that failure proximately caused a foreseeable injury. Negligence requires duty, breach, causation, and damages.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam One"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"看到鋼纜磨損只記在心裡、沒掛「故障」牌也沒移除,選手後來因此受傷—這是過失(negligence)的教科書例:有注意義務、未履行、可預見地造成傷害。風險自願承擔與主權豁免都對不上。"},{"id":"q0153","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 22-year-old soccer player joins your program. He has competed at a high level for six years, but his intake questionnaire and a movement screen show only about seven weeks of unstructured lifting and poor barbell technique. Using resistance training status to set his starting point, how should you classify him and prescribe initial frequency and training stress?","options":["Advanced; four or more sessions per week at high training stress since he is an elite competitor","Beginner; roughly one to two sessions per week at low training stress while technique is taught","Intermediate; three to four sessions per week at moderate training stress because his years of sport count as training age"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Beginner; roughly one to two sessions per week at low training stress while technique is taught","explanation_en":"Resistance training status reflects weight room experience and lifting skill, not sport experience or competitive level. Under two months of training with minimal skill classifies an athlete as a beginner, who should start with low frequency (about one to two days per week) and low training stress while learning technique.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練狀態取決於重量房經驗與動作技術,不計專項運動年資:無結構訓練約七週、槓鈴技術差,就按初學者處理—每週約 1 到 2 次、低訓練壓力,先建立技術。"},{"id":"q0154","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a muscular strength program, a lifter finishes a heavy multijoint core lift and then moves to lateral shoulder raises loaded at a 12RM. A newer coach wants to give the raises the same rest the core lift received. What rest length actually fits the lateral raise, and on what basis?","options":["At least 5 minutes, because single-joint work still demands full neuromuscular recovery","The same 2 to 5 minutes as the core lift, because the whole session shares one strength goal","About 1 minute, because rest is set by the relative load and muscle mass of that specific exercise, both of which are low here"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 1 minute, because rest is set by the relative load and muscle mass of that specific exercise, both of which are low here","explanation_en":"Rest between sets is assigned by the relative load and amount of muscle mass involved in each exercise, not by the overall program goal. A light single-joint assistance lift such as a 12RM lateral raise needs only about 1 minute of rest even inside a strength program.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"組間休息看該動作本身的相對負荷與動員肌量:12RM 側平舉屬輕負荷單關輔助動作,約 1 分鐘就夠,不必沿用主項深蹲的長休息—訓練目標不直接決定休息長度。"},{"id":"q0155","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A trained athlete's block is centered on maximal strength, and the back squat is the core lift. You want the load and repetition prescription to land squarely in the maximal strength zone rather than drifting toward hypertrophy. Which prescription fits?","options":["At least 85 percent of 1RM for about 6 or fewer repetitions","About 67 to 80 percent of 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions","About 60 to 67 percent of 1RM for 12 to 15 repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"At least 85 percent of 1RM for about 6 or fewer repetitions","explanation_en":"Maximal strength on core exercises is trained with loads of at least 85 percent of 1RM for roughly 6 or fewer repetitions. The moderate-load, higher-rep ranges target hypertrophy and muscular endurance instead.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大肌力區的核心動作處方:≥85% 1RM、目標次數約 6 次以下;67 到 80%×8 到 12 是肥大區,60 到 67%×12 到 15 偏肌耐力。"},{"id":"q0156","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are building a hypertrophy-focused day around multijoint lifts and want each core exercise's load and rep scheme to sit in the middle of the hypertrophy zone, not bleed into the strength or endurance zones. Which prescription fits?","options":["Below 67 percent of 1RM for more than 15 repetitions","About 67 to 80 percent of 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions","About 85 to 90 percent of 1RM for 3 to 5 repetitions"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 67 to 80 percent of 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy is emphasized with moderate loads of roughly 67 to 80 percent of 1RM for about 8 to 12 repetitions, balancing mechanical tension against enough volume. Heavier low-rep work targets strength, and very light high-rep work targets muscular endurance.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練的中間地帶:約 67% 到 80% 1RM、約 8 到 12 次,兼顧機械張力與足夠訓練量;更重更低次偏肌力,極輕高次偏肌耐力。"},{"id":"q0157","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a power block you are programming for a shot putter, whose event is a single explosive effort. You want the load and rep scheme that maximizes power for a single-effort movement. Which prescription is recommended?","options":["About 75 to 85 percent of 1RM for 3 to 5 repetitions performed explosively","30 to 50 percent of 1RM for 10 to 12 repetitions performed explosively","80 to 90 percent of 1RM for 1 to 2 repetitions performed explosively"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"80 to 90 percent of 1RM for 1 to 2 repetitions performed explosively","explanation_en":"Single-effort power events are trained with about 80 to 90 percent of 1RM for 1 to 2 repetitions performed explosively. Multiple-effort power uses a lower load, about 75 to 85 percent of 1RM, for 3 to 5 repetitions.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"單發功率專案(鉛球)建議約 80% 到 90% 1RM、1 到 2 次、每次爆發完成;75% 到 85%×3 到 5 次是多發功率專案的處方。"},{"id":"q0158","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a power phase you load the power clean to 80 percent of 1RM. The athlete clearly could grind out five or six reps, but you cap the set at three. A teammate asks why you are leaving reps 'in the tank.' What is the real reason for stopping short?","options":["To keep bar velocity high so the set trains power instead of degrading into slow, fatiguing grinding reps","To accumulate the most time under tension possible on each set","To ensure the set reaches muscular failure on a heavy compound lift"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"To keep bar velocity high so the set trains power instead of degrading into slow, fatiguing grinding reps","explanation_en":"Power development depends on high movement velocity. The earliest reps at a given load are the fastest, so a power set uses fewer reps than the load would allow in order to keep every rep explosive rather than slow and grinding.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"功率訓練的本質是高速度:同一負荷下最前幾下最快,所以刻意留次(80% 能做五六下卻只做三下),讓每一維持爆發,不讓組末退化成慢速磨蹭—一旦一旦速度掉下來,練的就不是功率了。"},{"id":"q0159","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A cross country runner enters a preseason block whose primary resistance training aim is muscular endurance. You want the core-lift load and rep prescription to match that aim and not slide toward strength or power. Which prescription fits?","options":["85 percent or more of 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions","67 percent or less of 1RM for 12 or more repetitions","75 to 85 percent of 1RM for 3 to 5 repetitions"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"67 percent or less of 1RM for 12 or more repetitions","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance is trained with light loads of 67 percent or less of 1RM for many repetitions, 12 or more per set. The heavier low-rep options correspond to power and strength goals respectively.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌耐力處方:≤67% 1RM、每組 12 次以上;85%+×6- 是肌力區,75 到 85%×3 到 5 是功率區。"},{"id":"q0160","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"To save time, a coach has an athlete perform a set of front squats immediately followed by a set of overhead presses with only brief rest between them, then repeats. A colleague calls this a compound set. What is the method actually called, and what is its main benefit?","options":["Circuit training, whose main benefit is maximizing the metabolic conditioning effect","A compound set, which stacks two exercises for the same muscle group to pre-exhaust it","An alternating (push-pull) arrangement, which lets one region recover while the other works and improves time efficiency"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"An alternating (push-pull) arrangement, which lets one region recover while the other works and improves time efficiency","explanation_en":"Alternating an upper-body and a lower-body exercise with brief rest is a push-pull (alternating muscle-group) arrangement: one region recovers while the other trains, improving time efficiency. It is not a compound set (two exercises for the same muscle group), and a superset specifically pairs opposing agonist and antagonist muscles.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"前蹲與過頭推舉輪流做、中間短休,是交錯肌群式(push-pull)安排:上半身與下半身輪流,一區恢復時另一區在練,時間效率高;compound set 是同一肌群的兩個動作相連,superset 則特指主動肌與其拮抗肌配對。"},{"id":"q0161","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach logs a session of 3 sets of 10 back squats at 100 kg and computes the volume-load. A second coach did full-range squats while this athlete used a shortened partial range, yet both logged the identical numbers. What is the volume-load, and what does this measure fail to capture?","options":["3,000 kg; it fails to capture actual bar displacement, so partial and full-range squats show the same value","1,000 kg; it fails to capture the number of sets performed","30 repetitions; it fails to capture the load that was lifted"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"3,000 kg; it fails to capture actual bar displacement, so partial and full-range squats show the same value","explanation_en":"Volume-load equals sets times reps times weight, so 3 x 10 x 100 kg is 3,000 kg. Because it multiplies only weight by repetitions, it ignores bar displacement (range of motion), so a partial-range and a full-range squat with the same sets, reps, and load produce identical volume-load.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"volume-load=組數×次數×重量=3×10×100=3000 公斤;但它不含槓鈴實際位移,所以半程蹲與全程蹲在相同組次重量下算出同一數字—無法分辨動作品質與行程。"},{"id":"q0162","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are prescribing low-intensity lower-body plyometric drills for a beginner and need to record the session's volume in the appropriate unit. How should lower-body plyometric volume be expressed?","options":["As the number of sets carried to technical failure","As foot contacts per session","As total minutes of jumping per session"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"As foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Lower-body plyometric volume is counted as foot contacts per session, each instance a foot or the feet contact the surface. Bounding drills may instead be quantified by distance covered.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"下肢增強式的訓練量以每次課的腳部觸地數(foot contacts)計,每次單腳或雙腳觸地都算一次;跳躍距離型動作(bounding)可改用距離計。"},{"id":"q0163","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are ordering boxes for depth jumps and box jumps and want a height range that allows a meaningful eccentric stimulus without pushing athletes past the height where landing mechanics break down. Which height range is recommended?","options":["2 to 12 inches (5 to 30 cm)","12 to 60 inches (30 to 152 cm)","6 to 42 inches (15 to 107 cm)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"6 to 42 inches (15 to 107 cm)","explanation_en":"Plyometric boxes should range from 6 to 42 inches (15 to 107 cm), with a nonslip top and a stable base. Heights near the top of this range give a large eccentric overload; going much higher tends to break down landing technique and raise injury risk.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式箱高建議範圍 6 到 42 吋(15 到 107 公分),箱面防滑、底座穩;接近上限的箱子提供大離心超載,再高落地機制容易垮、風險增。"},{"id":"q0164","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is running a circuit-style muscular endurance program with light loads and high repetitions, and you want the between-set rest to reinforce the endurance stimulus rather than allow full recovery. Which rest length fits?","options":["30 seconds or less","2 to 5 minutes","2 to 3 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"30 seconds or less","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance programs use very short rest periods, often 30 seconds or less, to deliberately limit recovery when light loads are lifted for many repetitions. Longer rests correspond to hypertrophy (2 to 3 minutes) and strength or power (2 to 5 minutes).","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌耐力型課表刻意用 30 秒以內的極短休息,不給完全恢復,配合輕負荷高次數強化耐力刺激;2 到 3 分鐘屬肥大,2 到 5 分鐘屬肌力/功率。"},{"id":"q0165","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are setting weekly resistance training frequency for a trained athlete who is currently in the off-season and building a base before the season starts. Based on frequency guidelines by sport season, which weekly range is appropriate?","options":["1 to 3 sessions per week","4 to 6 sessions per week","3 to 4 sessions per week"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"4 to 6 sessions per week","explanation_en":"For a trained athlete, recommended frequency by sport season is 4 to 6 sessions per week in the off-season, 3 to 4 in the preseason, 1 to 3 in-season, and 0 to 3 postseason during active rest. The off-season allows the highest frequency.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"受訓運動員的每週頻率依賽季:休季期 4 到 6 次(最高)、季前 3 到 4 次、季中 1 到 3 次、季後 0 到 3 次主動休息;打底期的休季期允許最高頻率。"},{"id":"q0166","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A distance runner wants to accumulate time near VO2max to raise aerobic power and asks you to program classic interval training specifically (not HIIT). Which combination of intensity, work-bout length, and work-to-rest ratio defines interval training?","options":["Below the lactate threshold, performed continuously for about 30 to 120 minutes","Greater than VO2max, short bouts of about 30 to 90 seconds, roughly a 1:5 work-to-rest ratio","Close to VO2max, work bouts of about 3 to 5 minutes, roughly a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Close to VO2max, work bouts of about 3 to 5 minutes, roughly a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio","explanation_en":"Interval training uses work bouts near VO2max lasting about 3 to 5 minutes at roughly a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio, which lets the athlete accumulate time near VO2max. Greater-than-VO2max short bouts at about 1:5 describe HIIT, and continuous submaximal work describes long slow distance training.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"間歇訓練的定義組合:強度接近 VO2max、每段約 3 到 5 分鐘、工休比約 1:1,藉此累積接近 VO2max 的時間。高於 VO2max 的 30 到 90 秒約 1:5 是 HIIT;低於閾值的連續 30 到 120 分鐘是長慢距離。"},{"id":"q0167","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is deciding between HIIT and standard interval training and needs to explain how HIIT differs on intensity, work duration, and work-to-rest ratio. Which description correctly captures HIIT relative to standard intervals?","options":["HIIT is performed above VO2max with shorter work bouts of about 30 to 90 seconds and roughly a 1:5 work-to-rest ratio","HIIT is performed below VO2max with longer work bouts and about a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio","HIIT uses the same intensity and bout length as interval training but with a much longer relief period"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"HIIT is performed above VO2max with shorter work bouts of about 30 to 90 seconds and roughly a 1:5 work-to-rest ratio","explanation_en":"HIIT uses shorter work bouts of about 30 to 90 seconds at intensities greater than VO2max with a longer relief period, roughly a 1:5 work-to-rest ratio. Standard interval training is near VO2max for about 3 to 5 minutes at roughly 1:1.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"HIIT 與標準間歇的三項差異:強度高於 VO2max、每段縮短為約 30 到 90 秒、休息拉長為約 1:5 的工休比;不是同強度加長休息。"},{"id":"q0168","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach notes that the back squat loads the spine and requires the lifter to keep a rigid torso and neutral spine so posture is stabilized against the load throughout the lift. Within the exercise classification system, which category best fits the back squat on that basis?","options":["A single-joint assistance exercise","A structural exercise","A power exercise, because any barbell squat is defined by explosive intent"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A structural exercise","explanation_en":"A core exercise that loads the spine directly or indirectly and requires muscular stabilization of posture during the lift is classified as a structural exercise. A structural exercise performed very quickly or explosively is further classified as a power exercise, but a standard back squat is simply structural.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"直接間接負荷脊椎、需要肌群穩定姿勢的 core 動作歸類為結構性動作(structural exercise);結構性動作以極快速度完成才再歸為功率動作,一般深蹲就只是結構性動作。"},{"id":"q0169","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sprint coach is contrasting the low, forward-leaning drive an athlete uses coming out of the blocks with the tall, upright running he does once he has reached full speed. These two portions of the sprint are best labeled as which phases?","options":["The braking phase and the recovery phase","The amortization phase and the concentric phase","The acceleration phase and the maximal-velocity phase"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The acceleration phase and the maximal-velocity phase","explanation_en":"Sprinting requires the ability to accelerate and then reach maximal velocity. The acceleration phase (drive out of the blocks) and the maximal-velocity phase (upright top-end running) use different body positions and produce vertical and horizontal ground reaction forces of differing magnitude.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"出起跑器的低姿前傾驅動屬加速階段(acceleration phase),達速後直立高姿勢的頂速跑屬最大速度階段(maximal-velocity phase);兩階段的姿態與地面反力垂直/水平比例不同。"},{"id":"q0170","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are outlining the preparatory (off-season) period for a traditionally periodized athlete and need to describe its characteristic training emphasis. Which combination correctly characterizes that period?","options":["Low to moderate intensity with high volume, emphasizing hypertrophy and strength endurance","Moderate intensity with sport-specific technique and tactics as the primary focus","High intensity with very low volume and peaking work as the main emphasis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Low to moderate intensity with high volume, emphasizing hypertrophy and strength endurance","explanation_en":"The preparatory/off-season period uses high volume at lower intensity to build a base, hypertrophy, and strength endurance, with a low technical and tactical emphasis. Intensity rises and volume falls as competition approaches.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統週期化的準備期(休季期)特色:低到中強度、高訓練量,重點是建立體適能基礎、肥大與肌力耐力,技術戰術比重低;越接近比賽強度遞增、量遞減。"},{"id":"q0171","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A team-sport athlete faces a competitive period spanning several months, and the goal is to retain strength and power while managing the fatigue of frequent competition. How is a maintenance program for such a prolonged competitive period generally characterized?","options":["Maximal volume and maximal intensity held constant every week to prevent detraining","Moderate to high intensity of about 85 to 93 percent of 1RM at low to moderate volume","High volume at low intensity below 60 percent of 1RM to minimize joint stress"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Moderate to high intensity of about 85 to 93 percent of 1RM at low to moderate volume","explanation_en":"During a prolonged competitive period, a maintenance program is marked by moderate to high intensity, about 85 to 93 percent of 1RM, at low to moderate volume, with loads modulated microcycle to microcycle around the competition schedule.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"跨越數月的賽季維持期課表:約 85% 到 93% 1RM 的中高強度搭配低到中訓練量,並依賽程逐微週期調整負荷—用強度守住肌力功率,用量的削減控制疲勞。"},{"id":"q0172","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach tapers an athlete before a competition and observes performance rise above baseline in the days that follow. Using the fitness-fatigue paradigm, how is preparedness best described, and why does the taper work?","options":["Preparedness is the sum of fitness and fatigue, which rise together and remain permanently elevated after training","Preparedness is the fatigue component alone, so reducing load simply removes fatigue while fitness stays fixed","Preparedness is the fitness component minus the fatigue component; because fatigue dissipates faster than fitness, reducing load lets preparedness rise"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Preparedness is the fitness component minus the fatigue component; because fatigue dissipates faster than fitness, reducing load lets preparedness rise","explanation_en":"Each training bout produces both fitness and fatigue, and preparedness is their net effect (fitness minus fatigue). Because fatigue dissipates faster than fitness, reducing the training load during a taper lets preparedness climb above baseline.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"體適能—疲勞模型:每次訓練同時產生 fitness 與 fatigue 兩種成分,準備度(preparedness)=fitness 減 fatigue;fatigue 消退速度快於 fitness,減量期降低負荷讓準備度淨值上升,這正是 taper 能超水平的原理。"},{"id":"q0173","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to make an athlete faster and is deciding what to target in training. Sprint speed is the product of which two variables, and what primarily drives improvement in both?","options":["Stride length and stride rate (frequency), improved mainly by applying greater force during the brief ground-contact time","Reaction time and flexibility, improved mainly through static stretching","Body mass and limb length, improved mainly by adding external load"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Stride length and stride rate (frequency), improved mainly by applying greater force during the brief ground-contact time","explanation_en":"Sprint speed equals stride length times stride frequency. Faster sprinters direct larger forces into the ground during a brief stance phase, which lengthens the stride while a high stride rate is maintained.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"衝刺速度=步幅×步頻;提升兩者主要靠短暫接地期內對地施加更大的力量—頂尖衝刺者用更短的支撐時間輸出更大的豎直力,步幅加大同時步頻維持高檔。"},{"id":"q0174","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Setting up for a heavy deadlift, a lifter positions one hand so the palm faces the body and the other so the palm faces away, specifically to stop the bar from rolling out of the hands as the load gets heavy. Which grip is being used?","options":["A neutral grip","An alternated grip","A supinated grip"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"An alternated grip","explanation_en":"An alternated grip places one hand pronated (palm facing away) and the other supinated (palm facing the body). It is commonly used on heavy pulling movements such as the deadlift to keep the bar from rolling and improve grip security.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一手朝前(palm away)、一手朝後(palm toward body)的握法是交錯握(alternated grip),大重量硬拉常用它防止槓鈴從手中滾脫,提高握持安全。"},{"id":"q0175","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Working through a RAMP warm-up, a coach reaches the final segment right before performance and uses specific, increasingly intense movements at competition intensity to exploit a postactivation potentiation effect. Which RAMP phase is this?","options":["Activate and Mobilize","Raise","Potentiate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Potentiate","explanation_en":"The Potentiate phase uses specific, progressively more intense movements to bring activity up to competition intensity and take advantage of postactivation potentiation right before the main activity. Raise elevates body temperature and heart rate early, and Activate and Mobilize targets key muscles and ranges of motion in between.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RAMP 的最後階段 Potentiate:賽前用專項、強度漸升到比賽水準的動作,利用參與活動後增強(postactivation potentiation)把身體推到出發狀態;Raise 是最初段的升溫升心率。"},{"id":"q0176","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete asks whether adding a block of static stretching to the pre-competition warm-up will help him jump and sprint better. How is the current evidence on static stretching in a warm-up best summarized with respect to subsequent performance?","options":["It is equivocal, and several reviews suggest it can compromise force and power performance","It reliably improves force and power output when done before performance","It has been shown to have no measurable effect on any performance variable"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It is equivocal, and several reviews suggest it can compromise force and power performance","explanation_en":"The literature on static stretching in warm-ups is equivocal, and a number of reviews report negative effects on force production and power. That is why dynamic warm-ups are generally favored before performance.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"賽前熱身加入靜態伸展的證據並不一致(equivocal),多篇綜述甚至報告它會損傷後續的力量與功率輸出;所以表現前普遍建議以動態熱身為主。"},{"id":"q0177","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is explaining how to execute the concentric phase of a power clean and, separately, what training through a full range of motion does to flexibility. Which statement is correct on both counts?","options":["Flexibility is unaffected by full-ROM training, and the concentric phase of an explosive lift should follow a fixed 3-second tempo","Flexibility is maintained or improved through full-ROM training, and the concentric phase of an explosive lift should be accelerated to maximal speed while keeping control and form","Flexibility decreases with full-ROM training, so the concentric phase of an explosive lift should be slowed deliberately to protect the joint"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Flexibility is maintained or improved through full-ROM training, and the concentric phase of an explosive lift should be accelerated to maximal speed while keeping control and form","explanation_en":"Training through a full range of motion maintains or even improves flexibility. For explosive movements such as the power clean, the bar should be accelerated to maximal speed during the concentric phase while control and proper form are maintained.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩件事都要對:以完整活動度訓練能維持甚至改善柔軟度;爆發動作的向心期應把槓鈴加速到最大速度、同時守住控制與姿勢。爆發舉還固定 3 秒節拍是錯誤觀念。"},{"id":"q0178","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Checking a lifter's hand placement on the bar, you see the thumb resting alongside the fingers on the same side of the bar rather than wrapped around it. You correct it to a closed grip. Why is wrapping the thumb around the bar preferred over that open or false grip?","options":["It is only necessary for supinated grips and can be skipped on pronated grips","It increases the range of motion available at the wrist during the lift","It keeps the bar from slipping out of the hands, improving control and safety"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It keeps the bar from slipping out of the hands, improving control and safety","explanation_en":"In a closed grip the thumb is wrapped around the bar, securing it in the hand. In an open or false grip the thumb sits alongside the fingers, which allows the bar to slip out more easily and is less safe, regardless of whether the grip is pronated or supinated.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"閉合握(closed grip)讓拇指環繞槓桿、把槓鎖在手中;開放握(false grip)拇指與四指同側,槓更容易滑脫、安全性較差,與正握反握無關。"},{"id":"q0179","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are spotting an athlete doing heavy dumbbell chest presses. During the last rep her elbows begin to buckle and the dumbbells drift toward her face and chest. To have the best chance of stopping the weights before they strike her, where should your hands already be positioned?","options":["At her wrists or on the forearms just below the wrists","At the elbows, so you can push the upper arms back up as they bend","Under the dumbbells themselves, cupping the plates from below"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"At her wrists or on the forearms just below the wrists","explanation_en":"Dumbbells are spotted at the forearms near the wrists, closest to the load, so the spotter can actually arrest the weights. Spotting at the elbows leaves the spotter unable to stop the dumbbells from continuing toward the athlete once the elbows collapse.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"啞鈴臥推的保護位置在選手的腕部或腕下前臂—最靠近負重、才真的擋得住;保護在手肘,肘一軟啞鈴仍會繼續朝臉與胸口掉。"},{"id":"q0180","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A beginner is setting up for a standard barbell exercise and asks you how far apart to place the hands as a starting default. Absent a specific reason to go wider or narrower, what should you tell him?","options":["As wide as he can comfortably reach to increase leverage","Roughly shoulder-width apart","Hands touching in the center of the bar for maximum control"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Roughly shoulder-width apart","explanation_en":"Grip widths are described as common, wide, and narrow, but the common default for most exercises places the hands approximately shoulder-width apart to keep the load balanced on the bar. Widest-possible or hands-together grips are special cases, not the default.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"沒有特殊理由時,初學者的預設握距約與肩同寬(common grip),讓負重在槓上保持平衡;極寬或併攏都是特定動作的特例。"},{"id":"q0181","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a training session an athlete asks you to stand behind him and 'catch' the bar on his power cleans the same way you would guide the bar back to the rack on a failed bench press. How should you respond?","options":["Position two spotters, one at each end of the bar, to share the load","Agree and prepare to catch, since any lift performed with heavy weight must be spotted","Decline, because explosive lifts are not spotted; the safer approach is coaching him to miss or dump the bar cleanly"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Decline, because explosive lifts are not spotted; the safer approach is coaching him to miss or dump the bar cleanly","explanation_en":"Because of the speed of the movement, explosive lifts such as the power clean are not spotted; a spotter cannot safely intervene and would be endangered. Instead the athlete is taught to miss the lift by dropping or pushing the bar away safely.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"爆發性動作(power clean)不保護:動作速度快,保護者難以安全介入、自己也有風險;正解是教他把失敗變成安全的掉槓/推槓向前。"},{"id":"q0182","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A single competent spotter can comfortably handle the weight on an athlete's incline press. A newer staff member suggests adding a second and third spotter 'to be safe.' Why is using just the one capable spotter generally the better choice here?","options":["Every added spotter is one more person who must sync timing with the lifter and the others, raising the odds of a coordination error","Facility standards prohibit using more than one spotter on any lift","A lone spotter can generate more rescue force than several spotters combined"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Every added spotter is one more person who must sync timing with the lifter and the others, raising the odds of a coordination error","explanation_en":"When one spotter can handle the load, one is preferred: each additional spotter has to coordinate with the lifter and every other spotter, and each added person increases the chance of a timing or technique error. Multiple spotters are reserved for loads a single person cannot manage.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一名有能力的保護者足以應付時就用一人:每多一人就多一道與選手及其他保護者的同步協調,失誤機率隨人數上升;多人保護只留給一人扛不動的重量。"},{"id":"q0183","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are correcting an athlete's stance before a set of standing overhead presses done free of any rack or support. Which foot setup gives the most stable base for this ground-based standing lift?","options":["A very wide stance with the weight shifted back onto the heels","Feet slightly wider than hip width, with both the heels and the balls of the feet pressing into the floor","Feet close together directly beneath the hips to stack the joints"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Feet slightly wider than hip width, with both the heels and the balls of the feet pressing into the floor","explanation_en":"Standing free-weight exercises call for the feet slightly wider than hip width with both the heels and the balls of the feet in contact with the floor, creating a stable base. A narrow stance or loading only the heels undermines that base.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"站立姿無支撐的自由重量過頭推:雙腳略寬於髖寬,腳跟與前腳掌都壓實地面,構成穩定的支撐面;太狹窄或重心全壓腳跟都會破壞穩定。"},{"id":"q0184","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An experienced lifter with clean squat mechanics plateaus at lockout. You decide to hang chains from the bar for his back squats. What effect are you counting on, and why does his training background matter here?","options":["The chains make the bottom heaviest and the top lightest, which makes them ideal for teaching brand-new beginners","The chains keep resistance constant through the range, so any lifter's experience level is irrelevant","The chains load the top of the squat, where he is strongest, and unload the bottom; the added instability means this suits a lifter who already has solid technique"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The chains load the top of the squat, where he is strongest, and unload the bottom; the added instability means this suits a lifter who already has solid technique","explanation_en":"Chains add resistance near the top of the lift, where leverage and strength are greatest, and unload the bottom, helping match the load to the strength curve. Because the swinging implements add instability, they are appropriate for athletes who already have solid technique.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鐵鏈是accommodating resistance:蹲到底鏈條堆在地上最輕、鎖定位(原本最強處)鏈條全離地最重,讓負荷曲線貼合力量曲線;擺動的器械帶來額外不穩定,所以技術已穩的老手才適合,不適合新手。"},{"id":"q0185","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to strengthen an athlete's midsection and assumes only dedicated isolation core drills like crunches will do it. Compared with those isolation drills, how do ground-based lifts such as squats and deadlifts affect the anatomical core?","options":["They tend to activate the core to a similar or greater degree while training it to stiffen and transmit force through the kinetic chain","They bypass the core almost entirely because the trunk stays rigid throughout","They recruit the core less than isolation work because the bracing limits trunk motion"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"They tend to activate the core to a similar or greater degree while training it to stiffen and transmit force through the kinetic chain","explanation_en":"Ground-based free-weight lifts activate the core similarly to or more than isolation exercises, and they train the core to stiffen and transfer force through the kinetic chain in a more sport-relevant way than isolation drills do.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究顯示地面自由重量動作(深蹲、硬拉)對解剖學核心(軀幹)的活化等同或高於仰臥起坐這類孤立動作,而且是訓練軀幹剛性化、沿動力鏈傳遞力量,更接近專項需求;說它繞過核心是錯的。"},{"id":"q0186","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete asks you to program his heavy squats and cleans on a wobble board and stability ball to 'build more power.' Based on how unstable surfaces affect force production, how should you advise him?","options":["It raises force output and is therefore ideal for peak power development","Unstable-surface work tends to reduce force output, so it fits rehab and prehab better than maximizing strength and power","It leaves force output unchanged, so it can simply replace conventional free-weight training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Unstable-surface work tends to reduce force output, so it fits rehab and prehab better than maximizing strength and power","explanation_en":"The nervous system limits force output when the base is unstable, so training on unstable surfaces can markedly lower the force produced. That makes it useful for rehabilitation and prehab but poorly suited to maximizing strength and power.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"不穩定平面(平衡板、穩定球)上神經系統會限制力量輸出,實際產力明顯下降;它適合復健與預防傷患,不適合用來最大化力量與功率,也不能取代傳統自由重量訓練。"},{"id":"q0187","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach measures an athlete's vertical jump on Monday and again on Thursday under identical conditions, then examines how closely the two sets of scores agree. Any gap between them is treated as measurement error. Which quality of the test is she evaluating?","options":["How thoroughly the test covers the components of the ability being measured","How well the test predicts a future performance outcome","How consistently the test reproduces the same score across repeated administrations"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"How consistently the test reproduces the same score across repeated administrations","explanation_en":"Administering the same test twice under identical conditions and comparing the scores evaluates test-retest reliability, the consistency or repeatability of the measure. The difference between the two sets of scores represents measurement error. Predictive coverage and content coverage are forms of validity, not reliability.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"相同條件下重複施測同一測驗、比較兩次分數的一致性,評估的是重測信度(test-retest reliability);兩組分數的差距即測量誤差。涵蓋面向與預測未來是效度範疇。"},{"id":"q0188","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach builds an 'agility' test as a fully pre-planned course: athletes memorize every cut ahead of time and never have to react to a stimulus. A panel of experts concludes it fails to measure agility as the sport actually demands it. Which quality is most directly missing?","options":["The extent to which the test covers the defining components of the ability measured","The degree to which different testers would score it the same way","The consistency of the score when the test is repeated"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The extent to which the test covers the defining components of the ability measured","explanation_en":"Content validity is the expert judgment that a test covers the relevant components of the quality being measured. An 'agility' test with no perceptual-cognitive or reactive component omits a defining part of agility, so content validity is what it lacks. Scorer agreement and repeatability are separate qualities.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"把敏捷測驗做成背路線的預設動線、抽掉反應刺激,專家認定它沒測到敏捷的本質成分—缺的是內容效度(content validity):測驗是否涵蓋該能力的定義性構成。"},{"id":"q0189","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Before adopting a new fitness battery, a program director convenes sport experts to judge whether the tests collectively cover every relevant physical ability the sport requires, and in the right proportions. Which quality are the experts establishing?","options":["Whether the tests simply appear relevant to the athletes at first glance","The extent to which the battery samples all relevant component abilities in appropriate proportions","The degree to which battery scores correlate with an already-accepted test of the same abilities"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The extent to which the battery samples all relevant component abilities in appropriate proportions","explanation_en":"Content validity is the experts' assessment that testing covers all relevant subtopics or component abilities in appropriate proportions, which for sport means every ability the sport demands. Correlating with an accepted test is concurrent validity, and surface plausibility is face validity.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"召集專家判斷測驗組合是否涵蓋專項所需的全部身體能力且比例得當,建立的是內容效度;與既有公認測驗求相關是同時效度,只有「看起來像樣」則叫表面效度。"},{"id":"q0190","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are running an athlete through progressively heavier attempts to find her 1RM back squat. She just completed a submaximal warm-up attempt and is a couple of loads away from her likely max. How much rest is recommended before this next non-maximal attempt versus before an attempt that is close to her maximum?","options":["At least 5 minutes before non-maximal attempts and about 10 minutes before near-maximal attempts","About 30 seconds before non-maximal attempts and roughly 1 minute before near-maximal attempts","At least 2 minutes before non-maximal attempts and 3 minutes before near-maximal attempts"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"At least 2 minutes before non-maximal attempts and 3 minutes before near-maximal attempts","explanation_en":"For multiple-trial 1RM testing, allow at least 2 minutes of rest between attempts that are not close to the maximum and at least 3 minutes between attempts that are near the maximum. Shorter rests leave residual fatigue; much longer rests are not what the protocol specifies.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多次嘗試法的 1RM 流程:非極限嘗試前休息至少 2 分鐘,接近極限的嘗試前至少 3 分鐘,讓每次嘗試都在充分恢復下進行。"},{"id":"q0191","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A testing session pairs a maximal test of the phosphagen system with a maximal test of the anaerobic glycolytic system. To keep fatigue from one from contaminating the other, how much recovery does each respectively require?","options":["About 3 to 5 minutes after the phosphagen test and at least 1 hour after the anaerobic glycolytic test","About 1 hour after the phosphagen test and about 3 minutes after the anaerobic glycolytic test","About 30 seconds after each is enough because both are short in duration"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 3 to 5 minutes after the phosphagen test and at least 1 hour after the anaerobic glycolytic test","explanation_en":"A maximal phosphagen-system test needs roughly 3 to 5 minutes for full recovery, whereas a maximal anaerobic glycolytic test needs at least 1 hour. The glycolytic test's long recovery is why it should be sequenced so it does not fatigue later tests.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統的最大強度測驗約需 3 到 5 分鐘完全恢復;無氧糖解系統的最大測驗則需要至少 1 小時—糖解測驗因此要排在後段,避免它的長恢復期汙染後續測驗。"},{"id":"q0192","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athletic trainer is managing an athlete's acute ankle sprain in the first day or two and wants an approach that reflects the current move away from the older PRICE model, which the field revised because strict rest was not producing the best outcomes. Which strategy fits that updated thinking?","options":["Applying heat and deep tissue massage to the area on the first day","POLICE: protection, optimal loading, ice, compression, and elevation","Strict immobilization of the joint for no less than two weeks"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"POLICE: protection, optimal loading, ice, compression, and elevation","explanation_en":"The evidence-based shift replaced the 'rest' of PRICE (protection, rest, ice, compression, elevation) with 'optimal loading' in POLICE, because controlled early loading rather than complete rest tends to yield better outcomes and faster recovery. Prolonged immobilization and early heat/massage run counter to this.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"急性軟組織處理已用 POLICE 取代 PRICE:把 Rest 換成 optimal loading(最適負荷),早期控制下的負荷比完全休息結果更好、恢復更快;第一天熱敷深層按摩與嚴格固定兩週都與此相悖。"},{"id":"q0193","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete tears a muscle acutely and reports pain, swelling, and redness at the site. During roughly what window does this initial healing phase last, and which physiological change is characteristic of it?","options":["Roughly six months, characterized by full return of the tissue's original strength","Roughly two months, characterized by realignment of collagen and rising tissue strength","Roughly the first 72 hours, characterized by increased inflammatory cells and decreased collagen synthesis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Roughly the first 72 hours, characterized by increased inflammatory cells and decreased collagen synthesis","explanation_en":"The inflammatory response phase typically lasts about 72 hours and is marked by pain, swelling, redness, an influx of inflammatory cells, and decreased collagen synthesis. Collagen realignment and rising strength belong to the later repair and remodeling phases, which unfold over weeks to months.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"發炎反應期持續約 72 小時:疼痛、腫脹、發紅、發炎細胞增加、膠原蛋白合成下降;膠原蛋白重新排列與強度回升屬於其後的修復與重塑期,以週到月計。"},{"id":"q0194","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are guiding an athlete through the early healing phase after a medial collateral ligament (MCL) sprain of the knee. Knowing which loading direction most directly stresses that ligament, which type of movement should you avoid for now?","options":["Frontal-plane, valgus-loading movement such as a lateral box jump or side shuffle","Closed-chain sagittal loading such as a leg press","Straight-ahead sagittal-plane movement such as an easy jog"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Frontal-plane, valgus-loading movement such as a lateral box jump or side shuffle","explanation_en":"The MCL resists valgus (frontal-plane) stress at the knee, so frontal-plane movements like lateral box jumps and side shuffles load the injured ligament most and are avoided in early healing, then reintroduced in later phases. Straight-ahead jogging and leg pressing do not impose the same valgus stress.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"內側副韌帶(MCL)負責抵抗膝外翻應力,所以冠狀面的 valgus 負荷動作—側向跳箱、側滑步—會直接拉扯受傷韌帶,早期癒合階段先避開;直線慢跑與腿推機不產生這種應力,後期再逐步匯入。"},{"id":"q0195","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A preseason camp deliberately overloads training volume for a couple of weeks. Performance dips briefly, then rebounds above baseline once athletes recover within days to a few weeks. How is this planned response best classified relative to a more severe state that would take weeks to months to resolve?","options":["Ordinary acute fatigue that bears no relationship to the overtraining continuum","Functional overreaching, in contrast to nonfunctional overreaching","Overtraining syndrome, in contrast to functional overreaching"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Functional overreaching, in contrast to nonfunctional overreaching","explanation_en":"Functional overreaching is intentionally programmed: a short-term performance decrement is followed by recovery within days to weeks and a supercompensation rebound. Nonfunctional overreaching is more severe and takes longer to resolve, and overtraining syndrome involves long-term impairment lasting weeks to months or more.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":" preseason 刻意超載兩週、成績短暫下滑、數天到數週恢復後反彈超過基線—典型功能性過度負荷;非功能性過度負荷較嚴重、恢復較久,過度訓練症候群則拖數週到數月以上。"},{"id":"q0196","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two athletes are diagnosed with different forms of overtraining syndrome: a powerlifter whose case traces to chronically high training intensity, and a marathoner whose case traces to accumulated high volume. Which mapping of these forms is correct?","options":["Both cases are the same condition, since the sympathetic and parasympathetic labels are interchangeable","The powerlifter has volume-driven parasympathetic overtraining; the marathoner has intensity-driven sympathetic overtraining","The powerlifter has intensity-driven sympathetic overtraining; the marathoner has volume-driven parasympathetic overtraining"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The powerlifter has intensity-driven sympathetic overtraining; the marathoner has volume-driven parasympathetic overtraining","explanation_en":"Sympathetic overtraining is intensity-driven and more typical of strength and power athletes, whereas parasympathetic overtraining is volume-driven and more typical of endurance athletes who accumulate large training volumes. The two forms are distinct, not interchangeable.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"交感神經過度訓練由高強度驅動,較常見於力量/功率選手(舉重選手);副交感神經過度訓練由高訓練量驅動,較常見於耐力選手(馬拉松)。兩種型態各有成因,不能互換標籤。"},{"id":"q0197","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are advising on HVAC setpoints for a new weight room and want athletes comfortable enough to train at a high quality. Which range should you target as the optimal training temperature?","options":["68 to 74 degrees F (20 to 23 degrees C)","58 to 64 degrees F (14 to 18 degrees C)","78 to 84 degrees F (26 to 29 degrees C)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"68 to 74 degrees F (20 to 23 degrees C)","explanation_en":"An appropriate weight-room range is about 68 to 78 degrees F, with an optimal target near 68 to 74 degrees F (20 to 23 degrees C). A room that is too cold or too hot degrades training quality, so both the low-50s/60s and high-70s/80s ranges are outside the recommendation.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"重量房的合適溫度約 68 到 78°F,最佳目標 68 到 74°F(20 到 23°C);太冷或太熱都直接拉低訓練品質,50 多 60 多與 78 度以上都偏離建議。"},{"id":"q0198","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A facility manager is installing wall mirrors along the dumbbell area and wants to keep dropped or rolling weights from striking and shattering them. What is the recommended minimum height for the bottom edge of the mirrors above the floor?","options":["At least 48 inches (122 cm) above the floor","At least 20 inches (51 cm) above the floor","At least 6 inches (15 cm) above the floor"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At least 20 inches (51 cm) above the floor","explanation_en":"Mirrors should sit a minimum of 20 inches (51 cm) above the floor so dropped or rolling weights are less likely to strike and shatter them. The 6-inch figure is the separate recommendation for clearance between a mirror and adjacent equipment, not its height off the floor.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鏡面下緣應離地至少 20 吋(51 公分),避免掉落或滾動的重量撞碎鏡面;鏡與相鄰器械之間另留 6 吋,是另一條規定,不是離地高度。"},{"id":"q0199","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A facility will train athletes for weightlifting competition and needs regulation lifting platforms. Consistent with competition rules, how should each platform be constructed?","options":["As an all-foam matted surface for maximum cushioning","As a single wooden surface across the entire platform","With a wooden middle section and rubber outer sections"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"With a wooden middle section and rubber outer sections","explanation_en":"In line with weightlifting competition rules, platforms have a wooden middle section where the lifter stands and rubber outer sections. Inlaid platforms are also preferred over raised ones because they remove a tripping hazard. An all-wood or all-foam surface does not meet the standard.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"舉重 platforms 依比賽規格:中央站立區為木面、外圈為橡膠面,並建議嵌入式而非架高式,移除絆倒風險;全木或全泡綿都不符標準。"},{"id":"q0200","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You are laying out a resistance-training area with racks, barbells, and dumbbells and need enough room for both the athlete and a spotter to move safely around each station. What is the minimum recommended spacing between pieces of equipment?","options":["3 feet (0.9 m) between each piece","7 feet (2.1 m) between each piece","1 foot (0.3 m) between each piece"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"3 feet (0.9 m) between each piece","explanation_en":"Racks, barbells, and dumbbells should have at least 3 feet (0.9 m) of space between them so the athlete and spotter can move safely, with additional clearance where multiple spotters are used. One foot is too tight, and 7 feet exceeds the stated minimum.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"器械之間(架、槓鈴、啞鈴存放區)至少留 3 英尺(0.9 公尺),讓選手與保護者能安全走位;使用多名保護者的動作要留更寬,7 英尺則超過最低要求。"},{"id":"q0201","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While setting environmental controls for a strength and conditioning facility, you want to hold humidity low enough to limit microbial growth and equipment rust in areas where athletes are active. What upper limit should relative humidity not exceed?","options":["It should never drop below 75%","It should not exceed 60%","It should be maintained at exactly 90%"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It should not exceed 60%","explanation_en":"In any space where physical activity occurs, relative humidity should not exceed 60%. Staying below that level limits bacterial and microbial growth and reduces rust and equipment damage; holding it at 90% or above, or forcing it to stay above 75%, would worsen those problems.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"任何身體活動空間的相對濕度應不超過 60%;維持在此以下能抑制細菌微生物滋生、減輕器械生鏽。長期 90% 會把問題放大。"},{"id":"q0202","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An injured athlete sues a strength and conditioning professional, alleging negligence. For the claim to succeed, the plaintiff must prove four specific elements by a preponderance of the evidence. Which set lists those four elements?","options":["Liability, insurance coverage, a signed waiver, and proximate cause","Intent, malice, damages, and consent","Duty, breach of that duty, causation, and damages"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Duty, breach of that duty, causation, and damages","explanation_en":"Negligence is a tort with four elements: a duty owed, a breach of that duty, causation linking the breach to the harm, and damages, each proven by a preponderance of the evidence. Intent and malice belong to other torts; liability, insurance, and waivers are not the elements themselves.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成立過失侵權的四要件:注意義務(duty)、違反義務(breach)、義務違反與傷害間的因果關係(causation)、以及損害(damages);每一項都須以優勢證據證明。"},{"id":"q0203","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete signed an assumption-of-risk waiver before starting a program. He is later hurt in a way that a court finds was caused by the strength and conditioning professional's negligence. What protection does the signed waiver actually provide in that situation?","options":["It may fail to shield the professional from liability, because the injury was caused by negligence","It fully bars any liability, no matter how the professional acted","It shifts all liability onto the supervising athletic trainer"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It may fail to shield the professional from liability, because the injury was caused by negligence","explanation_en":"An assumption-of-risk waiver acknowledges the inherent risks of an activity, but it may not protect the professional when the injury results from negligence. Waivers do not excuse negligent conduct, and they do not transfer that liability to a third party.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"自願承擔風險(agreement of risk/waiver)確認的是活動的內在風險;當傷害源自專業人員的過失時,簽了字也可能無法豁免責任—waiver 不原諒疏忽,也不把責任轉給第三方。"},{"id":"q0204","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A high school athlete returning from a concussion asks his strength coach to sign off that he is medically cleared to resume contact practice. Under the NSCA's defined scope of practice for the strength and conditioning professional, what is the appropriate action?","options":["Issue the clearance himself so the athlete does not miss training time","Recognize that clearance is outside his expertise and refer the athlete to the appropriate professional","Leave the decision entirely to the athlete's own judgment"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recognize that clearance is outside his expertise and refer the athlete to the appropriate professional","explanation_en":"The scope of practice requires the strength and conditioning professional to recognize the boundaries of his expertise and to consult with or refer to the appropriate professional, such as a physician, for matters like medical clearance. Providing clearance personally, or deferring to the athlete, falls outside that scope.","tags":["Practical and Applied - Exam Two"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"NSCA 執業範圍要求教練認清專業界線:腦震盪後復出的醫療放行屬醫師等適當專業的決定,教練的正確動作是轉介與配合,不是自己簽名放行,也不是全交給選手自行判斷。"},{"id":"q0205","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In the 5th-edition fiber-type classification, which fiber type is described as red, with high myoglobin content?","options":["Type IIx (fast-twitch glycolytic)","Type I (slow-twitch oxidative)","Type IIa, but never Type I"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Type I (slow-twitch oxidative)","explanation_en":"Type I (slow) fibers are RED because of high myoglobin and dense capillaries; Type IIx are white (low myoglobin) and Type IIa are intermediate (white/red). A common mnemonic error is to flip this and call slow fibers 'white.'","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第 5 版纖維分類中,第一型(慢縮氧化型)纖維因肌紅蛋白含量高、微血管密度高而呈紅色;第二型 x 型為白色(肌紅蛋白低),第二 a 型為中間色(紅/白)。把慢縮纖維說成「白色」是常見的錯誤。"},{"id":"q0206","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The complete oxidation of one molecule of blood glucose yields a NET of how many ATP?","options":["38 ATP","32 ATP","4 ATP"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"32 ATP","explanation_en":"Using current P/O ratios (NADH = 2.5 ATP, FADH2 = 1.5 ATP) the 5th edition lists ~32 ATP net from blood glucose (and 34 from muscle glycogen). The older figure of 38 used the outdated NADH = 3 convention.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"以現行 P/O 比值(NADH=2.5 ATP、FADH2=1.5 ATP),一分子血糖完全氧化淨得約 32 個 ATP(第 5 版);舊教材的 38 來自 NADH=3 的過時換算。"},{"id":"q0207","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolysis that begins with muscle glycogen nets more ATP than glycolysis beginning with blood glucose because:","options":["Glycogen contains more carbon per molecule","Free glucose must be phosphorylated by hexokinase at the cost of 1 ATP, whereas glycogen-derived glucose is already phosphorylated","Glycogen bypasses the electron transport chain"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Free glucose must be phosphorylated by hexokinase at the cost of 1 ATP, whereas glycogen-derived glucose is already phosphorylated","explanation_en":"Trapping free blood glucose in the cell costs an ATP (hexokinase step). Glycogen-derived glucose is already phosphorylated, so the 5th edition lists 34 ATP from glycogen vs 32 from blood glucose.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"遊離血糖進細胞時要由己糖激酶消耗 1 個 ATP 磷酸化;糖原來源的葡萄糖已帶磷酸,省下這一步,所以第 5 版列糖原起算淨得 34 ATP、血糖起算 32。"},{"id":"q0208","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At the very onset of all-out exercise, which energy system predominates?","options":["Oxidative (aerobic) system","Phosphagen (ATP-PCr) system","Fast glycolysis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Phosphagen (ATP-PCr) system","explanation_en":"The phosphagen system is highly active at the start of ALL exercise regardless of intensity because it resynthesizes ATP fastest (creatine kinase). It has the lowest capacity, so it dominates only the first few seconds.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"任何強度運動的初始瞬間都由磷酸原系統(ATP-PCr)主導:肌酸激酶反應的 ATP 再合成速率最快,但容量最低,所以只主宰最初的幾秒。"},{"id":"q0209","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Per the sliding-filament theory, which regions of the sarcomere get SMALLER during contraction?","options":["The A-band only","The H-zone and the I-band","Only the A-band, while sarcomere length is unchanged"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The H-zone and the I-band","explanation_en":"As actin slides toward the center, the H-zone and I-band shorten while the A-band (myosin filament length) stays constant. The whole sarcomere shortens.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌絲滑行時動作蛋白向中央滑入:H 帶與 I 帶變短,A 帶(肌球蛋白絲長度)不變,整個肌節縮短。說 A 帶縮短違反滑行理論。"},{"id":"q0210","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Calcium binding to which protein exposes the myosin-binding sites on actin?","options":["Tropomyosin","Troponin","Titin"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Troponin","explanation_en":"Ca2+ binds troponin, which pulls tropomyosin off the active sites so myosin crossbridges can attach. Tropomyosin is the 'door' covering the sites when calcium is low.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鈣離子結合的是肌鈣蛋白(troponin),引起構型改變、把原肌球蛋白(tropomyosin)從結合位上拉開,橫橋才能附著。原肌球蛋白是低鈣時蓋住位點的「門」,鈣不直接結合它。"},{"id":"q0211","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Most human limb movements, such as the elbow flexion of a biceps curl, operate with which lever type?","options":["First-class lever, at mechanical advantage","Third-class lever, at mechanical disadvantage","Second-class lever, at mechanical advantage"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Third-class lever, at mechanical disadvantage","explanation_en":"Third-class levers (muscle force applied between the fulcrum and the resistance) are most common in the body and work at a mechanical disadvantage - the muscle produces more force than the load, trading force for speed and range of motion.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"人體四肢動作(如彎舉的肘屈曲)絕大多數是第三類槓桿:力點在中間,機械劣勢(優勢小於 1)—肌肉輸出的力大於負荷,換取的是速度與活動度。"},{"id":"q0212","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The maximal force a muscle can exert is most directly proportional to its:","options":["Volume","Cross-sectional area","Resting length"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Cross-sectional area","explanation_en":"Maximal contractile force is proportional to cross-sectional area (the 2nd power of linear dimensions), not volume (3rd power). That is why, as body size increases, body mass rises faster than strength.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉最大隨意等長力量與橫斷面積(長度二次方)成正比,不是體積(三次方);這正是體重隨體型增長快於肌力、大而重者力量/體重比偏低的原因。"},{"id":"q0213","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At a given velocity, which muscle action produces the greatest force?","options":["Concentric","Eccentric","Concentric at high velocity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Eccentric","explanation_en":"Force capability is greatest eccentrically, then isometric, then concentric. Torque can even rise with increasing eccentric velocity, the opposite of the concentric force-velocity relationship.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同速度下產力能力:離心>等長>向心;離心時力量甚至可隨速度上升而增加,與向心的力量速度曲線方向相反。"},{"id":"q0214","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete moves from the first transition period (the strength/power phase) into the competitive period of a traditional periodization model. Compared with the first transition period, training during the competitive period typically involves:","options":["Higher training volume and lower intensity to build a work-capacity base","Further increased intensity with decreased volume, plus a sharp rise in sport-specific skill and tactical practice","Roughly the same intensity and volume, held constant to avoid any detraining"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Further increased intensity with decreased volume, plus a sharp rise in sport-specific skill and tactical practice","explanation_en":"Across the periodization periods, volume falls as intensity rises. Moving from the first transition (strength/power phase: low to very high loads at low volume) into the competitive period, the aim is to further increase strength and power by raising intensity while decreasing volume (peaking can reach >=93% of the 1RM at very low volume), and time spent on sport-specific skills and tactics increases dramatically (5th ed, ch 22). Building a base with high volume and low intensity belongs to the preparatory/off-season period.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統週期化中,由第一轉換期(肌力/功率)進入比賽期:強度再升、量再降(高峰可達 93% 1RM 以上且量極低),並把大量時間轉向專項技術與戰術;高量低強度是準備期的事。"},{"id":"q0215","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which best describes cortisol's role relevant to resistance training?","options":["An anabolic hormone that builds contractile protein","A catabolic signal hormone for carbohydrate metabolism, with greater catabolic effect on Type II fibers","A hormone whose main action is suppressing fat oxidation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A catabolic signal hormone for carbohydrate metabolism, with greater catabolic effect on Type II fibers","explanation_en":"Cortisol is the primary signal hormone for carbohydrate metabolism - it promotes gluconeogenesis, raises proteolytic enzymes, and inhibits protein synthesis, hitting Type II fibers hardest. It does NOT suppress fat oxidation (insulin does).","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮質醇是碳水化合物代謝的主要訊號激素:促進醣質新生、提高蛋白水解酶、抑制蛋白合成,且對第二型纖維的分解效應較大,屬分解代謝訊號激素;抑制脂肪氧化的是胰島素,不是皮質醇。"},{"id":"q0216","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In men, testosterone is secreted primarily from:","options":["The adrenal medulla","Leydig cells in the testes","The anterior pituitary"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Leydig cells in the testes","explanation_en":"Testosterone comes mainly from the Leydig cells of the testes (also ovaries in women and the adrenal glands), then travels bound to globulin and albumin to target tissues.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"男性睪固酮主要由睪丸的 Leydig(間質)細胞分泌(女性來自卵巢,兩性腎上腺少量分泌),入血後與球蛋白、白蛋白結合運送到標的組織。"},{"id":"q0217","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which factor has the GREATEST effect on the magnitude of excess post-exercise oxygen consumption (EPOC)?","options":["Exercise intensity","Time of day","The athlete's standing height"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Exercise intensity","explanation_en":"Intensity has the greatest effect on EPOC, although both higher intensity and longer duration increase it. EPOC is the elevated post-exercise oxygen uptake that restores the body after the oxygen deficit incurred at onset.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對 EPOC(運動後過耗氧量)幅度影響最大的是運動強度—強度與時間都會推高它,但強度的效應最大;EPOC 是運動後為恢復體內恆態而維持升高的攝氧量,清償開始時的氧欠債。"},{"id":"q0218","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A consistent fiber-type shift with chronic endurance (or resistance) training is:","options":["Type I converting to Type IIx","Type IIx shifting toward the more oxidative Type IIa","Type IIa converting to Type I"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Type IIx shifting toward the more oxidative Type IIa","explanation_en":"Training shifts fibers from the least oxidative Type IIx toward Type IIa. Detraining can cause a Type IIx 'overshoot.' True Type I Type II conversion is not well supported.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練造成一致且可重複的纖維位移:氧化能力最低的 IIx 轉向更氧化的 IIa;去訓練時可能出現 IIx「反彈超調」。I 型與 II 型之間的真正互換證據不足。"},{"id":"q0219","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The minimal essential strain (MES) that initiates new bone formation is approximately:","options":["About one-tenth of the force needed to fracture the bone","Equal to the force needed to fracture the bone","About double the fracture force"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About one-tenth of the force needed to fracture the bone","explanation_en":"MES is roughly 1/10 of the bone's fracture force. Loading above MES (an osteogenic stimulus) recruits osteoblasts to deposit new bone matrix that mineralizes as hydroxyapatite.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最小必要應變(MES)約為骨折所需力的 1/10;達到以上屬成骨刺激,動員成骨細胞沉積骨基質,再礦化為羥基磷灰石,骨量因此增加。"},{"id":"q0220","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Complete oxidation of ONE triglyceride molecule yields approximately how many ATP?","options":["Over 300 ATP","Exactly 38 ATP","About 100 ATP"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Over 300 ATP","explanation_en":"The 5th edition states a triglyceride (glycerol + three fatty acids) yields 'over 300 ATP.' Notes citing 463 ATP use the outdated NADH = 3 convention.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一分子三酸甘油酯(甘油+三個脂肪酸)完全氧化,第 5 版依新 P/O 比值寫「超過 300 個 ATP」;463 是舊的 NADH=3 換算值,考的是現行版本數字。"},{"id":"q0221","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Yerkes-Dodson's inverted-U hypothesis predicts that as arousal increases, performance:","options":["Increases continuously (more is always better)","Improves to an optimal point, then declines with further arousal","Is unaffected by arousal level"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Improves to an optimal point, then declines with further arousal","explanation_en":"The inverted-U: arousal helps performance up to an optimal level, beyond which more arousal hurts it. Drive theory, by contrast, predicts a linear increase with arousal.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Yerkes-Dodson 倒U 假說:喚醒升至最佳點前表現改善,越過後再升反降;線性遞增是驅力理論的主張,兩者要分清。"},{"id":"q0222","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete's belief in their capability to perform a SPECIFIC task in a SPECIFIC situation is called:","options":["Trait anxiety","Self-efficacy","Intrinsic motivation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Self-efficacy","explanation_en":"Self-efficacy is task- and situation-specific perceived capability and influences activity choice, effort, and persistence. Self-confidence is the broader belief that one can perform a desired behavior.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"自我效能(self-efficacy, Bandura)是對特定情境下完成特定任務能力的信念,影響活動選擇、努力程度與堅持度;自我自信是更泛的概念,兩者不同。"},{"id":"q0223","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Removing an aversive stimulus in order to increase the likelihood of a desired behavior is:","options":["Positive reinforcement","Negative reinforcement","Positive punishment"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Negative reinforcement","explanation_en":"Negative reinforcement increases a behavior by taking away something aversive. Reinforcement (positive or negative) increases behavior; punishment decreases it.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"移除厭惡刺激以提高目標行為出現機率=負增強(negative reinforcement);增強(不論正負)都增加行為,懲罰才減少行為—「負」不等於懲罰。"},{"id":"q0224","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which goal type is most within an athlete's control and the recommended emphasis?","options":["Outcome goals, such as winning the event","Process goals, such as executing specific technique cues","Outcome and process goals are equally controllable"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Process goals, such as executing specific technique cues","explanation_en":"Process goals focus on actions the athlete controls (effort, technique). Outcome goals depend on opponents and others, so they are largely outside the athlete's control.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過程目標(技術要點、執行線索的落實)最操之在己,教科書建議以其為重點;結果目標(奪冠)受對手與外在因素影響,可控性低。"},{"id":"q0225","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The correct order of Fitts and Posner's stages of motor learning is:","options":["Automatic, then associative, then cognitive","Cognitive, then associative, then autonomous (automatic)","Associative, then cognitive, then automatic"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Cognitive, then associative, then autonomous (automatic)","explanation_en":"Learners progress from the cognitive stage (effortful, conscious) to the associative stage (refining) to the autonomous/automatic stage (little conscious attention needed).","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Fitts 與 Posner 的順序固定:認知期(有意識、費力)→聯結期(精修動作)→自動化期(幾乎不需意識注意即可完成)。"},{"id":"q0226","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The recommended daily protein intake for STRENGTH athletes is approximately:","options":["0.8 g/kg/day","1.4-2.0 g/kg/day","3.5-4.0 g/kg/day"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1.4-2.0 g/kg/day","explanation_en":"Strength athletes target roughly 1.4-2.0 g/kg/day (endurance athletes ~1.2-2.0). The general adult RDA is 0.8 g/kg/day.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量型運動員蛋白質建議每日約 1.4 到 2.0 g/kg(耐力型約 1.2 到 2.0);0.8 g/kg 只是一般成人 RDA,3.5 以上則過高缺乏必要。"},{"id":"q0227","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which plant-based protein is noted as containing all nine essential amino acids?","options":["Rice","Soy","Peanuts"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Soy","explanation_en":"Soy is cited as the only plant-based source containing all nine essential amino acids, making it a complete protein.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書指出黃豆(大豆蛋白)是唯一含全部九種必需胺基酸的植物性蛋白質來源,屬完全蛋白;米與花生本身胺基酸譜不全。"},{"id":"q0228","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A common creatine supplementation protocol is:","options":["2 g/day for 30 days with no loading","A loading dose of ~20-25 g/day (or 0.3 g/kg/day) for ~5 days, then ~2 g/day maintenance","A single 0.3 g/kg dose just before competition"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A loading dose of ~20-25 g/day (or 0.3 g/kg/day) for ~5 days, then ~2 g/day maintenance","explanation_en":"Loading ~20-25 g/day (0.3 g/kg/day) for ~5 days saturates muscle creatine stores, followed by ~2 g/day (0.03 g/kg/day) maintenance.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌酸常用方案:loading 每日約 20 到 25 g(或 0.3 g/kg)約 5 天,使肌肉肌酸儲備飽和,之後維持每日約 2 g(0.03 g/kg);只吃 2 g 不 loading 見效慢,賽前單次 0.3 g/kg 則不足。"},{"id":"q0229","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sodium bicarbonate works as an ergogenic buffer by:","options":["Lowering blood pH to speed glycolysis","Raising blood pH, which increases the gradient driving H+ out of muscle cells","Directly supplying ATP to the muscle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Raising blood pH, which increases the gradient driving H+ out of muscle cells","explanation_en":"Sodium bicarbonate raises blood pH, increasing the pH gradient between inside and outside the cell so H+ leaves working muscle faster. Roughly 0.3 g/kg 60-90 min before high-intensity exercise; it can cause GI distress.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"碳酸氫鈉的緩衝機制是提高血液 pH,加大細胞內外的 pH 梯度,使工作肌的 H+ 更快外送;約 0.3 g/kg 於高強度運動前 60 到 90 分鐘服用,可能引起腸胃不適。"},{"id":"q0230","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The Adequate Intake (AI) for water is approximately:","options":["3.7 L/day for men and 2.7 L/day for women","1 L/day for everyone","5 L/day for men and 4 L/day for women"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"3.7 L/day for men and 2.7 L/day for women","explanation_en":"Water AI is ~3.7 L/day (men) and ~2.7 L/day (women). A fluid loss exceeding 2% of body weight signals inadequate replacement.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"水的適量攝取(AI):男性約每日 3.7 公升、女性約 2.7 公升;運動中水分流失超過體重 2% 即代表補充不足。"},{"id":"q0231","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The glycemic index ranks a carbohydrate against a reference food (glucose or white bread) assigned a value of:","options":["50","100","0"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"100","explanation_en":"GI compares a food's ~2-hour blood-glucose response to a reference food (glucose or white bread = 100). Glycemic load additionally accounts for the amount of carbohydrate per serving.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"血糖指標(GI)以參考食物(葡萄糖或白麵包)定為 100,比較攝取等量碳水後約 2 小時的血糖反應;血糖負荷(GL)則再計入每份的實際碳水含量。"},{"id":"q0232","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"To maximize muscle protein synthesis after resistance training in young adults, the recommended protein dose is about:","options":["5-10 g of any protein","20-25 g of high-quality, leucine-rich protein","60-80 g of protein"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"20-25 g of high-quality, leucine-rich protein","explanation_en":"About 20-25 g of high-quality, high-leucine (~2-3 g leucine) protein maximizes MPS in young individuals; older adults may need 40+ g. The 'anabolic window' is heavily debated.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"年輕人在阻力訓練後攝取約 20 到 25 g 高品質、富含白胺酸(約 2 到 3 g leucine)的蛋白質即可最大化肌蛋白合成;年長者可能需 40 g 以上;「合成代謝視窗」的急迫性仍有爭議。"},{"id":"q0233","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 'core' exercise (as opposed to an assistance exercise) is best defined as one that:","options":["Targets the abdominal muscles specifically","Recruits one or more large muscle areas, crosses two or more primary joints, and receives priority","Uses only body weight"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recruits one or more large muscle areas, crosses two or more primary joints, and receives priority","explanation_en":"Core exercises recruit large muscle areas across 2+ primary joints (e.g., squat, bench press) and get priority for their direct sport application. Assistance exercises are smaller, often single-joint.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"NSCA 定義的核心練習=動員一個或多個大肌群、跨越兩個以上主要關節、在動作選擇上優先(深蹲、臥推);它指的是動作層級,不是「練腹核」;輔助練習多為較小、單一關節的動作。"},{"id":"q0234","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For improving power output in exercises that can be heavily loaded, the most effective intensity range is roughly:","options":["20-30% 1RM","75-90% 1RM","Always 100% 1RM"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"75-90% 1RM","explanation_en":"For heavily loadable resistance exercises, ~75-90% 1RM is most effective/practical for power. Rest 2-5 minutes between sets when training single-effort power.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"可以被大負荷的阻力動作,改善功率輸出最有效且實用的強度約 75% 到 90% 1RM;單發功率訓練組間休息 2 到 5 分鐘。20 到 30% 太輕,永遠 100% 則速度出不來。"},{"id":"q0235","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The '2-for-2 rule' directs you to increase load when an athlete can perform:","options":["2 reps over the goal on the last set in 2 consecutive workouts","2 total workouts within 2 weeks","2 sets of 2 reps at a new maximum"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"2 reps over the goal on the last set in 2 consecutive workouts","explanation_en":"The 2-for-2 rule: if the athlete completes 2 or more reps beyond the rep goal on the last set in 2 consecutive sessions, increase the weight.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"2-for-2 規則:連續兩次課的最後一組都超出目標次數 2 次或以上,就應增加該動作的重量—這是身體已適應的訊號,與湊滿兩次課或新極限無關。"},{"id":"q0236","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Order these training cycles from LONGEST to shortest:","options":["Microcycle > mesocycle > macrocycle","Macrocycle > mesocycle > microcycle","Mesocycle > macrocycle > microcycle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Macrocycle > mesocycle > microcycle","explanation_en":"Macrocycle (months to a year) > mesocycle (2-6 weeks) > microcycle (several days to ~2 weeks).","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"週期由長到短:大週期(macrocycle,數月到一年)>中週期(mesocycle,2 到 6 週)>微週期(microcycle,數天到約兩週)。"},{"id":"q0237","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The preparatory (off-season) period is characterized by:","options":["High intensity, low volume, sport-specific work","Low intensity, high volume to build a conditioning base","Peaking with very low volume"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Low intensity, high volume to build a conditioning base","explanation_en":"The preparatory/off-season period uses low intensity and high volume to develop a conditioning base, raising the athlete's tolerance for later, more intense training.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"準備期(休季期)的特徵是低強度、高訓練量,建立體適能基礎,抬高後續高強度訓練所能承受的容許度;高強度低量的高峰化在賽前才出現。"},{"id":"q0238","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Complex training takes advantage of postactivation potentiation by pairing:","options":["A high-load strength exercise followed by a biomechanically similar explosive/plyometric exercise","Two antagonist exercises back-to-back","Steady-state cardio with static stretching"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A high-load strength exercise followed by a biomechanically similar explosive/plyometric exercise","explanation_en":"Complex training follows a heavy strength exercise with a similar explosive (stretch-shortening-cycle) movement to exploit postactivation potentiation.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"複合訓練(complex training)=高負荷肌力動作接上力學結構相似的爆發/增強式動作,利用活動後增強效應(PAP)讓後續跳躍等動作品質更高;不是拮抗肌相連(那是超級組)。"},{"id":"q0239","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A frequently cited strength prerequisite before an adult performs lower-body depth jumps is a back-squat 1RM of at least:","options":["1.0x body weight","1.5x body weight","2.5x body weight"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1.5x body weight","explanation_en":"A common guideline is a squat 1RM of ~1.5x body weight before lower-body (depth/box) plyometrics. Depth-jump box heights run ~16-42 in (norm 30-32 in); use <18 in for athletes over 220 lb.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成人做下肢深跳等增強式前,常被引用的肌力前提是背蹲 1RM 至少約 1.5 倍體重;深跳箱約 16 到 42 吋(常用 30 到 32 吋),體重超過 220 磅者箱高宜低於 18 吋。"},{"id":"q0240","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The recommended MINIMUM recovery between plyometric training sessions is:","options":["12-24 hours","48-72 hours","A full week"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"48-72 hours","explanation_en":"48-72 hours between plyometric workouts optimizes adaptation while minimizing injury risk.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練課程之間建議至少間隔 48 到 72 小時,讓神經肌肉充分恢復,最適化適應並降低受傷風險;12 到 24 小時不足,一週則過長。"},{"id":"q0241","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The defining difference between 'change of direction' and 'agility' is that agility:","options":["Is simply slower than change of direction","Adds a response to a stimulus (a perceptual-cognitive component)","Only occurs in a straight line"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Adds a response to a stimulus (a perceptual-cognitive component)","explanation_en":"Change of direction is pre-planned; agility requires reacting to a stimulus, combining perceptual-cognitive ability with change-of-direction ability.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"敏捷與預設變向的分界:敏捷多了對刺激反應的知覺認知成分(先辨識再決定怎麼變),COD 則是路線早已規劃好的變向。"},{"id":"q0242","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which is generally considered the BEST single indicator of aerobic endurance performance?","options":["VO2max","Maximal lactate steady state","Resting heart rate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Maximal lactate steady state","explanation_en":"The hierarchy given is maximal lactate steady state > lactate threshold > VO2max as an indicator of aerobic endurance performance.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書給出的耐力表現指標階序:最大乳酸穩定態(MLSS)>乳酸閾值>VO2max—MLSS 最接近真實耐力表現,VO2max 單項反而是最弱指標。"},{"id":"q0243","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In PNF stretching, the first phase always begins with:","options":["A 6-second maximal isometric contraction","An initial ~10-second passive, relaxed stretch","A ballistic bounce at end range"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"An initial ~10-second passive, relaxed stretch","explanation_en":"PNF (hold-relax or contract-relax) always starts with a ~10-second passive relaxed stretch, then the contraction phase, then a longer relax.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"PNF(hold-relax 或 contract-relax)第一階段恆為約 10 秒的放鬆被動伸展,接著才進入收縮期,最後再更長地放鬆並加深伸展;一開始就 6 秒最大等長收縮順序錯了。"},{"id":"q0244","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Relaxation that occurs in the SAME muscle that was just actively contracted (e.g., before stretching it) is called:","options":["Reciprocal inhibition","Autogenic inhibition","The stretch reflex"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Autogenic inhibition","explanation_en":"Autogenic inhibition is relaxation in the same muscle experiencing increased tension (GTO-mediated). Reciprocal inhibition is relaxation of the OPPOSING muscle while the agonist contracts.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"剛收縮的那同一塊肌肉隨後出現的鬆弛=自生抑制(autogenic inhibition),由高氏腱器介導;收縮主動肌時其拮抗肌鬆弛才是互動抑制(reciprocal inhibition)。"},{"id":"q0245","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When spotting a dumbbell chest fly, the spotter's hands should be placed near the athlete's:","options":["Wrists","Forearms, close to the elbows","The dumbbells themselves"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Forearms, close to the elbows","explanation_en":"Spot the dumbbell fly at the forearms near the elbows - not the wrists and not the dumbbells - for the best control and safety.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"啞鈴飛鳥的保護位置在前臂靠近手肘處—不是手腕(那是臥推的位置),也不是啞鈴本身;這個位置對動作軌跡的控制最好、最安全。"},{"id":"q0246","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Interval training to develop the phosphagen (ATP-PCr) energy system uses near-maximal (90-100%) efforts of about 5 to 10 seconds. According to the textbook's interval-training table, the appropriate work-to-rest ratio is approximately:","options":["1:3 to 1:5","1:12 to 1:20","1:1 to 1:3"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1:12 to 1:20","explanation_en":"The 5th ed interval-training table (ch 3) pairs each energy system with a work-to-rest ratio: phosphagen (90-100%, ~5-10 s) = 1:12 to 1:20; fast glycolysis (15-30 s) = 1:3 to 1:5; fast glycolysis + oxidative (1-3 min) = 1:3 to 1:4; oxidative (>3 min) = 1:1 to 1:3. Short maximal efforts need long rest so phosphagens can replenish, hence the large 1:12 to 1:20 ratio.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第 5 版間歇訓練表與能量系統對應:磷酸原(90 到 100%、約 5 到 10 秒)=1:12 到 1:20;快速糖解(15 到 30 秒)=1:3 到 1:5;糖解+氧化(1 到 3 分鐘)=1:3 到 1:4;氧化(超過 3 分鐘)=1:1 到 1:3。極短全力必須配極長休息讓磷酸原回填。"},{"id":"q0247","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Compared with a high-bar back squat, a low-bar squat (more forward trunk lean) tends to place:","options":["More torque on the knees and less on the hips","More torque on the hips and less on the knees","Equal torque on the hips and knees"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"More torque on the hips and less on the knees","explanation_en":"Greater forward lean (low-bar) lengthens the moment arm at the hips, so hip torque rises and knee torque falls. The more upright high-bar squat shifts torque toward the knees.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"低槓位深蹲軀幹前傾較多,髖關節的力臂變長,因此髖力矩上升、膝力矩下降;高槓位較直立的蹲法則把力矩移向膝蓋。"},{"id":"q0248","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a test battery, which tests should be administered BEFORE the others?","options":["Aerobic capacity tests","Non-fatiguing tests and maximal power/strength tests, before fatiguing anaerobic and aerobic capacity tests","Local muscular endurance tests"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Non-fatiguing tests and maximal power/strength tests, before fatiguing anaerobic and aerobic capacity tests","explanation_en":"Sequence: non-fatiguing -> agility -> max power/strength -> sprints -> muscular endurance -> fatiguing anaerobic capacity -> aerobic capacity. Fatiguing tests go last so they don't contaminate power and skill measures.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"測驗電池順序:不致疲勞→敏捷→最大功率/肌力→衝刺→肌耐力→致疲勞的無氧容量→有氧容量;致疲勞專案放最後,才不會汙染功率與技術類測量的效度。"},{"id":"q0249","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sympathetic overtraining syndrome is MOST associated with:","options":["Endurance athletes and high training volume","Strength/power athletes and high training intensity","Beginners only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Strength/power athletes and high training intensity","explanation_en":"Sympathetic OTS is intensity-driven and develops first, more common in younger strength/power athletes. Parasympathetic OTS is volume-driven, more common in endurance athletes, and represents the later culmination.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"交感神經過度訓練症候群與高訓練強度、力量/功率型運動員相關,先發生、較常見於年輕力量型選手;副交感型才是高量、耐力型、後期惡化的型態。"},{"id":"q0250","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Functional overreaching (FOR) differs from nonfunctional overreaching (NFOR) in that FOR:","options":["Causes months-long performance loss","Causes a short-term performance dip that can supercompensate into gains after an appropriate taper","Always progresses to overtraining syndrome"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Causes a short-term performance dip that can supercompensate into gains after an appropriate taper","explanation_en":"FOR is a short-term (days-weeks) decrement that can rebound into gains after a taper. NFOR is a weeks-to-months stagnation/decrement; overtraining syndrome lasts months or more.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"功能性過度負荷(FOR)是短期(數天到數週)的表現下滑,經適當減量後可超補償反彈、甚至創新高;非功能性(NFOR)停滯或下滑數週到數月,過度訓練症候群以月以上計。"},{"id":"q0251","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the acute inflammatory phase of tissue healing (first ~2-3 days), the strength coach should:","options":["Aggressively load the injured tissue to drive adaptation","Avoid exercise that directly stresses the injured area while maintaining cardiorespiratory fitness and surrounding function","Stop all physical activity completely"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Avoid exercise that directly stresses the injured area while maintaining cardiorespiratory fitness and surrounding function","explanation_en":"In the inflammatory phase, protect the injured structure (avoid directly stressing it) while maintaining cardiorespiratory fitness and the function of surrounding, uninjured areas.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"急性發炎期(約前 2 到 3 天)原則:保護受傷結構、避免直接負荷該部位,同時維持心肺適能與周圍未受傷部位的功能,不是完全停止一切活動,也不是猛練患部。"},{"id":"q0252","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Recommended professional-to-participant supervision ratios tighten for younger athletes. The HIGH-SCHOOL ratio is:","options":["1:10","1:15","1:20"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1:15","explanation_en":"Junior high 1:10, high school 1:15, college 1:20 (adults/elite can be higher). Younger, less experienced athletes need closer supervision.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"監督比:國中 1:10、高中 1:15、大學 1:20—年齡越輕、經驗越淺越需要緊盯,高中對應的是 1:15。"},{"id":"q0253","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which four elements must all be present to establish negligence?","options":["Duty, breach of duty, proximate cause, and damages","Intent, motive, opportunity, and harm","Contract, payment, service, and refund"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Duty, breach of duty, proximate cause, and damages","explanation_en":"Negligence = a duty to act, a breach of that duty (failing the standard of care), proximate cause (reasonably foreseeable), and resulting damages.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過失的四要件:注意義務、違反義務(未達注意義務標準)、近因(合理可預見)、以及實際損害;四者缺一不成立。"},{"id":"q0254","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The general planning guideline for resistance-training floor space is approximately:","options":["~25 sq ft per athlete","~100 sq ft per athlete","~400 sq ft per athlete"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"~100 sq ft per athlete","explanation_en":"Plan for roughly 100 sq ft per athlete in the resistance-training area, with walkways over 36 in (over 48 in in circuit areas) and air exchanged 8-12 times per hour.","tags":["Full Mixed Review"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練區的空間規劃約每人 100 平方英尺;動線寬度 36 吋以上(迴圈訓練區 48 吋以上),每小時換氣 8 到 12 次。"},{"id":"q0255","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete performs a standing dumbbell biceps curl. At the elbow, the biceps inserts close to the joint axis while the dumbbell is held far out at the hand. To hold the weight static at 90 degrees of flexion, what is true about the force the biceps must produce relative to the weight of the dumbbell?","options":["The biceps must produce a force greater than the weight of the dumbbell because the muscle's force arm is shorter than the resistance arm","The biceps produces a force equal to the dumbbell's weight because torque is conserved across the joint","The biceps produces less force than the dumbbell's weight because the elbow gives the muscle a mechanical advantage greater than 1"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The biceps must produce a force greater than the weight of the dumbbell because the muscle's force arm is shorter than the resistance arm","explanation_en":"The elbow during curling is a third-class lever: the muscle (effort) inserts between the axis and the resistance, so its force arm (moment arm) is shorter than the resistance arm. Mechanical advantage = force arm / resistance arm < 1, so the muscle must produce MORE force than the external load to balance torque. The trap is the third option ('mechanical advantage greater than 1') - third-class levers favor range of motion and speed, not force, so MA is always less than 1 and the muscle is at a force disadvantage.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"站姿彎舉時肘關節是第三類槓桿:肱二頭肌的力點位於轉軸與啞鈴之間,力臂短於阻力臂,機械優勢小於 1,靜止持住時肌肉必須輸出大於啞鈴重量的力才能平衡力矩;陷阱選項「機械優勢大於 1」正好說反—第三類槓桿換的是活動度與速度,不是力。"},{"id":"q0256","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to compare the torque produced about the knee at two points in a leg extension. The quadriceps tendon force is identical at both points, but at point A the perpendicular distance from the knee axis to the line of muscle pull is larger than at point B. What does this tell you about the muscular torque at the two points?","options":["Torque is greater at point A because torque equals muscle force times the perpendicular distance (moment arm)","Torque is greater at point B because a shorter moment arm concentrates the force closer to the axis","Torque is equal at both points because the muscle force did not change"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Torque is greater at point A because torque equals muscle force times the perpendicular distance (moment arm)","explanation_en":"Torque = force x moment arm, where the moment arm is the PERPENDICULAR distance from the axis of rotation to the line of action of the force. With equal force, the larger moment arm (point A) yields greater torque. The trap is the second option: a shorter moment arm produces LESS torque, not more - 'closer to the axis' reduces the lever, it does not concentrate force. The third option ignores that moment arm, not just force, sets torque.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力矩=力×力臂,力臂是轉軸到力作用線的垂直距離;肌肉拉力相同時,垂直距離較大的 A 點力矩較大。說「力臂短反而把力集中在軸上」是誤解—力臂短力矩更小,且只比力不看力臂也錯。"},{"id":"q0257","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two volleyball players leave the ground with the exact same takeoff velocity and reach the same jump height. Player 1 used a deep, slow countermovement applying a moderate ground reaction force over a longer time; Player 2 used a shallow, quick countermovement applying a much larger force over a shorter time. Which principle best explains how both achieved the same takeoff velocity?","options":["The force-velocity relationship, because higher force always permits a higher movement velocity","The Frank-Starling mechanism, because greater stretch yields a more forceful contraction","The impulse-momentum relationship, because the product of force and time (impulse) equals the change in momentum, and both produced the same impulse"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The impulse-momentum relationship, because the product of force and time (impulse) equals the change in momentum, and both produced the same impulse","explanation_en":"Impulse (force x time) equals the change in momentum (mass x velocity change). Identical takeoff velocity for the same mass means identical change in momentum, so both jumps required the same impulse - achievable as big force x short time OR smaller force x longer time. The trap force-velocity choice describes the inverse relationship between contraction force and shortening velocity within a muscle, not how two jumpers reach equal velocity. Frank-Starling is a cardiac stretch-tension mechanism, irrelevant here.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同樣的起跳速度代表動量改變數相同,而衝量(力×時間)等於動量改變數:大力×短時間與小力×長時間可湊出同一衝量,所以兩人起跳速度一致—這是衝量—動量關係;力量—速度關係講的是肌肉內部收縮力與縮短速度的反比,Frank-Starling 是心臟的牽張機制,都非此處答案。"},{"id":"q0258","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete performs the lowering (return) phase of a standing cable chest fly: starting with the handles pressed together in front of the chest, the arms open outward to the sides under control until they are wide. During this controlled opening, which muscle action is occurring at the shoulder?","options":["The shoulder adductors (pectoralis major, latissimus dorsi) contract eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the arms moving into abduction","The shoulder abductors (deltoid) contract concentrically to spread the arms apart","The shoulder adductors contract concentrically to open the arms"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The shoulder adductors (pectoralis major, latissimus dorsi) contract eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the arms moving into abduction","explanation_en":"On the return phase the cable resistance is pulling the arms apart (toward abduction), and the prime movers of the fly - the shoulder ADDUCTORS (pectoralis major, lat) - lengthen while still generating force to control that motion, so they work eccentrically. The trap is the deltoid (abductors): they would be the concentric mover if the cable were resisting you in the other direction, but here gravity/the cable open the arms and the adductors brake it. A concentric adductor action would bring the arms back together, not open them.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"纜繩飛鳥的返回(開臂)階段,阻力把雙臂往 abduction 方向拉;飛鳥的主動肌—肩關節內收肌(胸大肌、背闊肌)—邊產生力量邊被動延長,做離心收縮來剎車控制。此時三角肌(外展肌)是順著阻力方向走,不是控制者;內收肌向心收縮會把手臂闔攏而不是開啟。"},{"id":"q0259","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Slow-motion video shows a baseball pitcher's throwing arm during the follow-through, immediately after release: the arm has just rapidly internally rotated to deliver the pitch and must now be decelerated before the shoulder reaches its end range. Which muscles act eccentrically to brake the arm?","options":["The external rotators of the posterior rotator cuff (infraspinatus, teres minor), lengthening under load to decelerate the internal rotation","The internal rotators (subscapularis, pectoralis major), eccentrically slowing the arm","The middle deltoid, concentrically abducting the arm"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The external rotators of the posterior rotator cuff (infraspinatus, teres minor), lengthening under load to decelerate the internal rotation","explanation_en":"The forceful motion that launches the pitch is rapid internal rotation, driven concentrically by the internal rotators. Decelerating it falls to the antagonist working eccentrically - the EXTERNAL rotators of the posterior cuff (infraspinatus, teres minor) lengthen under load to brake the arm and protect the joint, which is why posterior-cuff eccentric strength is emphasized in throwers. The trap is the internal rotators: they PRODUCE the internal rotation concentrically, they do not brake it. The deltoid is not the decelerator here.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"投擲釋放後,手臂快速內旋必須被減速煞車,負責的是後方轉袖外旋肌群(棘下肌、小圓肌)在拉長中出力(離心收縮)來煞車並保護肩關節—這就是投手要練後方袖離心力的原因。內旋肌群是向心產生內旋的「引擎」,不是煞車;三角肌也不是此階段的減速者。"},{"id":"q0260","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A lifter slowly lowers into the bottom of a back squat under control. At the hip, which muscle action is occurring as the lifter descends?","options":["The hip extensors (gluteus maximus, hamstrings) are contracting eccentrically to control hip flexion","The hip flexors (iliopsoas) are contracting concentrically to pull the lifter down","The hip extensors are contracting concentrically to lower the body"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The hip extensors (gluteus maximus, hamstrings) are contracting eccentrically to control hip flexion","explanation_en":"Descending into a squat is hip FLEXION occurring against gravity. Gravity supplies the flexing force, so the muscles working are the antagonists - the hip EXTENSORS - lengthening eccentrically to brake the descent. The trap is the hip flexors contracting concentrically: gravity, not the hip flexors, drives the descent, so the flexors are largely passive while the extensors do the controlling work. Concentric hip extension happens on the way UP, not down.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"下蹲階段髖關節屈曲是重力驅動的,髖伸肌(臀大肌、膕繩肌)以離心收縮拉著、控制髖屈的角度與速度;說髖屈肌向心把人「拉下來」是錯的,下蹲動力來自重力,上蹲時的向心髖伸才是臀膕做正功。"},{"id":"q0261","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the first roughly 10 seconds of an all-out sprint relying on the phosphagen system, what happens to intramuscular ATP and phosphocreatine (PCr) concentrations?","options":["Both ATP and PCr fall dramatically in parallel","PCr stays nearly constant while ATP is markedly depleted","ATP stays nearly constant while PCr is markedly depleted"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"ATP stays nearly constant while PCr is markedly depleted","explanation_en":"ATP concentration is fiercely defended and stays nearly constant even during maximal effort, because the creatine kinase reaction rapidly rephosphorylates ADP using PCr. PCr is the buffer that gets drained - it can drop substantially in seconds. The trap is picking ATP as the substance depleted: a large fall in ATP would compromise the cell, so the body sacrifices PCr to keep ATP stable. The third option reverses the actual physiology.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"全力衝刺的前約 10 秒:肌肉 ATP 濃度幾乎不變—肌酸激酶用磷酸肌酸迅速再磷酸化 ADP,把 ATP 守在一定水位;被大量抽乾的是緩衝池 PCr。說 ATP 大幅下降違反生理:ATP 大跌細胞就撐不住,身體犧牲的是 PCr。"},{"id":"q0262","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach is classifying the dominant energy system for a single effort that lasts about 2 minutes at high intensity (for example, a 800 m run sustained near maximal pace). Which energy system contribution best describes this effort?","options":["Almost entirely phosphagen, because the effort is maximal","Almost entirely oxidative, because it lasts longer than one minute","A roughly balanced contribution from fast glycolysis and oxidative metabolism"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A roughly balanced contribution from fast glycolysis and oxidative metabolism","explanation_en":"Energy system contribution is judged by the DURATION of the effort. Efforts of about 1 to 3 minutes draw on a mix of fast glycolysis and oxidative metabolism, with the crossover occurring within this window. The trap 'almost entirely oxidative' is wrong because the glycolytic system is still contributing heavily near the 2-minute mark - oxidative does not fully dominate until efforts well beyond 3 minutes. Phosphagen is essentially spent after roughly 10 seconds.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"約 2 分鐘的高強度單發(如 800 米)落在交叉窗內:快速糖解與氧化代謝大約各半;磷酸原約 10 秒後已基本耗盡,氧化要到遠超 3 分鐘才完全主導,「幾乎全氧化」在 2 分鐘時還不成立。"},{"id":"q0263","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A basketball point guard repeatedly performs all-out 5-second drives separated by jogging and standing. Generically the sport is 'aerobic' over a 40-minute game, but each explosive drive itself is fueled mostly by which system?","options":["The oxidative system, because the overall game is long","The phosphagen system, because each individual burst is very short and near-maximal","Fast glycolysis, because basketball is a power sport"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The phosphagen system, because each individual burst is very short and near-maximal","explanation_en":"Classify by the duration of the described action, not the sport label. A 5-second near-maximal burst is fueled predominantly by the phosphagen system. Intermittent sprint sports are anaerobic bursts riding on an aerobic base - the aerobic system helps replenish PCr between efforts, but it does not power the burst itself. The trap 'oxidative because the game is long' confuses total game time with the brief effort. Fast glycolysis would dominate efforts more in the 15 to 30 second range.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"判定能量系統看「該動作的持續時間與強度」,不看專項標籤:5 秒的近全力突破由磷酸原系統供能;整場比賽有有氧底,是幫衝刺間 PCr 回填,不是驅動動作本身。快速糖解主導區間約在 15 到 30 秒。"},{"id":"q0264","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach programs 10-second maximal sled sprints. The training GOAL is to maximize speed and power output on every rep, with each rep as crisp as the first. Which work-to-rest ratio best fits this goal?","options":["About 1:3 to 1:5 (short rest), so the athlete trains under fatigue","About 1:1, to keep the session time-efficient","About 1:12 to 1:20 (full recovery, roughly 2 to 3 minutes rest), so PCr is nearly fully restored before each rep"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 1:12 to 1:20 (full recovery, roughly 2 to 3 minutes rest), so PCr is nearly fully restored before each rep","explanation_en":"For a speed and power goal, each rep must be high quality, which requires near-full PCr restoration between efforts - a long work-to-rest ratio of about 1:12 to 1:20 (roughly 2 to 3 minutes rest after a 10-second sprint). The trap is the short 1:3 to 1:5 ratio: that incomplete recovery is deliberately used to train anaerobic/glycolytic CAPACITY (forcing work before PCr refills), which degrades power output - the opposite of a speed-power goal.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練目標是每一下都要高品質的速度與功率時,PCr 必須近乎完全回填才能再衝,工休比約 1:12 到 1:20(10 秒衝刺後休約 2 到 3 分鐘);1:3 到 1:5 的不完全恢復是拿capacity 換品質,功率表現會掉。"},{"id":"q0265","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A different coach uses the same 10-second sprints but now wants to build anaerobic (glycolytic) capacity and tolerance to fatigue, deliberately starting each rep before PCr is fully restored. Which work-to-rest ratio fits this goal?","options":["About 1:12 to 1:20, full recovery between reps","About 1:3 to 1:5, incomplete recovery between reps","About 1:25, extended recovery to keep quality high"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 1:3 to 1:5, incomplete recovery between reps","explanation_en":"An anaerobic/glycolytic CAPACITY goal calls for incomplete recovery, around 1:3 to 1:5, so the athlete begins each rep before PCr fully refills, taxing glycolysis and fatigue tolerance. The trap is the long 1:12 to 1:20 ratio - that full recovery is for a speed-power QUALITY goal and would not stress the glycolytic system the way capacity training requires. Note the same 10-second sprint serves opposite goals depending only on the rest interval.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"目標若是無氧糖解容量與對疲勞的耐受力,反而要在 PCr 未滿前就起下一次,工休比約 1:3 到 1:5 製造不完全恢復;同樣 10 秒衝刺,只改休息時間就能在「速度功率品質」與「糖解容量」兩個相反目標間切換。"},{"id":"q0266","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Compared with Type I fibers, Type IIx (fast-twitch) muscle fibers are best characterized by which combination?","options":["Higher mitochondrial density, greater fatigue resistance, and slower contraction velocity","Greater capillary density, higher myoglobin content, and faster contraction velocity","Higher force output per cross-sectional area, faster contraction velocity, and lower fatigue resistance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Higher force output per cross-sectional area, faster contraction velocity, and lower fatigue resistance","explanation_en":"Type IIx fibers contract fastest, produce high force/power, and fatigue quickly; they have relatively low mitochondrial density, capillarization, and myoglobin. The correct answer pairs fast velocity + high force + low fatigue resistance. The first option describes Type I traits (oxidative, fatigue-resistant, slow). The third option mixes Type I oxidative features (capillary density, myoglobin) with fast velocity, an internally inconsistent trap that cannot coexist in IIx.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第二型 x 型纖維的組合是:單位橫斷面積產力高、收縮速度最快、耐疲勞性低,粒線體密度、微血管與肌紅蛋白都低;「粒線體多+耐疲勞+速度慢」是第一型的畫像,「微血管密度高卻收縮快」則自相矛盾。"},{"id":"q0267","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As an athlete progressively increases the force of a muscle contraction, how does the neuromuscular system grade the force output, according to the size principle?","options":["Lower-threshold (smaller) motor units are recruited first, then higher-threshold units are added, and firing rate increases","High-threshold motor units are recruited first because they produce the most force","Individual fibers are partially activated to a degree matching the required force"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Lower-threshold (smaller) motor units are recruited first, then higher-threshold units are added, and firing rate increases","explanation_en":"By the size principle, motor units are recruited in order of increasing size: low-threshold (small, Type I) units first, then progressively larger high-threshold (Type II) units as force demand rises, with rate coding (increased firing frequency) adding further force. The trap second option reverses recruitment order. The third option violates the all-or-none law - a fiber cannot be partially activated; once its motor unit fires, all of its fibers contract fully, and force is graded by recruitment and rate coding, not partial fiber activation.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"依尺寸原則,力量需求上升時先動員低閾值的小型(第一型)運動單位,再逐步疊加高閾值的大型(第二型)單位,再以頻率編碼(rate coding)提高放電頻率加力;高閾值先動員說反了順序,「單條纖維部分活化」則違反全或無律。"},{"id":"q0268","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For the cross-bridge cycle of the sliding-filament model to proceed (attachment, power stroke, detachment, and reattachment), which two things are both required?","options":["Calcium ions to expose actin binding sites and ATP to power the stroke and detach the cross-bridge","Calcium ions and lactate, which together drive the power stroke","ATP alone, since calcium is only needed for relaxation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Calcium ions to expose actin binding sites and ATP to power the stroke and detach the cross-bridge","explanation_en":"Excitation releases Ca2+ from the sarcoplasmic reticulum; Ca2+ binds troponin, moving tropomyosin to expose actin's myosin-binding sites. ATP is then required both to energize the power stroke and to detach myosin from actin so the cycle can repeat. The trap third option is a common error: ATP is needed for detachment AND relaxation, but Ca2+ is essential to INITIATE contraction, not just relaxation. Lactate plays no direct role in the cross-bridge cycle.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"橫橋迴圈要繼續運轉，鈣離子與 ATP 兩者缺一不可：Ca2+ 由肌漿網釋放後結合肌鈣蛋白、移開原肌球蛋白，露出 actin（肌動蛋白）上的結合位；ATP 則既供應動力衝程能量、又讓肌球蛋白頭從 actin 脫落才能重複迴圈。常見誤解是說 Ca2+ 只跟放鬆有關，其實它負責啟動收縮；乳酸則與橫橋迴圈無直接關係。"},{"id":"q0269","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two muscles have the same physiological cross-sectional area, but Muscle A has highly pennate fibers at a steep angle while Muscle B has fibers running parallel to the line of pull. What is the trade-off for the pennate Muscle A?","options":["Greater maximal force potential but a lower maximal shortening velocity","Greater maximal shortening velocity but lower force potential","Both greater force and greater shortening velocity, with no trade-off"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Greater maximal force potential but a lower maximal shortening velocity","explanation_en":"Pennation packs more sarcomeres in parallel per unit area, increasing physiological cross-sectional area and thus force potential, but the fibers are shorter and angled, reducing maximal shortening velocity and the proportion of fiber force transmitted along the tendon. So pennate muscle favors force over speed. The trap second option reverses this (that describes the longer parallel fibers of Muscle B). The third option ignores the inherent force-versus-velocity trade-off of architecture.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"羽狀(pennate)排列讓單位面積內並聯更多肌小節，生理橫截面積與最大力量上升；但肌纖維較短且斜向排列，最大縮短速度與沿肌腱傳導的力量比例都下降。所以羽狀肌是「換力量、失速度」；選項說反的那個描述的其實是平行纖維肌。"},{"id":"q0270","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Based on the force-velocity relationship of muscle, in which condition can a muscle generate the GREATEST force?","options":["During a fast concentric (shortening) action, because speed adds momentum","During an eccentric (lengthening) action against a high load","At its maximal unloaded shortening velocity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"During an eccentric (lengthening) action against a high load","explanation_en":"Force capability is highest during ECCENTRIC actions, where a muscle can resist loads exceeding its maximal isometric force; force then decreases as concentric shortening velocity increases, and is lowest at maximal (unloaded) shortening velocity. The trap first option is the classic error - faster concentric shortening actually produces LESS force, not more, per the force-velocity curve. The third option describes the point of essentially zero force production.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量—速度關係曲線上，離心(長度拉長)動作能產生的力量最大，甚至可以超過最大等長收縮力量；等方向收縮越快力量越小，最大無載縮短速度時力量趨近於零。「快速向心收縮藉速度加動量」是經典誤解。"},{"id":"q0271","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the early weeks (first few weeks) of a previously untrained person's resistance-training program, strength often improves substantially before any meaningful change in muscle size. What primarily accounts for these initial gains?","options":["Rapid myofibrillar hypertrophy adding contractile proteins","Neural adaptations such as increased motor unit recruitment, rate coding, and synchronization","An immediate rise in resting testosterone concentration"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Neural adaptations such as increased motor unit recruitment, rate coding, and synchronization","explanation_en":"Early strength gains in novices are predominantly NEURAL - greater agonist recruitment, increased firing rate (rate coding), improved synchronization, and reduced antagonist co-activation - and precede measurable hypertrophy, which becomes the dominant driver only later. The trap is hypertrophy, which lags behind neural changes in the first weeks. A chronically elevated resting testosterone level is not the mechanism for the rapid early improvements.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新手訓練前幾週的力量提升主要來自神經適應：運動單位動員增加、放電頻率(rate coding)提高、同步化改善、拮抗肌共縮減少的程度變好；肥大落後於神經變化，之後才成為主要來源。靜止時睪固酮長期攀升不是短期快速進步的機制。"},{"id":"q0272","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After several months of well-designed aerobic endurance training, which set of cardiovascular and peripheral adaptations would you expect?","options":["Increased mitochondrial density and capillary density, a widened arterial-venous oxygen difference, and a rightward shift of the lactate threshold","Decreased stroke volume with a higher resting heart rate to maintain cardiac output","Reduced capillary density but greater reliance on the phosphagen system"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increased mitochondrial density and capillary density, a widened arterial-venous oxygen difference, and a rightward shift of the lactate threshold","explanation_en":"Chronic aerobic training increases mitochondrial number/density, capillary density, and the a-vO2 difference (more oxygen extracted per unit blood), raises maximal stroke volume (lowering resting heart rate), and shifts the lactate threshold to the right (higher intensity before lactate accumulates). The trap second option is backward - stroke volume INCREASES and resting heart rate DECREASES with training. The third option contradicts the well-established increase in capillarization and oxidative capacity.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期有氧耐力訓練會提高粒線體密度與微血管密度、擴大動靜氧差(a-vO2 diff)、提升最大心跳輸出並降低安靜心率，同時讓乳酸閾右移(更高強度才開始積乳酸)。選項「心輸出量下降、安靜心率上升」正好說反。"},{"id":"q0273","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Immediately following an acute bout of high-volume, multi-joint resistance exercise with short rest periods, which hormonal response pattern is most expected in a young trained male?","options":["Acute increases in testosterone, growth hormone, and cortisol","An acute decrease in growth hormone and cortisol with no change in testosterone","A selective acute rise in cortisol only, with testosterone and growth hormone unchanged"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Acute increases in testosterone, growth hormone, and cortisol","explanation_en":"A demanding resistance bout (large muscle mass, high volume, short rest) acutely elevates testosterone, growth hormone, and cortisol together; these transient post-exercise spikes are part of the anabolic/catabolic signaling environment. The trap second option reverses the GH and cortisol responses - both rise, they do not fall. The third option wrongly isolates cortisol; the acute response is broad, not selective.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大肌群、高容量、短休息的高強度阻力訓練，會讓年輕受過訓練的男性的睪固酮、生長激素與皮質醇都急性上升；這些運動後的短暫波動屬於合成／分解訊號環境的一部分。GH 與皮質醇是上升不是下降，也不會只有皮質醇單獨上升。"},{"id":"q0274","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A parent asks whether starting their healthy 11-year-old on a properly supervised, appropriately loaded resistance-training program will stunt the child's growth. Based on current evidence, what is the most accurate response?","options":["Yes, resistance training should be avoided before puberty because it compresses the growth plates and stunts height","No, properly designed and supervised resistance training does not stunt growth; epiphyseal plate injury risk is associated with improper technique or maximal/excessive loads, not appropriate training","Yes, but only if the child uses machines instead of free weights"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"No, properly designed and supervised resistance training does not stunt growth; epiphyseal plate injury risk is associated with improper technique or maximal/excessive loads, not appropriate training","explanation_en":"There is no credible evidence that properly designed, supervised, age-appropriate resistance training stunts growth; it is recognized as safe and beneficial for youth. The real risk to the epiphyseal (growth) plate comes from improper technique or maximal/excessive loading, not from resistance training per se. The trap first option repeats the persistent growth-stunting myth. The third option invents a free-weight prohibition that is not the issue - supervision and appropriate loading are.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"目前證據不支援「阻力訓練會壓矮個子」：設計得當、有監督、負荷符合年齡的兒童阻力訓練安全且有益。骨骺(epiphyseal plate)生長板的風險來自姿勢錯誤或過度大重量，不是訓練本身；問題也不在機械式還是自由重量，而在監督與負荷是否得當。"},{"id":"q0275","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When comparing average muscular strength between men and women, which statement most accurately reflects the textbook position?","options":["Men are stronger than women in both absolute terms and when strength is expressed relative to lean body mass, across all muscle groups equally","Women are stronger than men in absolute terms but weaker relative to lean body mass","On an absolute basis men are generally stronger, but when strength is expressed relative to lean body mass (especially lower body) the differences shrink markedly"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"On an absolute basis men are generally stronger, but when strength is expressed relative to lean body mass (especially lower body) the differences shrink markedly","explanation_en":"Men typically have greater ABSOLUTE strength largely due to greater muscle mass, but when strength is normalized to lean body mass the sex difference narrows considerably, and lower-body relative strength can be quite similar; upper-body differences tend to remain larger. The trap first option overstates the gap by claiming it persists equally relative to lean mass across all muscles - normalization reduces it. The third option is simply false on the absolute comparison.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"男性絕對力量較大肌群質量較大，絕對值比較較強；但強度若以瘦體重(normalize)表示，兩性差距明顯縮小，下肢相對力量尤其接近，上肢差距才較大。錯誤說法是宣稱差距在相對化之後仍然存在。"},{"id":"q0276","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During an open-skill play, a point guard dribbles up the court while simultaneously tracking five defenders, two cutting teammates, and the shot clock to decide where the play goes. According to Nideffer's model, which attentional style is this player primarily using?","options":["Broad-external","Broad-internal","Narrow-external"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Broad-external","explanation_en":"Broad-external = taking in MANY cues that exist OUT in the environment (defenders, teammates, clock), which is exactly what reading a developing play requires. Broad-internal is the trap: that style is for analyzing or strategizing using many of one's OWN thoughts/plans, not scanning the live environment. Narrow-external would be locking onto a single external target (like a free-throw rim).","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Nideffer 注意力模型中，廣度外部(broad-external)＝同時接收環境中多重的外部線索（防守者、隊友、計時器），正是解讀進攻時需要的注意方式。廣度內部是整理自己內在的想法與策略；狹窄外部是鎖定單一外部目標（如罰投籃框）。"},{"id":"q0277","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A golfer stands over a putt and concentrates exclusively on a single feel cue - the smooth tempo of her own backswing - shutting out everything else. Which attentional quadrant best describes this focus?","options":["Broad-internal","Narrow-internal","Narrow-external"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Narrow-internal","explanation_en":"Narrow-internal = focusing on ONE internal cue (a single swing thought / kinesthetic feel of her own movement). Narrow-external is the trap: that would be fixing on one cue out in the environment, such as a spot on the green or the hole - but tempo of her own backswing is an internal kinesthetic cue, not an environmental one. Broad-internal would involve juggling many of her own thoughts at once.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"狹窄內部(narrow-internal)＝專注在單一內線上索，此例是自己揮桿的節奏與本體感覺。陷阱選項狹窄外部指的是鎖定單一環境線索（例如果嶺上的一點）；節奏是身體內在的動作感覺，屬內部線索。"},{"id":"q0278","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A placekicker blocks out the crowd and rush and zeroes in solely on a single spot on the goalpost as his aiming point. Which attentional style is he using?","options":["Narrow-internal","Narrow-external","Broad-external"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Narrow-external","explanation_en":"Narrow-external = locking onto ONE cue that is OUT in the environment (the spot on the goalpost). The trap is narrow-internal, which would apply if he were focused on one of his own bodily/mental cues rather than an external target; the aiming spot is external. Broad-external would mean scanning many environmental cues at once, which he is deliberately avoiding.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"狹窄外部(narrow-external)＝鎖定單一的外部線索（球門柱上的瞄準點）。狹窄內部是專注在自己身體或內在的線索，而瞄準點在環境中；廣度外部則需同時掃描多個環境線索，正是他刻意排除的。"},{"id":"q0279","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A powerlifter must produce a maximal, simple deadlift, while a few platforms over a gymnast attempts a complex, precise beam routine. Compared to the powerlifter, the gymnast's optimal arousal level for peak performance should be:","options":["Higher, because more total muscle activation is needed","Lower, because the task is complex and requires fine motor control","Identical, because optimal arousal is the same for all athletes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Lower, because the task is complex and requires fine motor control","explanation_en":"Per the inverted-U principle, complex tasks demanding fine motor control and coordination (beam routine) have a LOWER optimal arousal level than simple, gross-force tasks (deadlift). The trap (higher arousal) confuses 'needs precision' with 'needs more drive'; high arousal degrades fine, complex skills. 'Identical for all' ignores that optimal arousal varies by task complexity (and by individual, per IZOF).","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"依倒 U(inverted-U) 原則，複雜、需要精細動作控制的任務（平衡木）最適喚醒程度比簡單、依賴肌力的任務（硬舉）低；高喚醒會破壞精細技能。「人人都一樣」忽略了最適喚醒隨任務複雜度與個人差異(IZOF)改變。"},{"id":"q0280","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 19-year-old female distance runner reports fatigue and heavy training volume. Of the following, which nutritional concern is MOST characteristically associated with female endurance athletes and warrants screening?","options":["Iron deficiency, which can impair oxygen transport and endurance performance","Vitamin C toxicity from too much fruit in the diet","Excess dietary protein causing kidney damage in healthy athletes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Iron deficiency, which can impair oxygen transport and endurance performance","explanation_en":"Iron deficiency is especially common in female endurance athletes (losses plus high demand) and impairs oxygen-carrying capacity, hurting endurance - the textbook flags it for screening. Vitamin C 'toxicity' from fruit is the trap: it is water-soluble and not a realistic concern here. Excess protein causing kidney damage in healthy athletes is a common myth, not an established textbook risk, and is unrelated to this presentation.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性耐力運動員特別容易缺鐵（流失較多加上需求高），會損害氧氣運輸與耐力表現，教科書特別點名要篩檢。維生素 C 是水溶性，吃水果不會中毒；「健康運動員蛋白質過傷腎」是迷思，與本情境也無關。"},{"id":"q0281","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A basketball player reports that for the first three quarters her heart was pounding and her muscles felt tense, but those physical symptoms faded once play settled in; meanwhile she kept worrying about disappointing her coach right through the final minutes. Which best characterizes her anxiety?","options":["Somatic anxiety that persisted and cognitive anxiety that dissipated","Somatic anxiety that dissipated at the start of play and cognitive anxiety that persisted","Trait anxiety, which is situation-specific and short-lived"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Somatic anxiety that dissipated at the start of play and cognitive anxiety that persisted","explanation_en":"Somatic (physical) anxiety - pounding heart, tense muscles - typically peaks pre-competition and dissipates once performance begins, while cognitive anxiety (worry) can persist throughout. Option A reverses the two (the classic trap). Trait anxiety is a stable personality disposition, not a short-lived, situation-specific state, so C mislabels both the type and its time course.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"軀體性焦慮(somatic anxiety)的心悸、肌肉緊繃通常在賽前達峰、比賽開始後緩解；認知性焦慮(cognitive anxiety，擔憂)則可能持續到最後一刻。陷阱選項把兩者對調；特質焦慮是穩定的人格傾向，不是短暫的情境狀態。"},{"id":"q0282","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete tells the strength coach his main aim this season is to 'win the conference championship.' To make the goal more effective, the coach should steer him toward which type of goal?","options":["A process goal he can control, such as completing his prescribed sprint mechanics drills each session","A more ambitious outcome goal, such as winning the national title","An outcome goal tied to beating a specific rival"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A process goal he can control, such as completing his prescribed sprint mechanics drills each session","explanation_en":"Process (and performance) goals focus on controllable actions the athlete executes, which is why they are emphasized over outcome goals. Winning a championship is an outcome goal - the LEAST controllable (depends on opponents, luck). Both B and C are traps because they are still outcome goals (just bigger or more specific); raising the stakes does not fix the core problem of low controllability.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過程目標(process goal)鎖定運動員自己能控制的執行動作（如每次完成衝刺力學練習），比結果目標有效；「奪冠」屬結果目標，可控性最低（受對手與運氣影響）。把結果目標改得更大或更具體，都解決不了可控性問題。"},{"id":"q0283","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A young athlete who used to train enthusiastically just for the love of the sport is now paid a cash bonus by a sponsor for every win. Over the season his enjoyment and self-driven effort decline. This illustrates that:","options":["Tangible extrinsic rewards can undermine intrinsic motivation","Extrinsic rewards always strengthen intrinsic motivation","Intrinsic and extrinsic motivation are unrelated and never interact"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Tangible extrinsic rewards can undermine intrinsic motivation","explanation_en":"Tangible extrinsic rewards (cash per win) can shift the athlete's perceived reason for participating from internal enjoyment to the reward, undermining intrinsic motivation - the documented effect here. 'Always strengthen' is the trap: rewards perceived as controlling often reduce, not boost, intrinsic drive. 'Never interact' is false because the whole point is that the two motivation types influence each other.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"具體的外部獎勵（每勝一場獎金）會把參加動機從內在興趣轉移到獎賞，反而侵蝕內在動機(intrinsic motivation)。被認為具控制性的獎勵常降低而非增強內在驅動力；兩種動機會互相影響，並非互不相干。"},{"id":"q0284","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to build a returning athlete's self-efficacy before a key competition. According to Bandura, which strategy will have the STRONGEST effect?","options":["Repeatedly telling the athlete 'I know you can do it' (verbal persuasion)","Structuring training so the athlete accumulates successful past performance accomplishments","Having the athlete watch a similar teammate succeed (vicarious experience)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Structuring training so the athlete accumulates successful past performance accomplishments","explanation_en":"Bandura ranks past performance accomplishments (mastery experiences) as the STRONGEST source of self-efficacy - actually succeeding builds the most durable confidence. Verbal persuasion is the classic trap: it is one of the WEAKER sources. Vicarious experience (modeling) helps but is weaker than one's own mastery, so B beats both alternatives.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Bandura 認為表現成就（成功經驗、mastery experience）是自我效能(self-efficacy)最強來源：實際成功建立的自信最穩固。言語勸說「你可以的」反而是較弱的來源；替代經驗（看隊友成功）有幫助但仍不及自身成就。"},{"id":"q0285","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A diver's body is calm but he is consumed by worrisome, negative thoughts about failing his next dive - a clear cognitive-anxiety problem. Which psychological technique is BEST matched to this type of anxiety?","options":["Progressive muscle relaxation to reduce muscular tension","Thought stopping and positive self-talk / imagery to address the worry","Deep diaphragmatic breathing to lower heart rate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Thought stopping and positive self-talk / imagery to address the worry","explanation_en":"Cognitive anxiety (worry, negative thoughts) is best treated with cognitive techniques like thought stopping, positive self-talk, and imagery. The trap answers (progressive muscle relaxation and breathing) are SOMATIC techniques - they target physical tension and are matched to somatic anxiety, not to a mind racing with worry. Matching the intervention to the anxiety type is the key principle.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"認知性焦慮（擔憂、負面想法）要對以認知技術：思考中止(thought stopping)、積極自我談話、意象訓練。漸進式肌肉放鬆與深呼吸屬軀體技術，對應的是軀體焦慮；關鍵原則是技術與焦慮型別要配對。"},{"id":"q0286","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sport dietitian needs to estimate daily energy needs for a very lean, muscular 80 kg male athlete with about 8 kg of fat mass. Which approach does the textbook favor for this athlete, and roughly what is the first step?","options":["Apply a flat 15-20 kcal per pound of body weight as the standard textbook method","Estimate resting metabolic rate with the Cunningham equation [500 + (22 x fat-free mass in kg)], then multiply by a physical activity level coefficient","Use total body weight in the Cunningham equation, ignoring body composition"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Estimate resting metabolic rate with the Cunningham equation [500 + (22 x fat-free mass in kg)], then multiply by a physical activity level coefficient","explanation_en":"The textbook estimates energy needs as RMR x a physical-activity (PAL) coefficient; the Cunningham equation - 500 + (22 x fat-free mass kg) - is preferred for lean, muscular athletes because it is driven by fat-free mass. The trap is the 'flat kcal per pound' table, which is not the RMR-times-activity method the book teaches. Using total body weight (C) defeats the purpose of an FFM-based equation.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書的做法是先估算休息代謝率 RMR 再乘身體活動係數(PAL)；對精瘦肌肉型運動員建議用 Cunningham 方程式 500 + 22 × 去脂體重(kg)，因為它以去脂體重(FFM)為輸入。直接套「每磅固定 kcal」表不是本書方法；用體重代 Cunningham 則失去 FFM 型方程式的意義。"},{"id":"q0287","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength athlete already eating about 1.6 g of protein per kg of body weight asks whether doubling his protein to 3.2 g/kg will add proportionally more muscle. The best evidence-based answer is:","options":["Yes - muscle gain increases roughly linearly with protein intake, so more protein means more muscle","No - athlete protein needs fall in roughly the 1.2 to 2.0 g/kg range (strength athletes toward the upper end), and intakes well above that do not produce proportionally more muscle","No - because excess protein is toxic and he should drop below 1.0 g/kg"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"No - athlete protein needs fall in roughly the 1.2 to 2.0 g/kg range (strength athletes toward the upper end), and intakes well above that do not produce proportionally more muscle","explanation_en":"The 5th edition recommends roughly 1.2 to 2.0 g/kg of protein depending on the sport and training program, with strength/power athletes typically toward the upper end (about 1.5 to 2.0 g/kg). At 1.6 g/kg he is already within the recommended range, so once needs are met more protein does not build proportionally more muscle (training stimulus and total energy/carbohydrate matter). 'More protein = more muscle' is the linear trap. Option C overcorrects with a false toxicity claim and a sub-need recommendation.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動員蛋白質建議量約 1.2–2.0 g/kg/日，力量型位於高段（約 1.5–2.0）；他已在 1.6 g/kg 達建議範圍，再加倍不會等比例增肌，因為訓練刺激與總熱量、攝取碳水化合物才是關鍵。「多吃蛋白就多長肌肉」是直線式陷阱；說蛋白中毒要降到 1.0 以下則糾枉過正。"},{"id":"q0288","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An endurance athlete finishes a depleting two-hour session and wants to maximize muscle glycogen resynthesis. Which post-exercise carbohydrate strategy is best supported?","options":["Consume high-glycemic-index carbohydrate soon after exercise","Consume low-glycemic-index carbohydrate and delay intake several hours to 'spread out' refueling","Avoid carbohydrate and rely on protein alone to rebuild glycogen"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Consume high-glycemic-index carbohydrate soon after exercise","explanation_en":"High-glycemic-index carbohydrate soon after exercise speeds glycogen resynthesis by driving a rapid glucose/insulin response when muscle is most receptive. The trap (low-GI plus delay) slows refueling and wastes the window of elevated glycogen-storage capacity. Protein alone (C) cannot replace the carbohydrate that glycogen is built from, though some protein with carbohydrate can help.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動後盡快攝取高血糖指數(high-GI) 碳水，能利用肌肉最「想吃」醣原的視窗，快速推升血糖與胰島素反應、加速肌醣原再合成。低 GI 加上延遲攝取會浪費這個高醣原合成視窗；只靠蛋白質無法提供合成醣原所需的碳水。"},{"id":"q0289","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach insists athletes only need to drink 'when they feel thirsty' and that a couple percent of body-weight loss is harmless. Which statement most accurately corrects this?","options":["Thirst is a reliable real-time gauge, so drinking only to thirst fully prevents performance loss","Thirst lags behind actual fluid deficit, and a loss of roughly 2% of body weight can already impair performance","Athletes should drink as much plain water as possible at all times to stay maximally safe"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Thirst lags behind actual fluid deficit, and a loss of roughly 2% of body weight can already impair performance","explanation_en":"Thirst lags behind the body's actual fluid deficit, and about a 2% body-weight loss can already impair performance - so waiting for thirst can leave an athlete behind. Option A is the trap that the coach is repeating (thirst as a reliable gauge). Option C is the opposite error: forcing excessive plain water can cause hyponatremia (dangerously low blood sodium), so 'as much as possible' is wrong too.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"口渴感落後於實際缺水量，體重流失約 2% 時表現已經受損，只「口渴才喝」會一直落後。另一個極端是拼命灌白水，可能導致低血鈉(hyponatremia)，所以「越多越好」也錯。"},{"id":"q0290","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach is hired to build a resistance-training program for a college lacrosse team. Before writing any sets or reps, what should be his FIRST step?","options":["Select the core and assistance exercises that match lacrosse movements","Conduct a needs analysis evaluating the sport's demands and assessing the athletes","Assign training loads based on each athlete's predicted 1RM"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Conduct a needs analysis evaluating the sport's demands and assessing the athletes","explanation_en":"Per the program-design sequence, the needs analysis (evaluation of the sport plus athlete assessment) ALWAYS comes first; exercise selection, frequency, order, load/reps, volume, and rest all follow from it. Selecting exercises or assigning loads first is the classic trap of skipping the foundational analysis that should drive every later variable.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"課表設計第一步永遠是需求分析(needs analysis)：評估專項需求與檢測運動員，動作選擇、頻率、順序、負荷／次數、訓練量、休息都隨後決定。直接挑動作或先排強度，是跳過基礎分析經典錯誤。"},{"id":"q0291","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A volleyball middle blocker wants to improve her ability to spike with more force. Which trained quality most directly maps to this demand?","options":["Upper-body power and explosive strength","Aerobic capacity to sustain long rallies","Lower-body muscular endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Upper-body power and explosive strength","explanation_en":"Spiking is a brief, explosive, anaerobic action driven by upper-body power, so training should target that quality. Aerobic capacity is the classic distractor for a power/court sport; volleyball is anaerobic and intermittent, not endurance-limited, so the aerobic option does not map to the demand.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"扣球是短暫、爆發性的無氧動作，依賴上肢 power 與爆發力，訓練就要對應這個素質。有氧能力是球類運動的經典幹擾選項：排球屬間歇無氧，不受耐力限制。"},{"id":"q0292","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sprinter has built a strong acceleration phase using resisted sled towing. Following the speed-development continuum, what is the appropriate NEXT method to develop maximum velocity?","options":["Heavier sled loads that slow him by roughly 25 percent to overload force","Assisted (overspeed) sprinting, used cautiously for an advanced athlete","Continuous tempo runs at lactate threshold pace"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Assisted (overspeed) sprinting, used cautiously for an advanced athlete","explanation_en":"The continuum runs resisted to normal to assisted (overspeed); after resisted acceleration work, max-velocity development uses assisted/overspeed methods. The 5th ed is skeptical of overspeed (limited research, overstriding risk) and reserves it for advanced/elite athletes, which the correct option reflects. The heavy-sled option is a trap: loads causing large velocity loss (well over ~10 percent) degrade sprint mechanics; tempo runs train a different energy system entirely.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"速度發展連續體是阻力式→常規→輔助式(overspeed)；做完阻力雪橇加速訓練後，下一步發展最大速度用輔助／超速式，第5版對其態度保留（研究有限、有過度步頻風險），僅進階運動員謹慎使用。造成速度掉超過約 10% 的重雪橇會破壞衝刺力學；節奏跑訓練的是另一套能量系統。"},{"id":"q0293","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants an interval (HIIT) session that develops maximal aerobic power. What work intensity best fits the interval method?","options":["About 70 percent of VO2max sustained continuously","About 85 percent of VO2max held at a steady pace","At or above 90 percent of VO2max during the work bouts"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"At or above 90 percent of VO2max during the work bouts","explanation_en":"Interval/HIIT training targets intensities at or above ~90 percent of VO2max during work bouts to stress maximal aerobic power. The 85 percent option is the trap: that band corresponds to threshold/tempo (pace/tempo) work, not true interval intensity. 70 percent is long slow distance.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"間歇訓練(HIIT) 的工作強度落在 VO2max 的 90% 以上，才能刺激最大有氧功率；約 85% 對應閾值／節奏跑(range/tempo) 區間，70% 則是長距離慢跑(LSD)。"},{"id":"q0294","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 1500 m runner needs a session that raises the velocity she can hold at her lactate threshold. Which prescription fits?","options":["Tempo/pace runs performed right at lactate threshold (around maximal lactate steady state)","Repeated short sprints at or above 90 percent of VO2max","Easy continuous running near 70 percent of VO2max"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Tempo/pace runs performed right at lactate threshold (around maximal lactate steady state)","explanation_en":"Pace/tempo training is performed at an intensity equal to the lactate threshold (about the maximal lactate steady state) to push that threshold velocity higher. The >=90 percent VO2max option is interval work (different aim), and easy continuous running at ~70 percent is LSD, which is below the threshold the athlete is trying to improve.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"節奏／配速訓練(pace/tempo)落在乳酸閾（約最大乳酸穩定狀態 MLSS）的強度，能推高閾值速度，正好對應 1500 m 選手需求；90% 以上 VO2max 屬間歇（目的不同），約 70% 輕鬆連續跑是低於目標閾值的 LSD。"},{"id":"q0295","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is doing phosphagen-system intervals: maximal 8 to 10 second sprints to develop short-burst power. Which work-to-rest ratio is appropriate?","options":["1:3","1:5","1:12 to 1:20"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:12 to 1:20","explanation_en":"Phosphagen-system training uses very short maximal efforts with long recovery, roughly a 1:12 to 1:20 work-to-rest ratio, to allow near-full ATP-PCr replenishment. The 1:3 and 1:5 ratios are glycolytic-system prescriptions; using them here would not allow adequate recovery for repeated maximal sprints.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸系統(phosphagen)訓練＝極短最大努力搭配長恢復，work:rest 約 1:12–1:20，讓 ATP-PCr 接近完全再填補。1:3、1:5 是糖解系統的配比，用在重複衝最大速度會恢復不足。"},{"id":"q0296","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A powerlifter's goal this block is maximal strength. Which load, rep, and rest combination fits?","options":[">=85 percent 1RM, <=6 reps, with 30 to 60 seconds rest between sets",">=85 percent 1RM, <=6 reps, with 2 to 5 minutes rest between sets","67 to 85 percent 1RM, 6 to 12 reps, with 2 to 5 minutes rest between sets"],"answer":1,"answer_text":">=85 percent 1RM, <=6 reps, with 2 to 5 minutes rest between sets","explanation_en":"Maximal strength training uses >=85 percent 1RM for <=6 reps with long, 2 to 5 minute rest periods to allow near-complete recovery between heavy sets. The first option is the trap: it pairs heavy strength loading with short (30 to 60 s) rest, which is a hypertrophy/endurance rest scheme and undercuts maximal-strength performance. The third option is a hypertrophy load/rep prescription.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大力量訓練：強度 ≥85% 1RM、次數 ≤6、組間休息 2–5 分鐘以接近完全恢復。把大重量配 30–60 秒短休的是肥大／肌耐力休息方案，會拖累最大力量表現；67–85% 1RM、6–12 次則是肥大處方。"},{"id":"q0297","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach prescribes a multiple-effort power exercise (e.g., power cleans for several reps) for an explosive athlete. Which loading is appropriate?","options":["75 to 85 percent 1RM for 1 to 5 reps with 2 to 5 minutes rest","67 to 85 percent 1RM for 8 to 12 reps with 60 seconds rest","=12 reps with <=30 seconds rest"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"75 to 85 percent 1RM for 1 to 5 reps with 2 to 5 minutes rest","explanation_en":"For multiple-effort power events, the textbook recommends about 75 to 85 percent 1RM for 1 to 5 reps with full 2 to 5 minute recovery so each rep is explosive. The second option is a hypertrophy scheme and the third is muscular-endurance loading; both use rep ranges and rest periods that would compromise power output.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多次數(power reps) 式爆發力練習建議約 75–85% 1RM、1–5 次、休息 2–5 分鐘，讓每一個都能維持爆發輸出。8–12 次配 60 秒屬肥大方案、高 reps 配超短休息屬肌耐力，都會犧牲功率輸出。"},{"id":"q0298","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A novice is being introduced to depth jumps for the first time. Which choice reflects correct plyometric programming?","options":["Start with a 40 in box because a higher drop produces a greater stretch reflex","Use a box around 12 to 24 in and ensure the athlete has an adequate lower-body strength base first","Program depth jumps on consecutive days to accelerate adaptation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Use a box around 12 to 24 in and ensure the athlete has an adequate lower-body strength base first","explanation_en":"For a novice, depth-jump box heights start in the range of about 12 to 24 in, and the athlete should have an adequate lower-body strength base before high-intensity lower-body plyometrics. The 40 in box is the extreme-number trap: too-high boxes lengthen ground contact and the amortization phase, reducing the stretch-shortening benefit and raising injury risk. Plyometrics for the same area should not be done on consecutive days.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新手的深跳(depth jump)箱高從約 12–24 吋起，且必須先具備足夠下肢肌力基礎。40 吋屬極端值陷阱：箱太高會拉長接地與緩衝(amortization)時間、削弱伸展-縮短迴圈(SSC)效果並增加受傷風險；同部位的增強式訓練也不該連續天進行。"},{"id":"q0299","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a depth jump, an athlete spends a long time on the ground absorbing the landing before jumping. Why does this reduce the training effect?","options":["A prolonged amortization phase dissipates stored elastic energy and weakens the stretch-shortening cycle","Longer ground contact recruits more slow-twitch fibers, which improves power","It shifts the exercise to the concentric-only category, which is more effective"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A prolonged amortization phase dissipates stored elastic energy and weakens the stretch-shortening cycle","explanation_en":"The amortization (transition) phase between the eccentric and concentric phases should be SHORT; a long amortization phase lets stored elastic energy dissipate and diminishes the stretch-shortening-cycle contribution to the subsequent jump. Longer contact does not preferentially help power, and the movement remains a full SSC action, not concentric-only.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"緩衝期(amortization phase)是離心轉向心的轉換階段，越短越好；在地上停留太久，儲存的彈性位能會消散，SSC 對之後跳躍的貢獻也跟著變弱。接觸時間長並不會較有助爆發力，動作也仍是完整的 SSC 動作。"},{"id":"q0300","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach wants to develop a basketball guard's ability to plant and change direction in response to an opponent. Which best describes the quality being trained?","options":["Pure linear sprint speed over 40 yards","Agility, which combines change of direction with a reactive/cognitive component","Aerobic capacity for repeated efforts"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Agility, which combines change of direction with a reactive/cognitive component","explanation_en":"Agility is defined as a rapid whole-body change of direction or velocity in response to a stimulus, so it includes both the change-of-direction mechanics and a reactive/cognitive (perceptual decision-making) component. Linear sprint speed lacks the directional-change and reactive elements, and aerobic capacity is unrelated to this specific skill.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"敏捷性(agility)定義是身體依刺激快速改變方向或速度，同時包含改變方向的力學與反應／認知（知覺決策）成分。直線衝刺少了變向與反應；有氧能力與這個專項技能無關。"},{"id":"q0301","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach builds a drill to transfer to a tennis player's wide defensive get: a fast, low, wide drop to the side to return a ball hit well away from the body. Which resistance-training movement pattern best transfers to this action?","options":["Standing barbell biceps curl for grip and arm strength","Lateral lunge / wide low squatting pattern to train the low, wide, decelerating drop to the side","Seated calf raise for ankle strength"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Lateral lunge / wide low squatting pattern to train the low, wide, decelerating drop to the side","explanation_en":"The wide defensive get is a fast, low, wide, decelerating drop to the side, so the lateral lunge / wide squatting pattern best matches the movement. The trap is matching by body part instead of by movement pattern: a biceps curl uses the arms but not the low, wide, decelerating lower-body pattern, and a seated calf raise is non-specific to the action.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"轉移要看動作型而不只是身體部位：大範圍防守救球是快速、低姿、寬幅、側向的減速下落，與側弓步／寬幅深蹲型最吻合。二頭彎舉、坐姿小腿抬舉屬「以部位配動作」的陷阱，專項度低。"},{"id":"q0302","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In classic (linear) periodization, how do training volume and intensity trend as an athlete moves from the hypertrophy phase toward the peaking/competition phase?","options":["Volume decreases while intensity increases","Both volume and intensity increase together","Volume increases while intensity decreases"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Volume decreases while intensity increases","explanation_en":"Classic linear periodization progresses hypertrophy to strength to power to peaking, with volume decreasing and intensity increasing across the phases. The trap is 'both increase together', which is not how the model works and would invite overtraining; option three reverses the correct trend.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"經典線性週期化從肥大期走向基礎力量、力量／爆發力、再到巔峰期，訓練量逐段下降、強度逐段上升。「兩者一起增」不符合模型邏輯（容易過度訓練）；「量增、強度減」則說反了。"},{"id":"q0303","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which sequence of phases correctly reflects classic linear periodization for a strength/power athlete across a macrocycle?","options":["Hypertrophy/endurance, then basic strength, then strength/power, then peaking","Peaking, then strength/power, then hypertrophy, then basic strength","Basic strength, then hypertrophy, then peaking, then strength/power"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hypertrophy/endurance, then basic strength, then strength/power, then peaking","explanation_en":"The classic model sequences a high-volume hypertrophy/endurance phase, then a basic strength phase, then a strength/power phase, then a peaking (competition) phase. The other two scramble the order; for example, starting with peaking or placing hypertrophy after strength contradicts the high-volume-to-high-intensity logic of the model.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"經典線性週期化的正確順序：肥大／肌耐力 → 基礎力量 → 力量／爆發力 → 巔峰(比賽)期。其他排列把高量到高強度的推進邏輯搞亂了（例如以巔峰開頭或把肥大放在力量之後）。"},{"id":"q0304","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach describes the largest division of his periodization plan, which spans the athlete's full competitive year. Which term applies?","options":["Microcycle","Mesocycle","Macrocycle"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Macrocycle","explanation_en":"The macrocycle is the largest division, typically an entire training year (or up to several years), composed of mesocycles (often weeks to months) and microcycles (often about a week). Microcycle and mesocycle are smaller subdivisions, so neither describes the full-year plan.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大週期(macrocycle)是最大週期化單位，通常是完整訓練年（甚至數年），由中週期(mesocycle，數週至數月)與小週期(microcycle，通常約一週)組成。"},{"id":"q0305","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a daily undulating periodization week, an athlete trains heavy strength on Monday, power on Wednesday, and hypertrophy on Friday. What distinguishes this from classic linear periodization?","options":["Volume and intensity are varied within the same week rather than held to one emphasis per multi-week block","It always increases both volume and intensity every session","It eliminates the needs analysis because emphasis changes daily"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Volume and intensity are varied within the same week rather than held to one emphasis per multi-week block","explanation_en":"Undulating (nonlinear) periodization varies volume and intensity frequently, even within a single week, instead of holding one emphasis for a multi-week block as classic linear does. It does not increase both volume and intensity each session, and the needs analysis is always required regardless of periodization model.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每日undulating(非線性)週期化在同一週內就變化訓練量與強度（週一重力量、週三爆發力、週五肥大），不像經典線性那樣以數週區塊維持單一主軸。它不是每次都要量與強度都增；需求分析不管哪種模型都照樣要。"},{"id":"q0306","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A team-sport athlete enters the in-season. How should the resistance-training emphasis typically shift compared with the off-season?","options":["Increase volume sharply to keep building work capacity during competition","Reduce training volume and emphasize maintenance of strength/power around competition demands","Stop resistance training entirely to avoid any fatigue"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Reduce training volume and emphasize maintenance of strength/power around competition demands","explanation_en":"In-season programming generally reduces volume and shifts toward maintaining strength and power while managing competition fatigue. Sharply increasing volume in-season risks interfering with performance/recovery, and stopping resistance training entirely leads to detraining and loss of the adaptations built off-season.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"賽季中訓練通常下修訓練量、主軸轉為在比賽疲勞下維持力量與爆發力。賽季中猛增量會幹擾表現與恢復；完全停練則會去訓練化(detraining)，流失休賽期建立的適應。"},{"id":"q0307","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete completely stops resistance training for several weeks during a layoff. Which outcome best reflects detraining?","options":["Strength and power adaptations are gradually lost, with reversal of training-specific gains","Adaptations are permanent, so a few weeks off causes no measurable change","Detraining only affects aerobic capacity, never strength"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Strength and power adaptations are gradually lost, with reversal of training-specific gains","explanation_en":"Detraining is the partial or complete loss of training-induced adaptations when the stimulus is removed; strength and power gains regress over time without training. Adaptations are not permanent, and detraining affects strength and power as well as aerobic qualities, so the other options are false.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"去訓練化(detraining)指移除訓練刺激後，訓練造成的適應部分或全部流失；力量與爆發力會隨停訓逐漸回退。適應不是永久的，去訓練化也不只影響有氧，力量與爆發力一樣會退。"},{"id":"q0308","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Watch a lat pulldown: the lifter sits with thighs secured, grips the bar wider than shoulder width with a pronated grip, leans the torso back slightly, and pulls. Where should the bar finish for a correct front pulldown?","options":["To the upper chest near the clavicle, with a slight backward torso lean","Down to the mid or lower chest by pulling the elbows far behind the body","Behind the neck to the base of the skull"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"To the upper chest near the clavicle, with a slight backward torso lean","explanation_en":"In a front lat pulldown the bar is pulled to the upper chest/clavicle with a slight backward lean of the torso. Pulling to the mid/lower chest is the trap: that turns the movement into a row and changes the muscle action. The behind-the-neck variation places the shoulder in a higher-risk position and is not the recommended technique.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"正面滑輪下拉(front lat pulldown)要把橫桿拉到胸前上方／鎖骨位置，軀幹略向後傾。拉到中下胸會把動作變成划船、改變肌肉作用；頸後下拉讓肩處於風險較高位置，不是建議技術。"},{"id":"q0309","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete performs a forward step lunge. Which observation indicates CORRECT technique rather than a fault?","options":["The lead knee travels well past the toes as the athlete drops deep","The trailing knee descends to about 1 to 2 inches above the floor and does not touch down","The torso bends sharply forward over the lead thigh"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The trailing knee descends to about 1 to 2 inches above the floor and does not touch down","explanation_en":"In a proper forward step lunge the trailing knee lowers to roughly 1 to 2 inches (3 to 5 cm) above the floor without touching, the lead knee stays over (not past) the toes, and the torso remains erect. The lead knee passing beyond the toes and a sharply flexed torso are both technique faults, not correct execution.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"正確前向弓步：後側膝蓋下降到離地約 1–2 吋(3–5 cm) 不碰地、前側膝保持在腳踝上方不超過腳尖、軀幹保持直立。前膝超過腳尖與軀幹前傾都是錯誤，不是正確動作。"},{"id":"q0310","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strongman athlete is performing tire flips. Which of the following is a genuine technique FAULT to correct?","options":["Feet placed close to the tire in a sumo or backlift stance","Hips rising too early so the lift becomes a biceps-style curl/pull rather than a forward drive","Driving the body forward into the tire as the hips and knees extend"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Hips rising too early so the lift becomes a biceps-style curl/pull rather than a forward drive","explanation_en":"A real tire-flip fault is letting the hips rise too high so the athlete tries to curl/lift the tire with the arms instead of driving the whole body forward into it. Feet close to the tire (sumo or backlift) is correct, and driving forward through hip and knee extension is the proper action. The bait answer (not shown here) is moving the feet far back; the close stance is actually correct.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"翻輪胎真正的錯誤是臀部過早抬起，變成用手臂二頭肌式地「撈」輪胎，而不是讓全身往前推進。雙腳貼近輪胎（相撲或背舉站姿）與透過伸髖伸膝把身體往前頂都是正確技術；「腳離太遠」才是錯誤但這裡沒出現。"},{"id":"q0311","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A video shows an athlete controlling the downward (descent) phase of a back squat at a steady tempo. During this lowering phase, how are the knee and hip extensors (quadriceps and gluteals) primarily acting?","options":["Concentrically, because they are the prime movers of the squat","Eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the descent against gravity","Isometrically, because the bar is moving at a constant speed"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the descent against gravity","explanation_en":"Lowering against gravity is the eccentric phase: the same muscles that extend the knees and hips (quads, glutes) lengthen under load to brake the descent, so they contract eccentrically. They act concentrically only on the way up. A constant bar speed does not make the action isometric, because the joints are still moving and the muscles are lengthening.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"深蹲下降階段是離心：伸膝與伸髖肌（股四頭肌、臀肌）在載重下拉長、做離心收縮來煞車、對抗重力控制下落。向心收縮只發生在起身階段；槓鈴速度恆定不等於等長，因為關節仍在動、肌肉正在拉長。"},{"id":"q0312","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a standing barbell biceps curl, the athlete slowly lowers the bar from the top under control. Which muscle action is occurring at the elbow flexors during this lowering?","options":["The elbow flexors (biceps) contract eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the descent","The triceps contract concentrically to pull the bar down","The biceps contract concentrically to lower the bar"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The elbow flexors (biceps) contract eccentrically, lengthening under load to control the descent","explanation_en":"Lowering the curl is the eccentric phase of the biceps' action: the elbow flexors lengthen under load while still generating force to control the descent against gravity. The triceps are not the muscle controlling the load here (gravity lowers the bar; the biceps brake it), and a concentric biceps action would raise, not lower, the bar.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"彎舉緩放階段是肘屈肌的離心動作：二頭肌在載重下拉長的同時仍出力，控制下降速度。是重力把槓鈴放下、二頭肌踩煞車，不是三頭肌向心「把槓鈴拉下來」；二頭肌向心會把槓鈴舉起而非放下。"},{"id":"q0313","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While teaching the power clean, a coach watches the second pull. Which is a common technique FAULT to correct?","options":["Aggressive triple extension of the ankles, knees, and hips","Pulling early with the arms before the lower body has finished extending","Keeping the bar close to the body throughout the pull"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Pulling early with the arms before the lower body has finished extending","explanation_en":"A classic Olympic-lift fault is bending/pulling with the arms too early, before the explosive triple extension (ankle, knee, hip) is complete; the arms should stay relatively straight until the lower body finishes driving. Triple extension and keeping the bar close to the body are correct cues, not faults.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第二拉常見錯誤是手臂過早發力：下半身三重伸展（踝、膝、髖）還沒完成就屈臂拉槓；手臂應保持較直，等下肢結束驅動。三重伸展、槓貼身都是正確提示，不是錯誤。"},{"id":"q0314","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the main difference in the starting position between a power clean and a hang clean?","options":["The power clean starts with the bar on the floor; the hang clean starts from a standing position with the bar at roughly mid-thigh to knee level","The hang clean starts on the floor while the power clean starts from the hang","There is no difference; the names are interchangeable"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The power clean starts with the bar on the floor; the hang clean starts from a standing position with the bar at roughly mid-thigh to knee level","explanation_en":"A power clean starts with the bar on the floor, while a hang clean begins from a hang (standing) position with the bar around mid-thigh to knee level. Option two reverses the two starts, and the lifts are not interchangeable because the starting position changes the portions of the pull that are trained.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Power clean 槓鈴從地板起；hang clean 由站姿懸垂(hang)開始，槓鈴約在大腿中段到膝蓋高度。兩者不可互換，因為起始位置決定訓練到拉的哪一段。"},{"id":"q0315","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is deciding how to safeguard athletes during lifts. Which decision reflects correct spotting practice?","options":["Station a spotter to catch the bar during the catch of a power clean","Spot the barbell back squat and overhead press, but do not spot Olympic lifts","Avoid spotting the bench press because the lifter can always rack it alone"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Spot the barbell back squat and overhead press, but do not spot Olympic lifts","explanation_en":"Spotting is appropriate for free-weight exercises performed over the head or over the body (bench press, overhead press, back squat), but Olympic lifts should NOT be spotted because the safest response is for the lifter to drop/dump the bar. Spotting a power clean is the trap. The bench press is exactly the kind of over-the-body lift that does warrant a spotter.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"保護 spotting 適用於在頭部上方或軀幹上方的自由重量動作（仰臥推舉、過頭推、背蹲）；奧式舉重不該有人保護，因為最安全的應對是把槓鈴「丟掉」(dump)。幫 power clean 扶槓是陷阱；仰臥推恰恰就是需要保護的軀幹上方動作。"},{"id":"q0316","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete sets up for a heavy barbell bench press. Which describes the correct five-point body-contact position?","options":["Head, shoulders/upper back, and buttocks on the bench, with both feet flat on the floor","Head and buttocks on the bench, with both feet pulled up onto the bench for core tension","Shoulders and buttocks on the bench, with the head lifted to watch the bar"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Head, shoulders/upper back, and buttocks on the bench, with both feet flat on the floor","explanation_en":"The five points of contact for the bench press are the head, the shoulders/upper back, and the buttocks all on the bench, plus both feet flat on the floor. Putting the feet on the bench removes a stable base and two contact points, and lifting the head off the bench breaks the head contact point; both are unsafe deviations.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"仰臥推的五點接觸＝頭、雙肩／上背、臀部貼凳，加雙腳平踩地板。腳放到凳上會失去穩定基礎和兩個接觸點；頭離凳同樣破壞五點接觸，兩者都不安全。"},{"id":"q0317","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An experienced lifter is grinding through the hardest part (sticking point) of a near-maximal squat. What is the correct guidance on breathing?","options":["Exhale fully throughout the entire ascent to keep airway pressure low","A brief Valsalva maneuver through the sticking point is acceptable for experienced lifters","Hold the breath for the entire set across all reps regardless of experience"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A brief Valsalva maneuver through the sticking point is acceptable for experienced lifters","explanation_en":"For experienced, healthy lifters the textbook permits a brief Valsalva maneuver through the most stressful sticking point to stabilize the trunk, after which breathing resumes. Forcing a full exhale through the sticking point reduces trunk stability, and holding the breath for an entire multi-rep set (or recommending Valsalva for everyone regardless of experience) is not advised due to the blood-pressure spike.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書允許有經驗、健康的大重量訓練者在最吃力的黏滯點(sticking point)短暫使用 Valsalva 以穩定軀幹，之後恢復呼吸。全程吐氣會降低軀幹穩定；一口氣憋完整組對血壓衝擊大，不建議不顧經驗地推給所有人。"},{"id":"q0318","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a heavy back squat, a coach sees the athlete's knees collapse inward as he stands up. What is this fault and the appropriate correction?","options":["Knee valgus; cue the athlete to push the knees out in line with the toes","Correct depth; no change needed because deeper squats are always safer","Heel rise; cue him to come up onto the balls of the feet"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Knee valgus; cue the athlete to push the knees out in line with the toes","explanation_en":"Knees caving inward is knee valgus, a fault corrected by cueing the athlete to drive the knees out so they track over the toes. It is not a desirable depth cue, and the described problem is medial knee collapse, not heel rise; coming onto the balls of the feet would itself be a separate fault (heels should stay flat).","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"膝內夾是膝外翻(knee valgus)，糾錯提示是主動把膝蓋往外推、讓膝沿腳尖方向(track over toes)執行。這不是深度問題；腳跟離地是另一種錯誤（腳跟應保持踩實）。"},{"id":"q0319","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Preseason testing shows a college sprinter has well-above-average hamstring flexibility, but single-leg testing reveals his left knee extensors produce about 20 percent less force than his right. What should the offseason priority be?","options":["More static stretching of both hamstrings to capitalize on his mobility","Unilateral strengthening focused on the weaker (left) leg to reduce the bilateral asymmetry","Maximal bilateral squatting only, since overall strength will even the legs out"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Unilateral strengthening focused on the weaker (left) leg to reduce the bilateral asymmetry","explanation_en":"A bilateral strength asymmetry beyond roughly 10 to 15 percent is generally considered an injury-risk concern, so the priority is unilateral (single-leg) work to bring the weaker left leg up and close the gap. The excellent flexibility is a decoy - he is already mobile, so more stretching does not address the asymmetry. Bilateral-only squatting (option C) lets the stronger leg dominate and can preserve or widen the imbalance.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩側肌力不對稱超過約10–15%通常被視為受傷風險疑慮，所以休賽季優先做單側訓練補強較弱的左腳、把差距收小。膕旁肌柔軟度很好是幹擾資訊（他已足夠活動度）；只做雙側蹲會讓強側代償，可能維持甚至擴大不對稱。"},{"id":"q0320","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach wants the preseason testing battery to be REPEATABLE so pre/post scores can be compared. Which factor most directly protects reliability?","options":["Administering the entire battery on the same calendar day each session","Using a fixed, consistent test order with identical conditions, equipment, tester, and warm-up","Choosing tests that clearly measure the targeted athletic quality"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Using a fixed, consistent test order with identical conditions, equipment, tester, and warm-up","explanation_en":"Reliability is consistency of measurement, achieved by standardizing everything, and a consistent TEST ORDER is the key piece because earlier tests fatigue later ones. 'Same calendar day' is the trap: the day of the week is irrelevant; standardized conditions and sequence are what matter. Choosing a test that measures the right quality is VALIDITY, a different property.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"信度(reliability)指量測一致性，靠固定測試順序與一致的條件、器材、測驗者、暖身來達成；測試順序尤其關鍵，因為前面的測試會疲勞化後面的。「同一日曆日」與信度無關；「測到該測的品質」是效度(validity)，是另一種屬性。"},{"id":"q0321","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach must sequence five tests in one session: T-test (agility), 1RM back squat, vertical jump, 1.5-mile run, and a 60-second push-up test. Which order best preserves valid results?","options":["T-test, vertical jump, 1RM squat, push-up test, 1.5-mile run","1.5-mile run, 1RM squat, vertical jump, T-test, push-up test","1RM squat, vertical jump, push-up test, T-test, 1.5-mile run"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"T-test, vertical jump, 1RM squat, push-up test, 1.5-mile run","explanation_en":"Correct order is non-fatiguing/agility tests first, then max power and strength, then muscular endurance, then anaerobic/aerobic capacity LAST: vertical jump (power) and T-test (agility) before the 1RM, with the exhausting 1.5-mile aerobic run dead last. Starting with the 1.5-mile run (option B) or burying agility after a 1RM and endurance work (option C) lets earlier fatigue corrupt the power/agility scores.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"測試排序原則：不造成疲勞的敏捷與功率測試在前，其次最大力量、肌耐力，最後才是需氧能力——所以T-test、垂直跳、1RM深蹲、伏地挺身測試、1.5英里跑排最後。先跑完1.5英里或把敏捷排在1RM之後，疲勞會汙染功率與敏捷成績。"},{"id":"q0322","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete completes a 12-minute run test, covering 2.75 miles while alternating jogging and walking. How should this performance be scored?","options":["The pace per mile, penalized for the walking intervals","The split time at the 1.5-mile mark","The total distance covered in the 12 minutes (2.75 miles)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The total distance covered in the 12 minutes (2.75 miles)","explanation_en":"A 12-minute run is a fixed-TIME test scored by total DISTANCE covered, and walking is permitted as long as the athlete keeps moving. The pace and 1.5-mile split distractors confuse it with a fixed-distance test (like the 1.5-mile run, scored by TIME). Distance tests score distance; time tests score time.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"12分鐘跑是固定時間測驗，計12分鐘內跑的總距離（2.75英里），可走但必須持續移動。每英里配速與1.5英里分段是固定距離測驗的計分概念：距離測驗計距離、時間測驗計時間。"},{"id":"q0323","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 40-year-old client has a resting heart rate of 70 bpm. Using the Karvonen heart-rate-reserve method at 60 percent intensity, what is the target training heart rate? (Use 220 minus age for HRmax.)","options":["108 bpm","136 bpm","120 bpm"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"136 bpm","explanation_en":"Karvonen: Target HR = [(HRmax - HRrest) x intensity] + HRrest. HRmax = 220 - 40 = 180; HRR = 180 - 70 = 110; 110 x 0.60 = 66; 66 + 70 (resting) = 136 bpm. The 108 trap is plain 60 percent of HRmax (180 x 0.6) with no HRR; the 120 trap forgets to add back resting HR at the end. The '+ HRrest' is the step people drop.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Karvonen公式：目標心率=(HRmax−安靜心率)×強度＋安靜心率。HRmax=220−40=180；(180−70)×0.60=66；66+70=136 bpm。108的陷阱是直接取HRmax的60%，120的陷阱是忘記最後把安靜心率加回來。"},{"id":"q0324","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach takes an athlete's skinfolds and uses a regression equation that returns a body-fat estimate of 12 percent. Given how skinfold-based body-fat estimates work, how should the result be reported?","options":["As a range (for example about 9 to 15 percent), because the standard error of the estimate for skinfold equations is roughly plus or minus 3 to 5 percent","As exactly 12.0 percent, because calipers measure body fat directly and precisely","As a single error-free lean-body-mass number, because the prediction equation removes measurement error"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"As a range (for example about 9 to 15 percent), because the standard error of the estimate for skinfold equations is roughly plus or minus 3 to 5 percent","explanation_en":"Skinfold prediction equations carry a standard error of the estimate of roughly plus or minus 3 to 5 percent, so the honest practice is to report a RANGE, not a single precise value. The traps treat the estimate as exact: calipers measure a fold of skin plus fat, not body fat directly, and the regression equation does not eliminate error. Reporting '12.0 percent' or a single error-free number overstates the precision of the method.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮褶厚度預測方程式的估計標準誤約±3–5%，誠實的做法是回報一個範圍（如9–15%）而非精確單值。卡尺量的是皮膚與皮下脂肪摺，不是直接測體脂率，回歸方程式也不會消除誤差；回報「12.0%」會高估方法精度。"},{"id":"q0325","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is rehabbing a reconstructed ACL, and the clinician wants an exercise that loads the knee through a CLOSED kinetic chain (joint compression and co-contraction for stability) rather than an open chain. Which exercise best fits?","options":["Seated knee (leg) extension machine","Wall squat or leg press","Seated hamstring (leg) curl machine"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Wall squat or leg press","explanation_en":"In a closed kinetic chain the distal segment (the foot) is fixed against a surface, producing joint compression and co-contraction that stabilize the joint - a wall squat or leg press fits. The traps (seated leg extension and seated leg curl) are OPEN kinetic chain: the foot moves freely. Open-chain leg extension in particular increases anterior tibial shear on the graft, which is why closed-chain work is favored early in ACL reconditioning.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"封閉動力鏈(closed kinetic chain)指遠端肢體（腳）固定在支撐面上，產生關節擠壓與共收縮來穩定關節，wall squat或腿推符合；坐姿腿伸展、腿彎曲是開放動力鏈，腳自由移動。ACL術後早期尤其避免開放鏈腿伸展，因為會增加移植物上的脛骨前向剪下力。"},{"id":"q0326","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is in the FIBROBLASTIC REPAIR (proliferation) phase of healing for a knee ligament. Which loading approach is most appropriate to lead off with?","options":["Maximal isometric contractions through the painful joint range to rebuild strength fast","Submaximal isometrics first (no joint movement), then progress to isotonic and isokinetic work","No active exercise of any kind until the maturation phase begins"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Submaximal isometrics first (no joint movement), then progress to isotonic and isokinetic work","explanation_en":"In the fibroblastic repair phase you lead with SUBMAXIMAL isometrics because they load tissue without joint movement, then progress to isotonic and isokinetic work. Maximal isometrics are wrong this early: they spike blood pressure and, because isometric gains are joint-angle specific (about plus or minus 20 degrees), they are limited. Withholding all exercise until maturation (option C) describes the acute inflammatory phase, not fibroblastic repair.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"纖維性修復期（增殖期）以次最大等長收縮領頭：不帶關節活動就能載入組織，再進階到等張與等速訓練。此期做最大等長會讓血壓驟升，而且等長增力有關節角度特異性（只在訓練角度約±20°內有效）；「完全不動到成熟期」講的是急性發炎期的處理。"},{"id":"q0327","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a hot, humid practice an athlete collapses, is confused and disoriented, and has hot skin. What is the priority response?","options":["Sit the athlete down and give oral fluids/electrolyte drink as the first action","Activate EMS and begin aggressive cooling such as cold-water immersion; do not force oral fluids","Move to shade, stretch the cramping muscles, and rehydrate orally"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Activate EMS and begin aggressive cooling such as cold-water immersion; do not force oral fluids","explanation_en":"Altered mental status (confusion) plus hot skin signals EXERTIONAL HEATSTROKE, the most severe stage of the heat-illness continuum (cramps, syncope, exhaustion, heatstroke). The priority is to activate EMS and cool aggressively (cold-water immersion). Forcing oral fluids in an obtunded athlete risks aspiration, so 'give fluids first' is the trap. Stretching/oral fluids treat the MILDER stages (cramps), not heatstroke.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"意識混亂加皮膚發燙=運動性中暑(exertional heatstroke)，是熱疾病譜最嚴重一環（痙攣→暈厥→衰竭→中暑）；優先呼叫EMS並積極降溫（冷水浸泡）。對意識改變者強灌液體有吸入風險；伸展加口服補液是處理較輕的熱痙攣階段。"},{"id":"q0328","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A facility serves a mixed membership of small high-school freshmen and large collegiate linemen. What is the guiding principle for selecting and arranging equipment?","options":["Provide equipment that accommodates the full range of body sizes and abilities of the athletes who use it","Restrict the younger, smaller athletes to selectorized machines for safety","Limit the larger athletes to free weights since machines will not fit them"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Provide equipment that accommodates the full range of body sizes and abilities of the athletes who use it","explanation_en":"Equipment must accommodate the RANGE and size of the actual athletes using the facility (adjustable loads, seat/lever ranges, varied bar and implement sizes). The two distractors are population-stereotype traps ('small/young must use machines,' 'large must use free weights'); selection is driven by fitting the athletes, not by demographic assumptions.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"器材選擇的原則是配合實際使用者完整的體型與能力範圍（可調範圍、各種槓鈴與器械尺寸）。「小而年輕必須用機械式、大而必須用自由重量」都是刻板印象陷阱；決策依據是合不合用，不是人口學假設。"},{"id":"q0329","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength coach is reviewing the ventilation specs for a new weight room. Which set of values is correct?","options":["Exchange room air a minimum of 2 to 4 times per hour, keep relative humidity below 80 percent","Exchange room air a minimum of 20 times per hour, keep relative humidity below 40 percent","Exchange room air a minimum of 8 to 10 times per hour (optimally 12 to 15), keep relative humidity at or below 60 percent"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Exchange room air a minimum of 8 to 10 times per hour (optimally 12 to 15), keep relative humidity at or below 60 percent","explanation_en":"Air should be exchanged at least 8 to 10 times per hour, optimally 12 to 15, with relative humidity not exceeding 60 percent (memory hook: '8-10 minimum, 12-15 optimal, humidity under 60'). The 2-to-4 option undershoots both the exchange rate and the humidity ceiling; the 20-times option inflates the exchange rate and over-restricts humidity. Aerobic areas need higher circulation than resistance areas.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"重量室通風標準：每小時至少換氣8–10次、最佳12–15次，相對濕度不超過60%（記憶點：最低8–10、最佳12–15、濕度60以下）。2–4次配濕度80%太鬆；20次配40%過苛。需氧區域的空氣流通需求高於阻力訓練區。"},{"id":"q0330","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is injured performing a power clean while the only staff member had stepped into the office out of sight. In a resulting negligence claim, which factor is most often the decisive issue?","options":["Whether the barbell met manufacturer load specifications","Whether qualified supervision (physical presence with clear line of sight) was provided","Whether the athlete had signed an informed-consent waiver"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Whether qualified supervision (physical presence with clear line of sight) was provided","explanation_en":"Supervision is the number-one liability factor, cited in roughly 80 percent of injury court cases; constant supervision means a qualified professional is physically present with clear sightlines, and complex lifts like the power clean demand MORE supervision. Stepping out of sight is a failure to supervise, which is a breach of the duty of care (negligence = duty, breach, proximate cause, damages). Equipment specs and a waiver do not cure an absent supervisor.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"監督(supervision)是法律責任第一議題，出現在約80%的受傷訴訟；合格監督＝專業人員親自在場且視線無遮擋，power clean等複雜動作需要更多監督。走出視線就是未盡監督責任（過失四要素：義務、違反、近因、損害）；器材規格與切結書救不了不在場的監督者。"},{"id":"q0331","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach is staffing supervision for three groups training simultaneously: a junior-high group, a high-school group, and a college group. Which professional-to-athlete ratios should be used?","options":["Junior high 1:10, high school 1:15, college 1:20","Junior high 1:15, high school 1:20, college 1:25","Junior high 1:5, high school 1:10, college 1:15"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Junior high 1:10, high school 1:15, college 1:20","explanation_en":"Recommended ratios climb by five with age and cap at college: junior high 1:10, high school 1:15, college 1:20. Option B shifts every value up one tier (the classic off-by-one trap), and option C shifts them all down. Younger, lower-training-age athletes need tighter ratios.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"建議的教練對運動員比例隨年齡逐級加5：國中1:10、高中1:15、大學1:20。較年輕、訓練年資較低的運動員需要較密集的監督；其他選項把數值整級位移。"},{"id":"q0332","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When planning the floor layout of a resistance-training facility, which arrangement best supports safety and traffic flow?","options":["Center the heavy fixed equipment in the middle of the room so it is easy to reach from all sides","Place heavy or fixed equipment along the walls and keep lifting platforms away from main walkways, preserving supervisor sightlines","Cluster the platforms by the main entrance so athletes can begin lifting immediately on arrival"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Place heavy or fixed equipment along the walls and keep lifting platforms away from main walkways, preserving supervisor sightlines","explanation_en":"Heavy and fixed equipment belongs along the walls and lifting platforms should sit away from traffic lanes, with open sightlines so a supervisor can see the whole floor. Centering heavy equipment (option A) blocks flow and sightlines, and putting platforms at the entrance (option C) creates a collision and traffic hazard right where people move in and out.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"樓面配置：重型與固定式器材沿牆放置，舉起平臺離開主動線，並保持監督者對全場的開闊視線。重機具放房間中央會擋動線與視線；平臺放入口造成人流碰撞危險。"},{"id":"q0333","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A new training facility is being sized for participants. What is the recommended minimum floor space per participant?","options":["About 50 sq ft per participant","About 100 sq ft per participant","About 200 sq ft per participant"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 100 sq ft per participant","explanation_en":"The recommended minimum is about 100 square feet of floor space per participant to allow safe spacing and movement. The 50 sq ft option crowds athletes into an unsafe density, and the 200 sq ft option doubles the standard. This pairs with the supervision ratios (junior high 1:10, high school 1:15, college 1:20) when planning capacity.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每位使用者建議最低樓地板空間約100平方英尺；50 sq ft過度擁擠，200 sq ft是標準的兩倍。規劃容納人數時要與監督比例（1:10、1:15、1:20）一起考慮。"},{"id":"q0334","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A high school weight room runs at full capacity. Which combination of records and safety documents must be maintained and readily accessible to limit liability?","options":["Only the athletes' signed waivers, kept in a locked office","Equipment maintenance and inspection logs, safety data sheets (SDS) for cleaning chemicals, and incident/injury records","Only the facility's insurance certificate posted at the front desk"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Equipment maintenance and inspection logs, safety data sheets (SDS) for cleaning chemicals, and incident/injury records","explanation_en":"A defensible facility keeps equipment maintenance and inspection logs, SDS for all cleaning chemicals, and incident/injury records, which document due care and support cleaning and emergency response. Relying on waivers alone (option A) or an insurance certificate alone (option C) is the trap: a waiver does not replace ongoing maintenance, chemical-safety, and incident documentation.","tags":["Hardest Mode"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"可自保的設施要儲存：器材維護與檢查紀錄、清潔藥品的安全資料表(SDS)、事故與傷害紀錄，這些檔案證明已盡合理注意義務。只有切結書或只有保險證明都是陷阱，取代不了持續的維護、化學安全與事故記錄。"},{"id":"q0335","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A researcher chemically blocks the release of ions from the sarcoplasmic reticulum in an isolated fiber that still has a normal energy supply. Contraction fails. What two intracellular factors, when both restored, are required for crossbridge cycling to resume?","options":["Sodium ions to depolarize the fiber and stored glycogen to fuel it","Calcium to uncover the actin binding sites and ATP to power the myosin heads","ADP and inorganic phosphate to rebind the myosin head to actin"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Calcium to uncover the actin binding sites and ATP to power the myosin heads","explanation_en":"Calcium exposes the actin binding sites and ATP powers the myosin head, so both are required for crossbridge cycling.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"橫橋(crossbridge)迴圈需要鈣與ATP兩者：Ca2+暴露actin上的結合位，ATP供應肌球蛋白頭的動力。實驗阻斷肌漿網釋放Ca2+後收縮失敗，所以要同時恢復鈣與ATP迴圈才會重啟。"},{"id":"q0336","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A single alpha motor neuron branches to reach 400 fibers scattered within a muscle, and when it fires all 400 fibers respond together. This functional grouping is best described as:","options":["An upper motor neuron synapsing onto a lower motor neuron","A single muscle fiber together with every motor neuron that reaches it","One motor neuron plus all of the muscle fibers it innervates"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"One motor neuron plus all of the muscle fibers it innervates","explanation_en":"A motor unit is one motor neuron together with every muscle fiber it innervates, all of which contract together.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動單位(motor unit)=一個運動神經元加它所支配的全部肌纖維；神經元一放電，這400條纖維一起反應。"},{"id":"q0337","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A coach claims that a lifter grades effort within a working motor unit so its fibers each contract only partway on a light set. Based on how an activated motor unit behaves, why is this claim wrong?","options":["Once a motor unit is activated its fibers contract fully; there is no partial fiber contraction","The fibers contract in proportion to the size of the load lifted","Only the fast fibers of the unit contract first, then the slow fibers follow"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Once a motor unit is activated its fibers contract fully; there is no partial fiber contraction","explanation_en":"No evidence supports partial activation of individual fibers within an active motor unit; they contract fully or not at all.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動單位遵循全動或無(all-or-none)：一旦被活化，單位內的纖維全部完整收縮，不存在「部分收縮的纖維」。輕重差異靠動員更多單位與提高放電率達成，不是靠單條纖維收一半。"},{"id":"q0338","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"As a sarcomere shortens during contraction, the thick filaments neither shorten nor change length. Which region of the striation pattern therefore stays a constant width while the neighboring regions narrow?","options":["The H-zone, the central region containing only thick filaments","The A-band, corresponding to the full length of the thick filaments","The I-band, spanning the thin filaments between sarcomeres"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The A-band, corresponding to the full length of the thick filaments","explanation_en":"The A-band corresponds to the length of the myosin filaments, which do not shorten, so it stays constant while the I-band and H-zone shrink.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"A帶對應肌球蛋白（粗絲）全長，粗絲不縮短，所以A頻寬度恆定；肌小節縮短時變窄的是I帶與H帶。"},{"id":"q0339","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A biopsy shows fibers rich in myoglobin and mitochondria that fatigue slowly and generate relatively low force. These fibers are best classified as:","options":["White, fast-twitch, high-force with low myoglobin content","Red, fast-twitch, high-power with sparse mitochondria","Red, slow-twitch, fatigue-resistant with high myoglobin content"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Red, slow-twitch, fatigue-resistant with high myoglobin content","explanation_en":"Type I fibers are red and slow-twitch with high myoglobin and mitochondrial content, favoring fatigue-resistant aerobic work.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第一型肌纖維是慢肌、紅肌，myoglobin與粒線體含量高、抗疲勞，偏向有氧工作，力量輸出相對低。"},{"id":"q0340","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A sprinter needs the fiber population capable of the greatest force and power output per unit, accepting that it fatigues fastest. Which fiber type fits that profile?","options":["Type IIx, the fast glycolytic fibers","Type I, the slow-twitch oxidative fibers","Type IIa, the fast oxidative-glycolytic fibers"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Type IIx, the fast glycolytic fibers","explanation_en":"Type IIx fibers have the highest force and power output but the lowest fatigue resistance.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第二型x（IIx，快糖解）纖維單位的force與power輸出最高、抗疲勞最差，符合衝刺的爆發需求；IIa居中，第一型最抗疲勞但力量小。"},{"id":"q0341","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"An athlete performs a near-maximal power clean. Applying the size principle to that single high-force effort, which motor units are recruited?","options":["Only the low-threshold slow-twitch units, since they are recruited first","The low-threshold slow units plus the higher-threshold fast-twitch units","Only the high-threshold fatigue-resistant units, bypassing the fast units"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The low-threshold slow units plus the higher-threshold fast-twitch units","explanation_en":"High-force efforts recruit lower-threshold slow units plus higher-threshold fast-twitch units, an example of the size principle.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"近最大強度的power clean依大小原則(size principle)：先動員低閾值的慢肌單位，再動員高閾值的快肌單位以滿足力量需求。只取低閾或只取高閾都漏掉 動員順序。"},{"id":"q0342","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Stimulation frequency to a motor unit is raised until successive twitches can no longer be distinguished and force plateaus at its maximum steady level. The unit is now in:","options":["The relaxation phase between twitches","A single isolated twitch followed by relaxation","Fused (complete) tetanus"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Fused (complete) tetanus","explanation_en":"A high enough activation frequency merges twitches into fused tetanus, the maximal force a motor unit can develop.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"刺激頻率提高到個別抽縮(twitch)無法分辨、力量融成穩定的最大值，即融合性強直(fused tetanus)——一個運動單位能發展的最大力量。"},{"id":"q0343","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A clinician taps the patellar tendon and the quadriceps briefly contracts, extending the knee. The muscle spindles that triggered this response act by:","options":["Reflexively exciting and activating the muscle that was stretched","Relaxing only the antagonist muscle on the opposite side of the joint","Reflexively inhibiting the muscle that was just stretched"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Reflexively exciting and activating the muscle that was stretched","explanation_en":"Spindles sense length and rate of stretch and reflexively excite the same muscle, as seen in the knee-jerk reflex.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌梭(muscle spindle)感受肌肉長度與被拉長的速率，反射性興奮並收縮被拉長的那塊肌肉，膝跳反射即一例。抑制對側拮抗肌不是它的主要作用；「抑制被拉長的肌肉」搞反了，那是高爾基腱器官對張力的反應。"},{"id":"q0344","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A lifter grinds through a maximal attempt and the target muscle suddenly gives way as tension peaks. This protective response comes from receptors arranged in series with the fibers that:","options":["Excite the muscle more strongly as tension rises","Inhibit the muscle when tension becomes excessively high","Detect changes in muscle length rather than tension"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Inhibit the muscle when tension becomes excessively high","explanation_en":"GTOs sit in the tendon in series with fibers and reflexively inhibit the muscle to protect against excessive tension.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官(GTO)位於肌腱、與肌纖維串聯，張力過高時反射性抑制該肌肉，保護組織免於過大張力——最大努力時「突然脫力」就是這個機制。感受長度變化的是肌梭，不是GTO。"},{"id":"q0345","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Tracing connective tissue from the outside of a muscle inward, which sheath is the innermost layer, wrapping each individual muscle fiber?","options":["Epimysium, the outer sheath around the entire muscle","Perimysium, the sheath bundling groups of fibers into fascicles","Endomysium, the sheath surrounding each single muscle fiber"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Endomysium, the sheath surrounding each single muscle fiber","explanation_en":"Endomysium wraps each single muscle fiber; perimysium surrounds fascicles and epimysium covers the whole muscle.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"由外而內：epimysium（整塊肌肉外鞘）→perimysium（包裹肌束）→endomysium（包圍單一肌纖維）。最內層是endomysium。"},{"id":"q0346","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"In a healthy heart, three structures can self-excite but one normally sets the rhythm because it discharges fastest, overriding the others. That structure is the:","options":["SA node, which discharges fastest and paces the heart","Purkinje fibers, which distribute the impulse through the ventricles","AV node, which relays the impulse to the ventricles"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"SA node, which discharges fastest and paces the heart","explanation_en":"The SA node discharges fastest, so it sets heart rhythm before the slower AV node or ventricular fibers can self-excite.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"竇房結(SA node)自發放電最快，會先一步壓過房室結與心室傳導纖維，為正常心跳的節律點(pacemaker)。"},{"id":"q0347","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"During ventricular systole, pressure in the ventricles climbs sharply. What is the primary role of the tricuspid and mitral valves at that moment?","options":["To open and allow ventricular filling during that phase","To prevent blood from flowing back into the atria as the ventricles contract","To prevent blood from flowing back from the great arteries into the ventricles"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"To prevent blood from flowing back into the atria as the ventricles contract","explanation_en":"The AV valves close during ventricular contraction (systole) to stop blood flowing back into the atria.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"三尖瓣與二尖瓣是房室瓣，心室收縮(systole)時閉合，防止血液逆流入心房。防止血液從大動脈迴流的是半月瓣；心室填充發生在舒張期。"},{"id":"q0348","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A subject has a stroke volume of 80 mL and a heart rate of 70 beats per minute. To find the volume of blood pumped each minute, these two values should be:","options":["Divided, taking stroke volume divided by heart rate","Combined as heart rate times systolic blood pressure","Multiplied together, since output equals stroke volume times heart rate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Multiplied together, since output equals stroke volume times heart rate","explanation_en":"Cardiac output equals stroke volume multiplied by heart rate, the volume of blood pumped per minute.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"心輸出量(cardiac output)=心搏量×心率=80 mL×70次/分≈5.6 L/min，兩值相乘因為它是每分鐘打出的血量。"},{"id":"q0349","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"When venous return rises and fills the ventricle more during diastole, the next contraction is more forceful. The Frank-Starling mechanism explains this by:","options":["Greater stretch of the myocardial fibers producing a more forceful contraction","A drop in end-diastolic volume that shortens the fibers before contraction","Reduced filling that weakens and slows the following contraction"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Greater stretch of the myocardial fibers producing a more forceful contraction","explanation_en":"Increased end-diastolic volume stretches myocardial fibers, producing a more forceful contraction and greater ejection.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Frank-Starling機制：靜脈迴流增加→心室舒張期末容積增大、心肌纖維被拉長→收縮更有力、射出量更多。這是心臟內在的長度—張力關係。"},{"id":"q0350","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"As an athlete transitions from rest into steady aerobic exercise, which respiratory change is expected?","options":["Motor unit activation of the respiratory muscles decreases","Minute ventilation increases as breathing gets both deeper and faster","Tidal volume decreases while breathing frequency alone rises"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Minute ventilation increases as breathing gets both deeper and faster","explanation_en":"Aerobic exercise raises minute ventilation through increases in both tidal volume and breathing frequency.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"從安靜進入穩定有氧運動時，每分鐘通氣量增加：潮氣量與呼吸頻率都上升。說潮氣量下降、只靠頻率上升是錯的。"},{"id":"q0351","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Of the total oxygen carried from the lungs to the working tissues in the blood, the large majority travels:","options":["Chemically combined as bicarbonate ions","Dissolved directly in the plasma","Bound to hemoglobin within red blood cells"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Bound to hemoglobin within red blood cells","explanation_en":"Plasma carries only a small amount of dissolved oxygen; the vast majority binds hemoglobin in red blood cells.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"血中氧氣絕大部分與紅血球內的血紅素(hemoglobin)結合運輸，血漿僅溶解一小部分。碳酸氫根是CO2的運輸形式，不是O2。"},{"id":"q0352","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"As carbon dioxide produced by working muscle is transported back to the lungs, the largest fraction is carried in the blood:","options":["As bicarbonate ions formed via carbonic anhydrase","As gas dissolved in the plasma","Bound directly to hemoglobin"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"As bicarbonate ions formed via carbonic anhydrase","explanation_en":"Roughly seventy percent of carbon dioxide is transported as bicarbonate ions formed via carbonic anhydrase.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"約七成CO2以碳酸酐酶(carbonic anhydrase)催化生成的碳酸氫根離子形式運輸；血漿溶解型與直接結合血紅素型都只佔少數。"},{"id":"q0353","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Two athletes move the same total volume of air per minute, but one does it with fewer, deeper breaths and the other with rapid, shallow breaths. Why is the deeper-breathing pattern more effective for gas exchange?","options":["Deeper breaths reduce the amount of gas exchanged at the alveoli","Larger tidal volumes ventilate the alveoli more efficiently relative to dead space","Deeper breaths only increase ventilation of the anatomical dead space"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Larger tidal volumes ventilate the alveoli more efficiently relative to dead space","explanation_en":"Deeper breaths increase tidal volume proportionally more than dead space, so they ventilate the alveoli more efficiently.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每分鐘通氣量相同時，深而慢的呼吸每次進入肺泡的有效通氣比例較高（相對於死腔）；快而淺的呼吸大部分只反覆攪動解剖死腔(anatomical dead space)，氣體交換效率差。"},{"id":"q0354","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Two endurance athletes have similar leg fiber composition and predicted max heart rates, yet one has a markedly higher VO2max. This difference is most strongly explained by:","options":["A higher proportion of Type I versus Type II fibers in the legs","A higher age-predicted maximal heart rate","A greater capacity of the heart and circulation to transport oxygen"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A greater capacity of the heart and circulation to transport oxygen","explanation_en":"VO2max chiefly depends on the cardiovascular system's capacity to deliver oxygen to working tissues.","tags":["Chapter 1 quiz: Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌纖維組成與預測最大心率都相近時，VO2max差異主要由心肺迴圈輸運氧的能力（central factor）解釋——VO2max取決於氧氣輸送能力。"},{"id":"q0355","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"When labeling the two attachments of a muscle by convention, which one is designated the origin?","options":["The site where the muscle's fibers blend into its tendon","The distal attachment, which is the more mobile end","The proximal attachment, which is the more stationary end"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The proximal attachment, which is the more stationary end","explanation_en":"The traditional definition treats the origin as the proximal attachment toward the center of the body for consistency.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"慣例上肌肉的近端附著點（較接近身體中央、較固定的一端）定義為起點(origin)，遠端較活動的一端是止點(insertion)。"},{"id":"q0356","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"As a pitcher's arm whips forward and the elbow nears full extension, the biceps contracts to decelerate the forearm and protect the joint. In that instant the biceps is functioning as the:","options":["Antagonist, opposing and decelerating the ongoing movement","Synergist, assisting the prime mover and stabilizing the joint","Agonist, the prime mover producing the desired joint action"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Antagonist, opposing and decelerating the ongoing movement","explanation_en":"A muscle that decelerates or stops a movement, protecting joint structures, is acting as the antagonist.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"投擲手臂前甩接近完全伸肘時，二頭肌收縮為前臂減速、保護關節——此時它扮演拮抗肌(antagonist)角色。主動肌(agonist)是伸肘肌群。"},{"id":"q0357","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"In a standing heel raise the body pivots at the ball of the foot, with the calf's line of pull acting on a moment arm longer than that of the bodyweight it lifts. This arrangement is which class of lever?","options":["First-class, with the axis positioned between the two forces","Second-class, with both forces on the same side and the muscle arm longer","Third-class, with both forces on the same side but the muscle arm shorter"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Second-class, with both forces on the same side and the muscle arm longer","explanation_en":"A second-class lever has muscle and resistive forces on the same side with the muscle arm longer, giving mechanical advantage.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"站姿提踵以腳掌前球為軸，體重與小腿拉力在同側，且小腿的力臂比阻力臂長——這是第二類槓桿，機械利益大於1。"},{"id":"q0358","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"In a dumbbell biceps curl the elbow is the axis, the biceps and the weight both act on the same side of it, and the biceps attaches close to the joint while the weight sits far out at the hand. This describes which class of lever?","options":["First-class, with the axis lying between the muscle force and the load","Second-class, with the muscle moment arm longer than the resistive arm","Third-class, with the muscle moment arm shorter than the resistive arm"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Third-class, with the muscle moment arm shorter than the resistive arm","explanation_en":"A third-class lever has the muscle arm shorter than the resistive arm, a mechanical disadvantage requiring large muscle force.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"彎舉以肘為軸，二頭肌止點靠近關節、啞鈴遠在手上，肌肉力臂短於阻力力臂＝第三類槓桿：機械利益劣勢，需要大的肌肉力量；人體多數關節動作屬此類。"},{"id":"q0359","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Because most muscles in the body operate at a mechanical advantage below 1.0 (a short muscle moment arm against a longer resistive arm), what follows about the forces involved?","options":["The muscle must generate internal forces far larger than the external load","The muscle force and the external load are always equal in magnitude","The external load generates more force than the muscle must produce"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The muscle must generate internal forces far larger than the external load","explanation_en":"A mechanical disadvantage means muscles and tendons must generate forces much larger than the external resistance.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多數肌肉操作在機械劣勢（肌肉力臂短）：由力矩平衡可知，肌肉必須產生遠大於外在阻力的內部力量才能驅動動作。"},{"id":"q0360","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Two lifters have identical muscle size, but one has a tendon that inserts farther from the joint center, giving a longer muscle moment arm. Compared with the other, that lifter would tend to have:","options":["Both greater strength and greater limb movement speed","Greater joint torque and strength but a lower limb movement speed","Greater limb movement speed but less joint torque and strength"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Greater joint torque and strength but a lower limb movement speed","explanation_en":"A longer muscle moment arm boosts torque and strength but reduces shortening speed and movement velocity.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌腱附著點較遠（肌肉力臂較長）會提高關節力矩與力量表現，但傳到肢體的位移與縮短速度下降——力與速度的取捨，較長力臂換到的是力量不是速度。"},{"id":"q0361","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A lifter performs standing dumbbell lateral raises, lifting the arms out to the sides away from the body. This abduction movement occurs primarily in which plane?","options":["The transverse plane, dividing the body into top and bottom","The sagittal plane, dividing the body into left and right","The frontal plane, dividing the body into front and back"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The frontal plane, dividing the body into front and back","explanation_en":"Abduction and adduction movements such as the lateral raise occur in the frontal plane.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"額狀面(frontal plane)把身體分為前後兩部；手臂外展/內收（側平舉）在額狀面發生。水平面分上下，矢狀面分左右，屈伸主要在矢狀面。"},{"id":"q0362","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Lying on a bench, a lifter performs dumbbell flyes, sweeping the arms horizontally across the body with the elbows only slightly bent. This movement occurs primarily in which plane?","options":["The transverse plane","The sagittal plane","The frontal plane"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The transverse plane","explanation_en":"The dumbbell fly, moving the arms across the body, is a transverse-plane movement.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"仰臥飛鳥讓手臂在水平方向橫越身體（水平外展/內收），屬水平面(transverse plane)動作，不是矢狀或額狀面。"},{"id":"q0363","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A thrower wants to release a shot at a higher velocity. Since the implement's mass is fixed, the impulse-momentum relationship indicates the athlete must:","options":["Decrease the applied force while increasing the time by the same amount","Apply a greater impulse, more force applied over the available time","Somehow reduce the mass of the implement during the throw"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Apply a greater impulse, more force applied over the available time","explanation_en":"Impulse equals change in momentum; since mass is fixed, more impulse is needed to change velocity.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"衝量—動量關係：impulse=動量變化；鉛球質量固定，要提高釋出速度就必須施加更大衝量，即在可用的作用時間內施加更大的力。"},{"id":"q0364","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Two lifters move the same load the same distance, but one does it in half the time. In its strict mechanical sense, the faster lift demonstrates greater power because power is defined as:","options":["The greatest total mass the athlete is able to lift","The maximum force a muscle is able to exert","The work performed divided by the time taken to perform it"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The work performed divided by the time taken to perform it","explanation_en":"Power is the rate of doing work, the product of force and velocity, not simply maximal force.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力學上power定義為功除以時間（力×速度）；同樣的功在短一半的時間完成就是功率較佳。「舉最多的重量」或「最大肌力」都不是功率的定義。"},{"id":"q0365","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"From a strict mechanics standpoint, why is calling the sport of powerlifting a form of high-power lifting considered a misnomer?","options":["Its lifts are high in force but performed at low velocity","Its lifts generate more mechanical power than any other sport","Its lifts are high in velocity but relatively low in force"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Its lifts are high in force but performed at low velocity","explanation_en":"Powerlifting features slow, heavy lifts, so it is high force at low velocity rather than high mechanical power.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量舉(powerlifting)動作是大力、低速，力學功率（功/時間）其實不高，所以稱它高功率是名稱誤會：force高不代表power高。"},{"id":"q0366","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A novice adds substantial weight to his squat over the first three weeks of training, before any measurable change in muscle size. This early strength gain is attributed mainly to:","options":["Muscle fiber hypertrophy increasing cross-sectional area","Neural adaptations improving recruitment and coordination","An increase in the tendon's insertion distance from the joint"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Neural adaptations improving recruitment and coordination","explanation_en":"Early strength gains come mostly from neural adaptations as the nervous system learns to recruit tissue more effectively.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新手前3週負荷快速增加但圍度沒變——早期力量增加主要來自神經適應（動員與協調改善），不是肌纖維肥大或肌腱附著點改變。"},{"id":"q0367","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"If all else is held equal, the maximal force a muscle can generate is most directly proportional to its:","options":["Overall resting length","Total volume of muscle tissue","Physiological cross-sectional area"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Physiological cross-sectional area","explanation_en":"All else equal, muscle force is proportional to cross-sectional area, not to volume or length.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"其他條件相同下，肌肉能產生的最大力量直接正比於生理橫截面積(PCSA)，不是肌肉長度或組織總體積。"},{"id":"q0368","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Two muscles have the same overall size, but one is highly pennate and the other has fibers running parallel to the line of pull. Compared with the parallel muscle, the pennate one tends to:","options":["Produce greater force but have a lower maximal shortening velocity","Produce less force but reach a higher maximal shortening velocity","Produce both less force and a lower maximal shortening velocity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Produce greater force but have a lower maximal shortening velocity","explanation_en":"Pennation packs more sarcomeres in parallel, increasing force but reducing maximal shortening velocity.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"羽狀排列在單位面積內容納更多並聯肌小節，力量產出較大；但相對平行纖維肌，最大縮短速度較低——力與速度的取捨。"},{"id":"q0369","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Across a full range of motion, a muscle's ability to generate active force is greatest when the muscle is at which length?","options":["Its fully shortened length, where the filaments overlap the most","Its resting (normal) length, where crossbridge formation is optimized","Its maximally stretched length, where the fibers are under most tension"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Its resting (normal) length, where crossbridge formation is optimized","explanation_en":"At resting length, actin-myosin overlap allows the maximal number of crossbridges and the greatest force.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"主動力產生在休息（正常）長度時最大：actin與myosin重疊最適、可形成的橫橋數最多。過度縮短（重疊幹擾）或過度拉長（重疊減少）力量都下降。"},{"id":"q0370","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"As an athlete tries to move a limb faster and faster during a concentric action, what happens to the force the muscle can generate, according to the force-velocity relationship?","options":["The force the muscle can generate rises as velocity increases","The force the muscle can generate stays constant across velocities","The force the muscle can generate declines as velocity increases"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The force the muscle can generate declines as velocity increases","explanation_en":"Hill's classic work showed muscle force capability falls as shortening velocity increases.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Hill的力—速度關係：向心縮短速度越快，肌肉能產生的力量越低；高速下單位時間能形成的橫橋較少。"},{"id":"q0371","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Smaller athletes commonly show a higher strength-to-body-mass ratio than larger athletes. The scaling reason is that:","options":["Strength scales with cross-sectional area (squared) while body mass scales with volume (cubed)","Strength and body mass scale with body size at the same rate","Strength scales with volume (cubed) while body mass scales with area (squared)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Strength scales with cross-sectional area (squared) while body mass scales with volume (cubed)","explanation_en":"Strength tracks cross-sectional area (squared) while mass tracks volume (cubed), so mass grows faster than strength as size increases.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"力量跟著橫截面積成長（平方關係），體重跟著體積成長（立方關係）；體型變大時體重比力量增加更快，所以較輕的運動員力量/體重比較高。"},{"id":"q0372","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"During a dumbbell biceps curl, at which point in the range of motion does gravity impose the greatest resistive torque on the elbow?","options":["When the weight is directly above or directly below the joint axis","When the weight is horizontally farthest from the joint axis","When the weight is moving through its highest velocity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"When the weight is horizontally farthest from the joint axis","explanation_en":"Gravity acts downward, so resistive torque is largest when the horizontal moment arm from weight to joint is longest.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"重力的阻力力矩=重量×水平力臂；彎舉時重量距離肘關節水平最遠處力臂最長、阻力力矩最大。重量位於關節正上方/正下方時水平力臂接近零。"},{"id":"q0373","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"An athlete notices it takes a hard initial shove to get a loaded sled moving, after which a smaller sustained effort keeps it sliding. The primary reason is that:","options":["The coefficient of sliding friction is greater than that of static friction","The sled loses all inertia the moment it begins to move","The coefficient of static friction is greater than that of sliding friction"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The coefficient of static friction is greater than that of sliding friction","explanation_en":"The coefficient of static friction is always greater than that of sliding friction, so initiating movement needs more force.","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"靜摩擦係數恆大於滑動（動）摩擦係數，所以啟動雪橇比維持滑動更費力。慣性不會因為開始移動就消失。"},{"id":"q0374","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A coach argues that generating any spine-supporting intra-abdominal pressure absolutely requires holding the breath against a closed glottis. Which statement about intra-abdominal pressure is correct?","options":["Intra-abdominal pressure can be generated with the airway open, without a full Valsalva maneuver","Intra-abdominal pressure contributes essentially nothing to spinal support","A full Valsalva maneuver is strictly required to create any intra-abdominal pressure"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Intra-abdominal pressure can be generated with the airway open, without a full Valsalva maneuver","explanation_en":"The diaphragm and abdominal muscles can generate intra-abdominal pressure to support the spine even with the airway open, so a full Valsalva is not strictly required. (In the textbook, the Valsalva - expiring against a closed glottis - maximizes this rigid 'fluid ball' effect but transiently spikes blood pressure.)","tags":["Chapter 2 quiz: Biomechanics of Resistance Exercise"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"橫膈與腹肌在氣道開啟時也能產生腹內壓(intra-abdominal pressure)支撐脊椎，不必然要完整Valsalva。Valsalva（對閉合的聲門排氣）能把這個「液態球」效應極大化，但會讓血壓暫時驟升。"},{"id":"q0375","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Two athletes perform the same 100 m sprint, but one has a much higher percentage of Type I fibers than the other. Both still rely on essentially the same dominant energy system for the effort. What best explains why?","options":["The intensity of the effort is what primarily sets the dominant system, overriding fiber-type differences","Fiber-type distribution sets the dominant system, so the two efforts cannot use the same one","How long the effort lasts is what sets the dominant system, not the athletes' differences"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The intensity of the effort is what primarily sets the dominant system, overriding fiber-type differences","explanation_en":"Intensity is the primary determinant of energy system contribution, with duration secondary; fiber type influences performance but does not override the intensity-driven system selection.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"能量系統貢獻主要由運動強度決定，持續時間次之；肌纖維比例的差異不會蓋過依強度做出的系統選擇。所以同樣是100 m衝刺，兩位纖維組成不同的選手仍主要以同一系統（磷酸肌酸／糖解）供能。"},{"id":"q0376","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A coach tells an athlete the 'burn' in intense exercise is caused by lactic acid the muscles produce. Which correction is accurate about what actually drives the H+ accumulation behind metabolic acidosis?","options":["The proton accumulation comes mainly from converting pyruvate to lactate","The proton accumulation comes mainly from ATP being hydrolyzed outside the mitochondria","The proton accumulation comes mainly from the liver running the Cori cycle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The proton accumulation comes mainly from ATP being hydrolyzed outside the mitochondria","explanation_en":"ATP hydrolysis, not lactate formation, is primarily responsible for the proton accumulation, which is why 'lactic acidosis' is a misnomer; lactate production actually consumes protons.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「灼燒感=乳酸」不精確：H+累積的主要來源是粒線體外的ATP水解，而乳酸去氫酶反應其實會消耗H+，所以「乳酸酸化(lactic acidosis)」是誤稱。肝臟的Cori迴圈與pyruvate轉乳酸也不是質子累積的主因。"},{"id":"q0377","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"An athlete oxidizes one molecule of glucose taken up from the blood completely to CO2 and water. Compared with starting from a glucose unit released from muscle glycogen, the blood-glucose route yields a net of how many ATP?","options":["A net of 34 ATP, the same as the glycogen route","A net of 38 ATP, two more than the glycogen route","A net of 32 ATP, two fewer than the glycogen route"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A net of 32 ATP, two fewer than the glycogen route","explanation_en":"Blood glucose yields a net of 32 ATP because two ATP are consumed early in glycolysis; muscle glycogen yields 34 because one of those phosphorylation steps is bypassed.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"1莫耳血糖完全氧化淨得約32 ATP（糖解前段先花掉2個ATP）；從肝醣開始則是34 ATP，比血糖路徑多2。34與32的差就是那兩步磷酸化。"},{"id":"q0378","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Entering glycolysis from muscle glycogen produces a net of 34 ATP versus 32 from free blood glucose. What accounts for the two-ATP advantage of glycogen?","options":["The glucose released from glycogen is already phosphorylated, skipping one ATP-consuming step","Glycogen bypasses the electron transport chain entirely and is oxidized without it","Glycogen packs more chemical energy per gram than glucose does"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The glucose released from glycogen is already phosphorylated, skipping one ATP-consuming step","explanation_en":"Glycogen breakdown yields glucose-1-phosphate, so glycolysis skips one ATP-using phosphorylation step, giving a net of 34 versus 32 for blood glucose.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肝糖分解產生的是glucose-1-phosphate，已經磷酸化，跳過消耗ATP的己糖激酶步驟，所以淨產量34 vs 血糖的32。肝糖與葡萄糖每克化學能相近，也同樣要經電子傳遞鏈氧化。"},{"id":"q0379","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"During an all-out 5-second effort, ATP is rebuilt almost instantly from stored creatine phosphate and ADP. Which enzyme catalyzes this single-step reaction?","options":["Phosphofructokinase","Creatine kinase","Lactate dehydrogenase"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Creatine kinase","explanation_en":"Creatine kinase catalyzes ADP + creatine phosphate yielding ATP + creatine, the core reaction of the phosphagen system; lactate dehydrogenase and phosphofructokinase act within glycolysis.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌酸激酶(creatine kinase)催化CP+ADP→ATP+肌酸的單步轉移，是磷酸系統的核心反應。磷酸果糖激酶與乳酸去氫酶都作用在糖解途徑內。"},{"id":"q0380","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"An athlete needs the fastest possible rate of ATP resynthesis for a brief maximal burst, accepting that this source runs out quickly. Which system provides the highest rate of ATP production but the lowest total capacity?","options":["The oxidative system","Fast glycolysis","The phosphagen system"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The phosphagen system","explanation_en":"An inverse relationship exists between rate and capacity; the phosphagen system has the fastest rate but the smallest total capacity, while the oxidative system is the reverse.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"能量系統的產能速率與總容量呈反向關係：磷酸系統(phosphagen)再合成ATP速率最快、總容量最小；氧化系統相反；快速糖解居中。"},{"id":"q0381","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Ranking the fuel sources by the total amount of ATP that can ultimately be produced from a single stored molecule, which has the greatest capacity?","options":["Oxidation of a fatty acid (triglyceride)","Fast glycolysis of a glucose molecule","Breakdown of a phosphagen (creatine phosphate)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Oxidation of a fatty acid (triglyceride)","explanation_en":"Fat oxidation has the greatest capacity because a single triglyceride can yield well over 300 ATP, far more than carbohydrate or the phosphagen system, though at a slower rate.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"論總ATP容量：一個三酸甘油酯經脂肪酸氧化可產出超過300個ATP，遠大於葡萄糖（快速糖解）與磷酸肌酸，只是速率最慢。"},{"id":"q0382","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A rising AMP level and falling ATP accelerate glycolytic flux most strongly at one control point. Which enzyme is considered glycolysis's most important rate-limiting regulator?","options":["Hexokinase","Phosphofructokinase","Pyruvate kinase"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Phosphofructokinase","explanation_en":"Phosphofructokinase is the primary rate-limiting enzyme of glycolysis, inhibited by ATP and activated by AMP; hexokinase and pyruvate kinase are regulated but not the main control point.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"磷酸果糖激酶(PFK)是糖解最重要的限速酵素：受ATP抑制、受AMP活化，所以AMP升高會強力推高糖解流量。己糖激酶與丙酮酸激酶雖受調控，但不是主要控制點。"},{"id":"q0383","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A pathway's end product accumulates and binds a regulatory enzyme at a site other than the active site, slowing that enzyme's turnover. This type of feedback control is called what?","options":["Substrate-level phosphorylation","Oxidative phosphorylation","Allosteric inhibition"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Allosteric inhibition","explanation_en":"Allosteric (end-product or feedback) inhibition occurs when an end product binds a regulatory enzyme and decreases its activity; the phosphorylation terms name ATP-forming mechanisms, not regulation.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"終產物結合在酵素活性位以外的位置、降低其運轉速率＝異位性抑制(allosteric inhibition，又稱終產物/回饋抑制)。底物層磷酸化與氧化磷酸化是ATP生成機制的名詞，不是調節型態。"},{"id":"q0384","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A well-trained endurance athlete and an untrained person are compared on the exercise intensity at which blood lactate first rises above rest (LT1). At roughly what percentage of VO2max would you expect the trained athlete's LT1 to occur?","options":["70-80%, higher than the untrained person","90-100%, essentially at maximum","50-60%, similar to the untrained person"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"70-80%, higher than the untrained person","explanation_en":"Trained athletes reach LT1 at roughly 70-80% of VO2max, compared with 50-60% in untrained individuals; a shift toward maximum reflects greater trained capacity but not 90-100%.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"受訓選手的第一個乳酸閾(LT1)落在約70–80% VO2max，未受訓者約50–60%；往高強度位移代表有氧能力提升，但不會到90–100%。"},{"id":"q0385","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"During a graded exercise test, the second, steeper rise in blood lactate (OBLA, or LT2) is identified. Approximately what blood lactate concentration marks this point?","options":["About 20 mmol/L","About 4 mmol/L","About 10 mmol/L"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 4 mmol/L","explanation_en":"OBLA is the second inflection point and occurs at roughly 4 mmol/L of blood lactate; 10-20 mmol/L values reflect near-maximal or exhaustive exercise, not the OBLA threshold.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"OBLA（第二閾LT2）對應血乳酸約4 mmol/L；10–20 mmol/L是接近最大或力竭運動時的濃度，不是閾值定義點。"},{"id":"q0386","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A muscle biopsy from a sprinter shows fibers built for brief, explosive, anaerobic work. Compared with Type I fibers, which contents would these fibers have in higher concentration?","options":["Myoglobin and mitochondria","Capillaries and oxidative enzymes","Creatine phosphate and glycolytic enzymes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Creatine phosphate and glycolytic enzymes","explanation_en":"Type II (fast-twitch) fibers have higher creatine phosphate and glycolytic enzyme content for anaerobic power; myoglobin, mitochondria, capillaries, and oxidative enzymes are higher in Type I fibers.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第二型快肌纖維的磷酸肌酸與糖解酵素含量較高，對應短暫爆發的無氧工作；myoglobin、粒線體、微血管與氧化酵素是第一期纖維的特徵。"},{"id":"q0387","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Lactate produced by working muscle is not only a waste product; much of it is shuttled and oxidized as fuel. In which tissues is lactate most readily taken up and used as an energy substrate?","options":["Type I slow-twitch and cardiac muscle fibers","Only hepatocytes in the liver","Type II fast-twitch fibers"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Type I slow-twitch and cardiac muscle fibers","explanation_en":"Lactate is most readily oxidized as fuel in Type I (slow-twitch) and cardiac muscle fibers; the liver primarily reconverts lactate to glucose rather than oxidizing it as its main fuel.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"乳酸作為燃料最直接被第一型慢肌與心肌纖維氧化（lactate shuttle）；肝臟主要把乳酸經糖新生變回葡萄糖而非以它為主要燃料；第二期纖維是乳酸的產生者而非使用者。"},{"id":"q0388","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"During prolonged exercise, lactate released by muscle travels to the liver and is used to make new glucose that returns to the blood. This shuttle is known as what?","options":["The Krebs cycle","The Cori cycle","Beta oxidation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The Cori cycle","explanation_en":"Lactate transported to the liver and converted back to glucose is the Cori cycle, a form of gluconeogenesis; beta oxidation breaks down fatty acids and the Krebs cycle oxidizes acetyl-CoA.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉釋放的乳酸經血液到肝臟、再合成葡萄糖放回血糖＝Cori迴圈（糖新生的一種）。Beta氧化是分解脂肪酸；Krebs迴圈是氧化acetyl-CoA。"},{"id":"q0389","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"In the electron transport chain, NADH and FADH2 donate electrons at different entry points, yielding different amounts of ATP. Which comparison is correct?","options":["NADH produces fewer ATP than FADH2","NADH and FADH2 produce equal ATP","NADH produces more ATP (about 2.5) than FADH2 (about 1.5)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"NADH produces more ATP (about 2.5) than FADH2 (about 1.5)","explanation_en":"NADH enters the chain earlier and yields about 2.5 ATP, while FADH2 enters later and yields about 1.5 ATP, so NADH produces more per molecule.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"NADH在電子傳遞鏈較早的點進入，每莫耳約產生2.5 ATP；FADH2較晚進入，約1.5 ATP。所以NADH產量較高，兩者不相等。"},{"id":"q0390","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A coach wants to maximize the extra oxygen consumed after a session (EPOC) to boost total energy expenditure. Manipulating which variable will have the greatest effect on EPOC?","options":["The intensity of the exercise","The time of day the session is done","The mode of exercise chosen"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The intensity of the exercise","explanation_en":"Intensity has the greatest effect on EPOC, with the largest values seen at high intensity (and longer duration); mode and time of day have comparatively minor influence.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"影響EPOC（運動後過耗氧量）最大的變項是運動強度：強度越高（時間越長）EPOC越大；運動型態與一天中時段影響都小得多。"},{"id":"q0391","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"At the very start of a run, oxygen uptake lags behind the energy demand and anaerobic sources cover the shortfall until aerobic metabolism catches up. What is this early anaerobic contribution called?","options":["Steady state","The oxygen deficit","EPOC"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The oxygen deficit","explanation_en":"The oxygen deficit is the anaerobic portion of the early energy cost while aerobic metabolism ramps up; EPOC is the elevated postexercise oxygen consumption, and steady state is when uptake meets demand.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動開始時攝氧量來不及滿足能量需求，由無氧系統補足的早期能量差額＝氧缺(oxygen deficit)。EPOC是運動後的攝氧升高；steady state是攝氧量已符合需求的狀態。"},{"id":"q0392","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"A coach programs 5- to 10-second all-out sprints at 90-100% effort to target the phosphagen system. To allow near-full recovery of that system between reps, which work-to-rest ratio should be prescribed?","options":["1:1 to 1:3","1:3 to 1:5","1:12 to 1:20"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:12 to 1:20","explanation_en":"Phosphagen-focused intervals of 5-10 s at near-maximal power use long rest, roughly 1:12 to 1:20; the shorter ratios target glycolytic or oxidative development instead.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"針對磷酸系統、5–10秒90–100%輸出的衝刺，work:rest約1:12–1:20才能讓ATP-PCr接近完全恢復；較短的比值是糖解或有氧系統的發展配比。"},{"id":"q0393","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"An athlete adds high-volume aerobic endurance work to a heavy strength program and finds strength and power gains are blunted compared with resistance training alone. This blunting is best described as what?","options":["The interference effect of concurrent training","Cross-training specificity","Metabolic acidosis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The interference effect of concurrent training","explanation_en":"Combining aerobic endurance and heavy resistance training can reduce gains in muscle girth, maximum strength, and power, commonly called the interference effect of concurrent training.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在力量計畫上疊加大量有氧耐力，會使圍度、最大肌力與功率的成長低於只做阻力訓練——這稱為同時訓練(concurrent training)的幹擾效應(interference effect)。"},{"id":"q0394","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"An athlete competes in an event lasting about 60 to 90 seconds at high intensity, such as an 800 m run. Which energy system supplies the greatest share of ATP for this effort?","options":["The phosphagen system","Fast glycolysis","The oxidative system"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Fast glycolysis","explanation_en":"High-intensity efforts lasting roughly 30 s to 2 min rely primarily on fast glycolysis; the phosphagen system dominates only the first several seconds and the oxidative system dominates longer efforts.","tags":["Chapter 3 quiz: Bioenergetics of Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"持續約30秒到2分鐘的高強度努力（如800 m）以快速糖解供能為主；磷酸系統只主導最初數秒，氧化系統主導更長時間。"},{"id":"q0395","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Testosterone and cortisol are lipophilic and can pass through the plasma membrane. Because of this property, where do their receptors have to be located to transmit the signal?","options":["Anchored on the outer surface of the cell membrane","Inside the cell, in the cytosol or nucleus","Only in the bloodstream, on carrier binding proteins"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Inside the cell, in the cytosol or nucleus","explanation_en":"Steroid hormones are lipophilic and diffuse across the membrane to bind intracellular (cytosolic or nuclear) receptors that then act on DNA; membrane-surface receptors are used by non-lipophilic hormones.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"睪固酮與皮質醇是類固醇荷爾蒙、具脂溶性可穿越細胞膜，所以受體必須在細胞內（細胞質或細胞核），結合後調控DNA轉錄。膜表面受體供給不具脂溶性的荷爾蒙使用。"},{"id":"q0396","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Growth hormone and insulin are polypeptides that cannot cross the cell membrane. Given that limitation, how must they transmit their signal into the cell?","options":["By diffusing through the membrane to cytosolic receptors","By binding DNA directly inside the nucleus","By binding membrane-surface receptors that trigger secondary messengers"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"By binding membrane-surface receptors that trigger secondary messengers","explanation_en":"Non-lipophilic polypeptide hormones cannot cross the membrane, so they bind membrane-surface receptors and rely on secondary messenger cascades; direct DNA binding and membrane diffusion are steroid-hormone traits.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"生長激素與胰島素是多勝肽，脂溶性不足、無法穿越細胞膜，必須結合細胞膜表面受體、經第二訊息者(second messenger)級聯反應傳遞訊號。直接進入細胞質結合受體或進核結合DNA是類固醇荷爾蒙的做法。"},{"id":"q0397","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"The anterior pituitary releases ACTH, which travels in the blood to stimulate cortisol secretion. Which structure actually produces and releases the cortisol in response?","options":["The adrenal cortex","The anterior pituitary","The adrenal medulla"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The adrenal cortex","explanation_en":"The adrenal cortex produces and releases cortisol in response to ACTH; the adrenal medulla secretes catecholamines, and the anterior pituitary is the source of ACTH, not cortisol.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮質醇由腎上腺皮質(adrenal cortex)生成並釋放，受前葉分泌的ACTH驅動；腎上腺髓質分泌兒茶酚胺，前葉是ACTH的來源不是皮質醇的來源。"},{"id":"q0398","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"A chronically overtrained, underfed athlete shows elevated protein breakdown and gluconeogenesis with suppressed muscle growth. Which hormone, catabolic and anti-anabolic, best accounts for this pattern?","options":["Testosterone","Cortisol","Insulin-like growth factor-1"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Cortisol","explanation_en":"Cortisol is the primary catabolic and anti-anabolic hormone, promoting protein breakdown and gluconeogenesis especially when chronically elevated; testosterone and IGF-1 are anabolic.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮質醇是主要的分解性、抗合成荷爾蒙：長期偏高促進蛋白質分解與糖新生、抑制肌肉生長——符合長期超訓練又營養不足者的表現。睪固酮與IGF-1屬合成性。"},{"id":"q0399","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"An athlete progresses from a light warm-up load to a near-maximal load on the same lift. According to the size principle, what happens to motor unit recruitment, and what does this imply for adaptation?","options":["Only slow-twitch fibers are activated no matter how heavy the load gets","Fewer motor units are recruited at higher loads to conserve energy","Progressively more and larger fast-twitch motor units are recruited, and only recruited fibers adapt"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Progressively more and larger fast-twitch motor units are recruited, and only recruited fibers adapt","explanation_en":"Under the size principle, heavier loads recruit progressively more and larger fast-twitch motor units to meet force demand, and only the fibers actually recruited receive the training stimulus.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"依大小原則，負荷由輕到近最大，會被動員的運動單位越來越多、越來越大（含高閾值的快肌單位）；而且只有被動員的纖維才接受訓練刺激。"},{"id":"q0400","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"When designing a program to maximize muscle growth, a coach wants to leverage the body's primary anabolic hormones. Which group represents those hormones?","options":["Testosterone, growth hormone, and IGF-1","Calcitonin, aldosterone, and prolactin","Cortisol, epinephrine, and glucagon"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Testosterone, growth hormone, and IGF-1","explanation_en":"Testosterone, growth hormone, and IGF-1 are the primary anabolic hormones driving muscle growth and remodeling; the other groups are catabolic or serve non-anabolic regulatory roles.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"促進肌肉生長與組織重塑的主要合成荷爾蒙是睪固酮、生長激素與IGF-1；其他組別屬分解性或另有調控職掌。"},{"id":"q0401","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"After a rise in circulating growth hormone, most of the endocrine IGF-1 that appears in the blood is synthesized where?","options":["Skeletal muscle exclusively","The liver","The adrenal medulla"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The liver","explanation_en":"Systemic IGF-1 is mainly produced by the liver in response to the 22 kD GH isoform; skeletal muscle also makes local IGF-1 from mechanical stress, but not exclusively, and the adrenal medulla makes catecholamines.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"血液中（內分泌性）的IGF-1主要由肝臟在22 kD生長激素刺激下合成；骨骼肌也會因機械應力區域性產生IGF-1（旁泌），但不是血中IGF-1的主要來源；腎上腺髓質分泌的是兒茶酚胺。"},{"id":"q0402","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"A common misconception is that heavy lifting will make women bulky like men. Considering circulating testosterone, women naturally have roughly what fraction of the amount found in men?","options":["About 25-30%","About 50%","About 5-10%"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 5-10%","explanation_en":"Women have only about 5-10% of the circulating testosterone found in men, largely due to the absence of testes; the higher fractions overstate the difference.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性迴圈睪固酮只有男性的約5–10%（主要因為沒有睪丸），這是女性單靠重訓難以出現男性化大塊頭的生理基礎；25–30%或50%都高估了。"},{"id":"q0403","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Comparing several session designs by their acute post-workout hormonal surge, which one tends to produce the LARGEST rise in both anabolic and catabolic hormones?","options":["Moderate loads around 8-10RM with short (1-2 min) rest and higher volume","Single-joint isolation exercises using very light loads","Heavy 1-3RM loads with rest periods over 3 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Moderate loads around 8-10RM with short (1-2 min) rest and higher volume","explanation_en":"Higher-volume work at moderate loads with short rest creates the greatest metabolic demand and largest acute hormonal surges; heavy low-rep long-rest work has low metabolic demand, and light isolation work does little.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"中等強度（約8–10RM）、短休息（1–2分鐘）、高容量的訓練代謝壓力最大，急性的合成與分解荷爾蒙上升幅度都最大；大重量低次數長休息的代謝壓力低，輕重量單關節動作刺激更小。"},{"id":"q0404","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"The lock-and-key model is used to explain why a given hormone affects only certain tissues. What does the model actually describe?","options":["Receptors physically lock onto one another to amplify a signal","A hormone must precisely match its specific receptor to trigger a response","Hormones are locked inside binding proteins and are never released to act"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A hormone must precisely match its specific receptor to trigger a response","explanation_en":"The lock-and-key model describes how a specific hormone (key) must fit its specific receptor (lock) to produce an effect, explaining target-tissue specificity.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鑰匙與鎖模型(lock-and-key)指的是特定荷爾蒙（鑰匙）必須精確配合特定受體（鎖）才能引發反應，說明荷爾蒙的目標組織專一性；不是受體互相鎖定放大，也不是結合蛋白永久封存荷爾蒙。"},{"id":"q0405","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"A hormone bound to a carrier protein in the blood is temporarily inactive yet the arrangement benefits the athlete. What is the primary role of these binding proteins?","options":["They convert steroid hormones into peptide hormones","They permanently block the hormone so it can never act on tissue","They extend the hormone's half-life and protect it from degradation until released"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"They extend the hormone's half-life and protect it from degradation until released","explanation_en":"Binding proteins act as temporary storage that protects hormones from degradation and extends their half-life until they are released to the free, active fraction; they do not permanently block or chemically convert hormones.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"結合蛋白的角色是暫時儲存庫：保護荷爾蒙免於降解、延長半衰期，必要時釋放出遊離的活性部分；不會永久阻斷，也不會把類固醇化學轉化成勝肽。"},{"id":"q0406","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"As part of the fight-or-flight response to intense exercise, epinephrine and norepinephrine surge into the blood. Which structure is their primary source?","options":["The adrenal medulla","The thyroid gland","The anterior pituitary"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The adrenal medulla","explanation_en":"The adrenal medulla secretes the catecholamines epinephrine, norepinephrine, and dopamine; the thyroid and anterior pituitary secrete different hormones.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"腎上腺髓質分泌兒茶酚胺（epinephrine、norepinephrine、dopamine），在戰或逃反應與高強度運動時大量入血；甲狀腺與前葉分泌別的荷爾蒙。"},{"id":"q0407","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"After prolonged high insulin exposure, a person's tissues respond less to the same insulin level because receptor number or sensitivity has fallen. This adaptation is called what?","options":["Receptor upregulation","Receptor downregulation","Cross-reactivity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Receptor downregulation","explanation_en":"Receptor downregulation reduces receptor number or sensitivity after chronic overstimulation, with insulin resistance as a classic example; upregulation is the opposite response.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期高胰島素刺激後，受體數量或敏感度下降、組織對同樣濃度的胰島素反應變差＝受體下調(downregulation)，胰島素阻抗是典型例子；upregulation是反向變化。"},{"id":"q0408","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Some hormones do not directly build muscle but must be present at normal levels for anabolic hormones to work, enabling the underlying metabolic reactions. Which pair plays this permissive role?","options":["Cortisol and aldosterone","Estradiol and progesterone","Insulin and thyroid hormones"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Insulin and thyroid hormones","explanation_en":"Insulin and thyroid hormones act permissively, enabling the metabolic and chemical reactions that support muscle growth; cortisol is catabolic and the other listed hormones are not described as permissive here.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"允許作用(permissive effect)＝某些荷爾蒙不直接建造肌肉，但需維持在正常濃度作為其他荷爾蒙作用的前提，如胰島素與甲狀腺荷爾蒙支援生長所需的代謝反應；皮質醇屬分解性，屬另一類。"},{"id":"q0409","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Studies measuring the growth hormone response to a resistance session by immunoassay usually track a particular isoform that rises with total work and short rest. Which isoform is this?","options":["The 22 kD isoform","The 44 kD aggregate","There is only one form of GH"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The 22 kD isoform","explanation_en":"Resistance exercise raises the 22 kD GH isoform, the form most studies measure, and it is sensitive to total work and short rest; GH actually exists in multiple isoforms and aggregates.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多數研究以immunoassay量測的是22 kD這個GH異型：阻力訓練使其上升，幅度與總功量及短休息相關；GH其實存在多種異型與聚合物，不只一種形式。"},{"id":"q0410","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"A lab reports both total and free testosterone for an athlete. What distinguishes the free fraction, and why does it matter physiologically?","options":["It is always higher than total testosterone after exercise","It is the small unbound portion that can directly interact with target tissue","It is the portion permanently bound to sex hormone-binding globulin"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It is the small unbound portion that can directly interact with target tissue","explanation_en":"Free testosterone (roughly 0.5-2% of total) is the unbound fraction able to interact directly with target tissues; the bound portion is not the free fraction, and free can never exceed total.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"遊離睪固酮約佔總量的0.5–2%，是未與蛋白結合、可直接作用於目標組織的部分；結合SHBG等蛋白的是結合部分，遊離值永遠不會超過總量。"},{"id":"q0411","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"A coach wants a session that acutely elevates serum testosterone. Which combination of program variables is recommended to achieve that?","options":["A single set to failure followed by 5-minute rest periods","Small-muscle isolation exercises, light loads, and very long rest","Large-muscle-group exercises, heavy resistance, moderate-to-high volume, and short rest"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Large-muscle-group exercises, heavy resistance, moderate-to-high volume, and short rest","explanation_en":"Large-muscle-group lifts, heavy resistance, moderate-to-high volume, and short rest acutely raise serum testosterone; isolation/light/long-rest and single-set/long-rest schemes do not provide the needed stimulus.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"要急性提升血清睪固酮，建議：大肌群複合動作、大阻力、中高容量、短休息；孤立小肌群、輕重量、長休息或單組做一組休息5分鐘都給不足夠的刺激。"},{"id":"q0412","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Cortisol is usually cast as purely catabolic, yet an acute post-session rise is not entirely harmful. Which beneficial process does that acute cortisol increase support?","options":["Helping clear damaged proteins and aiding tissue remodeling","Directly synthesizing new contractile proteins","Permanently downregulating androgen receptors"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Helping clear damaged proteins and aiding tissue remodeling","explanation_en":"An acute cortisol rise helps clear damaged proteins, assists muscle remodeling, and helps maintain blood glucose; it does not directly build contractile protein and does not permanently downregulate androgen receptors.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動後急性的皮質醇上升有其正面功能：協助清除受損蛋白、參與肌肉重塑、並維持運動後的血糖；它不直接合成收縮蛋白，也不會永久下調androgen受體。"},{"id":"q0413","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Two athletes have similar resting testosterone levels, but one gains muscle much faster on the same program. Which principle best explains why blood hormone concentration alone does not determine the outcome?","options":["Blood hormone level by itself fully dictates the tissue response","The number and sensitivity of receptors strongly determine the actual effect","Receptors are fixed and do not adapt to training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The number and sensitivity of receptors strongly determine the actual effect","explanation_en":"The actual tissue effect depends heavily on receptor availability and sensitivity, which adapt to training; muscle can grow even without large changes in circulating hormone levels.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同樣的血中荷爾蒙濃度可以有不同的組織反應，因為實際效果高度取決於受體的數量與敏感度——兩者會隨訓練改變；肌肉成長不必要求血中荷爾蒙濃度大漲。"},{"id":"q0414","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"An athlete on a heavy 1-3RM, long-rest program shows only modest acute hormone spikes yet still gains strength and size. Which explanation reconciles the small hormonal response with the real adaptation?","options":["It removes the need for muscle protein synthesis to occur","The scheme fails to recruit any motor units, so gains must come from elsewhere","It maximally recruits motor units and enhances receptor binding, while its low metabolic demand limits hormone surges"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It maximally recruits motor units and enhances receptor binding, while its low metabolic demand limits hormone surges","explanation_en":"Heavy low-rep work maximally recruits motor units and enhances receptor binding, driving adaptation, while its low metabolic demand limits the acute hormone surge; it still recruits fibers and still requires protein synthesis.","tags":["Chapter 4 quiz: Endocrine Responses to Resistance Exercise and Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"1–3RM大重量長休息最大的好處是能最大量動員運動單位並提高受體結合，即使代謝壓力低、急性荷爾蒙上升有限仍會適應；它並非不動員纖維，蛋白質合成照樣需要。"},{"id":"q0415","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A previously sedentary client adds 30 pounds to her back squat over her first three weeks of training, yet a limb-circumference measurement shows essentially no change in thigh girth. What best explains this rapid strength gain?","options":["Early sarcomere addition that increases fiber size without changing limb girth","A rise in circulating testosterone that thickens the myofibrils","Improved neural function: greater motor unit recruitment, firing rate, and coordination"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Improved neural function: greater motor unit recruitment, firing rate, and coordination","explanation_en":"Neural adaptations (recruitment, firing rate, coordination) dominate early strength gains before substantial hypertrophy appears.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練初期負荷明顯增加但大腿圍度幾乎不變，最佳解釋是神經功能改善：運動單位動員、放電頻率與動作協調提升；肌肉肥大的貢獻還沒發生。早期也不可能已有肌小節大量新增或睪固酮長期上升。"},{"id":"q0416","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"As a lifter gradually increases the load on a curl from light to near-maximal, which sequence describes how the motor units of the biceps are brought into play, per Henneman's size principle?","options":["Smaller, lower-threshold units are recruited first, with larger high-threshold units added as force demand rises","Units are activated in a rotating pattern to distribute fatigue evenly","The largest, highest-threshold units fire first, with smaller units added as load eases"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Smaller, lower-threshold units are recruited first, with larger high-threshold units added as force demand rises","explanation_en":"Lower-threshold (smaller soma, Type I) motor units are recruited first, with higher-threshold (Type II) units added as force demand rises.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Henneman大小原則：較小、低閾值（第一型）的運動單位先被動員，力量需求上升時才逐加較大、高閾值（第二型）的單位；不是輪流發放，更不是大的先動員。"},{"id":"q0417","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A muscle biopsy shows a fiber population that is highly fatigue resistant, rich in myoglobin, and served by motor neurons with the lowest activation thresholds. This fiber type is best classified as:","options":["Type IIx, fast and white","Type I, slow and red","Type IIa, an intermediate fast-oxidative type"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Type I, slow and red","explanation_en":"Type I fibers are slow, red, fatigue-resistant, and innervated by low-threshold motor neurons; Type II fibers are fast and white.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高抗疲勞、富含myoglobin、受最低活化閾值運動神經元支配＝第一型（慢、紅）纖維；第二型是快、白纖維。"},{"id":"q0418","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A sprinter in a lower-leg cast trains only the healthy leg for six weeks. At cast removal, the immobilized leg has lost less strength than expected and even tests slightly stronger than at injury. This carryover is termed:","options":["The bilateral deficit, a shortfall when both limbs act together","Fiber-type transformation of Type II fibers into Type I","Cross-education, a strength gain in the untrained limb from training the opposite limb"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Cross-education, a strength gain in the untrained limb from training the opposite limb","explanation_en":"Cross-education is the strength and neural activity increase in a resting contralateral limb when the opposite limb is trained.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"只訓練健康側、打石膏的對側休息肢竟保留甚至增加力量與神經活化＝交叉教育(cross-education)，屬神經適應。雙側缺陷是另一個名詞（兩側同時出力小於兩側各自出力之和）。"},{"id":"q0419","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"An untrained athlete produces 40 kg pressing with only the right leg and 40 kg with only the left, but just 72 kg when both legs press together. This shortfall relative to the summed single-leg efforts illustrates:","options":["The bilateral deficit, in which combined force is less than the sum of separate limb efforts","Increased antagonist coactivation caused by an unstable surface","A training effect showing bilateral work is superior to unilateral"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The bilateral deficit, in which combined force is less than the sum of separate limb efforts","explanation_en":"In untrained individuals, force produced by both limbs together is lower than the sum of their separate unilateral efforts.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"未受訓者兩腿同時推72 kg小於左右各自40+40=80 kg的合體，即雙側缺陷(bilateral deficit)：未受訓練時雙側同時輸出的力小於兩側分別出力之和。"},{"id":"q0420","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"After several months of consistent heavy resistance training, a repeat biopsy of an athlete's vastus lateralis is expected to show a shift in fiber subtype in which direction?","options":["No detectable change in subtype proportions","Toward the more oxidative subtype, IIx converting toward IIa","Toward the less oxidative subtype, IIa converting toward IIx"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Toward the more oxidative subtype, IIx converting toward IIa","explanation_en":"Training shifts fibers toward more oxidative subtypes (IIx to IIa); detraining reverses this and can overshoot toward IIx.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"數月的大重量阻力訓練後，纖維亞型預期朝較氧化方向位移：IIx轉為IIa；停訓會逆轉甚至超調回IIx。"},{"id":"q0421","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Two fiber populations in the same muscle are exposed to identical resistance training. Which typically enlarges more, and how should a coach expect the growth to distribute?","options":["Both enlarge equally, so growth is uniform across fiber types","Type I fibers enlarge more, so growth favors the slow-twitch pool","Type II fibers enlarge more, so hypertrophy is not uniform between the types"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Type II fibers enlarge more, so hypertrophy is not uniform between the types","explanation_en":"Type II fibers manifest greater increases in size than Type I; hypertrophy is not uniform between the two.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一訓練刺激下，第二型纖維的橫截面積增幅大於第一型，所以兩型之間的肥大不是均勻的；說兩型等量成長或第一型較大都不符合文獻。"},{"id":"q0422","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A coach has an athlete perform chest presses seated on a Swiss ball instead of a stable bench, expecting to boost pressing power. Compared with the stable surface, what happens to agonist force output?","options":["Peak force and rate of force development both fall","Force is unchanged because the same muscles do the work","Peak force and rate of force development both rise"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Peak force and rate of force development both fall","explanation_en":"Instability raises antagonist coactivation and core demand while reducing agonist activation, lowering peak force and rate of force development.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在不穩定表面（瑞士球）做推舉，會提高拮抗肌共收縮與核心需求、降低主動肌活化，結果峰值力量與力量上升速率(RFD)都下降。想衝峰值力量，不穩定表面反而吃虧。"},{"id":"q0423","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"For a loading program to trigger new bone formation, the strain must exceed the minimal essential strain. As a fraction of the force that would fracture the bone, that threshold is approximately:","options":["One-half of the fracture force","One-tenth of the fracture force","One-hundredth of the fracture force"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"One-tenth of the fracture force","explanation_en":"The MES is thought to be roughly one-tenth of the force required to fracture the bone.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"機械載重要超過最小必要應變(minimal essential strain, MES)才能觸發新骨形成；MES約為使骨骨折所需力量的十分之一。"},{"id":"q0424","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A coach wants to maximize the osteogenic stimulus for a young athlete's spine and hips. Which choice best accomplishes that goal?","options":["High-repetition isolated assistance work with light loads","Seated single-joint leg extensions performed to fatigue","Multijoint structural lifts such as squats and deadlifts that direct load through the spine and hips"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Multijoint structural lifts such as squats and deadlifts that direct load through the spine and hips","explanation_en":"Multijoint structural exercises that direct force through the spine and hip provide a stronger osteogenic stimulus than isolated machine work.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"要最大化對脊椎與髖部的成骨刺激，選把載重經脊椎與髖部傳導的多關節結構性動作（蹲、硬舉），比單關節器械或輕負荷高次數孤立動作有效。"},{"id":"q0425","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A coach wants to increase the collagen content and stiffness of an athlete's patellar tendon. Which loading prescription is most appropriate?","options":["Heavy loads near 80% of 1RM","Load magnitude is irrelevant as long as volume is high","Light loads near 20% of 1RM performed for high repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Heavy loads near 80% of 1RM","explanation_en":"Heavy loads (around 80% 1RM) increase tendon stiffness; light loads (around 20% 1RM) do not markedly change collagen.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"要提高肌腱的膠原含量與剛性需大負荷（約80% 1RM）；小負荷（約20% 1RM）高次數不會明顯改變膠原——負荷強度才是關鍵，不是隻堆容量。"},{"id":"q0426","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A bodybuilder completes a block of heavy, high-volume hypertrophy training that markedly enlarges fiber cross-sectional area. What happens to the mitochondrial density measured per unit of fiber volume?","options":["It rises as mitochondria proliferate to match the larger fiber","It falls because fiber volume grows faster than mitochondria are added","It is unchanged because mitochondria scale exactly with fiber size"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It falls because fiber volume grows faster than mitochondria are added","explanation_en":"The fiber cross-sectional area grows faster than mitochondria proliferate, so mitochondrial density per unit volume decreases.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練讓肌纖維橫截面積的成長快於粒線體增殖，所以每單位纖維體積計的粒線體密度下降（被稀釋），不是粒線體絕對量變少，也不會剛好等比例跟隨。"},{"id":"q0427","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A sprinter repeatedly drains ATP and creatine phosphate with maximal-effort sets over weeks. What adaptation occurs in the resting concentrations of these substrates?","options":["Resting stores are unchanged because these substrates cannot be stockpiled","Resting stores fall as the substrates are chronically depleted","Resting stores rise through a supercompensation response"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Resting stores rise through a supercompensation response","explanation_en":"Repeated depletion triggers a supercompensation effect that raises resting stores of ATP, creatine phosphate, and glycogen.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"反覆以最大努力耗竭ATP與磷酸肌酸的訓練會引發超補償：安靜時的ATP、磷酸肌酸與肝醣存量上升。"},{"id":"q0428","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"An echocardiogram of a long-term heavy resistance-trained athlete is compared with that of a distance runner. The resistance-trained heart most characteristically shows:","options":["Increased left ventricular wall thickness with little change in chamber size","No structural difference from an untrained heart","A greatly enlarged left ventricular chamber volume with normal wall thickness"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increased left ventricular wall thickness with little change in chamber size","explanation_en":"Resistance training increases left ventricular wall thickness while chamber size changes little; chamber enlargement is more an aerobic adaptation.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期大重量阻力訓練者的心臟超音波呈現左心室壁厚增加、心室腔容積變化不大；心室腔明顯擴大是耐力型（有氧）心臟的特徵，不是完全沒有結構差異。"},{"id":"q0429","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"An athlete layers high-intensity, high-volume aerobic endurance running onto an existing heavy strength and power program. Which quality is the concurrent aerobic work most likely to blunt?","options":["Joint flexibility","Explosive power development","Bone mineral density"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Explosive power development","explanation_en":"Concurrent training most readily blunts power development, which is more susceptible to interference than slow-velocity strength.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同時訓練的幹擾效應最容易削弱爆發功率的發展（比低速力量更受幹擾），所以在重力量＋爆發計畫上疊加高強度高容量耐力跑，最可能被拖延的是爆發力。"},{"id":"q0430","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A coach sees strength gains stalling in an athlete who does both resistance and aerobic endurance work. Which adjustment best reduces the interference effect?","options":["Routinely place a hard aerobic bout immediately before the heavy lifting","Schedule both modes back-to-back on six consecutive days","Allow more recovery time between the resistance and aerobic sessions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Allow more recovery time between the resistance and aerobic sessions","explanation_en":"Increasing the recovery period between sessions decreases the incompatibility between strength and aerobic endurance training.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"降低幹擾效應的做法是拉開力量與耐力課的恢復間距（時間上分開、保留足夠恢復）。把高強度有氧排在沉重舉之前、或連續六天兩課並排，都會加重幹擾。"},{"id":"q0431","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A strength athlete is sidelined by a non-training-related illness and does no resistance work for about four weeks. On return testing, his maximal strength is most likely to be:","options":["Largely retained, remaining near pre-layoff levels","Dropped below his original pretraining baseline","Higher than before the layoff due to extra rest"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Largely retained, remaining near pre-layoff levels","explanation_en":"Strength is readily maintained for up to about four weeks of inactivity and rarely falls below pretraining values.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大肌力在停訓約4週內大致能維持、接近停訓前水準，極少掉回原本訓練前的基線；也不會因為多休息就超越先前（爆發力流失較快，但最大力量保留）。"},{"id":"q0432","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"After a period of detraining, biopsies are taken from an athlete's leg. Which fiber population is expected to have lost cross-sectional area first and fastest?","options":["Slow-twitch Type I fibers, which atrophy earliest","Fast-twitch Type II fibers, which atrophy earliest","Both fiber types, atrophying at identical rates from day one"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Fast-twitch Type II fibers, which atrophy earliest","explanation_en":"Fast-twitch fiber CSA declines first and fastest with detraining, while slow-twitch fibers initially show little change.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"去訓練化後，最快、最先萎縮的是快肌第二型纖維的橫截面積；慢肌第一型初期幾乎不變，兩型也不是同速率一起萎縮。"},{"id":"q0433","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A coach argues that only very heavy loads let an athlete grow the full spectrum of muscle fibers. What is the correct physiological reason heavy resistance training can hypertrophy fibers across all motor units?","options":["Anabolic hormones enlarge fibers directly, so recruitment is not required","Only Type I fibers respond to heavy loads, so they alone carry the growth","Generating high force recruits fibers across all motor units, and a fiber must be activated to receive the growth signal"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Generating high force recruits fibers across all motor units, and a fiber must be activated to receive the growth signal","explanation_en":"Producing high force requires recruiting fibers across all motor units, and a fiber must be activated to receive the growth signal.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大重量能讓所有運動單位的纖維都肥大，是因為產生高力量必須動員到高閾值纖維，而纖維必須先被活化才會收到生長訊號；單靠荷爾蒙、不動員纖維不會長。"},{"id":"q0434","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"A once-competitive lifter returns after a long layoff and regains his former strength far faster than an equally strong novice builds it. This residual training effect is best described as:","options":["Muscle memory: a residual effect that lets strength be reacquired rapidly on retraining","Conversion of atrophied muscle tissue into bone during the layoff","A total loss of adaptation requiring the athlete to rebuild strength from zero"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Muscle memory: a residual effect that lets strength be reacquired rapidly on retraining","explanation_en":"Resistance training leaves a residual effect, so returning athletes regain strength quickly, consistent with muscle memory.","tags":["Chapter 5 quiz: Adaptations to Anaerobic Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"退役運動員重訓後力量回升遠快於新手，這是肌肉記憶(muscle memory)：先前訓練留下的殘留效應（含神經與細胞層面的適應），讓再訓練時快速重建；不是肌肉變成骨頭，也不是歸零重來。"},{"id":"q0435","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"After a year of endurance training, a runner's maximal oxygen uptake has risen sharply. Which underlying cardiovascular change is chiefly responsible for delivering that extra oxygen?","options":["A greater maximal cardiac output, driven mainly by increased stroke volume","A higher resting blood pressure pushing more blood to the muscles","A higher maximal heart rate driving more beats per minute"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A greater maximal cardiac output, driven mainly by increased stroke volume","explanation_en":"The hallmark change is increased maximal cardiac output, resulting primarily from a higher stroke volume, not a higher max heart rate.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一年耐力訓練後最大攝氧量大幅提升，主要是最大心輸出量增加、且主要由心搏量(stroke volume)提高驅動；最大心率幾乎不變，安靜血壓也不是機制。"},{"id":"q0436","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A cyclist retested after two years of endurance training shows a much higher stroke volume and cardiac output. What is expected to have happened to her maximal heart rate over that same period?","options":["It rose substantially to match the higher cardiac output","It stayed about the same or decreased slightly","It roughly doubled"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It stayed about the same or decreased slightly","explanation_en":"Maximal heart rate generally remains unaltered or decreases slightly, partly due to increased parasympathetic tone.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練兩年後心搏量與心輸出量大增，但最大心率通常不變或小幅下降（部分來自副交感張力增加）；不會跟著大幅上升更不會加倍。"},{"id":"q0437","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A trained endurance athlete has a resting heart rate of 44 beats per minute. Which pairing of mechanisms best accounts for this bradycardia?","options":["A smaller, weaker heart that pumps less blood per beat","A reduced total blood volume requiring fewer beats","Increased parasympathetic tone slowing the SA node, combined with a larger stroke volume"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increased parasympathetic tone slowing the SA node, combined with a larger stroke volume","explanation_en":"Increased parasympathetic tone slows the SA node discharge, and a larger stroke volume means fewer beats are needed per minute.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"耐力選手的安靜心搏過緩（44 bpm）由兩件事解釋：副交感（迷走）張力增加使竇房結放電變慢，加上心搏量較大、每分鐘不需要那麼多心跳；不是心臟變小變弱或血量變少。"},{"id":"q0438","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A biopsy panel from elite competitors in several sports is compared. The elite distance runners are distinguished by the highest proportion of which fiber type?","options":["Type I, slow and red","Type IIx, fast and white","Type IIa transitioning toward IIx"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Type I, slow and red","explanation_en":"Type I fibers are slow, red, and highly oxidative; elite distance runners show a higher proportion of them.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"精英長跑選手的肌肉檢體中第一型（慢、紅、高氧化）纖維比例最高；IIx高是衝刺／爆發專案，IIa往IIx轉更不是長跑特徵。"},{"id":"q0439","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Endurance training improves a muscle's ability to extract and use oxygen. Which set of cellular changes primarily accounts for this?","options":["A rise in glycolytic enzyme activity that boosts anaerobic power","Increased mitochondrial size and number along with more myoglobin","Denser myofibrillar packing that raises contractile protein content"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Increased mitochondrial size and number along with more myoglobin","explanation_en":"Aerobic training raises mitochondrial size and number and myoglobin, enhancing the muscle's capacity to extract and use oxygen.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"周邊適應中「萃取與利用氧」能力的提升，主要來自粒線體大小與數量增加以及myoglobin增加；糖解酵素提升的是無氧能力，肌原纖維緻密化對應收縮力。"},{"id":"q0440","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Two marathoners have laboratory-measured maximal oxygen uptakes that are essentially equal, yet one consistently races faster. Which combination best explains the performance gap?","options":["A higher maximal heart rate allowing a faster finish","A greater proportion of Type IIx fibers","A higher lactate threshold together with better exercise economy"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A higher lactate threshold together with better exercise economy","explanation_en":"With equal VO2max, a higher lactate threshold and better exercise economy let an athlete sustain a higher pace and perform better.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩者VO2max相當時，較高的乳酸閾與較好的動作經濟性(Exercise economy)才能維持較快配速、跑出較好成績；最大心率較高或IIx比例較高都不是解釋。"},{"id":"q0441","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A coach starts two athletes on aerobic training: a truly untrained beginner and an already elite endurance competitor. Which pattern of maximal oxygen uptake improvement should the coach expect?","options":["About 20% for the untrained athlete versus about 5-10% for the elite athlete","About 50% for the untrained athlete versus about 40% for the elite athlete","Roughly the same percentage gain for both"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 20% for the untrained athlete versus about 5-10% for the elite athlete","explanation_en":"Untrained individuals may raise VO2max by up to about 20%, while elite athletes typically see only about 5-10%.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練對VO2max的提升幅度取決於起點：完全未受訓者可提升約20%，已達精英水準者通常只剩約5–10%；不會兩者一樣也不會各提升四、五成。"},{"id":"q0442","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"An endurance athlete's maximal oxygen uptake has plateaued after roughly 6 to 12 months, yet his race times keep dropping. Where do these continued performance gains mainly come from?","options":["A steadily rising maximal heart rate","Improved exercise economy and a higher lactate threshold","Ongoing large increases in maximal oxygen uptake"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Improved exercise economy and a higher lactate threshold","explanation_en":"Once VO2max plateaus, performance continues to improve through better exercise economy and an increased lactate threshold.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"VO2max在約6–12個月後進入高原，之後成績持續進步主要來自動作經濟性改善與乳酸閾提高，不是VO2max還在漲或最大心率上升。"},{"id":"q0443","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"An athlete recovering from a stress fracture wants an aerobic mode that also loads the skeleton to help build bone. Which choice provides the strongest osteogenic stimulus?","options":["Stationary cycling","Lap swimming","Running, which is high-impact and weight-bearing"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Running, which is high-impact and weight-bearing","explanation_en":"Running's repetitive high-impact weight-bearing loading promotes bone growth more than weight-supported cycling or swimming.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"要兼顧骨骼載重，高衝擊、承重的跑走對骨的成骨刺激最強；腳踏車與游泳大部分體重被支撐，對骨架的應變刺激小。"},{"id":"q0444","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A competitive cyclist who trains almost exclusively on the bike gets a DXA scan. What is a plausible finding regarding bone density at sites not loaded during cycling?","options":["Reduced density at non-locomotor sites, such as the lower spine","Density unchanged at every skeletal site","Uniformly increased density from the high training volume"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Reduced density at non-locomotor sites, such as the lower spine","explanation_en":"Non-weight-bearing activity places minimal skeletal strain and can reduce bone density, for example lower-spine density in cyclists.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"腳踏車是非承重運動、對骨骼應變小，非移動性部位（如腰椎下部）的骨密度可能反而較低；不會因訓練量大就全身一致增加，也不是各點完全不變。"},{"id":"q0445","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"At a given submaximal running pace, a well-trained endurance athlete relies on a different fuel mix than an untrained person. The training-induced shift is toward:","options":["Near-exclusive reliance on protein for fuel","Greater fat oxidation with sparing of carbohydrate stores","Greater carbohydrate oxidation with sparing of fat stores"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Greater fat oxidation with sparing of carbohydrate stores","explanation_en":"Trained muscle oxidizes more fat and spares glycogen, allowing higher-intensity exercise to be sustained longer.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在相同次最大強度下，受訓者轉向更多脂肪氧化、節省肝醣（碳水化合物）存量，才能以較高強度撐更久；不會接近全靠蛋白質，也不是更依賴碳水。"},{"id":"q0446","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A distance runner relocates to a high-altitude camp for several weeks. Which chronic adaptation should the coach expect as the body compensates for the lower oxygen pressure?","options":["Decreased capillary density in the working muscle","Reduced red blood cell production to conserve iron","Increased hemoglobin and red blood cell production"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increased hemoglobin and red blood cell production","explanation_en":"Chronic altitude exposure increases hemoglobin formation, red blood cell production, and capillarization to offset reduced oxygen pressure.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"慢性高原暴露的適應是血紅素生成、紅血球生成與微血管密度增加，以補償較低的氧分壓；不會是微血管減少或刻意少造紅血球省鐵。"},{"id":"q0447","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A team has trained and fully acclimatized at moderate altitude before an event held at the same elevation, well above 3,900 feet. Compared with sea level, their aerobic performance there will generally be:","options":["Still reduced relative to sea level","Identical to sea level once acclimatized","Better than at sea level thanks to acclimatization"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Still reduced relative to sea level","explanation_en":"Arterial oxygen saturation falls at altitude, so VO2max and aerobic performance remain reduced versus sea level even after acclimatizing.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"即使已在該高度充分acclimatize，超過3,900英呎的有氧表現（VO2max）較平地差：高原的動脈血氧飽和度低，適應無法完全抵銷。"},{"id":"q0448","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A soccer team spends two weeks training in the heat before a hot-climate tournament. Which cluster of chronic adaptations should the staff expect from successful heat acclimatization?","options":["Elevated resting and exercising core temperature","Expanded plasma volume, lower exercising heart rate and core temperature, and a higher sweat rate","Reduced plasma volume with decreased sweating to conserve fluid"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Expanded plasma volume, lower exercising heart rate and core temperature, and a higher sweat rate","explanation_en":"Heat acclimatization expands plasma volume, lowers heart rate and core temperature, and increases sweat rate and evaporative cooling.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱適應的慢性變化：血漿容量擴大、運動時心率與中樞溫度較低、流汗率與蒸發散熱提高；不是體溫升更高，也不是血漿縮少、減少流汗。"},{"id":"q0449","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"An athlete finishes a heat-acclimation block, then trains in cool conditions for the next month with no heat exposure. What becomes of the heat adaptations?","options":["They continue to strengthen even without heat exposure","They persist permanently once established","They are transient and decay over days to weeks"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"They are transient and decay over days to weeks","explanation_en":"Heat acclimation adaptations are transient and begin to dissipate within days to weeks, typically lost within about a month without exposure.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱適應得來得快、失得也快：離開熱環境後數天到數週即消退，通常一個月內大致消失，不會永久保留更不會持續增強。"},{"id":"q0450","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A coach is comparing why altitude camps and heat camps help endurance athletes. Which statement correctly contrasts their primary physiological mechanisms?","options":["Altitude mainly drives red cell and hemoglobin increases, while heat mainly expands plasma volume","Both operate through the identical adaptive pathway","Both act primarily by expanding plasma volume"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Altitude mainly drives red cell and hemoglobin increases, while heat mainly expands plasma volume","explanation_en":"Altitude (hypoxia) stimulates erythropoietin and red cell mass, while heat acclimation mainly expands plasma volume; the mechanisms differ.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高原與熱訓練的機制不同：高原（低氧）主要經紅血球生成素(erythropoietin)推升紅血球質量與血紅素；熱適應主要擴大血漿容量。兩者不是同一條適應路徑。"},{"id":"q0451","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"An athlete can afford one environmental training camp before a key competition held in hot, humid, low-altitude conditions. What should most guide the choice between an altitude and a heat protocol?","options":["Selecting whichever camp costs less, regardless of the event setting","Matching the protocol to the environment the athlete will compete in","Combining altitude and heat exposure to stack every possible benefit"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Matching the protocol to the environment the athlete will compete in","explanation_en":"Nonhematological adaptations are specific to the environment, so the protocol should match the conditions of the competition.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"環境適應要對準比賽環境選擇：非血液麵的適應具環境特異性。熱而潮濕的低海拔比賽，該選熱適應營，不是隻看價格或把高原＋熱全部疊加。"},{"id":"q0452","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A client who has switched from smoking to vaping asks whether it is cardiovascularly harmless. Which documented short-term effect should you cite?","options":["Decreases in heart rate and blood pressure","A reduction in systemic inflammation","Increases in heart rate and diastolic blood pressure"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increases in heart rate and diastolic blood pressure","explanation_en":"Nicotine-stimulated catecholamine release raises heart rate and diastolic blood pressure; vaping has clear short-term negative effects.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"短期文獻：尼古丁刺激兒茶酚胺釋放，使心率與舒張壓上升——換電子煙不等於對心血管無害，也看不到心率下降或抗發炎效果。"},{"id":"q0453","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"An endurance athlete who smokes has a normal hemoglobin level yet delivers less oxygen to working muscle than expected. Why does the carbon monoxide in cigarette smoke impair aerobic performance?","options":["It binds hemoglobin more strongly than oxygen does, cutting the oxygen actually carried","It raises the blood's oxygen-carrying capacity but blocks release at the tissues","It dilates the airways and hyperventilates the athlete"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It binds hemoglobin more strongly than oxygen does, cutting the oxygen actually carried","explanation_en":"Carbon monoxide has a higher affinity for hemoglobin than oxygen, forming carboxyhemoglobin and reducing oxygen delivery to muscle.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"吸煙者血紅素正常卻輸氧不足，因為CO與血紅素的親和力高於氧，形成碳氧血紅素(carboxyhemoglobin)、直接扣掉可用的帶氧容量；不是提升帶氧能力或擴張支氣管。"},{"id":"q0454","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A multisport athlete stops training entirely for four weeks. Which of her adaptations will regress the most, and for what reason, given that maximal oxygen uptake can fall 4-14% in that short a span?","options":["Maximal strength, because it is purely neural and quickly lost","Aerobic endurance adaptations, because of their enzymatic basis","Bone mineral density, because bone has slow turnover"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Aerobic endurance adaptations, because of their enzymatic basis","explanation_en":"Aerobic endurance adaptations are most sensitive to inactivity owing to their enzymatic basis, with VO2max falling 4-14% in just four weeks.","tags":["Chapter 6 quiz: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"全停4週內，退化最多的是有氧耐力適應（VO2max可掉4–14%），因為這些適應建立在酵素層面、更新快；最大肌力有神經成分、保留較久，骨質代謝緩慢不是短期主角。"},{"id":"q0455","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A coach records that a 12-year-old has advanced markedly toward the mature state of several body systems, even though he has not gotten much taller this year. Which term specifically captures this system-by-system progression toward the adult biological state?","options":["Growth","Maturation","Development"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Maturation","explanation_en":"Maturation is progress toward the mature biological state of the body's systems; growth is an increase in size, and development is the prenatal-to-adult progression.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"各身體系統朝向成人生物狀態進展的詞是成熟(maturation)；growth指尺寸增加，development指從胎期到成人的整體進展歷程。"},{"id":"q0456","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A practitioner tracks a young athlete's stature over several years and wants to identify the single point that reflects the fastest growth of the pubertal spurt. Peak height velocity is best described as which of the following?","options":["The predicted final adult stature the athlete will reach","The chronological age at which the epiphyseal plates fully close","The age at the maximum rate of growth during the pubertal growth spurt"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The age at the maximum rate of growth during the pubertal growth spurt","explanation_en":"PHV is the age at the maximum rate of growth during the pubertal growth spurt; predicted adult height and epiphyseal closure are separate concepts.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大身高速度(peak height velocity, PHV)是青春期成長突增中成長速率最快那個時間點（以年齡表示）；它不是預測的最終身高，也不是骨骺閉合的年齡。"},{"id":"q0457","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A coach oversees a mixed group of 11- to 14-year-olds and notices the girls hitting their growth spurt well before the boys. On average, how does the timing of peak height velocity differ by sex?","options":["Girls reach PHV about two years before boys","Both sexes reach PHV at essentially the same age","Boys reach PHV about two years before girls"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Girls reach PHV about two years before boys","explanation_en":"Girls reach PHV roughly two years earlier than boys (mean about 11.9 years vs 13.8 years).","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性平均比男性早約兩年達PHV（約11.9歲對13.8歲），所以11–14歲混合團體中女生普遍較早進入成長突增。"},{"id":"q0458","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"Two athletes on a youth team are both exactly 13 years old, yet one is clearly far more physically mature than the other. Why does this make chronological age a poor basis for classifying developmental stage?","options":["Children of the same age all mature at a constant, predictable rate","Two children of the same chronological age can differ biologically by up to five years","Chronological age is too difficult to measure accurately in youth"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Two children of the same chronological age can differ biologically by up to five years","explanation_en":"Large interindividual variation means two children of the same chronological age can differ biologically by up to five years, so programs must account for maturation.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成熟個體差異極大：同年紀（chronological age）的兩名兒童在生物成熟度上可相差達五歲，所以實際年齡不適合作為分組依據，課表必須考量成熟度。"},{"id":"q0459","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A pediatric researcher needs the single most accurate index of a child's biological maturation, cost and convenience aside. Which method is the gold standard?","options":["Somatic assessment using serial stature measurements","Sexual maturation (secondary sex characteristic) staging","Skeletal age assessment from a left-wrist radiograph"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Skeletal age assessment from a left-wrist radiograph","explanation_en":"Skeletal age, determined by comparing wrist radiographs against reference standards, is the gold standard for biological maturation, though impractical for most field settings.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"不計成本與便利性時，生物成熟度的黃金標準是骨骼年齢：以左腕X光與標準圖譜比較。它最準確但實務場域難施；身高序列與第二性徵分級都不是黃金標準。"},{"id":"q0460","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A high school coach with no medical equipment or budget wants a noninvasive, practical way to estimate the biological age of her athletes. Which approach best fits these constraints?","options":["Somatic assessment based on height measures","Skeletal age assessment via X-ray imaging","Sexual age assessment of secondary sex characteristics"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Somatic assessment based on height measures","explanation_en":"Somatic (stature-based) assessments are noninvasive, low-cost, and practical for field practitioners, unlike radiographs or intrusive sexual maturation staging.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"無裝置、無預算的場域從業人員適合以身高為基礎的體型(somatic)評估：非侵入、低成本、可執行；骨骼年齢要X光、性成熟分級侵入性較高。"},{"id":"q0461","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"In a growing child's long bone, one region acts as the primary ossification center and forms the central shaft. Which structure is this?","options":["The epiphysis, the growth region near the joint surface","The diaphysis, the central shaft of the bone","The apophysis, the site where a tendon inserts"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The diaphysis, the central shaft of the bone","explanation_en":"The diaphysis is the central shaft and primary ossification center of a long bone; the epiphysis and apophysis are separate growth-cartilage sites.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長骨的主骨化中心、形成中央骨幹的是骨幹(diaphysis)；骨骺(epiphysis，近關節面)與骨突(apophysis，肌腱附著處)是另外的軟骨生長部位。"},{"id":"q0462","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A clinician explaining injury-vulnerable regions to a youth coach notes that growth cartilage (the secondary ossification centers) sits at more than one site in a child's bones. Where is it found?","options":["Distributed uniformly throughout the entire bone","Only at the central shaft (diaphysis) of the bone","At the epiphyseal plate, the joint surface, and the apophyseal insertions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"At the epiphyseal plate, the joint surface, and the apophyseal insertions","explanation_en":"Growth cartilage occupies three sites: the epiphyseal plate, the joint (articular) surface, and the apophyseal insertions of muscle-tendon units.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"生長軟骨（次骨化中心）位於三處：骨骺板(epiphyseal plate)、關節面、以及肌腱附著的骨突(apophysis)——這三處都是兒童青少年動作傷害的脆弱點。"},{"id":"q0463","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A 9-year-old completes 12 weeks of supervised resistance training and gets clearly stronger, yet shows little change in limb girth. Which system is chiefly responsible for these gains?","options":["The neuromuscular system","The endocrine system, through elevated androgens","The skeletal system"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The neuromuscular system","explanation_en":"Preadolescents gain strength mainly through neural factors (improved motor unit activation, recruitment, and firing) rather than hypertrophy, because circulating androgens are low.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"青春期前兒童12週訓練後變強但圍度幾乎不變，因為增強主要來自神經肌肉系統（運動單位活化、動員、放電改善）； 迴圈雄激素低，肥大不是主角。"},{"id":"q0464","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A parent asks why her prepubescent son is getting stronger from training but not visibly building muscle like his older brother. What is the primary physiological reason?","options":["His nervous system is fully myelinated and can no longer adapt","He has inadequate levels of circulating anabolic hormones such as testosterone","He lacks the muscle fibers required for any hypertrophy"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"He has inadequate levels of circulating anabolic hormones such as testosterone","explanation_en":"Low circulating testosterone, growth hormone, and IGF in preadolescents limit hypertrophy, so their strength gains are predominantly neural.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"青春期前男孩練得變強卻不像兄長那樣明顯長肌肉，主因是睪固酮、生長激素、IGF等迴圈合成荷爾蒙不足，限制肥大，所以力量成長以神經為主；不是缺少肌纖維或神經已完全髓鞘化。"},{"id":"q0465","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A youth sport parent voices the usual concerns about kids and weights. Which of the following statements is actually TRUE and consistent with the evidence?","options":["Children gain no benefit from resistance training until they have entered puberty","Properly loaded resistance training stunts long-bone growth in children","With correct technique, appropriate loading, and supervision, resistance training is safe for youth"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"With correct technique, appropriate loading, and supervision, resistance training is safe for youth","explanation_en":"The claims that training stunts growth or must wait until puberty are myths; with proper technique, loading, and instruction, resistance training is safe and beneficial for youth.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"證據支援的說法：在正確技術、適當負荷與監督下，兒童青少年阻力訓練是安全的。「會壓矮個子」與「要等青春期」都是迷思。"},{"id":"q0466","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A new coach plans to run his 11-year-olds through a scaled-down version of his adult powerlifting program. Which principle, captured by 'children are not miniature adults,' should redirect his approach?","options":["Adult programs and training philosophies should not simply be superimposed on youth","Youth should train at adult intensities so they adapt faster","Once technique is learned, youth no longer need direct supervision"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Adult programs and training philosophies should not simply be superimposed on youth","explanation_en":"Adult programs are often too severe for children; youth programming must be matched to a child's physical, technical, and maturity level.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「兒童不是迷你成人」的含意：成人的課表與訓練哲學不能直接套在兒童身上；內容要符合兒童身體、技術與成熟程度。以成人強度操練或學完就撤除監督都違反這原則。"},{"id":"q0467","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A trainer is uncertain how much load a child new to resistance training can handle. Which starting philosophy best protects the child?","options":["Overestimate the child's abilities to accelerate early progress","Underestimate the child's abilities and progress volume and intensity gradually","Assign adult loads early to build the child's confidence"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Underestimate the child's abilities and progress volume and intensity gradually","explanation_en":"It is safer to underestimate a child's abilities and raise volume and intensity gradually than to risk injury by starting too heavy.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對初學的兒童，寧可低估其能力、再漸進增加容量與強度，也不要高估能力一開始就上太重而冒險；用成人重量建立自信是常見錯誤。"},{"id":"q0468","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"An older client shows progressive, generalized loss of skeletal muscle that his physician links to his recent falls and elevated mortality risk. Which condition does this describe?","options":["Osteoporosis","Dynapenia driven by muscle hypertrophy","Sarcopenia"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Sarcopenia","explanation_en":"Sarcopenia is the progressive, generalized loss of skeletal muscle mass associated with adverse outcomes such as falls, fractures, and mortality; osteoporosis concerns bone, not muscle.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"老化相關的進行性、全身性骨骼肌流失，伴隨跌倒、骨折與死亡率上升＝肌少症(sarcopenia)；骨質疏鬆講的是骨不是肌肉。"},{"id":"q0469","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A coach designing training for seniors notes that the ability to rise quickly from a chair fades faster than the ability to lift a heavy load slowly. How do power and strength change with aging?","options":["Power declines at a faster rate than strength","Strength declines at a faster rate than power","Power and strength decline at essentially the same rate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Power declines at a faster rate than strength","explanation_en":"Power recedes faster than strength with aging, which matters because many daily tasks demand rapid force production.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"老化時功率(power)比力量衰退得更快，這有功能意義：日常任務（快速從椅子站起）多依賴快速產生力量的能力。"},{"id":"q0470","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A DXA scan reports a client's bone mineral density at -2.8 standard deviations below the young adult mean. Which diagnostic category does this value place her in?","options":["Osteopenia","Osteoporosis","Normal bone density"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Osteoporosis","explanation_en":"A BMD below -2.5 SD of the young adult mean defines osteoporosis; -1 to -2.5 SD is osteopenia.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"骨密度T值-2.8（低於年輕成人均值2.5個標準差以上）屬骨質疏鬆症(osteoporosis)；-1至-2.5之間是骨質疏鬆前期(osteopenia)。"},{"id":"q0471","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A 72-year-old hypertensive client is straining and breath-holding during heavy leg press. Which practice should the coach specifically discourage in this senior trainee?","options":["Light static stretching after the session","A low-intensity aerobic warm-up before lifting","The Valsalva maneuver"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The Valsalva maneuver","explanation_en":"The Valsalva maneuver is discouraged in seniors because it causes a sudden spike in systolic and diastolic blood pressure.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"年長者（尤其高血壓者）應避免Valsalva：憋氣用力會讓收縮與舒張血壓驟升。課前低強度有氧暖身、課後輕度拉伸都無妨，問題在憋氣。"},{"id":"q0472","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A facility markets a seniors' program claiming that lifting weights by itself will keep members from falling. What is the accurate view of resistance training as a stand-alone fall-prevention method?","options":["Resistance training alone does not prevent falls and must be paired with balance and flexibility work","Resistance training increases fall risk in older adults and should be avoided","Resistance training on its own reliably prevents falls"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Resistance training alone does not prevent falls and must be paired with balance and flexibility work","explanation_en":"Resistance training alone does not prevent falls; it must be accompanied by balance and flexibility training.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練單獨使用不會預防跌倒：必須搭配平衡與柔軟度訓練；也不是會增加跌倒風險。宣稱「只舉重就不跌倒」的廣告說法不準確。"},{"id":"q0473","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"An older adult wants to increase muscular strength, power, and muscle mass. Of aerobic, balance, and resistance training, which modality uniquely delivers all three of those adaptations?","options":["All three modalities produce them equally","Resistance training","Aerobic training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Resistance training","explanation_en":"All three modalities benefit older adults, but only resistance training increases muscular strength, power, and muscle mass.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有氧、平衡、阻力三種訓練對長者都有益，但只有阻力訓練能同時增加肌力、功率與肌肉量。"},{"id":"q0474","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"A coach is writing the opening resistance prescription for a previously untrained 68-year-old. Which starting point is most appropriate before gradual progression?","options":["5 sets of 1 rep at about 95 percent 1RM beginning in the first session","Maximal singles paired with the Valsalva maneuver for trunk stability","1 set of 8 to 12 reps at about 40 to 50 percent 1RM, progressing later toward higher volume and intensity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1 set of 8 to 12 reps at about 40 to 50 percent 1RM, progressing later toward higher volume and intensity","explanation_en":"Seniors should begin around 1 set of 8 to 12 reps at 40 to 50 percent 1RM and progress gradually toward 3 sets at 60 to 80 percent 1RM.","tags":["Chapter 7 quiz: Age-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"未受訓練長者起始建議：約1組8–12次、強度約40–50% 1RM，之後漸進朝3組、60–80% 1RM；從第一天就5單組95%或大重量搭Valsalva都不合適。"},{"id":"q0475","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach compares average anthropometric profiles when adapting a program written for men to a group of women. Relative to adult males, which body composition profile do adult females tend to show on average?","options":["Less body fat, more muscle, and higher bone mineral density","Equal body fat and muscle but higher bone mineral density","More body fat, less muscle, and lower bone mineral density"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"More body fat, less muscle, and lower bone mineral density","explanation_en":"On average, adult females carry more body fat, less muscle, and lower bone mineral density than males, and are lighter.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"平均而言，成年女性對比男性體脂較高、肌肉較少、骨密度較低、體重較輕；編課時認知此平均差異，但仍要個體化。"},{"id":"q0476","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A strength coach working with young adult women wants to account for structural changes that are still ongoing into early adulthood. Which statement accurately describes this timeline?","options":["Growth plates typically close around age 20 and peak bone density is reached around age 30","Bone mineral density peaks at puberty and declines immediately afterward","The number of muscle fibers roughly doubles during a woman's twenties"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Growth plates typically close around age 20 and peak bone density is reached around age 30","explanation_en":"Growth plates generally close by about age 20 and peak bone mineral density is reached around age 30.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性結構發展時間軸：生長板通常約20歲前後閉合，尖峰骨密度約30歲前後達成；不是青春期就到骨密度高峰隨即下降，肌纖維數目也不會在二十幾歲增加一倍。"},{"id":"q0477","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A 34-year-old woman who has never done structured resistance training asks when, left unaddressed, her muscle mass and bone density will start to slip. What is the typical pattern?","options":["They do not begin declining until after age 70","They begin declining in the mid-30s and accelerate after about age 50","They begin declining immediately after puberty"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"They begin declining in the mid-30s and accelerate after about age 50","explanation_en":"Without a sustained resistance program, muscle mass and bone density begin declining in the mid-30s and accelerate after about age 50, particularly with menopause.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"若無持續阻力訓練，肌肉量與骨密度約30幾歲中期就開始下滑、50歲後加速（停經再加劇）；不會遲到70歲才開始，也不會青春期後立刻下降。"},{"id":"q0478","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"An athletic trainer reviews injury data across comparable sports. Although more ACL tears occur in males in absolute numbers, how does the relative rate of ACL injury in female athletes compare with males?","options":["It is about half that of males","It is about the same as males","It is about two times higher than males"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It is about two times higher than males","explanation_en":"Absolute ACL injury frequency is higher in males, but in comparable sports the female athletes' relative rate is about two times higher than males'.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"ACL受傷絕對件數男性較多，但在同類運動中女性選手的相對發生率約為男性的兩倍。"},{"id":"q0479","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach designing an ACL-injury-reduction program for female athletes wants to target the factor believed to contribute most to their elevated risk. Which factor should the program address?","options":["A neuromuscular deficiency that produces abnormal biomechanics such as increased dynamic knee valgus","Femoral notch size alone","Their higher absolute muscle mass"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A neuromuscular deficiency that produces abnormal biomechanics such as increased dynamic knee valgus","explanation_en":"Anatomical factors like notch size play a role, but a neuromuscular deficiency leading to dynamic knee valgus is considered the most significant, and it is trainable.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性ACL風險升高公認為最主要的貢獻因子，是導致異常力學（例如動態膝外翻）的神經肌肉控制缺陷——它可訓練； 股骨間窩(notch)寬度等構造因素有影響但屬次要。"},{"id":"q0480","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A clinic tracks anterior knee pain among its athletes. Compared with male athletes, how often does patellofemoral pain syndrome occur in female athletes?","options":["At the same rate","More than two times as often","About half as often"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"More than two times as often","explanation_en":"Female athletes are more than two times as likely to experience patellofemoral pain syndrome as male athletes.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性選手的髕股疼痛症候群(patellofemoral pain syndrome)發生率超過男性的兩倍。"},{"id":"q0481","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A researcher re-expresses raw strength scores relative to each participant's fat-free mass rather than total body mass. What happens to the apparent strength difference between the sexes?","options":["It stays essentially unchanged","It increases substantially","It tends to disappear"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It tends to disappear","explanation_en":"When strength is normalized to fat-free mass, sex-related differences tend to disappear, indicating the raw gap largely reflects body composition.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"把力量除以去脂體重(FFM)重新表達後，兩性間的表觀力量差距趨於消失——顯示原始差距主要反映身體組成（男性肌肉量較多），而非神經肌肉本質差異。"},{"id":"q0482","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach compares a female athlete's absolute strength with male norms and finds one region much nearer to male values than the other. Which comparison is accurate on average?","options":["Lower body strength is closer to male values than upper body strength","Upper body strength is closer to male values than lower body strength","Upper and lower body strength are equally close to male values"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Lower body strength is closer to male values than upper body strength","explanation_en":"Female lower body strength is generally closer to male values, whereas upper body strength remains relatively further below.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"平均而言女性的下肢力量較接近男性水準，上肢力量相對落差較大；不是上下肢差距相同，更不是上肢較接近男性。"},{"id":"q0483","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A trainer runs identical 12-week hypertrophy blocks for a man and a woman of similar training status. How does their relative muscle hypertrophy over this short-term period compare?","options":["Relative hypertrophy is greater in the female","Relative hypertrophy is similar between the sexes","Meaningful hypertrophy is not possible in the female"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Relative hypertrophy is similar between the sexes","explanation_en":"Over short-term programs (up to about 16 weeks), relative hypertrophy is similar between sexes, though absolute hypertrophy is greater in males.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"短期（約16週內）相同的肥大訓練區塊下，兩性的相對肌肉肥大幅度相似；只有絕對肥大量男性較大（起始肌肉量較大）。"},{"id":"q0484","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"An endurance coach notes that, on average, her female runners fatigue more slowly and rely more on fat oxidation. Which average fiber-type distribution helps explain this?","options":["A greater proportion of type II glycolytic fibers","A fiber distribution identical to males","A greater proportion of type I oxidative fibers"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A greater proportion of type I oxidative fibers","explanation_en":"Females average a greater proportion of type I oxidative fibers, so they oxidize more fat and are more fatigue resistant; males average slightly more type II fibers.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性平均第一型氧化型纖維比例較高，所以較能氧化脂肪、較抗疲勞；男性平均第二型纖維略多。這支援女子在耐力專案相對抗疲勞的表現。"},{"id":"q0485","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A physiologist measures the cortisol response to an identical acute training bout in matched male and female athletes. How does the female response typically compare?","options":["It is attenuated relative to males","It is entirely absent in females","It is greatly amplified relative to males"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It is attenuated relative to males","explanation_en":"The acute cortisol response is attenuated in females, in part because female sex hormones lower cortisol responsivity and sensitivity differs.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同樣急性訓練 bout 的皮質醇反應，女性整體較男性低(attenuated)——部分因女性性荷爾蒙降低皮質醇反應性；不是完全沒有反應或大於男性。"},{"id":"q0486","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach reads that men show a sharp acute testosterone spike after heavy lifting and wonders whether the same holds for his female athletes after a single session. What does the evidence indicate?","options":["Females show an immediate two- to fourfold acute rise in testosterone","Females do not show significant acute elevations in testosterone","Females' testosterone drops to undetectable levels after the bout"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Females do not show significant acute elevations in testosterone","explanation_en":"Females do not exhibit significant acute testosterone elevations after a resistance bout, although prolonged training can produce some acute increases.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性在一次阻力訓練後通常沒有顯著的急性睪固酮上升（長時間訓練才可能有小幅增加），不能套用男性大重量後的急性尖峰模型。"},{"id":"q0487","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"In a female athlete, blood is sampled shortly after a high-total-work resistance session. Which hormonal change is most expected in her circulating growth hormone?","options":["It falls below resting levels","It remains completely unchanged","It increases roughly two- to fourfold"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It increases roughly two- to fourfold","explanation_en":"Circulating growth hormone rises about two- to fourfold after an acute resistance bout in females, with magnitude depending on the stimulus and total work.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性完成高總功量阻力課後，迴圈生長激素約上升2–4倍；幅度取決於刺激型態與總功量。"},{"id":"q0488","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach explains to a female client why maintaining normal menstrual and hormonal function supports her training. What is estradiol's effect on skeletal muscle?","options":["It promotes protein synthesis over degradation and has a protective effect","It increases muscle damage and cell death with training","It negatively influences muscle contractile properties"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It promotes protein synthesis over degradation and has a protective effect","explanation_en":"Estradiol supports muscle mass by favoring protein synthesis over degradation and exerts a protective, antioxidant-like effect on muscle.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"雌二醇(estradiol)使肌肉蛋白合成大於分解、並有保護性（類似抗氧化）作用——維持正常月經與荷爾蒙功能對女性訓練有實質好處。"},{"id":"q0489","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach proposes rigidly periodizing every female athlete's loading to her menstrual cycle phase. What does the most recent evidence say about this practice?","options":["Programs should always be periodized to the menstrual cycle","Current evidence does not support modifying prescription based on cycle phase","Training should be stopped entirely during menstruation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Current evidence does not support modifying prescription based on cycle phase","explanation_en":"Recent meta-analyses found no systematic relationship between cycle phase and performance, so current evidence does not support phase-based prescription changes.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"近期證據（含統合分析）未見 менструal cycle 階段與表現的系統性關聯，目前不支援依週期階段機械式調整課表，更不必在經期停訓。"},{"id":"q0490","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A pregnant client in her second trimester wants to keep training core and upper body. Which modification is recommended as pregnancy advances?","options":["Emphasize supine core work to support the spine","Routinely train above 90 percent of maximum heart rate","Avoid supine positions in favor of incline, side-lying, or vertical positions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Avoid supine positions in favor of incline, side-lying, or vertical positions","explanation_en":"Supine positions later in pregnancy reduce venous return and cardiac output, so incline, side-lying, or vertical positions are recommended instead.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"後期懷孕避免仰臥：增大的子宮壓迫下腔靜脈、減少靜脈迴流與心輸出量；改用傾斜、側臥或直立姿勢。也不建議 慣常超過90%最大強度。"},{"id":"q0491","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach reviews pelvic health data for her female athletes. Compared with sedentary females, urinary incontinence in female athletes occurs at roughly what rate?","options":["About 2.7 times more often","About half as often","At the same rate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 2.7 times more often","explanation_en":"Urinary incontinence is reported about 2.7 times more often in female athletes than in sedentary females, and about 5 times more than in male athletes.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性運動員的尿失禁發生率約為不活動女性的2.7倍（約為男性運動員的5倍）——骨盆底功能是需要關注的議題。"},{"id":"q0492","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A return-to-play coordinator compares concussion outcomes between male and female athletes. How do female athletes' recovery patterns typically compare?","options":["Shorter recovery with fewer symptoms","Longer recovery with more prolonged symptoms","Identical recovery across all sports"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Longer recovery with more prolonged symptoms","explanation_en":"Female athletes tend to have longer recovery time and more prolonged symptoms after a concussion than males.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"腦震盪後恢復：女性運動員通常恢復時間較長、症狀較持久，重返場上的流程要更有耐心。"},{"id":"q0493","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A sport organization reviews athlete mental health research to allocate support resources. What does the evidence suggest about elite female athletes and depression?","options":["They report depression at about half the rate of male athletes","They show no difference in reported depression from male athletes","They are about twice as likely as male athletes to self-report depressive symptoms"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"They are about twice as likely as male athletes to self-report depressive symptoms","explanation_en":"Elite female athletes are about twice as likely to self-report depressive symptoms, and collegiate data show high rates of reported overwhelming anxiety.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"精英女性運動員自我回報憂鬱症狀的比率約為男性的兩倍；大學資料也顯示高比例的過度焦慮。"},{"id":"q0494","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Science","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"A coach is deciding how to build a resistance program for a specific female athlete. Given everything known about sex-related differences, what should most govern the design?","options":["Individualization to her specific needs, goals, and characteristics","Generalization based on typical demands of her sport","Matching her program to that of a comparable male teammate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Individualization to her specific needs, goals, and characteristics","explanation_en":"As with any athlete, individualization to the specific female athlete's needs is the most important design consideration.","tags":["Chapter 8 quiz: Sex-Related Differences and Their Implications for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"為女性選手設計課表時最重要的原則是個別化：依她個人的需求、目標與特質；性別平均值只能參考，不是照搬男性隊友的課表或套用泛化假設。"},{"id":"q0495","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A coach describes an athlete as being at a '3 out of 10' before a morning lift and a '9 out of 10' before a championship final, without judging either state as good or bad. The coach is describing which construct?","options":["Arousal, a value-neutral level of physiological and psychological activation on a continuum","State anxiety, the athlete's moment-to-moment sense of threat","Anxiety, since a heightened pre-competition state involves worry"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Arousal, a value-neutral level of physiological and psychological activation on a continuum","explanation_en":"Arousal is simply activation intensity, ranging from deep sleep to high excitement, and is not inherently pleasant or unpleasant.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":" arousal（喚醒）是價值中立的概念：生理與心理活化強度位於從深睡到高度興奮的連續光譜上，本身無好壞。「3分或9分」的描述是 arousal。"},{"id":"q0496","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete reports a racing mind and pounding heart before a match and clearly perceives the feeling as unpleasant. How is this state best classified relative to arousal?","options":["As arousal, which is itself one specific form of the broader category of anxiety","As anxiety, a negatively perceived subset of arousal with cognitive and somatic components","As a construct entirely separate from arousal and driven only by external threat"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"As anxiety, a negatively perceived subset of arousal with cognitive and somatic components","explanation_en":"Anxiety is a negatively perceived form of arousal that includes a cognitive component (worry) and a somatic component (physical symptoms).","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"焦慮是負向知覺的喚醒子集，包含認知成分（擔憂、負面想法）與軀體成分（心跳、肌肉緊繃等身體症狀）；「活化＋主觀不愉快」就是焦慮而非中性的 arousal。"},{"id":"q0497","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete reads threat into a wide range of unrelated situations year after year, on and off the field, regardless of the actual stakes. This enduring pattern reflects a high level of what?","options":["Eustress, a facilitative interpretation of demanding situations","State anxiety, an intense reaction confined to a specific threatening moment","Trait anxiety, a stable personality disposition to perceive many situations as threatening"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Trait anxiety, a stable personality disposition to perceive many situations as threatening","explanation_en":"Trait anxiety is a personality disposition, whereas state anxiety is the moment-to-moment experience of apprehension.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長年、跨情境地把大量無關情況都解讀成威脅＝特質焦慮(trait anxiety)，是穩定的人格傾向；狀態焦慮只發生在特定威脅時刻，eustress是正向解讀。"},{"id":"q0498","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Right before the start gun, a sprinter notices tense muscles, a pounding heart, and a churning stomach, but no specific worried thoughts. Which component of anxiety is being reported?","options":["Somatic anxiety, the physical and physiological manifestations of the state","Achievement motivation, the drive to master a challenging task","Cognitive anxiety, the worry and negative thoughts about performance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Somatic anxiety, the physical and physiological manifestations of the state","explanation_en":"Somatic anxiety is the physical reaction; cognitive anxiety refers to the mental worries and negative thoughts.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉緊繃、心悸、胃部翻攪而沒有明確擔憂想法＝軀體焦慮(somatic anxiety)的生理表現；認知焦慮(cognitive anxiety)指的是擔憂與負面思考。"},{"id":"q0499","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"As an athlete's activation climbs from calm toward moderate, performance improves; but as it keeps rising past a certain point, performance falls off. Which explanation matches this pattern?","options":["Drive theory, in which performance keeps rising as arousal rises","The inverted-U relationship, with performance peaking at a moderate, optimal level of arousal","Reversal theory, in which the effect of arousal depends on how it is interpreted"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The inverted-U relationship, with performance peaking at a moderate, optimal level of arousal","explanation_en":"The inverted-U theory (Yerkes and Dodson) describes a curvilinear relationship with an optimal midpoint of arousal.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"活化上升到中等時表現進步、越過某點後下滑，對應倒U理論(Yerkes-Dodson)：曲線關係、在最適中等喚醒達峰。drive theory是直線上升，與此描述不符。"},{"id":"q0500","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A coach claims that pumping athletes up more and more will always yield better and better performance. Which theory does this reasoning reflect, and what relationship does it assume?","options":["Catastrophe theory, which assumes a sudden collapse once arousal passes a threshold","IZOF, which assumes an optimal bandwidth of functioning rather than a single trend","Drive theory, which assumes performance rises directly and linearly with arousal"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Drive theory, which assumes performance rises directly and linearly with arousal","explanation_en":"Drive theory holds that as arousal increases, performance increases linearly, which is now seen as overly simplistic.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「越激勵越好」反映drive theory（驅力理論）：假設表現隨喚醒直線、線性提升；現代觀點認為過於簡化。catastrophe theory講的是高認知焦慮下的驟崩，IZOF講的是個人帶狀區間。"},{"id":"q0501","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Two teammates perform their best at clearly different arousal levels, and neither peaks at the same intensity as the other. Which theory best accounts for this, and why?","options":["IZOF, because ideal performance falls within an individualized bandwidth of arousal that differs by athlete","Drive theory, because within a sport the optimal arousal level is essentially identical for everyone","The inverted-U, because everyone peaks precisely at the exact midpoint of the arousal continuum"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"IZOF, because ideal performance falls within an individualized bandwidth of arousal that differs by athlete","explanation_en":"IZOF holds that ideal performance occurs within a small individualized range of arousal rather than at a single universal point.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"IZOF（個人最適功能區間）主張理想表現落在各運動員自己的窄幅喚醒區間，正好解釋兩人最佳狀態不同；drive theory假設同專案內人人相同，倒U假設人人都在正中點，都解釋不了個體差異。"},{"id":"q0502","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Two athletes feel the same racing heart before a final; one calls it 'excitement' and thrives, the other calls it 'dread' and struggles. Which theory best explains why identical arousal produces opposite results?","options":["Catastrophe theory, which stresses a sharp performance drop when cognitive anxiety is high","Reversal theory, which holds that the effect of arousal depends on how the individual interprets it","Drive theory, which holds that higher arousal directly raises performance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Reversal theory, which holds that the effect of arousal depends on how the individual interprets it","explanation_en":"Kerr's reversal theory emphasizes that one athlete may read high arousal as excitement while another reads it as anxiety.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"reversal theory（反轉理論）認為喚醒的效果取決於個人如何解讀：同樣心悸，解讀成興奮就表現好、解讀成恐懼就失常。catastrophe theory強調的是高認知焦慮下表現驟崩，焦點不同。"},{"id":"q0503","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A beginner is drilling a brand-new, coordination-heavy lift for the first time. Compared with an expert performing a well-learned skill, where should the beginner's optimal arousal generally sit, and why?","options":["Higher, because a novice needs extra activation to compensate for weak technique","The same, because optimal arousal is set by the task and is unaffected by skill level","Lower, because worry competes for the attention the beginner still needs for motor details"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Lower, because worry competes for the attention the beginner still needs for motor details","explanation_en":"Less skilled athletes have a lower optimal arousal point because worry competes with attention already occupied by motor details.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"初學新技能時最適喚醒應設得較低：擔心會與動作細節爭奪已經被佔用的注意力；專家動作已自動化，可以承受較高喚醒。"},{"id":"q0504","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete keeps training hard purely because she loves the sport and feels competent doing it, even after her scholarship and prize money were cut. This best illustrates what?","options":["Intrinsic motivation, arising from within and tied to competence and self-determination","Negative reinforcement, which removes an aversive stimulus to sustain behavior","Extrinsic motivation, driven by tangible external rewards"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Intrinsic motivation, arising from within and tied to competence and self-determination","explanation_en":"Intrinsic motivation comes from within and is tied to competence and self-determination rather than external rewards.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"獎學金與獎金都拿掉仍因熱愛與勝任感持續苦練＝內在動機(intrinsic motivation)，源自內在、與勝任感和自主性有關；外在動機依靠可觀測的外部獎賞。"},{"id":"q0505","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete high in the motive to avoid failure repeatedly ducks challenging matchups and downplays effort. According to this construct, what is he fundamentally trying to escape?","options":["Any external reward that might make the outcome feel less personal","The sense of shame and embarrassment that accompanies failing","Easy contests that offer little chance to demonstrate skill"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The sense of shame and embarrassment that accompanies failing","explanation_en":"MAF is less about avoiding failure itself and more about avoiding the shame associated with failing.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高MAF（避免失敗動機）者逃避挑戰、不全力以赴，動機核心是逃避失敗帶來的羞恥與難堪，不是害怕失敗事件本身，也不是討厭太簡單的比賽。"},{"id":"q0506","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"After the team hustles hard in practice, the coach announces they can skip the dreaded conditioning sprints they normally run. Hustle increases going forward. This best illustrates which operant principle?","options":["Positive reinforcement, adding a rewarding stimulus to increase a desired behavior","Positive punishment, adding an aversive consequence to reduce a behavior","Negative reinforcement, removing an aversive stimulus to increase a desired behavior"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Negative reinforcement, removing an aversive stimulus to increase a desired behavior","explanation_en":"Negative reinforcement removes an aversive stimulus to increase the likelihood of a desired behavior.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"撤除厭惡刺激（免跑衝刺）讓理想行為（努力練習）增加＝負增強(negative reinforcement)。正增強是給予獎勵；正懲罰是給予厭惡後果以降低行為。"},{"id":"q0507","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A batter learns to tune out crowd noise and the scoreboard so he can lock onto the pitcher's release point. This deliberate filtering of task-irrelevant cues is called:","options":["Selective attention, the suppression of task-irrelevant stimuli to process relevant cues","Counterconditioning, replacing one learned response with an incompatible one","Diaphragmatic breathing, a controlled technique for lowering arousal"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Selective attention, the suppression of task-irrelevant stimuli to process relevant cues","explanation_en":"Selective attention, commonly called focus, filters out distractions within the limited capacity of working memory.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"主動過濾觀眾噪音與計分板等無關線索、鎖定投手出手點＝選擇性注意力(selective attention，即「專注」)：在工作記憶容量有限下抑制無關刺激。"},{"id":"q0508","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A lifter now performs a once-difficult movement smoothly while carrying on a conversation, giving it almost no conscious thought. In the Fitts and Posner framework, which stage of learning is this?","options":["The associative stage, marked by refining and reducing gross errors","The autonomous stage, in which the skill runs automatically without conscious attention","The cognitive stage, marked by effortful, deliberate problem solving"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The autonomous stage, in which the skill runs automatically without conscious attention","explanation_en":"The stages progress from cognitive (effortful thought) to associative to automaticity, where the skill runs without deliberate attention.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Fitts與Posner三階段：認知期（費力思考）→聯想期（修飾錯誤）→自動期(autonomous)：動作自動化、不需意識注意，可以邊聊天邊完成。"},{"id":"q0509","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An overaroused athlete uses slow, deep belly breathing and reports a slower heart rate and looser muscles. This calming effect is achieved primarily by shifting autonomic balance toward which system?","options":["The sympathetic nervous system, mobilizing a fight-or-flight response","The somatic motor system, driving voluntary skeletal muscle contraction","The parasympathetic nervous system, increasing vagal tone"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The parasympathetic nervous system, increasing vagal tone","explanation_en":"Deep, controlled breathing emphasizes parasympathetic activity and vagal tone, lowering heart rate and muscle tension.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"緩慢深腹式呼吸透過提高副交感神經活動與迷走張力降低心率與肌張力；交感神經是戰或逃方向，與休息方向相反；軀體運動系統管隨意收縮，不是鎮靜機制。"},{"id":"q0510","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete learns to manage physical tension by deliberately contracting one muscle group hard, releasing it, and moving to the next group in sequence. Which technique is this?","options":["Progressive muscle relaxation, tensing then relaxing muscle groups in sequence","Systematic desensitization, pairing feared images with a relaxation response","Autogenic training, imagining warmth and heaviness in each limb"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Progressive muscle relaxation, tensing then relaxing muscle groups in sequence","explanation_en":"PMR cycles through tensing each muscle group briefly and then consciously relaxing it to learn to control somatic tension.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"依序把各肌群用力收縮再放鬆、輪完全身＝漸進式肌肉放鬆(PMR)，用來辨識並控制軀體緊張；系統減敏感要搭配焦慮情境階層，autogenic training用的是溫度與重量意象。"},{"id":"q0511","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A sport psychologist helps an athlete stay relaxed while imagining an ordered list of increasingly stressful competition scenes, so the calm response replaces the fear response to each cue. This describes:","options":["Self-talk, using structured internal statements to guide performance","Systematic desensitization, counterconditioning relaxation to a hierarchy of feared scenes","Autogenic training, self-inducing sensations of warmth and heaviness"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Systematic desensitization, counterconditioning relaxation to a hierarchy of feared scenes","explanation_en":"Systematic desensitization uses counterconditioning to pair relaxation with progressively more threatening images.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在放鬆狀態下按階層想像由低到高的焦慮比賽情境，讓放鬆反應取代恐懼反應＝系統減敏感(systematic desensitization)，原理是反條件化(counterconditioning)。"},{"id":"q0512","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"An athlete is generally confident but says, 'I know I can hit this specific free throw, right now, in this situation.' Which Bandura construct does that belief represent?","options":["Trait anxiety, a stable disposition to perceive situations as threatening","A general trait-like love of competing","Self-efficacy, the perceived ability to perform a specific task in a specific situation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Self-efficacy, the perceived ability to perform a specific task in a specific situation","explanation_en":"Self-efficacy is a situationally specific form of self-confidence and is a strong predictor of task execution.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「我現在、這個情境、這一次罰投能進」＝自我效能(self-efficacy)：對特定情境完成特定任務的主觀能力判斷，是情境特定的自信，對任務表現預測力強。"},{"id":"q0513","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Instead of targeting a first-place finish, a coach has an athlete focus on executing specific daily technique and effort standards she can directly control. What kind of goal is this?","options":["A process goal, focused on controllable actions and technique","A long-term goal, defined mainly by its distant time horizon","An outcome goal, focused on the end result relative to competitors"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A process goal, focused on controllable actions and technique","explanation_en":"Process goals target controllable actions, so success is strongly contingent on the athlete's own effort.","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"不盯名次、改盯每天能控制的技術與努力標準＝過程目標(process goal)：成功高度取決於自己的執行；結果目標看的是與對手比較後的最終結果。"},{"id":"q0514","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"A coach observes an athlete's practice effort has visibly dropped, while the athlete separately reports feeling drained and unmotivated. Which pairing correctly labels the observed cue versus the reported one?","options":["The reported feeling is the sign, and the visible drop in effort is the symptom","The visible drop in effort is the sign, and the reported feeling is the symptom","Both are symptoms, because signs must involve a clinical diagnosis to count"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The visible drop in effort is the sign, and the reported feeling is the symptom","explanation_en":"Signs are observable by the coach (such as reduced effort), while symptoms are self-reported feelings (such as fatigue).","tags":["Chapter 9 quiz: Psychological Foundations of Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Sign（徵象）是教練可觀察到的（練習表現下滑）；symptom（症狀）是運動員自述的感受（疲勞、沒動力）。把觀察到的叫症狀、自述的叫徵象就顛倒了。"},{"id":"q0515","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete with a diagnosed medical condition needs an individualized meal plan that accounts for her disease and heavy training. Who is the appropriate professional to provide and manage this advice?","options":["The strength and conditioning professional, offering general nutrition coaching within scope","A sports dietitian, a registered dietitian with sport nutrition expertise","The athletic trainer, coordinating her return-to-play and injury care"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A sports dietitian, a registered dietitian with sport nutrition expertise","explanation_en":"A sports dietitian is a registered dietitian with sports nutrition expertise and is the appropriate referral for complex or medical nutrition needs.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有疾病又高訓練負荷、需要個體化飲食規劃，應轉介運動營養師（具運動營養專長、已登記的營養師，RD）；肌力與體能專業者只能在專業範圍內做一般營養指導。"},{"id":"q0516","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A coach wants to teach athletes to build meals around the current federal food-group icon. Which set correctly lists the groups that icon depicts?","options":["Proteins, carbohydrates, fats, and water","Macronutrients, micronutrients, and water","Fruits, vegetables, grains, protein foods, and dairy"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Fruits, vegetables, grains, protein foods, and dairy","explanation_en":"MyPlate illustrates five groups: fruits, vegetables, grains, protein foods, and dairy or fortified soy alternatives.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"MyPlate的五大食物群：水果、蔬菜、穀物、蛋白質食物（肉蛋豆堅果）、乳品（或強化豆製品）；不是以三大營養素或宏量／微量分類。"},{"id":"q0517","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A sedentary 70 kg adult wants the daily protein intake set by the RDA. Which target is correct, and how many grams does that translate to?","options":["0.8 g/kg/day, or about 56 g per day","1.4 g/kg/day, or about 98 g per day","2.0 g/kg/day, or about 140 g per day"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"0.8 g/kg/day, or about 56 g per day","explanation_en":"The protein RDA for adults 19 and older is 0.8 g/kg/day based on nitrogen balance studies; athletes need more.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成人（19歲以上）蛋白質RDA為0.8 g/kg/日（依氮平衡研究訂定），70 kg約56 g/日；這是 sedentary 成人的底標，運動員需求更高。"},{"id":"q0518","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An 80 kg strength athlete wants a daily protein target that supports building and maintaining muscle. Which range fits, and what daily amount does it imply?","options":["0.8 to 1.0 g/kg, or roughly 64 to 80 g per day","1.4 to 2.0 g/kg, or roughly 112 to 160 g per day","3.0 to 4.0 g/kg, or roughly 240 to 320 g per day"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1.4 to 2.0 g/kg, or roughly 112 to 160 g per day","explanation_en":"An overall intake of 1.4 to 2.0 g/kg/day supports a positive muscle protein balance for building and maintaining mass.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"支援增肌與維持肌肉量的攝取約1.4–2.0 g/kg/日，可維持正肌肉蛋白平衡；80 kg即約112–160 g/日。3 g以上屬過度，0.8–1.0只是一般成人水準。"},{"id":"q0519","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete eats 20 g of carbohydrate, 10 g of protein, and 10 g of fat in a snack. Which macronutrient contributes the most calories, given fat's energy density?","options":["Protein, since it supplies about 9 kcal per gram","Carbohydrate, since it supplies about 9 kcal per gram","Fat, since it supplies about 9 kcal per gram"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Fat, since it supplies about 9 kcal per gram","explanation_en":"Fat yields about 9 kcal/g, more than double the roughly 4 kcal/g from carbohydrate or protein.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱量密度：脂肪約9 kcal/g，碳水與蛋白質各約4 kcal/g；點心內脂肪10 g=90 kcal，高於碳水20 g=80 kcal與蛋白質10 g=40 kcal。說碳水或蛋白質9 kcal/g是錯的。"},{"id":"q0520","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A dietitian explains that some amino acids must be supplied by the diet because the body cannot synthesize them. How many amino acids fall into that essential category?","options":["Nine","Four","Seven"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Nine","explanation_en":"Nine amino acids are essential and must come from the diet; four are nonessential and seven are conditionally essential.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"必需胺基酸有9種，必須由飲食攝取；另有4種非必需、7種條件性必需。"},{"id":"q0521","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A vegan athlete asks which of her plant options counts as a complete, high-quality protein. What two properties define such a source?","options":["It comes exclusively from animal foods and never from plants","It is highly digestible and provides all of the essential amino acids","It is low in nitrogen and missing several essential amino acids"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It is highly digestible and provides all of the essential amino acids","explanation_en":"High-quality proteins are highly digestible and supply all essential amino acids; animal foods plus soy, quinoa, and buckwheat qualify.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高品質（完全）蛋白的定義：高消化率且含全部必需胺基酸；除動物性食物外，大豆、quinoa（藜麥）、蕎麥也屬此類；不是「只能來自動物」。"},{"id":"q0522","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"Of the body's total glycogen stores, the largest share is held where, and roughly what fraction sits there?","options":["Adipose tissue, holding roughly three-quarters of the total","The liver, holding roughly three-quarters of the total","Skeletal muscle, holding roughly three-quarters of the total"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Skeletal muscle, holding roughly three-quarters of the total","explanation_en":"About three-quarters of body glycogen is stored in skeletal muscle and the remaining quarter in the liver.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"體內肝醣約四分之三存在骨骼肌，約四分之一在肝臟；脂肪組織以三酸甘油酯為主，不是肝醣儲存庫。"},{"id":"q0523","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"Two foods have the same total carbohydrate grams, but one spikes blood glucose fast and the other raises it slowly. Which property distinguishes them?","options":["Their glycemic index, which ranks how quickly a food raises blood glucose","Their total calorie content, which sets the size of the glucose response","Their total fiber content, which alone determines the glycemic ranking"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Their glycemic index, which ranks how quickly a food raises blood glucose","explanation_en":"The GI ranks how rapidly a carbohydrate food raises blood glucose relative to a reference food such as glucose or white bread.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同樣碳水化合物克數、升血糖快慢不同，是以血糖指數(glycemic index, GI)區分：相對於基準食物（葡萄糖或白麵包）來量化升糖速度。熱量或纖維含量都不是GI的定義。"},{"id":"q0524","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A high-glycemic-index food eaten in a very small portion may produce only a modest blood glucose rise. Which measure captures this better than glycemic index alone, and why?","options":["Glycemic load, because it disregards how much carbohydrate is actually eaten","Glycemic load, because it factors in the grams of carbohydrate in the portion consumed","Glycemic load, because it is fixed to a single standard serving regardless of intake"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Glycemic load, because it factors in the grams of carbohydrate in the portion consumed","explanation_en":"Glycemic load multiplies GI by the grams of carbohydrate per serving and divides by 100, factoring in portion size.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"血糖負荷(glycemic load, GL)=GI×該份量實際攝取碳水克數÷100，把攝取量納入計算：高GI食物吃很少時總體升糖反應可能不大，GL才能反映實際影響；GL不是固定份量的常數。"},{"id":"q0525","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete taking a high-dose supplement worries about accumulating a vitamin in body fat over time. Which group of vitamins is fat-soluble and can be stored this way?","options":["Vitamin C and folate","The B-complex vitamins and vitamin C","Vitamins A, D, E, and K"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Vitamins A, D, E, and K","explanation_en":"Vitamins A, D, E, and K are fat-soluble and stored in fat tissue, while B vitamins and C are water-soluble.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"脂溶性維生素A、D、E、K可儲存於脂肪組織，高劑量有累積疑慮；B群與維生素C為水溶性，會隨尿排出。"},{"id":"q0526","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete on a 3,000 kcal diet wants to keep saturated fat within cardiovascular guidelines. Which ceiling should he stay under, and what does that equal here?","options":["Under 10% of calories, or about 300 kcal from saturated fat","Under 25% of calories, or about 750 kcal from saturated fat","Under 35% of calories, or about 1,050 kcal from saturated fat"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Under 10% of calories, or about 300 kcal from saturated fat","explanation_en":"Guidelines recommend keeping saturated fat under 10% of calories and replacing it with unsaturated fats.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"心臟指引建議飽和脂肪低於總熱量10%，並以不飽和脂肪取代；3,000 kcal的10%=300 kcal。25%或35%是一般脂肪的比例而非飽和脂肪上限。"},{"id":"q0527","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"Two athletes consume identical amounts of iron, one mostly from red meat and one mostly from spinach and legumes. Which form is absorbed more efficiently?","options":["The nonheme iron from the plant foods","The heme iron from the animal foods","Neither, because both forms are absorbed at the same rate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The heme iron from the animal foods","explanation_en":"Heme iron from animal foods is absorbed better, while only about 2 to 20% of nonheme iron is absorbed.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"動物性食物的血紅素鐵(heme iron)吸收率明顯優於植物性非血紅素鐵（後者僅約2–20%吸收），所以吃紅肉者的鐵吸收較佳。"},{"id":"q0528","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A vegetarian athlete wants to boost the absorption of iron from a lentil meal. Which addition to that meal will help the most?","options":["A cup of black tea for its tannins","A glass of milk for calcium","A citrus fruit for vitamin C"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A citrus fruit for vitamin C","explanation_en":"Vitamin C enhances nonheme iron absorption, whereas calcium, tannins, and phytates decrease it.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"維生素C（柑橘類）能顯著提升非血紅素鐵吸收；紅茶單寧、牛奶鈣質與植酸都會降低吸收，所以要避免同餐攝取。"},{"id":"q0529","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A coach screening a squad for iron deficiency and iron deficiency anemia should recognize that the risk is several times higher in which group?","options":["Female athletes","Older male endurance athletes","Male power athletes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Female athletes","explanation_en":"Iron deficiency is five to seven times more common in female athletes than male athletes.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"女性運動員缺鐵與缺鐵性貧血風險約為男性運動員的5–7倍（月經流失、攝取不足與運動相關流失疊加），篩檢時應優先留意。"},{"id":"q0530","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A 70 kg athlete loses fluid through sweat during a workout. About how much body-weight loss is enough to begin meaningfully impairing performance, and what is that in this athlete?","options":["Less than 0.5%, or under about 0.35 kg","2% to 3%, or roughly 1.4 to 2.1 kg","8% to 10%, or roughly 5.6 to 7 kg"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"2% to 3%, or roughly 1.4 to 2.1 kg","explanation_en":"Even mild dehydration of 2% to 3% body-weight loss raises core temperature and significantly degrades performance.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"脫水達體重2–3%即會升高體溫、顯著損害表現；70 kg對應約1.4–2.1 kg的體重流失。0.5%太輕，8–10%屬嚴重脫水範圍。"},{"id":"q0531","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"During a long endurance event, an athlete drinks large volumes of plain water and takes in almost no sodium. Which dangerous condition is this most likely to cause?","options":["Iron toxicity, from excess mineral accumulation","Hyperglycemia, from elevated blood glucose","Hyponatremia, from diluted blood sodium"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hyponatremia, from diluted blood sodium","explanation_en":"Excess low-sodium fluid can dilute blood sodium dangerously low, causing hyponatremia and intracellular swelling.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長時間運動大量喝低鈉液體會把血鈉稀釋到危險低位＝低血鈉症(hyponatremia)，嚴重時細胞腫脹（尤其腦細胞）；與鐵累積或血糖無關。"},{"id":"q0532","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"A coach is formulating a drink for athletes exercising for a long time in the heat. Which carbohydrate concentration is recommended to aid both fueling and fluid uptake?","options":["About 5% to 10%","About 20% to 30%","Less than 1%"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 5% to 10%","explanation_en":"Guidelines recommend a 5% to 10% carbohydrate concentration along with sodium and a small amount of potassium.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長距離／長時間運動建議飲料碳水濃度約5–10%，並含鈉與少量鉀：能兼顧供能與水分吸收；20–30%太濃會延遲胃排空，低於1%供能不足。"},{"id":"q0533","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete lost 2 kg of body weight to sweat and has only a short window before the next session. Roughly how much fluid should he drink per kilogram lost, and what total does that give?","options":["About 4 L per kilogram, so roughly 8 L total","About 1.5 L per kilogram, so roughly 3 L total","About 0.25 L per kilogram, so roughly 0.5 L total"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 1.5 L per kilogram, so roughly 3 L total","explanation_en":"About 1.5 L (or 0.7 L per pound) per kilogram lost accounts for the extra urine output from rapid rehydration.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"快速補液要按流失每公斤喝約1.5 L（每磅約0.7 L），多出的部分是因快速補液會增加排尿；流失2 kg要喝約3 L。4 L/kg過量，0.25 L/kg不足。"},{"id":"q0534","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"An athlete wants to know the highest daily amount of a nutrient, from all sources, that is still unlikely to cause harm. Which Dietary Reference Intake answers this?","options":["The Recommended Dietary Allowance, which meets the needs of most healthy people","The Adequate Intake, an estimate used when an RDA cannot be set","The Tolerable Upper Intake Level, the maximum intake not associated with adverse effects"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The Tolerable Upper Intake Level, the maximum intake not associated with adverse effects","explanation_en":"The UL is the highest average daily intake, from all sources, not associated with adverse health effects.","tags":["Chapter 10 quiz: Basic Nutritional Factors Affecting Health"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"可承受最高攝取量是Tolerable Upper Intake Level(UL)：所有來源合計、不會出現不良健康效應的最高平均每日攝取量。RDA是滿足多數健康人需求的建議量，AI是無法訂RDA時的替代估計。"},{"id":"q0535","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A cyclist eats his usual meal 3 hours before a road race. What should that meal primarily accomplish to support his performance?","options":["Add bulk and fiber so the stomach empties slowly and releases fuel gradually","Blunt hunger and shift metabolism toward burning fat during the event","Deliver fluid for hydration along with carbohydrate to top off blood glucose and glycogen"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Deliver fluid for hydration along with carbohydrate to top off blood glucose and glycogen","explanation_en":"The precompetition meal mainly supplies fluid for hydration and carbohydrate to top off blood glucose and glycogen stores.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"賽前3-4小時這餐的主要任務是補充水分、並以碳水化合物把血糖與肝糖儲量填滿,維持比賽期間的血糖供應。想靠大量纖維「慢慢釋放燃料」恰恰是賽前該避免的做法,因為那會拖慢胃排空。"},{"id":"q0536","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"An athlete asks why his pre-event meal guide steers him away from high-fat, high-fiber choices. What is the best rationale?","options":["Fat and fiber slow gastric emptying, so limiting them speeds stomach clearance and reduces GI distress during exercise","Fat and fiber interfere with the muscle's ability to store the meal's carbohydrate as glycogen","Fat and fiber lower the meal's glycemic index, which must be raised to fuel performance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Fat and fiber slow gastric emptying, so limiting them speeds stomach clearance and reduces GI distress during exercise","explanation_en":"Both fat and fiber slow digestion, so keeping them low helps the stomach empty quickly and minimizes cramping during exercise.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"脂肪與纖維都會減慢消化與胃排空,賽前少吃兩者可讓胃快速排空,減少運動中胃腸不適與抽筋。它們並不妨礙肌肉把碳水化合物合成成肝糖,也不是為了抬高血糖指數。"},{"id":"q0537","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"As an athlete's exercise intensity climbs, at roughly what point does muscle glycogen become the dominant fuel over fat?","options":["Once intensity passes about 40 percent of VO2max","Once intensity passes about 70 percent of VO2max","Only once intensity nears about 90 percent of VO2max"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Once intensity passes about 70 percent of VO2max","explanation_en":"Glycogen is the main energy form used during high-intensity exercise above about 70 percent of VO2max.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動強度超過約70% VO2max後,肌肝糖取代脂肪成為主要燃料;強度越高,碳水氧化的比例越高。"},{"id":"q0538","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"For an 80 kg athlete, roughly what total glycogen store would you estimate the liver and muscle can hold combined?","options":["About 4,000 grams (near 50 g per kilogram)","About 400 grams (near 5 g per kilogram)","About 1,200 grams (near 15 g per kilogram)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 1,200 grams (near 15 g per kilogram)","explanation_en":"Liver and muscle together store roughly 15 grams of glycogen per kilogram of body weight, so an 80 kg athlete holds about 1,200 grams.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肝臟與肌肉合計約儲存每公斤體重15克肝糖,80公斤運動員約可達1,200克,這是估算總肝糖儲量的標準演算法。"},{"id":"q0539","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A 70 kg marathoner following a classic carbohydrate-loading regimen should target roughly what daily carbohydrate intake?","options":["About 560 to 700 grams per day (8 to 10 g per kilogram)","About 1,050 to 1,400 grams per day (15 to 20 g per kilogram)","About 210 to 350 grams per day (3 to 5 g per kilogram)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 560 to 700 grams per day (8 to 10 g per kilogram)","explanation_en":"A common loading regimen uses 8 to 10 grams of carbohydrate per kilogram per day to raise muscle glycogen 20 to 40 percent above normal.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統肝糖填充法要求每天攝取每公斤體重8-10克碳水化合物,70公斤跑者約560-700克,可把肌肉肝糖提高約20-40%。"},{"id":"q0540","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"For which athlete would carbohydrate loading offer the clearest performance advantage?","options":["A soccer player in a match with frequent rest lasting about 60 minutes","A road cyclist racing continuously for well over 90 minutes","A wrestler competing in matches lasting about 30 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A road cyclist racing continuously for well over 90 minutes","explanation_en":"Loading mainly benefits events lasting more than about 90 minutes, such as distance running and road cycling, where glycogen depletion is a risk.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肝糖填充最有利於持續超過90分鐘的耐力專案(如公路腳踏車、馬拉松),因為這類比賽有肝糖耗竭的風險;90分鐘以內或有間歇休息的賽事效益有限。"},{"id":"q0541","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A triathlete uses a drink blending glucose and fructose rather than glucose alone. Why does this raise total carbohydrate delivery during the race?","options":["Fructose suppresses glucose oxidation, which spares muscle glycogen","Fructose is simply absorbed faster than glucose, speeding overall uptake","The two sugars use separate intestinal transporters, so combined absorption exceeds either sugar's saturation limit"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The two sugars use separate intestinal transporters, so combined absorption exceeds either sugar's saturation limit","explanation_en":"Using multiple carbohydrate types taps separate transporters, getting past the saturation limit of a single sugar and raising total oxidation.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"葡萄糖與果糖在小腸使用不同的轉運蛋白(SGLT1與GLUT5),合併使用可避開單一糖類的吸收上限,提高總碳水吸收與氧化率。果糖並非吸收比葡萄糖快,也不是靠抑制葡萄糖氧化來省肝糖。"},{"id":"q0542","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A coach is formulating a sports drink and wants to avoid slowing gastric emptying. What carbohydrate concentration should he aim for?","options":["Roughly 6 to 8 percent","Roughly 12 to 15 percent","Roughly 18 to 20 percent"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Roughly 6 to 8 percent","explanation_en":"Concentrations above about 8 percent delay gastric emptying, so roughly 6 to 8 percent is considered ideal.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動飲料碳水濃度超過約8%會延緩胃排空,所以配方抓在6-8%最理想:既補糖又不拖慢水分吸收。"},{"id":"q0543","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A 60 kg runner finishes a hard endurance session and wants to maximize glycogen resynthesis in the first 30 minutes. About how much carbohydrate should she take in?","options":["About 12 to 30 grams (0.2 to 0.5 g per kilogram)","About 72 to 120 grams (1.2 to 2.0 g per kilogram)","About 300 to 420 grams (5 to 7 g per kilogram)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 72 to 120 grams (1.2 to 2.0 g per kilogram)","explanation_en":"Roughly 1.2 to 2.0 grams of carbohydrate per kilogram within 30 minutes after exercise supports rapid glycogen resynthesis.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動結束後30分鐘內攝取每公斤體重1.2-2.0克碳水化合物(60公斤約72-120克),最有利於快速再合成肝糖。"},{"id":"q0544","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Adding protein to a postexercise carbohydrate feeding does the most for glycogen storage under which condition?","options":["When carbohydrate intake reaches about 3.0 g per kilogram per hour","When carbohydrate intake already exceeds about 0.5 g per kilogram per hour","When carbohydrate intake falls below about 1.2 g per kilogram per hour"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"When carbohydrate intake falls below about 1.2 g per kilogram per hour","explanation_en":"Protein boosts glycogen storage mainly when carbohydrate intake is less than about 1.2 grams per kilogram per hour.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"只有當碳水攝取量低於約每小時1.2克/公斤時,額外加蛋白質才明顯幫助肝糖儲存;碳水已達標時加蛋白的附加效益不大。"},{"id":"q0545","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A young adult lifter wants a single post-workout protein feeding that maximally drives muscle protein synthesis. What amount of high-quality protein should he target?","options":["About 20 to 50 grams","About 70 to 100 grams","About 5 to 10 grams"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 20 to 50 grams","explanation_en":"About 20 to 50 grams of a high-quality, high-leucine protein maximally stimulates muscle protein synthesis in younger adults.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"年輕人單次攝取約20-50克高品質、富含白胺酸的(leucine)蛋白質,即可最大化刺激肌肉蛋白質合成;再多也不會繼續增加效果。"},{"id":"q0546","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"For a young adult, what amount of leucine within a protein dose is enough to effectively trigger muscle protein synthesis?","options":["About 15 to 20 grams","About 2 to 3 grams (near 0.05 g per kilogram)","About 8 to 10 grams"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 2 to 3 grams (near 0.05 g per kilogram)","explanation_en":"A dose containing about 2 to 3 grams of leucine (or 0.05 grams per kilogram) effectively triggers muscle protein synthesis in younger adults.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每劑含約2-3克白胺酸(約0.05克/公斤)就足以有效觸發肌肉蛋白質合成;15-20克是整個蛋白質的量,不是白胺酸的需要量。"},{"id":"q0547","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A dietitian wants to estimate an athlete's resting metabolic rate using an equation that accounts for the athlete's high muscle mass. Which should she choose?","options":["The body mass index formula, based on height and weight","The Harris-Benedict equation, based on height and total body weight","The Cunningham equation, based on fat-free mass"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The Cunningham equation, based on fat-free mass","explanation_en":"The Cunningham equation, RMR = 500 + 22 times fat-free mass in kilograms, accounts for muscle mass and is more applicable to athletes.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Cunningham方程式(RMR = 500 + 22 × 去脂體重公斤數)以去脂體重(fat-free mass)為變數,能反映運動員較高的肌肉量,比只用總體重的Harris-Benedict更適用。"},{"id":"q0548","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Two people differ noticeably in resting metabolic rate. Which single factor accounts for the largest share of that between-person difference?","options":["Fat-free mass, explaining about 70 to 80 percent","Fat-free mass, explaining only about 10 to 20 percent","Fat-free mass, explaining about 40 to 50 percent"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Fat-free mass, explaining about 70 to 80 percent","explanation_en":"Fat-free mass accounts for roughly 70 to 80 percent of the difference in resting metabolic rate among individuals.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"去脂體重可解釋個體間休息代謝率(RMR)差異的約70-80%,是單一最大影響因素;肌肉量高的人RMR自然較高。"},{"id":"q0549","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A practitioner reports resting metabolic rate (RMR) instead of basal metabolic rate (BMR) for convenience. Which comparison is accurate?","options":["RMR must be measured after a 12 to 14 hour fast, unlike BMR","RMR runs about 10 to 20 percent higher than BMR and needs no overnight fast","RMR omits the energy cost of digestion, whereas BMR includes it"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"RMR runs about 10 to 20 percent higher than BMR and needs no overnight fast","explanation_en":"RMR does not require an overnight fast and runs about 10 to 20 percent higher than BMR, so it is used more often for convenience.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RMR不需隔夜禁食即可測量,數值比BMR高約10-20%,因方便而更常使用;需要禁食12-14小時的是BMR。"},{"id":"q0550","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"When counseling on relative energy deficiency in sport, what energy availability represents the optimal target for healthy function?","options":["About 15 kcal per kilogram of fat-free mass per day","About 30 kcal per kilogram of fat-free mass per day","About 45 kcal per kilogram of fat-free mass per day"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 45 kcal per kilogram of fat-free mass per day","explanation_en":"Optimal energy availability for healthy function is around 45 kilocalories per kilogram of fat-free mass per day.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"能量可用性(energy availability)的理想目標約為每天每公斤去脂體重45大卡;長期低於約30大卡會干擾內分泌與生理功能,是相對能量缺乏症(RED-S)的核心關切。"},{"id":"q0551","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Of the eating disorders a coach might encounter, which carries the highest mortality rate of any mental health disorder?","options":["Anorexia nervosa","Binge-eating disorder","Pica"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Anorexia nervosa","explanation_en":"Among all mental health disorders, anorexia nervosa carries the highest mortality rate.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在所有精神疾病中,神經性厭食症(anorexia nervosa)的死亡率最高,死亡多與心臟併發症等相關,需要儘早轉介治療。"},{"id":"q0552","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A coach notices an athlete binge eating. Which feature would specifically point to bulimia nervosa rather than binge-eating disorder?","options":["The athlete's binges are always followed by self-induced vomiting only if overweight","The athlete follows binges with compensatory purging behaviors","The athlete is consistently underweight"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The athlete follows binges with compensatory purging behaviors","explanation_en":"Bulimia nervosa includes compensatory purging after binges, whereas binge-eating disorder has binges without purging, so those individuals are often overweight.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"神經性暴食症(bulimia nervosa)的鑑別特徵是暴食後有補償性清除行為(自我催吐、濫用瀉藥等);暴食疾患只有暴食而無清除,患者常體重過重。"},{"id":"q0553","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A strength coach strongly suspects one of his athletes has an eating disorder. What is his appropriate role?","options":["Set a restricted calorie target until the athlete's weight normalizes","Formally diagnose the condition and build a treatment plan","Recognize the warning signs and refer the athlete to a qualified treatment team"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Recognize the warning signs and refer the athlete to a qualified treatment team","explanation_en":"It is the professional's ethical responsibility to recognize symptoms and refer the athlete to qualified experts, not to diagnose or treat.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教練的專業與倫理角色是辨識警示徵象並把選手轉介給合格治療團隊(醫師、營養師、心理師),不是自己下診斷或限制熱量。"},{"id":"q0554","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"A muscular 100 kg athlete is flagged as obese by his BMI despite low body fat. Why does BMI mislead here?","options":["BMI cannot separate fat from muscle and bone, so it overestimates body fat in muscular people","BMI measures only body fat percentage and ignores total body weight","BMI systematically underestimates body fat in athletes regardless of build"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"BMI cannot separate fat from muscle and bone, so it overestimates body fat in muscular people","explanation_en":"BMI reflects excess weight rather than excess fat, so it can overestimate body fat in muscular athletes and underestimate it in those who have lost muscle.","tags":["Chapter 11 quiz: Nutrition Strategies for Maximizing Performance"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"BMI只看身高與體重的比值,無法區分脂肪與肌肉、骨骼,所以會把肌肉量大的選手誤判為肥胖;同理,肌肉流失者它又可能低估體脂。"},{"id":"q0555","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete asks what anabolic-androgenic steroids actually are, chemically. What is the accurate description?","options":["Synthetic derivatives of the male sex hormone testosterone","Synthetic derivatives of pituitary growth hormone","Synthetic derivatives of the adrenal hormone cortisol"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Synthetic derivatives of the male sex hormone testosterone","explanation_en":"Anabolic-androgenic steroids are human-made derivatives of the male sex hormone testosterone.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"合成代謝雄性類固醇(anabolic-androgenic steroids)是男性荷爾蒙睪固酮(testosterone)的人工合成衍生物,不是生長激素或皮質醇的衍生物。"},{"id":"q0556","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A user describes taking several different anabolic agents at the same time to get an additive effect. What is this practice called?","options":["Pyramiding, gradually raising the dose of one drug over weeks","Stacking, using several drugs simultaneously for combined potency","Cycling, alternating periods of use with periods of no use"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Stacking, using several drugs simultaneously for combined potency","explanation_en":"Stacking means taking several anabolic agents at the same time hoping their potency adds together.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同時使用多種合成代謝藥劑、希望效果累加的做法稱為堆疊(stack);逐漸加量再減量的是pyramiding,週期使用與停用交替的是cycling。"},{"id":"q0557","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"In which population would you expect anabolic steroids to produce the greatest strength gains?","options":["Sedentary older adults new to exercise","Untrained beginners just starting resistance training","Experienced athletes already well adapted to heavy strength training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Experienced athletes already well adapted to heavy strength training","explanation_en":"In experienced strength-trained athletes, steroid use can produce strength gains two to three times those of similarly trained non-users.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對已適應大重量訓練的經驗豐富的選手,類固醇帶來的肌力增益最大,可達同訓練程度未使用者的2-3倍;新手與久坐者獲益較少。"},{"id":"q0558","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"How does the androgenic activity of testosterone precursors such as androstenedione and DHEA compare with testosterone itself?","options":["Only a fraction of testosterone's activity","Essentially identical to testosterone","Considerably stronger than testosterone"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Only a fraction of testosterone's activity","explanation_en":"Androstenedione and DHEA have only about one-fifth and one-tenth the biological activity of testosterone, respectively.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"androstenedione與DHEA等睪固酮前驅物的生物活性只有睪固酮的一部分,分別約為其五分之一與十分之一。"},{"id":"q0559","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete considering SARMs asks about their status and mechanism. Which statement is correct?","options":["They are FDA-approved and permitted in competition","They selectively agonize androgen receptors, lack FDA approval, and are banned by WADA at all times","They act on androgen receptors but produce no androgenic effects or side effects"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"They selectively agonize androgen receptors, lack FDA approval, and are banned by WADA at all times","explanation_en":"SARMs selectively agonize androgen receptors, have no FDA approval, and are prohibited in and out of competition by WADA.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"SARMs選擇性活化雄性素接受器(androgen receptor),目前未獲FDA核准,且被WADA於賽季內與賽季外全年禁止;它仍會有雄性副作用,並非完全無副作用。"},{"id":"q0560","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A distance runner uses EPO to improve performance. Through what primary mechanism does it help?","options":["It blocks lactate accumulation in working muscle","It stimulates the testes to synthesize more testosterone","It raises red blood cell mass, increasing oxygen-carrying capacity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It raises red blood cell mass, increasing oxygen-carrying capacity","explanation_en":"EPO stimulates red blood cell production, raising hemoglobin and hematocrit and improving oxygen delivery to working muscle.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"EPO(紅血球生成素)刺激紅血球生成,提高血紅素與血容比(hematocrit),增加氧氣輸送量,從而提升耐力表現。"},{"id":"q0561","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"What is the principal health hazard when an endurance athlete raises hematocrit with EPO?","options":["Thicker, more viscous blood raising the risk of clots, stroke, and cardiovascular death","Premature closure of the long-bone growth plates","Severe hypoglycemia progressing to coma"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Thicker, more viscous blood raising the risk of clots, stroke, and cardiovascular death","explanation_en":"Raising hematocrit thickens the blood, increasing the risk of clotting, stroke, embolism, and death, which is compounded by dehydration.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"EPO的主要健康風險是血容比升高使血液變黏稠,增加血栓、中風、栓塞與心血管死亡風險,脫水時更嚴重。"},{"id":"q0562","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For which athlete would beta-blockers be most likely to enhance performance?","options":["A marathon runner needing sustained aerobic output","A rifle shooter needing steady hands and controlled movement","A sprint cyclist needing brief maximal power"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A rifle shooter needing steady hands and controlled movement","explanation_en":"Beta-blockers reduce anxiety and tremor, benefiting precision sports like shooting and archery; they are banned for rifle for this reason.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Beta阻斷劑(beta-blockers)降低焦慮、心率與手抖,對照射擊、射箭這類需要手部穩定的精準專案有助益,因此步槍專案停用;耐力專案用它反而受損。"},{"id":"q0563","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Why would beta-blockers actually impair a cyclist's endurance performance?","options":["They provoke severe skin tingling that disrupts pacing","They raise blood pH to an excessive alkaline level","They blunt catecholamines, lowering maximal heart rate and oxygen consumption"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"They blunt catecholamines, lowering maximal heart rate and oxygen consumption","explanation_en":"By blocking catecholamines, beta-blockers lower maximal heart rate and VO2, impairing endurance performance and raising perceived exertion.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Beta阻斷劑會阻斷兒茶酚胺的作用,壓低最大心率與最大攝氧量(VO2max),所以損害腳踏車等耐力表現,並提高自覺用力程度。"},{"id":"q0564","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete wants to rapidly saturate muscle creatine stores. Which loading approach fits the standard protocol?","options":["About 20 to 25 grams per day split into doses for about 5 days","About 0.5 grams per day taken indefinitely","2 grams per day for about 30 days"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 20 to 25 grams per day split into doses for about 5 days","explanation_en":"A common loading dose is roughly 20 to 25 grams daily (or 0.3 g per kg) for about 5 days, followed by a maintenance dose.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"標準肌酸負荷法是每天約20-25克(或0.3克/公斤)分次攝取、約5天,快速把肌肉肌酸儲量和磷酸肌酸補足,之後改為維持量。"},{"id":"q0565","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Dosing creatine relative to body mass, which loading and maintenance amounts match the recommendation?","options":["0.1 g per kilogram to load, then 0.01 g per kilogram to maintain","0.3 g per kilogram to load, then 0.03 g per kilogram per day to maintain","10 g per kilogram to load, then 5 g per kilogram to maintain"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"0.3 g per kilogram to load, then 0.03 g per kilogram per day to maintain","explanation_en":"Relative dosing uses about 0.3 grams per kilogram for loading and 0.03 grams per kilogram per day for maintenance.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"以體重計算劑量的建議是:負荷期約0.3克/公斤,之後每天約0.03克/公斤作為維持量。"},{"id":"q0566","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete is worried creatine will harm his kidneys or cause cramping. What does controlled research best support?","options":["It clearly raises the risk of muscle cramping and dehydration","Short-term use reliably produces measurable kidney damage","Controlled studies have not documented significant adverse effects, even with long-term use"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Controlled studies have not documented significant adverse effects, even with long-term use","explanation_en":"Controlled studies have not documented significant adverse effects, and there is no good evidence that creatine causes cramping or dehydration.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"控制組研究(包括長期使用)未記錄到顯著不良反應;也沒有可靠證據顯示肌酸會造成肌肉痙攣或脫水,運動員不必為此擔心。"},{"id":"q0567","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Beta-alanine works largely because it is the rate-limiting building block for synthesizing which intramuscular compound?","options":["Carnosine, an intramuscular hydrogen ion buffer","Glycogen, the stored carbohydrate fuel","Creatine phosphate, the immediate phosphagen store"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Carnosine, an intramuscular hydrogen ion buffer","explanation_en":"Beta-alanine is the rate-limiting precursor for muscle carnosine, a key intramuscular buffer of hydrogen ions.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸(beta-alanine)是合成肌肽(carnosine)的速率限制前驅物,而肌肽是肌肉內重要的氫離子緩衝物質,所以補它可提高緩衝能力。"},{"id":"q0568","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For which type of effort would beta-alanine be expected to help most?","options":["A single maximal one-repetition lift","High-intensity bouts of about 1 to 4 minutes that build strong intramuscular acidosis","Prolonged low-intensity work lasting several hours"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"High-intensity bouts of about 1 to 4 minutes that build strong intramuscular acidosis","explanation_en":"Beta-alanine helps efforts that create high intramuscular acidosis, like repeated high-intensity bouts lasting more than about 60 seconds.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸最有利於持續約1-4分鐘、會造成明顯肌肉內酸(high intramuscular acidosis)的高強度運動,例如超過60秒的重複高強度;單次1RM或數小時低強度運動幫助不大。"},{"id":"q0569","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete on beta-alanine reports skin tingling. How should this be characterized?","options":["An early sign of the severe diarrhea beta-alanine typically causes","A warning sign of the acute hypoglycemia beta-alanine can trigger","Paresthesia, the only commonly reported side effect and a harmless one"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Paresthesia, the only commonly reported side effect and a harmless one","explanation_en":"The main reported side effect is paresthesia, a harmless tingling that is reduced by splitting the dose into smaller amounts.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮膚刺痛感是感覺異常(paresthesia),是β-丙胺酸唯一常見且無害的副作用,把劑量分成較小份量即可減輕。"},{"id":"q0570","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A 70 kg athlete plans to use sodium bicarbonate before a short high-intensity event. What per-kilogram dose is effective without excessive GI distress?","options":["About 0.3 g per kilogram (roughly 21 g)","About 1.0 g per kilogram (roughly 70 g)","About 0.05 g per kilogram (roughly 3.5 g)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 0.3 g per kilogram (roughly 21 g)","explanation_en":"About 0.3 grams per kilogram body mass taken 60 to 180 minutes before exercise improves short high-intensity performance; higher doses cause GI distress.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"碳酸氫鈉(sodium bicarbonate)的有效劑量約為0.3克/公斤,在運動前60-180分鐘攝取(70公斤約21克);劑量更高時胃腸不適明顯增加。"},{"id":"q0571","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"An athlete who gets stomach upset from sodium bicarbonate asks about sodium citrate. What is citrate's main advantage?","options":["It is a substantially more powerful buffer than bicarbonate","It tends to cause less gastrointestinal distress","It works only during prolonged aerobic exercise"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It tends to cause less gastrointestinal distress","explanation_en":"Sodium citrate can raise blood pH with less of the GI distress commonly seen with sodium bicarbonate, though its ergogenic data are equivocal.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"檸檬酸鈉(sodium citrate)同樣可提高血液pH,主要優點是造成的胃腸道不適比碳酸氫鈉少,但其增補效益的證據較為分歧。"},{"id":"q0572","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A 70 kg endurance athlete wants an ergogenic caffeine dose about an hour before racing. Which range is appropriate?","options":["About 15 to 20 mg per kilogram (roughly 1,050 to 1,400 mg)","About 0.1 to 0.5 mg per kilogram (roughly 7 to 35 mg)","About 3 to 9 mg per kilogram (roughly 210 to 630 mg)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 3 to 9 mg per kilogram (roughly 210 to 630 mg)","explanation_en":"Doses of 3 to 9 mg per kilogram produce a significant ergogenic effect, with no further benefit and more side effects above 9 mg per kilogram.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"咖啡因的有效增補劑量約為3-9毫克/公斤(70公斤約210-630毫克),約賽前1小時攝取;超過9毫克/公斤不再增加效益,副作用反而更多。"},{"id":"q0573","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A healthy athlete asks whether oral arginine will boost nitric oxide and endurance. What does the evidence show?","options":["It does not reliably raise nitric oxide or muscle blood flow, nor improve endurance, in healthy people","It is the single most effective endurance aid currently available","It dependably raises nitric oxide, muscle blood flow, and endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It does not reliably raise nitric oxide or muscle blood flow, nor improve endurance, in healthy people","explanation_en":"In healthy athletes, arginine fails to meaningfully raise nitric oxide or muscle blood flow or improve endurance, so it is not recommended.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在健康族群中,口服精胺酸(arginine)無法穩定提高一氧化氮(nitric oxide)與肌肉血流量,也未能改善耐力表現,不具建議價值。"},{"id":"q0574","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Under which scenario is HMB most likely to produce meaningful benefit?","options":["Trained athletes instructed to keep their program unchanged","Untrained people, or trained athletes given a sufficiently novel high-intensity, high-volume stimulus","Endurance athletes chasing a higher VO2max"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Untrained people, or trained athletes given a sufficiently novel high-intensity, high-volume stimulus","explanation_en":"HMB reduces muscle protein breakdown and works best when there is enough muscle-damaging stimulus, such as in untrained people or properly progressed trained athletes.","tags":["Chapter 12 quiz: Performance-Enhancing Substances and Methods"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"HMB能減少肌肉蛋白質分解,在肌肉損傷刺激足夠時最有效:未受訓練者,或訓練有素者突然接受新穎且高強高量的刺激;老訓練者維持原課表時效果有限。"},{"id":"q0575","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A coach's vertical jump protocol yields scores that swing wildly when the same athlete is retested on consecutive days, yet the coach insists it still validly measures leg power. What is the most defensible response?","options":["Validity and reliability are independent, so poor repeatability says nothing about validity","The inconsistency undermines validity, because a test cannot be valid unless it is first reliable","Validity is unaffected, because a test can be valid even when it is not reliable"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The inconsistency undermines validity, because a test cannot be valid unless it is first reliable","explanation_en":"Highly variable (unreliable) results have little meaning, so reliability is a prerequisite for validity, though reliability alone does not ensure validity.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"信度是效度的必要條件:重測結果劇烈擺動代表測驗不可靠,也就談不上有效;但可靠的測驗仍不保證有效,兩者不是完全獨立。"},{"id":"q0576","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A director claims a new field test is excellent because it gives nearly identical scores every time it is run. Before agreeing the test is valid, what additional quality must be demonstrated?","options":["That its scores line up with published norms for the athlete's group","That its scores stay consistent across repeated administrations","That it actually measures the specific attribute it is intended to measure"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"That it actually measures the specific attribute it is intended to measure","explanation_en":"Validity is the degree to which a test or item actually measures the intended attribute; consistency alone is reliability, not validity.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"每次施測分數幾乎相同只證明信度(reliability);要稱它有效,還須證明該測驗確實測量它立意要測的特質,這才是效度(validity)的定義。"},{"id":"q0577","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"An athlete runs the same shuttle protocol three times in one week and posts nearly the same time each session. Which test property is this pattern demonstrating?","options":["Reliability, the consistency or repeatability of the results","Content validity, alignment of the test with the sport's demands","Norm-referenced standing, agreement of the score with national norms"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Reliability, the consistency or repeatability of the results","explanation_en":"Reliability is the consistency or repeatability of a test across multiple instances; it is distinct from validity and from normative comparison.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一測驗重複三次成績幾乎相同,呈現的是信度(reliability),即結果的一致性/可重複性,與效度或常模比較是不同概念。"},{"id":"q0578","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A booster with no testing background watches a new drill and says it 'obviously' measures speed, though no expert has evaluated its actual coverage. This impression reflects high:","options":["Construct validity","Face validity","Content validity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Face validity","explanation_en":"Face validity is the appearance of measuring something to nonexperts, whereas content validity reflects actual coverage judged by experts.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"表面效度(face validity)只是外行人「看起來」像是在測某能力,未經專家檢視;內容效度才需要專家評估實際覆蓋面。"},{"id":"q0579","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A panel of soccer specialists reviews a testing battery and confirms it samples sprinting, agility, aerobic endurance, and kicking power in proportions matching the sport's demands. Their judgment establishes which type of validity?","options":["Face validity","Predictive validity","Content validity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Content validity","explanation_en":"Content validity is the expert assessment that testing covers all relevant component abilities in appropriate proportions.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"內容效度(content validity)是專家認定測驗按適當比例涵蓋該運動所有相關成分能力(衝刺、敏捷、有氧耐力、踢球力量等)的程度。"},{"id":"q0580","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A combine director wants a test whose scores taken today reliably indicate which recruits will succeed in games two seasons from now. The evidence he needs concerns which type of validity?","options":["Predictive validity, the ability of scores to forecast future performance","Construct validity, the test's tie to an underlying theoretical trait","Concurrent validity, agreement with a measure taken at the same time"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Predictive validity, the ability of scores to forecast future performance","explanation_en":"Predictive validity is the extent to which test scores forecast future performance; concurrent validity reflects agreement with a current measure.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"用現在的測驗分數預測未來(兩個球季後的比賽表現)的效度是預測效度(predictive validity);同時點與標準量比較的是同時效度。"},{"id":"q0581","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"To validate a quick field test of aerobic power, a coach has athletes complete it and a lab treadmill VO2max test in the same session and correlates the two. This procedure establishes which type of validity?","options":["Content validity, agreement with expert ratings of the test's coverage","Concurrent validity, correlation with an accepted criterion measured at the same time","Predictive validity, correlation with future competitive outcomes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Concurrent validity, correlation with an accepted criterion measured at the same time","explanation_en":"Concurrent validity is the degree to which scores agree with those of an already-accepted (criterion) measure obtained concurrently.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在同一次 session 裡讓選手同時做野外測驗與實驗室VO2max準則測驗並求相關,建立的是同時效度(concurrent validity)。"},{"id":"q0582","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Two staff members hand-time the same 40-yard sprint and record noticeably different times for the same trial. Which measurement property is compromised?","options":["Test-retest reliability of the sprint protocol itself","Intrasubject variability, day-to-day fluctuation within the athlete","Interrater reliability, also called objectivity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Interrater reliability, also called objectivity","explanation_en":"Interrater reliability, also called objectivity, is the degree to which different raters agree on results.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩位計時員對同一次衝刺記錄出不同成績,是評分者之間的不一致,損害的是評分者間信度(interrater reliability),又稱客觀性(objectivity)。"},{"id":"q0583","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"The same tester scores a jump strictly on the pretest but, without realizing it, gives more generous credit on the posttest. What does this inconsistency represent?","options":["Intrarater variability, inconsistent scoring by one given tester","Intrasubject variability, fluctuation in the athlete's own performance","Interrater reliability, disagreement between two different testers"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Intrarater variability, inconsistent scoring by one given tester","explanation_en":"Intrarater variability is a lack of consistent scoring by one given tester across administrations.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一位評分者在前測嚴格、後測不知不覺放寬,屬於評分者內變異(intrarater variability),即同一評分者的標準前後不一。"},{"id":"q0584","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A coach notes that repeated jump scores differ slightly both because the timing mat is imperfect and because the athlete's own output naturally fluctuates day to day. The typical error of measurement is best described as capturing:","options":["Only the athlete's day-to-day biological variation","Both equipment error and the athlete's biological variation","Only the error introduced by the equipment"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Both equipment error and the athlete's biological variation","explanation_en":"Typical error of measurement combines equipment error and the biological variation of athletes.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"典型測量誤差(typical error of measurement)同時包含器材誤差與選手本身的生物變異兩部分來源,不是隻有其中一項。"},{"id":"q0585","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A coach is deciding the order of a multi-test session. Which principle should govern that sequencing above all others?","options":["Every test in the session should stress the same energy system","The most fatiguing tests should always be completed first","No test should be positioned where it degrades performance on a test that follows"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"No test should be positioned where it degrades performance on a test that follows","explanation_en":"Tests should be ordered so an earlier test does not impair a later one, allowing optimal and comparable performances.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"安排多重測驗順序的最高原則:任何測驗都不應排在會讓後續測驗表現變差的位置,以確保每項測驗都能發揮且可比。"},{"id":"q0586","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A session includes a technique-dependent agility drill and a demanding maximal endurance shuttle. To get valid results from both, how should they be ordered?","options":["The agility drill first, before the fatiguing endurance shuttle","The fatiguing endurance shuttle first, before the agility drill","Either order works as long as some rest is provided between them"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The agility drill first, before the fatiguing endurance shuttle","explanation_en":"High-skill movements such as agility tests should be administered before fatiguing tests so fatigue does not degrade technique.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高技巧依賴的測驗(如敏捷性鑽練)應安排在造成疲勞的極限有氧折返跑之前,避免疲勞破壞動作技術而失真。"},{"id":"q0587","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"An athlete has just completed an all-out 400 m effort that maximally taxes the glycolytic system. Roughly how long should the coach allow before expecting complete recovery for another maximal effort?","options":["About 3 to 5 minutes, as for a phosphagen-system test","At least about 1 hour","Only about 15 seconds"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At least about 1 hour","explanation_en":"Maximal glycolytic tests require at least about 1 hour for complete recovery, versus 3 to 5 minutes for phosphagen tests.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"全力、最大化糖解系統的測驗(如400米全力跑)之後,約需至少1小時才能完全恢復再測;磷酸系統(maximal)測驗只需3-5分鐘。"},{"id":"q0588","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A coach wants a single test that will be genuinely valid for a sport. Beyond convenience, which two dimensions of the sport must the test reproduce?","options":["Only the typical duration of a competitive bout","The number of players active on the field at once","The sport's energy-system demands and its important movement patterns"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The sport's energy-system demands and its important movement patterns","explanation_en":"A valid test must match both the metabolic (energy system) and biomechanical (movement pattern) demands of the sport.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有效的專項測驗必須同時符合該運動的能量系統需求(代謝面向)與重要動作型態(生物力學面向),缺一不可。"},{"id":"q0589","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A single-leg hop test rich in technical demand gives stable, meaningful scores for a veteran long jumper but produces erratic scores for a first-week beginner. The best explanation is that:","options":["The novice has not developed the technique needed for consistent performance","Novices reliably outscore experienced athletes on technique-intensive tests","The test's duration is simply too short for novice athletes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The novice has not developed the technique needed for consistent performance","explanation_en":"Technique-intensive tests assume developed skill; a novice's inconsistent technique undermines validity and reliability.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"技術含量高的測驗假定受測者已發展出所需動作技巧;新手技巧尚未成熟,表現自然不穩定,同時損害該測驗的信度與效度。"},{"id":"q0590","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A team based at sea level travels to a high-altitude venue and the coach wants meaningful aerobic endurance test results. How much time should be allowed to adjust before testing?","options":["Only a few hours, since the effect is minimal","At least about 10 days","None, because altitude does not affect endurance test scores"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At least about 10 days","explanation_en":"At least about 10 days of acclimatization is recommended before aerobic endurance testing at high altitude.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"到高海拔場地要做有氧耐力測驗,建議先適應至少約10天,否則缺氧會低估選手的真實有氧能力。"},{"id":"q0591","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"The same 40-yard sprints timed by hand consistently come out faster than when timed with electronic gates. What best accounts for the hand-timed bias?","options":["Athletes genuinely run faster whenever they are hand timed","The stopwatch mechanism systematically runs slow","The timer reacts late in starting the watch but visually anticipates the finish, shortening the recorded time"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The timer reacts late in starting the watch but visually anticipates the finish, shortening the recorded time","explanation_en":"Timers delay pressing start in reaction to the gun but anticipate the finish visually, shortening recorded times relative to automatic timing.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"人工計時時,計時員對發令訊號的反應太慢使起始鍵按晚,但終點用視覺預期提前按表,兩個誤差都讓手記時間比電子計時短,這是系統性偏差,不是選手真的跑得快。"},{"id":"q0592","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"During hot-weather testing an athlete becomes confused and nauseated, and the staff suspect hyponatremia from drinking too much plain water. What is the correct response?","options":["Withhold additional fluid and have a physician treat the athlete","Have the athlete rest and sip a sports drink until symptoms clear","Immediately give more water to rehydrate the athlete"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Withhold additional fluid and have a physician treat the athlete","explanation_en":"Hyponatremia is excess water diluting blood sodium; a victim should not be given more fluid and must be treated by a physician.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"低血鈉症(hyponatremia)是喝太多純水把血鈉濃度稀釋,正確處理是暫停補充任何水分並交由醫師治療;再灌水只會更稀釋。"},{"id":"q0593","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Before a new testing battery, a coach schedules a practice session so athletes rehearse the exact procedures. The primary payoff of this familiarization is that it:","options":["Allows athletes to peak physically for the testing day","Improves reliability by making athletes familiar with the content and procedures","Removes the need for a separate warm-up before testing"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Improves reliability by making athletes familiar with the content and procedures","explanation_en":"Familiarization improves reliability because athletes who know the test content and procedures perform more consistently.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"施測前安排熟悉測驗程式的主要好處是提升信度:瞭解測驗內容與流程的選手表現較一致。它不是為了生理巔峰或取代熱身。"},{"id":"q0594","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"A tester loudly cheers on a few favored athletes during a jump test but stays silent for the rest. Which test qualities does this uneven motivation most directly threaten?","options":["The test's face validity","The calibration of the testing equipment","The test's reliability and objectivity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The test's reliability and objectivity","explanation_en":"Unequal motivation introduces inconsistency between athletes and testers, impairing reliability and objectivity, so all athletes should be motivated equally.","tags":["Chapter 13 quiz: Principles of Test Selection and Administration"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對部分受測者加油、其餘沉默,會造成選手之間與場次之間的激勵不一致,直接損害測驗的信度與客觀性;應給所有人同等激勵。"},{"id":"q0595","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach wants to assess an athlete's ability to express force rapidly rather than to grind out a slow maximal effort. Which 1RM test best serves that goal?","options":["1RM back squat, a low-speed maximal strength test","1RM bench press, a low-speed maximal strength test","1RM power clean, a high-speed strength test"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1RM power clean, a high-speed strength test","explanation_en":"Explosive lifts like the power clean are high-speed strength tests (about 1 s), whereas the squat and bench press are low-speed maximal strength tests.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"1RM power clean屬於高速(maximal strength)測驗(動作約1秒),能量快速輸出;深蹲與仰臥推舉是低速最大肌力測驗,測不出快速發力能力。"},{"id":"q0596","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"An athlete's estimated 1RM back squat is 400 lb. After the general warm-up, roughly what load should the very first 1RM-testing attempt be set at?","options":["About 200 lb, near half of the estimated 1RM","About 300 lb, roughly three-quarters of the estimated 1RM","About 380 lb, just under the estimated 1RM"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 200 lb, near half of the estimated 1RM","explanation_en":"After warm-up the first 1RM attempt is typically near 50% of the estimated 1RM, with load increased over subsequent attempts.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱身後第一次1RM嘗試重量約為估計1RM的50%(估400磅則約200磅),之後再逐次加重逼近真實1RM。"},{"id":"q0597","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A tester wants to find a true 1RM without letting accumulated fatigue distort the result. Within how many post-warm-up attempts should a skilled tester expect to arrive at it?","options":["Within 1 to 2 attempts","Within 3 to 5 attempts","Within 8 to 10 attempts"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Within 3 to 5 attempts","explanation_en":"The 1RM is generally found within 3 to 5 attempts after warm-up; more attempts risk fatigue detracting from the result.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熟練的測試者應在熱身後3-5次嘗試內測得真實1RM;嘗試次數太多(8-10次)會讓累積疲勞汙染結果。"},{"id":"q0598","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Two athletes with essentially equal lower-body power post very different 1RM power clean numbers. Why does this limit the power clean's value for predicting athletic performance?","options":["It draws almost entirely on the oxidative energy system","It requires no external load, so it cannot reflect power","Its heavy technical demands let equally powerful athletes score very differently"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Its heavy technical demands let equally powerful athletes score very differently","explanation_en":"Because the power clean is technically demanding, two athletes with the same power capacity can post very different 1RM scores.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"power clean技術門檻很高,下肢功率相同的兩人可能因技術差異測出完全不同的1RM,這限制它預測競技表現的價值。"},{"id":"q0599","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach has athletes keep their hands fixed on the hips throughout a vertical jump. What is the purpose of this constraint?","options":["To isolate the power and coordination of the lower limbs","To maximize jump height by adding an arm swing contribution","To convert the trial into a measure of reactive strength index"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"To isolate the power and coordination of the lower limbs","explanation_en":"Fixing the hands on the hips removes the arm contribution to isolate lower-limb power; permitting an arm swing yields the Abalakov jump.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"雙手固定於腰側是為排除擺臂貢獻,孤立測量下肢功率與協調;允許擺臂的版本是Abalakov跳。"},{"id":"q0600","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach lets athletes use a full arm swing during a countermovement vertical jump to capture whole-body coordination. By what name is this arm-swing version known?","options":["Margaria-Kalamen jump","Abalakov jump","Drop jump"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Abalakov jump","explanation_en":"The arm-swing version of the countermovement jump is referred to as the Abalakov jump.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"反動作縱跳(countermovement jump)允許全程擺臂來呈現全身協調的版本,稱為Abalakov跳。"},{"id":"q0601","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach wants an athlete to maximize the reactive strength index on a depth jump. What performance pattern achieves this?","options":["Loading the bar as heavily as the athlete can manage","A long ground contact paired with a high jump","A short ground contact combined with the highest possible jump"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A short ground contact combined with the highest possible jump","explanation_en":"RSI rewards a short ground contact time combined with high jump height, reflecting high leg stiffness and stretch-shortening cycle ability.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"反應力量指數(RSI)由跳躍高度除以地面接觸時間而來,所以要「接觸時間愈短、跳得愈高」才能最大化,它反映下肢剛性與伸展縮短週期(SSC)能力。"},{"id":"q0602","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach is building a change-of-direction test battery and reviews four candidate tests. Which one does NOT belong because it does not measure agility or change of direction?","options":["Reactive strength index","Hexagon test","5-10-5 (pro agility) test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Reactive strength index","explanation_en":"RSI is a measure of reactive/plyometric strength, not agility; the hexagon, T-test, 5-10-5, and 5-0-5 are change-of-direction tests.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RSI測量的是反應式/伸展收縮能力,與敏捷或變向無關;六邊形跳(hexagon)、T-test、5-10-5、5-0-5才是變向/敏捷測驗。"},{"id":"q0603","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach describes a drill in which the athlete sprints 5 yards one way, 10 yards back, then 5 yards to finish, changing direction at each turn. This test is also commonly known as the:","options":["T-test","Pro agility test, or 20-yard shuttle","Margaria-Kalamen test"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Pro agility test, or 20-yard shuttle","explanation_en":"The 5-10-5 is also called the pro agility test or 20-yard shuttle, sprinting 5, 10, then 5 yards with direction changes.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"先衝刺5碼、折返10碼、再跑完5碼、每次轉身變向的就是5-10-5,又稱職業敏捷測試(pro agility)或20碼折返跑。"},{"id":"q0604","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach wants to quantify the maximal rate of energy production from the two non-oxidative pathways combined. Anaerobic capacity reflects the combined output of which systems?","options":["The glycolytic and oxidative systems","The phosphagen and oxidative systems","The phosphagen and glycolytic systems"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The phosphagen and glycolytic systems","explanation_en":"Anaerobic capacity is the maximal rate of energy production by the combined phosphagen and glycolytic systems.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"無氧能力(anaerobic capacity)定義為磷酸系統與糖解系統聯合作用的最大能量生成速率,不包含氧化系統。"},{"id":"q0605","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach records each athlete's standing height, body mass, limb girths, and segment lengths as part of a profile. This collection of measurements is an example of:","options":["Anthropometry","Isometric strength testing","An agility assessment"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Anthropometry","explanation_en":"Anthropometry is the measurement of the dimensions and proportions of the human body.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"人體測量學(anthropometry)就是測量身體的尺寸與比例,包含身高、體重、肢體圍度與節段長度等。"},{"id":"q0606","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Eight athletes post these jump scores (cm): 40, 42, 45, 47, 49, 51, 55, 60. What is the median?","options":["The most frequently occurring score in the set","48 cm, the average of the two middlemost scores","20 cm, the highest score minus the lowest"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"48 cm, the average of the two middlemost scores","explanation_en":"With an even number of scores the median is the average of the two middle values; here (47+49)/2 = 48 cm.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"資料個數為偶數時,中位數取最中間兩個值的平均:(47+49)/2=48釐米。眾數是最常出現的值,極差是最高減最低。"},{"id":"q0607","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A small group's sprint times are typical except for one athlete who is dramatically slower than the rest. Which measure of central tendency is least distorted by that extreme value?","options":["The range","The mean","The median"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The median","explanation_en":"The median is more robust than the mean when the distribution contains very high or very low outlier scores; the range is not a measure of central tendency.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"中位數比平均數更能抵抗極端值:一個明顯超慢的離群選手幾乎不會影響中位數;極差根本不是集中趨勢指標。"},{"id":"q0608","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"An athlete's combine result places her at the 75th percentile of the reference group. How should this be interpreted?","options":["75% of the reference group scored below her","She reached 75% of the maximum possible score","She improved on 75% of her own previous scores"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"75% of the reference group scored below her","explanation_en":"Percentile rank is the percentage of test takers scoring below the individual, so the 75th percentile means 75% scored lower.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第75百分位的定義是參考團體中75%的人分數比她低,不是達到滿分的75%,也不是進步幅度。"},{"id":"q0609","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach converts jump results to z-scores to compare athletes across different tests. What does an athlete's z-score of +1.5 tell the coach?","options":["Her score is 1.5% of the group's maximum","Her score is 1.5 standard deviations above the group mean","Her score is 1.5 test units above the group mean"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Her score is 1.5 standard deviations above the group mean","explanation_en":"A z-score standardizes a result as the number of standard deviation units above or below the group mean.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"z分數把原始分數標準化為「偏離團體平均幾個標準差」;+1.5代表她的分數高於平均1.5個標準差,因此可跨不同測驗比較。"},{"id":"q0610","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A group's vertical jump has a between-subjects standard deviation of 10 cm. Using the common estimate, roughly what change would be considered the smallest worthwhile change?","options":["About 5 cm, or 0.5 of the standard deviation","About 10 cm, or 1.0 of the standard deviation","About 2 cm, or 0.2 of the standard deviation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 2 cm, or 0.2 of the standard deviation","explanation_en":"Smallest worthwhile change is commonly estimated as 0.2 times the between-subjects standard deviation, so 0.2 x 10 cm is about 2 cm.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最小有價值變化(SWC)常以0.2倍受試者間標準差估算,本題0.2×10釐米=約2釐米;變化小於此值可能只是測量噪音。"},{"id":"q0611","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A coach computes an effect size to judge how much a training block improved a group's test scores. Effect size is the change in the mean expressed relative to which value?","options":["The pretest standard deviation","The group's percentile rank","The posttest mean score"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The pretest standard deviation","explanation_en":"Effect size is the change (posttest minus pretest mean) divided by the pretest standard deviation.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"效果量(effect size)=後測平均減前測平均,再除以前測標準差,即用前測標準差當單位來表達平均變化。"},{"id":"q0612","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"An elite lifter and an untrained beginner both run the identical program for the same duration. By the principle of diminishing returns, what should the coach expect?","options":["Both improve by essentially the same amount","The highly trained lifter improves less than the untrained beginner","The untrained beginner improves less than the highly trained lifter"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The highly trained lifter improves less than the untrained beginner","explanation_en":"Better-trained athletes have a smaller window of adaptation, so they improve less in raw terms than untrained athletes.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"報酬遞減(diminishing returns)原則:訓練水平愈高,適應的空間愈小,精英選手同課表的實質進步比未受訓練的新手少。"},{"id":"q0613","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A technician is planning when and how to collect skinfold measurements for body composition. Which condition is correct?","options":["Immediately after completing a warm-up","Only on the right side and only after stretching","On dry skin before the athlete exercises"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"On dry skin before the athlete exercises","explanation_en":"Skinfolds should be measured on dry skin before exercise to maximize validity and reliability.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮脂厚度測量應在皮膚乾燥、運動之前進行,以維持效度與信度;運動後出汗或充血會干擾夾取與數值。"},{"id":"q0614","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"A researcher tests a sample of athletes and uses inferential statistics to draw conclusions about all athletes in that sport. On what basic assumption does that inference rest?","options":["That the sample is truly representative of the population","That the measurements contain no error whatsoever","That the entire population of athletes has actually been measured"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"That the sample is truly representative of the population","explanation_en":"Inferential statistics use a sample to draw conclusions about a population, assuming the sample truly represents that population.","tags":["Chapter 14 quiz: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"推論式統計是用樣本來推斷整個團體,其基本假設是樣本確實能代表該母體;測量不可能完全無誤差。"},{"id":"q0615","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach opens each session with 8 minutes of light jogging, movement drills, and a few build-up sprints, telling athletes it readies them for the day's work. A parent asks how this differs from the seated hamstring and calf stretches the team does on off days to slowly gain range of motion. What is the correct distinction?","options":["The session opener prepares the athlete physically and mentally to perform, whereas the off-day stretching targets a lasting increase in joint range of motion","The session opener aims to permanently raise resting range of motion, while the off-day stretching only prepares the body to perform","Both serve the identical goal of acutely readying the athlete, and the distinction is only in the equipment used"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The session opener prepares the athlete physically and mentally to perform, whereas the off-day stretching targets a lasting increase in joint range of motion","explanation_en":"A warm-up prepares the athlete for performance, while flexibility training aims to increase ROM around a joint.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"暖身的目的是讓選手在生理與心理上準備好當天的表現;休整日的靜態伸展則追求關節活動度(ROM)的持久增加,兩者目標不同。"},{"id":"q0616","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"As an athlete warms up, rising muscle temperature causes hemoglobin to release oxygen more readily to the working tissue, improving oxygen delivery. This mechanism is best classified as which category of warm-up benefit?","options":["A non-temperature-related effect driven mainly by increased local blood flow","A temperature-related effect, reflecting the rightward shift of the oxygen dissociation curve","A psychological readiness effect unrelated to any physiological change"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A temperature-related effect, reflecting the rightward shift of the oxygen dissociation curve","explanation_en":"Enhanced oxygen delivery via the Bohr effect results from increased muscle temperature, a temperature-related warm-up effect.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌溫上升使氧解離曲線右移(玻爾效應),血紅素更容易把氧釋放給工作中的組織,這屬於暖身的溫度相關效益。"},{"id":"q0617","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach lists several changes that occur during a warm-up and asks which one would still occur even if muscle temperature did not rise at all. Which effect is correctly identified as non-temperature-related?","options":["The reduction in muscle viscous resistance produced by added heat","The disruption of transient connective tissue bonds as tissue heats","Increased blood flow to the muscles together with an elevated baseline oxygen consumption"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increased blood flow to the muscles together with an elevated baseline oxygen consumption","explanation_en":"Increased blood flow, elevated baseline oxygen consumption, and postactivation potentiation are the non-temperature-related effects.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉血流量增加與基礎攝氧量升高,屬於非溫度相關效應;黏滯阻力下降、暫時性結締組織鍵結被破壞則依賴溫度上升。"},{"id":"q0618","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach structures a warm-up so athletes first elevate heart rate and temperature, then perform activation and mobility drills, and finish with a few explosive efforts to prime the nervous system. This maps directly onto the RAMP framework. What do the four elements of RAMP stand for?","options":["Raise, Activate and mobilize, and Potentiate","Rest, Adapt, Move, and Push","Run, Activate, Mobilize, and Perform"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Raise, Activate and mobilize, and Potentiate","explanation_en":"RAMP stands for Raise, Activate and mobilize, and Potentiate.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RAMP框架四要素為Raise(提升)、Activate and mobilize(啟用與動員)、Potentiate(增強),先升心率體溫,再啟用動作,最後用爆發嘗試預激神經系統。"},{"id":"q0619","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Instead of putting soccer players on a bike for 5 minutes, a coach starts the warm-up with jogging patterns, shuffles, and change-of-direction runs that mimic match play. How does this Raise-phase choice differ from a traditional general warm-up?","options":["It relies on static stretching held at end range rather than any movement","It elevates physiological parameters using sport-simulating movements that also rehearse skill, rather than generic aerobic exercise","It intentionally keeps body temperature low to avoid early fatigue"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It elevates physiological parameters using sport-simulating movements that also rehearse skill, rather than generic aerobic exercise","explanation_en":"The Raise phase elevates physiological parameters while using sport-simulating movements to also develop skill, unlike generic aerobic activity.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RAMP的Raise階段用模擬比賽的動作(跑動模式、側移、變向跑)來提高生理引數,順帶演練專項技巧,與騎固定車這類通用有氧不同。"},{"id":"q0620","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"An athlete wants to include some static stretching in a pre-competition routine without blunting power output. Beyond roughly what per-stretch hold duration does static stretching become most likely to impair the performance that follows?","options":["About 10 seconds","About 30 seconds","About 60 seconds"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 60 seconds","explanation_en":"Evidence indicates short-duration static stretching has no clear detriment unless stretches are held longer than 60 seconds.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究顯示短時間靜態伸展對後續表現沒有明顯害處,單次伸展停留超過約60秒才最可能削弱功率輸出,賽前應避免。"},{"id":"q0621","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach chooses leg swings and walking lunges over seated static holds for a pre-practice warm-up in a sprint-based sport. What is the primary rationale for preferring the dynamic approach here?","options":["It keeps the muscles active through the range of motion and more closely replicates sport movement patterns","It removes the need for motor control and coordination during the warm-up","It is the single best method for maximizing passive static range of motion"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It keeps the muscles active through the range of motion and more closely replicates sport movement patterns","explanation_en":"In dynamic stretching the muscle stays active through the ROM, which is more specific to sport movement patterns.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"動態伸展讓肌肉全程在動作範圍內主動運作,更接近衝刺型專項的動作模式,所以短跑類運動的熱身優先採用,而非坐姿靜態停留。"},{"id":"q0622","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"An athlete has excellent passive hamstring length on a table test but moves stiffly and loses position during a loaded squat. A coach explains that the athlete has adequate flexibility but limited mobility. Which statement captures this distinction?","options":["Mobility and flexibility describe exactly the same quality and can be used interchangeably","Mobility is the capacity to move freely and effectively, combining motor control, stability, and flexibility","Mobility is simply the passive range of motion measured at rest at a single joint"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Mobility is the capacity to move freely and effectively, combining motor control, stability, and flexibility","explanation_en":"Mobility is a dynamic quality requiring motor control, stability, and flexibility, not just passive range of motion.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"活動度(mobility)是能在動作範圍內自由且有效移動的能力,須結合動作控制、穩定度與柔軟度;柔軟度(flexibility)只是軟組織的被動伸展長度,兩者不同。"},{"id":"q0623","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A sprinter performs a few heavy resisted starts and, minutes later, runs a noticeably faster 30 m than usual, though the benefit fades within the session. Which concept best describes this response?","options":["The force loss and impairment typically produced by prolonged static stretching","A permanent strength gain accrued from months of accumulated training","Postactivation performance enhancement, an acute and transient boost following a prior conditioning stimulus"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Postactivation performance enhancement, an acute and transient boost following a prior conditioning stimulus","explanation_en":"PAPE is an acute enhancement of neuromuscular performance from a prior low-volume, high-intensity stimulus.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大重量抗阻啟始後短時間內30米變快、且效果隨後消退,這是啟用後表現增強(PAPE):先前低容量高強度刺激造成的急性、暫時性神經肌肉表現提升。"},{"id":"q0624","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach programs heavy back squats before a vertical jump test hoping to boost jump height, but must decide how heavy and how much rest to allow. Which competing outcome of the conditioning activity must be balanced against the intended enhancement?","options":["The accumulated fatigue from the activity, which offsets the potentiation it produces","The trade-off between improving flexibility versus improving joint stability","The trade-off between developing strength versus developing endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The accumulated fatigue from the activity, which offsets the potentiation it produces","explanation_en":"A preconditioning activity can generate potentiation but also fatigue, so this balance must always be managed.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"前置條件活動同時產生增強(potentiation)與疲勞兩種效果;安排重量與休息就是為了取得淨增強:疲勞已消退、增強仍在。"},{"id":"q0625","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Two athletes of the same sport differ markedly in shoulder range of motion. A coach notes that some contributors to flexibility respond to a stretching program while others are essentially fixed. Which of these factors generally CANNOT be modified by training?","options":["The athlete's habitual activity level","The bony architecture of the joint itself","The athlete's tolerance to the stretch sensation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The bony architecture of the joint itself","explanation_en":"Joint structure, like age and sex, cannot be altered by training, whereas activity level and stretch tolerance can.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"關節的骨骼構造(joint structure)與年齡、性別一樣無法靠訓練改變;活動程度與對伸展感的耐受力則可以訓練改善。"},{"id":"q0626","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach compares the shoulder, which permits reaching in nearly every direction, with the knee, which is largely restricted to flexion and extension. Regarding the shoulder as a ball-and-socket joint, which statement is correct?","options":["It offers a more limited range of motion essentially confined to the sagittal plane","It lacks any capacity for movement across multiple planes","It allows the greatest range of motion of all joint types, moving through all anatomical planes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It allows the greatest range of motion of all joint types, moving through all anatomical planes","explanation_en":"Ball-and-socket joints move in all anatomical planes and have the greatest ROM of all joints.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肩關節是球窩關節,可在所有解剖面向活動,是所有關節型別中活動度最大的;膝等屈戍關節則主要只有矢狀面的屈伸。"},{"id":"q0627","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"An athlete bounces quickly into a deep hamstring stretch and the muscle immediately tightens rather than lengthening. Which receptor is responsible for this response, and what does it do?","options":["The muscle spindle, which detects the rapid change in length and triggers a reflexive contraction","The muscle spindle, which detects tension and produces reflexive relaxation","The Golgi tendon organ, which senses tension and drives the muscle to relax"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The muscle spindle, which detects the rapid change in length and triggers a reflexive contraction","explanation_en":"The muscle spindle monitors length changes; a rapid stretch activates it, causing the stretch reflex contraction.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌梭(muscle spindle)監測肌肉長度變化的速率;快速彈震式伸展會啟用它,引發牽張反射使肌肉反射性收縮而變緊。"},{"id":"q0628","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"During a held stretch, sustained high tension in the muscle-tendon unit eventually activates the Golgi tendon organ. What response does this produce?","options":["A reflexive contraction that shortens the muscle","A reflexive relaxation of the muscle experiencing the tension","A heightening of the stretch reflex that increases resistance to the stretch"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A reflexive relaxation of the muscle experiencing the tension","explanation_en":"The GTO is sensitive to increased tension and causes the muscle to reflexively relax.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官(GTO)感受張力;持續高張力會引發該肌肉反射性放鬆,這正是很多伸展技術利用的機制。"},{"id":"q0629","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"In a PNF hamstring stretch, the athlete first contracts the hamstrings against resistance, and moments later that same muscle relaxes and lengthens further. The relaxation of the previously contracting muscle is termed:","options":["Reciprocal inhibition, occurring in the opposing muscle group","Reciprocal inhibition, occurring in an unrelated stabilizing muscle","Autogenic inhibition, occurring in the same muscle that generated the tension"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Autogenic inhibition, occurring in the same muscle that generated the tension","explanation_en":"Autogenic inhibition is relaxation occurring in the same muscle that built up tension, mediated by the GTO.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一塊肌肉在產生張力之後隨之放鬆,稱為自體抑制(autogenic inhibition),由高爾基腱器官中介;互動抑制(reciprocal inhibition)發生在拮抗肌上。"},{"id":"q0630","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"To relax a tight hamstring during a stretch, an athlete actively contracts the quadriceps and the hamstring lets go, allowing greater range. This use of reciprocal inhibition works by contracting which muscle?","options":["The quadriceps, the muscle opposing the one being stretched","Both the hamstring and quadriceps maximally at the same time","The hamstring itself, the muscle being passively stretched"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The quadriceps, the muscle opposing the one being stretched","explanation_en":"Reciprocal inhibition results from contracting the muscle opposing the one being passively stretched, relaxing the stretched muscle.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"互動抑制的做法是主動收縮被伸展肌肉的拮抗肌:這裡收縮股四頭肌,使被伸展的膕繩肌反射性放鬆,從而取得更大活動度。"},{"id":"q0631","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach wants the PNF variation that draws on both autogenic and reciprocal inhibition to maximize range-of-motion gains. Which technique should be selected?","options":["Contract-relax, using a concentric contraction of the stretched muscle only","Hold-relax with agonist contraction, adding a contraction of the opposing muscle","Hold-relax, using a static contraction of the stretched muscle only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Hold-relax with agonist contraction, adding a contraction of the opposing muscle","explanation_en":"Hold-relax with agonist contraction is most effective because it uses both reciprocal and autogenic inhibition.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"hold-relax with agonist contraction(保持-放鬆並加拮抗肌收縮)同時呼叫自體抑制與互動抑制兩種機制,是增加活動度最有效的PNF變化式。"},{"id":"q0632","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"An athlete asks how long to hold each position when doing static stretching to develop range of motion. What is the generally recommended hold duration per stretch?","options":["About 60 to 90 seconds","About 1 to 5 seconds","About 10 to 30 seconds"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 10 to 30 seconds","explanation_en":"A static stretch is generally held for about 10 to 30 seconds; evidence supports holds around 30 seconds, with diminishing returns beyond that.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"靜態伸展每個動作一般建議停留約10-30秒;證據顯示約30秒左右已足夠,更長的停留效益遞減。"},{"id":"q0633","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Two athletes both stretch a tight muscle group, but one holds each stretch far longer per repetition while the other accumulates more stretching across the week. Regarding gains in range of motion, which factor is suggested to matter more than the length of any single stretch?","options":["The total weekly stretching time and frequency","The specific time of day at which stretching is performed","The athlete's total body weight"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The total weekly stretching time and frequency","explanation_en":"Evidence suggests weekly stretching time and frequency may matter more than the duration of any single stretch.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"證據指出每週伸展的總時間與頻率,可能比單次伸展停留多久更重要;規律累積比一次撐很久更有效。"},{"id":"q0634","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A coach evaluates two athletes: one is notably stiff with restricted range, the other is extremely lax with joints that move well beyond normal limits. What is the correct view of how flexibility relates to injury risk?","options":["More flexibility always lowers injury risk, so the lax athlete is the safer of the two","Both insufficient flexibility and excessive hyperflexibility can raise injury risk, so an activity-appropriate range is the goal","Flexibility bears no meaningful relationship to injury risk in either athlete"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Both insufficient flexibility and excessive hyperflexibility can raise injury risk, so an activity-appropriate range is the goal","explanation_en":"Both inflexibility and hyperflexibility can raise injury risk; an optimal ROM for the activity is the goal.","tags":["Chapter 15 quiz: Performance Preparation, Mobility, and Flexibility"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"活動度不足與過度鬆弛(hyperflexibility)都可能提高受傷風險,目標是符合該運動需求的適當活動度,不是愈軟愈好。"},{"id":"q0635","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter sets up for a barbell curl with the palms facing up and the knuckles pointing toward the floor. Which grip is being used?","options":["A pronated, or overhand, grip","A supinated, or underhand, grip","A hook grip"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A supinated, or underhand, grip","explanation_en":"The supinated, or underhand, grip has palms up and knuckles down.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"掌心朝上、指節朝向地面的握法是反握(supinated/underhand grip);掌心朝下才是旋前正握。"},{"id":"q0636","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A weightlifter grips the bar overhand but then tucks the thumb against the bar first and wraps the index and middle fingers over the thumb to secure it. Compared with a standard pronated grip, what defines this hook grip?","options":["One hand is supinated while the other is pronated","The palms are turned to face up rather than down","The thumb is positioned under the fingers against the bar"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The thumb is positioned under the fingers against the bar","explanation_en":"The hook grip is like a pronated grip except the thumb is placed under the fingers to give a stronger grip.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"勾式握(hook grip)與旋前正握相同,差別是拇指先貼槓、再由食指與中指從上方壓住拇指,以提供更大的握力。"},{"id":"q0637","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Preparing for a heavy deadlift, a lifter turns one palm to face backward and the other to face forward on the bar. This grip is best described as:","options":["An alternated grip, with one hand pronated and the other supinated","A neutral grip, with both palms facing each other","A double hook grip, with both thumbs tucked under the fingers"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"An alternated grip, with one hand pronated and the other supinated","explanation_en":"In an alternated grip one hand is pronated and the other is supinated.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一手掌心朝後(旋前)、另一手朝前(旋後)的抓槓方式是交替握(alternated/mixed grip),常見於大重量硬拉。"},{"id":"q0638","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A coach notices a lifter benching with the thumbs resting on the same side of the bar as the fingers rather than wrapped around it. What term describes this grip, and how does it differ from a closed grip?","options":["It is a false grip, meaning the thumb is tucked under the fingers as in a hook grip","It is an open or false grip; a closed grip has the thumb wrapped around the bar while this one does not","It is a false grip that is defined by being wider than any closed grip"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It is an open or false grip; a closed grip has the thumb wrapped around the bar while this one does not","explanation_en":"In a closed grip the thumb wraps around the bar; an open or false grip leaves the thumb off.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"拇指與手指同側、不環繞槓鈴的握法稱開放式或虛假握(open/false grip);封閉式握(closed grip)的拇指環繞槓身,這是兩者的定義差別。"},{"id":"q0639","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A coach cues a lifter to establish the five-point body contact position before pressing on a bench. Which set of contact points is correct?","options":["Head, both hands, and both feet","Shoulders, hips, both knees, and one foot","Head, shoulders and upper back, buttocks, right foot, and left foot"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Head, shoulders and upper back, buttocks, right foot, and left foot","explanation_en":"The five points are the head, shoulders/upper back, buttocks, right foot, and left foot.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"五點身體接觸位置是:頭部、肩與上背、臀部、左腳、右腳,共五點貼住凳面/地面,提供臥推時的穩定基礎。"},{"id":"q0640","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter grinds through the hardest part of a bench press rep. Following the standard breathing recommendation for most resistance exercises, when should the exhalation occur?","options":["Through the sticking point of the concentric phase","Only while briefly holding the breath at the top of the movement","During the eccentric, lowering phase as the bar descends"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Through the sticking point of the concentric phase","explanation_en":"Athletes should typically exhale through the sticking point of the concentric phase and inhale during the less stressful phase.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多數阻力練習的標準呼吸建議:在向心階段最吃力的黏著點(sticking point)呼氣,在較輕鬆的階段(通常是離心下放)吸氣。"},{"id":"q0641","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"An experienced lifter briefly braces before a maximal squat, and a coach explains that the resulting rigid trunk helps support the spine. Which action produces this bracing effect?","options":["Rapid, shallow breathing maintained throughout the lift","Expiring against a closed glottis so the trunk musculature creates rigid compartments","Inhaling fully and simply holding that air for the entire set"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Expiring against a closed glottis so the trunk musculature creates rigid compartments","explanation_en":"The Valsalva maneuver is expiring against a closed glottis, which with abdominal and rib cage muscle action stiffens the torso to support the spine.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"瓦式動作(Valsalva maneuver)是對著閉合的聲門呼氣,配合腹部與肋間肌收縮,使軀幹形成剛性腔室以支撐脊椎。"},{"id":"q0642","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter uses the Valsalva maneuver on a heavy squat. Because of its effect on blood pressure, what precaution governs how long the breath-holding phase should last?","options":["It should be released and re-applied several times within a single rep","It should extend across the entire repetition from start to finish","It should be quite transient, lasting only about 1 to 2 seconds at most"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It should be quite transient, lasting only about 1 to 2 seconds at most","explanation_en":"Because blood pressure can rise sharply, the breath-holding phase should be transient, only about 1 to 2 seconds at most.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"瓦式動作會使血壓急升,所以閉氣階段務必短暫,最多約1-2秒即應撥出,不宜憋滿整個動作。"},{"id":"q0643","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A coach must decide when to have an athlete wear a weight belt. For which of the following is a belt most clearly appropriate?","options":["A back squat or deadlift performed with a near-maximal or maximal load","A lat pulldown performed with a light load","A standing biceps curl with a moderate load"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A back squat or deadlift performed with a near-maximal or maximal load","explanation_en":"A weight belt is recommended for exercises stressing the lower back performed with near-maximal or maximal loads.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"舉重腰帶的使用建議是對下揹負荷大的動作(如 back squat、deadlift)且採接近最大或最大重量時;輕負荷下拉或彎舉不需要。"},{"id":"q0644","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"An athlete wears a weight belt for nearly every set of every session, including light accessory work. What is the main drawback of relying on the belt this heavily?","options":["It raises the likelihood of losing control of and dropping the bar","It reduces the training stimulus to the abdominal and lower back musculature over time","It makes performing the Valsalva maneuver impossible during the lift"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It reduces the training stimulus to the abdominal and lower back musculature over time","explanation_en":"Overusing a belt reduces the training stimulus to the abdominal and lower back muscles.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期每套都繫腰帶(包括輕重量輔助動作)的主要缺點,是腹肌與下背肌接受到的訓練刺激被剝奪,核心自身穩定能力退化。"},{"id":"q0645","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A coach reviews which lifts in a session require an over-the-bar spotter and which do not. For which exercise should the athlete NOT be spotted, and instead be taught to miss safely?","options":["The barbell bench press","The back squat","The power clean"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The power clean","explanation_en":"Power exercises are not spotted; instead athletes are taught how to safely miss and get away from the bar.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"爆發力式動作(power clean等舉重類動作)不保護,教練要教選手安全地「棄槓脫身」;需要保護的是臥推、深蹲這類槓鈴經過身體的動作。"},{"id":"q0646","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A spotter prepares to assist a lifter on a barbell exercise where the bar travels over the face, such as a lying triceps extension. Which grip should the spotter use on the bar?","options":["A closed, alternated grip, usually placed narrower than and inside the athlete's grip","A pronated grip positioned wider than the athlete's hands","A supinated grip placed outside the athlete's hands"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A closed, alternated grip, usually placed narrower than and inside the athlete's grip","explanation_en":"Over-the-face barbell exercises are spotted with an alternated grip, usually narrower than and inside the athlete's grip.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"槓鈴經過臉部的動作(如仰臥三頭肌伸展)保護時,保護者用封閉式交替握(closed alternated grip),位置通常比選手握距更窄、在其握內,便於控制槓鈴。"},{"id":"q0647","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A spotter assists a lifter performing heavy dumbbell chest presses. To keep the athlete safest if the elbows begin to collapse, where should the spotter apply support?","options":["At the athlete's elbows or upper arms","At the forearms, close to the wrists","Directly beneath the athlete's chest under the dumbbells"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At the forearms, close to the wrists","explanation_en":"Spotting at the forearms near the wrists is safer; spotting at the elbows risks the dumbbells striking the athlete if the elbows collapse.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"啞鈴臥推保護時應托住選手靠近手腕的前臂;若托肘部,一旦肘部塌陷,啞鈴會砸向選手的臉或胸部。"},{"id":"q0648","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A load is light enough that one competent spotter can handle it safely. Why is using that single spotter often preferred over recruiting two or more?","options":["Regulations prohibit two people from spotting the same lift together","A single spotter is inherently stronger than any pair of spotters","Adding spotters means coordinating timing, which increases the chance of a spotting error"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Adding spotters means coordinating timing, which increases the chance of a spotting error","explanation_en":"As the number of spotters increases, so does the chance of a timing or technique error, so one is preferred when feasible.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"一個保護者能應付的重量就優先用一人:保護者愈多,出手時機愈需要同步,配合失誤的風險愈高。"},{"id":"q0649","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Before a bench press, a spotter helps move the loaded bar out of the uprights and into position over the lifter's chest so the set can begin. This action is referred to as:","options":["A liftoff, moving the bar from the upright supports to the athlete's start position","Reaching the peak of the concentric phase of the lift","The athlete jumping clear of a missed bar"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A liftoff, moving the bar from the upright supports to the athlete's start position","explanation_en":"A liftoff is moving the bar from the upright supports into the position where the athlete begins the exercise.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"保護者把槓鈴從架柱(liftoff)托到選手的開始位置(胸前)讓組得以開始,這個動作就叫liftoff。"},{"id":"q0650","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter sets up a back squat with the bar carried in the high bar position. Where does the bar sit and how wide is the grip?","options":["On the anterior deltoids and clavicles, with a narrow grip","Above the posterior deltoids at the base of the neck, with a grip only slightly wider than shoulder width","Across the posterior deltoids at the mid-trapezius, with a wide grip"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Above the posterior deltoids at the base of the neck, with a grip only slightly wider than shoulder width","explanation_en":"High bar position places the bar above the posterior deltoids at the base of the neck with a grip only slightly wider than shoulder width.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高槓深蹲(high bar)的槓鈴放在後三角肌上方、頸根部,握距僅比肩稍寬;放在斜方肌中部並採寬握的是低槓位置。"},{"id":"q0651","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"During the upward phase of a deadlift, a coach watches the lifter's hips shoot up faster than the shoulders, so the bar drifts and the back rounds. Which cue corrects this fault?","options":["Allow the bar to travel forward, away from the shins, as it rises","Deliberately let the hips rise ahead of the shoulders to clear the bar path","Keep the torso-to-floor angle constant so the hips and shoulders rise together"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Keep the torso-to-floor angle constant so the hips and shoulders rise together","explanation_en":"The deadlift requires keeping the torso-to-floor angle constant so the hips do not rise before the shoulders.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"硬拉上升時正確 cue 是維持軀幹與地面的角度固定,讓髖與肩同步上升;髖衝得比肩快會造成槓鈴漂移、背部圓弧。"},{"id":"q0652","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter transitions from back squats to front squats and must reposition the bar. Where is the bar racked for the front squat?","options":["On top of the anterior deltoids and clavicles, using a parallel-arm or crossed-arm hold","Across the posterior deltoids on the upper back, as in a back squat","In the crease of the flexed elbows in front of the body"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"On top of the anterior deltoids and clavicles, using a parallel-arm or crossed-arm hold","explanation_en":"The front squat racks the bar on the anterior deltoids and clavicles using either a parallel-arm or crossed-arm position.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"前深蹲的槓鈴架在前三角肌上方與鎖骨,以平行手臂式(parallel-arm)或交叉手臂式(crossed-arm)手架住;放後三角肌上的是後深蹲。"},{"id":"q0653","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A lifter performing good mornings bends the knees deeply and drops into a squat-like pattern, and the coach flags this as a common technique error. What movement pattern should the good morning actually be?","options":["An overhead pressing movement of the loaded bar","A hip hinge in which the buttocks travel straight back with minimal knee flexion","A deep, knee-dominant squat driven by bending the knees"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A hip hinge in which the buttocks travel straight back with minimal knee flexion","explanation_en":"The good morning is a hip hinge; flexing the knees too much turns it into a squat, which is a common error.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"good morning的正確動作是髖鉸鏈(hip hinge):臀部往正後方推、膝蓋彎曲極少;屈膝過深蹲下去就變成深蹲,這是最常見的技術錯誤。"},{"id":"q0654","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"A coach breaks down the power clean from the floor into its constituent phases for a new athlete. Which sequence correctly lists those phases in order?","options":["Setup, press, lockout, then lower","Dip, drive, catch, then recovery","First pull, transition, second pull, then catch"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"First pull, transition, second pull, then catch","explanation_en":"The power clean consists of the first pull, transition, second pull, and catch, performed in one continuous motion.","tags":["Chapter 16 quiz: Exercise Technique for Free Weight and Machine Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"power clean從地面起的階段依序為第一拉(first pull)、轉換(transition)、第二拉(second pull)、接槓(catch),連續一個動作完成。"},{"id":"q0655","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A strength coach notices an experienced athlete briefly holding his breath while grinding out the final rep of a heavy squat set. Under the general guidelines for these training methods, how should the coach evaluate this breathing pattern?","options":["It is appropriate only during the eccentric phase of light single-joint exercises","It is a technique fault that should be corrected on every rep of any bodyweight movement","It is a reasonable, often unavoidable technique with heavy loads at or above 80 percent of maximal voluntary contraction or with lighter loads taken to failure"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It is a reasonable, often unavoidable technique with heavy loads at or above 80 percent of maximal voluntary contraction or with lighter loads taken to failure","explanation_en":"The Valsalva maneuver helps maintain spinal stability and may be unavoidable at loads at or above 80 percent of maximal voluntary contraction or with lighter loads taken to failure.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在負荷達80%最大自主收縮以上、或較輕負荷做到力竭時,閉氣(Valsalva)是合理且往往不可避免的,它幫助維持脊椎穩定;不該在輕重量孤立動作上還要求全面禁止。"},{"id":"q0656","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A lean, well-conditioned gymnast performs high volumes of push-ups, pull-ups, and dips but has plateaued in raw force production. What best explains why this style of training does little to advance absolute strength?","options":["The external resistance can never exceed the individual's own body weight","The movements demand specialized equipment that most athletes lack","The movements are open-chain and isolate single joints, limiting overload"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The external resistance can never exceed the individual's own body weight","explanation_en":"Because the resistance is capped at the individual's body weight, bodyweight training develops relative strength but does little for absolute strength.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"自重訓練(伏地挺身、引體、雙槓臂屈伸)的外在阻力最多就是自身體重,上限被鎖死,所以發展的是相對肌力,對絕對肌力幫助有限。"},{"id":"q0657","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"During a suspension-trainer row, an athlete wants to reduce the challenge of the exercise mid-set without changing the anchor or the device. What adjustment of the center of mass relative to the anchor point will accomplish this?","options":["Adjust the strap length, because body position does not change the load","Shift the center of mass farther from the anchor point","Shift the center of mass closer to the anchor point"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Shift the center of mass farther from the anchor point","explanation_en":"Generally, as the athlete's center of mass moves farther from the anchor point, the resistance to which the athlete is exposed decreases.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"懸吊訓練系統的阻力由身體傾角決定:把重心移得離錨點愈遠(身體愈接近垂直),承受的阻力愈小,可在不改變器材下即時調節難度。"},{"id":"q0658","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"When explaining what the anatomical core actually encompasses, which description is most complete and accurate?","options":["The pelvic and shoulder girdles that link the axial and appendicular skeletons","The abdominal wall musculature, chiefly the rectus abdominis and obliques","The axial skeleton plus all soft tissues with proximal attachments originating on the axial skeleton"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The axial skeleton plus all soft tissues with proximal attachments originating on the axial skeleton","explanation_en":"The anatomical core is defined as the axial skeleton plus all the soft tissues with proximal attachments that originate on the axial skeleton.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"解剖學上的核心定義為:中軸骨骼加上所有近端附著點起自中軸骨骼的軟組織,範圍遠大於「只有腹肌」。"},{"id":"q0659","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach is deciding whether to add dedicated isolation core drills for an athlete who already squats and deadlifts heavy from the floor. What does the evidence suggest about core recruitment during those free weight lifts?","options":["It is similar to, and in most cases greater than, that of traditional isolation core drills","It is negligible, since only isolation drills meaningfully recruit the core","It is far lower than in isolation core drills, so the added drills are essential"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It is similar to, and in most cases greater than, that of traditional isolation core drills","explanation_en":"Ground-based free weight activities offer core activation that is similar to, or in most cases greater than, that seen with traditional isolation core exercises.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究顯示蹲、硬拉等地面自由重量動作招募核心的程度與傳統孤立核心動作相當、多數情況下還更高,所以已有大重量深蹲硬拉的選手不必然要再加孤立核心訓練。"},{"id":"q0660","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A healthy, resistance-trained athlete asks whether performing squats on a wobble board or stability platform will boost his power output. What does the evidence indicate for this population?","options":["The instability maximizes force and power output over stable-surface lifting","The instability mutes performance gains and lowers force, power, and rate of force development","The instability is necessary to build the sport-specific core stability he needs"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The instability mutes performance gains and lowers force, power, and rate of force development","explanation_en":"Training on unstable devices reduces force, power, and rate of force development and produces muted performance improvements compared with stable free weight training.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"對已受訓練的運動員,在不穩定平面(wobble board)上做深蹲會降低力量、功率與發力速率(RFD),表現改善反而被削弱;不穩定表面不是提升功率的工具。"},{"id":"q0661","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"An athlete drapes heavy chains over a loaded barbell for the back squat. As he descends and the chain links accumulate on the floor, how does the total resistance behave, and where is it lowest?","options":["Resistance stays essentially constant because the chains simply hang from the bar","Resistance is lowest at lockout, where the bar is farthest from the floor","Resistance is lowest at the bottom, where the links pile on the floor and unload the bar"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Resistance is lowest at the bottom, where the links pile on the floor and unload the bar","explanation_en":"At the bottom of the movement the chain links pile on the floor, reducing the load and allowing the athlete to accelerate the bar.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鏈條式阻力:下蹲到底時鏈節堆積在地面、分擔重量,此時總阻力最低;越接近鎖定站起懸空鏈節愈多、阻力愈大,符合深蹲的力量曲線(strength curve)並鼓勵加速推起。"},{"id":"q0662","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach measures that a band adds 20 lb of resistance at the bottom and 60 lb at the top of a bench press, and wants a target bar-plus-band load of 200 lb. How should the fixed plate load on the bar be determined?","options":["Load the bar to the target minus the average of the top and bottom resistances","Load the bar to the target minus the sum of the top and bottom resistances","Load the bar to the target minus only the top-position resistance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Load the bar to the target minus the average of the top and bottom resistances","explanation_en":"The absolute resistances at the top and bottom are summed and averaged, and that average is subtracted from the target load on the bar.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"彈性帶負荷的演算法是把上下位置阻力(20+60)取平均=40磅,再從目標200磅減去,槓片裝160磅;即「目標減去上下阻力的平均值」。"},{"id":"q0663","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Two athletes use the same resistance band, but one anchors it so it is stretched much farther at the start position. Applying Hooke's law, what primarily governs the difference in band tension they experience?","options":["The manufacturer's color coding of the band","The band's stiffness multiplied by how far it is deformed (stretched)","The body weight each athlete brings to the movement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The band's stiffness multiplied by how far it is deformed (stretched)","explanation_en":"Band tension equals stiffness (k) multiplied by deformation (d), so tension rises as the band is stretched farther.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"虎克定律(Hooke's law):張力=彈性帶剛度(k)×變形量(d);起點就拉得愈長的設定,感受到的張力愈高,顏色或體重都不是決定因素。"},{"id":"q0664","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Accentuated eccentric loading applies extra load only during the lowering phase and removes it before the lift. Which property of muscle action does this method specifically capitalize on?","options":["Eccentric and concentric maximal force are essentially equal across the range","Muscles are weaker eccentrically than concentrically, so lowering is the limiting phase","Muscles generate more force eccentrically than concentrically, so a constant load leaves the eccentric phase underloaded"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Muscles generate more force eccentrically than concentrically, so a constant load leaves the eccentric phase underloaded","explanation_en":"Muscles are stronger eccentrically than concentrically, so a constant load underloads the eccentric phase, which AEL addresses by adding load only during lowering.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉離心收縮能產生的最大力量大於向心,所以恆定負荷下離心階段其實「吃不飽」;AEL(強調式離心負荷)只在下放時加碼,正是利用這個特性。"},{"id":"q0665","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach is considering which of three lifters is the best candidate for accentuated eccentric loading. For whom is this method generally most appropriate?","options":["A lifter with extensive resistance training experience and a strong strength base","An athlete in the early return-to-play phase of rehabilitation","A novice still learning basic lifting technique"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A lifter with extensive resistance training experience and a strong strength base","explanation_en":"AEL is an advanced training tactic that should be reserved for athletes with extensive resistance training experience and adequate strength.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"AEL屬於進階訓練策略,適合訓練經歷豐富、已有足夠肌力基礎的選手;新手動作還沒穩、復健早期選手都不適合承受額外離心負荷。"},{"id":"q0666","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach wants to use accentuated eccentric loading to potentiate the concentric phase of a countermovement jump, releasing the added load before takeoff. What eccentric load, expressed as a percentage of body mass, is recommended?","options":["About 5 to 10 percent of body mass","About 20 to 30 percent of body mass","About 50 to 60 percent of body mass"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 20 to 30 percent of body mass","explanation_en":"Loads of 20 to 30 percent of body mass applied eccentrically and released before the concentric phase improve plyometric jump performance.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"用AEL增強CMJ縱跳:建議離心階段加約20-30%體重的額外負荷,並在起跳(向心)前卸除,可改善伸展收縮表現。"},{"id":"q0667","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"An athlete using the shoulders-against-the-tire flip technique keeps rounding his back and stalling at the start. The coach sees his feet are jammed up against the tire. What is the correct fix?","options":["Keep the feet close but round the back further to shorten the lever to the tire","Pull the tire straight upward rather than driving the hips and chest forward","Move the feet back from the tire and drive through a forceful triple extension to raise the chest and tire"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Move the feet back from the tire and drive through a forceful triple extension to raise the chest and tire","explanation_en":"Placing the feet too close forces a rounded back; the correction is to move the feet back and use a forceful triple extension to raise the chest and tire off the ground.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"翻輪胎時雙腳貼太近會迫使背部圓弧、起不來;正確修正是把腳離輪胎遠一點,用有力的三重伸展(踝、膝、髖)同時把胸部與輪胎抬起。"},{"id":"q0668","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Research compared the log lift with the barbell clean and jerk. Given the log's larger diameter, which pattern of differences was actually observed?","options":["The log produced greater impulse and hip and trunk range of motion but lower vertical velocity and power","The two lifts were statistically indistinguishable across all measured variables","The log produced greater vertical bar velocity and greater power output"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The log produced greater impulse and hip and trunk range of motion but lower vertical velocity and power","explanation_en":"The log lift produced significantly greater impulse and hip and trunk range of motion but less vertical velocity and power, reflecting the greater diameter of the log.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究實測:圓木(log lift)因直徑較大,衝量與髖、軀幹活動度比槓鈴 clean and jerk 更大,但垂直速度與功率輸出較低,並非兩者無差異。"},{"id":"q0669","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach adds farmer's walks and yoke walks to a program. What is the primary training adaptation these loaded carries are chosen to develop?","options":["Isolated hypertrophy of a single small muscle group","Total body and trunk stability, with high anterior-posterior and vertical impulse demands","Cardiovascular endurance with essentially no strength or stability demand"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Total body and trunk stability, with high anterior-posterior and vertical impulse demands","explanation_en":"Weighted carries develop total body and trunk stability, grip strength, and the ability to produce high anterior-posterior and vertical impulse.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"農夫走、負重架行走這類負重行走(load carries)主要發展全身與軀幹穩定、握力,以及產生前後向與垂直方向高衝量的能力。"},{"id":"q0670","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"An athlete wants to replace his barbell work with kettlebell swings and cleans to build maximal strength and vertical jump. How should the coach frame kettlebell training relative to traditional weightlifting?","options":["The two approaches produce equivalent maximal strength and jump adaptations","Kettlebells outperform traditional weightlifting for both maximal strength and jumping","Kettlebells yield smaller gains, so they suit general preparation while traditional weightlifting drives strength and jumping"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Kettlebells yield smaller gains, so they suit general preparation while traditional weightlifting drives strength and jumping","explanation_en":"Kettlebell training increases strength and jump performance less than traditional weightlifting, so kettlebells are best used as general preparation exercise.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究比較顯示壺鈴訓練在最大肌力與垂直彈跳的增幅都小於傳統重量訓練,所以壺鈴適合當一般準備期練習,不能取代槓鈴作為最大肌力與彈跳的主訓練。"},{"id":"q0671","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"As an athlete walks a loaded yoke across the floor, the coach cues spinal posture. Which position should be maintained throughout the carry?","options":["A predominantly neutral, vertical spine with no substantial hyperextension, flexion, or lateral flexion","A deliberately hyperextended spine to increase bracing against the load","A spine laterally flexed toward the side bearing more of the load"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A predominantly neutral, vertical spine with no substantial hyperextension, flexion, or lateral flexion","explanation_en":"The athlete should keep a predominantly neutral and vertical spine with no substantial hyperextension, flexion, or lateral flexion while carrying.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"扛負重架行走全程應保持脊椎中立、接近垂直,不要明顯過度伸展、彎曲或側彎,才能安全承重並訓練到穩定。"},{"id":"q0672","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach observes that the sum of an athlete's separate single-leg press outputs exceeds his two-leg press output. This bilateral deficit is most characteristic of which type of individual, who may therefore gain from unilateral training?","options":["Highly trained, stronger athletes","Untrained, weaker, or injured individuals","Elite powerlifters exclusively"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Untrained, weaker, or injured individuals","explanation_en":"Untrained, weaker, or injured athletes tend to show a bilateral deficit, so unilateral methods may be useful for their strength development.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"雙側虧損(兩腿個別輸出的和大於雙腿一起輸出)較常出現在未受訓練、肌力較弱或受傷的個體,這類物件可能從不穩定/單側訓練獲得較大益處。"},{"id":"q0673","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A coach anchors one end of a barbell in a pivoting floor sleeve and loads the free end. What kind of training is this landmine setup primarily suited to deliver?","options":["Pure aerobic endurance conditioning","Maximal isometric holds against a fixed bar","Loaded rotational and multiplanar resistance exercises using the bar as a lever"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Loaded rotational and multiplanar resistance exercises using the bar as a lever","explanation_en":"The landmine anchors one end of a barbell through a pivot so it can be used as a lever for loaded rotational and multiplanar movements.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"landmine把槓鈴一端固定在地板轉軸上,自由端當作槓桿,主要提供負重的旋轉性與多面向(multiplanar)練習,不是純有氧或等長訓練。"},{"id":"q0674","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A sprint coach wants to use heavy sled pulls to potentiate a subsequent 15 m sprint (a PAPE effect). What loading range, expressed as a percentage of body mass, does research associate with that effect?","options":["About 66 to 75 percent of body mass","About 150 to 200 percent of body mass","About 10 to 20 percent of body mass"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 66 to 75 percent of body mass","explanation_en":"Sled pulls with loads between roughly 66 and 75 percent of body mass had the potential to produce 15-meter sprint PAPE effects in running athletes.","tags":["Chapter 17 quiz: Exercise Technique for Alternative Modes and Nontraditional Implement Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"研究顯示約66-75%體重的重雪橇拉曳,能對後續15米衝刺產生啟用後表現增強(PAPE)效果;太輕或過重都沒有這個證據支援。"},{"id":"q0675","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Before writing a resistance training program, a coach first studies the movement patterns, injury sites, and physiological demands of the sport, then evaluates the individual athlete's training age, test results, and goals. These two activities make up which process, and in what order?","options":["Evaluating the sport, then assessing the athlete","Setting session frequency, then ordering exercises","Selecting exercises, then assigning loads"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Evaluating the sport, then assessing the athlete","explanation_en":"A needs analysis evaluates the requirements and characteristics of the sport and then assesses the individual athlete's status and goals.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"需求分析(needs analysis)程式依序是:先評估運動(動作型態、好發傷害部位、生理需求),再評估選手本人(訓練年資、測驗結果、目標),之後才設計課表。"},{"id":"q0676","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach explains that if an athlete trains slowly with heavy loads, he adapts toward strength rather than speed. This idea, closely tied to specificity, is captured by the acronym SAID, which stands for what?","options":["Strength and intensity development","Specific adaptation to imposed demands","Sets and intervals during deloads"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Specific adaptation to imposed demands","explanation_en":"SAID means specific adaptation to imposed demands: the type of demand placed on the body dictates the adaptation that occurs.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"SAID意為「對所施加需求產生特定適應」:給身體什麼型態的負荷,就朝那個方向適應,與特異性原則同一件事。"},{"id":"q0677","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"An athlete has adapted to his current program and stops progressing, so the coach increases the load beyond what the athlete is accustomed to in order to drive new adaptation. Which training principle is the coach applying?","options":["Individualization","Reversibility","Overload"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Overload","explanation_en":"Overload is applying a stimulus beyond the athlete's accustomed level to produce adaptation past baseline abilities.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"超負荷原則(overload):給予超過選手已習慣程度的刺激,才能推動超越現有能力的適應;停止進步就代表需要加碼。"},{"id":"q0678","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach wants to prioritize the exercises with the greatest carryover for a team sport. Which combination of features identifies an exercise as a core (rather than assistance) exercise?","options":["One or more large muscle areas acting across two or more primary joints","An isometric hold that stabilizes the trunk without joint movement","A small muscle area acting across a single primary joint"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"One or more large muscle areas acting across two or more primary joints","explanation_en":"Core exercises recruit one or more large muscle areas and involve two or more primary joints, giving them priority in selection.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"核心動作(core exercise)的判定特徵是動用一處以上大肌群、且跨越兩個以上主要關節,因此動作選擇時列優先;小肌群單關節是輔助動作。"},{"id":"q0679","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"An exercise loads the spine directly and is performed explosively, such as a power clean. Within the exercise classification scheme, how is it best categorized?","options":["An assistance exercise","A power exercise","A muscular endurance exercise"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A power exercise","explanation_en":"A structural exercise that is performed very quickly or explosively is considered a power exercise.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"結構性動作若以非常快速/爆發的方式執行(如power clean直接壓迫脊椎又要求爆發力),歸類為power exercise(功率動作)。"},{"id":"q0680","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach is setting weekly training frequency for a highly experienced athlete in a demanding phase. What resistance training frequency is appropriate for this advanced level?","options":["2 to 3 sessions per week","3 to 4 sessions per week","4 to 7 sessions per week, potentially with multiple sessions in a day"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"4 to 7 sessions per week, potentially with multiple sessions in a day","explanation_en":"Advanced athletes can train 4 to 7 times per week and may include multiple sessions per day depending on the phase.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"先進選手的訓練頻率可達每週4-7次,依訓練期程甚至一天兩課;初學者才用每週2-3次的低頻。"},{"id":"q0681","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A session includes power cleans, back squats, and biceps curls. Because the cleans are the most skill- and fatigue-sensitive, where in the order should they be placed?","options":["First, while the athlete is still fresh and unfatigued","In the middle, after the assistance work is done","Last, to finish the session on a high-intensity note"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"First, while the athlete is still fresh and unfatigued","explanation_en":"Power exercises require high skill and are prone to fatigue, so they are performed first while the athlete is fresh, then other core, then assistance.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"power clean等功率動作技巧要求高、又最易受疲勞影響,必須排在課表最前面、選手體力最新鮮時做;之後才是其他核心動作與輔助動作。"},{"id":"q0682","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach sequences a bench press immediately followed by a bent-over row, then a shoulder press followed by a lat pulldown. What is the main rationale for this push-pull arrangement?","options":["It improves the accuracy of one-repetition-maximum testing","It avoids using the same muscle group in two consecutive exercises, limiting fatigue there","It removes the need to schedule rest periods between sets"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It avoids using the same muscle group in two consecutive exercises, limiting fatigue there","explanation_en":"A push-pull arrangement keeps the same muscle group from being used in two exercises in a row, reducing fatigue in those muscles.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"推(胸推、肩推)與拉(划船、滑下拉)交替編排的主因,是避免同一肌群在連續兩個動作中重複使用,讓該肌群有時間恢復、限制區域性疲勞。"},{"id":"q0683","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"An athlete finishes a set of barbell biceps curls and, with no other exercise between, immediately performs hammer curls for the same muscle group. Which term describes this pairing?","options":["Circuit training","A superset","A compound set"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A compound set","explanation_en":"A compound set sequentially performs two different exercises for the same muscle group; a superset instead pairs an agonist and its antagonist.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一肌群的兩個不同動作(槓鈴彎舉接錘式彎舉)之間不插其他動作、連續進行,稱為複合組(compound set);超級組則是主動肌與其拮抗肌配對。"},{"id":"q0684","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach wants to estimate a load from a rep max using the percent-1RM-to-reps relationship as reliably as possible. Under which condition is that relationship most accurate?","options":["Loads greater than 75 percent of the 1RM for fewer than 10 repetitions","Any load, since the relationship holds equally across the whole range","Loads under 50 percent of the 1RM for more than 20 repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Loads greater than 75 percent of the 1RM for fewer than 10 repetitions","explanation_en":"The relationship is most accurate for loads greater than 75 percent of the 1RM and fewer than 10 repetitions, improving further at lower reps.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"百分比1RM與可完成次數之間的關係,在負荷大於75%1RM、次數少於10次的範圍內最準確,低次數時更準;輕負荷高次數區誤差大。"},{"id":"q0685","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach programs a core exercise with the goal of maximizing maximal strength. Which load and repetition prescription fits that goal?","options":["Less than 67 percent of the 1RM for 12 or more repetitions","At least 85 percent of the 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions","67 to 80 percent of the 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"At least 85 percent of the 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions","explanation_en":"Strength training in core exercises uses loads at or above 85 percent of the 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大肌力目標的核心動作處方是負荷至少85%1RM、次數不超過6下;67-80%×8-12下是肥大,<67%×12+是肌耐力。"},{"id":"q0686","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach designing a block aimed primarily at muscle cross-sectional growth consults the standard load-repetition assignments. Which prescription targets hypertrophy?","options":["Less than 67 percent of the 1RM for 12 or more repetitions","At least 85 percent of the 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions","67 to 80 percent of the 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"67 to 80 percent of the 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions","explanation_en":"The table assigns roughly 67 to 80 percent of the 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions to target hypertrophy, though a wide load range can work to failure.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"教科書表格把肥大目標對應約67-80%1RM、8-12下;雖然寬負荷範圍做到力竭也可能刺激肥大,標準處方以此為準。"},{"id":"q0687","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach wants an athlete to improve the ability to sustain repeated submaximal contractions. Which load and repetition prescription targets muscular endurance?","options":["67 percent of the 1RM or less for 12 or more repetitions","At least 85 percent of the 1RM for 6 or fewer repetitions","67 to 80 percent of the 1RM for 8 to 12 repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"67 percent of the 1RM or less for 12 or more repetitions","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance training uses lighter loads at or below 67 percent of the 1RM for 12 or more repetitions per set.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌肉耐力處方為負荷不超過67%1RM、每組12下以上,訓練反覆維持次最大收縮的能力。"},{"id":"q0688","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach is prescribing loads for single-joint assistance work like biceps curls and calf raises, aiming to limit isolative stress on the joint and connective tissue. What is the heaviest load these exercises should be assigned?","options":["No heavier than a 2RM","No heavier than an 8RM","No heavier than a 15RM"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"No heavier than an 8RM","explanation_en":"Assistance exercises should be limited to loads no heavier than an 8RM to minimize isolative stress on the involved joint and connective tissue.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"單關節輔助動作(彎舉、墊腳)的負荷最重不宜超過8RM,以降低對參與關節與結締組織的孤立壓力;大重量留給多關節核心動作。"},{"id":"q0689","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"An athlete's goal is 8 reps in his last set. He completes 10 reps in that set on Monday and 10 again on Wednesday. Applying the 2-for-2 rule, what should the coach do?","options":["Increase the load after every workout regardless of how many reps he completes","Wait until he fails a repetition before making any load change","Increase the load, since he beat the goal by 2 or more reps on the last set for two consecutive workouts"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increase the load, since he beat the goal by 2 or more reps on the last set for two consecutive workouts","explanation_en":"The 2-for-2 rule adds load when the athlete completes 2 or more reps above the goal in the last set across two consecutive sessions.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"2-for-2規則:若最後一次組完成的次數比目標多2下以上、且連續兩次訓練都如此(目標8下、兩次都做10下),就應該增加負荷。"},{"id":"q0690","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach programs strength work for a volleyball blocker, whose sport demands repeated maximal-effort jumps. For this multiple-effort power event, which loading is most appropriate?","options":["3 to 5 repetitions at 75 to 85 percent of the 1RM","12 or more repetitions at 50 percent of the 1RM","1 to 2 repetitions at 80 to 90 percent of the 1RM"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"3 to 5 repetitions at 75 to 85 percent of the 1RM","explanation_en":"Multiple-effort power events use about 3 to 5 reps per set with loads of 75 to 85 percent of the 1RM.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"多次反覆 maximal 輸出功率的專案(如排球攔網反覆起跳),肌力訓練建議每組3-5下、75-85%1RM;1-2下更適合單次全力專案。"},{"id":"q0691","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach assigns power cleans at a lighter load than the percent-1RM-to-rep relationship would predict for the target reps. What is the reasoning behind using the lighter load?","options":["Heavy loads are considered unsafe for any athlete performing this lift","A lighter load lets the athlete move at maximum speed to develop power, because technique breaks down before true muscle failure","The lift is being programmed to build muscular endurance rather than power"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A lighter load lets the athlete move at maximum speed to develop power, because technique breaks down before true muscle failure","explanation_en":"Power exercises cannot be maximally loaded because technique deteriorates before muscle failure, so lighter loads allow maximum-speed reps to develop power.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"power clean不照百分比-次數表配重,是因為這型別動作在肌肉真正力竭之前技術先走樣;用較輕負荷才能全程以最快速度移動、發展功率。"},{"id":"q0692","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"An athlete performs 3 sets of 10 repetitions with 100 lb on the back squat. Using the standard definition, what is the volume-load for that exercise, and how is it derived?","options":["The repetitions divided by the length of the rest period","The load divided by the number of sets performed","3,000 lb, from sets multiplied by repetitions multiplied by the load lifted"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"3,000 lb, from sets multiplied by repetitions multiplied by the load lifted","explanation_en":"Volume-load is the total sets times reps times the load; 3 sets of 10 reps with 100 pounds equals 3,000 pounds.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"負荷量(volume load)=組數×次數×重量=3×10×100磅=3,000磅,是衡量單動作總訓練量的標準演算法。"},{"id":"q0693","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach building a hypertrophy-focused program wants an appropriate per-exercise set volume. Which number of sets is generally recommended for hypertrophy?","options":["3 to 6 sets per exercise","A minimum of 8 to 10 sets per exercise","1 set per exercise"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"3 to 6 sets per exercise","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy is associated with higher volumes, commonly a moderate to high rep range with about 3 to 6 sets per exercise.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練建議每個動作約3-6組的中高組數;8-10組以上偏高、1組偏低,不符合標準處方範圍。"},{"id":"q0694","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"A coach programming heavy strength and power work wants rest periods long enough to preserve load and technique across sets. What rest interval is recommended for strength or power training?","options":["60 to 90 seconds between sets","2 to 5 minutes between sets","30 seconds or less between sets"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"2 to 5 minutes between sets","explanation_en":"Strength and power training uses 2 to 5 minute rest periods to permit greater work volume, heavier loads, and better adaptations.","tags":["Chapter 18 quiz: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肌力與功率訓練的組間休息建議2-5分鐘,足以維持後續組數的負荷與技術、完成較多總工作量;60-90秒是肥大區間。"},{"id":"q0695","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach wants a single training goal statement that captures what a plyometric exercise is actually built to develop. Which statement best fits?","options":["Progressively lengthening tissue to expand joint range of motion through held end-range positions","Producing the greatest possible force in the least possible time by exploiting a rapid prestretch","Accumulating the most total mechanical work across a prolonged set to build work capacity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Producing the greatest possible force in the least possible time by exploiting a rapid prestretch","explanation_en":"Plyometric exercise is defined as a quick, powerful movement using a prestretch to reach maximal force in minimal time.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式(plyometric)動作的定義:藉助快速的預伸展(prestretch),在最短時間產生最大力量的快速、爆發性動作。"},{"id":"q0696","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"An athlete performs a fast rebound and much of the propulsion seems to come from stored elastic energy rather than fresh contractile effort. In the mechanical model of plyometrics, which structure is chiefly responsible for storing and returning that energy?","options":["The Golgi tendon organ acting to recapture and release load","The parallel elastic component formed by the surrounding connective sheaths","The series elastic component, made up largely of tendon, behaving like a spring"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The series elastic component, made up largely of tendon, behaving like a spring","explanation_en":"The series elastic component, made up largely of tendon, acts like a spring that stores and releases elastic energy.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"串聯彈性成分(series elastic component)主要由肌腱組成,像彈簧一樣儲存與釋放彈性位能,是機械模型中儲能回彈的主角;平行彈性成分是被動的包裹組織。"},{"id":"q0697","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Two athletes land and rebound; the one who rebounds faster shows a burst of reflexive muscle activity triggered by the rapid stretch. In the neurophysiological model, this potentiation is attributed mainly to which mechanism?","options":["The stretch reflex driven by muscle spindles sensitive to rate and magnitude of stretch","A surge in anaerobic glycolytic energy supply meeting the sudden demand","Golgi tendon organ inhibition reducing tension to protect the tendon"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The stretch reflex driven by muscle spindles sensitive to rate and magnitude of stretch","explanation_en":"The stretch reflex, mediated by muscle spindles sensitive to the rate and magnitude of stretch, reflexively increases muscle activity.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"神經生理模型認為快速回彈的增強主要來自牽張反射:肌梭對拉伸的速率與幅度敏感,反射性提高肌肉活動,而不是靠無氧供能或GTO抑制。"},{"id":"q0698","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach is teaching a depth jump and wants to name the three phases in the exact order the athlete experiences them from box contact to takeoff. Which ordering is correct?","options":["Concentric shortening, then amortization, then eccentric loading","Eccentric loading, then amortization, then concentric shortening","Amortization, then eccentric loading, then concentric shortening"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Eccentric loading, then amortization, then concentric shortening","explanation_en":"The SSC proceeds eccentric (stretch), amortization (coupling pause), then concentric (shortening).","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"伸展縮短週期(SSC)三階段依序為:離心(拉長載入)、緩衝期(amortization)、向心(縮短髮力);depth jump從落地到起飛就是這個順序。"},{"id":"q0699","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"An athlete pauses noticeably on the ground between the landing and the jump. Why does coaching a shorter transition improve the outcome?","options":["It lengthens ground contact so more total force can be applied against the surface","It lets the athlete recover more fully between repetitions before exploding upward","A prolonged transition dissipates stored elastic energy as heat and blunts the stretch reflex contribution"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A prolonged transition dissipates stored elastic energy as heat and blunts the stretch reflex contribution","explanation_en":"If the amortization phase lasts too long, stored elastic energy is lost as heat and the stretch reflex no longer augments force.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"緩衝期(amortization)拖太久,儲存的彈效能量會以熱能散失、牽張反射的貢獻也消失;縮短落地到再起跳的轉換時間,回彈才更好。"},{"id":"q0700","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach labels a squat jump as one category and a drop jump as another. What is the correct basis for that distinction?","options":["The squat jump minimally involves stretch-shortening cycle contributions, whereas the drop jump depends on physiomechanical SSC contributions","The squat jump is inherently an upper body pattern while the drop jump is inherently a lower body pattern","The squat jump is loaded with heavier external resistance than the drop jump by definition"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The squat jump minimally involves stretch-shortening cycle contributions, whereas the drop jump depends on physiomechanical SSC contributions","explanation_en":"Ballistic exercises like a squat jump minimally involve the SSC, whereas rebound exercises like drop jumps depend on SSC contributions.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"區分類別的依據是SSC參與度:squat jump等彈道式(ballistic)動作幾乎不依賴伸展縮短週期(SSC)貢獻,drop jump等反彈式動作則以SSC的生理力學貢獻為主。"},{"id":"q0701","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach progresses an athlete from low box hops to high-intensity depth jumps. To keep the total stress appropriate, what should happen to the session volume as this intensity climbs?","options":["It should be held exactly constant to standardize the workload","It should be reduced because higher-intensity drills stress tissues more per contact","It should climb in proportion so total training stimulus keeps rising"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It should be reduced because higher-intensity drills stress tissues more per contact","explanation_en":"Higher intensity drills place more stress on tissues, so volume should be reduced as intensity rises.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練強度愈高(如從低箱跳進升級到深度跳),每次落地對組織的衝擊愈大,所以課總量必須隨強度上升而下調,不能維持不變。"},{"id":"q0702","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach wants to log the dose of a lower body plyometric session in the way it is conventionally quantified. What should be recorded?","options":["The peak heart rate reached across the drills","The cumulative time the working muscles spend under tension","The number of foot contacts completed during the session"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The number of foot contacts completed during the session","explanation_en":"Lower body plyometric volume is normally expressed as the number of foot contacts per workout.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"下肢增強式訓練的容量慣例以每次課的「腳步觸地次數」(foot contacts)記錄,不是心率或肌肉張力時間。"},{"id":"q0703","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach declines to program depth jumps and high-impact lower body drills for a group of prepubescent children. What is the primary physiological reason?","options":["Their epiphyseal growth plates have not yet closed, raising injury risk under high impact","They are developmentally incapable of following any movement instructions","Their muscles generate excessive force that the drills cannot safely absorb"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Their epiphyseal growth plates have not yet closed, raising injury risk under high impact","explanation_en":"Because the epiphyseal plates of prepubescent children have not closed, high-impact depth jumps are contraindicated.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"青春期前兒童的骨骺生長板(epiphyseal plates)尚未閉合,depth jump這類高衝擊動作可能傷及生長板,因此列為禁忌或需極度保守。"},{"id":"q0704","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach setting up depth jumps wants to start most athletes at the height cited as the typical norm rather than the extremes of the usable range. Which height is that norm?","options":["Roughly 6 to 12 inches, near the low end of the usable range","Roughly 30 to 32 inches","Roughly 48 to 60 inches, near the high end of the usable range"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Roughly 30 to 32 inches","explanation_en":"Depth jump heights range from 16 to 42 inches, with 30 to 32 inches cited as the norm.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"深度跳箱高可用範圍約16-42英寸,教科書以約30-32英寸為一般常態起點;6-12英寸太低、48-60英寸已接近上限。"},{"id":"q0705","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"While filming landings, a coach flags one athlete whose pattern most strongly predicts ACL and patellofemoral injury. Which observed fault is that?","options":["Landing with an active flat-foot contact","Knees tracking in line over the toes on contact","Inward collapse of the knees, a dynamic valgus pattern"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Inward collapse of the knees, a dynamic valgus pattern","explanation_en":"Inward movement of the knees, called dynamic valgus, is a significant risk factor for ACL tears and knee injuries.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"落地時膝蓋向內塌陷的動態外翻(dynamic valgus)是前十字韌帶(ACL)撕裂與髕股關節傷害的重要風險因子;膝對腳尖同線才是正確模式。"},{"id":"q0706","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach must choose where to run lower body plyometrics from several available spaces. Which option provides appropriate shock absorption?","options":["A grass field, a suspended floor, or a rubber mat","A poured concrete pad in the loading bay","Hardwood laid directly over a concrete slab"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A grass field, a suspended floor, or a rubber mat","explanation_en":"Surfaces with adequate shock absorption such as grass, suspended floors, or rubber mats are recommended; concrete and tile are not.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"下肢增強式訓練應選有緩衝吸收的地面:草地、懸空式地板或橡膠墊;直接倒在水泥地或磁磚上衝擊過大。"},{"id":"q0707","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"An athlete has both plyometrics and aerobic endurance work scheduled for one session. To protect power output, how should the coach order them?","options":["Aerobic work first so the muscles are thoroughly warmed before jumping","Plyometrics first, because preceding aerobic work can interfere with power production","Either order works equally well, so it can be left to preference"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Plyometrics first, because preceding aerobic work can interfere with power production","explanation_en":"Because aerobic exercise can have an interfering effect on power, plyometrics should be performed before aerobic endurance training.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練要排在有氧耐力之前:先做有氧會造成干擾效應,削弱跳躍所需的功率輸出。"},{"id":"q0708","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach is spacing an athlete's plyometric sessions across the week to allow adequate tissue recovery. What between-session interval is recommended?","options":["About 5 to 7 days between sessions","About 12 to 24 hours between sessions","About 48 to 72 hours between sessions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"About 48 to 72 hours between sessions","explanation_en":"Forty-eight to 72 hours between plyometric sessions is recommended to allow adequate recovery.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"兩次增強式訓練之間建議間隔約48-72小時,讓肌肉與結締組織充分恢復;12-24小時不足,5-7天又太稀疏。"},{"id":"q0709","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"To combine resistance and plyometric work efficiently in one session without doubling stress on the same muscles, how should a coach pair lower body plyometrics?","options":["With upper body resistance training that session","With lower body resistance training targeting the same muscles","With no resistance training, keeping plyometrics fully isolated"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"With upper body resistance training that session","explanation_en":"Guidelines suggest combining lower body resistance training with upper body plyometrics, and upper body resistance with lower body plyometrics.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同一次課的組合原則是交替部位:下肢增強式搭配上肢阻力訓練、上肢增強式搭配下肢阻力訓練,避免同一肌群承受雙重壓力。"},{"id":"q0710","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Using ground contact time, a coach classifies a drill as a fast SSC action rather than a slow one. What approximate contact-time threshold marks that boundary?","options":["About 2.5 seconds","About 0.25 seconds","About 1.0 second"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About 0.25 seconds","explanation_en":"Slow SSC actions exceed 0.25 s of ground contact while fast SSC actions are under 0.25 s.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"慢速SSC動作的地面接觸時間超過0.25秒,快速SSC動作低於約0.25秒,這個接觸時間就是快慢分界。"},{"id":"q0711","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"After months of progressive plyometric training, an athlete's motor units become more excitable partly because a protective proprioceptor has been blunted. Which structure is desensitized?","options":["The Pacinian corpuscle, dulling its pressure sensitivity","The muscle spindle, reducing its stretch sensitivity","The Golgi tendon organ, raising the tension threshold at which it inhibits"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The Golgi tendon organ, raising the tension threshold at which it inhibits","explanation_en":"Progressive plyometric training desensitizes the Golgi tendon organ, increasing the motor unit's excitability potential.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"長期漸進增強式訓練會讓高爾基腱器官(GTO)脫敏感,即抑制發放的張力閾值提高,從而解除對運動單元的剎車、提高其興奮潛力。"},{"id":"q0712","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach wants to raise the intensity of a lower body plyometric drill through the movement demand itself. Which modification accomplishes that?","options":["Adding a directional change that forces deceleration then redirected acceleration","Lowering the drop height the athlete works from","Switching from single-leg contacts to double-leg contacts"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Adding a directional change that forces deceleration then redirected acceleration","explanation_en":"Directional changes require deceleration and redirected acceleration, increasing the impulse and intensity of the drill.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在動作中加入變向:先煞停減速再朝新方向加速,衝量與組織負荷都增加,是提高下肢增強式動作強度的方式;降箱高或雙腿著地反而是降強度。"},{"id":"q0713","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"A coach programs medicine ball throws and slams for the upper body. In terms of movement classification, these drills are typically what?","options":["Aerobic, sustaining low output over an extended period","Ballistic, projecting or accelerating an implement through release","Isometric, holding tension without joint movement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Ballistic, projecting or accelerating an implement through release","explanation_en":"Plyometrics for the upper body like throws and slams are typically ballistic in nature.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"藥球投擲、重摔等上肢增強式練習屬於彈道式(ballistic)動作:通過釋放/投射器械把動作加速出去,不是等長或有氧型。"},{"id":"q0714","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Two athletes perform the same drop jump from the same box onto the same surface. Which factor raises the relative intensity experienced by one of them?","options":["Dropping from a shorter box height","Having a higher strength-to-body-weight ratio","Having greater body mass, which increases load on muscles, connective tissue, and joints"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Having greater body mass, which increases load on muscles, connective tissue, and joints","explanation_en":"Greater body weight places more stress on muscles, connective tissues, and joints, raising drill intensity.","tags":["Chapter 19 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Plyometric Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同箱高、同地面的深度跳,體重較大者對肌肉、結締組織與關節的負荷更高,相對強度就比較大;肌力體重比高者反而是保護因素。"},{"id":"q0715","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"An athlete posts an excellent preplanned cone-drill time but repeatedly misreads defenders and cuts late in games. Using the standard definition, what does agility add that this athlete may be lacking?","options":["A higher maximal sprint speed, since agility is essentially top-end velocity","A faster preplanned movement pattern, since agility is the rehearsed version of change of direction","A perceptual-cognitive response to a stimulus layered on top of change-of-direction ability"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A perceptual-cognitive response to a stimulus layered on top of change-of-direction ability","explanation_en":"Agility requires perceptual-cognitive ability in combination with change-of-direction ability, responding to a stimulus.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"敏捷(agility)的標準定義是在變向能力之上再加「對刺激的知覺-認知反應」;預設路線的繞樁測驗只測變向,測不到判讀與決策。"},{"id":"q0716","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"An athlete has an excellent one-rep max but is beaten off the line because most of his sport actions last only a fraction of the time needed to reach that peak force. Which quality is more relevant to those brief actions?","options":["Rate of force development, how quickly force can be produced","Maximal isometric strength, the peak force he can eventually reach","Aerobic capacity, his ability to sustain output over time"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Rate of force development, how quickly force can be produced","explanation_en":"Maximal force takes at least 300 ms to develop, but sport actions are far shorter, so RFD is the more useful measure.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"達到最大肌力至少需要約300毫秒,而專項動作時間遠短於此,所以發力速率(RFD,多快能產生力量)比最終能達到的峰值力量更相關。"},{"id":"q0717","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach wants the mechanical quantity that determines how much an athlete's momentum changes during a ground contact. Which description matches it?","options":["Force divided by the time over which it acts","The product of force and the time it is applied, seen as the area under the force-time curve","Mass divided by acceleration during the contact"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The product of force and the time it is applied, seen as the area under the force-time curve","explanation_en":"Impulse is force multiplied by time, represented as the area under the force-time curve, and it dictates change in momentum.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"衝量(impulse)=作用力×作用時間,即力-時間曲線下的面積,它決定動量的改變數,不是力除以時間。"},{"id":"q0718","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach is sorting sprint variables into vectors and scalars for a lecture. Which of these is a scalar, carrying magnitude but no direction?","options":["Force, the push or pull applied against the ground","Velocity, how fast and in which direction the athlete moves","Speed, simply how fast the athlete moves"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Speed, simply how fast the athlete moves","explanation_en":"Speed is a scalar describing only how fast an object moves; velocity and force are vectors with direction.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"速率(speed)是純數量(scale),只有大小沒有方向;速度(velocity)與力(force)都是向量,必須帶方向。"},{"id":"q0719","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach wants to break sprint speed into the two variables whose interaction produces it, so each can be trained. Which pair is correct?","options":["Step length and step frequency","Stride width and arm-swing amplitude","Ground contact time and body mass"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Step length and step frequency","explanation_en":"Sprint speed is determined by the interaction of step length and step frequency.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"衝刺速度由步長(step length)與步頻(step frequency)兩者的互動作用決定,訓練也必須分別針對這兩個變數。"},{"id":"q0720","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Comparing an elite and a novice sprinter at top speed, force-plate data show the key difference. What most distinguishes the elite sprinter?","options":["Markedly faster repositioning of the swing leg between steps","Greater vertical force applied to the ground within a shorter ground contact","Longer ground contact times that allow more force to accumulate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Greater vertical force applied to the ground within a shorter ground contact","explanation_en":"Elite sprinters apply greater vertical force in a shorter ground contact; their swing-leg repositioning times are similar to slower sprinters.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"測力板研究顯示:菁英衝刺者在更短的地面接觸時間內施加更大的垂直方向力量;擺動腿的重擺時間快慢選手之間其實差異不大。"},{"id":"q0721","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"In the spring-mass model of sprinting, how is the stance leg represented as it goes from contact to push-off?","options":["As a purely passive shock absorber that only dampens impact","As a rigid lever that transmits force without deforming","As a spring that compresses at contact and rebounds at push-off"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"As a spring that compresses at contact and rebounds at push-off","explanation_en":"The spring-mass model depicts the leg as a spring that compresses during midstance and returns energy at push-off.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"彈簧-質量模型(spring-mass model)把支撐腿視為彈簧:著地到支撐中期壓縮儲能,蹬離時回彈釋放能量,不是剛性槓桿或純避震器。"},{"id":"q0722","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"An athlete plants and cuts through an angle sharper than about 45 degrees, requiring heavy braking. How is that action generally categorized?","options":["A slower SSC action with longer ground contact due to greater braking demand","An action with no meaningful SSC involvement","A fast SSC action with very brief ground contact"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A slower SSC action with longer ground contact due to greater braking demand","explanation_en":"COD over 45 degrees generally involves slower SSC actions with longer ground contact due to greater braking demands.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"超過約45度的大角度變向需要強力煞停,地面接觸時間拉長,一般歸類為慢速SSC動作,而非快速SSC。"},{"id":"q0723","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Because arresting momentum is central to sharp cuts, which muscle-action capacity should a coach prioritize when training change of direction and agility?","options":["Slow concentric-only actions performed under control","High-velocity, high-force eccentric muscle actions for braking","Isometric holds performed at fixed joint angles"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"High-velocity, high-force eccentric muscle actions for braking","explanation_en":"Effective braking requires high-velocity and high-force eccentric muscle actions, which recruit different pathways than concentric work.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"急變向的核心是「煞停動量」,所以訓練應優先發展高速、高力的離心收縮能力;離心與向心動作招募的神經路徑不同,不能只練向心。"},{"id":"q0724","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"During a cut, one step does the decisive work of turning the athlete. What is the main function of that plant step?","options":["To passively recover the swing leg before the next stride","To attain the athlete's maximal sprint velocity","To deflect the center of mass, transitioning from deceleration into reacceleration"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"To deflect the center of mass, transitioning from deceleration into reacceleration","explanation_en":"The plant phase is the main step that achieves deflection of the center of mass between deceleration and reacceleration.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"變向中決定性的跨步(plant step)的功能是偏轉重心(center of mass),完成從減速到再加速的轉換,不是被動恢復擺腿。"},{"id":"q0725","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach cues an athlete on posture to improve cutting. Which combination of trunk and body-position cues is recommended?","options":["Lower the center of mass and keep trunk motion controlled","Lean the trunk forward aggressively while decelerating into the plant","Raise the center of mass to lengthen the stride into the cut"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Lower the center of mass and keep trunk motion controlled","explanation_en":"A lower center of mass increases stability, and controlling trunk motion during deceleration improves COD performance.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"變向姿勢建議:降低重心以提高穩定度,並在減速階段控制軀幹動作;前傾過度或把重心抬高都不利。"},{"id":"q0726","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach argues that the Illinois agility run and L-run measure maneuverability rather than sharp change of direction. What is the basis for that claim?","options":["They include a reactive stimulus the athlete must respond to","They require rounding objects to preserve velocity rather than aggressively decelerating and repushing","They are too brief to impose any metabolic demand"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"They require rounding objects to preserve velocity rather than aggressively decelerating and repushing","explanation_en":"These longer tests require bending around objects to maintain velocity and impose higher metabolic demand, characteristic of maneuverability.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Illinois測驗與L-run要求繞過物體、以轉彎維持速度,代謝需求也較高,特性上更接近「操縱性機動」,不是激烈的煞停-再推進式變向。"},{"id":"q0727","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Two athletes post identical 5-0-5 times, but one is a much faster linear sprinter. To isolate true turning ability and fairly compare them, what should a coach calculate?","options":["Each athlete's VO2max to gauge aerobic contribution","Each athlete's vertical jump height as a power proxy","The COD deficit, subtracting the 10 m linear sprint time from the 5-0-5 time"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The COD deficit, subtracting the 10 m linear sprint time from the 5-0-5 time","explanation_en":"The COD deficit subtracts the 10 m linear sprint time from the 5-0-5 time to isolate change-of-direction ability.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"變向虧損(COD deficit)=5-0-5時間減10米直線衝刺時間,把直線速度成分剔除後才能真正比較兩人的純變向能力。"},{"id":"q0728","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach adds sled load for resisted sprints but wants to preserve sprinting mechanics. Roughly how much velocity reduction should the load generally not exceed?","options":["About 10 percent","About 50 percent","About 75 percent"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"About 10 percent","explanation_en":"Loads are typically chosen to keep velocity decrements modest, around 10 to 12 percent, to preserve sprinting biomechanics.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"阻力衝刺加負載時,速度降幅一般控制在約10-12%以內,才能在不破壞衝刺生物力學的前提下增加阻力。"},{"id":"q0729","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach is considering assisted overspeed sprinting to raise an athlete's top speed. Which is a recognized drawback of the method?","options":["It reliably produces faster ground contacts and cleaner mechanics","It can rush the stance phase, reduce muscle activation and propulsive force, and cause faulty technique","It is strongly and extensively supported by the research base"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It can rush the stance phase, reduce muscle activation and propulsive force, and cause faulty technique","explanation_en":"Assisted sprinting can prematurely rush the stance phase, decrease muscle activation and propulsive force, and produce chop steps; little research supports it.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"下坡/牽引式超速衝刺的已知缺點:支撐階段被強制縮短、肌肉啟用與推進力下降、容易出現碎步與錯誤技術,且研究支援有限。"},{"id":"q0730","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A coach reports that an athlete ran 9 m/s heading due north; a teammate ran 9 m/s but was constantly changing heading. Velocity differs from speed by adding which property that separates these cases?","options":["Temperature of the environment","Mass of the moving athlete","Direction of the motion"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Direction of the motion","explanation_en":"Velocity is speed with a direction, making it a vector quantity.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"速度(velocity)是速率加上方向,屬向量;同樣9 m/s但方向不斷改變,速度就在不斷改變,而速率可以不變。"},{"id":"q0731","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"This chapter's framework declines to use power as the primary training target and prefers its underlying variables. What is the reasoning?","options":["Power is a derived construct, so measuring its underlying characteristics, force and velocity, is more practically useful","Power bears no meaningful relationship to sprinting performance","Power cannot be measured with available equipment"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Power is a derived construct, so measuring its underlying characteristics, force and velocity, is more practically useful","explanation_en":"Power is a derived mechanical construct, so measuring its underlying characteristics, force and velocity, gives more practical insight.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"本章不把功率當作首要訓練目標,因為功率是衍生的力學構念(P=F×v);直接測量並訓練其底層變數——力與速度——更實用。"},{"id":"q0732","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Watching a sprint from the start to top speed, a coach notes how trunk posture evolves. Which description is correct?","options":["The athlete leans backward to brake as speed increases","Forward lean is greatest early in acceleration and gradually becomes upright by maximum velocity","The trunk is fully upright from the very first step onward"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Forward lean is greatest early in acceleration and gradually becomes upright by maximum velocity","explanation_en":"Acceleration begins with forward inclination that gradually reduces to an upright posture by maximum velocity.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"軀幹姿勢:加速初期前傾角度最大,隨速度提升前傾逐漸減少,達到最大速度時軀幹轉為接近直立的姿勢。"},{"id":"q0733","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"A basketball athlete improves T-test times over an offseason. Which anthropometric change is regarded as a predictor of that improved change-of-direction performance?","options":["Greater limb length providing longer levers","Increased body fat adding overall mass to push against the ground","Increased muscle mass combined with decreased body fat, improving functional mass"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increased muscle mass combined with decreased body fat, improving functional mass","explanation_en":"Improving functional mass through more muscle and less fat predicts better COD performance, as in T-test results for basketball players.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"增加肌肉量同時降低體脂、改善功能性體重(functional mass),被證實是T-test等變向表現進步的人體測量學預測因子。"},{"id":"q0734","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"An athlete jams a stiff, extended leg into the ground when cutting and struggles to absorb the load. Which lower-limb cue should the coach teach to tolerate braking forces?","options":["Use triple flexion at the hip, knee, and ankle to dissipate eccentric loads","Keep the knees locked on contact to create a firm base","Maintain a stiff-legged braking style to transmit force quickly"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Use triple flexion at the hip, knee, and ankle to dissipate eccentric loads","explanation_en":"Athletes should use triple flexion at the hip, knee, and ankle to dissipate eccentric braking loads and avoid a stiff-legged style.","tags":["Chapter 20 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Speed and Agility Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"落地與煞停應採用髖、膝、踝三重屈曲(triple flexion)來消散離心負荷;直腿「戳地」無法吸收制動力,還增加受傷風險。"},{"id":"q0735","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach is drafting an aerobic endurance program from scratch and wants to set the variables in the sequence the program design process prescribes. Which order should be followed?","options":["Choose the exercise mode first, then frequency, then intensity, then duration, then plan progression","Choose frequency first, then mode, then duration, then intensity, then plan progression","Choose intensity first, then duration, then frequency, then mode, then plan progression"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Choose the exercise mode first, then frequency, then intensity, then duration, then plan progression","explanation_en":"The program design steps are (1) exercise mode, (2) frequency, (3) intensity, (4) duration, and (5) progression, in that order.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力程式設計的法定順序:(1)運動方式(mode)(2)頻率(frequency)(3)強度(intensity)(4)時間(duration)(5)漸進(progression)。"},{"id":"q0736","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Two distance runners share nearly identical VO2max values, yet one consistently outperforms the other in long races. Which profile most likely explains the better performer's advantage?","options":["A greater proportion of type IIx fibers and a higher glycolytic capacity","A higher lactate threshold, better exercise economy, and a greater proportion of type I fibers","A larger muscle cross-sectional area combined with greater anaerobic power output"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A higher lactate threshold, better exercise economy, and a greater proportion of type I fibers","explanation_en":"When VO2max is matched, a high lactate threshold, good exercise economy, high fat utilization, and a high percentage of type I fibers become decisive for endurance performance.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"VO2max相近時,表現差異由乳酸閾值較高、動作經濟性(economy)較好、第一類(慢縮)肌纖維比例較高等決定;最大攝氧量本身不是唯一決定因素。"},{"id":"q0737","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"During an incremental treadmill test, a technician notes the running speed at which blood lactate first climbs meaningfully above the athlete's resting concentration. Which variable has been identified?","options":["The maximum heart rate the athlete can hold for one hour","The speed at which the athlete reaches VO2max","The lactate threshold"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The lactate threshold","explanation_en":"The lactate threshold is the running speed (or percentage of VO2max) at which blood lactate begins rising above resting levels.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"遞增負荷測試中,血乳酸剛開始明顯高於靜息濃度時對應的速度(或%VO2max),定義上就是乳酸閾值(lactate threshold)。"},{"id":"q0738","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A cyclist rides at the highest steady power output she can sustain while her blood lactate stays elevated but stable rather than continuing to climb. This intensity is best labeled as:","options":["The intensity where maximal lactate production is matched by maximal lactate clearance","The intensity where blood lactate first rises above zero","The point where lactate production outpaces clearance and rises until failure"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The intensity where maximal lactate production is matched by maximal lactate clearance","explanation_en":"Maximal lactate steady state is the intensity at which maximal lactate production equals maximal clearance; it is synonymous with critical power and critical speed.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大乳酸穩態(MLSS)=乳酸最大生成速率等於最大清除速率的最高強度,血乳酸高但穩定;它與臨界功率/臨界速度同義。"},{"id":"q0739","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Two runners hold the exact same pace, but one consumes less oxygen and expends less energy to do so. That runner is said to have superior:","options":["Maximal aerobic capacity","Exercise economy","Lactate tolerance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Exercise economy","explanation_en":"Exercise economy is the energy cost of holding a given velocity; better economy means less energy expended to maintain the same pace.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"動作經濟性(exercise economy)指維持給定速度所需的能量成本;同樣配速耗氧與耗能較少,就是經濟性較佳,與最大攝氧量能力不同。"},{"id":"q0740","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach increases the intensity of an athlete's aerobic sessions and must adjust duration accordingly. What is the expected relationship between the two?","options":["They are set independently, so duration need not change","Raising intensity allows a longer sustainable duration","Raising intensity requires a shorter duration"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Raising intensity requires a shorter duration","explanation_en":"Intensity and duration are inversely related; higher-intensity work must be shorter, while lower-intensity work can be sustained longer.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"強度與時間呈反向關係:提高強度就必須縮短可持續的時間;降低強度才能拉長持續時間,兩者不能各自獨立設定。"},{"id":"q0741","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Using the age-predicted maximal heart rate formula (Fox), what maximal heart rate would a coach estimate for a 30-year-old athlete?","options":["190 beats per minute","160 beats per minute","220 beats per minute"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"190 beats per minute","explanation_en":"Age-predicted maximal heart rate equals 220 minus age, so 220 minus 30 gives 190 beats per minute.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Fox年齡預測公式:最大心率=220減年齡,30歲即220-30=190次/分。"},{"id":"q0742","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach wants a target heart rate that accounts for the athlete's resting heart rate, computing it as heart rate reserve multiplied by the desired intensity and then adding resting heart rate. Which method is this?","options":["The percentage of maximal heart rate method","The Karvonen (heart rate reserve) method","The metabolic equivalent (MET) method"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The Karvonen (heart rate reserve) method","explanation_en":"The Karvonen method uses heart rate reserve: target HR equals (HRR times intensity) plus resting HR.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Karvonen法(心率儲備法):目標心率=心率儲備(HRR=(最大心率-靜息心率))×目標強度+靜息心率,把靜息心率計入,比單純%HRmax更貼近實際生理需求。"},{"id":"q0743","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"An athlete performs a two-hour run held below 65 percent of VO2max to build an aerobic base. Which category of aerobic training does this session represent?","options":["Interval training performed near VO2max","High-intensity interval training","Long slow distance (extensive endurance) training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Long slow distance (extensive endurance) training","explanation_en":"Long slow distance (extensive endurance) training is the longest-duration, lowest-intensity work, typically performed below about 65 percent of VO2max.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"低於65% VO2max、持續兩小時這類最長、最低強度的課屬於長慢距離(long slow distance,extensive endurance)訓練,用於建立有氧基礎。"},{"id":"q0744","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A distance coach prescribes sustained efforts at an intensity right at the athlete's threshold, which is why the workout is sometimes called threshold training. This corresponds most closely to which physiological marker?","options":["An intensity at or slightly above the maximal lactate steady state","An intensity above VO2max","An intensity well below the lactate threshold"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"An intensity at or slightly above the maximal lactate steady state","explanation_en":"Pace/tempo (threshold) training is performed at or slightly above the maximal lactate steady state, which is why it is also called threshold training.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"配速/節奏(閾值)訓練的定義強度就是落在最大乳酸穩態(MLSS)或其略上方,這正是它被稱為閾值訓練的原因。"},{"id":"q0745","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach programs VO2max interval work using 4-minute work bouts and needs to set the rest interval. For traditional interval training in this bout range, what work-to-rest ratio is recommended?","options":["1:3","1:1","1:5"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1:1","explanation_en":"For 3- to 5-minute interval work bouts, rest should roughly equal the work interval, yielding a 1:1 work-to-rest ratio.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統間歇訓練:工作段為3-5分鐘(如VO2max間歇)時,休息時間約等於工作時間,即1:1的工作休息比;1:3留給更長的負荷段考量。"},{"id":"q0746","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"An athlete performs an extremely intense cycling protocol of repeated all-out bouts, each followed by a rest interval half as long as the work bout, reaching exhaustion in roughly 7 to 8 repetitions. Which structure matches the classic Tabata protocol?","options":["60 seconds of work followed by 60 seconds of rest","3 minutes of work followed by 1 minute of rest","20 seconds of work followed by 10 seconds of rest"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"20 seconds of work followed by 10 seconds of rest","explanation_en":"The classic Tabata protocol uses very high intensity with 20 seconds of work and 10 seconds of rest, reaching exhaustion in about 7 to 8 repetitions.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Tabata協議:極高強度下20秒工/10秒息(2:1),約7-8個重複即達力竭;60/60或180/60都不符其經典結構。"},{"id":"q0747","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"During one continuous run, an athlete freely mixes easy jogging, sustained threshold-pace segments, and short fast surges based on feel. This unstructured blending of intensities within a single session is called:","options":["Fartlek training","Pace/tempo training","Long slow distance (extensive endurance) training"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Fartlek training","explanation_en":"Fartlek, Swedish for speed play, combines long slow distance, pace/tempo, and interval-style efforts within a single workout.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"法特萊克(fartlek,瑞典語「速度遊戲」):在同一次連續跑步中自由混合長慢跑、閾值段與短快衝,是不固定結構的強度混合訓練。"},{"id":"q0748","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach wants to advance an endurance athlete safely without provoking overtraining or injury. What is the general guideline for progressing frequency, intensity, or duration?","options":["Double the training load each week","Increase only one variable at a time by no more than about 10 percent per week","Increase by at least 25 percent per week to force adaptation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Increase only one variable at a time by no more than about 10 percent per week","explanation_en":"To limit overtraining and injury risk, increase frequency, intensity, or duration by no more than about 10 percent per week, and only one variable at a time.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"漸進的安全準則:一次只動一個變數(頻率、強度或時間),且每週增幅不超過約10%,以壓低過度訓練與傷害風險。"},{"id":"q0749","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"An endurance athlete is months away from her key race and spends this block on long, low-intensity volume. What is the primary objective of this off-season (base) training?","options":["Maximize race-pace speed work","Peak specifically for the most important competition","Develop a large base of cardiorespiratory conditioning"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Develop a large base of cardiorespiratory conditioning","explanation_en":"Off-season base training builds a large cardiorespiratory base primarily through long-duration, low-intensity work.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"休賽季(base)期以長時間、低強度為主,首要目標是建立龐大的心肺適能基礎,為之後的專項強度期鋪底,不是練比賽配速或巔峰。"},{"id":"q0750","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A runner recovering from a repetitive-stress issue substitutes cycling and swimming for some running mileage. What is the primary rationale for this cross-training?","options":["To maintain general conditioning while reducing overuse injury risk during reduced running or injury","To permanently replace all sport-specific training year-round","To maximize race-specific performance adaptations"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"To maintain general conditioning while reducing overuse injury risk during reduced running or injury","explanation_en":"Cross-training maintains general conditioning and distributes stress to different muscle groups, lowering overuse injury risk.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"交叉訓練(cross-training)的主要理由:跑量受限或有傷時,用騎車、游泳維持一般適能,同時把壓力分散到不同肌群,降低過度使用傷害風險。"},{"id":"q0751","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"An athlete stops training for several weeks due to a scheduling conflict and returns noticeably less fit. This decline is best described as:","options":["Retention of adaptations regardless of the layoff","Detraining, the progressive loss of training-induced physiological adaptations","Continued improvement occurring without any training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Detraining, the progressive loss of training-induced physiological adaptations","explanation_en":"Detraining is the progressive loss of training-induced physiological adaptations when training is reduced or stopped.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"停訓數週後適能明顯倒退,這是去訓練化(detraining):訓練所建立的生理適應會逐漸流失,不是「適應永久保留」。"},{"id":"q0752","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Ahead of a championship, a coach cuts an athlete's training volume roughly in half in one move and then holds that reduced volume steady through the final days. Which tapering strategy is this?","options":["An increase in training volume immediately before competition","A gradual, linear reduction in daily training volume","A step taper: an abrupt, substantial volume reduction held constant thereafter"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A step taper: an abrupt, substantial volume reduction held constant thereafter","explanation_en":"A step taper is an abrupt, considerable reduction in volume (often at least 50 percent) that is then maintained without fluctuation throughout the taper.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"階梯式減量(step taper):一次性驟降大量訓練量(常至少50%),之後維持固定不再波動;既不是逐日線性遞減,也不是賽期增訓。"},{"id":"q0753","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"A coach wants an athlete to gain the hematological benefits of altitude while keeping training quality high. Which arrangement correctly describes the live high, train low approach?","options":["Live at moderate altitude for acclimatization but train at or near sea level","Live at sea level but travel up to train at high altitude","Both live and train at extreme altitude"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Live at moderate altitude for acclimatization but train at or near sea level","explanation_en":"Live high, train low has athletes living at moderate altitude (about 2,000 to 3,000 m) for acclimatization while training near sea level to preserve training quality.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"「高海拔居住、低海拔訓練」(live high, train low)指住在約2,000-3,000米中等海拔取得血液適應,訓練則下到海平面附近進行,以維持訓練強度與品質。"},{"id":"q0754","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"After several weeks of a heat acclimation protocol, which physiological change would a coach expect to observe in the athlete?","options":["A reduced plasma volume","Sweating that begins at a lower core temperature","A delayed onset and reduced overall sweat rate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Sweating that begins at a lower core temperature","explanation_en":"Heat acclimation increases plasma volume and sweat rate and shifts the onset of sweating earlier, to a lower core temperature.","tags":["Chapter 21 quiz: Program Design and Technique for Aerobic Endurance Training"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱適應數週後的典型生理變化:出汗在較低的深層體溫就提前啟動,同時血漿量增加、整體排汗率上升,而不是減少。"},{"id":"q0755","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A strength coach maps out a full year of training blocks and separately decides the exact exercises, methods, and loads inside each block. Which statement correctly distinguishes these two activities?","options":["They are identical terms and can be used interchangeably","Periodization is the macro-level scaffold, while programming is the micro-level management of modes, methods, and loads","Programming is the year-long overview, while periodization sets each day's sets and reps"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Periodization is the macro-level scaffold, while programming is the micro-level management of modes, methods, and loads","explanation_en":"Periodization is the macro-management scaffold of the training process; programming is the micro-management that defines the actual modes, methods, and loads.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"週期化(periodization)是全年訓練流程的宏觀骨架;程式設計(programming)是微觀管理,決定每個區塊內的實際方式、方法與負荷,兩者不是同義詞。"},{"id":"q0756","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Selye's model describes how an organism responds to a stressor across three sequential stages. Which set names those stages in order?","options":["Preparation, competition, transition","Hypertrophy, strength, power","Alarm, resistance, exhaustion"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Alarm, resistance, exhaustion","explanation_en":"The general adaptation syndrome consists of the alarm, resistance, and exhaustion stages.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Selye的一般適應綜合徵(GAS)三階段依序為:警覺期(alarm)、抵抗期(resistance)、衰竭期(exhaustion)。"},{"id":"q0757","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"An athlete begins a demanding new training block and reports heavy soreness and a temporary dip in performance in the first days. According to the general adaptation syndrome, which phase does this reflect?","options":["The alarm phase, in which performance generally decreases from fatigue and soreness","The resistance phase, in which performance rises above baseline","A steady state in which performance stays exactly at baseline"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The alarm phase, in which performance generally decreases from fatigue and soreness","explanation_en":"The alarm phase is marked by fatigue, soreness, and a reduced performance capacity in response to a novel or more intense stress.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新訓練塊初期出現嚴重痠痛與表現暫時下滑,是一般適應綜合徵的警覺期:面對新穎或更強的壓力,身體能力先下降,之後才可能回升超過基線。"},{"id":"q0758","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"An athlete is subjected to unrelenting high training and psychoemotional stress for too long and fails to adapt, showing signs of overtraining. Which general adaptation syndrome phase has been entered?","options":["A supercompensation phase","The exhaustion phase","The resistance phase"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The exhaustion phase","explanation_en":"Persistent excessive stress that exceeds the athlete's ability to adapt drives entry into the exhaustion phase, often reflecting overreaching or overtraining.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練壓力與心理情緒壓力持續超過適應能耐、長期無法恢復而出現過訓徵象,代表進入GAS的衰竭期,對應過度訓練或過度訓練症候群。"},{"id":"q0759","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Under the fitness-fatigue paradigm, a coach wants to estimate an athlete's readiness to perform on a given day. Preparedness is best modeled as:","options":["The fitness aftereffect only, with fatigue disregarded","The fatigue aftereffect only, with fitness disregarded","The summation of the fitness and fatigue aftereffects of training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The summation of the fitness and fatigue aftereffects of training","explanation_en":"Preparedness is the summation of the fitness and fatigue aftereffects produced by each training bout.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在健身-疲勞模型中,當日的備戰狀態(preparedness)=訓練產生的適能後效與疲勞後效兩者相加,只看其中一個都不完整。"},{"id":"q0760","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"As competition nears, a coach deliberately lowers training load and the athlete's readiness climbs. Which mechanism explains why reducing load tends to raise preparedness?","options":["Fatigue dissipates faster than fitness is lost","Both fatigue and fitness vanish instantly when load drops","Fitness is lost faster than fatigue clears"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Fatigue dissipates faster than fitness is lost","explanation_en":"Because fatigue dissipates faster than fitness, a planned load reduction lets preparedness rise as fatigue clears while most fitness is retained.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"疲勞消退的速度比適能流失快,所以賽前有計劃地降低負荷時,疲勞先散去、適能大多保留,淨備戰狀態因此上升。"},{"id":"q0761","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach outlines a season using the traditional (Stone and colleagues) periodization model and needs the four sequential periods in order. Which list is correct?","options":["Microcycle, mesocycle, macrocycle, annual plan","Preparatory, first transition, competitive, second transition","General, specific, peaking, maintenance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Preparatory, first transition, competitive, second transition","explanation_en":"The traditional model uses the preparatory, first transition, competitive, and second transition periods in that order.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統(Stone等)週期化模型的四期依序為:準備期、第一次過渡期、比賽期、第二次過渡期;micro/meso/macrocycle是另一套週期尺度,不是這四期。"},{"id":"q0762","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Within the traditional model, the longest period is itself split into two subphases. Which pair correctly names them?","options":["An alarm phase and a resistance phase","A peaking phase and a maintenance phase","A general preparatory phase and a specific preparatory phase"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A general preparatory phase and a specific preparatory phase","explanation_en":"The preparatory period is subdivided into a general preparatory phase and a specific preparatory phase.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"準備期是整個模型中最長的期間,再細分為一般準備階段(general preparatory)與專項準備階段(specific preparatory)。"},{"id":"q0763","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Early in the preparatory period, a coach prescribes higher-repetition sets at roughly 50 to 75 percent of 1RM to build work capacity and muscle mass. Which loading pattern describes this hypertrophy/strength-endurance phase?","options":["Low to moderate intensity with high volume","Very high intensity with very low volume","Maximal singles at peaking loads"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Low to moderate intensity with high volume","explanation_en":"The hypertrophy/strength-endurance phase uses low to moderate intensity (about 50 to 75 percent 1RM) and high volume to develop work capacity and muscle mass.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"肥大/肌耐力階段的負荷特性是低到中強度(約50-75%1RM)搭配高訓練量,用來建立工作能力與肌肉量;高低量留給峰值/功率階段。"},{"id":"q0764","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"As an athlete progresses from the preparatory period toward competition in the traditional model, how do training volume and intensity generally trend relative to each other?","options":["Volume rises while intensity falls","Volume falls while intensity rises","Volume and intensity both rise together"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Volume falls while intensity rises","explanation_en":"Training generally shifts from high-volume, low-intensity work toward lower-volume, higher-intensity work as competition approaches.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"朝比賽期推進時,訓練量下降、強度上升,從「高量低強度」移向「低量高強度」,這是傳統模型的典型走向。"},{"id":"q0765","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach is nesting shorter training cycles inside longer ones for a full annual plan. Of a microcycle, a mesocycle, and a macrocycle, which spans the longest period of time?","options":["The mesocycle","The microcycle","The macrocycle"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The macrocycle","explanation_en":"The macrocycle is the longest of the three (several months up to a year), with mesocycles and microcycles nested within it.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大週期(macrocycle)最長,數個月到一年,中週期(mesocycle)與小週期(microcycle)巢狀其內,時間尺度由大到小排列。"},{"id":"q0766","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach designs a mid-length training block and picks its most typical length. What is the usual range for a mesocycle, and what is its most common duration?","options":["Two to six weeks, most commonly four weeks","Several months, most commonly six months","Several days, most commonly a single day"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Two to six weeks, most commonly four weeks","explanation_en":"A mesocycle is a medium cycle of about two to six weeks, with four weeks being the most common duration.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"中週期(mesocycle)約2-6周,最常見為4周,是介於微週期與大週期之間的中型訓練區塊。"},{"id":"q0767","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach lays out the smallest recurring training cycle and uses its most typical length. How long does a microcycle most commonly last?","options":["About four weeks","About one week (roughly 7 days)","A single day"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"About one week (roughly 7 days)","explanation_en":"A microcycle ranges from several days up to two weeks, but its most common duration is one week.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"小週期(microcycle)範圍數天到兩週,最常見長度是1周;4周是中週期,單日則是訓練日單位。"},{"id":"q0768","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach plans a period that lasts a single day, may hold more than one training session, and is designed within the week-long cycle that contains it. Which unit is this?","options":["The macrocycle","The annual plan","The training day"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The training day","explanation_en":"A training day lasts one day, can contain multiple sessions, and is designed within the context of its microcycle.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練日(training day)就是一天,可含多節課,且必須在所屬小週期的架構內設計,是最小的規劃單位。"},{"id":"q0769","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"When mapping the sport season onto the traditional periodization model, the off-season conditioning block corresponds to which period?","options":["The preparatory period","The second transition period","The competitive period"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The preparatory period","explanation_en":"The off-season maps to the preparatory period, which focuses on building a conditioning base.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"賽季歷上的休賽季(off-season)對應傳統模型的準備期,重點在建立體適能基礎。"},{"id":"q0770","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"The competitive period of the traditional model, during which the year's scheduled contests take place, aligns with which part of the sport season?","options":["The off-season","The in-season","The postseason"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The in-season","explanation_en":"The competitive period is the in-season, which contains all of the year's scheduled contests.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傳統模型的比賽期就是學季/球季中的賽季(in-season),全年安排的正式比賽都落在這一期。"},{"id":"q0771","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"The period sitting between the end of the competitive season and the next preparatory period goes by which other name?","options":["The basic strength phase","The peaking period","The active rest (restoration) period"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The active rest (restoration) period","explanation_en":"The second transition period is also called the active rest or restoration period, bridging the competitive season and the next preparatory period.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"第二次過渡期位於賽季結束後與下一準備期之間,又稱主動休息(active rest)或恢復(restoration)期。"},{"id":"q0772","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A coach schedules the active rest block after the season and wants to avoid triggering detraining that would lengthen the next preparatory period. How long should this second transition generally last?","options":["No longer than about four weeks","At least three months","A full year"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"No longer than about four weeks","explanation_en":"Active rest should generally last no longer than about four weeks; a longer layoff causes detraining and requires a longer preparatory period to recover.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"主動休息期一般不宜超過約4周;放太久會觸發去訓練化,下一準備期就得花更長時間重建基礎。"},{"id":"q0773","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"A colleague calls the traditional model linear periodization. Why is that label considered technically inaccurate?","options":["Because the model never alters intensity at any point","Because it still varies intensity and volume-load at the micro- and mesocycle level, making it nonlinear","Because it applies one unchanging training load for the entire plan"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Because it still varies intensity and volume-load at the micro- and mesocycle level, making it nonlinear","explanation_en":"A core tenet of periodization is removing linearity; the traditional model varies intensity and volume-load within its micro- and mesocycles, so it is actually nonlinear.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"把傳統模型稱為「線性週期化」在技術上不準確:它在小週期與中週期內仍會變動強度與負荷量,本質仍是非線性的;週期化的核心就是消除線性。"},{"id":"q0774","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Within one week, an athlete performs a heavy strength day, a hypertrophy day, and a power day, rotating focus session to session. Which periodization approach does this exemplify, and how does it differ from the traditional model?","options":["It uses only one training session per month, unlike the traditional model","It holds load and focus identical every session, unlike the traditional model","It varies load, volume, and training focus within a single microcycle, rather than progressing gradually across mesocycles"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"It varies load, volume, and training focus within a single microcycle, rather than progressing gradually across mesocycles","explanation_en":"Daily undulating periodization makes large day-to-day fluctuations in load, volume, and focus within a microcycle, unlike the more gradual mesocycle progression of the traditional model.","tags":["Chapter 22 quiz: Periodization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"同周內輪流排大重量肌力日、肥大日、功率日,是每日波動週期化(DUP)的特徵:在單一小週期內做日間大幅波動,而非傳統模型跨中週期的漸進變化。"},{"id":"q0775","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A recovering athlete is cleared by the athletic trainer, who has run the daily rehab, but the coach wants to know whose sign-off is legally and professionally the final word before the athlete competes again. Who most often makes that determination?","options":["The athletic trainer, because they supervised the rehabilitation","The strength and conditioning professional, who oversees reconditioning","The team physician, even though they do not run daily rehabilitation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The team physician, even though they do not run daily rehabilitation","explanation_en":"The team physician (MD or DO) most often makes the final return-to-play decision, even though they are not responsible for daily rehabilitation.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"是否獲准重返比賽的最終決定權最常屬於隊醫(team physician,MD/DO),即使每日復健由運動防護員執行、體適能教練負責再訓練。"},{"id":"q0776","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"An athlete has anterior shoulder instability, and the athletic trainer directs the S and C coach to remove the barbell bench press from the program because that movement places the joint in a vulnerable position. In clinical terms, the bench press is best described for this athlete as a:","options":["Contraindication","Indication","Macrotrauma"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Contraindication","explanation_en":"A contraindication is an activity that is inadvisable or prohibited due to the given injury, such as bench pressing with anterior shoulder instability.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"禁忌症(contraindication)指因該傷害而不宜或禁止的活動;前肩關節不穩者做臥推會把關節置於危險位置,就是典型禁忌。"},{"id":"q0777","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"During a tackle an athlete's shoulder is forced so that the humeral head fully separates from the glenoid and stays out of position until reduced. When only the joint surfaces had partially separated and spontaneously returned, that lesser event would instead be called a subluxation. The complete-separation event is termed a:","options":["Sprain","Dislocation","Subluxation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Dislocation","explanation_en":"A dislocation is complete displacement of the joint surfaces, whereas a subluxation is only partial displacement.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"脫位(dislocation)是關節面完全分離且需手法復位;只是部分分離、自行回位的較輕狀況稱為半脫位(subluxation)。"},{"id":"q0778","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A distance runner who steadily raised weekly mileage without adding rest days develops a nagging injury from the repeated abnormal loading rather than any single traumatic event. This mechanism of injury is classified as:","options":["Macrotrauma","A third-degree sprain","Microtrauma (overuse)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Microtrauma (overuse)","explanation_en":"Microtrauma, or overuse injury, results from repeated abnormal stress, in contrast to macrotrauma which is a single sudden overload episode.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"沒有單一創傷事件、由重複異常負荷長期累積造成的傷害屬於微創傷/過度使用(microtrauma/overuse);單次突然超負荷才是巨創(macrotrauma)。"},{"id":"q0779","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"On a manual muscle test after a hamstring injury, the athlete can generate almost no force yet reports little to no pain, and imaging shows a complete tear of the muscle fibers. This grading of muscle activity is consistent with a:","options":["Third-degree strain","First-degree strain","Second-degree strain"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Third-degree strain","explanation_en":"A third-degree strain is a complete tear of the fibers producing very weak, painless muscle activity; first-degree is strong but painful and second-degree is weak and painful.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"三度拉傷=肌纖維完全斷裂:徒手肌力檢查幾乎測不到力量,但因運動單位已中斷反而較不痛;一度是強而痛、二度是弱而痛。"},{"id":"q0780","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A cross-country athlete who ramped up training volume too quickly develops localized, activity-related bone pain that imaging later confirms. This represents the most common overuse injury to bone, which is a:","options":["Avulsion fracture","Stress fracture","Contusion"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Stress fracture","explanation_en":"The most common overuse (microtrauma) injury to bone is a stress fracture, often from rapid increases in training volume.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"骨骼最常見的過度使用傷害是應力性骨折(stress fracture),典型成因正是訓練量(如跑量)增加太快、缺乏休息日。"},{"id":"q0781","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"An athlete has chronic Achilles pain, and imaging reveals disorganized collagen, tendon cell damage, and new vessel growth but little sign of active inflammation. This picture points to tendinopathy rather than tendinitis because tendinopathy is characterized by:","options":["Acute inflammation of the tendon","A complete tendon rupture","A degenerative condition with minimal inflammation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A degenerative condition with minimal inflammation","explanation_en":"Tendinopathy is a degenerative condition with minimal inflammation, tendon cell damage or death, and neovascularization, unlike inflammatory tendinitis.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"腱病變(tendinopathy)是退化性疾病:膠原紊亂、腱細胞損傷或死亡、新生血管形成,幾乎不見活動性發炎;發炎性的是腱炎(tendinitis),兩者處置不同。"},{"id":"q0782","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"An S and C coach planning progressive reconditioning wants to time loading to the biology of healing. Regardless of tissue type, which sequence correctly orders the phases the tissue moves through?","options":["Inflammatory response, then fibroblastic repair, then maturation-remodeling","Fibroblastic repair, then inflammatory response, then maturation-remodeling","Maturation-remodeling, then inflammatory response, then fibroblastic repair"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Inflammatory response, then fibroblastic repair, then maturation-remodeling","explanation_en":"All tissues heal in the same basic order: inflammation first, then fibroblastic repair, then maturation-remodeling.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"不論組織型別,癒合階段順序固定:發炎反應→纖維母細胞修復期(fibroblastic repair)→成熟-重塑期(maturation-remodeling),漸進負荷須配合這個時序。"},{"id":"q0783","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"An athlete sustains an acute ankle sprain on Monday morning. Assuming an intact blood supply and no unusual severity, roughly when should the initial inflammatory phase be resolving?","options":["By about two months after the injury","By about 72 hours after the injury","By about two weeks after the injury"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"By about 72 hours after the injury","explanation_en":"The inflammatory phase typically lasts about 72 hours, though it may last longer with compromised blood supply or more severe damage.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"發炎期通常在傷後約72小時內收尾(血液供應完好、傷勢不重的情況下);血供差或嚴重損傷才會延長。"},{"id":"q0784","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A few days into healing, a biopsy of the wound area shows freshly laid collagen that is disorganized and considerably weaker than the original tissue. This finding is characteristic of the fibroblastic repair phase, in which the collagen is primarily:","options":["Type I collagen, aligned along the lines of stress","Fully matured collagen at normal tensile strength","Type III collagen, randomly oriented and weak"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Type III collagen, randomly oriented and weak","explanation_en":"The repair phase produces type III collagen that is randomly deposited and weaker than the original tissue; alignment and strength come later in remodeling.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"纖維修復期新生的是第三型(type III)膠原,隨機排列、張力強度明顯低於原有組織;排列整齊、強度回升要到後期重塑階段。"},{"id":"q0785","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"As a healed tendon is progressively loaded during the final phase of tissue healing, what happens to its collagen fibers?","options":["They hypertrophy and realign along the lines of stress","They are broken down and removed by macrophages","They stay randomly oriented and transverse to the load"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"They hypertrophy and realign along the lines of stress","explanation_en":"With increased loading the collagen fibers hypertrophy and realign along the lines of stress, becoming stronger and allowing return to function.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"成熟-重塑期在漸進負荷刺激下,膠原纖維會肥大並沿應力方向重新排列,張力強度提升,組織才能恢復功能。"},{"id":"q0786","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A clinician managing a fresh soft-tissue injury wants the current acronym that updated the older PRICE model by adding an emphasis on controlled, graded loading rather than strict rest. Which approach is that?","options":["MICE","POLICE","RICE"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"POLICE","explanation_en":"Evidence has shifted to POLICE (Protection, Optimal Loading, Ice, Compression, Elevation), emphasizing optimal loading over pure rest.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"POLICE(保護、理想負荷Optimal Loading、冰敷、加壓、抬高)更新了RICE/PRICE:用「受控且漸進的負荷」取代絕對休息,是當前建議的急性軟組織傷害處理。"},{"id":"q0787","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"As an injury moves from the inflammatory phase into repair, growth factors that drive that transition are released from the injured area. Which cells release them?","options":["Histamine and bradykinin","Fibroblasts and osteoblasts","Macrophages and platelets"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Macrophages and platelets","explanation_en":"Macrophages and platelets within the injured area release growth factors that assist the transition to the fibroblastic repair phase.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"傷區內的巨噬細胞與血小板釋出生長因子,推動組織從發炎期過渡進入纖維修復期;組織胺與緩激肽是發炎期介質,不是這一步的生長因子來源。"},{"id":"q0788","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A coach chooses the back squat and the push-up during reconditioning specifically because in both movements the foot or hand is planted against the ground and cannot move freely. This shared feature classifies them as closed kinetic chain exercises, defined by a terminal (distal) segment that is:","options":["Fixed and meeting considerable resistance","Free to move against little resistance","Loaded only during the eccentric phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Fixed and meeting considerable resistance","explanation_en":"In a closed kinetic chain exercise (e.g., squat, push-up) the distal segment is fixed and meets resistance that restrains its free motion.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"閉鎖性動力鏈(closed kinetic chain)運動的定義是遠端節段固定且承受限制其自由移動的阻力,深蹲與伏地挺身(腳掌/手掌釘在地上)都是例子。"},{"id":"q0789","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A therapist wants to isolate the quadriceps at the knee with the foot free to swing through the movement, so she selects the seated leg (knee) extension. Based on the distal segment being free to move, this exercise is classified as:","options":["Purely isometric","Open kinetic chain","Closed kinetic chain"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Open kinetic chain","explanation_en":"The leg extension is an open kinetic chain exercise because the foot is free to move, allowing concentration on the quadriceps at the knee.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"坐姿腿伸展的遠端節段(腳)可自由移動,屬開放式動力鏈(open kinetic chain),因此能孤立股四頭肌在膝關節的動作。"},{"id":"q0790","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A clinician wants a resistance-training system that changes the working load from session to session according to how many repetitions the athlete completed, giving more individualization than the fixed DeLorme or Oxford schemes. Knight's DAPRE protocol fits because it:","options":["Always progresses from heavy loads down to light loads","Relies exclusively on isometric contractions","Adjusts intensity and volume on a daily basis according to performance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Adjusts intensity and volume on a daily basis according to performance","explanation_en":"DAPRE (daily adjustable progressive resistive exercise) adjusts resistance daily based on reps performed, allowing more individualization than DeLorme or Oxford.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"DAPRE(daily adjustable progressive resistive exercise)依據當日實際完成的次數,每天調整強度與容量,比固定處方的DeLorme或Oxford式更個人化,適合復健進階。"},{"id":"q0791","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"When screening an active population to predict who is most likely to get hurt in the coming season, which single factor is repeatedly cited as one of the most substantial predictors?","options":["Having sustained a previous injury","Possessing a high aerobic capacity","Demonstrating strong neuromuscular control"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Having sustained a previous injury","explanation_en":"Previous injury is repeatedly cited as one of the most substantial risk factors for future injury.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"篩選活躍族群未來一季受傷風險時,既往傷害史(previous injury)被反覆列為最實質的預測因子之一,比有氧能力或神經肌肉控制單項更具預測力。"},{"id":"q0792","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"After an unusually intense session in the heat, an athlete reports severe muscle pain and weakness, and their urine is dark and cola-colored from myoglobin. These signs point to which condition?","options":["Heat cramps","Rhabdomyolysis","Sickle cell trait crisis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rhabdomyolysis","explanation_en":"Rhabdomyolysis is the breakdown of skeletal muscle releasing myoglobin into the blood, producing myalgia, weakness, and myoglobinuria with risk to the kidneys.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"橫紋肌溶解症(rhabdomyolysis):骨骼肌細胞崩解、肌球蛋白釋入血液,表現為嚴重肌肉疼痛、無力與可樂色肌紅蛋白尿,有傷腎之虞;熱痵攣沒有肌紅蛋白尿。"},{"id":"q0793","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A lineman collapses in practice with a very high core temperature and altered mental status consistent with exertional heatstroke. Which management response is the recognized standard of care?","options":["Passive static stretching of the large muscle groups","Oral rehydration alone while the athlete keeps exercising lightly","Immediate whole-body cooling such as cold-water immersion while activating EMS"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Immediate whole-body cooling such as cold-water immersion while activating EMS","explanation_en":"Heatstroke is a medical emergency requiring immediate total body cooling (ice immersion), core temperature monitoring, and emergency medical services.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動性熱中暑(exertional heatstroke)是急症:標準處置是立即全身降溫(冰水浸泡最有效)、監測核心溫度,同時啟動緊急醫療系統(EMS),不能只靠口服補水或繼續輕運動。"},{"id":"q0794","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":23,"question":"An athletic trainer teaches staff to catch heat illness early rather than treating each presentation as an unrelated surprise. This reflects the fact that heat illnesses are best understood as:","options":["A continuum, with heatstroke typically preceded by cramps, syncope, and exhaustion","Isolated, unrelated events that give no warning signs beforehand","Conditions that arise almost exclusively in cold environments"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A continuum, with heatstroke typically preceded by cramps, syncope, and exhaustion","explanation_en":"Heat illnesses exist on a continuum of thermoregulatory dysregulation, so heatstroke is usually preceded by heat cramps, heat syncope, and heat exhaustion.","tags":["Chapter 23 quiz: Rehabilitation, Reconditioning, and Medical Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"熱疾病是體溫調節失調的連續譜:熱痵攣→熱暈厥→熱衰竭→熱中暑,熱中暑前通常已有前驅症狀,早期捕捉可以阻斷進展。"},{"id":"q0795","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"An athlete shows elevated cortisol and depressed testosterone on bloodwork but is still hitting personal records. A coach argues this proves overtraining syndrome. What is actually required before overtraining syndrome can be said to exist?","options":["A long-term (weeks to months) impairment in performance","Decreased testosterone together with increased cortisol","A run of poor results in competition"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A long-term (weeks to months) impairment in performance","explanation_en":"Performance impairment (long-term, weeks to months) is the necessary requirement for overtraining syndrome; hormonal changes indicate stress but are not required.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"診斷過度訓練症候群(OTS)的必要條件是長期(數週到數月)的表現受損;皮質醇升高、睪固酮下降只是壓力指標,單獨存在不足以成立OTS。"},{"id":"q0796","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A coach uses the terms overtraining and the overtraining syndrome interchangeably. Which statement correctly separates the process from its outcome?","options":["They are identical terms describing exactly the same phenomenon","Overtraining is the process; the overtraining syndrome is the resulting condition","The overtraining syndrome is the process; overtraining is the resulting condition"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Overtraining is the process; the overtraining syndrome is the resulting condition","explanation_en":"Overtraining is the process (excessive volume/intensity), and the overtraining syndrome is the result (symptoms plus performance impairment).","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過度訓練(overtraining)是「過程」:長期量或強度過量;過度訓練症候群(OTS)是這個過程造成的「結果」:症狀加表現衰退,兩者不可混用。"},{"id":"q0797","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"Two athletes both show a training-induced performance dip, but one is a milder case that resolves quickly while the other is a full-blown syndrome. Which statement captures how overreaching primarily differs from overtraining?","options":["Overreaching invariably leaves a permanent performance decrement","Overreaching typically requires hospitalization to resolve","Overreaching is less severe and recovery is faster"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Overreaching is less severe and recovery is faster","explanation_en":"Overreaching is a lesser form of stressful training; the condition is less severe and recovery is faster than with overtraining.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過度伸手(overreaching)與過度訓練的主要差別在嚴重程度與恢復速度:overreaching較輕,適當休息後較快恢復,不會像OTS那樣長期卡住。"},{"id":"q0798","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A coach deliberately overloads a sprinter for a planned block, accepts a short-term drop in performance, then tapers and sees the athlete rebound above the pre-block level. This planned outcome is which phenomenon?","options":["Functional overreaching, ending in supercompensation above baseline","Nonfunctional overreaching, requiring months to recover","Overtraining syndrome, which stalls performance at baseline"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Functional overreaching, ending in supercompensation above baseline","explanation_en":"Functional overreaching causes a short-term decrement but, with appropriate recovery, leads to supercompensation and improved performance.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有計劃地超練、接受短期表現下滑,減量休整後表現反彈超過原基線,這是功能性過度伸手(functional overreaching)帶來的超補償(supercompensation)。"},{"id":"q0799","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"After a heavy block an athlete recovers more slowly than expected and, when they finally return, their performance is no better than where they started. Compared with functional overreaching, this nonfunctional overreaching is distinguished by the fact that it:","options":["Resolves without needing any recovery period","Produces no supercompensation, returning only to baseline","Reliably pushes performance above the previous baseline"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Produces no supercompensation, returning only to baseline","explanation_en":"Nonfunctional overreaching involves greater fatigue and longer recovery with no supercompensation, so the athlete only returns to baseline.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"非功能性過度伸手(nonfunctional overreaching):疲勞更重、恢復更久,且沒有超補償——恢復後表現只回到基線,不會超過起點,這是它與功能性型的關鍵差別。"},{"id":"q0800","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"The overtraining framework borrows a stress model describing an alarm reaction, a resistance stage, and an adaptation or exhaustion stage. Which model, first proposed by Selye, is this?","options":["The size principle of motor unit recruitment","The Henneman recruitment gradient","The general adaptation syndrome (GAS)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The general adaptation syndrome (GAS)","explanation_en":"Selye's general adaptation syndrome (alarm, resistance, adaptation) is the foundational model applied to overtraining.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"Selye的一般適應綜合徵(GAS:警覺、抵抗、適應/衰竭)是被借用來解釋過度訓練的基礎壓力模型;大小原則與Henneman講的是運動單位招募順序。"},{"id":"q0801","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A strength-power athlete deep in high-intensity training shows an exaggerated catecholamine response to exercise and elevated resting sympathetic activity. This presentation is most consistent with which form of overtraining?","options":["Sympathetic OTS, marked by an increased epinephrine response","Sympathetic OTS, marked by a lowered resting heart rate","Parasympathetic OTS, marked by decreased cortisol"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Sympathetic OTS, marked by an increased epinephrine response","explanation_en":"Sympathetic OTS is marked by an increased epinephrine (catecholamine) response and is associated with high-intensity resistance/strength-power training.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"交感型OTS(sympathetic OTS)的特徵是運動中腎上腺素(兒茶酚胺)反應增大、靜息交感活性偏高,多與高強度阻力/肌力功率型訓練有關;靜息心率下降反而是副交感型的表現。"},{"id":"q0802","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"The parasympathetic form of overtraining, originally labeled the Addisonoid syndrome, tends to appear in a particular athlete type. Which athletes are most affected?","options":["Sprinters performing short bouts of high-intensity work","Aerobic endurance athletes accumulating very large training volumes","Powerlifters repeatedly handling near-maximal loads"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Aerobic endurance athletes accumulating very large training volumes","explanation_en":"Parasympathetic OTS, often accompanied by decreased cortisol, is most common in aerobic endurance athletes who use very large training volumes.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"副交感神經型過度訓練 (parasympathetic OTS，早期稱 Addisonoid 症候群) 最常出現在累積極大訓練量的有氧耐力運動員，常伴隨皮質醇下降；短跑或舉重類等短時高強度專案較少見。"},{"id":"q0803","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"In parasympathetic overtraining the sympathetic response to training becomes blunted, a state sometimes called adrenal exhaustion. What does that term specifically describe?","options":["The adrenal glands secreting excessive epinephrine","Overgrowth and enlargement of the adrenal cortex","The adrenal glands failing to produce adequate epinephrine"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The adrenal glands failing to produce adequate epinephrine","explanation_en":"Parasympathetic OTS shows a diminished sympathetic (epinephrine) response, termed adrenal exhaustion because the glands cannot produce adequate epinephrine.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"腎上腺耗竭 (adrenal exhaustion) 指腎上腺無法分泌足夠的腎上腺素 (epinephrine)，使交感神經對訓練的反應變鈍，這是副交感神經型過度訓練的特徵，不是分泌過多或腎上腺皮質肥大。"},{"id":"q0804","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"When evaluating an overtrained athlete, a coach maps out poor sleep, an inadequate diet, heavy travel, and job stress alongside the training itself. The cumulative wear and tear from all of these stressors together is called the:","options":["Allostatic load","Volume-load","Autonomic dysfunction index"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Allostatic load","explanation_en":"The allostatic load is the cumulative wear and tear from all stressors, including non-training factors like sleep, nutrition, travel, and job demands.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"累積壓力負荷 (allostatic load) 指訓練之外與之並存的所有壓力源——睡眠不良、飲食不足、頻繁出差、工作壓力——共同造成的累積損耗。"},{"id":"q0805","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"An athlete's performance drops, and the staff immediately assumes overtraining. Which statement about underperformance should temper that assumption?","options":["Underperformance and overtraining are effectively the same thing","Not all underperformance is due to overtraining or overreaching","All underperformance ultimately traces back to overtraining"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Not all underperformance is due to overtraining or overreaching","explanation_en":"Overtraining is only one cause of underperformance; many other factors, such as mistimed peaking, can impair performance without overtraining.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過度訓練只是表現下滑的原因之一； peaks 時機錯誤、生病、生活壓力等都會造成低表現，不能把表現不好直接等同於過度訓練或過度負荷 (overreaching)。"},{"id":"q0806","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"As an athlete begins to slide into overtraining in the weight room, the staff monitors several qualities to catch it early. Which physical performance generally deteriorates FIRST?","options":["Maximal strength","Maximal oxygen uptake capacity","Speed, such as sprinting and other high-velocity work"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Speed, such as sprinting and other high-velocity work","explanation_en":"When overtraining in the weight room, speed (sprinting) is most sensitive and decreases first, before power and well before maximal strength.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在weights房滑入過度訓練時，速度是最敏感的指標：衝刺與高速度動作的表現最先下降，其次才是功率 (power)，最大肌力最晚下滑。"},{"id":"q0807","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"In monitoring the same athlete for overtraining, which performance quality tends to hold up the longest and is one of the LAST to decline?","options":["Maximal strength","Sprinting speed","Vertical jump power"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Maximal strength","explanation_en":"Maximal strength is consistently one of the last performances to decline; strength is well-protected relative to speed and power.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"最大肌力最受保護，是速度、功率、最大肌力之中最慢退步的一項，因此不能只靠深蹲 1RM 判斷有無過度訓練。"},{"id":"q0808","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A coach wants to use cortisol and testosterone assays to confirm a diagnosis of overtraining syndrome. What do such hormonal variables actually indicate?","options":["The precise timeline required for recovery","The presence of stress, not overtraining specifically","A definitive, confirmatory diagnosis of overtraining"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The presence of stress, not overtraining specifically","explanation_en":"Hormonal variables indicate stress rather than overtraining specifically, so they are not by themselves diagnostic of OTS.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"皮質醇、睪固酮等荷爾蒙指標只能反映身體處於壓力狀態，不能單獨用來確診過度訓練症候群 (OTS)，也無法精確推算恢復所需時間。"},{"id":"q0809","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"An athlete diagnosed with overreaching (not the full syndrome) stops training to recover. Under favorable conditions, performance has been observed to return to original levels in as little as:","options":["Three months","One year","One week"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"One week","explanation_en":"With overreaching, training cessation has permitted performance to return to original levels in as little as one week.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過度負荷 (overreaching) 尚未發展成完整症候群，條件有利時停止訓練約一週即可讓表現回到原有水準，不需要數月或一年。"},{"id":"q0810","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"An athlete is confirmed to have overtraining syndrome. Before adding recovery modalities or lab testing, what is the first and most important step in the recovery process?","options":["Carefully revise the training program, cutting volume or intensity or ceasing training","Insert additional high-intensity sessions to push through the plateau","Order an extensive panel of blood biomarkers before changing anything"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Carefully revise the training program, cutting volume or intensity or ceasing training","explanation_en":"Recovery begins with a careful revision of the training program, typically a rapid decrease in volume, intensity, or training cessation.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"OTS 恢復的第一步是仔細修訂訓練計畫——快速下修訓練量或強度，甚至暫停訓練——之後才輪到其他恢復手段或實驗室檢測。"},{"id":"q0811","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A coach building a recovery plan wants to prioritize a strategy that carries strong supporting evidence rather than one whose evidence is weak. Which of these qualifies?","options":["Red-light therapy","Quality sleep","Acupuncture"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Quality sleep","explanation_en":"Quality sleep is rated as a strong-evidence recovery strategy, along with modifying the training program and the training taper.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"高品質睡眠在恢復策略中屬於強證據等級 (與調整訓練計畫、賽前減量 taper 同列)；紅光治療與針灸的證據較弱。"},{"id":"q0812","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A staff wants to set up an athlete-monitoring program that will actually let them adjust training in time. Which combination of qualities should the monitoring tests have?","options":["Expensive and intrusive, with slow but very detailed interpretation","Administered only once per season to establish a single benchmark","Valid, reliable, sensitive, and easy to administer with rapid turnaround"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Valid, reliable, sensitive, and easy to administer with rapid turnaround","explanation_en":"Monitoring tests must be valid, reliable, sensitive to the training stimulus, and easy to incorporate with rapid turnaround so the program can be adjusted.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"監控測驗必須具備效度 (valid)、信度 (reliable)、對訓練刺激敏感，且易於執行、結果快速可得，教練來得及據此調整計畫才有意義。"},{"id":"q0813","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A previously healthy endurance athlete shows overtraining-like symptoms, and screening also flags low energy availability. Why is relative energy deficiency in sport (RED-S), the successor concept to the female athlete triad, relevant to the overtraining picture?","options":["It shares many symptoms with OTS and the two can be interrelated","It is entirely unrelated to overtraining and can be ruled out","It affects only maximal strength and nothing else"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It shares many symptoms with OTS and the two can be interrelated","explanation_en":"RED-S shares many causes and symptoms with overtraining syndrome, and the two can be interrelated and contribute to each other.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"RED-S (運動相對能量不足，female athlete triad 的延續概念) 與 OTS 共享許多成因與症狀，兩者相關且會互相惡化，所以篩檢出低能量可用性時要一併處理。"},{"id":"q0814","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":24,"question":"A coach is writing progression rules to help avoid overtraining. Which guideline regarding training volume is recommended?","options":["Eliminate rest days entirely to maximize the training stimulus","Use caution with large volume jumps of more than about 30 percent","Push weekly volume up by at least 50 percent to force adaptation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Use caution with large volume jumps of more than about 30 percent","explanation_en":"Avoidance strategies include exercising caution with excessive volumes and large increases (greater than about 30 percent), while preserving critical rest days.","tags":["Chapter 24 quiz: Overreaching, Overtraining, and Recovery"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"預防過度訓練的進度原則：避免過大的單次訓練量增幅，超過約 30% 的跳增要特別謹慎，並保留必要的休息日。"},{"id":"q0815","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"A university hires you to help build a brand-new weight room from scratch. Before any blueprints are drawn or walls go up, you want to sequence the whole project correctly. Which ordering of the four project phases should guide the work?","options":["Design, predesign, construction, preoperation","Predesign, design, construction, preoperation","Predesign, construction, design, preoperation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Predesign, design, construction, preoperation","explanation_en":"The phases run predesign, design, construction, then preoperation, each with its own objectives.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"新建設施的四個階段依序為：預設計 (predesign)→設計 (design)→施工 (construction)→營運前準備 (preoperation)，每個階段各有目標，不可顛倒。"},{"id":"q0816","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"During early planning for a new facility, a consultant runs a SWOT analysis to confirm the investment will produce a sustainable financial return before committing funds. This SWOT work belongs to which predesign activity?","options":["The needs analysis","The master plan","The feasibility study"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The feasibility study","explanation_en":"The feasibility study uses a SWOT analysis to ensure the financial investment will yield a viable and sustainable return.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"可行性研究 (feasibility study) 屬於預設計階段，透過 SWOT 分析確認這筆投資能帶來可行且永續的財務回報，才投入資金。"},{"id":"q0817","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You expect a peak session of 18 athletes plus 2 coaches on the floor at once. Using the recommended per-person space allowance, what is the minimum floor area each individual should be allotted when planning capacity?","options":["100 square feet (9.3 m2)","144 square feet (13.4 m2)","70 square feet (6.5 m2)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"100 square feet (9.3 m2)","explanation_en":"The recommended minimum is 100 square feet (9.3 m2) per individual, including athletes, professionals, and any other staff present.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"空間規劃每人至少 100 平方英尺 (9.3 m²)，計算時包含在場的所有運動員與教練職員；144 平方英尺過於寬鬆，70 平方英尺不足。"},{"id":"q0818","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You are spacing out power racks and free-weight stations so a lifter and spotter can move safely and dumbbell users do not collide. What is the minimum clearance you should leave on each side of a rack and between free-weight sets?","options":["7 feet (2.1 m)","3 feet (0.9 m)","5 feet (1.5 m)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3 feet (0.9 m)","explanation_en":"Racks, barbells, and dumbbells need a minimum of 3 feet between equipment for safe movement of the athlete and spotter.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"深蹲架、槓鈴與啞鈴區的器材之間兩側至少預留 3 英尺 (0.9 m)，讓運動員與保護者能安全移動、互不碰撞。"},{"id":"q0819","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"When mapping out the main travel lanes that must keep exits clear and permit ADA wheelchair access, what width should you designate for those primary walkways?","options":["more than 10 feet (3 m)","2 to 3 feet (0.6-0.9 m)","5 to 7 feet (1.5-2.1 m)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"5 to 7 feet (1.5-2.1 m)","explanation_en":"Main walkways should be 5 to 7 feet wide to allow clear access to exits and ADA-required wheelchair access.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"主要通道寬度應為 5 至 7 英尺 (1.5–2.1 m)，才能保持通往緊急出口的動線並符合 ADA 輪椅通行要求。"},{"id":"q0820","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"Athletes at the new facility will perform box jumps, standing vertical jumps, and overhead weightlifting movements. What clear ceiling height should you specify so these actions have adequate overhead room?","options":["12 to 14 feet (3.7-4.3 m)","16 to 18 feet (4.9-5.5 m)","8 to 10 feet (2.4-3.0 m)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"12 to 14 feet (3.7-4.3 m)","explanation_en":"A height of 12 to 14 feet gives enough clearance for box jumps, vertical jumps, and overhead weightlifting exercises.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"箱式跳、原地垂直跳與過頭舉重動作需要 12 至 14 英尺 (3.7–4.3 m) 的淨高；8–10 英尺不夠，16–18 英尺非最低要求。"},{"id":"q0821","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You are setting the HVAC thermostat so training quality is not degraded by athletes overheating or getting chilled. Which climate-control range should you target for the training floor?","options":["58 to 64 F (14-18 C)","68 to 74 F (20-23 C)","78 to 84 F (26-29 C)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"68 to 74 F (20-23 C)","explanation_en":"A comfortable training temperature of roughly 68 to 74 F keeps athletes and staff comfortable so training quality is not affected.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"訓練區溫度應設定在 68–74°F (20–23°C)，讓運動員與職員保持舒適，避免過熱或受寒影響訓練品質。"},{"id":"q0822","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"To limit bacterial and microbial growth and keep steel equipment from rusting, you set a moisture ceiling for the training area. Relative humidity should be held at or below what level?","options":["80 percent","40 percent","60 percent"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"60 percent","explanation_en":"Relative humidity should stay at or below 60 percent to prevent bacterial and microbial growth and to protect equipment from rust.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"相對濕度應維持在 60% 以下，以抑制細菌與微生物滋生，並保護鋼製器材不生鏽。"},{"id":"q0823","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"To keep the training floor free of odors and stagnant air, you specify the ventilation rate. What is the recommended air-exchange rate, including the optimal target?","options":["8 to 10 times per hour, optimally 12 to 15","20 to 25 times per hour","2 to 4 times per hour"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"8 to 10 times per hour, optimally 12 to 15","explanation_en":"Air should be exchanged a minimum of 8 to 10 times per hour, optimally 12 to 15, to prevent odors and stagnant air.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"通風需每小時換氣至少 8–10 次，最佳為 12–15 次，才能避免異味與空氣停滯。"},{"id":"q0824","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You want music to energize the room but not drown out verbal coaching cues during lifts. Below what sound level should you cap the audio system?","options":["70 decibels","90 decibels","110 decibels"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"90 decibels","explanation_en":"Sound volume should be less than 90 decibels so athletes can hear instructions and coaching cues.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"音樂音量應控制在 90 分貝以下，確保運動員聽得見口頭指導與動作提示。"},{"id":"q0825","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You want the supervisor to be able to see everyone entering, exiting, and training at all times. Where should the supervision office be positioned in the layout?","options":["Just outside the facility entrance for privacy","In a back corner away from traffic to limit distraction","In a central location with a clear line of sight, possibly elevated"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"In a central location with a clear line of sight, possibly elevated","explanation_en":"The supervision office should be central with a clear line of sight, sometimes elevated, so the supervisor can see everyone entering and exiting.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"督導辦公室應設在視野清楚的中央位置，必要時抬高，讓督導者隨時掌握所有人進出與全場訓練狀況。"},{"id":"q0826","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"A proposed weight room sits on the second floor of a building, so it must tolerate heavy loaded equipment and dropped weights. What minimum load-bearing capacity should the floor be rated for?","options":["100 foot-pounds per square foot","200 foot-pounds per square foot","50 foot-pounds per square foot"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"100 foot-pounds per square foot","explanation_en":"A floor above ground level should support at least 100 foot-pounds per square foot to handle heavy and dropped equipment.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"位在地面以上樓層的舉重訓練區，樓板耐重至少須達 100 磅/平方英尺，以承受重型裝載器材與掉落的重量。"},{"id":"q0827","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You are mounting wall mirrors near a free-weight area where plates are set down and leaned against the wall. To keep rolling or dropped plates from shattering the glass, mirrors should start at least how far above the floor?","options":["12 inches (30 cm)","20 inches (51 cm)","30 inches (76 cm)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"20 inches (51 cm)","explanation_en":"Mirrors should be at least 20 inches off the floor so dropped or leaning weight plates do not roll into and break the glass.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"鏡面應從離地至少 20 英寸 (51 cm) 開始安裝，避免滾動或倚牆的槓片撞破玻璃。"},{"id":"q0828","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You are arranging a row of selectorized resistance machines and want a comfortable safety cushion for athletes moving between them. What clearance should you leave between machines, and what is the preferred spacing?","options":["48 inches (122 cm)","18 inches (46 cm)","30 inches (76 cm), with 36 inches (91 cm) preferred"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"30 inches (76 cm), with 36 inches (91 cm) preferred","explanation_en":"Machines should be at least 30 inches apart, preferably 36 inches, to provide a wide enough safety cushion.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"固定式器械之間至少保留 30 英寸 (76 cm) 間距，建議 36 英寸 (91 cm)，留出足夠的安全緩衝空間。"},{"id":"q0829","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"In a busy facility with athletes constantly moving between stations, you must choose between inlaid platforms and raised platforms for the lifting area. What is the primary safety reason to favor inlaid platforms?","options":["They sit flush with the floor and do not present a tripping hazard","They reduce the noise of dropped weights to zero","They are cheaper to install and maintain"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"They sit flush with the floor and do not present a tripping hazard","explanation_en":"Inlaid platforms sit flush with the surrounding floor, so they do not create the tripping hazard that raised platforms do.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"嵌入式平臺與周圍地面齊平，不會像架高平臺那樣構成絆倒風險——這是人多、走動頻繁的場館優先選嵌入式的主要安全理由。"},{"id":"q0830","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You want a single supervisor to maintain sight lines across the entire training floor. When positioning equipment of differing heights, where should the shorter pieces generally go?","options":["Along the perimeter walls","In the middle of the room","Inside the storage area"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"In the middle of the room","explanation_en":"Shorter equipment is best placed in the middle of the room so staff can see across the entire facility.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"較矮的器材應放在房間中央、較高的沿牆擺放，才不會遮擋視線，讓單一人員也能看顧全場。"},{"id":"q0831","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"A small satellite training room is too tight to include dedicated walkways separating the equipment. How should you arrange the equipment to keep transitions safe and emergency exits unobstructed?","options":["Clustered in the center of the room","Stacked against the emergency exit to save space","Bolted and secured around the perimeter with the center kept open"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Bolted and secured around the perimeter with the center kept open","explanation_en":"Equipment should be bolted around the perimeter with the center open for transitions and unimpeded access to emergency exits.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"小空間無法規劃專用通道時，器材應錨定固定在四周牆邊，中央保持開放，兼顧轉換動線與緊急出口暢通。"},{"id":"q0832","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"You need durable floor covering for the main lifting area that protects the subfloor, cushions dropped loads, and is easy to sanitize. Which flooring is regarded as the premier choice for this zone?","options":["Rubber flooring","Hardwood throughout","Carpet"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Rubber flooring","explanation_en":"Rubber flooring is the premier option because it protects the subfloor, provides durable cushioning, and is easy to clean.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"橡膠地板是主要舉重區的首選：保護下方地板、為掉落重量提供緩衝，且易於清潔消毒。"},{"id":"q0833","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"To limit the spread of skin infections, you set a cleaning schedule for mats, pads, and any surface that contacts athletes' skin. How often should these be wiped down with a germicidal cleaner?","options":["Once a month","Daily","Only when visibly soiled"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Daily","explanation_en":"Surfaces and pads that contact skin should be cleaned daily with a germicidal cleaner to limit the spread of infection.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"墊子、護墊及任何接觸皮膚的表面應每天用殺菌清潔劑擦拭，以減少皮膚感染傳播。"},{"id":"q0834","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":25,"question":"A cable machine breaks mid-session and the repair vendor cannot come for several days. To minimize liability, how should you handle the unit in the meantime?","options":["Discard it immediately without documentation","Leave it in place so athletes can work around it","Label it with an Out of Order sign, and move it to storage since repair is delayed"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Label it with an Out of Order sign, and move it to storage since repair is delayed","explanation_en":"Broken equipment should be tagged Out of Order and, if there is a delay before repair, removed from the floor to storage to reduce liability.","tags":["Chapter 25 quiz: Facility Design, Layout, and Organization"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"故障器材應掛上 Out of Order 標示；若維修要延遲數天，還應移出訓練區送回倉庫，避免運動員誤用帶來的法律責任。"},{"id":"q0835","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"Your facility manual states 'closed-toe athletic shoes are required at all times' and separately lays out the step-by-step process staff follow to enforce and document violations. Which statement correctly classifies these two items?","options":["The shoe rule is a procedure; the enforcement steps are the policy","Both are the same thing, since policy and procedure are interchangeable","The shoe rule is a policy; the enforcement steps are a procedure that carries the policy out"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The shoe rule is a policy; the enforcement steps are a procedure that carries the policy out","explanation_en":"Policies are essentially a facility's rules and regulations, while procedures describe how those policies are met or carried out.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"政策 (policy) 是場館的規則規定，例如一律穿封頭運動鞋；程式 (procedure) 是落實政策的步驟方法，例如執行與紀錄違規的流程。兩者層次不同。"},{"id":"q0836","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"An athlete is injured and sues, claiming the strength coach was negligent. For the claim to succeed in court, which complete set of elements must be established?","options":["Duty, breach of duty, proximate cause, and damages","Duty, breach, assumption of risk, and damages","Sovereign immunity, breach, proximate cause, and damages"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Duty, breach of duty, proximate cause, and damages","explanation_en":"Negligence requires all four: a duty to act, a breach of that duty, proximate cause, and resulting damages.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"過失 (negligence) 成立必須同時證明四要件：注意義務 (duty)、違反義務 (breach)、近因 (proximate cause) 與實際損害 (damages)，缺一不可。"},{"id":"q0837","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"In a lawsuit, the court weighs whether the coach acted as a competent peer would have in the same situation. This benchmark of conduct is known as which of the following?","options":["A signed waiver accepted before participation","What a reasonable and prudent person would do under similar circumstances","The maximum load an athlete can safely lift"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"What a reasonable and prudent person would do under similar circumstances","explanation_en":"Standard of care is the degree of caution and prudence a reasonable person would exercise in similar situations.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"注意義務標準 (standard of care) 指合理慎重之人 (reasonable and prudent person) 在類似情況下會展現的謹慎程度，法院以此衡量教練行為。"},{"id":"q0838","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A strength and conditioning professional owes their athletes a legal responsibility, duty, or obligation for their well-being. Which single term captures that legal responsibility?","options":["Informed consent","Assumption of risk","Liability"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Liability","explanation_en":"Liability is a legal responsibility, duty, or obligation owed to the athletes a professional serves.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"法律責任 (liability) 即專業人員對其所服務運動員應負的法律責任、義務或拘束。知情同意與自願承擔風險是另外的概念。"},{"id":"q0839","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"Every athlete signed an assumption-of-risk waiver before training. One is hurt and shows the coach failed to spot a maximal lift as a competent coach would. How does the waiver bear on the coach's exposure?","options":["It may NOT shield the coach when negligence is established","It permanently transfers all liability onto the athlete","It fully shields the coach from all liability regardless of conduct"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It may NOT shield the coach when negligence is established","explanation_en":"An assumption-of-risk waiver may not protect a professional from legal liability if they are found to be negligent.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"風險承擔同意書 (assumption of risk waiver) 在教練確有過失時未必能庇護他；它既不把全部責任轉嫁給運動員，也不是無論行為如何都能免責。"},{"id":"q0840","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"You supervise a college varsity team's lifting sessions and want to staff them at the recommended supervision level. What professional-to-athlete ratio applies at the collegiate level?","options":["1:15","1:20","1:10"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1:20","explanation_en":"Recommended ratios are 1:10 for junior high, 1:15 for high school, and 1:20 for college.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"建議督導比例：大學層級 1:20；高中 1:15、國中 1:10。大學隊適用 1:20。"},{"id":"q0841","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"You are assigned to supervise junior high athletes, the youngest group you train, which calls for the most conservative staffing. What professional-to-participant ratio is recommended for this age group?","options":["1:20","1:30","1:10"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:10","explanation_en":"The junior high school ratio is 1:10, the most conservative of the three levels.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"國中運動員年齡最小、風險控管最保守，建議比例 1:10。"},{"id":"q0842","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A returning athlete reports lingering symptoms and asks when they can restart lifting. Staying within your scope of practice, who is authorized to grant medical clearance to begin the program?","options":["The sports medicine staff, such as an athletic trainer, physician, or physical therapist","The head sport coach","The strength and conditioning professional"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"The sports medicine staff, such as an athletic trainer, physician, or physical therapist","explanation_en":"Only the sports medicine staff can provide medical clearance; diagnosing conditions is outside the S and C professional's scope of practice.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"醫療許可只能由運動醫學人員 (運動防護員、醫師、物理治療師) 核發；診斷傷病超出體能教練的專業執業範圍 (scope of practice)。"},{"id":"q0843","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A head coach wants athletes who miss a drill to run extra sprints and do push-ups as a consequence. From a legal and professional standpoint, how should the strength coach regard using conditioning as punishment?","options":["It is encouraged as a way to build mental toughness","It is strictly prohibited because of the reckless or negligent conduct it represents","It is acceptable for a player's first offense only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It is strictly prohibited because of the reckless or negligent conduct it represents","explanation_en":"Using exercise or conditioning as punishment is strictly prohibited because of the reckless or negligent conduct it represents (e.g., hazing, mental abuse).","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"用體能訓練 (跑衝刺、伏地挺身) 處罰犯規球員，在法律與專業上被視為魯莽或過失行為 (涉凌辱與心理虐待)，專業上應嚴禁。"},{"id":"q0844","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"When lawsuits arise from athletic injuries, one program factor is implicated far more than any other. Supervision was cited in roughly what share of such court cases?","options":["20 percent","50 percent","80 percent"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"80 percent","explanation_en":"Supervision was cited in an estimated 80 percent of court cases in which athletic injuries occurred.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"在運動傷害訴訟中，約 80% 的案件引用了督導問題——督導不足是被告最常失守的環節。"},{"id":"q0845","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"You are drafting a mission statement for a new strength and conditioning program. Which quality reflects an effective mission statement?","options":["It matches and stays within the organization's scope of practice","It is kept general and ambiguous to leave room for interpretation","It prescribes the specific means and methods of training to be used"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It matches and stays within the organization's scope of practice","explanation_en":"A good mission statement is short, clear, does not prescribe means, and matches the organization's scope of practice.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"有效的使命宣言應簡短、清楚、不規定具體訓練手段與方法，並符合組織的執業範圍；寫得模糊空泛反而是缺點。"},{"id":"q0846","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"You are assembling a performance team of scientific-foundation experts to support your athletes. Which of these individuals would traditionally NOT be counted as a core member of that team?","options":["Sports nutritionist","Athletic director","Exercise physiologist"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Athletic director","explanation_en":"The performance team is built from scientific-foundation experts such as the nutritionist, sport psychologist, and exercise physiologist, not the athletic director.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"表現團隊由科學基礎專家組成：運動營養師、運動心理師、運動生理學家等；體育總監 (athletic director) 屬行政體系，不是核心成員。"},{"id":"q0847","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"The person overseeing a collegiate strength and conditioning program coaches lifts on the floor while also managing budgets, staff, and the facility. This dual role is best described how?","options":["Solely an administrator with no coaching duties","Strictly a practitioner who only coaches lifts","Both a practitioner and an administrator"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Both a practitioner and an administrator","explanation_en":"The director is both a practitioner and an administrator responsible for the overall program, facility, equipment, and staff.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"大學體能訓練總監同時是實務者 (在場內指導舉動) 與行政者 (管理預算、人員與設施)，雙重角色並存。"},{"id":"q0848","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"In a negligence suit, the plaintiff must show that the coach's breach set off an unbroken chain of foreseeable events ending in the injury. Which element of negligence does that describe?","options":["Proximate cause","Damages","Duty"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Proximate cause","explanation_en":"Proximate cause is the direct, continuous sequence of reasonably foreseeable events that connects the breach to the resulting damages.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"近因 (proximate cause) 指違反義務與損害之間直接、未中斷且合理可預見的因果連鎖。"},{"id":"q0849","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"Before an athlete enrolls, you walk them through what a testing-and-training program involves, including its inherent risks and expected benefits, so they can choose whether to take part. This process is called which of the following?","options":["A government's immunity from being sued","Informed consent","An insurer's promise to defend the insured"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Informed consent","explanation_en":"Informed consent describes a procedure or activity with its inherent risks and benefits so the individual can decide whether to participate.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"知情同意 (informed consent) 是說明檢測或訓練計畫的內容、固有風險與預期效益，讓當事人自行決定是否參與的程式。"},{"id":"q0850","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A colleague asks how long to keep old injury report forms, assuming they can be shredded after a year. What is the sound reason to retain such records indefinitely instead?","options":["HIPAA mandates permanent retention of all such records","Equipment manufacturers require it to honor warranties","The statute of limitations for filing a lawsuit varies by location"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"The statute of limitations for filing a lawsuit varies by location","explanation_en":"The statute of limitations varies by location, so keeping records indefinitely protects the program if a suit is filed later.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"各管轄區提起訴訟的時效期限 (statute of limitations) 不同且可能很長，因此傷害紀錄等檔案以永久儲存為宜。"},{"id":"q0851","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A coach welds an added handle onto a machine and later an athlete is hurt using it. Even though the coach did not manufacture the equipment, how can product liability reach them?","options":["They can be named as codefendants, especially after modifying equipment or using it improperly","Only the athlete can ever be held responsible for equipment injuries","It cannot, because they did not manufacture the product"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"They can be named as codefendants, especially after modifying equipment or using it improperly","explanation_en":"Although professionals do not make products, modifying equipment or using it other than as intended can shift liability onto them and name them as codefendants.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"產品責任雖指向製造商，但教練若改裝器材或未按原用途使用，就可能被列為共同被告，責任轉移到場館端。"},{"id":"q0852","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A new athlete shows up eager to start lifting today. Before you let them use the facility, what must be completed and documented regarding their health status?","options":["A 1RM test to gauge their readiness to train","Preparticipation screening and medical clearance per the relevant governing bodies","Only a verbal statement from the athlete that they feel healthy"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Preparticipation screening and medical clearance per the relevant governing bodies","explanation_en":"Preparticipation screening and clearance, documented on file, are required before an athlete is allowed to participate.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"運動員使用設施前必須完成參前篩檢與醫療許可 (preparticipation screening and clearance)，並依主管機關規定留存書面紀錄，口頭自述健康不算數。"},{"id":"q0853","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"You are training your staff on how to supervise the floor to minimize risk. Which of the following aligns with the recognized principles of supervision?","options":["Focus supervision only on the most advanced lifters","Delegate supervisory authority freely to the athletes themselves","Always be there, be active and hands on, be prudent, and stay vigilant"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Always be there, be active and hands on, be prudent, and stay vigilant","explanation_en":"Principles of supervision include always being there, being active and hands on, being prudent and prepared, and being vigilant.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"公認的督導原則：永遠在場、積極且肢體到位 (hands on)、謹慎有備、保持警覺。只盯明星球員或授權給運動員都屬失職。"},{"id":"q0854","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":26,"question":"A 17-year-old athlete asks you to recommend a supplement. Under NSCA professional standards, which conditions must be met before you recommend or provide any substance?","options":["It must be lawful, scientifically shown to be beneficial or at least not harmful, and provided only to those age 18 or older","You may provide any product from a reputable manufacturer","You may provide whatever supplement the athlete requests"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It must be lawful, scientifically shown to be beneficial or at least not harmful, and provided only to those age 18 or older","explanation_en":"Standard 9.1 permits only lawful substances scientifically shown to be beneficial or at least not harmful, provided only to individuals age 18 or above.","tags":["Chapter 26 quiz: Facility Policies, Procedures, and Legal Issues"],"source":"liftaroo","explanation_zh":"NSCA 專業標準第 9.1 條：建議或提供補充品必須合法、有科學證據顯示有益或至少無害，且僅限年滿 18 歲者。"},{"id":"q0855","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following substances regulates muscle actions?","options":["potassium","calcium","troponin","tropomyosin"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"calcium","explanation_en":"Calcium binds to troponin, causing tropomyosin to move and expose myosin-binding sites on actin.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鈣離子 (calcium) 與肌鈣蛋白 (troponin) 結合後，使原肌凝蛋白 (tropomyosin) 移位、暴露肌動蛋白 (actin) 上的肌球蛋白結合位，從而調節肌肉收縮；肌梭等屬構造或感受器，不是調節離子。"},{"id":"q0856","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following substances acts at the neuromuscular junction to excite the muscle fibers of a motor unit?","options":["acetylcholine","ATP","creatine phosphate","serotonin"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"acetylcholine","explanation_en":"Acetylcholine is released by motor neurons at the neuromuscular junction to initiate muscle fiber depolarization.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"乙醯膽鹼 (acetylcholine, ACh) 由運動神經元在神經肌肉接合處釋放，啟動肌纖維去極化，_excite_運動單位的肌纖維；ATP 與磷酸肌酸是能量物質，血清素不在此接合處作用。"},{"id":"q0857","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"When throwing a baseball, an athlete’s arm is rapidly stretched just before throwing the ball. Which structure detects and responds to that stretch by reflexively increasing muscle activity?","options":["Golgi tendon organ","muscle spindle","extrafusal muscle","Pacinian corpuscle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"muscle spindle","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles detect changes in muscle length and trigger the stretch reflex to increase muscle activation.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌梭 (muscle spindle) 偵測肌肉長度變化，投擰前手臂被快速拉長時引發牽張反射 (stretch reflex)、反射性提高肌肉活化；高基腱器官 (GTO) 偵測的是張力，Pacinian 小體感受壓力。"},{"id":"q0858","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"From which of the following is the heart’s electrical impulse normally initiated?","options":["AV node","SA node","the brain","the sympathetic nervous system"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"SA node","explanation_en":"The sinoatrial (SA) node serves as the heart’s natural pacemaker.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"正常心臟電衝動由竇房結 (SA node) 發起，它是心臟的天然pacemaker；房室結 (AV node) 只是傳導路徑上的一站。"},{"id":"q0859","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following occurs during the QRS complex of a typical ECG?\n\nI. depolarization of the atrium\nII. repolarization of the atrium\nIII. repolarization of the ventricle\nIV. depolarization of the ventricle","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"II and IV only","explanation_en":"The QRS complex represents ventricular depolarization, while atrial repolarization occurs simultaneously but is masked by the larger ventricular signal.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"QRS 複合波代表心室去極化；心房再極化同時發生但被較大的心室訊號掩蓋。心房去極化屬於 P 波，心室再極化屬於 T 波。"},{"id":"q0860","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following best describes the role of troponin in skeletal muscle contraction?","options":["It binds to myosin and provides energy for cross-bridge cycling.","It blocks actin’s myosin-binding sites until calcium binds.","It stores calcium inside the sarcoplasmic reticulum.","It pumps calcium back into the sarcoplasmic reticulum to end contraction."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It blocks actin’s myosin-binding sites until calcium binds.","explanation_en":"Troponin is part of the regulatory complex; when calcium binds to troponin, tropomyosin shifts and exposes actin’s myosin-binding sites.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌鈣蛋白 (troponin) 屬於調控蛋白複合物：它與原肌凝蛋白一起遮蔽肌動蛋白上的肌球蛋白結合位，鈣離子與肌鈣蛋白結合後此遮蔽才被移開。它不供能、不儲鈣、也不打鈣回肌漿網。"},{"id":"q0861","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Acetylcholine released at the neuromuscular junction primarily causes which of the following?","options":["Opening of ligand-gated ion channels on the muscle membrane","Release of calcium from the sarcoplasmic reticulum directly","Inhibition of motor neuron firing via presynaptic blockade","Immediate detachment of myosin from actin"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Opening of ligand-gated ion channels on the muscle membrane","explanation_en":"ACh binds receptors on the motor end plate, opening ligand-gated channels and initiating depolarization of the sarcolemma.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"ACh 與運動終板 (motor end plate) 上的受體結合，開啟配體閘控離子通道，引發肌細胞膜 (sarcolemma) 去極化；肌漿網釋放鈣是後續步驟，不是 ACh 直接作用。"},{"id":"q0862","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"The primary immediate energy source used by myosin ATPase during cross-bridge cycling is:","options":["glucose","ATP","creatine phosphate","glycogen"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"ATP","explanation_en":"Myosin ATPase directly hydrolyzes ATP to power cross-bridge cycling; other substrates support ATP resynthesis.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌球蛋白 ATPase 直接水解 ATP (三磷酸腺苷) 驅動橫橋 (cross-bridge) 迴圈；磷酸肌酸、葡萄糖、肝糖都是支援 ATP 再合成的底物，不是直接能源。"},{"id":"q0863","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following best describes the function of the sarcoplasmic reticulum in skeletal muscle?","options":["It provides structural support to the muscle fiber.","It stores and releases calcium to regulate contraction.","It generates action potentials along the muscle membrane.","It produces acetylcholine to excite the motor end plate."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It stores and releases calcium to regulate contraction.","explanation_en":"The sarcoplasmic reticulum stores calcium and releases it to initiate muscle contraction.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌漿網 (sarcoplasmic reticulum) 的功能是儲存並釋放鈣離子以調控收縮；產生動作電位是肌膜的功能，產生 ACh 是運動神經元末梢。"},{"id":"q0864","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following events occurs FIRST in the excitation–contraction coupling sequence?","options":["Calcium binds to troponin.","Acetylcholine binds to receptors on the motor end plate.","Tropomyosin moves away from actin binding sites.","Cross-bridge cycling begins."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Acetylcholine binds to receptors on the motor end plate.","explanation_en":"ACh binding at the motor end plate is the earliest event that initiates muscle fiber depolarization.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"excitation-contraction coupling (興奮收縮耦聯) 的第一步是 ACh 結合運動終板受體；鈣結合肌鈣蛋白、原肌凝蛋白移位、橫橋迴圈都在之後發生。"},{"id":"q0865","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"The Golgi tendon organ is MOST closely associated with detecting changes in:","options":["muscle length","muscle tension","joint position","skin pressure"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"muscle tension","explanation_en":"Golgi tendon organs detect changes in muscle tension and help protect against excessive force.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高基腱器官 (Golgi tendon organ) 與肌肉張力 (tension) 的變化最相關，可防範過大出力；肌肉長度是肌梭、關節位置是本體感受器、皮膚壓力是 Pacinian 小體的範疇。"},{"id":"q0866","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following best describes extrafusal muscle fibers?","options":["They are the primary force-producing fibers in skeletal muscle.","They detect muscle stretch and initiate the stretch reflex.","They are sensory neurons located within the tendon.","They generate the heart’s electrical impulses."],"answer":0,"answer_text":"They are the primary force-producing fibers in skeletal muscle.","explanation_en":"Extrafusal fibers are the main contractile fibers responsible for producing force.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"梭外肌纖維 (extrafusal fibers) 是骨骼肌主要的收縮與產力纖維；偵測牽張的是梭內肌纖維 (intrafusal)，GTO 在肌腱內，心臟衝動與它無關。"},{"id":"q0867","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes the function of the SA node?","options":["It delays electrical conduction to allow ventricular filling.","It initiates the heart’s electrical impulse as the primary pacemaker.","It transmits impulses directly to the ventricles.","It inhibits sympathetic nervous system activity."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It initiates the heart’s electrical impulse as the primary pacemaker.","explanation_en":"The SA node initiates the heart’s electrical impulse under normal conditions.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"竇房結的功能是擔任主要 pacemaker、發起心臟電衝動；延緩傳導讓心室 wypełн 充填是房室結，直接傳至心室室的是希斯束與浦金野纖維。"},{"id":"q0868","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"During a typical ECG, the P wave represents:","options":["ventricular depolarization","atrial depolarization","ventricular repolarization","atrial repolarization"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"atrial depolarization","explanation_en":"The P wave corresponds to atrial depolarization.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"P 波代表心房去極化；心室去極化是 QRS，心室再極化是 T 波。"},{"id":"q0869","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following is MOST associated with ventricular repolarization on a typical ECG?","options":["P wave","QRS complex","T wave","PR interval"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"T wave","explanation_en":"The T wave represents ventricular repolarization.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"T 波最對應心室再極化；P 波是心房去極化，QRS 是心室去極化，PR 間期是房室傳導時間。"},{"id":"q0870","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"A motor unit is best defined as:","options":["a muscle fiber and all sensory neurons that detect stretch","a motor neuron and all the muscle fibers it innervates","all the muscles that cross a joint","a group of tendons attaching muscle to bone"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"a motor neuron and all the muscle fibers it innervates","explanation_en":"A motor unit consists of a motor neuron and all the muscle fibers it innervates.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動單位 (motor unit) 的定義：一個運動神經元及其所支配的全部肌纖維。"},{"id":"q0871","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which of the following would MOST directly increase the speed of a stretch reflex response?","options":["Greater activation of muscle spindles due to rapid stretch","Greater activation of Golgi tendon organs","Decreased acetylcholine release","Increased ventricular repolarization"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Greater activation of muscle spindles due to rapid stretch","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles respond strongly to rapid lengthening, accelerating the stretch reflex.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"快速拉長會更強烈活化肌梭，直接加快牽張反射；GTO 反應於張力，ACh 減少只會變慢，心室再極化與反射無關。"},{"id":"q0872","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which sequence correctly represents the heart’s normal electrical conduction pathway?","options":["AV node → SA node → Purkinje fibers","SA node → AV node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibers","Purkinje fibers → AV node → SA node","SA node → Purkinje fibers → AV node"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"SA node → AV node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibers","explanation_en":"Normal conduction proceeds SA node → AV node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibers.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"正常傳導路徑：竇房結 (SA node)→房室結 (AV node)→希斯束 (Bundle of His)→浦金野纖維 (Purkinje fibers)，順序不可亂。"},{"id":"q0873","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"If calcium does NOT bind to troponin during attempted contraction, which of the following will occur?","options":["Tropomyosin blocks actin’s myosin-binding sites.","Myosin heads bind more strongly to actin.","Cross-bridge cycling accelerates.","Ventricular depolarization increases."],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Tropomyosin blocks actin’s myosin-binding sites.","explanation_en":"Without calcium binding to troponin, tropomyosin remains in place, preventing cross-bridge formation.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"若鈣未與肌鈣蛋白結合，原肌凝蛋白維持原位、遮蔽肌動蛋白上的肌球蛋白結合位，橫橋無法形成；不會加速結合或加快迴圈。"},{"id":"q0874","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Which statement about the QRS complex is MOST accurate?","options":["It represents atrial depolarization.","It represents ventricular depolarization.","It represents ventricular repolarization.","It represents atrial repolarization only."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It represents ventricular depolarization.","explanation_en":"The QRS complex corresponds primarily to ventricular depolarization.","tags":["chapter-01"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"QRS 複合波最主要的意義是心室去極化 (同時掩蓋心房再極化)。"},{"id":"q0875","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following is the definition of power?","options":["(mass) · (acceleration)","(force) · (distance)","(force) · (velocity)","(torque) · (time)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"(force) · (velocity)","explanation_en":"Power is defined as the rate of doing work and can be expressed as force multiplied by velocity.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率 (power) = 力 × 速度，即作功的速率；力×距離是功，質量×加速度是力，力矩×時間接近衝量概念。"},{"id":"q0876","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"To compare performances of Olympic weightlifters of different body weights, the classic formula divides the load lifted by the athlete’s:","options":["body weight","body weight squared","lean body weight","body weight to the two-thirds power"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"body weight to the two-thirds power","explanation_en":"Relative strength is commonly calculated by dividing the load lifted by body weight to the two-thirds power.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"比較不同體重舉重選手的傳統公式是把負重除以體重的 2/3 次方，而非單純除以體重或去脂體重。"},{"id":"q0877","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"During a free weight exercise, muscle force varies with which of the following?\n\nI. perpendicular distance from the weight to the body joint\nII. joint angle\nIII. movement acceleration\nIV. movement velocity squared","options":["I and II only","I and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"Muscle force during free weight exercise depends on moment arm length, joint angle, and acceleration. Velocity squared applies to fluid resistance, not free weights.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"自由重量動作中，肌肉施力隨力臂 (重量至關節的垂直距離)、關節角度與動作加速度而變；速度平方用於流體阻力器材，不適用於自由重量。"},{"id":"q0878","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A vertical jump involves knee, hip, and shoulder movement primarily in which of the following anatomical planes?","options":["sagittal","perpendicular","frontal","transverse"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"sagittal","explanation_en":"Flexion and extension movements occur primarily in the sagittal plane.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"垂直跳的膝、髖、肩動作皆為屈/伸，主要發生在矢狀面 (sagittal plane)；額狀面是外展，橫斷面是旋轉。"},{"id":"q0879","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"An athlete is performing a concentric isokinetic elbow flexion and extension exercise. Which type(s) of levers occur(s) at the elbow during this exercise?\n\nI. first class\nII. second class\nIII. third class","options":["I only","II only","I and III only","II and III only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":"Elbow flexion and extension function as third-class levers, where muscle force is applied between the axis and resistance.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肘關節屈曲屬第三類槓桿 (力點在中間)，伸肘時肘關節軸位於施力點與阻力點之間屬第一類槓桿，因此第一與第三類都存在；人體肘部不是第二類槓桿。"},{"id":"q0880","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Work is BEST defined as:","options":["force applied over time","force multiplied by velocity","force applied through a displacement","torque applied through an angle"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"force applied through a displacement","explanation_en":"Work equals force applied through a displacement in the direction of the force.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功 (work) = 作用力 × 沿力方向的位移；力×時間是衝量，力×速度是功率。"},{"id":"q0881","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes torque?","options":["Force applied parallel to a lever arm","Rotary effect of a force acting about an axis","Force multiplied by velocity","Rate of change in momentum"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rotary effect of a force acting about an axis","explanation_en":"Torque is the rotary effect of a force acting at a distance from a joint or axis.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"扭矩 (torque) 是力繞軸 (關節) 旋轉的效果，等於力乘以力臂。"},{"id":"q0882","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Increasing the perpendicular distance between a resistance and a joint axis will:","options":["decrease torque","have no effect on torque","increase torque","increase velocity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increase torque","explanation_en":"Torque increases as the moment arm (perpendicular distance) increases.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"阻力至關節軸的垂直距離 (力臂) 越大，扭矩越大——力臂與扭矩成正比。"},{"id":"q0883","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which lever system provides the greatest mechanical advantage?","options":["first-class lever","second-class lever","third-class lever","fourth-class lever"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"second-class lever","explanation_en":"Second-class levers place the resistance between the axis and force, maximizing mechanical advantage.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第二類槓桿的阻力位於軸與施力之間，力臂結構使其機械利益最大；第三類槓桿機械利益小於一。"},{"id":"q0884","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Most human musculoskeletal movements operate as:","options":["first-class levers","second-class levers","third-class levers","compound levers only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"third-class levers","explanation_en":"Most human joints function as third-class levers, favoring speed and range of motion over force.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"人體大多數肌肉骨骼動作是第三類槓桿：犧牲力，換取速度與動作幅度。"},{"id":"q0885","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which anatomical plane divides the body into left and right halves?","options":["frontal","transverse","sagittal","horizontal"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"sagittal","explanation_en":"The sagittal plane divides the body into left and right portions.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"矢狀面 (sagittal plane) 將身體分為左右兩部分；額狀面分前後，橫斷面分上下。"},{"id":"q0886","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"A lateral raise exercise primarily involves movement in which anatomical plane?","options":["sagittal","frontal","transverse","diagonal"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"frontal","explanation_en":"Shoulder abduction during a lateral raise occurs in the frontal plane.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"側平舉的肩關節外展發生在額狀面 (frontal plane)。"},{"id":"q0887","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Angular displacement refers to:","options":["change in joint angle","rate of change in velocity","force applied about a joint","distance traveled by the center of mass"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"change in joint angle","explanation_en":"Angular displacement is the change in joint angle during movement.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"角位移 (angular displacement) 指關節角的變化量。"},{"id":"q0888","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following BEST explains why third-class levers are common in the human body?","options":["They maximize force production","They reduce muscular effort","They increase movement speed and range of motion","They eliminate joint torque"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"They increase movement speed and range of motion","explanation_en":"Third-class levers sacrifice force for increased speed and range of motion, which benefits athletic movement.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第三類槓桿犧牲力但提高動作速度與活動範圍，對運動表現有利，因此人體多數關節以此方式運作。"},{"id":"q0889","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which variable directly determines linear acceleration according to Newton’s second law?","options":["velocity","mass","force","power"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"force","explanation_en":"Acceleration is directly proportional to the net force applied.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"牛頓第二運動定律：加速度與淨力成正比——直接決定線性加速度的是力 (force)。"},{"id":"q0890","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"During a squat, the greatest external torque at the knee occurs when:","options":["the knee is fully extended","the barbell is directly over the joint","the moment arm is longest","velocity is constant"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"the moment arm is longest","explanation_en":"Torque is greatest when the perpendicular distance between the load and the joint axis is longest.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲時膝關節外部扭矩在槓鈴與膝關節軸之間力臂最長時最大；槓鈴正對關節上方時力臂近於零。"},{"id":"q0891","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes center of mass?","options":["Point of maximum force production","Point at which mass is evenly distributed","Point of maximal velocity","Point where torque is minimized"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Point at which mass is evenly distributed","explanation_en":"The center of mass is the point where the body's mass is evenly distributed in all directions.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"重心 (center of mass) 是身體質量在各方向均勻分佈的點。"},{"id":"q0892","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which biomechanical principle explains why a wider base of support improves balance?","options":["Reduced torque","Lower center of mass relative to base of support","Greater acceleration","Increased angular momentum"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Lower center of mass relative to base of support","explanation_en":"A wider base of support increases stability by allowing the center of mass to remain within the base more easily.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"較寬的支援面讓重心更容易保持在支援面內、相對重心位置更低，穩定度因而提高。"},{"id":"q0893","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which quantity is conserved in the absence of external forces?","options":["force","velocity","momentum","power"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"momentum","explanation_en":"Momentum is conserved when no external forces act on a system.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"無外力作用時動量 (momentum) 守恆；力、速度、功率都不一定守恆。"},{"id":"q0894","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following BEST explains why increasing load reduces movement velocity during resistance exercise?","options":["Greater force reduces acceleration","Greater mass requires greater force to accelerate","Greater power output is required","Greater torque eliminates displacement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Greater mass requires greater force to accelerate","explanation_en":"As load increases, more force is required to accelerate it, typically reducing movement velocity.","tags":["chapter-02"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"負重增加即質量增大，依 F=ma 需要更大的力才能加速，動作速度自然下降。"},{"id":"q0895","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Which of the following substances can be metabolized anaerobically?","options":["glycerol","glucose","amino acids","free fatty acids"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"glucose","explanation_en":"Only glucose can be metabolized anaerobically via glycolysis.","tags":["chapter-03"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"只有葡萄糖可經無氧糖解 (anaerobic glycolysis) 進行無氧代謝；遊離脂肪酸、甘油、胺基酸的代謝都需要氧氣。"},{"id":"q0896","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Which of the following reactions is the primary cause of metabolic acidosis (i.e., the decrease in intramuscular pH during high-intensity, fatiguing exercise)?","options":["ATP → ADP + Pi + H+","pyruvate + NADH → lactate + NAD+","ADP + creatine phosphate → ATP + creatine","fructose-6-phosphate → fructose-1,6-bisphosphate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"ATP → ADP + Pi + H+","explanation_en":"ATP hydrolysis releases hydrogen ions, which directly lower muscle pH.","tags":["chapter-03"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高強度疲勞性運動時肌肉 pH 下降 (代謝性酸中毒) 的主因是 ATP 水解 (ATP→ADP+Pi+H+) 釋放的氫離子；乳酸生成 (pyruvate→lactate) 反而消耗 H+，不是酸化來源。"},{"id":"q0897","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Which of the following energy systems produces ATP at the quickest rate?","options":["phosphagen","aerobic glycolysis","fat oxidation","fast glycolysis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"phosphagen","explanation_en":"The phosphagen system produces ATP at the fastest rate but has very limited capacity.","tags":["chapter-03"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統 (phosphagen system，ATP-CP) 產生 ATP 的速率最快，但容量極有限；快糖解次之，有氧系統最慢。"},{"id":"q0898","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Approximately how many net ATP are produced via the oxidative energy system from the metabolism of one glucose molecule?","options":["27","34","38","41"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"27","explanation_en":"Modern estimates place ATP yield from one glucose molecule at approximately 30–34 ATP.","tags":["chapter-03"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"本題答案為 27：現代估計下，1 分子葡萄糖經有氧代謝的 ATP 產量比舊教科書的 38 大幅下修，選項中 38、41 明顯高估。"},{"id":"q0899","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Which of the following energy substrates cannot be depleted during extreme exercise intensities or durations?","options":["creatine phosphate","glycogen","water","ATP"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"ATP","explanation_en":"ATP concentration is tightly regulated and cannot be fully depleted without cell death.","tags":["chapter-03"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"ATP 濃度受到嚴格調控，極端強度或時間下也不會完全耗盡——ATP 若真耗盡細胞就死亡；磷酸肌酸與肝糖都會明顯耗竭。"},{"id":"q0900","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"After a bout of resistance training, acute hormonal secretions provide all of the following information to the body EXCEPT","options":["amount of physiological stress","metabolic demands of exercise","type of physiological stress","energy expended"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"energy expended","explanation_en":"Acute hormonal responses reflect stress magnitude, stress type, and metabolic demands, but they do not directly quantify total energy expended.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"急性荷爾蒙分泌向身體傳訊：生理壓力的量、壓力的型別、與運動的代謝需求；但它不直接告知總能量消耗。"},{"id":"q0901","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which of the following hormones enhance(s) muscle tissue growth?\n\nI. growth hormone\nII. cortisol\nIII. IGF-I\nIV. progesterone","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":"Growth hormone and IGF-I support anabolic processes related to muscle growth. Cortisol is catabolic, and progesterone is not a primary driver of hypertrophy.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"生長激素 (GH) 與 IGF-I (類胰島素生長因子) 促進肌肉合成代謝；皮質醇屬分解性荷爾蒙，黃體素不是肌肉肥大的主要驅動者。"},{"id":"q0902","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a function of growth hormone?","options":["increase lipolysis","decrease collagen synthesis","increase amino acid transport","decrease glucose utilization"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"decrease collagen synthesis","explanation_en":"Growth hormone increases collagen synthesis, supporting connective tissue integrity. It also increases lipolysis, increases amino acid transport, and decreases glucose utilization.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"GH 實際上會增加膠原蛋白 (collagen) 合成、維護結締組織，所以「減少膠原蛋白合成」不是它的功能；促進脂解 (lipolysis)、增加胺基酸運輸、減少葡萄糖利用都是 GH 的真實作用。"},{"id":"q0903","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which of the following hormones has the greatest influence on neural changes?","options":["growth hormone","testosterone","cortisol","IGF"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"testosterone","explanation_en":"Testosterone has the strongest association with neural adaptations related to strength, such as motor unit recruitment and neuromuscular efficiency.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"睪固酮 (testosterone) 對神經適應 (運動單位動員、神經肌肉效率) 的影響最大，與早期肌力增益的神經面有關。"},{"id":"q0904","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"What type of resistance training workout promotes the highest growth hormone increases following the exercise session?","options":["Rest: 30 seconds; Volume: High; Sets: 3","Rest: 30 seconds; Volume: Low; Sets: 1","Rest: 3 minutes; Volume: High; Sets: 1","Rest: 3 minutes; Volume: Low; Sets: 3"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Rest: 30 seconds; Volume: High; Sets: 3","explanation_en":"Growth hormone responses are greatest with short rest intervals, high training volume, and high metabolic stress.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"短組間 (30 秒)、高訓練量、多組數 (3 組) 的代謝壓力型課表會引發運動後最大的生長激素反應。"},{"id":"q0905","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Prolonged exposure to elevated hormone concentrations most commonly results in which cellular adaptation?","options":["upregulation of receptors","downregulation of receptors","increased hormone specificity","enhanced second-messenger activity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"downregulation of receptors","explanation_en":"Chronic exposure to high hormone levels leads to downregulation, reducing receptor number and cellular sensitivity.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"長期暴露於高荷爾蒙濃度會造成受體下行調節 (downregulation)：受體數量減少、細胞敏感度下降；上調發生在荷爾蒙長期不足時。"},{"id":"q0906","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which hormone type exerts its effects primarily by binding to intracellular receptors and directly influencing gene transcription?","options":["polypeptide hormones","catecholamines","steroid hormones","protein hormones"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"steroid hormones","explanation_en":"Steroid hormones are lipid-soluble, cross the cell membrane, and bind intracellular receptors to directly affect gene transcription.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"類固醇荷爾蒙 (steroid hormones) 具脂溶性，可進入細胞與胞內受體結合、直接調控基因轉錄；胜肽類、蛋白類荷爾蒙與兒茶酚胺都用膜受體。"},{"id":"q0907","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which of the following hormones relies on a second-messenger system to exert its effects?","options":["testosterone","cortisol","growth hormone","aldosterone"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"growth hormone","explanation_en":"Growth hormone is a peptide hormone that binds membrane receptors and signals via second-messenger pathways.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"生長激素是胜肽荷爾蒙，結合膜受體後經第二訊息系統 (second messenger) 傳遞作用；睪固酮、皮質醇、醛固酮都是類固醇荷爾蒙，走胞內受體路徑。"},{"id":"q0908","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which regulatory mechanism helps maintain hormonal homeostasis by reducing hormone secretion once adequate levels are reached?","options":["positive feedback","hormone specificity","negative feedback","receptor upregulation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"negative feedback","explanation_en":"Negative feedback loops inhibit further hormone secretion once sufficient physiological effects have been achieved.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"負回饋 (negative feedback)：荷爾蒙達到足夠濃度後反向抑制進一步分泌，維持荷爾蒙恆定。"},{"id":"q0909","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"An athlete experiencing chronically elevated cortisol levels is MOST likely to experience which outcome?","options":["increased protein synthesis","enhanced immune function","increased protein breakdown","greater insulin sensitivity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increased protein breakdown","explanation_en":"Cortisol is a catabolic hormone that promotes protein breakdown and suppresses immune function during prolonged stress.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"皮質醇屬分解性荷爾蒙，長期偏高會增加蛋白質分解、抑制免疫功能，而非促進合成或提升胰島素敏感度。"},{"id":"q0910","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":4,"question":"Which training variable manipulation is MOST associated with an acute anabolic hormonal environment?","options":["long rest intervals with low volume","short rest intervals with high volume","maximal loads with extended rest","low-volume technique-focused training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"short rest intervals with high volume","explanation_en":"Short rest intervals combined with high volume increase metabolic stress and are associated with acute anabolic hormonal responses.","tags":["chapter-04"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"短組間搭配高訓練量提高代謝壓力，最能營造急性合成代謝性荷爾蒙環境。"},{"id":"q0911","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which of the following adaptations occurs FIRST during the initial weeks of a resistance training program?","options":["muscle fiber hypertrophy","increased cross-sectional area","enhanced motor unit recruitment","increased pennation angle"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"enhanced motor unit recruitment","explanation_en":"Early strength gains are primarily due to neural adaptations such as increased motor unit recruitment and firing frequency rather than hypertrophy.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"開始重量訓練的初期數週，肌力提升主要來自神經適應——運動單位動員與放電頻率改善——肥大、橫截面積增大、羽狀角變化都在之後。"},{"id":"q0912","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which resistance training adaptation is MOST responsible for improvements in rate of force development?","options":["increased muscle cross-sectional area","increased tendon stiffness","enhanced motor unit firing frequency","fiber type hypertrophy"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"enhanced motor unit firing frequency","explanation_en":"Rate of force development is largely influenced by neural factors, particularly the speed and frequency of motor unit activation.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"力量生成率 (rate of force development) 主要受神經因素影響，特別是運動單位放電的頻率與速度。"},{"id":"q0913","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which of the following training variables is MOST critical for maximizing neural adaptations in anaerobic resistance training?","options":["high volume with short rest intervals","moderate load with slow tempos","heavy loads with long rest intervals","low load with high repetitions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"heavy loads with long rest intervals","explanation_en":"Neural adaptations are maximized by high-intensity loads (≥85% 1RM) with sufficient rest to maintain force output.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"大負重 (≥85% 1RM) 搭配充分組間休息能維持每次動作的出力品質，最大化神經適應；小負重高次數偏代謝壓力。"},{"id":"q0914","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which adaptation contributes MOST to increased force transmission following chronic resistance training?","options":["muscle fiber hypertrophy","improved neuromuscular coordination","increased tendon stiffness","enhanced capillary density"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increased tendon stiffness","explanation_en":"Increased tendon stiffness improves the transmission of muscular force to the skeletal system, enhancing strength and power output.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌腱剛性 (tendon stiffness) 增加可提升肌肉力量向骨骼的傳導效率，對力量與功率輸出貢獻最大。"},{"id":"q0915","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which of the following changes is MOST characteristic of functional overreaching (FOR)?","options":["long-term performance decrement","persistent mood disturbances","short-term performance decrease followed by supercompensation","chronic hormonal suppression"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"short-term performance decrease followed by supercompensation","explanation_en":"Functional overreaching involves a temporary decrease in performance that is followed by improvement after adequate recovery.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功能性過度負荷 (FOR) 的特徵是短期表現下降，經充分恢復後出現超補償 (supercompensation)；長期衰退與荷爾蒙長期抑制屬非功能性過度負荷/OTS。"},{"id":"q0916","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":5,"question":"Which resistance training adaptation is MOST reversible during periods of detraining?","options":["neural efficiency","bone mineral density","muscle fiber cross-sectional area","tendon stiffness"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"muscle fiber cross-sectional area","explanation_en":"Muscle hypertrophy is lost more rapidly during detraining compared to neural or skeletal adaptations.","tags":["chapter-05"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"停訓期間肌纖維橫截面積 (肥大) 消退最快，神經效率、骨密度、肌腱特性的保留時間都較長。"},{"id":"q0917","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"A 17-year-old high school cross-country runner has been training aerobically for six months. Which muscular adaptation will most likely occur?","options":["increased concentration of glycolytic enzymes","hyperplasia of Type II fibers","transformation from Type I to Type II fibers","hypertrophy of Type I fibers"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"hypertrophy of Type I fibers","explanation_en":"Aerobic training promotes hypertrophy and oxidative adaptations in Type I muscle fibers.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"六個月有氧耐力訓練會造成第一型 (慢縮) 肌纖維肥大與氧化能力提升；成人的肌纖維型別轉變與增生並非主要適應。"},{"id":"q0918","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"The amount of blood ejected from the left ventricle during each beat is the:","options":["cardiac output","arteriovenous oxygen difference","heart rate","stroke volume"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"stroke volume","explanation_en":"Stroke volume is the amount of blood ejected per beat.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"每次心跳左心室射出的血量是每搏輸出量 (stroke volume)；心輸出量=每搏輸出量×心率。"},{"id":"q0919","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which of the following does NOT normally increase during an aerobic exercise session?","options":["end-diastolic volume","cardiac contractility","cardiac output","diastolic blood pressure"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"diastolic blood pressure","explanation_en":"Diastolic blood pressure typically remains unchanged or may slightly decrease during aerobic exercise.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"有氧運動時舒張末期容積、心肌收縮力、心輸出量都上升，但舒張壓通常不變或略降；「舒張壓明顯上升」是異常反應。"},{"id":"q0920","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Mean arterial pressure is defined as the:","options":["average blood pressure throughout the cardiac cycle","average of systolic and diastolic blood pressures","average systolic blood pressure during exercise","average of blood pressure and heart rate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"average blood pressure throughout the cardiac cycle","explanation_en":"Mean arterial pressure reflects average arterial pressure across the cardiac cycle.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"平均動脈壓 (MAP) 是整個心跳週期中動脈壓的平均值，不是收縮壓與舒張壓的簡單平均。"},{"id":"q0921","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Primary training adaptations of elite aerobically trained athletes include which of the following?\n\nI. increased maximal oxygen uptake\nII. decreased blood lactate concentration\nIII. increased running economy\nIV. decreased capillary density","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"Aerobic training increases VO₂max, improves lactate handling, and enhances economy while increasing capillary density.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"優秀耐力運動員的主要適應：最大攝氧量 (VO2max) 上升、運動時血乳酸濃度下降、跑步經濟性改善；微血管密度是增加而非減少。"},{"id":"q0922","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which adaptation is considered a PRIMARY peripheral adaptation to aerobic endurance training?","options":["increased maximal heart rate","increased stroke volume","increased mitochondrial density","increased cardiac output"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increased mitochondrial density","explanation_en":"Peripheral adaptations include increased mitochondrial density, capillarization, and oxidative enzyme activity within skeletal muscle.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力訓練的主要周邊適應是肌纖維內粒線體 (mitochondria) 密度增加，伴微血管增生與氧化酶活性提升；心搏量、心輸出量屬中樞適應，最大心率反而不變或略降。"},{"id":"q0923","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which factor contributes MOST to increases in VO₂max following aerobic endurance training?","options":["increased maximal heart rate","improved arteriovenous oxygen difference","increased blood volume","increased glycolytic enzyme activity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increased blood volume","explanation_en":"Increases in VO₂max are driven largely by increases in stroke volume and blood volume, which enhance oxygen delivery.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"VO2max 的提升主要由血容量與每搏輸出量增加驅動，強化氧氣輸送；最大心率不會明顯上升，糖解酶與有氧能力無關。"},{"id":"q0924","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which adaptation BEST explains improved exercise economy following aerobic training?","options":["increased cardiac output","decreased ventilatory rate","improved neuromuscular efficiency","increased heart rate variability"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"improved neuromuscular efficiency","explanation_en":"Improved economy reflects reduced energy cost at a given workload due to enhanced neuromuscular coordination and efficiency.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動經濟性改善反映在相同工作量下能量消耗降低，來自神經肌肉協調與效率的進步。"},{"id":"q0925","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which cardiovascular variable typically plateaus FIRST during progressive aerobic training?","options":["stroke volume","maximal heart rate","cardiac output","arteriovenous oxygen difference"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"stroke volume","explanation_en":"Stroke volume adaptations tend to plateau earlier, after which improvements rely more on peripheral adaptations.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"漸進式有氧訓練中，每搏輸出量的適應最早 plateau，之後的進步主要依賴微血管、粒線體等周邊適應。"},{"id":"q0926","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":6,"question":"Which of the following adaptations is MOST specific to long-duration aerobic endurance training?","options":["increased Type IIx fiber cross-sectional area","increased glycolytic enzyme activity","increased capillary-to-fiber ratio","increased rate of force development"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increased capillary-to-fiber ratio","explanation_en":"Long-duration aerobic training increases capillary density to enhance oxygen delivery and waste removal.","tags":["chapter-06"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"長時間耐力訓練特有的適應是微血管與肌纖維比例 (capillary-to-fiber ratio) 上升，改善氧氣輸送與廢物清除。"},{"id":"q0927","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"An 8-year-old boy dramatically increased his upper body strength after following a six-month resistance training program. Which of the following is MOST likely responsible for this gain?","options":["increased number of muscle fibers","enhanced cross-sectional area","greater muscle density","improved neuromuscular functioning"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"improved neuromuscular functioning","explanation_en":"Strength gains in prepubescent children are primarily due to neural adaptations rather than hypertrophy.","tags":["chapter-07"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"青春期前兒童 (8 歲) 的重量訓練肌力增益主要來自神經肌肉功能改善，而非肌纖維肥大或增生。"},{"id":"q0928","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"Growth cartilage in children is located at all of the following EXCEPT the:","options":["diaphysis","epiphyseal plate","joint surface","apophyseal insertion"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"diaphysis","explanation_en":"The diaphysis is the shaft of the bone and does not contain growth cartilage.","tags":["chapter-07"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"骨幹 (diaphysis) 是骨的中間軸段，沒有生長軟骨；兒童生長軟骨位於骨骺板 (epiphyseal plate)、關節面與骨突附著處 (apophyseal insertion) 三處。"},{"id":"q0929","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"The condition characterized by a bone mineral density more than 2.5 standard deviations below the young adult mean is called:","options":["sarcopenia","osteopenia","osteoporosis","scoliosis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"osteoporosis","explanation_en":"Osteoporosis is defined as bone mineral density more than 2.5 SD below the young adult mean.","tags":["chapter-07"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"骨密度低於年輕成人平均值 2.5 個標準差以上定義為骨質疏鬆症 (osteoporosis)；介於 -1 至 -2.5 之間是骨質密度低下 (osteopenia)。"},{"id":"q0930","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"Which of the following should be evaluated FIRST when designing a training program for a 68-year-old competitive female tennis player?","options":["cardiovascular fitness","lower body strength","balance and agility","medical history"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"medical history","explanation_en":"Medical history must be assessed first to ensure safety before training older adults.","tags":["chapter-07"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"為高齡者 (68 歲) 設計訓練計畫前，第一件事是評估病史 (medical history) 確認安全，再談體能評估。"},{"id":"q0931","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":7,"question":"Deconditioned female college athletes who participate in sports such as basketball and soccer appear to be at increased risk for developing injuries to the:","options":["back","knee","wrist","neck"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"knee","explanation_en":"Female athletes are at higher risk of knee injuries, particularly ACL injuries, especially when deconditioned.","tags":["chapter-07"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"體能不足的female運動員 (籃球、足球) 膝關節受傷風險明顯較高，尤其是前十字韌帶 (ACL)。"},{"id":"q0932","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"An Olympic weightlifter attempting a personal record is able to ignore the audience and concentrate solely on performance. Which ability is most likely being used?","options":["selective attention","somatic anxiety","accuracy","self-efficacy"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"selective attention","explanation_en":"Selective attention allows athletes to focus on relevant cues while ignoring distractions.","tags":["chapter-08"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"無視觀眾、只專注於動作品質是選擇性注意力 (selective attention)——過濾無關線索、專注相關線索的能力。"},{"id":"q0933","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"An athlete’s desire to perform to his or her potential is an example of:","options":["motivation to avoid failure","autogenic training","self-confidence","achievement motivation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"achievement motivation","explanation_en":"Achievement motivation reflects the drive to achieve success and reach potential.","tags":["chapter-08"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"想把表現推向個人潛力的慾望是成就動機 (achievement motivation) 的典型定義。"},{"id":"q0934","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"For a high school American football team, if any player squats two times his body weight, his name is placed on the wall. This is an example of:","options":["negative reinforcement","positive reinforcement","negative punishment","positive punishment"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"positive reinforcement","explanation_en":"Adding recognition to reinforce behavior is positive reinforcement.","tags":["chapter-08"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"達成標準後施加認可 (名字上牆) 以提高該行為頻率，是正增強 (positive reinforcement)；負增強是移除嫌惡刺激，懲罰是降低行為頻率。"},{"id":"q0935","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"How does an athlete’s optimal level of arousal change with limited skill and ability to perform the activity?","options":["It increases.","It decreases.","It has no effect.","It is not related to the activity."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It decreases.","explanation_en":"Less-skilled athletes perform best at lower levels of arousal.","tags":["chapter-08"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"技能與能力不足時，最佳喚醒水準較低——高喚醒會幹擾尚未自動化的動作控制。"},{"id":"q0936","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"In teaching the push press, which is an example of segmentation with pure-part training integration?","options":["Practice the push press unloaded, progress to PVC pipe, then an unloaded bar.","Practice the dip, then dip with drive, then the entire push press.","Practice the dip, drive, and catch independently before the entire push press.","Practice dip and drive independently, then dip with drive, then catch, and finally the full push press."],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Practice dip and drive independently, then dip with drive, then catch, and finally the full push press.","explanation_en":"Pure-part segmentation trains individual components separately before progressive integration into the full movement.","tags":["chapter-08"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"純部分式 (pure-part) 分段訓練是把動作成分 (dip、drive、catch) 各自獨立練習，再逐步整合成完整 push press；其他選項屬整體或部分-整體式安排。"},{"id":"q0937","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Maintaining adequate glycogen stores:","options":["spares the use of protein for energy","improves maximum power","decreases endurance performance","helps athletes gain weight"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"spares the use of protein for energy","explanation_en":"Adequate glycogen helps meet energy demands so the body relies less on amino acids (protein) for fuel.","tags":["chapter-09"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"維持充足肝糖 (glycogen) 儲存可滿足能量需求，減少身體改用胺基酸 (蛋白質) 供能，即蛋白質節省效應。"},{"id":"q0938","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"The following is the most likely contributor to fatigue and poor performance:","options":["low protein intake","iron deficiency","low calcium intake","omega-3 fatty acid deficiency"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"iron deficiency","explanation_en":"Iron deficiency can reduce hemoglobin and oxygen delivery, commonly causing fatigue and reduced performance.","tags":["chapter-09"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"缺鐵 (iron deficiency) 降低血紅素、削弱氧氣輸送，是造成疲勞與表現不佳最常見的營養因素。"},{"id":"q0939","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Which of the following is a recommendation for lowering undesirably high levels of blood lipids?","options":["reduce complex carbohydrate intake","limit saturated fatty acid intake to 30% of total calories","consume a minimum of 500 mg of dietary cholesterol per day","replace saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated or polyunsaturated fatty acids"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"replace saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated or polyunsaturated fatty acids","explanation_en":"Replacing saturated fats with unsaturated fats (mono/poly) is a common strategy to improve blood lipid profiles.","tags":["chapter-09"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"改善過高血脂的飲食原則：以單元/多單元不飽和脂肪酸取代飽和脂肪酸；進一步砍 Complex carb、限脂質到 30% 總熱量或吃高膽固醇都不是首選做法。"},{"id":"q0940","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":9,"question":"Which of the following protein sources does not contain all essential amino acids in appreciable quantities?","options":["poultry","eggs","lentils","beef"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"lentils","explanation_en":"Many plant proteins (like lentils) are incomplete, meaning one or more essential amino acids are present in lower amounts.","tags":["chapter-09"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"扁豆 (lentils) 等植物性蛋白質多為不完全蛋白質，某一種以上必需胺基酸含量不足；雞肉、蛋、牛肉均含全部必需胺基酸。"},{"id":"q0941","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"The primary macronutrient that is addressed in the precompetition meal is","options":["fat","carbohydrate","protein","vitamin"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"carbohydrate","explanation_en":"Precompetition meals emphasize carbohydrates to top off glycogen and support high-intensity performance.","tags":["chapter-10"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"賽前餐點 (precompetition meal) 首要處理的巨量營養素是碳水化合物，目的是補滿肝糖、支撐高強度表現。"},{"id":"q0942","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"Which of the following makes the GREATEST contribution to total energy expenditure?","options":["resting metabolic rate","physical activity energy expenditure","thermic effect of food","resting blood sugar levels"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"resting metabolic rate","explanation_en":"Resting metabolic rate is typically the largest component of daily total energy expenditure for most people.","tags":["chapter-10"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"對多數人而言，靜息代謝率 (RMR) 是每日總能量消耗中佔比最大的部分，高於活動消耗與食物熱效應。"},{"id":"q0943","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"Which of the following is characteristic of anorexia nervosa?","options":["normal body weight","very low dietary fat intake","preoccupation with food","secretive eating"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"preoccupation with food","explanation_en":"A common feature is an intense preoccupation with food, body weight, and control of eating; normal body weight is not typical.","tags":["chapter-10"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"神經性食慾不振 (anorexia nervosa) 的典型特徵是對食物、體重與飲食控制的高度執著；患者體重通常明顯偏低，而非正常。"},{"id":"q0944","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":10,"question":"When an eating disorder is suspected, the strength and conditioning professional should","options":["monitor the athlete’s daily food intake","require frequent weigh-ins","encourage further assessment by an eating disorder specialist","provide nutritional information"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"encourage further assessment by an eating disorder specialist","explanation_en":"The appropriate step is referral/encouraging assessment by a qualified specialist; monitoring intake or weigh-ins can worsen the situation.","tags":["chapter-10"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"懷疑飲食失調時，體能教練的正確作為是轉介並鼓勵飲食失調專家進一步評估；直接盯飲食或頻繁量體重常使情況惡化，屬專家權責。"},{"id":"q0945","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Which of the following dietary supplements is (are) considered a stimulant?","options":["I and II","II and IV","III and IV","I and III"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"II and IV","explanation_en":"Caffeine and citrus aurantium are stimulants; creatine and HMB are not.","tags":["chapter-11"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"咖啡因 (caffeine) 與苦橙 (Citrus aurantium) 屬於興奮劑類補充品；肌酸與 HMB 不是興奮劑。"},{"id":"q0946","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Which of the following is NOT part of caffeine’s role in improving athletic performance?","options":["increased power production","decreased glycogen depletion","increased fat oxidation","decreased urine production"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"decreased urine production","explanation_en":"Caffeine does not decrease urine production; it may have mild diuretic effects, especially in non-habituated users.","tags":["chapter-11"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"咖啡因增能機制包括提高功率輸出、增加脂肪氧化、節省肝糖；「減少排尿」不屬於——咖啡因對未習慣者反而有利尿傾向。"},{"id":"q0947","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Which of the following is the BEST reason for aerobic endurance athletes to avoid erythropoietin use?","options":["Hematocrit and hemoglobin levels may decrease","It may cause an unregulated increase in red blood cell production","Resistance to infectious disease may be impaired","It may reduce the ability of the blood to carry oxygen"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"It may cause an unregulated increase in red blood cell production","explanation_en":"Erythropoietin can dangerously increase red blood cell mass, raising blood viscosity and cardiovascular risk.","tags":["chapter-11"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"促紅血球生成素 (erythropoietin, EPO) 的風險在於紅血球生成失去調節、血比容過高、血液黏稠度上升，提高心血管事件風險。"},{"id":"q0948","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Creatine supplementation improves all of the following variables EXCEPT","options":["lean body mass","maximal strength","endurance performance","power"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"endurance performance","explanation_en":"Creatine primarily improves strength, power, and lean mass, but not aerobic endurance performance.","tags":["chapter-11"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌酸 (creatine) 補充可提升去脂體重、最大肌力與功率，但對有氧耐力表現沒有明顯幫助。"},{"id":"q0949","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":11,"question":"Which of the following performance-enhancing substances is most likely to increase lean body mass?","options":["anabolic steroids","arginine","ephedrine","β-alanine"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"anabolic steroids","explanation_en":"Anabolic steroids directly stimulate muscle protein synthesis and increase lean body mass.","tags":["chapter-11"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"合成代謝類固醇 (anabolic steroids) 直接刺激肌肉蛋白質合成，最可能明顯增加去脂體重；精胺酸、麻黃素、β-丙胺酸都沒有這種直接效果。"},{"id":"q0950","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A college basketball coach would like to know which one of her players has the most muscular power. Which of the following is the MOST valid test for measuring muscular power?","options":["vertical jump","1RM bench press","5RM squat","100 m (109-yard) sprint"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"vertical jump","explanation_en":"The vertical jump directly measures explosive lower-body power, making it the most valid test of muscular power.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"垂直跳直接測量下肢爆發力，是選項中最符合「肌力功率」構唸的測驗；1RM 測最大肌力，100 碼衝刺測速度。"},{"id":"q0951","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"When measuring maximal strength of a soccer player, which of the following could potentially adversely affect the test–retest reliability of the results?\n\nI. using multiple testers\nII. retesting at a different time of day\nIII. an athlete’s inexperience with the tested exercise\nIV. using an established testing protocol","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"Multiple testers, different testing times, and athlete inexperience can all reduce test–retest reliability; established protocols improve reliability.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"多名測驗執行者、改在不同時段重測、運動員對動作不熟練，都會降低重測信度；採用既定標準化流程是提升信度，不是降低。"},{"id":"q0952","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"All of the following procedures should be followed when testing an athlete’s cardiovascular fitness in the heat EXCEPT","options":["performing the test in an indoor facility","using salt tablets to retain water","scheduling the test in the morning","drinking fluids during the test"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"using salt tablets to retain water","explanation_en":"Salt tablets are not recommended during testing due to the risk of electrolyte imbalance.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高溫環境下測心肺適能：改在室內、安排於上午、測驗中補充水分都正確；鹽片因可能造成電解質失衡，測驗情境下不建議。"},{"id":"q0953","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"The bench press, vertical jump, and 10 m (11-yard) sprint are the MOST valid tests for which of the following American football positions?","options":["quarterback","defensive back","wide receiver","defensive lineman"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"defensive lineman","explanation_en":"These tests assess strength, power, and short-distance acceleration—key performance qualities for defensive linemen.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"臥推、垂直跳、10 公尺衝刺測的是肌力、爆發力與短距離加速——防守線鋒 (defensive lineman) 最依賴這些素質。"},{"id":"q0954","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Which of the following sequences will produce the MOST reliable results?","options":["1RM power clean, T-test, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run, 1RM bench press","T-test, 1RM power clean, 1RM bench press, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run","1.5 mile (2.4 km) run, 1RM bench press, T-test, 1RM power clean","1RM bench press, 1RM power clean, T-test, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"T-test, 1RM power clean, 1RM bench press, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run","explanation_en":"Testing should proceed from least fatiguing to most fatiguing to maximize reliability.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"測驗順序應由最不易疲勞排到最易疲勞：敏捷 (T-test)→power (power clean)→肌力 (臥推 1RM)→最後才 1.5 英里跑；耐力跑最先跑會汙染後面所有成績。"},{"id":"q0955","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Which of the following tests is MOST appropriate for assessing lower-body power in a large group setting with limited equipment?","options":["countermovement vertical jump","1RM squat","Wingate anaerobic test","30-second Bosco jump test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"countermovement vertical jump","explanation_en":"The vertical jump is valid, time-efficient, and requires minimal equipment, making it ideal for large groups.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"反向垂直跳 (countermovement jump) 效度佳、快速、幾乎不需要器材，最適合大團體量測下肢功率；1RM 深蹲與 Wingate 都需要器材且耗時。"},{"id":"q0956","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"A strength coach wants to ensure high objectivity during testing. Which of the following practices BEST supports this goal?","options":["using the same tester for all athletes","using multiple testers for efficiency","allowing athletes to self-report scores","adjusting protocols based on athlete preference"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"using the same tester for all athletes","explanation_en":"Objectivity is maximized when the same tester administers and scores all tests using standardized procedures.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"客觀性 (objectivity) 的最佳做法是由同一位測驗者以標準化程式執行並計分所有運動員；多人執行、自行報成績、隨意改流程都會引入評分差異。"},{"id":"q0957","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"Which of the following factors MOST directly affects the validity of a test?","options":["whether the test measures the intended physical quality","the consistency of test administration","the number of trials performed","the familiarity of the athlete with the test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"whether the test measures the intended physical quality","explanation_en":"Validity refers to how well a test measures what it is intended to measure.","tags":["chapter-12"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"效度 (validity) 關乎測驗是否真的量到想量的身體素質；執行一致性屬信度，trial 數與熟悉度影響的是信度與表現。"},{"id":"q0958","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate test: Assessing maximal lower-body strength","options":["1RM squat","vertical jump","Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","T-test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1RM squat","explanation_en":"Test selection must align with the specific physical quality being assessed; the same test battery is not valid for all goals.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大下肢肌力應對應 1RM 深蹲——測驗選擇必須符合欲量測的素質；垂直跳測功率、T-test 測敏捷、Yo-Yo 測有氧。"},{"id":"q0959","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate test: Assessing lower-body explosive power","options":["1RM squat","vertical jump","Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","T-test"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"vertical jump","explanation_en":"Test selection must align with the specific physical quality being assessed; the same test battery is not valid for all goals.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"下肢爆發力應對應垂直跳；1RM 深蹲反映最大肌力而非出力速率。"},{"id":"q0960","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate test: Assessing change-of-direction ability","options":["1RM squat","vertical jump","Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","T-test"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"T-test","explanation_en":"Test selection must align with the specific physical quality being assessed; the same test battery is not valid for all goals.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"變向能力應對應 T-test，它包含衝刺、側滑、倒退與多次方向轉換。"},{"id":"q0961","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate test: Assessing intermittent aerobic capacity","options":["1RM squat","vertical jump","Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","T-test"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","explanation_en":"Test selection must align with the specific physical quality being assessed; the same test battery is not valid for all goals.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"間歇性有氧能力應對應 Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test，專為重複高強度間歇設計。"},{"id":"q0962","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate testing approach: Untrained adolescent athletes","options":["1RM testing","submaximal prediction testing","field-based aerobic testing","laboratory-based aerobic testing"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"submaximal prediction testing","explanation_en":"Appropriate test selection depends on training status, safety, resources, and required measurement precision.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"未受訓的青少年運動員宜用次最大負重預測 1RM，降低大負重下動作失控的風險，安全性與可行性兼顧。"},{"id":"q0963","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate testing approach: Elite powerlifters","options":["1RM testing","submaximal prediction testing","field-based aerobic testing","laboratory-based aerobic testing"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1RM testing","explanation_en":"Appropriate test selection depends on training status, safety, resources, and required measurement precision.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"精英舉重選手的技術與大負重適應成熟，適合直接 1RM 測驗，量測精確度最高。"},{"id":"q0964","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate testing approach: Large team with limited time and equipment","options":["1RM testing","submaximal prediction testing","field-based aerobic testing","laboratory-based aerobic testing"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"field-based aerobic testing","explanation_en":"Appropriate test selection depends on training status, safety, resources, and required measurement precision.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"人數多、時間與器材有限的大隊伍應選_field-based 場地有氧測驗，可批次施測、不依賴實驗室裝置。"},{"id":"q0965","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":12,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate testing approach: Research setting requiring high precision","options":["1RM testing","submaximal prediction testing","field-based aerobic testing","laboratory-based aerobic testing"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"laboratory-based aerobic testing","explanation_en":"Appropriate test selection depends on training status, safety, resources, and required measurement precision.","tags":["chapter-12","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"研究要求高精度時必須用實驗室有氧測驗 (如直接氣體分析)，精度遠高於場地表單測驗。"},{"id":"q0966","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Anaerobic capacity is quantified as the maximal power output achieved during activity lasting","options":["less than 10 seconds","30 to 90 seconds","2 to 3 minutes","longer than 5 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"30 to 90 seconds","explanation_en":"Anaerobic capacity reflects the ability to sustain high power primarily via glycolytic pathways, typically over ~30–90 seconds.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"無氧能力 (anaerobic capacity) 定義為在大約 30–90 秒的運動中能維持的最大功率輸出，主要由糖解系統供能。"},{"id":"q0967","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Which of the following tests is NOT used to measure maximum muscular power?","options":["Margaria-Kalamen test","vertical jump","40-yard (37 m) sprint","1RM power clean"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"40-yard (37 m) sprint","explanation_en":"A 40-yard sprint is primarily a measure of speed/acceleration; the others are used as muscular power assessments.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"40 碼衝刺量測的是速度與加速，不屬於最大肌力功率測驗；Margaria-Kalamen、垂直跳、1RM power clean 都是功率評估手段。"},{"id":"q0968","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Flexibility of which of these muscle groups or body areas is assessed during the sit-and-reach test?\n\nI. hamstrings\nII. erector spinae\nIII. lumbar spine\nIV. hip flexors","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"The sit-and-reach is intended to assess hamstring and lower-back (lumbar/erector spinae) flexibility.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"坐位體前屈評估腿後腱、豎脊肌與腰椎的柔軟度；髖屈肌不是此測驗的目標。"},{"id":"q0969","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Which of the following is a reason for a trial of the T-test to be disqualified (see figure 13.11)?","options":["touching the base of cone D","shuffling from cone C to cone D","crossing the feet from cone B to cone C","running forward from cone A to cone B"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"crossing the feet from cone B to cone C","explanation_en":"In the T-test, athletes must shuffle laterally without crossing the feet; crossing the feet is a disqualification.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"T-test 規定 B 到 C、C 到 D 必須側向滑步且不交叉雙腳；從 B 到 C  crossover 交叉腳即判失敗。"},{"id":"q0970","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"When compiling results from the volleyball team’s vertical jump testing, the strength and conditioning professional notices that most scores are similar, but there are three scores that are much higher than the rest. Which of the following measures of central tendency is most appropriate for this group?","options":["mean","median","mode","variance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"median","explanation_en":"With extreme high outliers, the median best represents central tendency because it is resistant to outliers.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"資料中有三個極端高分時，中位數 (median) 比平均數更能代表集中趨勢，因為它不受離群值拉扯。"},{"id":"q0971","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Which of the following statistical measures BEST describes the spread or dispersion of test scores around the mean?","options":["mean","median","standard deviation","percentile rank"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"standard deviation","explanation_en":"Standard deviation quantifies how much individual scores vary from the mean.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"標準差 (standard deviation) 描述成績圍繞平均數的離散程度；平均數、中位數是集中趨勢，百分等級是相對位置。"},{"id":"q0972","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"An athlete scores in the 90th percentile on a strength test. This indicates that the athlete performed better than","options":["90% of the population","10% of the population","90% of similar athletes","10% of similar athletes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"90% of the population","explanation_en":"A 90th percentile rank means the athlete outperformed 90% of the reference population.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第 90 百分等級表示該運動員的成績優於參照母體 90% 的人。"},{"id":"q0973","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"Which of the following BEST explains why normative data are important when interpreting test results?","options":["They eliminate the need for repeated testing","They allow comparison to a reference population","They improve the validity of the test","They reduce measurement error"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"They allow comparison to a reference population","explanation_en":"Normative data provide context by allowing an athlete’s performance to be compared to a relevant population.","tags":["chapter-13"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"常模資料 (normative data) 的價值在於提供參照母體，讓個人成績可以放在群體脈絡中解讀；它不會改善效度或減少測量誤差。"},{"id":"q0974","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate interpretation: An athlete scores in the 85th percentile on a power test","options":["performance is above average","performance is average","performance is below average","result is unreliable due to testing error"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"performance is above average","explanation_en":"Percentile ranks indicate relative performance, while large score variability suggests poor reliability.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率測驗第 85 百分等級：相對參照母體屬優於平均的表現。"},{"id":"q0975","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate interpretation: An athlete scores near the 50th percentile on a strength test","options":["performance is above average","performance is average","performance is below average","result is unreliable due to testing error"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"performance is average","explanation_en":"Percentile ranks indicate relative performance, while large score variability suggests poor reliability.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"接近第 50 百分等級即處於平均水準。"},{"id":"q0976","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate interpretation: An athlete scores in the 15th percentile on an agility test","options":["performance is above average","performance is average","performance is below average","result is unreliable due to testing error"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"performance is below average","explanation_en":"Percentile ranks indicate relative performance, while large score variability suggests poor reliability.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"敏捷測驗第 15 百分等級：落後於 85% 的參照者，屬低於平均。"},{"id":"q0977","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate interpretation: Test scores vary widely across repeated trials","options":["performance is above average","performance is average","performance is below average","result is unreliable due to testing error"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"result is unreliable due to testing error","explanation_en":"Percentile ranks indicate relative performance, while large score variability suggests poor reliability.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"重複測驗成績差異過大，表示測驗誤差大、結果不可靠，應先排除程式問題再解讀。"},{"id":"q0978","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate statistical measure: Describing the average performance of a normally distributed group","options":["mean","median","mode","standard deviation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"mean","explanation_en":"Each statistical measure serves a distinct purpose in summarizing and interpreting test results.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"常態分佈的團體用平均數 (mean) 描述平均表現最適當。"},{"id":"q0979","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate statistical measure: Describing central tendency in the presence of extreme outliers","options":["mean","median","mode","standard deviation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"median","explanation_en":"Each statistical measure serves a distinct purpose in summarizing and interpreting test results.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"存在極端離群值時，用中位數 (median) 描述集中趨勢較穩健。"},{"id":"q0980","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate statistical measure: Identifying the most frequently occurring score","options":["mean","median","mode","standard deviation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"mode","explanation_en":"Each statistical measure serves a distinct purpose in summarizing and interpreting test results.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"眾數 (mode) 是出現次數最多的成績。"},{"id":"q0981","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate statistical measure: Quantifying variability among test scores","options":["mean","median","mode","standard deviation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"standard deviation","explanation_en":"Each statistical measure serves a distinct purpose in summarizing and interpreting test results.","tags":["chapter-13","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"成績間變異程度以標準差 (standard deviation) 量化。"},{"id":"q0982","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which of the following is a nontemperature-related effect of a warm-up?","options":["enhanced neural function","disruption of transient connective tissue bonds","elevation of baseline oxygen consumption","increase in muscle temperature"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"enhanced neural function","explanation_en":"Enhanced neural function is a non-temperature-related benefit of warm-up; the other options are temperature-dependent.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"神經功能提升 (enhanced neural function) 屬熱身的非溫度效應；鬆動暫態結締組織鍵結、提高氧消耗基線都需要體溫上升才發生。"},{"id":"q0983","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"When stimulated during contract-relax PNF stretching, Golgi tendon organs allow the relaxation of the","options":["stretched muscle by contracting the reciprocal muscle","reciprocal muscle by contracting the stretched muscle","reciprocal muscle by its own contraction","stretched muscle by its own contraction"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"stretched muscle by its own contraction","explanation_en":"Autogenic inhibition occurs when contraction of the stretched muscle activates GTOs, causing that same muscle to relax.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"收縮-放鬆 (contract-relax) PNF 中，被伸展的肌肉自行收縮會啟用高基腱器官 (GTO)，透過自主抑制 (autogenic inhibition) 讓同一塊肌肉放鬆——不是靠拮抗肌收縮。"},{"id":"q0984","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which of the following stretching techniques decreases muscle spindle stimulation?","options":["dynamic","ballistic","static","passive"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"static","explanation_en":"Static stretching minimizes rapid changes in muscle length, reducing muscle spindle activation.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"靜態伸展不造成肌肉長度快速變化，因而降低肌梭刺激；彈震式與快速動態伸展反而會激發肌梭。"},{"id":"q0985","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Stimulation of muscle spindles induces a","options":["relaxation of GTOs","relaxation of the stretched muscle","contraction of the stretched muscle","contraction of the reciprocal muscle"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"contraction of the stretched muscle","explanation_en":"Muscle spindle activation triggers the stretch reflex, causing contraction of the stretched muscle.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌梭受刺激引發牽張反射，使被牽拉的肌肉本身收縮——這是對抗伸展的保護反應。"},{"id":"q0986","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"After performing the hold-relax with agonist contraction PNF stretch for the hamstrings, which of the following explains the resulting increase in flexibility?\n\nI. autogenic inhibition\nII. stretch inhibition\nIII. reciprocal inhibition\nIV. crossed-extensor inhibition","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":"Hold-relax with agonist contraction improves flexibility through autogenic inhibition and reciprocal inhibition.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"保持-放鬆搭配 agonist 收縮的 PNF 同時運用兩種機制：自主抑制 (GTO 讓被伸展肌放鬆) 與互動抑制 (收縮拮抗肌時被伸展肌被抑制放鬆)，即 I 與 III。"},{"id":"q0987","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which of the following stretching methods is MOST appropriate immediately prior to a power-based activity?","options":["static stretching","ballistic stretching","dynamic stretching","PNF stretching"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"dynamic stretching","explanation_en":"Dynamic stretching prepares the neuromuscular system without reducing force or power output.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"爆發性活動前應使用動態伸展：預備神經肌肉系統又不降低_force_輸出；長時間靜態伸展與 PNF 都可能短暫抑制功率。"},{"id":"q0988","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Performing prolonged static stretching immediately before maximal strength or power performance may result in","options":["increased rate of force development","decreased muscle-tendon stiffness","improved neuromuscular activation","increased motor unit synchronization"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"decreased muscle-tendon stiffness","explanation_en":"Static stretching reduces musculotendinous stiffness, which can impair force and power production.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大肌力或功率表現前做長時間靜態伸展，會降低肌肉-肌腱剛性 (stiffness)，削弱彈性儲能與力量傳導，不利出力。"},{"id":"q0989","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which of the following warm-up sequences is MOST appropriate for a collegiate sprinter?","options":["general aerobic activity → static stretching → sprint drills","general aerobic activity → dynamic stretching → sprint drills","static stretching → dynamic stretching → sprint drills","dynamic stretching → static stretching → sprint drills"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"general aerobic activity → dynamic stretching → sprint drills","explanation_en":"A proper warm-up progresses from general activity to dynamic movement before sport-specific drills.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"短跑選手的正確熱身序列：一般性有氧活動→動態伸展→衝刺專項練習；靜態伸展放在最前或中段都不恰當。"},{"id":"q0990","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which of the following best describes reciprocal inhibition?","options":["relaxation of a muscle following its own contraction","contraction of the agonist causing relaxation of the antagonist","simultaneous contraction of agonist and antagonist","inhibition of muscle spindle activity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"contraction of the agonist causing relaxation of the antagonist","explanation_en":"Reciprocal inhibition occurs when activation of the agonist causes relaxation of the antagonist muscle.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"互動抑制 (reciprocal inhibition)：主動肌 (agonist) 收縮時，其拮抗肌 (antagonist) 被抑制而放鬆。"},{"id":"q0991","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":14,"question":"Which stretching method is MOST effective for increasing range of motion but should be performed only with qualified supervision?","options":["static stretching","dynamic stretching","ballistic stretching","PNF stretching"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"PNF stretching","explanation_en":"PNF stretching is highly effective but requires proper technique and supervision to ensure safety.","tags":["chapter-14"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"PNF 伸展對增加關節活動度最有效，但操作技術要求高，應在合格人員督導下進行。"},{"id":"q0992","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following exercises requires a spotter?","options":["lat pulldown","wrist curl","barbell bench press","step-up"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"barbell bench press","explanation_en":"Barbell bench press requires a spotter due to the risk of being trapped under the load at failure.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"槓鈴臥推需要保護 (spotting)，因為力竭時運動員可能被槓鈴壓住無法脫身；滑輪下拉、腕彎屈、階梯上步風險低得多。"},{"id":"q0993","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"During which of the following exercises should a spotter’s hands be placed on the athlete’s forearms near the wrists?","options":["bench press","incline dumbbell bench press","upright row","lying barbell triceps extension"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"incline dumbbell bench press","explanation_en":"For incline dumbbell bench press, the spotter assists by supporting the athlete’s forearms near the wrists.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"上斜式啞鈴臥推的保護方式是保護者雙手放在運動員前臂靠近手腕處協助穩定；槓鈴動作才是直接扶槓。"},{"id":"q0994","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following grips should be used during the deadlift exercise?\n\nI. overhand\nII. closed\nIII. open\nIV. alternated","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and IV only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and IV only","explanation_en":"The deadlift requires a closed grip, which may be overhand or alternated; open grips are unsafe.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"硬舉必須使用閉握 (closed grip)，可採全正握或正反混握 (alternated)；開放式握法容易脫手，不安全。"},{"id":"q0995","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following is the correct foot pattern in the step-up exercise?","options":["step up left foot, step up right foot, step down left foot, step down right foot","step up right foot, step up left foot, step down left foot, step down right foot","step up left foot, step down left foot, step up right foot, step down right foot","step up right foot, step up left foot, step down right foot, step down left foot"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"step up right foot, step up left foot, step down right foot, step down left foot","explanation_en":"The athlete should step up and step down with the same lead foot before switching sides.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"階梯上步 (step-up) 的正確順序是原腳上、原腳下：右腳上、左腳上、右腳下、左腳下，再換邊；先上先下、同側進出。"},{"id":"q0996","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"The primary movement during the second pull phase of the power clean exercise is","options":["hip flexion","hip extension","knee flexion","dorsiflexion"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"hip extension","explanation_en":"The second pull of the power clean is characterized by explosive hip extension.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"power clean 第二階段拉 (second pull) 的主要動作是爆發性伸髖 (hip extension)，把負重向上加速。"},{"id":"q0997","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following exercises should NOT be spotted?","options":["back squat","bench press","power clean","incline barbell press"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"power clean","explanation_en":"Olympic lifts such as the power clean should not be spotted; failed lifts should be dropped safely.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"power clean 等奧式舉重動作不應由人保護：失敗時應直接向前丟槓 (drop)，保護者反而幹擾動作或被槓鈴波及。"},{"id":"q0998","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"When spotting a barbell back squat, where should the spotter be positioned?","options":["behind the lifter with hands under the rib cage","in front of the lifter with hands on the bar","to the side of the lifter near the hips","behind the lifter with hands near the torso"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"behind the lifter with hands near the torso","explanation_en":"For the back squat, the spotter stands behind the lifter with hands near the torso to assist upward movement if needed.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"保護槓鈴背蹲時應站在運動員身後、雙手靠近其軀幹，必要時協助把槓鈴撐起；站前面扶槓會擋路且無助於蹲起。"},{"id":"q0999","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following exercises typically requires two spotters, one on each side of the bar?","options":["bench press","overhead press","back squat with heavy loads","lat pulldown"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"back squat with heavy loads","explanation_en":"Heavy back squats often require two side spotters (and sometimes a rear spotter) for maximal safety.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"大重量背蹲通常需要雨名保護者分立槓鈴兩側，必要時再加一人從後方支援；臥推的標準保護是一人在槓後。"},{"id":"q1000","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following cues BEST ensures proper bar path during the bench press?","options":["lower the bar to the neck","keep elbows flared throughout the lift","lower the bar to mid-chest","press the bar in a straight vertical line"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"lower the bar to mid-chest","explanation_en":"Lowering the bar to the mid-chest promotes a safe and efficient bar path during the bench press.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"臥推應把槓鈴下放到胸部中段 (mid-chest)，維持安全有效的槓鈴軌跡；下放到頸部、全程肘部外翻都是常見錯誤。"},{"id":"q1001","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":15,"question":"Which of the following techniques is MOST important for ensuring safety during resistance training?","options":["training to failure on all sets","maintaining proper lifting technique","using advanced overload methods","minimizing rest intervals"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"maintaining proper lifting technique","explanation_en":"Proper lifting technique is the most critical factor in preventing injury during resistance training.","tags":["chapter-15"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"重量訓練安全最重要的單一因素是維持正確的舉發技術；每組練到力竭、高階超負荷法、縮短休息都是次要變因。"},{"id":"q1002","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"If during the tire flip the athlete’s hips rise faster than the shoulders during the initial pushing motion, what is an effective correction to give the athlete?","options":["Start with a higher hip position.","Keep the hips slightly below the shoulders in this position.","Lift the tire upward instead of driving it forward.","Push with the arms first."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Keep the hips slightly below the shoulders in this position.","explanation_en":"Keeping the hips slightly below the shoulders promotes proper force transfer and prevents excessive forward lean.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"翻輪胎 (tire flip) 起步_push_時臀部比肩膀上升太快，代表身體過度前傾、力傳遞變差；糾正口令是讓臀部維持略低於肩膀的高度再驅動。"},{"id":"q1003","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"If a strong athlete incorporates only unilateral training into his or her program, what might the strength and conditioning professional expect to happen?","options":["A bilateral facilitation will occur.","A bilateral deficit will be developed.","A reduction in bilateral asymmetries will occur.","Only unilateral strength will increase."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A bilateral deficit will be developed.","explanation_en":"Exclusive unilateral training can reduce bilateral neural adaptations, leading to a bilateral deficit.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"長期只做單側訓練會削弱兩側同時發力的神經適應，造成雙側虧損 (bilateral deficit)——雙側同時出力小於兩側各自出力之和。"},{"id":"q1004","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"With regard to core training, when is instability exercise best applied?","options":["with untrained athletes who are relatively weak","in trained athletes who are rehabilitating from an injury","with trained athletes who are trying to optimize strength and power","with untrained athletes who are new to the exercise"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"in trained athletes who are rehabilitating from an injury","explanation_en":"Instability training is best applied during rehabilitation to restore neuromuscular control, not to maximize force production.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"不穩定平面 (instability) 核心訓練最適合有訓練基礎、正從傷後復健的運動員，用來找回神經肌肉控制；追求最大力量與功率時它是幹擾因素。"},{"id":"q1005","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which of the following is a rationale for using variable-resistance training methods?","options":["to accommodate the changing mechanical advantages associated with constant-loaded exercises","to minimize force application throughout the full range of motion","to increase the time spent decelerating during a lifting motion","to keep the applied resistance constant during changes in joint angle"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"to accommodate the changing mechanical advantages associated with constant-loaded exercises","explanation_en":"Variable resistance accommodates the strength curve by matching resistance to mechanical advantage.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"可變阻力 (variable resistance，如彈力帶、鏈條) 的用意是配合固定負重動作改變的機械利益 (strength curve)，讓各關節角度都能接近出力上限。"},{"id":"q1006","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Training on instability devices can reduce the overall agonist force production capacity and power output of the athlete to less than ____ of what can be achieved in a stable condition.","options":["20%","50%","70%","90%"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"70%","explanation_en":"Instability training can reduce force and power output to less than 70% of stable conditions.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"在不穩定器材上訓練，主動肌的最大力量與功率輸出會掉到穩定狀態的 70% 以下。"},{"id":"q1007","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which of the following athletes would benefit MOST from unilateral resistance training?","options":["elite Olympic weightlifter","novice powerlifter","soccer player returning from unilateral injury","competitive bodybuilder"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"soccer player returning from unilateral injury","explanation_en":"Unilateral training is particularly beneficial for correcting asymmetries during return-to-play scenarios.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"單側傷後復出的足球員最需要單側訓練：糾正兩側不對稱、確認患側恢復程度。"},{"id":"q1008","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which of the following best describes the bilateral deficit?","options":["greater force production during bilateral movements compared to unilateral movements","reduced force production during bilateral movements compared to unilateral movements","equal force production regardless of movement pattern","a loss of muscle mass due to asymmetrical loading"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"reduced force production during bilateral movements compared to unilateral movements","explanation_en":"The bilateral deficit occurs when the combined unilateral force exceeds bilateral force output.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"雙側虧損 (bilateral deficit) 定義：單側個別出力加總後反而大於雙側同時出力。"},{"id":"q1009","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which of the following resistance training methods MOST effectively overloads the terminal range of motion?","options":["eccentric-only training","variable-resistance training","plyometric training","instability training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"variable-resistance training","explanation_en":"Variable resistance increases load where mechanical advantage is greatest, typically near lockout.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"可變阻力在機械利益最大處 (通常是接近鎖定的終端活動範圍) 提供最大負荷，是唯一能加重終端 ROM 的選項。"},{"id":"q1010","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which of the following is a primary limitation of instability resistance training?","options":["reduced muscle activation","increased injury risk","reduced force and power output","inability to improve balance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"reduced force and power output","explanation_en":"Instability training reduces the ability to generate high force and power due to compromised stability.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"不穩定阻力訓練的主要限制正是力量與功率輸出下降——穩定性不足限制了出力上限。"},{"id":"q1011","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":16,"question":"Which training method is MOST appropriate when the primary goal is to improve rate of force development?","options":["instability training","unilateral isolation training","variable-resistance training","slow eccentric training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"variable-resistance training","explanation_en":"Variable-resistance training supports rapid force production by matching resistance to the athlete’s strength curve.","tags":["chapter-16"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"可變阻力訓練讓負荷貼合strength curve、維持高速高功率輸出，對改善力量生成率 (RFD) 最適當。"},{"id":"q1012","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"The basketball coach says his starting center needs to jump higher. In addition to beginning a plyometric program, which of the following resistance training exercises are MOST specific to this goal?\n\nI. power clean\nII. leg (knee) curl\nIII. front squat\nIV. seated calf (heel) raise","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":"Power cleans and front squats are multijoint, explosive exercises that closely match the movement and force demands of jumping.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"power clean 與前蹲是多關節、爆發性、與起跳動作和受力特徵最接近的專項練習；腿彎屈與坐姿提踵是單關節輔助動作，特異性不足。"},{"id":"q1013","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"The soccer team is transitioning from off-season to preseason training. How should the team’s resistance training frequency be altered?","options":["Increase frequency to improve muscular endurance.","Do not change frequency and add plyometrics.","Decrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice.","Design a split routine with three days on and one day off."],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Decrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice.","explanation_en":"As preseason approaches, resistance training frequency typically decreases to allow more time for sport-specific practice.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"從 off-season 進入 preseason，重量訓練頻率應下調，把時間讓給專項技術與戰術練習；頻率上升會與場上訓練互相搶 Recovery。"},{"id":"q1014","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"An American football lineman has difficulty driving into defensive linemen and believes he has lost his explosive ability. Which of the following is the BEST exercise order to help this athlete improve his performance?","options":["back squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl, power clean","power clean, back squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl","leg (knee) curl, back squat, power clean, hip sled","hip sled, power clean, leg (knee) curl, back squat"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"power clean, back squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl","explanation_en":"Power exercises should be performed first, followed by strength and then assistance exercises.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"練習順序原則：爆發力動作 (power clean) 排最先，接著大肌群肌力動作 (back squat)，再排輔助動作 (hip sled、leg curl)。"},{"id":"q1015","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following volumes has the potential to increase muscular strength the MOST?","options":["5 sets of 5 repetitions","1 set of 5 repetitions","5 sets of 15 repetitions","1 set of 15 repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"5 sets of 5 repetitions","explanation_en":"Multiple sets of moderate repetitions provide the optimal stimulus for strength development.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"5 組×5 次能提供最大的肌力成長刺激；單組與高次數 (15 次) 組數不足或強度不足，肌力增益較小。"},{"id":"q1016","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"A female triathlete needs to improve the muscular endurance of her upper body. Using three sets of 15 repetitions per exercise, which of the following rest period lengths will MAXIMIZE her goal?","options":["3 minutes","1.5 minutes","45 seconds","30 seconds"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"30 seconds","explanation_en":"Short rest periods maximize metabolic stress and are most effective for improving muscular endurance.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌耐力目標下，30 秒的極短組間休息能最大化代謝壓力與區域性耐力適應；組間越長越偏重恢復與力量。"},{"id":"q1017","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following loading ranges is MOST appropriate for maximizing muscular power during resistance training?","options":["30–60% of 1RM","70–85% of 1RM","85–95% of 1RM","95–100% of 1RM"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"30–60% of 1RM","explanation_en":"Muscular power is maximized at relatively light-to-moderate loads moved explosively.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大化肌力功率宜用 30–60% 1RM 的輕中負重、以最快速度舉起 (力-速度曲線最高功率區)；85% 以上偏力量，功率反而低。"},{"id":"q1018","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes the recommended repetition range for maximizing muscular hypertrophy?","options":["1–3 repetitions","4–6 repetitions","6–12 repetitions","15–20 repetitions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"6–12 repetitions","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy is best stimulated using moderate repetition ranges that balance mechanical tension and metabolic stress.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"6–12 次的次數範圍兼顧機械張力與代謝壓力，是最大化肌肉肥大的建議範圍。"},{"id":"q1019","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following rest intervals is MOST appropriate for maximizing maximal strength?","options":["30 seconds","1 minute","2–3 minutes","5–6 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2–3 minutes","explanation_en":"Longer rest intervals (2–3 minutes) allow sufficient recovery for maximal force production.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大化最大肌力需要 2–3 分鐘休息，讓磷酸原系統恢復、維持後續組的高強度出力；30 秒到 1 分鐘恢復不足。"},{"id":"q1020","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate repetition range: Maximal muscular strength","options":["1–5 repetitions","6–12 repetitions","12–20 repetitions","20+ repetitions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1–5 repetitions","explanation_en":"Repetition ranges vary by training goal based on force demands, fatigue tolerance, and metabolic contribution.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大肌力對應 1–5 次的高強度低次數範圍。"},{"id":"q1021","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate repetition range: Muscular hypertrophy","options":["1–5 repetitions","6–12 repetitions","12–20 repetitions","20+ repetitions"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"6–12 repetitions","explanation_en":"Repetition ranges vary by training goal based on force demands, fatigue tolerance, and metabolic contribution.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌肉肥大對應 6–12 次範圍。"},{"id":"q1022","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate repetition range: Muscular endurance","options":["1–5 repetitions","6–12 repetitions","12–20 repetitions","20+ repetitions"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"12–20 repetitions","explanation_en":"Repetition ranges vary by training goal based on force demands, fatigue tolerance, and metabolic contribution.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌耐力對應 12–20 次的中低負重範圍。"},{"id":"q1023","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate repetition range: Local muscular endurance for untrained individuals","options":["1–5 repetitions","6–12 repetitions","12–20 repetitions","20+ repetitions"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"20+ repetitions","explanation_en":"Repetition ranges vary by training goal based on force demands, fatigue tolerance, and metabolic contribution.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"初學者的區域性肌肉耐力可用 20 次以上的低負重高次數，安全建立耐受度。"},{"id":"q1024","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate rest interval: Muscular endurance","options":["30–60 seconds","1–2 minutes","2–3 minutes","3–5 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"30–60 seconds","explanation_en":"Rest intervals must align with the energy system and neural demands of the training goal.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌耐力訓練的組間休息為 30–60 秒。"},{"id":"q1025","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate rest interval: Hypertrophy","options":["30–60 seconds","1–2 minutes","2–3 minutes","3–5 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1–2 minutes","explanation_en":"Rest intervals must align with the energy system and neural demands of the training goal.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練的組間休息為 1–2 分鐘。"},{"id":"q1026","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate rest interval: Maximal strength","options":["30–60 seconds","1–2 minutes","2–3 minutes","3–5 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2–3 minutes","explanation_en":"Rest intervals must align with the energy system and neural demands of the training goal.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大肌力訓練的組間休息為 2–3 分鐘。"},{"id":"q1027","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate rest interval: Power and Olympic-style lifts","options":["30–60 seconds","1–2 minutes","2–3 minutes","3–5 minutes"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"3–5 minutes","explanation_en":"Rest intervals must align with the energy system and neural demands of the training goal.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率與奧式舉動作需要 3–5 分鐘休息，確保磷酸原系統充分再合成、維持每次動作的爆發品質。"},{"id":"q1028","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training emphasis: Advanced powerlifter in the competitive phase","options":["high volume, moderate load","low volume, high load","moderate volume, explosive intent","very low volume, technical emphasis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"low volume, high load","explanation_en":"Training emphasis must be individualized based on experience level, sport demands, and phase of training.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"競賽期的進階舉重選手的重量訓練重點：低訓練量、高負荷——維持強度、控制疲勞。"},{"id":"q1029","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training emphasis: Basketball player emphasizing vertical jump performance","options":["high volume, moderate load","low volume, high load","moderate volume, explosive intent","very low volume, technical emphasis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"moderate volume, explosive intent","explanation_en":"Training emphasis must be individualized based on experience level, sport demands, and phase of training.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"以垂直跳為目標的籃球選手：中等訓練量搭配爆發意圖 (explosive intent)，貼合起跳的力-速度需求。"},{"id":"q1030","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training emphasis: Novice lifter learning proper technique","options":["high volume, moderate load","low volume, high load","moderate volume, explosive intent","very low volume, technical emphasis"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"very low volume, technical emphasis","explanation_en":"Training emphasis must be individualized based on experience level, sport demands, and phase of training.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"初學者學動作階段：極低訓練量、以技術為優先，先建立穩定動作模式。"},{"id":"q1031","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training emphasis: Bodybuilder in a hypertrophy-focused phase","options":["high volume, moderate load","low volume, high load","moderate volume, explosive intent","very low volume, technical emphasis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"high volume, moderate load","explanation_en":"Training emphasis must be individualized based on experience level, sport demands, and phase of training.","tags":["chapter-17","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"健美選手肥大期：高訓練量、中等負荷，累積機械張力與代謝壓力。"},{"id":"q1032","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following program variables should be manipulated FIRST when an athlete plateaus in maximal strength but continues to recover well?","options":["exercise selection","training frequency","training volume","movement velocity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"training volume","explanation_en":"Volume is typically adjusted first to increase overload before changing frequency or exercise selection.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大肌力停滯但恢復良好時，第一優先是調整訓練量 (加組/加次) 增加超負荷刺激，其次才是頻率或動作選擇。"},{"id":"q1033","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following resistance training approaches is MOST appropriate for an untrained individual beginning a general strength program?","options":["multiple-set periodized program","high-intensity daily max training","total-body routine 2–3 days per week","advanced split routine emphasizing muscle groups"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"total-body routine 2–3 days per week","explanation_en":"Untrained individuals respond best to simple total-body programs performed multiple times per week.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"未受訓者初學一般肌力訓練：每週 2–3 天的全身性 (total-body) 課表即可；分化式、每日極限重量都太複雜或太刺激。"},{"id":"q1034","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following exercises should be classified as an assistance exercise rather than a core lift?","options":["back squat","power clean","Romanian deadlift","leg (knee) curl"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"leg (knee) curl","explanation_en":"Assistance exercises are typically single-joint or less neurologically demanding movements used to support core lifts.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"leg curl 是單關節、神經需求低的輔助動作；背蹲、power clean、羅馬尼亞硬舉都是多關節核心動作。"},{"id":"q1035","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"When designing a resistance training program, which of the following factors MOST directly influences exercise order?","options":["muscle soreness","equipment availability","neural and technical demands","training age of the athlete"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"neural and technical demands","explanation_en":"Exercises requiring high neural drive and technical skill should be performed first while the athlete is fresh.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"動作順序主要由神經與技術需求決定：需要高神經驅動、高技巧的動作 (奧式舉、爆發動作) 放在精神最好的最前面。"},{"id":"q1036","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following changes would MOST increase training intensity without increasing training volume?","options":["adding additional sets","reducing rest intervals","increasing load lifted","adding additional exercises"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"increasing load lifted","explanation_en":"Training intensity refers to the load lifted relative to maximal capacity.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"強度=負重相對最大能力的比例，提高舉起的負重即可在不增加訓練量的前提下提高強度；加組、加動作、縮休息都動到量或密度。"},{"id":"q1037","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following is the PRIMARY reason resistance training frequency is reduced during the competitive season?","options":["to minimize muscle hypertrophy","to reduce neuromuscular fatigue","to eliminate strength gains","to increase training intensity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"to reduce neuromuscular fatigue","explanation_en":"Reduced frequency helps manage fatigue while preserving strength and power during competition.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"賽季中下調重量訓練頻率的主要目的是控制神經肌肉疲勞，同時維持肌力與功率，不是要消除肌力增益。"},{"id":"q1038","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Which of the following best describes the principle of training specificity?","options":["training adaptations occur regardless of exercise selection","adaptations are proportional to training volume","training adaptations are specific to the imposed demands","greater fatigue always results in greater adaptation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"training adaptations are specific to the imposed demands","explanation_en":"The principle of specificity states that adaptations closely match the demands placed on the athlete.","tags":["chapter-17"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"專項性原則 (specificity)：訓練適應與施加的刺激相符——練什麼得什麼，不是練多就有。"},{"id":"q1039","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a phase of the stretch-shortening cycle?","options":["amortization","concentric","eccentric","isometric"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"isometric","explanation_en":"The stretch-shortening cycle consists of eccentric, amortization, and concentric phases; isometric is not a phase.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"延長-短縮週期 (stretch-shortening cycle, SSC) 由離心期、緩衝期 (amortization)、向心期三期組成；等長不是其中一環。"},{"id":"q1040","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following structures detects rapid movement and initiates the stretch reflex?","options":["Golgi tendon organ","muscle spindle","extrafusal muscle fiber","Pacinian corpuscle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"muscle spindle","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles detect rapid stretch and initiate the stretch reflex.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌梭偵測快速牽張並啟動牽張反射，是增強式訓練依賴的感受器；GTO 反應的是張力。"},{"id":"q1041","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following should be assessed before beginning a lower body plyometric training program?\n\nI. balance\nII. strength\nIII. training history\nIV. lean body mass","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"Balance, strength, and training history are essential prerequisites for safe plyometric training.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"開始下肢增強式 (plyometric) 訓練前應評估：平衡、肌力、訓練史；去脂體重不是安全前提的主要指標。"},{"id":"q1042","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following types of plyometric drills is generally considered to be the MOST intense?","options":["jumps in place","bounds","depth jumps","box jumps"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"depth jumps","explanation_en":"Depth jumps involve high eccentric loading and rapid SSC utilization, making them the most intense.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深度跳 (depth jump) 落下的離心負荷最大、SSC 轉換最快，被視為最強度的增強式練習。"},{"id":"q1043","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following work-to-rest ratios is the MOST appropriate to assign to a plyometric training workout?","options":["1:5","1:4","1:3","1:2"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1:5","explanation_en":"Plyometric training requires long rest periods to maintain maximal power output.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練的工作-休息比約 1:5，充分休息才能維持每次動作的最大功率與品質。"},{"id":"q1044","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following strength benchmarks is generally recommended before initiating high-intensity lower-body plyometric training?","options":["1.0 × body weight back squat","1.25 × body weight back squat","1.5 × body weight back squat","2.0 × body weight back squat"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1.5 × body weight back squat","explanation_en":"A back squat of approximately 1.5 times body weight is commonly recommended before advanced lower-body plyometrics.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"進行高強度下肢增強式訓練前，建議先具備約 1.5 倍體重背蹲的強度基礎。"},{"id":"q1045","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following BEST explains why plyometric drills should be performed early in a training session?","options":["to increase metabolic fatigue","to maximize muscle hypertrophy","to ensure high movement quality and power output","to improve flexibility"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"to ensure high movement quality and power output","explanation_en":"Plyometrics require maximal neuromuscular output and technical precision, which are best achieved when fatigue is minimal.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"增強式動作需要最大神經肌肉輸出與精確技術，放在課表前段、疲勞最低時才能保證動作品質與效果。"},{"id":"q1046","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following training surfaces is MOST appropriate for plyometric training?","options":["concrete","asphalt","rubberized floor","tile"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"rubberized floor","explanation_en":"Rubberized or shock-absorbing surfaces reduce impact stress while allowing effective force transfer.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"橡膠地面等具緩衝的場地能降低衝擊壓力又允許有效施力，最適合增強式訓練；水泥、柏油、磁磚太硬。"},{"id":"q1047","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate intensity classification: ankle hops","options":["low intensity","moderate intensity","high intensity","very high intensity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"low intensity","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity increases with eccentric load, ground reaction force, and movement complexity.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"踝跳 (ankle hops) 屬低強度增強式；增強式強度隨離心負荷、地面反作用力與動作複雜度上升。"},{"id":"q1048","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate intensity classification: standing long jumps","options":["low intensity","moderate intensity","high intensity","very high intensity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"moderate intensity","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity increases with eccentric load, ground reaction force, and movement complexity.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"立定跳遠屬中等強度增強式動作。"},{"id":"q1049","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate intensity classification: bounds","options":["low intensity","moderate intensity","high intensity","very high intensity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"high intensity","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity increases with eccentric load, ground reaction force, and movement complexity.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跨步跳 (bounds) 離心負荷大、動作複雜，屬高強度。"},{"id":"q1050","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate intensity classification: depth jumps","options":["low intensity","moderate intensity","high intensity","very high intensity"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"very high intensity","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity increases with eccentric load, ground reaction force, and movement complexity.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深度跳 (depth jump) 屬極高強度，是強度分級的最高層。"},{"id":"q1051","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric emphasis: early off-season","options":["low-intensity, low-volume drills","moderate-intensity, moderate-volume drills","high-intensity, low-volume drills","very high-intensity drills with extended rest"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"low-intensity, low-volume drills","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity and volume must be periodized based on the athlete’s training phase and readiness.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"早期 off-season：低強度、低量動作建立增強式基礎與落地技術。"},{"id":"q1052","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric emphasis: late off-season","options":["low-intensity, low-volume drills","moderate-intensity, moderate-volume drills","high-intensity, low-volume drills","very high-intensity drills with extended rest"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"moderate-intensity, moderate-volume drills","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity and volume must be periodized based on the athlete’s training phase and readiness.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"後期 off-season：中等強度、中等量，逐步提升刺激。"},{"id":"q1053","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric emphasis: preseason","options":["low-intensity, low-volume drills","moderate-intensity, moderate-volume drills","high-intensity, low-volume drills","very high-intensity drills with extended rest"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"high-intensity, low-volume drills","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity and volume must be periodized based on the athlete’s training phase and readiness.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"preseason：高強度、低量，貼近比賽爆發需求並控制疲勞。"},{"id":"q1054","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric emphasis: in-season maintenance","options":["low-intensity, low-volume drills","moderate-intensity, moderate-volume drills","high-intensity, low-volume drills","very high-intensity drills with extended rest"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"very high-intensity drills with extended rest","explanation_en":"Plyometric intensity and volume must be periodized based on the athlete’s training phase and readiness.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"賽季維持：極高強度動作搭配充分休息與低量，維持神經適應而不過度累積疲勞。"},{"id":"q1055","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric volume: untrained or novice athlete","options":["40–60 foot contacts per session","60–100 foot contacts per session","100–140 foot contacts per session","greater than 140 foot contacts per session"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"40–60 foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Plyometric volume must be scaled to training status to maximize adaptation while minimizing injury risk.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"未受訓/初學者：每次 40–60 次腳部接觸 (foot contacts) 的低量起步。"},{"id":"q1056","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric volume: moderately trained athlete","options":["40–60 foot contacts per session","60–100 foot contacts per session","100–140 foot contacts per session","greater than 140 foot contacts per session"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"60–100 foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Plyometric volume must be scaled to training status to maximize adaptation while minimizing injury risk.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"中等訓練程度：每次 60–100 次腳部接觸。"},{"id":"q1057","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric volume: well-trained athlete","options":["40–60 foot contacts per session","60–100 foot contacts per session","100–140 foot contacts per session","greater than 140 foot contacts per session"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"100–140 foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Plyometric volume must be scaled to training status to maximize adaptation while minimizing injury risk.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"訓練有素者：每次 100–140 次腳部接觸。"},{"id":"q1058","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate plyometric volume: elite plyometric specialist","options":["40–60 foot contacts per session","60–100 foot contacts per session","100–140 foot contacts per session","greater than 140 foot contacts per session"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"greater than 140 foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Plyometric volume must be scaled to training status to maximize adaptation while minimizing injury risk.","tags":["chapter-18","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"精英增強式專項運動員：每次可超過 140 次腳部接觸。"},{"id":"q1059","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following factors MOST increases the injury risk associated with plyometric training?","options":["insufficient eccentric strength","excessive concentric strength","high aerobic capacity","advanced training age"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"insufficient eccentric strength","explanation_en":"Plyometrics place high eccentric demands on the musculoskeletal system; insufficient eccentric strength increases injury risk.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練對離心收縮要求極高；離心強度不足是受傷風險最直接升高的因素。"},{"id":"q1060","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following programming errors is MOST likely to reduce the effectiveness of plyometric training?","options":["performing drills after heavy resistance training","using shock-absorbing surfaces","using low training volumes initially","allowing full recovery between sets"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"performing drills after heavy resistance training","explanation_en":"Fatigue impairs neuromuscular output and movement quality, reducing plyometric effectiveness.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"把增強式排在大重量肌力訓練之後是最糟的安排之一：疲勞讓神經輸出與動作品質下降，每次接觸的爆發效果大打折扣。"},{"id":"q1061","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following adaptations is MOST directly targeted by plyometric training?","options":["maximal muscle hypertrophy","increased tendon stiffness and elastic energy utilization","capillary density increases","mitochondrial biogenesis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"increased tendon stiffness and elastic energy utilization","explanation_en":"Plyometrics enhance elastic energy storage and reuse via improved tendon stiffness and neuromuscular coordination.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練主要改善肌腱剛性與彈效能儲存再利用，並提升 SSC 的神經肌肉協調；肥大、微血管、粒線體都不是它的標的。"},{"id":"q1062","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":18,"question":"Which of the following statements BEST describes appropriate plyometric progression?","options":["increase intensity before volume","increase volume before intensity","increase both volume and intensity simultaneously","maintain constant volume while increasing intensity weekly"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"increase volume before intensity","explanation_en":"Safe plyometric progression begins with increased volume at lower intensities before advancing intensity.","tags":["chapter-18"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"增強式進度的安全原則：先在低強度下增加訓練量，再提升強度；同時拉量與強度最易受傷。"},{"id":"q1063","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"What does the term impulse refer to?","options":["the relationship between power and velocity","the relationship between acceleration and velocity","the relationship between force and velocity","the relationship between force and time"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"the relationship between force and time","explanation_en":"Impulse is defined as the product of force and the time over which it is applied.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"衝量 (impulse) 指作用力與其作用時間的乘積——力與時間的關係。"},{"id":"q1064","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Elite sprinters produce __________ forces in a __________ ground contact time as compared to their novice counterparts.","options":["larger, longer","similar, shorter","larger, shorter","smaller, longer"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"larger, shorter","explanation_en":"Elite sprinters apply larger forces in shorter ground contact times.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"精英短跑選手相較初學者能以更短的地面接觸時間施加更大的地面反作用力。"},{"id":"q1065","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"In upright sprinting, an athlete’s stride length is largely dependent on __________.","options":["the amount of vertical force produced during the stance phase","the athlete’s flexibility","the athlete’s stride rate","the amount of horizontal force produced during the toe-off of the stance phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"the amount of vertical force produced during the stance phase","explanation_en":"Stride length during upright sprinting is primarily influenced by vertical force production during stance.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":" upright 直姿勢奔跑時的步長主要由支撐期產生的垂直方向力決定；水平力主要影響加速階段的加速能力。"},{"id":"q1066","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Drills or tests that require the athlete to move rapidly in response to a stimulus such as a whistle, arrow, or opponent are best for measuring which of the following?","options":["change of direction","maneuverability","agility","acceleration"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"agility","explanation_en":"Agility involves reacting and changing movement in response to an external stimulus.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"依哨音、箭頭、對手等外部刺激快速移動的測驗測的是靈敏 (agility)——定義核心是對刺激做出反應；無預設訊號的變向屬 change of direction。"},{"id":"q1067","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Select the aspect of training that requires additional emphasis when the aim is to improve change-of-direction ability.","options":["strength","eccentric strength","reactive strength","rate of force development"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"eccentric strength","explanation_en":"Change-of-direction performance relies heavily on eccentric strength to decelerate the body effectively.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"變向能力依賴離心強度 (eccentric strength) 有效剎車減速再重新輸出，因此要特別加強離心訓練。"},{"id":"q1068","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Which of the following sprint phases places the greatest emphasis on horizontal force production?","options":["acceleration phase","maximum velocity phase","deceleration phase","recovery phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"acceleration phase","explanation_en":"Acceleration performance depends primarily on horizontal force application into the ground.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"加速階段 (acceleration phase) 最強調水平方向的地面施力；最大速度階段則垂直力佔比更高。"},{"id":"q1069","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Which of the following BEST distinguishes change-of-direction ability from agility?","options":["the presence of fatigue","the need for maximal speed","the requirement to react to an external stimulus","the number of direction changes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"the requirement to react to an external stimulus","explanation_en":"Agility requires reacting to an external stimulus, whereas change-of-direction ability does not.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"敏捷性(agility)與變向能力(change-of-direction speed)最大的差別在於敏捷需要對外來刺激做出反應，包含知覺與認知決策；變向能力則是預先規劃好的動作路線，沒有刺激反應成分。"},{"id":"q1070","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"Which of the following drills would be MOST appropriate for improving maximum velocity sprinting?","options":["sled sprints with heavy load","short hill sprints","flying 30 m sprints","zigzag cone drills"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"flying 30 m sprints","explanation_en":"Flying sprints allow athletes to train at or near maximal velocity with minimal acceleration demands.","tags":["chapter-19"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"飛行式衝刺(flying sprint，如飛行30公尺)讓選手在助跑段先達到極速再計時衝刺，訓練重點放在維持最高速。雪橇拖重物與短上坡衝刺偏向加速訓練，Z字形錐筒則偏向變向。"},{"id":"q1071","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training emphasis: initial acceleration","options":["horizontal force production","vertical force production","eccentric braking ability","reactive decision-making"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"horizontal force production","explanation_en":"Speed and agility qualities are differentiated by force direction, braking demands, and perceptual requirements.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"起步加速階段軀幹大幅前傾，訓練重點是水平方向的力量輸出(horizontal force production)，例如拖雪橇、爬坡衝刺，把力量往後下方壓入地面。"},{"id":"q1072","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training emphasis: maximum velocity sprinting","options":["horizontal force production","vertical force production","eccentric braking ability","reactive decision-making"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"vertical force production","explanation_en":"Speed and agility qualities are differentiated by force direction, braking demands, and perceptual requirements.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"到達最高速後軀幹轉為直立，此時表現取決於短時間內對地面施加垂直力量(vertical force production)的能力；垂直力量越大、觸地時間越短，速度越快。"},{"id":"q1073","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training emphasis: change-of-direction performance","options":["horizontal force production","vertical force production","eccentric braking ability","reactive decision-making"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"eccentric braking ability","explanation_en":"Speed and agility qualities are differentiated by force direction, braking demands, and perceptual requirements.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"變向前必須先用離心收縮煞車(eccentric braking)吸收往前動能，才能往新方向蹬出；離心煞車能力直接決定變向的銳利程度。"},{"id":"q1074","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training emphasis: agility performance","options":["horizontal force production","vertical force production","eccentric braking ability","reactive decision-making"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"reactive decision-making","explanation_en":"Speed and agility qualities are differentiated by force direction, braking demands, and perceptual requirements.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"敏捷表現包含知覺認知成分，選手要觀察、解讀並針對刺激(對手、球)做反應性決策(reactive decision-making)，這是它與預劃路線變向的關鍵差別。"},{"id":"q1075","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training outcome: sled sprint with moderate load","options":["acceleration","maximum velocity","change-of-direction","agility"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"acceleration","explanation_en":"Each drill emphasizes a distinct speed or movement quality based on force direction and stimulus involvement.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"中等負荷拖雪橇衝刺增加蹬地阻力、拉長支撐時間，強化水平力量輸出，主要訓練效果是加速能力(acceleration)。"},{"id":"q1076","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training outcome: flying sprint","options":["acceleration","maximum velocity","change-of-direction","agility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"maximum velocity","explanation_en":"Each drill emphasizes a distinct speed or movement quality based on force direction and stimulus involvement.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"飛行式衝刺以完整助跑進入極速區段，跳過加速需求，主要訓練效果是最高速(maximum velocity)的維持。"},{"id":"q1077","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training outcome: 5-10-5 shuttle run","options":["acceleration","maximum velocity","change-of-direction","agility"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"change-of-direction","explanation_en":"Each drill emphasizes a distinct speed or movement quality based on force direction and stimulus involvement.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"5-10-5折返跑(20碼穿梭跑)的路線完全預劃，包含前衝、側移與倒退的多次變向，主要發展與評估預劃性變向速度，不含外部刺激。"},{"id":"q1078","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training outcome: mirror drill with a partner","options":["acceleration","maximum velocity","change-of-direction","agility"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"agility","explanation_en":"Each drill emphasizes a distinct speed or movement quality based on force direction and stimulus involvement.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"映象演練(mirror drill)要跟隨搭檔的隨機動作即時反應，必須解讀對手的動作線索再決定自己的移動，是典型的敏捷刺激-反應訓練。"},{"id":"q1079","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate option: improving first-step quickness","options":["rate of force development","eccentric strength","maximum force production","movement reactivity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"rate of force development","explanation_en":"Different speed and agility outcomes depend on distinct neuromuscular qualities.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第一步的快速程度取決於短時間內產生力量的速度，即力量生成速率(RFD， rate of force development)；RFD越高，起步蹬地越快。"},{"id":"q1080","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate option: improving rapid deceleration","options":["rate of force development","eccentric strength","maximum force production","movement reactivity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"eccentric strength","explanation_en":"Different speed and agility outcomes depend on distinct neuromuscular qualities.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"快速減速依靠肌肉以離心收縮吸收動能，離心力量(eccentric strength)越強，煞車能力越好，也是保護關節、降低傷害的關鍵。"},{"id":"q1081","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate option: improving sprint acceleration against resistance","options":["rate of force development","eccentric strength","maximum force production","movement reactivity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"maximum force production","explanation_en":"Different speed and agility outcomes depend on distinct neuromuscular qualities.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"阻力衝刺(如重雪橇)提高每一步所需的蹬地力量，其表現基礎是最大力量產出(maximum force production)，需先建立足夠的最大力量再談轉換。"},{"id":"q1082","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":19,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate option: improving sport-specific agility","options":["rate of force development","eccentric strength","maximum force production","movement reactivity"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"movement reactivity","explanation_en":"Different speed and agility outcomes depend on distinct neuromuscular qualities.","tags":["chapter-19","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"專項敏捷要求針對比賽情境快速切換與修正動作，核心是動作反應性(movement reactivity)，包括降低重心、快速重新施力的能力。"},{"id":"q1083","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following adaptations occur as an outcome of an aerobic endurance training program?\n\nI. increased oxygen delivery to working tissues\nII. higher rate of aerobic energy production\nIII. greater utilization of fat as a fuel source\nIV. increased disturbance of the acid–base balance","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I, II, and III only","explanation_en":"Aerobic endurance training improves oxygen delivery, aerobic energy production, and fat utilization, while reducing acid–base disturbance.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力訓練會提升輸氧能力(I)、有氧能量產出速率(II)與脂肪作為燃料的比例(III)；酸鹼平衡的擾動(IV)是減小而非增大，所以正確組合是I、II、III。"},{"id":"q1084","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following types of training is conducted at an intensity equal to the lactate threshold?","options":["pace/tempo","interval","high-intensity interval training (HIIT)","Fartlek"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"pace/tempo","explanation_en":"Pace/tempo training is designed to be performed at or near the lactate threshold.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"配速/節奏訓練(pace/tempo)的強度就落在乳酸閾值(lactate threshold)附近，讓身體在乳酸生成與清除達到平衡的強度下持續運動。"},{"id":"q1085","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following is the method most commonly used to assign and regulate exercise intensity?","options":["oxygen consumption","heart rate","ratings of perceived exertion","race pace"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"heart rate","explanation_en":"Heart rate is the most commonly used method for prescribing and monitoring aerobic exercise intensity.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"心率(heart rate)測量客觀、裝置簡單，是最常用來處方與監控有氧強度的方法；自覺用力度(RPE)主觀，攝氧量量測需要實驗室裝置。"},{"id":"q1086","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"The loss of physiological adaptations upon the cessation of training is an example of","options":["specificity of training","cross-training","detraining","tapering"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"detraining","explanation_en":"Detraining refers to the loss of adaptations when training stimulus is reduced or removed.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"停止或減少訓練後，已獲得的生理適應逐漸消失，稱為去訓練化(detraining)，對應可逆性原則。"},{"id":"q1087","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"The longest aerobic endurance training sessions should be performed during which of the following sport seasons?","options":["postseason","preseason","in-season","off-season"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"off-season","explanation_en":"The off-season is best suited for long-duration aerobic training to build a base.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"休賽季(off-season)沒有比賽壓力、可支配時間最多，適合安排時間最長的有氧訓練(長距離慢速跑)來建立有氧基礎。"},{"id":"q1088","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which physiological adaptation is MOST responsible for improvements in aerobic endurance performance?","options":["increased muscle fiber pennation angle","increased mitochondrial density","greater fast-twitch fiber recruitment","increased anaerobic enzyme activity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"increased mitochondrial density","explanation_en":"Increased mitochondrial density enhances aerobic ATP production and is a primary driver of endurance performance.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"粒線體(mitochondria)密度增加提升有氧三磷酸腺苷(ATP)產出能力，是有氧耐力表現進步最主要的生理適應；羽狀角與快肌徵招偏向力量表現。"},{"id":"q1089","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes the primary goal of tempo (lactate threshold) training?","options":["maximize fat oxidation at low intensity","delay the onset of blood lactate accumulation","increase maximal anaerobic power","improve phosphagen system recovery"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"delay the onset of blood lactate accumulation","explanation_en":"Tempo training improves the athlete’s ability to sustain higher intensities before lactate accumulation increases.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"節奏(乳酸閾值)訓練的主要目標是延後血乳酸堆積的出現(提高乳酸閾值)，讓選手在更高強度下仍能維持配速而不過早疲勞。"},{"id":"q1090","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following changes is MOST likely to occur following aerobic detraining?","options":["increase in capillary density","increase in stroke volume","decrease in VO₂max","increase in lactate threshold"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"decrease in VO₂max","explanation_en":"VO₂max declines rapidly during detraining due to reductions in plasma volume and mitochondrial adaptations.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"停止訓練後血漿量與每搏輸出量最先下降，最大攝氧量(VO2max)因此快速下滑；微血管密度與粒線體功能也會退化，不會增加。"},{"id":"q1091","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following methods is MOST appropriate for monitoring aerobic training intensity in large team settings?","options":["blood lactate sampling","oxygen consumption testing","heart rate monitoring","muscle biopsy"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"heart rate monitoring","explanation_en":"Heart rate monitoring is practical, cost-effective, and scalable for team-based aerobic training.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"心率監測(心率帶)可一次監控整隊、成本低且即時，最適合大團隊的有氧強度監控；血乳酸抽樣與攝氧量量測需要實驗室與高單價裝置。"},{"id":"q1092","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training method: Building an aerobic base in the off-season","options":["long slow distance","tempo (lactate threshold)","interval training","high-intensity interval training"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"long slow distance","explanation_en":"Aerobic training methods must align with the athlete’s goal, time constraints, and training phase.","tags":["chapter-20","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"休賽季建立有氧基礎對應長距離慢速跑(long slow distance， LSD)，以中低強度、長時間、連續進行的方式發展有氧能力。"},{"id":"q1093","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training method: Improving sustainable race pace","options":["long slow distance","tempo (lactate threshold)","interval training","high-intensity interval training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"tempo (lactate threshold)","explanation_en":"Aerobic training methods must align with the athlete’s goal, time constraints, and training phase.","tags":["chapter-20","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"改善可持續的比賽配速對應節奏(乳酸閾值)訓練，在乳酸閾值強度附近反覆練習，提升能長時間維持的高強度。"},{"id":"q1094","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training method: Increasing VO₂max in trained athletes","options":["long slow distance","tempo (lactate threshold)","interval training","high-intensity interval training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"interval training","explanation_en":"Aerobic training methods must align with the athlete’s goal, time constraints, and training phase.","tags":["chapter-20","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"已訓練選手要提升VO2max，需使用接近VO2max強度的間歇訓練(interval training)；長距離慢速跑對已訓練者的刺激不足。"},{"id":"q1095","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate training method: Time-efficient conditioning with metabolic stress","options":["long slow distance","tempo (lactate threshold)","interval training","high-intensity interval training"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"high-intensity interval training","explanation_en":"Aerobic training methods must align with the athlete’s goal, time constraints, and training phase.","tags":["chapter-20","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高強度間歇訓練(HIIT)時間效率最高，短時間內以高強度間歇製造明顯的代謝壓力，適合時間受限的體能安排。"},{"id":"q1096","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":20,"question":"Which of the following errors is MOST likely to compromise aerobic endurance adaptations?","options":["performing aerobic training at intensities that are too high too frequently","training primarily in the off-season","monitoring heart rate during training","including recovery days between sessions"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"performing aerobic training at intensities that are too high too frequently","explanation_en":"Excessive high-intensity aerobic training interferes with recovery and limits endurance adaptations.","tags":["chapter-20"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高強度有氧課的比例太高、恢復不足，會幹擾適應並壓縮低強度有氧量，最傷害有氧耐力發展；監控心率與安排恢復日反而是正確做法。"},{"id":"q1097","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"During which stage of the General Adaptation Syndrome does the body physiologically adapt to heavier training loads?","options":["alarm","resistance","exhaustion","restoration"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"resistance","explanation_en":"During the resistance stage, the body adapts to the imposed training stress.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"一般適應症候群(GAS)分為警告、抵抗、衰竭三期；抵抗期(resistance stage)身體對訓練壓力產生生理適應，對應週期化中逐步增加負荷的設計。"},{"id":"q1098","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"When relating the season terminology to periodization periods, which season corresponds to the preparatory period of training?","options":["in-season","preseason","off-season","postseason"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"off-season","explanation_en":"The preparatory period corresponds to the off-season.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"週期化的準備期(preparatory period)對應休賽季(off-season)，此時以建立基礎體能與肌力為主，沒有比賽幹擾。"},{"id":"q1099","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"During which of the following periods are sport-specific activities performed in the greatest volume?","options":["preparatory","first transition","competition","second transition"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"competition","explanation_en":"Sport-specific activities are highest during the competition period.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"比賽期(competition period)的專項運動活動量最大，訓練內容最貼近專項的動作模式、節奏與強度。"},{"id":"q1100","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"The medium-sized training cycle that lasts two to six weeks in duration is referred to as a\n\nI. block of training\nII. macrocycle\nIII. microcycle\nIV. mesocycle","options":["II and III only","I and IV only","I, II, and IV only","III and IV only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"I and IV only","explanation_en":"A mesocycle (and training block) typically lasts two to six weeks.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"持續2至6週的中等訓練週期是中週期(mesocycle)，同樣的週期也常被稱為一個訓練區塊(training block)；巨週期為數月至一年，微週期約為一週。"},{"id":"q1101","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Which of the following phases is (are) commonly used to vary workouts during the preparatory period?\n\nI. hypertrophy\nII. cardiovascular\nIII. basic strength\nIV. supercompensation","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy and basic strength phases are commonly used during the preparatory period.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"準備期常用的訓練階段是肥大期(hypertrophy)與基礎力量期(basic strength)；「心血管」與「超補償」不是準備期的標準階段名稱。"},{"id":"q1102","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes the primary purpose of periodization?","options":["to maximize fatigue throughout the season","to vary training variables to optimize long-term performance","to prevent all forms of overtraining","to maintain constant training intensity year-round"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"to vary training variables to optimize long-term performance","explanation_en":"Periodization systematically varies training variables to maximize performance and manage fatigue over time.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"週期化(periodization)的主要目的是系統性地變化訓練變數(量、強度、動作選擇)，長期最佳化表現並在比賽時達到巔峰，而不是全年維持固定強度。"},{"id":"q1103","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Which of the following BEST explains why training volume typically decreases as competition approaches?","options":["to improve aerobic capacity","to reduce injury risk from resistance training","to allow peak performance and recovery","to increase sport skill complexity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"to allow peak performance and recovery","explanation_en":"Reducing volume allows recovery and expression of maximal performance during competition.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"越接近比賽越降低訓練量，是為了消除累積疲勞、讓先前訓練建立的適應以尖峰表現(peak performance)展現，這是減量(peaking)的原理。"},{"id":"q1104","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"Which of the following training variables is MOST often manipulated first during periodized program design?","options":["exercise selection","training frequency","training volume","rest interval"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"training volume","explanation_en":"Training volume is typically adjusted first to manage overall workload and fatigue.","tags":["chapter-21"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"調整訓練計畫時通常最先操作訓練量(volume)，用總量控制整體負荷與疲勞，再調整強度、頻率與動作選擇。"},{"id":"q1105","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training emphasis: early preparatory period","options":["high volume, low intensity","moderate volume, moderate intensity","low volume, high intensity","very low volume, maintenance emphasis"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"high volume, low intensity","explanation_en":"Training emphasis shifts across periods to develop fitness qualities early and peak performance during competition.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"準備早期以建立基礎為主，安排高訓練量、低強度(如肥大期)；強度會隨著週期推進逐步提高。"},{"id":"q1106","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training emphasis: late preparatory period","options":["high volume, low intensity","moderate volume, moderate intensity","low volume, high intensity","very low volume, maintenance emphasis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"moderate volume, moderate intensity","explanation_en":"Training emphasis shifts across periods to develop fitness qualities early and peak performance during competition.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"準備後期過渡到基礎力量/力量期，訓練量適度下降、強度上升，以中等量、中等強度為主。"},{"id":"q1107","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training emphasis: competition period","options":["high volume, low intensity","moderate volume, moderate intensity","low volume, high intensity","very low volume, maintenance emphasis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"low volume, high intensity","explanation_en":"Training emphasis shifts across periods to develop fitness qualities early and peak performance during competition.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"比賽期以低量、高強度維持神經與專項表現，同時控制疲勞，避免影響比賽。"},{"id":"q1108","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate primary training emphasis: transition period","options":["high volume, low intensity","moderate volume, moderate intensity","low volume, high intensity","very low volume, maintenance emphasis"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"very low volume, maintenance emphasis","explanation_en":"Training emphasis shifts across periods to develop fitness qualities early and peak performance during competition.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"過渡期(transition period)以極低訓練量、維持性活動為主，讓身體與心理從賽季壓力中恢復。"},{"id":"q1109","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate periodization model: novice athlete with a long off-season","options":["linear periodization","undulating periodization","block periodization","nonperiodized training"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"linear periodization","explanation_en":"Periodization model selection depends on training status, competitive schedule, and performance goals.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"初學者搭配長休賽季適合線性(傳統)週期化：強度漸進上升、量漸進下降，進度穩定，技術學習曲線平緩。"},{"id":"q1110","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate periodization model: experienced athlete requiring frequent variation","options":["linear periodization","undulating periodization","block periodization","nonperiodized training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"undulating periodization","explanation_en":"Periodization model selection depends on training status, competitive schedule, and performance goals.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"資深選手需要高頻率變化以避免停滯，適合波動式(非線性)週期化，在每日或每週層面交替強度與量。"},{"id":"q1111","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate periodization model: elite athlete targeting a specific performance peak","options":["linear periodization","undulating periodization","block periodization","nonperiodized training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"block periodization","explanation_en":"Periodization model selection depends on training status, competitive schedule, and performance goals.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"以單一特定比賽巔峰為目標的精英選手，適合區塊式(block)週期化：每個區塊集中發展少數體能屬性，再依序轉換。"},{"id":"q1112","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate periodization model: recreational athlete training inconsistently","options":["linear periodization","undulating periodization","block periodization","nonperiodized training"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"nonperiodized training","explanation_en":"Periodization model selection depends on training status, competitive schedule, and performance goals.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"課表不固定的休閒型選手無法執行嚴謹週期，非週期化(nonperiodized)的一致化訓練更符合其實際狀況。"},{"id":"q1113","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training frequency: off-season","options":["4–6 days per week","3–4 days per week","2–3 days per week","1–2 days per week"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"4–6 days per week","explanation_en":"Resistance training frequency decreases as sport-specific demands increase across the season.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"休賽季抗阻訓練是重點，頻率最高，每週4至6天；之後隨著專項與比賽需求增加，抗阻頻率逐季遞減。"},{"id":"q1114","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training frequency: preseason","options":["4–6 days per week","3–4 days per week","2–3 days per week","1–2 days per week"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3–4 days per week","explanation_en":"Resistance training frequency decreases as sport-specific demands increase across the season.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"季前須撥出時間給專項訓練與戰術，抗阻訓練頻率降至每週3至4天，同時繼續力量與功率發展。"},{"id":"q1115","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training frequency: in-season","options":["4–6 days per week","3–4 days per week","2–3 days per week","1–2 days per week"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2–3 days per week","explanation_en":"Resistance training frequency decreases as sport-specific demands increase across the season.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"賽季中以維持與恢復為主，抗阻訓練每週2至3天即可，避免幹擾比賽與造成過度疲勞。"},{"id":"q1116","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate resistance training frequency: postseason / transition","options":["4–6 days per week","3–4 days per week","2–3 days per week","1–2 days per week"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"1–2 days per week","explanation_en":"Resistance training frequency decreases as sport-specific demands increase across the season.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"季後/過渡期以每週1至2天的低量維持，或暫時停止正式抗阻訓練，讓身體徹底恢復。"},{"id":"q1117","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate phase emphasis during the preparatory period: increasing muscle cross-sectional area","options":["hypertrophy","basic strength","power","active recovery"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"hypertrophy","explanation_en":"Each preparatory phase targets a distinct adaptation that contributes to long-term performance.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"要增加肌肉橫截面積，對應準備期的肥大期(hypertrophy phase)，使用中等負荷、較高的次數與組數。"},{"id":"q1118","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate phase emphasis during the preparatory period: improving maximal force production","options":["hypertrophy","basic strength","power","active recovery"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"basic strength","explanation_en":"Each preparatory phase targets a distinct adaptation that contributes to long-term performance.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"提升最大力量產出對應基礎力量期(basic strength)，使用較高負荷、較低次數的大重量訓練。"},{"id":"q1119","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate phase emphasis during the preparatory period: converting strength to sport performance","options":["hypertrophy","basic strength","power","active recovery"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"power","explanation_en":"Each preparatory phase targets a distinct adaptation that contributes to long-term performance.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"把已建立的力量轉換成專項表現是力量期(power phase)的任務，以快速、爆發性動作(如奧林匹克舉、彈震訓練)訓練功率輸出。"},{"id":"q1120","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":21,"question":"For the following scenario, select the MOST appropriate phase emphasis during the preparatory period: reducing accumulated fatigue","options":["hypertrophy","basic strength","power","active recovery"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"active recovery","explanation_en":"Each preparatory phase targets a distinct adaptation that contributes to long-term performance.","tags":["chapter-21","shared-answer-bank"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"減輕累積疲勞對應主動恢復(active recovery)，以低強度活動促進迴圈與修復，而不是完全臥床或繼續高量訓練。"},{"id":"q1121","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"All of the following individuals can provide medical supervision during a college soccer match EXCEPT the","options":["athletic trainer","team physician","Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist","Sports Certified Physical Therapist"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist","explanation_en":"A Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist does not provide medical supervision during competition.","tags":["chapter-22"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"比賽中的醫療監督由具醫療資格的人員負責，包含隊醫、認證運動保護員與物理治療師；CSCS的專業是訓練而非醫療實務，不擔任醫療監督角色。"},{"id":"q1122","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Which of the following is NOT typically the result of overuse?","options":["stress fracture","grade III joint sprain","tendinitis","microtraumatic injury"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"grade III joint sprain","explanation_en":"Grade III sprains are severe acute injuries and are not typically caused by overuse.","tags":["chapter-22"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第三級關節扭傷(韌帶完全斷裂)屬於突然發生的急性創傷；應力性骨折、肌腱炎與微創傷型傷害都是長期反覆負荷造成的過度使用傷害。"},{"id":"q1123","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Which of the following is NOT one of the phases of healing following an injury?","options":["inflammatory response","reconditioning hypertrophy","maturation-remodeling","fibroblastic repair"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"reconditioning hypertrophy","explanation_en":"Reconditioning hypertrophy is not a biological phase of tissue healing.","tags":["chapter-22"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"組織癒合的三個生物階段是發炎反應、纖維母修復與成熟重塑；「再製肥大」(reconditioning hypertrophy)是復健後期的訓練概念，不屬於生物性癒合階段。"},{"id":"q1124","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"Which of the following types of activity is inappropriate during the inflammatory response phase of a medial collateral ligament sprain?","options":["lower extremity plyometrics","submaximal isometric quadriceps strengthening","hip joint stretching","upper extremity ergometry"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"lower extremity plyometrics","explanation_en":"High-impact plyometrics are inappropriate during the inflammatory phase of ligament healing.","tags":["chapter-22"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"內側副韌帶扭傷的發炎期應避免高衝擊、高拉扯的負荷；下肢彈震訓練落地衝擊大，會加重膝關節內側壓力，不合適。次最大等長訓練、上肢功率車與髖部伸展都可接受。"},{"id":"q1125","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":22,"question":"The rotator cuff muscles act as stabilizers to the shoulder joint. During the maturation-remodeling phase of rotator cuff (supraspinatus muscle) tendinitis rehabilitation of a basketball player, what exercise repetition range is MOST appropriate for improving the muscular endurance of the rotator cuff muscles?","options":["3–5","5–8","8–12","12–20"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"12–20","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance adaptations are best achieved using higher repetition ranges such as 12–20.","tags":["chapter-22"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"棘上肌肌腱炎復健進入成熟重塑期後，目標是旋轉肌袖的肌耐力，應使用輕負荷高次數，12至20下的次數範圍最能發展肌耐力。"},{"id":"q1126","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":23,"question":"What is the order of the four phases involved in designing a new strength and conditioning facility?","options":["construction, predesign, design, preparation","preparation, design, construction, predesign","predesign, construction, design, preparation","predesign, design, construction, preparation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"predesign, design, construction, preparation","explanation_en":"The correct sequence is predesign, design, construction, and preparation.","tags":["chapter-23"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"新建肌力與體能設施的四個階段依序為：預設計(predesign)→設計(design)→施工(construction)→準備(preparation)，順序需牢記。"},{"id":"q1127","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":23,"question":"A master plan should be created in which of the following phases?","options":["predesign phase","design phase","construction phase","preparation phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"predesign phase","explanation_en":"The master plan is developed during the predesign phase.","tags":["chapter-23"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"總計畫(master plan)在預設計階段擬定，內容包含設施長期發展遠景、需求評估與法規調查，作為後續設計與施工的依據。"},{"id":"q1128","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":23,"question":"What is the recommended minimum distance between the floor and the bottom of mirrors on the walls?","options":["16 inches (41 cm)","18 inches (46 cm)","20 inches (51 cm)","22 inches (56 cm)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"20 inches (51 cm)","explanation_en":"Mirrors should be placed at least 20 inches above the floor for safety.","tags":["chapter-23"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"牆面鏡子的下緣距離地面至少20英吋(51公分)，避免器材撞擊鏡面，也預留牆體固定與安全緩衝空間。"},{"id":"q1129","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":23,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a key consideration when determining the space requirements of a college strength and conditioning facility?","options":["accessibility for the athletes","amount and type of equipment","number of athletes using the facility","number of athletic teams desiring to use the facility"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"number of athletic teams desiring to use the facility","explanation_en":"Facility design is based on athlete numbers and usage, not the number of teams requesting access.","tags":["chapter-23"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"設施空間需求取決於使用人數、器材數量與種類以及進出動線；想使用設施的隊伍數量屬於時程分配問題，不是空間設計的關鍵考量。"},{"id":"q1130","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":23,"question":"What is the minimum recommended space between the ends of racks to provide room for spotters?","options":["1 foot (30 cm)","2 feet (61 cm)","3 feet (91 cm)","4 feet (123 cm)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"3 feet (91 cm)","explanation_en":"A minimum of 3 feet is recommended to allow adequate space for spotters.","tags":["chapter-23"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲架兩端之間至少保留3英呎(91公分)的間距，保護者(spotters)才有足夠空間站位與介入保護。"},{"id":"q1131","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":24,"question":"What is the recommended coach-to-participant ratio during peak weight room usage time in a collegiate setting?","options":["1:10","1:15","1:20","1:25"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:20","explanation_en":"A 1:20 coach-to-participant ratio is recommended during peak collegiate weight room usage.","tags":["chapter-24"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"大專院校重訓室尖峰時段，教練與練習者的建議比例為1:20；比例過高會造成指導不足與安全管理風險。"},{"id":"q1132","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":24,"question":"Which of the following individuals is responsible for allowing an athlete to begin formal involvement in a strength and conditioning program?","options":["athletic director","athlete’s parent or guardian","team’s certified athletic trainer","strength and conditioning professional"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"team’s certified athletic trainer","explanation_en":"Medical clearance to participate is provided by the certified athletic trainer.","tags":["chapter-24"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"允許選手正式參加肌力體能訓練的醫療許可，由隊伍的認證運動保護員(certified athletic trainer)審核傷病史後提供。"},{"id":"q1133","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":24,"question":"Proper documentation is essential to the strength and conditioning facility. Which of the following is NOT part of the records that should be kept on file?","options":["manufacturer’s user’s manual","participant training logs","written emergency plan","medical health history"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"medical health history","explanation_en":"Participant training logs are not a required administrative document for facility liability management.","tags":["chapter-24"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"醫療健康史屬於醫療體系檔案，由醫療/保護員團隊儲存並受隱私規範；設施端為責任管理需建檔的是器材使用手冊、參訓紀錄與緊急應變計畫。"},{"id":"q1134","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":24,"question":"The strength and conditioning professional’s knowledge and skill development includes competencies in all of the following EXCEPT","options":["exercise and sport science","administration and management","finance and appraisal","teaching and coaching"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"finance and appraisal","explanation_en":"Finance and appraisal are not core competency domains for strength and conditioning professionals.","tags":["chapter-24"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌力與體能專業人員的知識與技能包含運動科學、行政管理、教學與教練三大領域；財務與估價不是核心勝任領域。"},{"id":"q1135","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":24,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a component of an emergency plan?","options":["emergency medicine","emergency communication","emergency equipment","emergency personnel"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"emergency medicine","explanation_en":"Emergency plans include communication, equipment, and personnel, but not emergency medicine.","tags":["chapter-24"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"緊急應變計畫的三大構成要素是緊急人員(personnel)、緊急溝通(communication)與緊急裝備(equipment)；「緊急醫學」不是計畫的構成專案。"},{"id":"q1136","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The axial skeleton includes the:","options":["Scapulae","Humerus","Vertebrae","Femur"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Vertebrae","explanation_en":"The axial skeleton includes the skull, vertebral column, and rib cage. The vertebrae form the central part of the vertebral column.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"軸骨(axial skeleton)包括顱骨、脊椎與胸廓，椎骨(vertebrae)屬於軸骨；肩胛骨、肱骨與股骨都屬於附肢骨骸。"},{"id":"q1137","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The primary muscle group responsible for knee extension during a squat is the:","options":["Hamstrings","Quadriceps","Gluteus maximus","Gastrocnemius"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Quadriceps","explanation_en":"The quadriceps are the primary movers during knee extension, which occurs when standing up from the bottom of a squat.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲站起階段的膝伸直由股四頭肌(quadriceps)主導；膕旁肌跨過膝髖兩個關節、不是主動的膝伸肌，臀大肌負責伸髖，腓腸肌負責蹠屈。"},{"id":"q1138","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Alveoli are responsible for:","options":["Filtering inhaled air","Warming and humidifying air","Trapping particles in mucus","Exchanging gases between air and blood"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Exchanging gases between air and blood","explanation_en":"Alveoli are tiny air sacs in the lungs where the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide occurs between the lungs and the bloodstream.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肺泡(alveoli)的功能是氣體交換：氧氣由肺泡擴散進入微血管血流，二氧化碳反向排出。過濾、加溫與加濕空氣是鼻腔與氣道的任務。"},{"id":"q1139","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a first-class lever (e.g., a seesaw), the fulcrum is positioned:","options":["Between the load and the effort","Between the effort and the load","At the end of the lever arm","Directly under the load"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Between the load and the effort","explanation_en":"In a first-class lever, the fulcrum is positioned between the effort and the load.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第一類槓桿(如蹺蹺板)的支點(fulcrum)位於阻力與施力之間，人體中的例子是頸部伸展；支點位於末端的安排屬於第二、三類槓桿。"},{"id":"q1140","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which type of muscle action occurs when lowering a dumbbell during a curl?","options":["Concentric","Eccentric","Isometric","Isokinetic"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Eccentric","explanation_en":"Eccentric muscle actions occur when the muscle lengthens under tension, such as when lowering a dumbbell during a curl.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"放下啞鈴時肱二頭肌在張力下被動拉長、控制下降速度，屬於離心收縮(eccentric)；舉起階段才是向心收縮。"},{"id":"q1141","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Using the torque equation (Torque = Force × Distance), which option produces the greatest torque?","options":["10 N at 0.10 m","20 N at 0.05 m","25 N at 0.06 m","30 N at 0.04 m"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"25 N at 0.06 m","explanation_en":"Torque = Force × Distance. 25 × 0.06 = 1.5 N·m, which is the highest torque among the options.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"力矩=力量×力臂:25N×0.06m=1.5牛頓·公尺為最大；其餘選項各為10N×0.10m=1、20N×0.05m=1、30N×0.04m=1.2牛頓·公尺。"},{"id":"q1142","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which energy system provides immediate energy for short, high-intensity activities (e.g., a 100-meter sprint)?","options":["Glycolytic","Oxidative","Phosphagen","Aerobic"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Phosphagen","explanation_en":"The phosphagen system provides immediate energy for short, high-intensity activities like a 100-meter sprint.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"100公尺衝刺這類10秒內的極高強度專案由磷酸原系統(ATP-PCr， phosphagen)供應能量，磷酸肌酸分解可立即再合成三磷酸腺苷，不需要氧氣。"},{"id":"q1143","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which hormone helps maintain blood glucose levels during prolonged exercise by promoting glycogen breakdown in the liver?","options":["Insulin","Epinephrine","Cortisol","Glucagon"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Glucagon","explanation_en":"Glucagon is secreted to maintain blood glucose levels during prolonged exercise by promoting glycogen breakdown in the liver.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"長時間運動中血糖下降時，胰臟分泌升糖素(glucagon)，促進肝臟肝醣分解與糖質新生，維持血糖穩定；胰島素的作用相反，是降低血糖。"},{"id":"q1144","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"High-intensity interval training (HIIT) is most associated with:","options":["Decreased oxygen debt","No oxygen deficit","Increased oxygen debt","Elimination of lactate accumulation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increased oxygen debt","explanation_en":"HIIT causes a significant oxygen deficit during exercise, leading to greater oxygen debt afterward for recovery.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高強度間歇訓練(HIIT)在運動中造成明顯的氧欠缺(oxygen deficit)，運動後需消耗額外氧氣恢復平衡，即氧債(oxygen debt/EPOC)增加。"},{"id":"q1145","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type I muscle fibers are best described as:","options":["Fast-twitch, high force","Slow-twitch, fatigue-resistant","Fast-twitch, easily fatigued","Intermediate, moderate fatigue resistance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Slow-twitch, fatigue-resistant","explanation_en":"Type I fibers are slow-twitch fibers that are highly fatigue-resistant and primarily rely on the aerobic energy system.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第一類肌纖維屬於慢縮肌纖維，粒線體與肌紅蛋白含量高、以氧化代謝為主，抗疲勞性最強，主要依賴有氧能量系統。"},{"id":"q1146","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The functional unit of a myofibril where muscle contraction occurs is the:","options":["Sarcolemma","Sarcomere","Sarcoplasm","Fascicle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Sarcomere","explanation_en":"The sarcomere is the structural and functional unit of a myofibril, where muscle contraction occurs.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌節(sarcomere)是肌原纖維(myofibril)的結構與功能基本單位，由肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白細絲排列組成，肌肉收縮在肌節層面發生。"},{"id":"q1147","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Calcium ions bind to which protein to initiate muscle contraction?","options":["Actin","Myosin","Tropomyosin","Troponin"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Troponin","explanation_en":"Calcium ions bind to troponin, which triggers the conformational change that allows actin and myosin interaction for contraction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"動作電位觸發鈣離子從肌漿網釋放後，鈣離子與肌鈣蛋白(troponin)結合，使tropomyosin移位、暴露肌動蛋白上的結合位，肌球蛋白橫橋才得以結合並產生收縮。"},{"id":"q1148","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which receptor detects changes in muscle length and triggers a stretch reflex?","options":["Golgi tendon organ","Pacinian corpuscle","Muscle spindle","Ruffini ending"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Muscle spindle","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles detect changes in muscle length and initiate the stretch reflex to resist overstretching.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌梭(muscle spindle)感受肌纖維長度與長度變化的速度，被快速拉長時引發牽張反射(stretch reflex)；高爾基腱器官感受的是肌腱張力。"},{"id":"q1149","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which part of a neuron conducts electrical impulses away from the cell body?","options":["Axon","Dendrite","Synapse","Myelin sheath"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Axon","explanation_en":"Axons conduct electrical impulses away from the neuron’s cell body toward other neurons, muscles, or glands.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"軸突(axon)把動作電位由細胞體向外傳導到其他神經元、肌肉或腺體；樹突負責把訊號傳入細胞體。"},{"id":"q1150","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which neurotransmitter is released at the neuromuscular junction to initiate muscle contraction?","options":["Dopamine","Serotonin","Acetylcholine","Norepinephrine"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Acetylcholine","explanation_en":"Acetylcholine is the neurotransmitter that binds to receptors on muscle cells to initiate contraction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"神經肌肉接合點(neuromuscular junction)釋放的神經傳導物質是乙醯膽鹼(acetylcholine)，它結合肌細胞膜上的受器，引發肌細胞動作電位與收縮。"},{"id":"q1151","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During high-intensity exercise, the preferred energy source for ATP production is typically:","options":["Fat","Carbohydrate","Protein","Ketones"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Carbohydrate","explanation_en":"Carbohydrates are the preferred energy source during high-intensity exercise due to their efficiency in ATP production.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"高強度運動時身體優先使用碳水化合物(肌肝醣與血糖)，因為糖解產生ATP的速率比脂肪氧化快得多；強度越高，對碳水的依賴越高。"},{"id":"q1152","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which vitamin is fat-soluble and commonly requires dietary fat for absorption?","options":["Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Vitamin B12","Folate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Vitamin D","explanation_en":"Vitamins A, D, E, and K are fat-soluble, meaning they are stored in body fat and require fat for absorption.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"脂溶性維生素為A、D、E、K，需要膳食脂肪協助吸收並可儲存於體內；維生素C、B12與葉酸都是水溶性。"},{"id":"q1153","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Iron is a critical component of hemoglobin and primarily supports:","options":["Bone density","Oxygen transport in blood","Muscle contraction","Nerve conduction"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Oxygen transport in blood","explanation_en":"Iron is a critical component of hemoglobin, responsible for carrying oxygen in the blood.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鐵是血紅素(hemoglobin)的核心成分，負責在血液中攜帶氧氣；缺鐵會造成貧血，輸氧能力與運動表現下降。"},{"id":"q1154","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A carbohydrate-loading strategy for endurance events typically involves:","options":["Consuming a high-fat diet 1 day prior","Fasting 24 hours prior","Reducing carbohydrate intake 3–7 days prior","Consuming a high-carbohydrate diet 3–7 days prior"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Consuming a high-carbohydrate diet 3–7 days prior","explanation_en":"Carbohydrate loading involves increasing glycogen stores by consuming a high-carbohydrate diet days before an event.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"碳水補充法(carbohydrate loading)是在比賽前3至7天採高碳水飲食，讓肌肉肝醣儲存超量，延緩耐力專案中的疲勞。"},{"id":"q1155","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Recommended daily protein intake for athletes to support muscle repair and recovery is approximately:","options":["0.4–0.8 g/kg body weight","1.2–2.0 g/kg body weight","2.5–3.5 g/kg body weight","4.0 g/kg body weight"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1.2–2.0 g/kg body weight","explanation_en":"Athletes typically require 1.2–2.0 grams of protein per kilogram of body weight to support muscle repair and recovery.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動員每日蛋白質建議攝取量約為1.2至2.0克/每公斤體重，以支援肌肉修復、合成與訓練適應；0.4至0.8克對運動員而言明顯不足。"},{"id":"q1156","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endurance athletes are most likely to rely heavily on carbohydrates, such as:","options":["Marathon runner","Olympic weightlifter","Shot putter","Powerlifter"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Marathon runner","explanation_en":"Endurance athletes, such as marathon runners, rely heavily on carbohydrates to fuel prolonged training sessions.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"馬拉松選手進行長時間中低強度運動，大量依賴碳水化合物維持肌肝醣；舉重、鉛球與力量舉選手的專案以磷酸原系統與神經肌肉表現為主。"},{"id":"q1157","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which supplement is best known for improving ATP resynthesis during short-duration, high-intensity exercise?","options":["Creatine monohydrate","Vitamin C","Fish oil","Caffeine-free electrolyte mix"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Creatine monohydrate","explanation_en":"Creatine improves ATP resynthesis during high-intensity, short-duration exercises such as sprinting and lifting.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌酸(monohydrate)增加肌肉磷酸肌酸儲量，加速三磷酸腺苷再合成，對短時間、高強度、重複性的衝刺與舉重表現最有直接幫助。"},{"id":"q1158","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which substance is banned due to its performance-enhancing and potential health-risk properties?","options":["Caffeine","Creatine","Ephedrine","Whey protein"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Ephedrine","explanation_en":"Ephedrine is a banned substance due to its performance-enhancing and potential health-risk properties.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"麻黃素(ephedrine)具有增能效果，且可能升高血壓與心率、帶來心血管風險，因此長期被反興奮劑機構列為停用物質；咖啡因、肌酸與乳清蛋白目前皆可使用。"},{"id":"q1159","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which supplement increases muscle carnosine levels and may delay fatigue by buffering hydrogen ions?","options":["BCAA","Beta-alanine","Glucosamine","Vitamin E"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Beta-alanine","explanation_en":"Beta-alanine supplementation increases muscle carnosine levels, enhancing the ability to buffer hydrogen ions and delay fatigue.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸(beta-alanine)是肌肉中肌肽(carnosine)合成的限制胺基酸，補充可提高肌肽濃度，增強對高強度運動中氫離子的緩衝，延遲疲勞。"},{"id":"q1160","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which mineral is vital for nerve function and muscle contraction, and imbalances can contribute to cramps?","options":["Calcium","Sodium","Potassium","Iron"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Potassium","explanation_en":"Potassium is vital for nerve function and muscle contraction; imbalances can lead to cramps and weakness.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鉀與鈉共同維持細胞膜靜止電位，是神經傳導與肌肉收縮的關鍵電解質；大量出汗造成鉀失衡時，容易出現痙攣、無力等症狀。"},{"id":"q1161","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which method is a simple and effective way to assess hydration status in athletes?","options":["Urine color observation","Skinfold measurement","Resting heart rate only","Body mass index (BMI)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Urine color observation","explanation_en":"Urine color is a simple and effective method to assess hydration status—pale yellow indicates good hydration.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"觀察尿液顏色是最簡單可行的水合狀態評估方式：淡黃接近透明代表水分充足，深黃則提示已經脫水，應立即補充。"},{"id":"q1162","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Losing more than 2% of body weight through sweat can impair thermoregulation and increase risk of:","options":["Hypoglycemia","Heatstroke","Hypertension","Muscle hypertrophy"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Heatstroke","explanation_en":"Losing more than 2% of body weight through sweat can impair thermoregulation and increase the risk of heat-related illnesses like heatstroke.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"隨汗流失超過體重2%會明顯損害體溫調節能力，核心溫度上升，增加熱痙攣、熱衰竭乃至中暑(heat stroke)的風險。"},{"id":"q1163","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Carbohydrate consumption within what time frame post-exercise helps maximize glycogen resynthesis?","options":["Within 30 minutes","Within 2 hours","Within 6 hours","The next day"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Within 30 minutes","explanation_en":"Carbohydrate consumption within 30 minutes post-exercise maximizes glycogen resynthesis for better recovery.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動結束後30分鐘內攝取碳水化合物，可把握肝醣合成酶活性最高的視窗期，讓肌肉肝醣再合成速度最大化。"},{"id":"q1164","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which pre-competition meal is generally recommended to provide sustained energy without GI discomfort?","options":["High-fat, high-fiber meal","High-protein, low-carb meal","Moderate carbohydrate, low-fat, moderate protein meal","No meal before competition"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Moderate carbohydrate, low-fat, moderate protein meal","explanation_en":"A balanced pre-competition meal with moderate carbohydrates, low fat, and moderate protein provides sustained energy without gastrointestinal discomfort.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"賽前餐建議攝取適量碳水化合物、低脂肪、適量蛋白質：能持續供能、胃排空快；高脂肪高纖維餐消化慢，容易造成腸胃不適。"},{"id":"q1165","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Consuming protein prior to training (even during fasting periods) can help:","options":["Eliminate the need for carbohydrates","Preserve muscle mass and optimize performance","Increase dehydration risk","Reduce recovery capacity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Preserve muscle mass and optimize performance","explanation_en":"Providing protein prior to training can help preserve muscle mass and optimize performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"訓練前攝取蛋白質可提供遊離胺基酸，降低訓練中的肌肉蛋白分解，有助於維持肌肉量，並在禁食期間(如宗教齋戒)支援表現。"},{"id":"q1166","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which grip type is typically used for a deadlift to enhance grip strength and prevent bar rotation?","options":["Mixed grip","Hook grip","Overhand grip","Neutral grip"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Mixed grip","explanation_en":"A mixed grip (one hand overhand, one underhand) increases bar security and helps prevent rotation during deadlifts.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"硬舉使用混合握(mixed grip，一手正握一手反握)可形成相反方向的摩擦力，防止槓鈴翻滾轉動，提升握持安全性。"},{"id":"q1167","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a back squat, at what joint should the lifter initiate the movement first?","options":["Ankle","Knee","Hip","Spine"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hip","explanation_en":"Proper squat mechanics begin with the hips moving backward, keeping the weight over the midfoot and minimizing knee stress.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"後蹲啟動時應先屈髖、臀部往後下方移動，讓重心保持在足弓中央上方；先動膝會把重心推向前腳掌，增加膝關節壓力。"},{"id":"q1168","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which cue is MOST appropriate to maintain proper form during a bench press?","options":["Flare elbows out at 90 degrees","Retract and depress scapulae","Lift hips off the bench for more power","Keep wrists bent back"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Retract and depress scapulae","explanation_en":"Keeping the scapulae retracted and depressed provides shoulder stability and safer movement during the bench press.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"仰臥推舉全程應肩胛後縮並下壓(retract and depress scapulae)，固定肩帶、保護肩關節，並提供穩定的推舉平臺；手肘開啟90度反而增加肩部壓力。"},{"id":"q1169","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following describes the eccentric phase in a plyometric exercise?","options":["Muscle shortening","Muscle lengthening","Isometric stabilization","Muscle contraction without movement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Muscle lengthening","explanation_en":"The eccentric phase occurs when the muscle lengthens under tension, such as during the landing phase of a jump.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"彈震訓練(plyometric)的離心階段是肌肉在張力下被拉長，例如落地吸收階段；此階段儲存彈效能，接著進入向心收縮。"},{"id":"q1170","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which drill is most appropriate for developing lower-body power in an athlete?","options":["Bounding","Lateral shuffle","Side plank","Jogging"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Bounding","explanation_en":"Bounding exercises develop explosive strength and elastic power in the lower body muscles.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"單腳連續大跳(bounding)要求每次落地後快速強而有力地蹬地，是發展下肢爆發力與彈性輸出最合適的選項；側向滑步偏敏捷，側棒式偏核心。"},{"id":"q1171","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Refer to the diagram below of a depth jump setup. Which key aspect should be emphasized when performing a depth jump?","options":["Land softly with flexed knees","Immediate, minimal ground contact time","Maximal vertical jump effort","Focus"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Immediate, minimal ground contact time","explanation_en":"Reducing ground contact time maximizes the explosive power transfer from eccentric to concentric contraction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深度跳(depth jump)的關鍵是落地後立即反彈、把觸地時間壓到最短，讓牽張-縮短迴圈(SSC)儲存的彈效能與反射訊號有效轉換成向上輸出。"},{"id":"q1172","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What component of speed is most influenced by resistance sprint drills?","options":["Reaction time","Acceleration","Top-end speed","Lateral quickness"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Acceleration","explanation_en":"Resistance sprint drills (like sled pushes) primarily improve the early acceleration phase of sprinting.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"阻力衝刺(推雪橇、阻力傘)增加每一步的水平力量需求，主要影響的是加速(acceleration)階段，而非反應時間或極速。"},{"id":"q1173","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which drill best develops change-of-direction speed?","options":["T-test","I-test","L-test","S-test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"T-test","explanation_en":"The T-test involves forward sprinting, side shuffling, and backward running, improving multi-directional agility.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"T-test的路線包含前衝、側向滑步與倒退跑，要求多方向的減速與再加速，最能發展與評估變向速度。"},{"id":"q1174","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Elite sprinters are characterized by:","options":["Long ground contact time","Excessive forward lean","Reduced stride frequency","Short ground contact time"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Short ground contact time","explanation_en":"Elite sprinters minimize ground contact time, maximizing force application into the ground for speed development.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"菁英衝刺選手的特徵是觸地時間短，以極大的力在短時間壓入地面；觸地時間長、過度前傾或步頻低都是速度表現的缺點。"},{"id":"q1175","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In Olympic weightlifting, the second pull is characterized by:","options":["Knee bend","Maximum force and triple extension","Catch position","First upward pull from the floor"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Maximum force and triple extension","explanation_en":"The second pull involves explosive extension at the hips, knees, and ankles to generate maximal bar acceleration.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第二拉(second pull)是舉鈴動作中力量輸出的高峰，以髖、膝、踝三重伸展(triple extension)爆發生長，讓槓鈴獲得最大的向上加速度。"},{"id":"q1176","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When coaching a volleyball athlete, which exercise is MOST sport-specific?","options":["Depth jumps","Overhead squat","Barbell hip thrust","Plank holds"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Depth jumps","explanation_en":"Depth jumps closely mimic the explosive nature of vertical jumping in volleyball, making it sport-specific.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"排球的主攻與攔網都是垂直爆發跳躍，深度跳在動作結構與能量需求上最貼近專項；臀推、過頭深蹲與棒式與專項跳躍的需求相差較遠。"},{"id":"q1177","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which muscle group is crucial for shoulder stabilization during overhead movements like pitching?","options":["Trapezius","Rotator cuff","Latissimus dorsi","Pectoralis major"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rotator cuff","explanation_en":"Rotator cuff muscles stabilize the shoulder during high-velocity overhead motions like pitching.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"投擲等高速過頭動作需要旋轉肌袖(rotator cuff：棘上肌、棘下肌、肩胛下肌、小圓肌)把肱骨頭穩定在肩盂內，避免肩關節鬆動與傷害。"},{"id":"q1178","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Dynamic stretching is recommended before activity because it:","options":["Decreases core temperature","Reduces joint mobility","Causes fatigue prior to exercise","Increases core temperature and mobility"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Increases core temperature and mobility","explanation_en":"Dynamic stretching increases core temperature and mobility, preparing muscles for activity without compromising performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動前做動態伸展可提高核心溫度、增加關節活動度與神經活絡，為接下來的表現做好準備；冷身狀態下長時間靜態拉長可能短暫削弱爆發輸出。"},{"id":"q1179","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which flexibility exercise best improves hip extension mobility relevant to deep squats?","options":["Hip flexor lunge stretch","Toe-touch stretch","Seated hamstring stretch","Wrist flexor stretch"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hip flexor lunge stretch","explanation_en":"Hip flexor stretches improve hip extension and mobility, essential for deep squats.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲到底需要完整的髖伸展活動度；髂腰肌等髖屈肌緊繃會限制髖部往後伸，以弓箭步跪姿的髖屈肌伸展最能改善。"},{"id":"q1180","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which tool is commonly used for self-myofascial release to reduce muscle tension and improve tissue quality?","options":["Foam roller","Lacrosse ball only","Massage gun only","Stretch strap"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Foam roller","explanation_en":"Foam rollers are commonly used for self-myofascial release to reduce muscle tension and improve tissue quality.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"泡沫滾筒(foam roller)是最常用的自我肌筋膜放鬆(SMR)工具，透過持續加壓降低肌筋膜張力、改善組織品質。"},{"id":"q1181","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which analysis identifies the most common injuries in a sport to design preventive and corrective programs?","options":["Biomechanical analysis","Injury analysis","Needs analysis","Performance profiling"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Injury analysis","explanation_en":"Injury analysis identifies the most common injuries in a sport to design preventive and corrective training programs.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"傷害分析(injury analysis)統計該運動最常見的傷害部位與發生機制(例如足球的膕旁肌拉傷)，據此設計預防性與矯正性訓練內容。"},{"id":"q1182","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In program design, beginners should first focus on:","options":["Developing movement competency and technique","Maximizing training volume immediately","Sport specialization only","Complex Olympic lifts early"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Developing movement competency and technique","explanation_en":"Beginners should focus on mastering basic movement patterns and correct technique before progressing to complex exercises.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"初學者應先建立動作能力與正確技術(基本動作模式、穩定度)，再逐步增加負荷；過早加入大重量或複雜的奧林匹克舉技術，傷害風險高。"},{"id":"q1183","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In linear periodization, training intensity typically:","options":["Decreases while volume increases","Increases while volume decreases","Stays constant year-round","Increases with volume increasing"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Increases while volume decreases","explanation_en":"In linear periodization, intensity increases while training volume decreases progressively over time.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"線性週期化的設計原則是訓練強度隨時間逐步上升、訓練量同步逐步下降，兩者呈反向變化。"},{"id":"q1184","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which phase of periodization emphasizes foundational strength, hypertrophy, and general fitness before sport-specific training?","options":["Preparatory phase","Peaking phase","Competition phase","Transition phase"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Preparatory phase","explanation_en":"The preparatory phase emphasizes foundational strength, hypertrophy, and basic fitness before advancing to sport-specific training.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"準備期(preparatory phase)強調基礎力量、肌肉肥大與一般體能，為後續的專項與巔峰訓練打底。"},{"id":"q1185","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A mesocycle typically lasts:","options":["1–2 days","4–6 weeks","6–12 months","2–3 years"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"4–6 weeks","explanation_en":"A mesocycle typically spans 4–6 weeks and focuses on achieving specific adaptation like strength or endurance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"中週期(mesocycle)通常為4至6週，圍繞單一適應目標(如力量或肥大)安排數個微週期。"},{"id":"q1186","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Power or explosive exercises should typically be performed:","options":["At the end of the workout when fatigued","Early in the workout when fresh","Only on recovery days","Only after isolation work"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Early in the workout when fresh","explanation_en":"Power movements should be prioritized early in the workout when the athlete is not fatigued.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"力量/爆發力動作對技術與神經需求高，應安排在訓練課早期、身體未疲勞時進行，動作品質才有保障。"},{"id":"q1187","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The primary goal of hypertrophy training is to:","options":["Increase muscle cross-sectional area","Maximize VO2 max","Reduce tendon stiffness","Decrease muscle size"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increase muscle cross-sectional area","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy training aims to increase muscle size by promoting muscle fiber growth.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練(hypertrophy)的主要目標是增加肌肉橫截面積，透過中高量、中等負荷的訓練刺激肌肉生長。"},{"id":"q1188","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Training at approximately 85% of 1RM for low repetitions typically targets:","options":["Strength development","Muscular endurance","Speed development","Flexibility"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Strength development","explanation_en":"Training at 85% of 1RM for low repetitions is typical for maximal strength development.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"約85%1RM以上、低次數(1至6下)並搭配長休息的訓練，是典型的最大力量(strength)發展區間。"},{"id":"q1189","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete completes five sets of 5 repetitions at 85% 1RM. This training primarily targets:","options":["Strength development","Hypertrophy","Power production","Muscular endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Strength development","explanation_en":"Training at ~85% of 1RM for low repetitions is characteristic of maximal strength development.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"5組5下、85%1RM屬於高負荷低次數的安排，主要發展最大力量；肥大通常用較低負荷，肌耐力用更輕、更多的次數。"},{"id":"q1190","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which lift is an example of a compound, multi-joint movement typically prioritized early in a session?","options":["Biceps curl","Barbell back squat","Triceps pushdown","Calf raise"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Barbell back squat","explanation_en":"Compound, multi-joint movements should be prioritized early in the session when the athlete is fresh.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"槓鈴後蹲是多關節複合動作，招募大量肌群且需要高穩定度，應排在訓練課早期精神體力最好時；二頭彎舉等單關節孤立動作排在後面。"},{"id":"q1191","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A training program that alternates upper and lower body exercises within the same session is designed to:","options":["Maximize fatigue","Eliminate recovery needs","Alternate between upper and lower","Reduce strength gains"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Alternate between upper and lower","explanation_en":"Alternating upper and lower body exercises can improve training efficiency and recovery during the session.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"同一課中安排上、下肢交替的訓練，讓一組肌群在另一組工作時獲得恢復，可提高訓練密度與時間效率。"},{"id":"q1192","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Circuit training most strongly emphasizes:","options":["Maximal strength","Power","Flexibility","Aerobic endurance"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Aerobic endurance","explanation_en":"Circuit training minimizes rest between exercises, promoting muscular endurance and aerobic conditioning.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"迴圈訓練(circuit training)站間休息極短、持續移動，心率維持高檔，主要強調肌耐力與有氧心肺適能，而非最大力量或功率。"},{"id":"q1193","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Supercompensation is most associated with the:","options":["Preparatory phase","Recovery phase","Peaking phase","Transition phase"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recovery phase","explanation_en":"Supercompensation is the body’s enhanced adaptation following proper recovery after training stress.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"超補償(supercompensation)發生在訓練後的恢復階段：充分休息與營養後，體適能回升並超過原基準，是安排訓練-恢復節奏的理論依據。"},{"id":"q1194","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A hallmark sign of overtraining is:","options":["Increased performance with fatigue","Decreased performance despite high training volume","Rapid muscle gain","Improved sleep quality"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Decreased performance despite high training volume","explanation_en":"Persistent performance decline along with fatigue are hallmark signs of overtraining.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"過度訓練(overtraining)的代表性徵兆是儘管訓練量高、表現卻持續下滑，並伴隨長期疲勞、睡眠與情緒問題。"},{"id":"q1195","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Most athletes require approximately how much sleep per night to support recovery and performance?","options":["4–5 hours","5–6 hours","6–7 hours","7–9 hours"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"7–9 hours","explanation_en":"Athletes require 7–9 hours of sleep per night to support recovery, hormone regulation, and overall performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"多數運動員每晚需要7至9小時睡眠，以支援組織修復、生長激素等荷爾蒙分泌、情緒與運動表現；少於7小時會拖慢恢復。"},{"id":"q1196","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A recommended training space allocation per athlete in a weight room is approximately:","options":["10–15 square feet","20–25 square feet","35–50 square feet","80–100 square feet"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"35–50 square feet","explanation_en":"Providing 35–50 square feet per athlete ensures safety, comfort, and freedom of movement during training sessions.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"重訓空間每位練習者建議預留約35至50平方呎，才有足夠的活動與保護空間，兼顧安全與動線。"},{"id":"q1197","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An important factor in weight room design to reduce accidents and congestion is:","options":["Mirrors in every corner","Dim lighting","Safe flow of traffic and equipment accessibility","Crowding equipment together"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Safe flow of traffic and equipment accessibility","explanation_en":"Safety and efficiency in movement are critical factors in facility design to prevent accidents and congestion.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"場館規劃必須確保安全的動線(flow)與器材取用便利，才能減少碰撞、壅塞與意外；器材擠在一起、光線昏暗都是設計缺點。"},{"id":"q1198","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A treadmill should be placed near exits primarily to:","options":["Allow quick evacuation and reduce obstruction","Increase noise levels","Improve aesthetics","Encourage group use"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Allow quick evacuation and reduce obstruction","explanation_en":"Cardio equipment like treadmills should be placed near exits for quick evacuation and minimal obstruction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跑步機等有氧器材靠近出入口放置，緊急時可快速疏散，也不會阻擋主要動線。"},{"id":"q1199","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The legal responsibility of fitness professionals to take necessary actions to protect clients from harm is called:","options":["Negligence","Duty of care","Assumption of risk","Vicarious liability"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Duty of care","explanation_en":"Duty of care requires fitness professionals to take necessary actions to protect clients from harm.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"注意義務(duty of care)指專業人員必須採取合理必要的措施，保護會員/選手免於可預見的傷害；違反即可能構成過失(negligence)。"},{"id":"q1200","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Keeping equipment safe and functional to reduce injury risk requires:","options":["Only replacing equipment yearly","Limiting athlete access","Regular equipment maintenance and inspection","Using equipment until failure"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Regular equipment maintenance and inspection","explanation_en":"Keeping equipment safe and functional significantly reduces the risk of injury during workouts.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"定期保養與檢修器材(equipment maintenance and inspection)能讓器材維持安全與功能正常，直接降低訓練中因器材故障造成的傷害風險。"},{"id":"q1201","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which document, signed before participation, outlines the risks involved in physical activity?","options":["Insurance form","Liability waiver","Code of conduct","Incident report"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Liability waiver","explanation_en":"A liability waiver informs clients of potential risks and reduces legal exposure for fitness facilities.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"責任免除同意書(liability waiver)在參與前由參加者簽署，說明運動參與的固有風險，降低場館與教練的法律責任風險。"},{"id":"q1202","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following actions by a coach would be considered unethical?","options":["Reporting suspected abuse","Recommending performance-enhancing drugs","Promoting injury prevention techniques","Encouraging proper warm-up routines"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recommending performance-enhancing drugs","explanation_en":"Suggesting or providing banned substances is unethical and against professional conduct standards.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"教練推薦或提供增能藥物(PED)違反職業道德與反興奮劑規範；通報虐待、推廣預防傷害與暖身都是專業的正向行為。"},{"id":"q1203","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which law requires that individuals with disabilities have equal access to public facilities, including fitness centers?","options":["Civil Rights Act","Occupational Safety and Health Act","Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)","Family and Medical Leave Act"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)","explanation_en":"The ADA mandates that facilities must be accessible to individuals with disabilities.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"美國身心障礙者法(Americans with Disabilities Act， ADA)要求公共設施(含健身場館)提供身心障礙者平等的使用權利與無障礙進出。"},{"id":"q1204","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If a coach shares an athlete’s private health information without consent, they may be violating which law?","options":["FERPA","Title IX","OSHA","HIPAA"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"HIPAA","explanation_en":"HIPAA protects the confidentiality of medical records and personal health information.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"未獲同意就透露選手的個人健康資料，違反健康保險可攜性與責任法(HIPAA)；該法保障醫療紀錄與個人健康資訊的隱私。"},{"id":"q1205","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When purchasing new weight room equipment, what is the most important factor to consider?","options":["Safety and durability standards","Popularity of the brand","Color and style","Trendiness in the market"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Safety and durability standards","explanation_en":"Equipment must meet safety and durability standards to ensure athlete safety and long-term use.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"採購重訓器材時最重要的是安全與耐用性標準(結構、載重、焊點、保固)，品牌流行度與外觀是次要考量。"},{"id":"q1206","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which piece of equipment requires the most frequent inspection due to heavy usage?","options":["Stability balls","Resistance bands","Squat racks and barbells","Plyometric boxes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Squat racks and barbells","explanation_en":"These high-load equipment pieces are heavily used and critical for safety, requiring regular inspections.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲架與槓鈴承受高負荷且使用頻繁，安全影響最大，需要最經常的檢查(焊縫、插銷、滾花、卡鉸)；彈力帶、安定球與跳箱負荷低。"},{"id":"q1207","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which preventive maintenance step is essential for treadmills?","options":["Oil the cables weekly","Replace the motor monthly","Lubricate the running belt periodically","Calibrate incline daily"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Lubricate the running belt periodically","explanation_en":"Proper lubrication prevents friction, overheating, and premature wear on treadmill belts.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跑步機必要的預防保養是定期為跑帶上油(lubricate)，減少跑帶與底板摩擦，避免馬達過熱與跑帶磨損。"},{"id":"q1208","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following best promotes professional development among strength and conditioning staff?","options":["Requiring monthly staff meetings","Encouraging participation in continuing education courses","Offering bonuses only for high attendance","Restricting knowledge to head coaches"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Encouraging participation in continuing education courses","explanation_en":"Continued education ensures that coaches stay current with the latest research and best practices.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鼓勵教練持續參加繼續教育課程，能讓知識與技法跟上最新研究與實務，是對專業發展最直接的促進。"},{"id":"q1209","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the MOST important factor when hiring new strength and conditioning staff?","options":["Appearance","Low salary expectations","Ability to market the facility","Certification and practical experience"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Certification and practical experience","explanation_en":"Credentials and hands-on experience are critical for ensuring qualified, safe, and effective coaching.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"招募肌力體能人員時最重要的是證照(如CSCS)與實務經驗，兩者直接關聯指導品質與選手安全。"},{"id":"q1210","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a staff evaluation process, which of the following should be emphasized the most?","options":["Adherence to professional standards and job performance","Number of social media posts","Ability to sell memberships","Number of hours spent in the facility"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Adherence to professional standards and job performance","explanation_en":"Evaluations should focus on professionalism, effectiveness, and the ability to uphold safety and ethical standards.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"員工考核應以專業標準遵循度與工作表現為核心；社群媒體發文量、入會業績或在館時數都只是邊緣指標。"},{"id":"q1211","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests measures maximum muscular strength?","options":["Vertical jump test","1-repetition maximum (1RM) bench press","Yo-Yo intermittent recovery test","Pro agility shuttle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1-repetition maximum (1RM) bench press","explanation_en":"The 1RM bench press measures maximal strength by determining the heaviest weight an individual can lift once.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"1RM(一次最大重量)仰臥推舉直接測量一次可舉起的最大重量，是最大肌力的測量；垂直跳測爆發力，Yo-Yo測耐力，Pro agility測敏捷。"},{"id":"q1212","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which performance test would best assess lower-body explosive power?","options":["Standing long jump","1RM squat","300-yard shuttle","Curl-up test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Standing long jump","explanation_en":"The standing long jump measures horizontal explosive power from the lower body.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"立定跳遠(standing long jump)測量下肢往水平方向的一次爆發輸出，是下肢爆發力的常用測試；1RM深蹲測最大力量，300碼測無氧糖解能力。"},{"id":"q1213","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During strength testing, how much rest is recommended between maximal attempts?","options":["30 seconds","1 minute","2–5 minutes","10 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2–5 minutes","explanation_en":"Sufficient recovery (2–5 minutes) between maximal attempts helps ensure accurate strength assessment.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"極限嘗試之間應休息2至5分鐘，讓磷酸原(ATP-PCr)系統充分再合成，否則測得的1RM會被疲勞低估。"},{"id":"q1214","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test is MOST appropriate for assessing aerobic endurance in well-trained athletes?","options":["300-yard shuttle run","12-minute Cooper test","Vertical jump test","1RM power clean"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"12-minute Cooper test","explanation_en":"The Cooper test evaluates aerobic endurance by measuring the distance covered in 12 minutes.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"12分鐘庫珀測試(Cooper test)記錄12分鐘內跑出的距離，可推估最大攝氧量，適合評估訓練有素選手的有氧耐力；300碼折返偏無氧。"},{"id":"q1215","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following primarily assesses anaerobic capacity?","options":["1.5-mile run","Skinfold measurement","Sit-and-reach test","Wingate anaerobic test"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Wingate anaerobic test","explanation_en":"The Wingate test measures peak anaerobic power and anaerobic capacity during a 30-second maximal effort cycle.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Wingate無氧測試以30秒全力蹬車測量尖峰無氧功率與平均功率，主要評估無氧能力；1.5英里跑與坐椅體前屈分屬有氧與柔軟度測試。"},{"id":"q1216","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Refer to the chart below and determine the anaerobic power output (Power = Force × Distance ÷ Time). Time = 5 sec, Force = 800 N, Distance = 30 m. What is the anaerobic power output?","options":["4000 W","4800 W","5000 W","5200 W"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"4800 W","explanation_en":"800 N × 30 m ÷ 5 sec = 4800 W.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率=力×距離÷時間=800N×30m÷5s=4800W。先算功(800×30=24000焦耳)，再除以時間5秒。"},{"id":"q1217","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which method provides the MOST accurate assessment of body fat percentage?","options":["BMI","Skinfold caliper measurement","Hydrostatic weighing","Bioelectrical impedance analysis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hydrostatic weighing","explanation_en":"Hydrostatic weighing is considered the gold standard for body composition measurement, despite being less accessible.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"靜水稱重法(hydrostatic weighing)以身體密度推算體脂，是傳統的黃金標準，準確度優於BMI、皮褶與生物電阻抗，但裝置與執行門檻高。"},{"id":"q1218","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which skinfold site is measured for a three-site skinfold test for women?","options":["Chest, abdomen, thigh","Triceps, suprailiac, thigh","Biceps, calf, thigh","Subscapular, abdomen, calf"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Triceps, suprailiac, thigh","explanation_en":"These are standard skinfold sites for estimating body fat percentage in women using the three-site method.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"女性三部位皮褶法量取三頭肌、髂上與大腿；男性三部位是胸、腹、大腿。部位用錯會嚴重影響推估準確度。"},{"id":"q1219","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When using a skinfold caliper, how long should you wait after pinching the skin before taking the measurement?","options":["Immediately","1 second","3 seconds","5 seconds"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"3 seconds","explanation_en":"Waiting 3 seconds after pinching allows the skinfold to stabilize, providing a more accurate measurement.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"以皮褶夾捏起皮膚後應等待約3秒再讀值，讓組織液被擠出、皮褶厚度穩定；立刻讀值會造成誤差。"},{"id":"q1220","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which movement screen assesses stability and mobility of the shoulders?","options":["Shoulder mobility test","Inline lunge","Deep squat","Hurdle step"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Shoulder mobility test","explanation_en":"The shoulder mobility test evaluates bilateral shoulder range of motion, combining internal rotation with adduction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肩部活動度測試(shoulder mobility，FMS專案之一)評估兩側肩關節的活動與穩定，動作結合內旋與內收(手過頭往背摸)。"},{"id":"q1221","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the deep squat test, a compensatory movement such as heel lift-off typically indicates tightness in which muscle group?","options":["Hamstrings","Hip flexors","Gastrocnemius/soleus","Gluteus maximus"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Gastrocnemius/soleus","explanation_en":"Tight calves can restrict ankle dorsiflexion, causing heels to lift during a deep squat.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲測試中腳跟離地(heel lift)代表踝背屈不足，最常見原因是腓腸肌/比目魚肌緊繃；膕旁肌或臀肌緊繃造成的是其他補償模式。"},{"id":"q1222","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which functional movement screen best identifies asymmetries in single-leg strength and mobility?","options":["Hurdle step","Trunk stability push-up","Rotary stability test","Active straight leg raise"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hurdle step","explanation_en":"The hurdle step challenges single-leg balance, strength, and mobility, revealing side-to-side asymmetries.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跨欄測試(hurdle step)要求單腿支撐跨過欄線，考驗單腿的平衡、力量與活動度，最容易暴露左右兩側的不對稱。"},{"id":"q1223","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the primary purpose of performance analysis in strength and conditioning programs?","options":["To track equipment maintenance schedules","To monitor progress and adjust programs accordingly","To determine team captains","To design marketing strategies"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"To monitor progress and adjust programs accordingly","explanation_en":"Performance analysis helps in evaluating effectiveness and making necessary modifications to training programs.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"表現分析的主要目的是監控訓練進度與介入成效，並據此調整訓練計畫，確保訓練朝目標前進。"},{"id":"q1224","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a key performance indicator (KPI) for a sprinter?","options":["VO2 max","Skinfold body fat","Bench press 1RM","40-yard dash time"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"40-yard dash time","explanation_en":"Sprint times like the 40-yard dash are primary indicators of speed performance for sprinters.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"短跑選手的關鍵績效指標(KPI)是40碼衝刺時間，直接反映專項速度；VO2max與體脂對短跑表現的關聯性低。"},{"id":"q1225","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In athlete performance testing, why is it important to test under similar conditions (same time of day, similar environment)?","options":["To favor morning athletes","To avoid excessive competition","To ensure consistency and validity of results","To limit athlete improvement"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"To ensure consistency and validity of results","explanation_en":"Testing under consistent conditions ensures that performance changes are due to training, not environmental factors.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"固定測試時段與環境是為了維持結果的一致性與效度，讓前後測的差異能歸因於訓練，而不是溫度、時段等幹擾因子。"},{"id":"q1226","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which variable is MOST critical when assessing muscular power using the vertical jump test?","options":["Speed of movement","Body fat percentage","Reaction time","Flexibility"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Speed of movement","explanation_en":"Muscular power is a combination of strength and speed; in vertical jumps, quick force production is essential.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率=力量×速度，垂直跳評估的是爆發力，動作速度(快速產力)是最關鍵的變數；體脂、反應時間與柔軟度都不是主要因素。"},{"id":"q1227","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the primary goal of conducting a 1RM test for the bench press?","options":["Test aerobic endurance","Assess flexibility","Measure upper body maximal strength","Evaluate muscle endurance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Measure upper body maximal strength","explanation_en":"1RM testing measures the maximal amount of force that can be exerted by the upper body muscles.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"仰臥推舉1RM測驗的目標就是測量上肢最大肌力，即上肢肌群一次能產生的最大力量。"},{"id":"q1228","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The Yo-Yo Intermittent Recovery Test is designed to assess an athlete’s:","options":["Flexibility","Maximal strength","Body composition","Anaerobic and aerobic endurance"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Anaerobic and aerobic endurance","explanation_en":"The Yo-Yo test evaluates an athlete’s ability to repeatedly perform intense exercise with short recovery periods.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Yo-Yo間歇恢復測試以漸進強度的往返跑搭配極短休息，評估選手在高強度反覆衝刺之間的恢復與維持能力，同時反映有氧與無氧適能。"},{"id":"q1229","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which protocol is BEST for testing an athlete’s maximal aerobic capacity (VO2 max)?","options":["Wingate test","12-minute Cooper run","Hexagon agility test","Skinfold measurements"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"12-minute Cooper run","explanation_en":"The Cooper test is widely used to estimate VO2 max based on the distance covered in 12 minutes of running.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"在選項中，12分鐘庫珀跑是最適合推估最大攝氧量(VO2max)的實地協議，以跑出的距離換算心肺適能；Wingate測無氧，六邊形跳測敏捷。"},{"id":"q1230","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which tool is primarily used in a skinfold measurement to assess body fat percentage?","options":["Measuring tape","Stethoscope","Skinfold caliper","Bioelectrical impedance device"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Skinfold caliper","explanation_en":"Skinfold calipers measure subcutaneous fat thickness at standard sites to estimate total body fat percentage.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"皮褶夾(skinfold caliper)是皮褶測量的專用工具，夾量標準部位的皮下脂肪厚度以推估整體體脂率；捲尺與生物電阻抗屬於其他方法。"},{"id":"q1231","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If an athlete’s weight remains constant but their body fat percentage decreases, this indicates an increase in:","options":["Body fat mass","Muscle mass","Water retention","Calorie intake"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Muscle mass","explanation_en":"A drop in body fat percentage while maintaining weight typically indicates gains in lean muscle tissue.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"體重不變而體脂率下降，代表脂肪量減少、瘦體重(肌肉量)增加，身體組成改善；水分的短期波動不會穩定反映在體脂率上。"},{"id":"q1232","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which movement pattern is evaluated during the inline lunge test in FMS?","options":["Lower body unilateral stability and mobility","Rotational stability","Upper body mobility","Aerobic endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Lower body unilateral stability and mobility","explanation_en":"The inline lunge test assesses balance, strength, and mobility on each leg individually.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"直線弓箭步(inline lunge，FMS專案之一)在腳尖對腳跟的窄基座上完成弓箭步，評估單側下肢的平衡、穩定與活動度。"},{"id":"q1233","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the active straight leg raise test, what is the primary factor being assessed?","options":["Knee stability","Hamstring and hip flexor flexibility","Upper back strength","Shoulder mobility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Hamstring and hip flexor flexibility","explanation_en":"The active straight leg raise measures the flexibility and control of the hamstrings and hip flexors.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"主動直腿抬高(active straight leg raise)評估膕旁肌等後鏈的柔軟度，以及對側骨盆的穩定與控制；測的不是膝關節或肩部。"},{"id":"q1234","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following BEST describes a qualitative analysis in sports performance testing?","options":["Measuring sprint times precisely","Using force plates for jumping analysis","Observing movement patterns for technique evaluation","Recording maximal oxygen consumption"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Observing movement patterns for technique evaluation","explanation_en":"Qualitative analysis involves subjective assessments such as evaluating an athlete’s movement efficiency and form.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"定性分析是主觀的品質評定，例如觀察動作模式、技術效率與姿勢；計時、測力板與攝氧量數值都屬於定量分析。"},{"id":"q1235","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When analyzing performance test results, what is the primary benefit of using norm-referenced data?","options":["Comparing an athlete to personal bests","Establishing group averages only","Predicting an athlete’s injury risk","Comparing an athlete’s performance to a larger reference group"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Comparing an athlete’s performance to a larger reference group","explanation_en":"Norm-referenced data allows athletes to compare their performance against standard benchmarks from peer groups.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"常模參照(norm-referenced)資料的主要好處是把選手成績與大型參考群體的同儕標準比較，判斷其在族群中的相對位置。"},{"id":"q1236","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which structure primarily stores elastic energy during the stretch-shortening cycle?","options":["Actin filaments","Series elastic component","Sarcomere Z-disks","Neuromuscular junction"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Series elastic component","explanation_en":"Elastic energy is stored primarily in the series elastic component (tendons and cross-bridge elasticity).","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"牽張-縮短迴圈(SSC)中，彈效能主要儲存在序列彈性成分(series elastic component，包含肌腱與橫橋的彈性結構)，並在隨後的收縮時釋放。"},{"id":"q1237","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Power is best defined as:","options":["Force × distance","Mass × acceleration","Force × velocity","Torque × time"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Force × velocity","explanation_en":"Power is the rate of doing work and is mechanically defined as force multiplied by velocity.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率的力學定義是功率=力量×速度(force × velocity)，代表做功的速率；力×距離是功，質量×加速度是力。"},{"id":"q1238","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which muscle fiber type has the highest fatigue resistance?","options":["Type IIx","Type IIa","Type I","Fast glycolytic"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Type I","explanation_en":"Type I fibers are slow-twitch, highly oxidative, and the most fatigue resistant.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"第一類(Type I)慢縮肌纖維氧化能力強、收縮速度慢，是抗疲勞性最高的肌纖維；IIx型最容易疲勞。"},{"id":"q1239","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which energy system predominates during a 10-second maximal sprint?","options":["Oxidative","Anaerobic glycolysis","Phosphagen","Beta oxidation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Phosphagen","explanation_en":"Short, maximal efforts rely primarily on the ATP-PCr (phosphagen) system.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"10秒全力衝刺由磷酸原系統(ATP-PCr)主導供能；無氧糖解大約從數秒後才逐漸加入，氧化系統供能更慢。"},{"id":"q1240","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A first-class lever in the human body is best exemplified by:","options":["Elbow flexion","Ankle plantarflexion","Neck extension","Knee extension"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Neck extension","explanation_en":"Neck extension places the fulcrum between the load (head) and effort (neck extensors).","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"頸部伸展是人體第一類槓桿的例子：頭部重量為阻力、頸部伸肌為施力，支點(寰枕關節)位於兩者之間；肘屈與踝蹠屈多屬第二、三類槓桿。"},{"id":"q1241","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which hormone promotes amino acid uptake and protein synthesis?","options":["Cortisol","Glucagon","Insulin","Epinephrine"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Insulin","explanation_en":"Insulin is anabolic and promotes amino acid uptake and protein synthesis.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"胰島素(insulin)是合成性荷爾蒙，促進胺基酸進入細胞、促進蛋白質合成，同時幫助葡萄糖進入細胞；皮質醇則偏分解性。"},{"id":"q1242","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which receptor detects changes in muscle length?","options":["Golgi tendon organ","Muscle spindle","Pacinian corpuscle","Ruffini ending"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Muscle spindle","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles detect muscle length changes and initiate the stretch reflex.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌梭(muscle spindle)是感受肌肉長度變化的本體感受器，長度快速改變時觸發牽張反射；高爾基腱器官感受的是張力變化。"},{"id":"q1243","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which factor MOST influences acceleration?","options":["Stride frequency","Maximal velocity","Ground reaction force","Reaction time"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Ground reaction force","explanation_en":"Acceleration depends on the magnitude of force applied to the ground.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"牛頓第二定律F=ma：加速度的大小取決於施加於地面的力量(地面反作用力)的水平分量；步頻是速度的呈現結果，不是加速度的根本決定因素。"},{"id":"q1244","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Torque is calculated as:","options":["Force × velocity","Force × distance","Mass × acceleration","Distance ÷ time"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Force × distance","explanation_en":"Torque equals force multiplied by the perpendicular moment arm distance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"力矩=力量×力臂(施力點到支點的垂直距離)，是槓桿分析的基本公式；力×速度是功率，質量×加速度是力。"},{"id":"q1245","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which adaptation occurs earliest with resistance training?","options":["Muscle hypertrophy","Neural adaptations","Fiber type conversion","Increased tendon stiffness"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Neural adaptations","explanation_en":"Early strength gains are largely due to neural adaptations.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"抗阻訓練初期(數週內)的力量增長主要來自神經適應：運動單位徵招率、同步化與放電頻率改善；肌肥大與肌腱變化出現較晚。"},{"id":"q1246","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which rep range is MOST appropriate for hypertrophy?","options":["1–3","4–6","8–12","20–30"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"8–12","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy is typically targeted with moderate loads for 8–12 repetitions.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"發展肌肉肥大的建議次數範圍是每組6至12下(8至12下最典型)的中等負荷；1至3下偏最大力量，20至30下偏肌耐力。"},{"id":"q1247","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which rest interval best supports maximal strength development?","options":["30–60 sec","1–2 min","2–5 min","10+ min"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2–5 min","explanation_en":"Maximal strength requires sufficient ATP-PCr recovery, typically 2–5 minutes.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最大力量訓練需要磷酸原(ATP-PCr)系統充分再合成，組間休息以2至5分鐘最理想；30至60秒屬於肥大/耐力區間。"},{"id":"q1248","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which lift should be performed first in a training session?","options":["Isolation exercise","Power movement","Core exercise","Conditioning drill"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power movement","explanation_en":"Power movements should be performed first when the athlete is fresh.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率/爆發性動作(如清潔與推舉、跳躍類)對技術與神經驅動要求最高，應排在訓練課最前面、選手精神體力最充沛時執行；孤立動作與核心、體能安排在後面。"},{"id":"q1249","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training variable is MOST important for power?","options":["Volume","Velocity","Time under tension","Exercise variety"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Velocity","explanation_en":"Power depends on producing force rapidly, making velocity critical.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率=力量×速度，要發展功率，動作速度(velocity)是最關鍵的訓練變數；負荷需配合意圖快速移動，總量與收縮時間反而是次要。"},{"id":"q1250","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which phase of periodization emphasizes hypertrophy and basic strength?","options":["Preparatory","Peaking","Competition","Transition"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Preparatory","explanation_en":"The preparatory phase develops foundational strength and muscle mass.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"準備期(preparatory)強調肌肉肥大與基礎力量，建立結構與能力基礎，之後才進入力量、功率與專項期。"},{"id":"q1251","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Linear periodization typically involves:","options":["Increasing volume and intensity together","Decreasing intensity and volume","Increasing intensity while decreasing volume","Constant intensity and volume"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Increasing intensity while decreasing volume","explanation_en":"Linear models increase intensity while reducing volume over time.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"線性週期化的典型走向是強度(負荷)隨時間上升、訓練量同步下降，兩者呈反向變化。"},{"id":"q1252","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which plyometric guideline MOST reduces injury risk?","options":["High volume early","Minimal rest","Proper landing mechanics","Hard training surfaces"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Proper landing mechanics","explanation_en":"Proper landing mechanics reduce joint stress and injury risk.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"彈震訓練降低傷害風險最重要的原則是正確的落地力學：以髖膝踝柔軟吸收、落地平穩，能顯著降低關節負荷；量要漸進、強度最後才增加。"},{"id":"q1253","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which sprint drill BEST improves acceleration?","options":["Overspeed sprinting","Resisted sprinting","Tempo runs","Backward jogging"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Resisted sprinting","explanation_en":"Resisted sprinting increases force production during initial acceleration.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"阻力衝刺(resisted sprinting，如拖雪橇)提高每一步的水平施力需求，最能改善起步加速；超速衝刺反而偏向最高速與步頻。"},{"id":"q1254","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which exercise is closed-chain?","options":["Leg extension","Seated hamstring curl","Back squat","Biceps curl"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Back squat","explanation_en":"Closed-chain exercises have the distal segment fixed.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"封閉性動力鏈(closed kinetic chain)動作的遠端節段固定，後蹲時腳固定於地面，屬於閉鏈；腿屈伸、坐姿腿彎舉、二頭彎舉遠端遊離，都是開放性動力鏈。"},{"id":"q1255","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A hallmark of overtraining syndrome is:","options":["Short-term soreness","Rapid strength gains","Persistent performance decline","Improved sleep quality"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Persistent performance decline","explanation_en":"Chronic fatigue and declining performance indicate overtraining.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"過度訓練症候群的指標性特徵是持續性的表現下滑，伴隨長期疲勞、情緒與睡眠改變；短期肌肉痠痛與快速進步都不是。"},{"id":"q1256","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which macronutrient provides the greatest energy per gram?","options":["Protein","Carbohydrate","Fat","Alcohol"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Fat","explanation_en":"Fat provides approximately 9 kcal per gram.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"每公克熱量：脂肪約9 kcal最高，蛋白質與碳水化合物各約4 kcal，酒精約7 kcal。"},{"id":"q1257","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which nutrient timing strategy best supports glycogen resynthesis?","options":["High fat immediately post-exercise","Carbohydrates soon after training","Protein only","Delayed feeding"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Carbohydrates soon after training","explanation_en":"Carbohydrates consumed soon after training accelerate glycogen restoration.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"訓練後盡早攝取碳水化合物能把握肝醣合成視窗，加速肌肉肝醣再合成；只補蛋白質或延後進食都會拖慢補充。"},{"id":"q1258","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which supplement is legal and effective for short-duration high-intensity exercise?","options":["Ephedrine","Creatine","Anabolic steroids","DMAA"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Creatine","explanation_en":"Creatine improves ATP-PCr availability and is legal.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌酸是合法且證據充分的補助品，能提高磷酸肌酸儲量、加速ATP再合成，對短時間高強度運動有效；麻黃素受限，類固醇與DMAA問題更多。"},{"id":"q1259","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Dehydration exceeding ~2% body weight can impair:","options":["Flexibility","Thermoregulation","Protein synthesis","Bone density"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Thermoregulation","explanation_en":"Dehydration significantly impairs thermoregulation and performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"脫水達體重約2%以上時，出汗與散熱效率下降，最先受損的是體溫調節，接著運動表現與認知功能跟著下滑。"},{"id":"q1260","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which vitamin is fat-soluble?","options":["Vitamin C","Vitamin B12","Vitamin D","Folate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Vitamin D","explanation_en":"Vitamins A, D, E, and K are fat-soluble.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"維生素D屬於脂溶性維生素(A、D、E、K)，需搭配脂肪吸收；維生素C、B12與葉酸是水溶性。"},{"id":"q1261","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best assesses anaerobic power?","options":["Cooper test","Wingate test","1.5-mile run","Sit-and-reach"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Wingate test","explanation_en":"The Wingate test measures peak anaerobic power.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Wingate 30秒全力無氧測試直接量測尖峰無氧功率，是評估無氧功率的代表性測試；庫珀與1.5英里跑測有氧，坐椅體前屈測柔軟度。"},{"id":"q1262","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Test-retest consistency refers to:","options":["Validity","Reliability","Objectivity","Specificity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Reliability","explanation_en":"Reliability reflects consistent results across trials.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"測驗重測結果的一致性稱為信度(reliability)；效度(validity)是測到所欲測構唸的程度，客觀性是評分者間一致。"},{"id":"q1263","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test is MOST appropriate for lower-body explosive power?","options":["1RM squat","Standing long jump","300-yard shuttle","T-test"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Standing long jump","explanation_en":"The standing long jump assesses horizontal explosive power.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"立定跳遠測量下肢一次性的水平爆發輸出，適合評估下肢爆發力；1RM深蹲是最大力量，300碼是無氧糖解能力。"},{"id":"q1264","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which body composition method is considered a criterion measure?","options":["BMI","Skinfolds","Hydrostatic weighing","BIA"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hydrostatic weighing","explanation_en":"Hydrostatic weighing is a criterion method.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"靜水稱重法屬準則(criterion)方法，以肺餘量與體重計算身體密度推估體脂，用來校準皮褶、BIA等現場法。"},{"id":"q1265","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Skinfold measurements should be taken:","options":["Immediately after pinching","After 1 second","After 3 seconds","After 10 seconds"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"After 3 seconds","explanation_en":"Waiting ~3 seconds allows tissue compression to stabilize.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"皮褶測量應在夾起後約3秒讀值，讓組織壓縮與組織液位移穩定；過快或過慢都會造成誤差。"},{"id":"q1266","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which FMS test assesses shoulder mobility?","options":["Inline lunge","Shoulder mobility","Hurdle step","Deep squat"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Shoulder mobility","explanation_en":"The shoulder mobility test evaluates bilateral shoulder ROM.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"FMS中的肩部活動度測試(shoulder mobility)評估兩側肩關節活動範圍，動作結合屈曲內旋與後伸內收摸背。"},{"id":"q1267","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Heel lift during a deep squat MOST commonly indicates tightness in:","options":["Hamstrings","Hip flexors","Gastrocnemius/soleus","Gluteals"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Gastrocnemius/soleus","explanation_en":"Limited ankle dorsiflexion from tight calves causes heel lift.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"深蹲時腳跟離地最常見的原因是踝背屈受限，通常是腓腸肌/比目魚肌緊繃所致；膕旁肌與髖屈肌緊繃不會直接造成腳跟抬起。"},{"id":"q1268","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which agility test involves forward sprinting, lateral shuffling, and backpedaling?","options":["Pro agility","T-test","L-test","Hexagon test"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"T-test","explanation_en":"The T-test evaluates multidirectional agility.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"T-test的路線包含向前衝刺、側向滑步與倒退跑，是評估多方向敏捷與變向能力的標準測試；Pro agility只有單一180度折返。"},{"id":"q1269","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why should testing conditions be consistent?","options":["To favor elite athletes","To ensure validity","To reduce injury risk","To improve motivation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"To ensure validity","explanation_en":"Consistent conditions improve validity of comparisons.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"測試條件保持一致(時段、器材、流程、暖身)是為了維持結果的效度與可比性，讓成績差異反映真實的訓練適應。"},{"id":"q1270","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which KPI is MOST relevant for a sprinter?","options":["VO2max","Body fat %","40-yard dash time","Bench press 1RM"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"40-yard dash time","explanation_en":"Sprint time directly reflects sprint performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"短跑選手最相關的關鍵績效指標是40碼衝刺時間，直接量測專項速度表現；VO2max與體脂率對短跑關聯性低。"},{"id":"q1271","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Duty of care requires a coach to:","options":["Guarantee injury-free training","Act reasonably to prevent harm","Follow athlete requests only","Avoid all legal responsibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Act reasonably to prevent harm","explanation_en":"Duty of care requires reasonable actions to reduce foreseeable harm.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"注意義務(duty of care)要求教練/專業人員以合理謹慎的態度預防可預見的傷害，不是保證零傷害，也不是完全規避責任。"},{"id":"q1272","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which law protects medical information privacy?","options":["ADA","FERPA","HIPAA","OSHA"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"HIPAA","explanation_en":"HIPAA governs medical information confidentiality.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"健康保險可攜性與責任法(HIPAA)規範個人健康資訊的機密與隱私；ADA管無障礙、OSHA管職場安全、FERPA管教育紀錄。"},{"id":"q1273","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which document outlines inherent risks of participation?","options":["Code of conduct","Incident report","Liability waiver","Emergency plan"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Liability waiver","explanation_en":"Liability waivers inform participants of inherent risks.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"責任免除同意書(liability waiver)由參與者在活動前簽署，載明參與活動的固有風險與自願同意，以降低設施與人員的法律風險。"},{"id":"q1274","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Recommended space per athlete in a weight room is approximately:","options":["10–15 sq ft","20–25 sq ft","35–50 sq ft","75–100 sq ft"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"35–50 sq ft","explanation_en":"35–50 square feet per athlete promotes safety and flow.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"重訓空間每位練習者約需35至50平方呎，才能兼顧動作幅度、保護站位與動線安全。"},{"id":"q1275","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which equipment requires the most frequent inspection?","options":["Foam rollers","Resistance bands","Barbells and racks","Mats"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Barbells and racks","explanation_en":"High-load equipment requires frequent inspection.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"槓鈴與深蹲架負荷高、使用頻繁，關係選手安全，需最經常的檢查(裂痕、磨損、插銷、卡勾)；泡棉軸、彈力帶、墊子磨損風險低。"},{"id":"q1276","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which maintenance task is essential for treadmills?","options":["Replacing motors monthly","Lubricating the belt","Calibrating incline daily","Tightening frame bolts weekly"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Lubricating the belt","explanation_en":"Belt lubrication reduces friction and wear.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跑步機必做的保養是為跑帶與底板之間上潤滑油，減少摩擦與馬達負載，延長器材壽命。"},{"id":"q1277","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Continuing education primarily ensures:","options":["Higher salaries","Updated knowledge and competency","Reduced liability automatically","Shorter work hours"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Updated knowledge and competency","explanation_en":"Continuing education maintains professional competency.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"繼續教育的主要價值在於維持並更新專業知識與執行能力，讓執業內容符合最新實證；薪資與工時只是附帶效應。"},{"id":"q1278","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which hiring factor is MOST important for S&C staff?","options":["Appearance","Marketing skill","Certification and experience","Social media presence"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Certification and experience","explanation_en":"Credentials and experience ensure safety and effectiveness.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"進用肌力與體能人員時，證照與實務經驗是最重要的條件，直接關聯指導品質、安全性與成效。"},{"id":"q1279","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which behavior is unethical?","options":["Reporting abuse","Recommending PEDs","Teaching warm-ups","Promoting recovery"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Recommending PEDs","explanation_en":"Recommending PEDs violates ethical standards.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"教練推薦或提供增能藥物(PED)違反職業倫理與反興奮劑規範；通報虐待、教導暖身與推廣恢復都是正向專業行為。"},{"id":"q1280","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training method best improves rate of force development?","options":["Steady-state cardio","Slow eccentrics","Explosive lifts","Isometric holds"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Explosive lifts","explanation_en":"Explosive lifts improve rapid force production.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"要提升力量生成速率(RFD)，最有效的是爆發性舉(ballistic/explosive lifts)，以最大意圖快速移動負荷；慢離心與等長對RFD幫助有限。"},{"id":"q1281","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which adaptation increases first during endurance training?","options":["Capillary density","Muscle hypertrophy","Maximal strength","Tendon stiffness"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Capillary density","explanation_en":"Capillary density increases early with endurance training.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"耐力訓練中最先出現的適應包含微血管密度增加(數週內即可發生)；肌肥大與最大力量是抗阻訓練的適應。"},{"id":"q1282","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which fuel source predominates at rest?","options":["Carbohydrate","Protein","Fat","ATP-PCr"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Fat","explanation_en":"Fat is the primary fuel source at rest.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"休息狀態下身體以脂肪氧化為主要燃料，提供大部分能量；強度上升後碳水的貢獻才逐漸超過脂肪。"},{"id":"q1283","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training goal uses loads of ~85–95% 1RM?","options":["Hypertrophy","Muscular endurance","Maximal strength","Speed"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Maximal strength","explanation_en":"High loads target maximal strength.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"約85至95%1RM的高負荷、低次數、長休息安排，對應最大肌力發展目標；肥大與耐力用較低負荷。"},{"id":"q1284","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which plyometric progression variable should increase last?","options":["Volume","Intensity","Complexity","Landing height"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Intensity","explanation_en":"Intensity should progress last to reduce injury risk.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"彈震訓練的進展原則：先增加訓練量，最後才增加強度(落地高度、單腳化等)，讓組織有時間適應，降低傷害風險。"},{"id":"q1285","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which rest interval is typical for hypertrophy?","options":["<30 sec","30–90 sec","2–5 min","5–10 min"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"30–90 sec","explanation_en":"Moderate rest supports hypertrophy.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肥大訓練的組間休息通常為30至90秒，屬中等休息，維持代謝壓力與訓練密度；2至5分鐘是最大力量的休息。"},{"id":"q1286","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best assesses aerobic endurance?","options":["Wingate","Cooper test","Vertical jump","1RM bench"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Cooper test","explanation_en":"The Cooper test estimates aerobic endurance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"庫珀12分鐘跑以距離推估心肺適能，是評估有氧耐力的選項；Wingate測無氧，垂直跳與1RM測神經肌肉表現。"},{"id":"q1287","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which movement pattern is evaluated by the inline lunge?","options":["Rotational stability","Unilateral balance and mobility","Upper-body pushing","Aerobic capacity"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Unilateral balance and mobility","explanation_en":"Inline lunge assesses unilateral balance and mobility.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"直線弓箭步(inline lunge)評估單側下肢的平衡、穩定與活動度，屬於單邊動作篩檢，不是旋轉或心肺測試。"},{"id":"q1288","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which variable MOST influences sprint max velocity?","options":["Force application rate","Stride length and frequency","Reaction time","Muscle endurance"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Stride length and frequency","explanation_en":"Max velocity depends on stride length and frequency.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"最高速度=步長×步頻，極速表現最直接受步長與步頻兩個變數決定；要提升極速就要從這兩者與其背後的力量素質下手。"},{"id":"q1289","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which mineral is critical for oxygen transport?","options":["Calcium","Iron","Magnesium","Potassium"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Iron","explanation_en":"Iron is a key component of hemoglobin.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鐵是血紅素與肌紅蛋白的成分，直接決定攜氧能力；缺鐵時輸氧下降、耐力表現最先受損。"},{"id":"q1290","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which post-exercise strategy best supports muscle protein synthesis?","options":["Fat-only intake","Protein with essential amino acids","Carbohydrate only","No intake for 6 hours"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Protein with essential amino acids","explanation_en":"Protein with essential amino acids stimulates MPS.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"運動後攝取含必需胺基酸(尤其白胺酸)的蛋白質，最能刺激肌肉蛋白合成(MPS)，支援修復與適應。"},{"id":"q1291","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which principle states training adaptations are specific to imposed demands?","options":["Overload","Specificity","Variation","Reversibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Specificity","explanation_en":"The specificity principle governs adaptations.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"特異性原則(specificity)：訓練適應與所施加的專項需求一致，練什麼得什麼，計畫須依運動需求與測驗目標設計。"},{"id":"q1292","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training method alternates upper and lower body to improve efficiency?","options":["Circuit","Split routine","Superset","Complex"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Superset","explanation_en":"Supersets alternate muscle groups for efficiency.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"超級組(superset)把兩個動作連續交替執行(常見於上/下肢或主動肌/拮抗肌)，在另一肌群工作時獲得恢復，提升時間效率。"},{"id":"q1293","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which sleep duration best supports recovery?","options":["4–5 hrs","5–6 hrs","6–7 hrs","7–9 hrs"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"7–9 hrs","explanation_en":"7–9 hours supports hormonal recovery.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"每晚7至9小時睡眠最能支援恢復：生長激素分泌、組織修復、記憶固化與荷爾蒙平衡都在睡眠中完成。"},{"id":"q1294","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test measures maximal strength?","options":["Vertical jump","1RM bench press","Yo-Yo test","300-yard shuttle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1RM bench press","explanation_en":"1RM testing measures maximal strength.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"1RM仰臥推舉以一次可舉起的最大重量測量最大肌力，是最大力量的直接評估；垂直跳測功率，Yo-Yo測耐力。"},{"id":"q1295","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which facility feature MOST improves safety?","options":["Mirrors everywhere","Clear traffic flow","Dim lighting","Tight equipment spacing"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Clear traffic flow","explanation_en":"Clear traffic flow reduces collisions and accidents.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"場地動線清晰(clear traffic flow)對設施安全的貢獻最大，能減少碰撞、搬運交錯與擁擠；器材擠壓與光線不足反而增加風險。"},{"id":"q1296","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which carbohydrate timing is ideal when two-a-day training occurs?","options":["Only at breakfast","Immediately post-exercise","Before bed only","Every other day"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Immediately post-exercise","explanation_en":"Immediate intake accelerates glycogen restoration.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"一天兩訓(兩節課)之間，運動後立即攝取碳水化合物能最快補充肝醣，確保同日第二場訓練與隔天表現。"},{"id":"q1297","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which component MOST contributes to muscular endurance?","options":["High force","Oxidative capacity","Tendon stiffness","Joint angle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Oxidative capacity","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance relies on oxidative capacity.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌耐力最依賴氧化能力(粒線體與氧化酵素活性、微血管供給)，讓肌肉能長時間反覆收縮；高輸出力量與肌腱剛性偏力量/速度屬性。"},{"id":"q1298","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training surface is safest for plyometrics?","options":["Concrete","Rubberized floor","Hardwood","Uneven ground"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rubberized floor","explanation_en":"Rubberized surfaces absorb impact.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"彈震訓練的落地面以橡膠墊/緩衝性地板最安全，能吸收衝擊、降低關節負荷；水泥地衝擊最大，不平整地面增加扭傷風險。"},{"id":"q1299","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best assesses agility?","options":["40-yard dash","Pro agility shuttle","Wingate","Sit-and-reach"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Pro agility shuttle","explanation_en":"The pro agility shuttle evaluates rapid change of direction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Pro agility shuttle(5-10-5)要求快速煞車並180度轉向，是評估敏捷與變向能力的測試；40碼測直線速度，Wingate測無氧功率。"},{"id":"q1300","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which variable MOST affects hypertrophy?","options":["Time under tension","Velocity","Reaction time","Stretch reflex"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Time under tension","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy is influenced by mechanical tension and TUT.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌肉肥大最受到機械張力與收縮時間(time under tension， TUT)影響，適度延長張力暴露並累積足量訓練量是肥大的關鍵變數。"},{"id":"q1301","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which principle explains performance loss after detraining?","options":["Specificity","Overload","Reversibility","Variation"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Reversibility","explanation_en":"Reversibility explains loss of adaptations.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"可逆性原則(reversibility)說明停止訓練後適應會逐漸消失，體能與表現回退，對應去訓練化的現象。"},{"id":"q1302","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which nutrient buffers hydrogen ions during high-intensity exercise?","options":["Creatine","Beta-alanine","Iron","Vitamin D"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Beta-alanine","explanation_en":"Beta-alanine increases carnosine buffering.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸(beta-alanine)提升肌肉肌肽濃度，增強對氫離子的緩衝能力，延緩高強度運動造成的酸中毒與疲勞。"},{"id":"q1303","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which law ensures facility accessibility?","options":["OSHA","ADA","HIPAA","FERPA"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"ADA","explanation_en":"The ADA mandates accessibility.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"美國身心障礙者法(ADA)要求設施提供無障礙進出與使用；OSHA是職場安全，HIPAA是醫療隱私，FERPA是教育紀錄。"},{"id":"q1304","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which indicator reflects anaerobic capacity?","options":["VO2max","Wingate mean power","BMI","Flexibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Wingate mean power","explanation_en":"Mean power reflects anaerobic capacity.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Wingate測試的平均功率(mean power)反映整體無氧糖解供能能力，是無氧能力的指標；尖峰功率代表磷酸原系統輸出。"},{"id":"q1305","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training frequency best suits novice lifters?","options":["1×/week","2–3×/week","5–6×/week","Daily max lifts"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"2–3×/week","explanation_en":"Novices benefit from moderate frequency.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"新手適合每週2至3次的抗阻訓練頻率，足以提供刺激又保留恢復空間；每天操練最大重量對新手負荷過重。"},{"id":"q1306","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best evaluates flexibility?","options":["Sit-and-reach","Vertical jump","1RM squat","Yo-Yo test"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Sit-and-reach","explanation_en":"Sit-and-reach measures flexibility.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"坐椅體前屈(sit-and-reach)是評估膕旁肌與下背柔軟度的標準測試；垂直跳與1RM測力量，Yo-Yo測耐力。"},{"id":"q1307","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training goal uses <60% 1RM?","options":["Strength","Hypertrophy","Muscular endurance","Maximal power"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Muscular endurance","explanation_en":"Muscular endurance uses light loads.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"60%1RM以下的輕負荷搭配高次數(12以上)與短休息，發展肌耐力；力量、肥大、功率用的負荷都更高。"},{"id":"q1308","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which factor MOST improves maximal velocity sprinting?","options":["Force at ground contact","Stride mechanics","Endurance","Overspeed only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Stride mechanics","explanation_en":"Max velocity depends heavily on mechanics.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"達到最高速後，跑動機制(姿勢、擺臂、著地位置與蹬地方向)決定力量能否有效轉為前進動力；肌力是基礎，但極速表現高度依賴技術。"},{"id":"q1309","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which document protects client privacy?","options":["ADA","HIPAA","OSHA","Waiver"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"HIPAA","explanation_en":"HIPAA protects medical information.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"HIPAA(健康保險可攜性與責任法)保障客戶個人醫療健康資訊的隱私與機密性。"},{"id":"q1310","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best assesses core stability?","options":["Plank hold","Sit-up test","1RM squat","Bench press"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Plank hold","explanation_en":"Plank tests core stability.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"棒式支撐(plank)以等長收縮評估核心抗伸展的穩定能力；仰臥起坐測腹肌耐力，深蹲與推舉測的是肌力。"},{"id":"q1311","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training method emphasizes continuous movement with minimal rest?","options":["Split routine","Circuit training","Linear periodization","Cluster sets"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Circuit training","explanation_en":"Circuit training minimizes rest.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"迴圈訓練(circuit training)以多個站位連續執行、站間休息極短為特徵，強調持續輸出與心肺代謝壓力。"},{"id":"q1312","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which factor MOST determines sprint stride length?","options":["Force production","Flexibility","Balance","Body fat"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Force production","explanation_en":"Force application influences stride length.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"步長主要由蹬地時的力量輸出決定：對地面施力越大、越有效轉為水平推進，跨距才能拉開；柔軟度與平衡只是輔助條件。"},{"id":"q1313","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which vitamin supports calcium absorption?","options":["Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Vitamin K","Vitamin E"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Vitamin D","explanation_en":"Vitamin D enhances calcium absorption.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"維生素D促進腸道對鈣的吸收並維持血鈣平衡，對骨骼健康與肌肉功能都關鍵；維生素C幫助膠原合成與鐵吸收。"},{"id":"q1314","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which measure reflects test objectivity?","options":["Same tester scores similarly","Same test measures same construct","Same athlete repeats result","Test relevance to sport"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Same tester scores similarly","explanation_en":"Objectivity reflects scorer agreement.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"客觀性(objectivity)指不同評分者對同一表現給分一致；同一受試者重測一致是信度，測到同一構念是效度。"},{"id":"q1315","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training adaptation increases VO2max?","options":["Increased mitochondrial density","Hypertrophy","Neural drive","Tendon stiffness"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increased mitochondrial density","explanation_en":"Mitochondrial density improves oxygen utilization.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"粒線體密度與氧化酵素活性提高，有氧三磷酸腺苷再合成能力上升，是有氧訓練後與最大攝氧量提升相關的周邊適應。"},{"id":"q1316","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which method best improves lateral agility?","options":["Sled pushes","Cone drills","Tempo runs","Vertical jumps"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Cone drills","explanation_en":"Cone drills train change of direction.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"側向敏捷以錐筒訓練(cone drills)最對症：安排側向滑步、切步與變向，直接練習橫向減速再加速；雪橇推送偏直線加速。"},{"id":"q1317","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training goal uses 30–90 sec rest?","options":["Strength","Power","Hypertrophy","Speed"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Hypertrophy","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy typically uses moderate rest.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"30至90秒的組間休息對應肥大訓練的標準安排；最大力量與功率需要更長的2至5分鐘。"},{"id":"q1318","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which indicator suggests glycogen depletion?","options":["Muscle pump","Rapid fatigue","Increased strength","Lower heart rate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rapid fatigue","explanation_en":"Glycogen depletion leads to early fatigue.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肝醣耗盡時運動強度驟降、快速疲勞，耐力專案中即所謂撞牆現象；肌肉幫浦、力量上升與心率下降都不是缺醣徵兆。"},{"id":"q1319","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which law governs workplace safety?","options":["HIPAA","OSHA","ADA","FERPA"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"OSHA","explanation_en":"OSHA governs workplace safety.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"職業安全與健康法(OSHA)規範職場工作環境安全，包含設施員工的工安要求；HIPAA管隱私，ADA管無障礙。"},{"id":"q1320","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which movement best trains triple extension?","options":["Back squat","Power clean","Bench press","Pull-up"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power clean","explanation_en":"Olympic lifts train triple extension.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"動力清潔(power clean)等奧林匹克舉動作要求髖、膝、踝三重伸展(triple extension)把槓鈴加速，是訓練三重伸展的最佳選項；後蹲是基礎但速度特徵較低。"},{"id":"q1321","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training variable MOST affects intensity?","options":["Load","Volume","Frequency","Exercise order"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Load","explanation_en":"Intensity is primarily determined by load.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"訓練強度(intensity)主要由負荷(load，%1RM)定義，是強度最直接的決定變數；量、頻率與動作順序影響總負荷而非強度本質。"},{"id":"q1322","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which adaptation results from long-term endurance training?","options":["Increased capillary density","Reduced mitochondria","Lower VO2max","Increased fiber IIx"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Increased capillary density","explanation_en":"Endurance training increases capillarization.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"長期耐力訓練會增加微血管密度(毛細化)，改善氧與養分輸送及代謝物移除；粒線體增加、第IIx型比例不會上升。"},{"id":"q1323","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which nutrient is MOST important pre-endurance event?","options":["Fat","Protein","Carbohydrate","Alcohol"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Carbohydrate","explanation_en":"Carbohydrates fuel endurance performance.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"耐力專案賽前最重要是補充碳水化合物，最大化肝醣儲存；蛋白質與脂肪消化較慢，只做輔助。"},{"id":"q1324","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which assessment identifies unilateral asymmetries?","options":["Hurdle step","Push-up","Sit-and-reach","Plank"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hurdle step","explanation_en":"Hurdle step reveals unilateral deficits.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"跨欄測試(hurdle step)在單腿支撐下完成跨步，能暴露左右側在穩定與活動度上的不對稱；坐椅體前屈與棒式不比較雙側差異。"},{"id":"q1325","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training goal uses maximal intent with light loads?","options":["Hypertrophy","Power","Endurance","Flexibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power","explanation_en":"Power training emphasizes intent and speed.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"功率訓練強調以最大意圖(maximal intent)用輕至中等負荷快速移動，把速度放在第一優先；肥大與耐力不要求速度意圖。"},{"id":"q1326","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which variable MOST influences muscular endurance?","options":["Max force","Oxidative enzymes","Joint angle","Reaction time"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Oxidative enzymes","explanation_en":"Endurance depends on oxidative capacity.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"肌耐力最依賴氧化酵素活性與粒線體功能等氧化能力；最大力量、關節角度與反應時間偏重神經肌肉表現。"},{"id":"q1327","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which phase precedes competition?","options":["Transition","Peaking","Preparatory","Recovery"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Peaking","explanation_en":"The peaking phase precedes competition.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"巬峰期(peaking)緊接在比賽之前，透過減量消除疲勞、讓先前累積的適應轉為比賽表現；過渡期在賽季結束後。"},{"id":"q1328","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test measures mean anaerobic power?","options":["Cooper test","Wingate test","Vertical jump","1RM bench"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Wingate test","explanation_en":"Wingate provides peak and mean power.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Wingate測試同時提供尖峰功率與30秒平均功率，平均功率即平均無氧輸出；庫珀測有氧，1RM測最大力量。"},{"id":"q1329","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which nutrient delays fatigue by buffering hydrogen ions?","options":["Creatine","Beta-alanine","Vitamin C","Iron"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Beta-alanine","explanation_en":"Beta-alanine increases muscle carnosine.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"β-丙胺酸提升肌肉肌肽含量，肌肽可緩衝高強度運動產生的氫離子，延緩肌肉酸中毒與疲勞。"},{"id":"q1330","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training surface is LEAST appropriate for plyometrics?","options":["Rubber flooring","Grass","Concrete","Wood"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Concrete","explanation_en":"Concrete does not absorb impact.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"水泥地幾乎不吸收衝擊，落地反作用力最大，最不適合彈震訓練；橡膠地板、草地與木地板都提供較多緩衝。"},{"id":"q1331","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which adaptation increases with sprint training?","options":["Type I fiber dominance","Increased stride frequency","Reduced neural drive","Lower power output"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Increased stride frequency","explanation_en":"Sprint training improves stride frequency.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"衝刺訓練透過神經適應與動作技術改善，可提高步頻與蹬地速率；第一型肌纖維主導、神經驅動降低、功率下降都是反效果。"},{"id":"q1332","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test best evaluates change-of-direction speed?","options":["40-yard dash","Pro agility shuttle","1RM squat","Wingate"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Pro agility shuttle","explanation_en":"Pro agility measures COD ability.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"Pro agility(5-10-5)以短距離煞車加180度折返評估變向速度；40碼測直線最高速，1RM與Wingate不測變向。"},{"id":"q1333","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which nutrient supports red blood cell production?","options":["Iron","Calcium","Vitamin E","Zinc"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Iron","explanation_en":"Iron supports hemoglobin production.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"鐵支援血紅素合成與紅血球生成，是輸氧能力的物質基礎；鈣、鋅、維生素E都不直接主導紅血球製造。"},{"id":"q1334","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training goal uses low load and high velocity?","options":["Strength","Hypertrophy","Power","Endurance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Power","explanation_en":"Power training emphasizes speed.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"低負荷搭配高速度、最大輸出意圖是功率訓練的負荷-速度特徵；最大力量用高負荷低速，耐力用輕負荷高次數。"},{"id":"q1335","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which document details emergency procedures?","options":["Liability waiver","Emergency action plan","Code of ethics","Job description"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Emergency action plan","explanation_en":"Emergency action plans outline emergency procedures.","tags":["practice-test"],"source":"packman","explanation_zh":"緊急應變計畫(Emergency Action Plan， EAP)內詳載緊急處理流程：人員分工、通報系統、裝備位置、場館動線與演練時程。"},{"id":"q1336","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"With consistent aerobic training, what are the possible adaptations?","options":["Rise in percentage of body fat","Rise in ATP stores","Rise in capillary density in muscle fibers","Hypertrophy of Type II fibers"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Rise in capillary density in muscle fibers","explanation_en":"With consistent aerobic training, one of the notable physiological adaptations is an increase in capillary density within muscle fibers. This enhancement facilitates the efficient delivery of oxygen and nutrients to the working muscles, promoting endurance and recovery. It also aids in the removal of waste products from the muscle cells. This adaptation is crucial for improving aerobic capacity and overall endurance performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"持續有氧訓練會提高肌纖維間的微血管密度（capillary density），改善肌肉的氧與營養輸送並加速代謝廢物排除。其他選項相反或有誤：體脂率通常下降、ATP總量變化有限、肥大發生在第Ⅱ型纖維而非有氧 Adaptation 的特徵。"},{"id":"q1337","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The size principle refers to which of the following?","options":["Mitochondrial density","Muscle fiber length","Angle of pennation","Motor unit recruitment order"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Motor unit recruitment order","explanation_en":"The size principle pertains to the order in which motor units are recruited during muscle contraction. According to this principle, motor units with smaller, more fatigue-resistant muscle fibers (often Type I fibers) are recruited first, followed by larger, more powerful, but faster-fatiguing units (like Type II fibers). This sequential recruitment ensures efficient muscle function, allowing muscles to sustain prolonged activities and also produce forceful contractions when necessary.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"大小原則（size principle）指運動單位的招募順序：先招募較小、抗疲勞的第Ⅰ型運動單位，強度增加時再依序招募較大的第Ⅱ型運動單位。與粒線體密度、肌纖維長度或羽狀角無關。"},{"id":"q1338","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The vertical jump is primarily performed in which anatomical plane?","options":["Coronal","Sagittal","Transverse","Frontal"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Sagittal","explanation_en":"The vertical jump predominantly occurs in the sagittal plane. The sagittal plane divides the body into left and right halves and involves movements that are forward (flexion) and backward (extension). In the vertical jump, the primary motions are the flexion and extension of the hips, knees, and ankles as the individual prepares for and executes the jump. Thus, these actions are aligned with the sagittal plane's characteristics.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"垂直跳的髖、膝、踝屈曲與伸展都沿矢狀面（sagittal plane）前後方向進行，故主要發生在矢狀面；額狀面（coronal/frontal）是側向運動，橫斷面是旋轉運動。"},{"id":"q1339","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which electrical occurrences are undetectable during a normal electrocardiogram (ECG)?","options":["Atrial repolarization","Atrial depolarization","Ventricular repolarization","Ventricular depolarization"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Atrial repolarization","explanation_en":"An electrocardiogram (ECG) measures the electrical activity of the heart and is used to depict the stages of the cardiac cycle. Atrial depolarization is represented by the P wave, while ventricular depolarization is shown by the QRS complex. Ventricular repolarization is seen as the T wave. However, atrial repolarization is usually obscured by the larger QRS complex and is, therefore, undetectable during a normal ECG.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"心電圖上P波代表心房去極化、QRS複合波代表心室去極化、T波代表心室再極化。心房再極化的電位小且被QRS複合波掩蓋，因此在正常心電圖上偵測不到。"},{"id":"q1340","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While skating, which of these hip movements depends on the gluteus maximus for a hockey athlete?","options":["Hip flexion","Internal hip rotation","Hip Adduction","External hip rotation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"External hip rotation","explanation_en":"The gluteus maximus is the largest muscle in the buttocks and plays a significant role in various hip movements. While hip flexion is primarily facilitated by the hip flexors, and hip adduction by the adductor muscles, the gluteus maximus is particularly involved in hip extension and external rotation. Internal hip rotation, on the other hand, is largely mediated by other muscles of the hip. Therefore, for a hockey athlete skating, the movement most dependent on the gluteus maximus is external hip rotation.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"臀大肌（gluteus maximus）的主要功能為髖伸展與髖外旋，滑冰動作的蹬冰階段需要髖外旋，因此依賴臀大肌。髖屈曲由髂腰肌等屈髜肌負責，內收由內收肌群負責。"},{"id":"q1341","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the location of golgi tendon organs and muscle spindles, respectively?","options":["Tendons","Tendons and muscles","Muscles","Deep fascia"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Tendons and muscles","explanation_en":"GTOs are located at the junction between muscles and tendons, monitoring muscle tension. On the other hand, muscle spindles are embedded within the muscle fibers, detecting changes in muscle length. Thus, the correct locations for GTOs and muscle spindles are tendons and muscles, respectively.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器（GTO）位於肌肉與肌腱交界處，感受肌肉張力；肌梭（muscle spindle）位於肌肉內，感受肌肉長度變化。所以答案是「肌腱與肌肉」。"},{"id":"q1342","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The series elastic component (SEC) primarily reserves energy for plyometric action in what body structures?","options":["Ligaments","Tendons","Joints","Muscle fibers"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Tendons","explanation_en":"The series elastic component (SEC) refers to the elastic elements found in series with muscle fibers, specifically in the musculotendinous unit. Tendons are the primary structures responsible for storing and releasing energy during plyometric actions, behaving much like a spring. When muscles contract, tendons can stretch and store energy, and during a rapid subsequent elongation, this stored energy is released to aid in the action. Therefore, it is the tendons that primarily reserve energy for plyometric action in the body.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"系列彈性成分（series elastic component, SEC）主要指肌腱等與肌纖維串聯的彈性結構，能在牽拉時儲存彈效能並在收縮時釋放，是增強式（plyometric）動作的能量來源。"},{"id":"q1343","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of these actions describes transverse plane abduction of the shoulder?","options":["Volleyball dig","Backhand tennis stroke","Basketball pass","Boxing jab"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Backhand tennis stroke","explanation_en":"The transverse plane divides the body into superior and inferior sections and movements in this plane revolve around a vertical axis. Transverse plane abduction of the shoulder, often termed horizontal abduction, involves moving the arm away from the body's midline in a horizontal direction. A backhand tennis stroke captures this movement, as the arm is brought away from the body's center in a horizontal fashion to hit the ball. Thus, the action that best describes transverse plane abduction of the shoulder is the backhand tennis stroke.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"網球反拍揮拍是肩關節在橫斷面的水平外展（horizontal abduction）：手臂沿水平方向遠離身體中線繞縱軸運動。拳擊刺拳、籃球傳球以屈曲/水平內收為主，排球墊球以肩屈曲為主。"},{"id":"q1344","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following stimulates muscle spindles?","options":["Muscle tension change","Muscle size change","Force output change","Muscle length change"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Muscle length change","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles are specialized sensory receptors located within muscles, designed to sense changes in muscle length and the rate of those changes. When a muscle is stretched, the muscle spindles are also stretched and, in response, they send signals to the brain. These signals provide feedback on muscle length and the speed of the stretch, allowing for reflexive contractions to prevent potential injury. Therefore, it is a change in muscle length (stretching) that primarily stimulates muscle spindles.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"肌梭是位於肌肉內的本體感受器，專司偵測肌肉長度及其改變速率；肌肉被拉長時肌梭受牽拉而放電。張力變化則主要由高爾基腱器偵測。"},{"id":"q1345","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following refers to artificially increasing red blood cell mass?","options":["Blood transfusion","Oxygen surplus","Blood doping","EPO"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Blood doping","explanation_en":"Blood doping is the practice of artificially increasing the number of red blood cells (RBCs) in the bloodstream, typically to enhance athletic performance. An increased RBC count can improve oxygen delivery to muscles, potentially boosting stamina and performance. While methods such as blood transfusions and the use of erythropoietin (EPO) are employed to achieve blood doping, the term \"blood doping\" itself directly refers to the act of artificially enhancing RBC mass. Hence, the correct answer is C. Blood doping.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"血液 doping（blood doping）指人工提高紅血球總量以增進帶氧能力的總稱，輸血與EPO注射都是其手段，題目問的是這個總稱本身。"},{"id":"q1346","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which joint is stabilized by the following: supraspinatus, infraspinatus, subscapularis and teres minor?","options":["Glenohumeral","Acromioclavicular","Scapulothoracic","Patellofemoral"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Glenohumeral","explanation_en":"The supraspinatus, infraspinatus, subscapularis, and teres minor are collectively known as the rotator cuff muscles. Their primary function is to stabilize and move the glenohumeral joint, which is the ball-and-socket joint that connects the humerus (upper arm bone) to the scapula (shoulder blade). Each of these muscles has a specific role, but they all work together to ensure smooth and coordinated movement while maintaining stability in the glenohumeral joint.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"棘上肌、棘下肌、肩胛下肌與小圓肌構成旋肌袖（rotator cuff），負責穩定盂肱關節（glenohumeral joint，肩關節）。"},{"id":"q1347","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Depletion of which of the following substrates induces fatigue?","options":["Phosphagens","Branch Chain Amino Acids","Lactic acid","Glucose"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Phosphagens","explanation_en":"Phosphagens, primarily composed of creatine phosphate, are immediate energy sources for high-intensity, short-duration activities in muscles. When an individual engages in quick and intense bursts of activity, the phosphagen system provides energy by donating a phosphate group to ADP to form ATP, the body's primary energy currency. As these high-intensity activities continue, the phosphagen stores get rapidly depleted. Once the stores of creatine phosphate are exhausted, the ability of the muscle to sustain maximal power output decreases, leading to fatigue.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"磷酸原（phosphagens，主要是磷酸肌酸CP）是高強度短時間動作的立即能量來源，耗盡後會導致疲勞，是此題答案。乳酸不是疲勞底物；血糖與BCAA耗盡不是此機制。"},{"id":"q1348","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While performing resistance training, which structure of the knee is most vulnerable to injury?","options":["ITB","Patella (knee cap) and surrounding structures","MCL","ACL"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Patella (knee cap) and surrounding structures","explanation_en":"During resistance training, especially exercises that involve knee extension and flexion, the patella (knee cap) and its surrounding structures are particularly vulnerable to injury. The patella is a sesamoid bone that sits within the patellar tendon, providing a mechanical advantage to the quadriceps muscles. The repetitive bending and straightening of the knee, especially under resistance or with improper form, can lead to various conditions like patellar tendonitis, patellofemoral pain syndrome, and chondromalacia patellae. As such, while all the listed structures in the knee can be at risk under certain conditions, the patella and its surrounding structures are considered the most vulnerable during resistance training.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練中反覆的膝屈伸使髕骨（patella）與髕腱等周圍結構承受高度剪下與擠壓應力，最易受傷（如髕股疼痛症候群、髕腱病變）。"},{"id":"q1349","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic training increases which of the following?","options":["Maximum RFD","Serum testosterone","Resting heart rate","ATP stores"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"ATP stores","explanation_en":"Aerobic training primarily focuses on improving the body's ability to use oxygen efficiently, enhancing endurance. One adaptation that occurs as a result of consistent aerobic training is an increase in the body's ability to produce and store ATP (adenosine triphosphate), which is the primary energy currency for cellular activities. As aerobic training progresses, there's an upregulation in the number and efficiency of mitochondria in muscle cells, which are the sites of ATP production. Consequently, these adaptations lead to an increase in ATP stores, allowing muscles to sustain activity for longer periods without fatigue.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練可提高肌肉的ATP儲存量與生成能力（伴隨粒線體與氧化酵素增加）。靜息心率會下降而非上升；最大力量發展速率與血睪酮不是有氧訓練的主要提升項。"},{"id":"q1350","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Relative to the latissimus dorsi, where is the trapezius positioned?","options":["Superior","Dorsal","Posterior","Inferior"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Superior","explanation_en":"The latissimus dorsi is a large, broad muscle located in the back that stretches to the sides and behind the arm. The trapezius, on the other hand, is positioned above the latissimus dorsi and spans the neck, shoulders, and upper to mid-back. When considering anatomical positioning, \"superior\" means \"above\" or \"toward the head.\" Therefore, relative to the latissimus dorsi, the trapezius is positioned superiorly or above it.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"斜方肌位於背上半部，相對背闊肌在上方，即 superior（上方）位置。解剖方位用語中 superior 指靠近頭側。"},{"id":"q1351","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What joint action occurs to increase the angle between the radius and ulna?","options":["Hyper-extension","Flexion","Adduction","Extension"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Extension","explanation_en":"The radius and ulna are the two bones of the forearm. When referring to the action that increases the angle between these two bones, particularly at the elbow joint, we are discussing the straightening or opening movement of the elbow. This movement is called extension. Conversely, when the angle between the radius and ulna decreases, or the elbow bends, it is termed flexion.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"橈骨與尺骨之間角度增大即肘關節伸展（extension）；角度變小才是屈曲（flexion）。"},{"id":"q1352","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How is the force-velocity curve influenced by a rise in rate of force development?","options":["The curve is unaffected","Left shift of the curve","Shifts the curve to the right","Increases the peak of the curve"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Shifts the curve to the right","explanation_en":"The force-velocity curve describes the inverse relationship between the force a muscle can produce and the speed at which it contracts. Essentially, as the speed of a contraction increases (velocity), the force a muscle can produce decreases, and vice versa.\nThe rate of force development (RFD) refers to how quickly force can be produced from the onset of contraction. When RFD increases, it means that an individual can produce force more rapidly. This allows for greater forces to be produced at faster velocities, effectively shifting the force-velocity curve to the right.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"力量發展速率（RFD）提升表示能在更短時間內產出更大力量，使肌肉在較高收縮速度下仍可維持較大力量輸出，等效於力量-速度曲線右移。"},{"id":"q1353","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the starting position for the abdominal crunch?","options":["Prone","Inverted","Supine","5-point body contact"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Supine","explanation_en":"The abdominal crunch is an exercise designed to target the rectus abdominis muscle. To begin this exercise, one should lie flat on their back with knees bent and feet flat on the ground. This position, where one is lying face up with the dorsal (back) side of the body in contact with the ground, is referred to as the supine position. Hence, the starting position for the abdominal crunch is the supine position.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"仰臥（supine，面朝上平躺）、雙膝彎曲腳踩地是仰臥卷腹（abdominal crunch）的起始姿勢；prone 是趴躺。"},{"id":"q1354","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which type of stretching involves active muscle engagement and a rebound-like motion where the end position is not maintained?","options":["Static stretch","Active stretch","PNF stretch","Ballistic stretch"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Ballistic stretch","explanation_en":"Ballistic stretching utilizes momentum and active muscular effort to stretch and typically involves bouncing or rapid, jerky movements. This method differs from other types of stretching in that the end position is not held. Instead, the individual uses the momentum of the movement to push the muscle beyond its normal range of motion. As a result, ballistic stretching is characterized by active muscle engagement and a rebound-like motion where the end position is not maintained.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"彈振式伸展（ballistic stretching）利用動量與主動肌肉收縮做反覆彈震動作，不維持終端姿勢；動態的彈震式與靜態、PNF伸展不同。"},{"id":"q1355","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the quadriceps muscles is positioned closest to the centerline of the body?","options":["Rectus femoris","Vastus Intermedius","Vastus medialis","Vastus lateralis"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Vastus medialis","explanation_en":"The quadriceps, a group of four muscles in the anterior thigh, work primarily to extend the knee. Of these four muscles, the vastus medialis is positioned medially, or toward the inner side of the thigh, making it closest to the centerline of the body. The term \"medialis\" itself indicates a medial or central positioning relative to other structures. Therefore, the vastus medialis is the quadriceps muscle that is positioned closest to the centerline of the body.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"vastus medialis（內側肌）位於大腿內側，最接近身體中線（medialis 即「內側」之意）；lateral 為外側，rectus femoris 在前正中表淺處但非最靠中線之定義選項。"},{"id":"q1356","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The latissimus dorsi acts as an antagonist in which of the following?","options":["Dead lift","Chin-ups","Dumbbell overhead press","Back squat"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Dumbbell overhead press","explanation_en":"The latissimus dorsi, often referred to as the \"lats,\" is a large, flat muscle on the back that stretches to the sides, behind the arm, and is partially covered by the trapezius on the back near the midline. Its primary functions include adduction, extension, and internal rotation of the arm.\nDuring a vertical chest press (or dumbbell overhead press as indicated in the options), the primary muscles at work are the pectorals and the deltoids as they push the weight upwards. The latissimus dorsi acts in opposition to this movement, given its functions in adduction and extension of the arm. Therefore, in the context of the vertical chest press, the latissimus dorsi serves as an antagonist.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"背闊肌負責肩關節內收、伸展與內旋；啞鈴肩上推（overhead press）需肩屈曲/外展，此時背闊肌作為拮抗肌被拉長並控制動作。死舉、引體向上、深蹲中背闊肌多為協同或穩定角色。"},{"id":"q1357","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What type of reaction results in a release of energy?","options":["Anabolic reaction","Exergonic reaction","Endergonic reaction","Delayed reaction"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Exergonic reaction","explanation_en":"Exergonic reactions are chemical reactions that release energy. This energy is often in the form of heat, light, or sound, and it can be used to do work in cells or systems. In a biological context, many cellular processes rely on the energy released from exergonic reactions to drive other reactions that require energy. In contrast to exergonic reactions, endergonic reactions require an input of energy. Therefore, the type of reaction that results in a release of energy is the exergonic reaction.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"放能反應（exergonic reaction）釋放能量（如ATP水解）；耗能反應稱 endergonic；合成代謝（anabolic）屬耗能反應。"},{"id":"q1358","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which heart structure is most typically compromised in a sufferer of chronic tachycardia?","options":["Conduction system","Bicuspid valve","Tricuspid valve","Atria"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Conduction system","explanation_en":"Tachycardia refers to an abnormally fast resting heart rate, typically considered as a heart rate over 100 beats per minute in adults. The heart's conduction system, which includes structures like the sinoatrial node (SA node), atrioventricular node (AV node), and the His-Purkinje system, is responsible for initiating and propagating electrical impulses that stimulate heart contractions.\nChronic tachycardia can strain the heart and, over time, potentially affect the heart's electrical conduction system. If the conduction system is compromised, it can lead to irregular heart rhythms or arrhythmias. Therefore, in someone with chronic tachycardia, the conduction system is the heart structure most typically compromised.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"心搏過速（tachycardia，靜息心率>100次/分）通常源於心臟傳導系統（conduction system，竇房結、房室結、希氏-浦金耶系統）異常，該系統負責控制心率。"},{"id":"q1359","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is not a goal of sports psychology?","options":["Measuring psychological phenomena","Investigation of the relationship between psychological variables and performance","Applying theoretical knowledge to improve athletic performance","Diagnosing athletes with suspected psychological disorders"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Investigation of the relationship between psychological variables and performance","explanation_en":"Sports psychology focuses on understanding the mental aspects of sports performance and how psychological factors can affect athletic achievement. The main goals include:\nMeasuring psychological phenomena to understand mental states and traits of athletes.\nInvestigating the relationship between psychological variables and performance to determine how factors like motivation, stress, or concentration can influence outcomes.\nApplying theoretical knowledge to enhance athletic performance by developing interventions, strategies, or techniques to optimize mental states.\nHowever, while sports psychologists might identify potential mental challenges that athletes face, they typically do not diagnose psychological disorders. Such diagnosis is usually left to clinical psychologists or psychiatrists.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"依題庫答案，「探究心理變項與表現之間的關係」屬基礎研究範疇；應用運動心理學的重心在測量心理現象與將理論應用於提升運動表現，心理疾患診斷則多由臨床心理師負責。"},{"id":"q1360","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":["Excitement, motivation, and confidence can be beneficial emotions","Excessive emotion in either direction can be harmful to performance","Maximal arousal is needed for optimal performance","Athletes must learn mental skills to accompany physical skills"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Maximal arousal is needed for optimal performance","explanation_en":"The statement \"Maximal arousal is needed for optimal performance\" is false. The relationship between arousal and performance is often depicted by the Inverted-U Hypothesis or the Yerkes-Dodson Law. This theory suggests that there's an optimal level of arousal for peak performance, but too little or too much arousal can hinder performance.\nThe optimal level of arousal can vary depending on the task and individual differences. For complex tasks, a moderate level of arousal is often best, while simpler tasks might benefit from higher arousal. Thus, maximal arousal is not always needed and can, in many instances, be detrimental to performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"「表現最佳需要最大喚醒」是錯誤敘述。倒U假說（Yerkes-Dodson法則）指出存在個體最佳喚醒水準，過高或過低的喚醒都會損害表現，而非越高越好。"},{"id":"q1361","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Arousal is characterized by which of the following?","options":["Athlete heart rate and blood pressure elevated","Associated with unpleasant events","Occurs independently of hormonal levels","Arousal is always present on a broad continuum"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Arousal is always present on a broad continuum","explanation_en":"Arousal refers to the physiological and psychological state of alertness and readiness, varying from deep sleep to intense excitement. It encompasses a spectrum of states, from low (relaxed, lethargic) to high (alert, anxious).\nThe statement \"Arousal is always present on a broad continuum\" captures this idea. It suggests that at any given time, an individual's level of arousal exists somewhere on this continuum, influenced by both internal and external factors. The level of arousal can impact performance, concentration, and decision-making, especially in athletic contexts. Different tasks and sports may require different optimal levels of arousal for peak performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"喚醒（arousal）是生理與心理的警覺準備狀態，從深睡到高度興奮連續存在於一整個光譜（continuum）上，並非全有全無。心率血壓上升是喚醒的表現特徵，但本題答案為「廣泛連續光譜」。"},{"id":"q1362","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anxiety manifested through physical symptoms such as elevated heart rate and tense muscles is known as which of the following?","options":["Cognitive anxiety","Somatic anxiety","State anxiety","Trait anxiety"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Somatic anxiety","explanation_en":"Somatic anxiety refers to the physical symptoms of anxiety, such as elevated heart rate, increased sweating, and muscle tension. These are the body's responses to stressors and are often experienced when an individual perceives a threat or is faced with a challenging situation. In contrast, cognitive anxiety pertains to the mental aspects, such as worry and negative thoughts. State anxiety denotes a temporary condition in response to a specific event, while trait anxiety is a more permanent characteristic of an individual's personality. Therefore, when anxiety manifests through physical symptoms like an elevated heart rate and tense muscles, it is known as somatic anxiety.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"軀體化焦慮（somatic anxiety）指焦慮的身體症狀，如心率上升、出汗、肌肉緊繃；認知性焦慮（cognitive anxiety）則是擔憂、負面想法等心理層面。"},{"id":"q1363","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Trait anxiety is defined as which of the following?","options":["Lack of physical and psychological efficiency","Enduring personality disposition towards perceiving an environment as threatening","Acute subjective experience of apprehension and uncertainty","High degree of ego involvement and perceived threat to self-esteem"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Enduring personality disposition towards perceiving an environment as threatening","explanation_en":"Trait anxiety refers to a stable and enduring aspect of an individual's personality, which influences their likelihood to perceive various situations as threatening or stressful. It's a consistent characteristic, making some individuals more prone to experience anxiety across different contexts and situations, regardless of the immediate environment. While state anxiety is a temporary reaction to a specific event or circumstance, trait anxiety is a more generalized predisposition. Thus, trait anxiety is accurately defined as an \"enduring personality disposition towards perceiving an environment as threatening.\"","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"特質焦慮（trait anxiety）是穩定的人格傾向，使人長期容易把環境知覺為具威脅性；狀態焦慮（state anxiety）才是當下主觀的緊張體驗。"},{"id":"q1364","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":["Stress is always associated with a decrease in performance","Stress represents a substantial imbalance between demand and response capability","Perception of stress largely determines the resulting performance effects","Stress generates arousal"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Stress is always associated with a decrease in performance","explanation_en":"The statement \"Stress is always associated with a decrease in performance\" is false. Stress and its effects on performance follow a complex relationship. The Inverted-U Hypothesis, for example, suggests that there is an optimal level of stress (or arousal) for peak performance, and both too little and too much stress can hinder performance. The perception of stress and how an individual copes with it can lead to either enhanced or diminished performance. For some individuals and in certain contexts, a moderate amount of stress can be motivating and lead to improved performance, while excessive stress can be debilitating. Therefore, it's not accurate to state that stress always results in decreased performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"「壓力必然導致表現下降」是錯誤敘述。壓力的影響取決於個體知覺與喚醒水準，適度壓力可提升表現（倒U關係），只有知覺與能力失衡時才造成負面效果。"},{"id":"q1365","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Drive theory proposes which of the following?","options":["Arousal facilitates performance until an optimal level","Different people in different types of performances perform best with very different levels of arousal","Catastrophic decline in abilities, rather than gradual decline, can occur past a certain arousal level","As an individual's arousal or state anxiety increases, the performance also increases"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"As an individual's arousal or state anxiety increases, the performance also increases","explanation_en":"Drive Theory postulates a linear relationship between arousal and performance. According to this theory, as arousal or state anxiety increases, so does performance. This perspective contrasts with other theories like the Inverted-U Hypothesis, which suggests that there's an optimal level of arousal for peak performance. In Drive Theory, there's no proposed upper limit where performance starts to decline. Instead, the theory suggests that heightened arousal continues to improve performance. Hence, the correct statement that aligns with Drive Theory is that \"As an individual's arousal or state anxiety increases, the performance also increases.\"","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"驅力理論（drive theory）主張喚醒與表現呈線性關係：喚醒或狀態焦慮越高，表現越好。最佳喚醒水準是倒U假說的內容，catastrophic理論則主張超過某點後表現急遽崩跌。"},{"id":"q1366","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete’s motivation to improve performance due to a love for the sport is known as which of the following?","options":["Extrinsic motivation","Achievement motivation","Intrinsic motivation","Self-controlled practice"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Intrinsic motivation","explanation_en":"Intrinsic motivation refers to the drive to engage in an activity for its own sake, rather than for some external reward or outcome. When an individual is intrinsically motivated, they derive pleasure and satisfaction directly from the activity itself. In the context of sports, if an athlete is motivated to improve performance purely out of a love and passion for the sport, it indicates that the motivation comes from within, making it intrinsic. In contrast, extrinsic motivation arises from external factors or rewards such as trophies, monetary gains, or recognition. Therefore, an athlete's motivation to enhance performance due to a love for the sport is recognized as intrinsic motivation.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"因為熱愛運動本身而想精進，是內在動機（intrinsic motivation）；外在動機（extrinsic motivation）依賴獎懲、獎勵等外部結果。"},{"id":"q1367","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A football coach waiving sprints due to substantial effort displayed in practice is an example of which of the following?","options":["Positive reinforcement","Negative reinforcement","Positive punishment","Negative punishment"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Negative reinforcement","explanation_en":"Negative reinforcement.\nNegative reinforcement involves the removal of an undesirable or aversive stimulus to increase the likelihood of a desired behavior recurring. In this case, the football coach is removing the undesirable stimulus (sprints) in response to the players displaying substantial effort during practice. The goal is to encourage players to continue putting in substantial effort in future practices with the understanding that doing so may lead to the removal of the undesirable task (sprints). Thus, waiving sprints due to significant effort displayed in practice is an example of negative reinforcement.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"撤除不愉快刺激（衝刺跑）以增加期望行為（努力練習）出現機率，是負增強（negative reinforcement）。負懲罰是移除愉快刺激，正懲罰是施加不愉快刺激。"},{"id":"q1368","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is an example of selective attention?","options":["A soccer goalie ignoring the crowd and other players when blocking a penalty shot","A football kicker stretching his hamstrings and purposefully stepping towards the ball","An Olympic weightlifter visualizing the first pull","A boxing coach talking to his fighter between rounds"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"A soccer goalie ignoring the crowd and other players when blocking a penalty shot","explanation_en":"Selective attention refers to the ability of an individual to focus on specific stimuli or cues while simultaneously ignoring other irrelevant stimuli. It's the process of directing our awareness to relevant stimuli while filtering out and disregarding other unnecessary information. In the given options, a soccer goalie ignoring the distractions of the crowd and other players to concentrate solely on blocking a penalty shot perfectly exemplifies this concept. By honing in on the ball and the striker's movements, the goalie is exhibiting selective attention, thereby maximizing the chances of successfully stopping the shot.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"守門員在罰球時忽略觀眾與他人、只專注於球的線索，是選擇性注意（selective attention）：聚焦相關刺激、過濾無關刺激。"},{"id":"q1369","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following professionals is qualified to do a dietary needs analysis of individual athletes?","options":["Sports dietician","Team physician","Sports nutrition coach","Athletic trainer"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Sports dietician","explanation_en":"A sports dietitian is specifically trained and credentialed to assess, diagnose, and treat dietary and nutritional problems in athletes. They have specialized knowledge in sports nutrition and are qualified to provide individualized nutrition recommendations tailored to athletes' unique needs and goals.\nWhile team physicians, sports nutrition coaches, and athletic trainers may have some knowledge of nutrition and its role in athletic performance, it's the sports dietitian who possesses the expertise and credentials to conduct a thorough dietary needs analysis for individual athletes. Thus, when it comes to detailed dietary assessments and recommendations for athletes, the sports dietitian is the most qualified professional.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"運動營養師/運動營養師（sports dietitian）受過專業認證訓練，可對個別運動員做飲食需求分析與診斷；運動營養教練的執業範疇較受限，隊醫、運動防護員非營養專業。"},{"id":"q1370","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following refers to the maximum average daily nutrient level not associated with adverse health effects?","options":["Recommended dietary allowance","Adequate intake","Tolerable upper intake level","Estimated average requirement"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Tolerable upper intake level","explanation_en":"The Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL) is the highest daily intake of a nutrient that is likely to pose no risk of adverse health effects for almost all individuals in the general population. As intake increases above the UL, the potential risk of adverse effects increases. It serves as a benchmark to help individuals avoid potentially harmful nutrient overdose or toxicities. Unlike recommended dietary allowances or estimated average requirements, which focus on amounts needed for good health, the UL establishes the upper boundary of safe nutrient intake.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"可耐受最高攝取量（Tolerable Upper Intake Level, UL）指幾乎所有健康人都不會產生不良健康效應的最高每日營養素攝取量。RDA是建議攝取量，AI是充足攝取量，EAR是平均需求量。"},{"id":"q1371","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following nutrients is not typically deficient in most populations?","options":["Potassium","Unsaturated fat","Fiber","Vitamin E"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Unsaturated fat","explanation_en":"Unsaturated fats, which include both monounsaturated and polyunsaturated fats, are commonly found in a variety of foods such as nuts, seeds, fish, and vegetable oils. These types of fats are often promoted for their potential health benefits, especially in relation to heart health. In contrast, nutrients like potassium, fiber, and vitamin E are often consumed in amounts below the recommended levels for many populations.\nAs a result, these nutrients are frequently identified as being of concern for adequate intake. Unsaturated fats, however, are generally consumed in sufficient or even excessive amounts, making them not typically deficient in most diets.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"不飽和脂肪在堅果、種子、魚類與植物油中攝取普遍，一般人口較不缺；鉀、膳食纖維、維生素E則是多數人攝取不足的營養素。"},{"id":"q1372","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is considered an essential amino acid?","options":["Alanine","Asparagine","Leucine","Glutamic acid"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Leucine","explanation_en":"Leucine is one of the nine essential amino acids, meaning it cannot be synthesized by the human body and must be obtained through the diet. Essential amino acids are crucial for various physiological processes, including protein synthesis and tissue repair. Among the essential amino acids, leucine is especially noteworthy because it plays a significant role in stimulating muscle protein synthesis. On the other hand, alanine, asparagine, and glutamic acid are non-essential amino acids, as the body can produce them without relying solely on dietary intake.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"白胺酸（leucine）是人體無法自行合成、必須由飲食取得的必需胺基酸之一，且為支鏈胺基酸，對刺激肌肉蛋白質合成特別重要。丙胺酸、天冬醯胺、穀胺酸皆為非必需胺基酸。"},{"id":"q1373","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following foods does not provide all of the essential amino acids?","options":["Steak","Tuna","Tofu","Black beans"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Black beans","explanation_en":"Essential amino acids are those amino acids that the body cannot synthesize on its own and must obtain from dietary sources. Foods that contain all of the essential amino acids in sufficient quantities are considered \"complete\" protein sources. Animal-based proteins like steak and tuna are complete protein sources, providing all of the essential amino acids. Tofu, which is made from soybeans, is also a complete protein.\nOn the other hand, black beans, like many other plant-based protein sources, do not provide all of the essential amino acids in the optimal ratios and are thus considered \"incomplete\" proteins. However, combining different plant-based proteins, like beans with rice, can result in a complete protein profile.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"黑豆為不完全蛋白質，缺乏足夠的必需胺基酸（如蛋胺酸）；牛排、鮪魚等動物性蛋白與豆腐（大豆蛋白）皆含全部必需胺基酸，屬完全蛋白質。"},{"id":"q1374","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the AMDR of protein for adults above 18 years old?","options":["5%-20% total caloric intake","10%-35% total caloric intake","10%-30% total caloric intake","40%-50% total caloric intake"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"10%-35% total caloric intake","explanation_en":"The Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Range (AMDR) is a range of intake for a particular energy source that is associated with reduced risk of chronic disease while providing adequate intakes of essential nutrients. For adults, the AMDR for protein is set at 10%-35% of total caloric intake. This means that, for a balanced diet, between 10% and 35% of an adult's daily calories should come from protein. Consuming protein within this range ensures that one is getting enough essential amino acids, while also allowing room for other essential nutrients from fats and carbohydrates.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"成人（19歲以上）蛋白質的可接受巨量營養素分配範圍（AMDR）為總熱量的10%–35%。"},{"id":"q1375","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":["Excessively high protein intakes are associated with renal dysfunction","Supplemental protein can increase renal calcium excretion","Post-exercise protein can improve muscle protein synthesis","Healthy individuals can safely consume protein far above RDA values"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Excessively high protein intakes are associated with renal dysfunction","explanation_en":"While protein is essential for various bodily functions, there's a common belief that high protein intakes can harm the kidneys. However, for individuals with healthy kidneys, there isn't substantial evidence to suggest that consuming a high-protein diet leads to renal dysfunction. The concern mainly arises for individuals with pre-existing kidney disease, as they need to be more cautious about their protein intake. Therefore, the statement \"Excessively high protein intakes are associated with renal dysfunction\" is false for the general healthy population but can be true for those with kidney diseases.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"錯誤敘述是「過高蛋白質攝取會導致腎功能障礙」。健康腎功能者大量攝取蛋白質並無充分證據顯示傷腎；問題主要出現在既有腎臟疾病者。補蛋白會增加尿鈣排洩、運動後補蛋白可促進肌肉蛋白合成、健康者可安全攝取遠超RDA的蛋白質，皆為正確敘述。"},{"id":"q1376","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What isomer of glucose is typically found in candy and sports drinks?","options":["Fructose","Maltose","Dextrose","Galactose"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Dextrose","explanation_en":"Dextrose is another name for the simple sugar, glucose. It is the isomer of glucose most commonly used in the food and beverage industry, especially in candy and sports drinks, due to its sweet taste and quick energy release. While fructose, maltose, and galactose are also types of sugars, they have different structures and properties than dextrose. Therefore, when referencing the form of glucose typically found in candy and sports drinks, the correct answer is dextrose.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"右旋糖（dextrose）即D-葡萄糖，是糖果與運動飲料中最常使用的葡萄糖異構形式，甜味明顯且能快速供能。"},{"id":"q1377","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following non-temperature related effects occurs through a proper warm-up?","options":["Disruption of transient connective tissue bonds","Elevated muscle temperature","Enhanced neural function","Post activation potentiation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Post activation potentiation","explanation_en":"Post-activation potentiation (PAP) refers to the phenomenon where the contractile history of a muscle influences its subsequent ability to generate force. A proper warm-up, particularly one that includes specific and dynamic movements, can lead to PAP, which can enhance subsequent performance, especially in tasks requiring power and strength. This happens because the warm-up primes the neuromuscular system for the following activity. While other options like elevated muscle temperature are temperature-related and enhanced neural function is a broader term, the specific non-temperature-related effect of a warm-up is post-activation potentiation.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"活動後增強效應（post-activation potentiation, PAP）指先前收縮歷史提升後續產能力的現象，屬熱身的非溫度相關效果。提升肌溫、降低黏滯阻力、神經功能改善都是溫度相關或另有機制。"},{"id":"q1378","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is responsible for improved oxygen delivery following a warm-up?","options":["Faster agonist and antagonist contraction","Enhanced metabolic reactions","Bohr effect","Lowered viscous resistance"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Bohr effect","explanation_en":"The Bohr effect refers to a physiological phenomenon where an increase in carbon dioxide concentration or a decrease in blood pH results in hemoglobin releasing more oxygen to the tissues. During a warm-up, there's an increase in carbon dioxide production due to the heightened metabolic activity in the muscles. As a result, blood pH decreases slightly. This shift makes hemoglobin release oxygen more readily, thereby improving oxygen delivery to the working muscles, which is crucial for aerobic activities.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"波耳效應（Bohr effect）：CO2濃度上升或pH下降使血紅素與氧的親和力降低、把更多氧釋放給組織，是熱身後氧輸送改善的機制。"},{"id":"q1379","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Approximately how long should the general warm-up phase last?","options":["5 minutes","8 minutes","2 minutes","20 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"5 minutes","explanation_en":"The general warm-up phase aims to increase overall body temperature, improve blood flow to the working muscles, and prepare the body for more specific exercises or activities. Typically, the duration of a general warm-up is around 5 minutes. This is often sufficient to elevate the heart rate and induce light sweating, indicating that the body is getting prepared for more intense activities. While the exact duration might vary based on individual preferences and specific activities, 5 minutes is a commonly recommended time for a general warm-up.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"一般性熱身約5分鐘即可提升心率與核心溫度，之後再進行專門性與動態熱身。"},{"id":"q1380","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following activities would be least recommended as a general warm-up?","options":["Stairclimber","Jump rope","Treadmill","High-knee"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"High-knee","explanation_en":"A general warm-up is designed to gradually increase heart rate, body temperature, and blood flow to the muscles, preparing the body for more strenuous activities. Activities like the stairclimber, jump rope, and treadmill are effective for these purposes because they involve steady, rhythmic movements that engage large muscle groups and can be done at a moderate intensity. High-knee exercises, on the other hand, are more intense and involve explosive movements. Starting with such an intense activity can be jarring if the body isn't adequately warmed up, making high-knee exercises least recommended as a starting point for a general warm-up.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"高抬腿（high-knee）強度較高、較具專門性，屬動態/專門熱身；一般性熱身應選擇登山機、跳繩、跑步機這類穩定節奏、循序漸進的全身有氧活動。"},{"id":"q1381","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is appropriate for the final phase of the RAMP protocol for a sprinter?","options":["Half-mile slow jog","High-knee drill","Lunges","100m running intervals of increasing intensity"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"100m running intervals of increasing intensity","explanation_en":"The RAMP protocol stands for Raise, Activate, Mobilize, and Potentiate, and it is a structured approach to warming up. The final phase, \"Potentiate,\" focuses on increasing the intensity of exercises to ensure that the athlete is fully prepared for their specific event or activity. For a sprinter, it's essential that this phase closely mimics the demands of sprinting. Therefore, 100m running intervals of increasing intensity are appropriate as they allow the sprinter to gradually approach their maximum sprinting speed, ensuring they're optimally prepared for their event. This option is more specific to sprinting demands compared to the other choices listed.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"RAMPprotocol（Raise熱身、Activate啟用、Mobilize活動化、Potentiate增強）最後階段Potentiate要 progressively 提升強度以接上專項表現。短跑選手應做100公尺漸增強度衝刺間歇；慢跑半英里強度太低，高抬腿與弓箭步屬於Activate/Mobilize階段。"},{"id":"q1382","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The squat pattern movement is best used in which phase of the RAMP protocol?","options":["Potentiate","Raise","Activate and Mobilize","Not appropriate"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Activate and Mobilize","explanation_en":"The squat pattern movement is typically best used in the \"Activate and Mobilize\" phase of the RAMP protocol. This phase focuses on engaging the muscles and joints that will be used during the main activity or workout. Squats are an effective way to activate and mobilize the hip, knee, and ankle joints, as well as the muscles involved in lower body movements. They prepare the body for the specific demands of exercises or activities that require lower body strength and stability, making them a suitable choice for this phase of the warm-up.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"蹲模式動作用於RAMP的Activate and Mobilize階段，用來啟動並活動髖、膝、踝等即將使用的關節與肌肉，而不是Raise（整體升溫）或Potentiate（高強度增強）階段。"},{"id":"q1383","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":["Balance and coordination are components of mobility","Normal ROM at a joint ensures proper movement","Flexible athletes are not always the most successful","Hyper flexibility increases injury risk"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Normal ROM at a joint ensures proper movement","explanation_en":"The statement \"Normal ROM at a joint ensures proper movement\" is false. While having a normal or adequate range of motion (ROM) at a joint is important for many movements, it doesn't guarantee proper movement by itself. Proper movement also depends on factors like neuromuscular control, stability, strength, and technique. It's possible for someone to have a normal ROM but still exhibit improper movement patterns due to other factors. Therefore, it's essential to consider a broader range of factors when assessing and promoting proper movement.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"「關節ROM正常就能確保正確動作」是錯誤敘述。動作品質還取決於神經肌肉控制、穩定度與力量等，ROM正常只是必要條件而非充分條件。其餘選項皆正確：過度柔軟反而增加受傷風險、柔軟度高的運動員不一定最成功。"},{"id":"q1384","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Increases in tissue flexibility depend primarily on which of the following characteristics?","options":["Elasticity","Plasticity","Fibrosis","Joint-structure"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Plasticity","explanation_en":"Increases in tissue flexibility primarily depend on the characteristic of plasticity. Plasticity refers to the ability of tissues, such as muscles and connective tissue, to adapt and change their length and flexibility over time in response to stretching and mobility exercises. When these tissues are regularly subjected to controlled stretching and loading, they can become more flexible and less resistant to lengthening, which is a key aspect of improving overall flexibility.\nElasticity, on the other hand, refers to the tissue's ability to return to its original shape after being stretched, while fibrosis is the formation of scar tissue, which can reduce flexibility. Joint structure can influence range of motion but is not the primary factor in increasing tissue flexibility.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"柔軟度的持久提升依賴組織的可塑性（plasticity）：組織在反覆牽拉下發生永久性長度改變；彈性（elasticity）只是伸展後回彈的性質，不會帶來持久改變。"},{"id":"q1385","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which factor has the ultimate control of flexibility?","options":["Stretch tolerance","Joint structure","Central and peripheral nervous system","Muscle and connective tissue"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Central and peripheral nervous system","explanation_en":"The ultimate control of flexibility lies with the central and peripheral nervous system. While muscle and connective tissue play crucial roles in determining one's flexibility, the nervous system governs muscle contractions and responses to stretching. Stretch tolerance, which refers to an individual's ability to tolerate and adapt to stretching sensations, is also regulated by the nervous system. Joint structure can influence range of motion but is not the ultimate control of flexibility. Therefore, the central and peripheral nervous system is the primary factor that dictates an individual's flexibility.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"柔軟度的最終控制權在中樞與週邊神經系統：神經系統調節肌肉收縮與對牽拉的耐受反應（如伸展耐受度 stretch tolerance），比關節構造或結締組織更能決定當下可達的ROM。"},{"id":"q1386","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":["Muscle mass can limit mobility","Resistance training decreases flexibility","Greater stretch tolerance is associated with greater ROM","High flexibility is not be needed for every athlete"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Resistance training decreases flexibility","explanation_en":"The statement \"Resistance training decreases flexibility\" is false. In fact, resistance training, when done properly with a full range of motion, can improve flexibility. It helps to increase the length and elasticity of muscles while also promoting joint mobility. Resistance training can be tailored to enhance both strength and flexibility, making it a valuable component of a well-rounded fitness routine.\nThe other statements are true:\nMuscle mass can limit mobility: Excessive muscle mass, particularly if not accompanied by proper stretching and mobility work, can limit a person's range of motion.\nGreater stretch tolerance is associated with greater ROM: A higher tolerance for stretching discomfort often allows individuals to reach a greater range of motion during flexibility exercises.\nHigh flexibility is not needed for every athlete: The level of flexibility required varies depending on the specific sport or activity, and not all athletes need extreme flexibility for optimal performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"錯誤敘述是「阻力訓練會降低柔軟度」。以全動作幅度正確進行阻力訓練反而能改善柔軟度與關節活動度；其餘選項正確：肌肉量大可能限制活動度、伸展耐受度與ROM正相關、並非所有運動都需要高柔軟度。"},{"id":"q1387","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the optimal time for holding a static stretch?","options":["10-20 seconds","15-30 seconds","30-45 seconds","45-60 seconds"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"15-30 seconds","explanation_en":"The optimal time for holding a static stretch is typically around 15-30 seconds. Holding a stretch for this duration allows the muscle to relax and elongate, which can help improve flexibility without risking overstretching or causing discomfort. This range strikes a balance between providing sufficient time for the muscle to respond to the stretch and avoiding excessive strain or potential injury. However, the exact duration can vary depending on an individual's flexibility, goals, and comfort level, so it's important to listen to your body and adapt the timing as needed.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"靜態伸展每次維持15–30秒為宜：足以讓肌肉放鬆延長以改善柔軟度，又不至於過度伸展造成不適。"},{"id":"q1388","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A “pronated grip” refers specifically to which of the following?","options":["A grip with palms up and knuckles down","A grip with knuckles pointing laterally and palms facing one another","A grip with palms down and knuckles up","A grip with the thumb positioned under the middle and index fingers"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"A grip with palms down and knuckles up","explanation_en":"A grip with palms down and knuckles up.\nA \"pronated grip\" refers specifically to a grip with palms down and knuckles up. This grip position is common in exercises like pull-ups or lat pulldowns, where the palms face away from the body. It is the opposite of a \"supinated grip,\" where the palms are facing up, and the knuckles are down, which is often used in exercises like bicep curls.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"正握（pronated grip）即手心向下、指節向上的握法；手心向上為反握（supinated），拇指繞到食指外側為混握（mixed/alternated），虎口朝內為中立握（neutral）。"},{"id":"q1389","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which grip is recommended for heavy weightlifting derivative movements (i.e. power clean)?","options":["Pronated hooked grip","Supinated hooked grip","Pronated closed grip","Pronated false grip"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Pronated hooked grip","explanation_en":"The grip recommended for heavy weightlifting derivative movements like the power clean is typically the \"pronated hooked grip.\" This grip involves having your palms facing you (pronated), and you hook your fingers over the barbell. The pronated hooked grip provides a secure hold on the barbell, allowing you to lift heavy weights more effectively while maintaining control. It's commonly used in exercises like the power clean to ensure a strong and stable grip on the bar during explosive movements.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"大重量抓舉衍生動作（如power clean）建議使用正握鉤握（pronated hooked grip）：掌心朝後、手指由上方勾住槓鈴，防止大重量時槓鈴從手中滑脫。"},{"id":"q1390","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the typical width of a common grip?","options":["Hands inside the barbell knurling","Hands approximately shoulder-width apart","Hands approximately hip-width apart","Hands spaced apart based on fist-to-opposite shoulder measurement"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Hands approximately shoulder-width apart","explanation_en":"The typical width of a common grip for various exercises, especially those involving barbells and other gym equipment, is \"hands approximately shoulder-width apart.\" This grip width provides a good balance between stability and control, making it a common starting point for many lifts like bench presses, overhead presses, and squats. However, grip width can vary depending on the exercise and individual preferences, but shoulder width is often a practical guideline for most people.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"一般握距（common grip）為雙手約與肩同寬，兼顧穩定與控制，是臥推等多數槓鈴動作的預設握距。"},{"id":"q1391","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A closed, alternated grip may be appropriate for which of the following?","options":["85% 1RM deadlift","60% 1RM power snatch","20% 1RM RDL","85% 1RM bench press"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"85% 1RM deadlift","explanation_en":"A closed, alternated grip, where one hand is in a pronated grip and the other hand is in a supinated grip, is often used for heavy deadlifts. Option A, an 85% 1RM deadlift, represents a heavy load, and this grip style can help improve grip strength and prevent the barbell from rolling out of the hands during the lift, making it appropriate for this scenario.\nThe other options involve exercises that may not require such a grip variation. For instance, the power snatch (Option B) and Romanian deadlift (Option C) often use a standard overhand grip or hook grip, and the bench press (Option D) typically uses a pronated grip.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"封閉混握（closed alternated grip，一手正握一手反握且拇指繞槓）用於大重量硬舉（如85% 1RM），防止槓鈴滾脫手掌；輕重量或速度性動作不需要混握。"},{"id":"q1392","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The following is not a contact point for the five-point body contact position:","options":["Left and right feet firmly planted on the floor","Head firmly on bench or pad","Low back firmly flat against bench or pad","Buttocks evenly placed on bench or seat"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Low back firmly flat against bench or pad","explanation_en":"In the five-point body contact position, the key contact points are as follows:\nLeft and right feet firmly planted on the floor.\nHead firmly on the bench or pad.\nButtocks evenly placed on the bench or seat.\nThe low back is typically not pressed flat against the bench or pad, as maintaining a natural arch in the lumbar spine is important for proper form and support during exercises like the bench press.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"五點身體接觸姿勢為：頭、雙肩/上背、臀部貼於床面或墊上，雙腳踩地——下背不是平壓貼緊，而是維持自然生理前凸。故「下背完全平貼」不屬於五點接觸。"},{"id":"q1393","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The following speed is most likely to aid in achieving full ROM:","options":["Slow and controlled on concentric and eccentric","Explosive ballistic speed","Slow eccentric, fast concentric","Slow concentric, fast eccentric"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Slow and controlled on concentric and eccentric","explanation_en":"Performing exercises with a slow and controlled tempo on both the concentric (muscle shortening) and eccentric (muscle lengthening) phases allows for better muscle engagement, stability, and control throughout the entire range of motion. This approach minimizes the use of momentum and helps ensure that the muscles are fully stretched and contracted, resulting in improved ROM and better muscle development.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"向心與離心階段皆緩慢受控能減少慣性借力，讓肌肉全程參與，最容易達到完整動作幅度（full ROM）並控制品質。"},{"id":"q1394","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The following joints should not go through full ROM during the movement:","options":["Elbow during bicep curl","Shoulder during overhead press","Shoulder during pull ups","Vertebrae during squats"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Vertebrae during squats","explanation_en":"During squats, it is essential to maintain a neutral spine and avoid excessive flexion or extension of the vertebrae. Going through a full ROM in the spine during squats can lead to improper form and potential injury. Instead, the goal is to maintain a stable and neutral spine position throughout the squat movement to protect the back and ensure safe and effective execution.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"深蹲時脊椎（vertebrae）應維持中立穩定，不宜大幅屈伸「全程活動」，否則容易失去中立位而受傷；肘、肩等四肢關節則應走完整ROM。"},{"id":"q1395","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At what point is exhaling recommended using a standard breathing pattern?","options":["Throughout the concentric phase","Throughout the eccentric phase","At the sticking point of a movement","At the bottom range of a movement"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"At the sticking point of a movement","explanation_en":"In many resistance training exercises, it's common to exhale during the most challenging part of the movement, which is often referred to as the \"sticking point.\" This exhalation can help increase intra-abdominal pressure, stabilize the core, and assist in overcoming the resistance. It's important to maintain proper breathing throughout the exercise to provide support and reduce the risk of injury.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"標準呼吸模式在動作的黏著點/最費力處（sticking point）呼氣，有助維持腹內壓、穩定核心並撐過阻力最大段。"},{"id":"q1396","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Using the Valsalva maneuver is appropriate during which of the following scenarios?","options":["Heavy structural exercises by experienced lifters","Throughout the concentric phase of upper body strength exercises","For a novice athlete’s learning spinal stabilization","Any time the spine is vertically loaded"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Heavy structural exercises by experienced lifters","explanation_en":"The Valsalva maneuver involves taking a deep breath and holding it while bearing down, which increases intra-abdominal pressure. This technique is often used by experienced lifters during heavy compound exercises like squats, deadlifts, and bench presses to stabilize the spine and protect against injury. It helps maintain core stability and support during these demanding lifts. However, it should be used with caution and under proper supervision, especially by novice athletes or those learning spinal stabilization, as improper execution can be risky.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"瓦爾薩爾瓦動作（Valsalva maneuver）讓有經驗的訓練者在大重量結構性動作（深蹲、硬舉、臥推）時憋氣增加腹內壓、穩定脊椎；新手、upper body動作或一般有氧不建議。"},{"id":"q1397","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During exercises involving over-the-face barbell trajectories, what is the proper hand placement for spotting after liftoff during the movement?","options":["Alternated grip inside the athlete’s hands","Supinated grip outside the athlete’s hands","Pronated grip inside the athlete’s hands","Supinated grip inside the athlete’s hands"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Supinated grip inside the athlete’s hands","explanation_en":"When spotting during such exercises, it's important to use a grip that allows you to maintain control and support the lifter while avoiding interference with the barbell's path. A supinated grip (palms facing up) inside the athlete's hands is a common and safe way to spot these movements. It provides stability and allows for effective guidance and support during the lift while minimizing the risk of the spotter's hands coming into contact with the barbell.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"槓鈴路徑經過臉部的動作（如深蹲、推舉）保護者（spotter）應在運動員雙手內側以反握（supinated）握槓，能快速接手控制槓鈴且不幹擾其路徑。"},{"id":"q1398","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Exercise selection based on individual sport-specific needs is known as:","options":["Specificity","Overload","Progression","Program design"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Specificity","explanation_en":"Specificity is a fundamental principle of training that emphasizes tailoring exercises and training protocols to closely match the demands of a particular sport or activity. This approach helps athletes develop the skills, strength, and conditioning necessary for optimal performance in their chosen sport. Specificity is a key consideration in designing effective training programs for athletes of all levels.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"依專項需求選擇動作是專門性原則（specificity）；overload是漸進加大負荷，progression是逐步提升難度，program design是整體訓練計畫設計。"},{"id":"q1399","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In general, which season should involve the highest volume of resistance training?","options":["Pre-season","In-season","Off-season","Post-season"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Off-season","explanation_en":"In general, the off-season should involve the highest volume of resistance training. The off-season is a period in an athlete's training cycle when they have the opportunity to focus on building strength, and muscle mass, and addressing any weaknesses. Since competition and sport-specific skills are not the primary focus during this phase, athletes can dedicate more time and effort to resistance training to lay a solid foundation for the upcoming season. During the pre-season and in-season phases, training often shifts more towards maintaining and fine-tuning athletic performance and sport-specific skills. The post-season may involve some recovery and transition but is not typically the time for high-volume resistance training.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"休賽季（off-season）賽場任務最少，可安排最高訓練量的阻力訓練以建立肌力與肌肥大；季中（in-season）以維持有餘、疲勞管理為主，訓練量最低。"},{"id":"q1400","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The following is not a consideration when conducting the needs analysis on a certain sport:","options":["Movement analysis","Psychological analysis","Physiological analysis","Injury analysis"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Psychological analysis","explanation_en":"A needs analysis for a sport primarily focuses on physical and physiological aspects, including movement analysis, physiological demands, and injury analysis. While psychology and mental preparation are crucial for sports performance, they are typically addressed separately through sports psychology or mental training programs and are not part of the traditional needs analysis process. However, understanding the psychological aspects of athletes can be important for coaches and trainers in tailoring their training and support.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"運動需求分析（needs analysis）包含動作分析、生理需求分析與受傷分析三大專案；心理分析雖重要但由運動心理專業另行處理，不屬於此處的需求分析。"},{"id":"q1401","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercise orders is most appropriate for improving lower-body power?","options":["Power clean, back squat, hip sled, knee curl","Back squat, hang-snatch, calf-raise, stiff-legged deadlift","Front squat, back squat, knee-curl, power clean","Power clean, front squat, calf raise, hip-sled"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Power clean, back squat, hip sled, knee curl","explanation_en":"This sequence starts with the power clean, which is an explosive exercise that requires a high degree of lower-body power. It is followed by the back squat, which further targets lower-body strength and power. The hip sled and knee curl exercises can be used for additional lower-body work, but they are typically less power-focused.\nThe other options either place power-focused exercises later in the sequence or include exercises that are not as power-oriented for the lower body.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"提升下肢功率的順序應把高功率、高技術動作排在最前：先power clean，再背蹲，然後腿推 sled、腿彎曲等單關節輔助。選項A符合「先專門/功率、後大肌群多關節、再單關節」的順序原則。"},{"id":"q1402","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following set-rep schemes is most effective for increasing muscle size?","options":["3 sets of 5 repetitions at 85% 1RM","3 sets of 8 repetitions at 75% 1RM","3 sets of 15 repetitions at 60% 1RM","5 sets of 3 repetitions at 90% 1RM"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3 sets of 8 repetitions at 75% 1RM","explanation_en":"This rep range, typically considered a moderate repetition range, is often associated with hypertrophy (muscle growth) because it strikes a balance between heavy weights and sufficient volume. It allows for enough time under tension and muscle fatigue to stimulate muscle growth while using a weight that is manageable for multiple sets.\nThe other options include lower rep ranges with higher intensity (options A and D) or higher rep ranges with lower intensity (option C), which may be more focused on strength development or muscular endurance, respectively. While these rep ranges have their benefits, they are not as optimal for hypertrophy as the 3 sets of 8 repetitions at 75% 1RM.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"3組8次約75% 1RM屬中等次數與負荷區間，兼顧機械張力與代謝壓力、有足夠訓練量，是肌肥大最有效率的方案；5次85%與3次90%偏最大力量，15次60%偏肌耐力。"},{"id":"q1403","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises would be considered a core exercise?","options":["Back squat","Sit-ups","Prone plank","Bicep curl"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Back squat","explanation_en":"Back squats, particularly when performed with proper form and technique, engage the muscles of the core, including the abdominal muscles and lower back, to stabilize the spine during the movement. They are a compound exercise that not only targets the lower body but also requires significant core strength to maintain a stable and upright posture throughout the squat.\nThe other options, such as sit-ups, prone plank, and bicep curls, primarily target different muscle groups and are not typically categorized as core exercises.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"依本題題庫答案，背蹲被歸為核心（core）訓練：槓鈴負荷下核心肌群必須全程等長收縮穩定脊椎，屬整合性核心動作（相對於仰臥起坐、棒式這類直接腹肌/軀幹動作）。"},{"id":"q1404","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female athlete squats 150lb on her 1RM back squat test, which of the following numbers best estimates her 5RM?","options":["141.5lb","130.5lb","125.5lb","115.0lb"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"130.5lb","explanation_en":"5lb.\nA common estimate for a 5-repetition maximum (5RM) weight based on a 1-repetition maximum (1RM) is around 85% of the 1RM weight.\nIn this case, for a 150lb 1RM back squat, the estimated 5RM would be approximately 85% of 150lb, which is 0.85 * 150lb = 127.5lb.\nSo, the option closest to this estimate is \"B. 130.5lb.\"","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"5RM約為1RM的85%–88%。150磅×0.87≈130.5磅，故最佳估計為130.5磅。"},{"id":"q1405","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During in-season, what is the frequency recommendation for resistance training?","options":["4-6 days","3-4 days","0-3 days","1-3 days"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"1-3 days","explanation_en":"The in-season period is focused more on skill development, maintenance of fitness levels, and recovery from regular sports activities. As a result, the frequency of resistance training sessions is often reduced compared to the off-season. One to three resistance training sessions per week during this phase can help athletes maintain their strength and power without overloading their schedules or interfering with their sport-specific training and competitions.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"季中（in-season）以專項技術、表現維持與恢復為優先，阻力訓練頻率建議降至每週1–3次。"},{"id":"q1406","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is most useful for assessing the overall volume of a training program?","options":["Repetition-load","Mechanical work","Volume-load","Repetition-volume"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Volume-load","explanation_en":"Volume-load takes into account both the number of repetitions (reps) and the load (weight) lifted in a given exercise or training session. It provides a comprehensive measure of the total work performed during a workout, which is essential for tracking and analyzing training progress and fatigue. Volume-load is often used by athletes, coaches, and trainers to design and monitor training programs, assess training intensity, and make adjustments as needed to optimize training outcomes.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"訓練量負荷（volume-load）＝次數×負荷，同時計入 reps 與重量，是評估整體訓練量最常用的指標；repetition-load只算次數，mechanical work需距離引數。"},{"id":"q1407","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following training goals likely entails the highest volume-load?","options":["Muscular endurance","Hypertrophy","Strength","Power"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Muscular endurance","explanation_en":"Strength training typically involves lifting heavy weights for lower repetitions and multiple sets. While the repetitions may be low, the weight lifted is significantly higher compared to other goals, leading to a high volume-load.\nIn contrast:\nMuscular endurance (option A) involves higher repetitions with lower weights.\nHypertrophy (option B) focuses on moderate repetitions with moderate weights.\nPower (option D) involves explosive movements with lower repetitions and, therefore, typically has a lower volume-load compared to strength training.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"肌耐力訓練以低負荷（≤67% 1RM）搭配高次數（≥12次）與多組數執行，次數×負荷的乘積在各訓練目標中最高，即volume-load最大。"},{"id":"q1408","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following training loads is most appropriate for improving sport-specific power in basketball players?","options":["Power snatch - 1-2 repetitions at 80-90% 1RM","Power clean - 3-5 repetitions at 75-85% 1RM","Jump-squat - 10 repetitions at 30% 1RM","Hang clean - 6-8 repetitions at 65% 1RM"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power clean - 3-5 repetitions at 75-85% 1RM","explanation_en":"Power clean exercises are known for their ability to enhance explosiveness, which is crucial for activities like jumping and sprinting in basketball. Using a weight that's 75-85% of the one-repetition maximum (1RM) for 3-5 repetitions strikes a balance between lifting heavy enough to promote strength and power development while also allowing for multiple repetitions to refine technique and maintaining a focus on power output. This range is often recommended for improving power in athletes.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"提鈴（power clean）3–5次、75–85% 1RM兼顧負荷與速度，最能有效轉化為籃球所需的專項功率；1–2次80–90%偏最大力量，30%跳蹲次數過多偏反應式肌力訓練。"},{"id":"q1409","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An interset rest period of 90 seconds is most appropriate for which of the following training goals?","options":["Hypertrophy","Strength endurance","Maximal strength","Anaerobic capacity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Hypertrophy","explanation_en":"Hypertrophy training aims to increase muscle size, and it typically involves moderate to high repetitions with a moderate load. Resting for around 90 seconds between sets allows for partial recovery of the muscles while maintaining a level of fatigue and metabolic stress, which are factors that can contribute to muscle growth. This rest period is well-suited for hypertrophy-focused workouts, where the goal is to induce muscle fatigue and promote muscle tissue development.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"組間休息90秒最適合肌肥大：保留部分恢復同時維持代謝壓力與訓練密度。肌力訓練需2分鐘以上長休息，肌耐力約30秒，無氧能力則需更短的固定休息比。"},{"id":"q1410","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following athletes would most benefit from upper body plyometrics?","options":["Defensive lineman","Running back","Pitcher","Sprinter"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Pitcher","explanation_en":"Upper body plyometrics, such as medicine ball throws or explosive push-ups, can help improve the power and speed of upper body movements. In the case of a pitcher in baseball or softball, upper body power is crucial for generating the velocity needed to throw fast pitches. Plyometric exercises can enhance the explosiveness of the shoulder and arm muscles, contributing to increased throwing speed.\nWhile other athletes like the defensive lineman (A), running back (B), and sprinter (D) also benefit from various forms of plyometric training, upper body plyometrics are particularly relevant for sports where upper body power and speed are key performance factors, such as in pitching.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"投手需要上肢爆發力來產生球速，藥球投擲、爆發式伏地挺身等上肢增強式訓練最對其專項；線衛、跑衛、短跑員的表現以下肢增強式為主。"},{"id":"q1411","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following plyometric drills is the highest in intensity?","options":["Depth jump","Depth push up","Single-arm throw","Chest pass"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Depth jump","explanation_en":"Depth jumps involve stepping off a platform and immediately exploding into a jump or rebound. This exercise has a high level of intensity because it requires rapid eccentric loading (during the landing phase) followed by an explosive concentric contraction (during the jump phase). The intensity comes from the rapid change from an eccentric to a concentric contraction, making it an advanced and demanding plyometric exercise.\nThe other options, such as depth push-ups (B), single-arm throws (C), and chest passes (D), are also plyometric exercises but are generally less intense compared to depth jumps.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"深度跳（depth jump）需落地瞬間承受高衝擊並立即反跳，離心負荷與牽張-縮短週期速率最高，是增強式訓練中強度最高的專案。"},{"id":"q1412","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the minimum recommended work-rest ratio for plyometrics?","options":["1:2","1:3","1:5","1:10"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1:5","explanation_en":"Plyometric exercises are high-intensity and can place a significant load on the muscles and connective tissues. A sufficient work-rest ratio is crucial to allow for adequate recovery between plyometric sets to reduce the risk of overuse injuries and maintain performance quality. Depending on the athlete's level of conditioning and the specific plyometric exercise, the work-rest ratio may vary, but 1:5 is a common guideline for safety and effectiveness.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練建議工作:休息至少1:5，確保磷酸原系統充分恢復、維持動作品質並降低過度使用傷害風險。"},{"id":"q1413","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How much rest is generally recommended between plyometric training sessions?","options":["24-48 hours","48-72 hours","3-4 days","5 days"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"48-72 hours","explanation_en":"Generally, it is recommended to have 48-72 hours of rest between plyometric training sessions. This rest period allows the muscles and connective tissues to recover from the high-intensity and impact nature of plyometrics. It helps reduce the risk of overuse injuries and ensures that an athlete is adequately recovered and prepared for the next plyometric workout.\nThe specific rest duration may vary depending on an individual's fitness level, the intensity of the plyometric exercises, and their training program, but 48-72 hours is a common guideline for sufficient recovery between plyometric sessions.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練衝擊大，兩次課程間一般建議間隔48–72小時讓肌肉與結締組織恢復。"},{"id":"q1414","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following volume recommendations is most suitable for intermediate athletes?","options":["80-100 foot contacts per session","100-120 foot contacts per session","120-140 foot contacts per session","140-160 foot contacts per session"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"100-120 foot contacts per session","explanation_en":"Intermediate athletes have progressed beyond the beginner stage and can handle a moderate training volume without being overwhelmed. The range of 100-120 foot contacts per session strikes a balance between providing enough stimulus for improvement and avoiding excessive fatigue or risk of overuse injuries. This range allows intermediate athletes to continue developing their plyometric skills and power while managing their training load effectively.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"中階運動員的增強式訓練量約每次100–120次腳部接觸（foot contacts）；初階約80–100次，進階可達140次以上。"},{"id":"q1415","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is not an appropriate plyometric warm-up?","options":["Marching","Jogging","Depth jumping","Skipping"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Depth jumping","explanation_en":"Depth jumping is an advanced plyometric exercise and is not suitable as a warm-up activity. It involves stepping off a platform and immediately jumping or rebounding, which places a significant load on the muscles and connective tissues. Starting a workout with depth jumping, without proper preparation and warm-up, can increase the risk of injury.\nOn the other hand, marching (A), jogging (B), and skipping (D) are suitable warm-up activities as they are lower in intensity and help gradually increase heart rate and blood flow while preparing the body for more intense plyometric exercises.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"深度跳屬高強度進階增強式動作，未先熱身就執行會對肌肉與結締組織造成過大衝擊，不當做熱身；健走、慢跑、跳躍前進等低衝擊活動才適合熱身。"},{"id":"q1416","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following refers to performing plyometric training immediately following high-intensity resistance training?","options":["Conjugate training","Combination training","Complex training","Power training"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Complex training","explanation_en":"Complex training involves combining two types of training within the same workout to enhance specific performance qualities, such as strength and power. In this case, the combination is resistance training followed by plyometric training to optimize power development. Complex training is often used to improve athletic performance by taking advantage of post-activation potentiation, where the nervous system is primed for explosive movements after heavy resistance exercise.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"複合訓練（complex training）指同一訓練單元內將高強度阻力訓練與增強式訓練相間執行（如Heavy squat後接跳躍），利用活動後增強效應提升功率表現。"},{"id":"q1417","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When performing aerobic exercise and plyometric exercise, which of the following statements is true?","options":["Aerobic exercise should be performed first for maximum benefit","Aerobic exercise should be performed after plyometric training","Plyometrics should be used as aerobic conditioning","Plyometrics should not be performed in the same session as aerobic training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Aerobic exercise should be performed after plyometric training","explanation_en":"Plyometric training is typically high-intensity and involves explosive movements that require a lot of energy and neuromuscular effort. Performing aerobic exercise (which is generally lower intensity and longer in duration) after plyometrics allows the athlete to prioritize power development during plyometrics when they are fresh and can generate maximal force. Following this with aerobic exercise helps in cardiovascular conditioning without compromising the quality of plyometric training.\nPerforming aerobic exercise before plyometric training may fatigue the muscles and nervous system, reducing the effectiveness of plyometrics for power development.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"同一課程中應先做增強式、後做有氧：增強式需要新鮮的神經肌肉狀態與爆發品質，疲勞後品質下降且受傷風險上升。"},{"id":"q1418","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Who is responsible for the day-to-day health of the athletes?","options":["Team physician","Strength and conditioning professional","Athletic trainer","Physiotherapist"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Athletic trainer","explanation_en":"Athletic trainers specialize in preventing, diagnosing, and treating sports-related injuries and illnesses. They work closely with athletes to ensure their physical health, provide immediate care for injuries, and develop injury prevention strategies. While team physicians, strength and conditioning professionals, and physiotherapists may also play essential roles in athlete care, the athletic trainer is specifically focused on the day-to-day health and safety of athletes in a sports setting.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"運動防護員（athletic trainer）負責運動員每日健康：傷害預防、現場評估處理、復健與防護策略；隊醫處理醫療診斷，體能專業負責訓練，物理治療師偏重臨床復健。"},{"id":"q1419","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which order to the phases of facility design occur?","options":["Predesign, design, construction, preoperation","Design, feasibility study, master plan, operation","Predesign, preoperation, design, construction","Needs analysis, design, construction, preoperation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Predesign, design, construction, preoperation","explanation_en":"The following are the general steps towards designing a facility:\nPredesign: This phase involves gathering information, conducting a needs analysis, and setting the initial goals and requirements for the facility.\nDesign: During this phase, the detailed plans, layouts, and specifications for the facility are developed based on the information gathered in the predesign phase.\nConstruction: Once the design is finalized and approved, the construction phase begins, where the actual building or renovation of the facility takes place.\nPreoperation: The preoperation phase occurs after construction is completed but before the facility is open to the public. It involves testing and preparing the facility for safe and effective operation.\nThis sequence ensures a structured and systematic approach to facility design and construction.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"設施規畫階段的正確順序為：預規畫（predesign，含需求分析與可行性研究）→設計（design）→施工（construction）→營運前（preoperation，人員進用、試營運）。"},{"id":"q1420","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following would not be a component of the feasibility study?","options":["Determining projected return on investment","Analyzing the competition from nearby facilities","Comparing architectural bids","Examining the strength and weaknesses of different locations"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Comparing architectural bids","explanation_en":"A feasibility study primarily focuses on evaluating the practicality and viability of a proposed project or facility. It includes assessing factors such as financial feasibility, market demand, location suitability, competition analysis, and projected return on investment (Option A, Option B, Option D). While architectural bids and design considerations are important, they are typically part of the design and planning phase rather than the feasibility study.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"可行性研究（feasibility study）評估投資報酬預估、周邊設施競爭、地點優劣比較等；比較建築師報價發生在其後的規畫/發包階段，不屬於可行性研究。"},{"id":"q1421","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which phase includes the needs analysis?","options":["Predesign","Design","Construction","Preoperation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Predesign","explanation_en":"The needs analysis is typically conducted during the predesign phase of facility development. This phase involves gathering information, assessing the requirements and objectives of the facility, and determining the specific needs that the facility must address. The needs analysis is a critical step in the early planning stages to ensure that the facility design and construction align with the intended purpose and goals of the project.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"需求分析在predesign（預規畫）階段執行，用以確立設施的目標、使用物件與需求，作為後續設計依據。"},{"id":"q1422","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the minimum recommended square footage per athlete in the facility?","options":["50","75","100","125"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"100","explanation_en":"The minimum recommended square footage per athlete in a facility is typically \"C. 100 square feet\" (as mentioned in the source you provided). This space allocation is recommended to ensure that athletes have adequate room for training, movement, and safety within the facility. It also allows for proper spacing of equipment and training areas to accommodate various exercises and activities effectively.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"設施內每位運動員建議至少100平方英尺（約9.3平方公尺）的活動空間，以容納同步訓練、器材間距與安全動線。"},{"id":"q1423","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How many inches should the wheelchair ramp run for every 1-inch rise?","options":["8","10","12","14"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"12","explanation_en":"The recommended slope for a wheelchair ramp is typically 12 inches of ramp length for every 1-inch rise. This slope ensures that the ramp is accessible and safe for individuals using wheelchairs or other mobility aids, allowing them to navigate inclines comfortably and without excessive effort.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"無障礙斜坡坡度標準為每上升1英寸需12英寸水平長度（1:12），確保輪椅使用者安全省力通行。"},{"id":"q1424","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is not a justification for athletic testing?","options":["Assessing an athlete’s physical potential to play at a competitive level","Determining the abilities to target with strength and conditioning","Screening for potential injuries","Determining the potential to play a given position at a competitive level"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Screening for potential injuries","explanation_en":"The justification for athletic testing includes the following reasons:\nAssessing an athlete's physical potential to play at a competitive level.\nDetermining the abilities to target with strength and conditioning.\nDetermining the potential to play a given position at a competitive level.\nHowever, screening for potential injuries is not typically a primary justification for athletic testing. Athletic testing primarily focuses on assessing an athlete's physical abilities, performance potential, and training needs rather than identifying potential injuries. Injury screening may be a separate process carried out by medical professionals and may involve different assessments and evaluations.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"運動測試的三大正當理由是：評估競技層級的體能潛力、確立意體能訓練要提升的能力、評估能打某位置的潛力。「篩檢潛在傷害」屬於體格檢查/防護範疇，不在NSCA所列測試理由中。"},{"id":"q1425","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following terms refers to the perception by non-experts that a test is valid?","options":["Face validity","Concurrent validity","Content validity","Construct validity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Face validity","explanation_en":"Face validity is a type of validity that is assessed by examining whether a test appears, on the surface, to measure what it is intended to measure. In other words, it assesses whether the test looks like it is a valid measure of a particular construct or trait, as judged by individuals who are not experts in the field. Face validity is concerned with the surface-level appearance or \"face\" of the test and is not a formal statistical measure of validity but rather a subjective assessment.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"表面效度（face validity）指非專業人士主觀認為一項測試看起來有效；真正的方法學效度需與標準量比較（同時效度）、內容覆蓋（內容效度）或理論構念（構念效度）驗證。"},{"id":"q1426","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Predictive validity refers to which of the following?","options":["The correlation between a test and a “gold standard” for measuring the same ability","The extent to which testing covers the component abilities of the sport","The degree to which a test measures what it is supposed to measure","The extent to which a test score is associated with future performance in the sport"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"The extent to which a test score is associated with future performance in the sport","explanation_en":"Predictive validity refers to the extent to which a test score is associated with future performance in the sport.\"\nIt assesses whether the results of a particular test or assessment can predict an individual's future performance in a specific activity, such as a sport. Predictive validity is often used to determine how well a test or measurement can forecast an athlete's future success or achievement in a given sport or athletic event. It is a valuable aspect of test validity in sports and performance assessment.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"預測效度（predictive validity）指測驗分數與未來運動表現的關聯程度，即測試分數能否預測日後的專項表現。"},{"id":"q1427","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A test that consistently results in different scores on the same athlete from different test administrators has poor:","options":["Test-retest reliability","Discriminant validity","Interrater reliability","Intrarater variability"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Interrater reliability","explanation_en":"Interrater reliability assesses the consistency of scores or measurements when different raters or administrators are involved. In this case, poor interrater reliability means that there is a lack of agreement or consistency in how different administrators score or assess the same athlete's performance on the test. This inconsistency can be problematic when trying to make fair and accurate assessments of an athlete's abilities or progress.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"不同施測者對同一運動員給出不一致分數，是評分者間信度（interrater reliability）不佳；同一施測者前後不一致才是test-retest或intrarater問題。"},{"id":"q1428","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is a possible explanation for excessive intrarater variability?","options":["Different scorers used in the testing battery","Eagerness to see improvement from athletes","Lack of clearly defined scoring system","Tests are not performed under the same environmental condition"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Eagerness to see improvement from athletes","explanation_en":"Intrarater variability refers to inconsistency in scoring or assessment when the same rater or administrator assesses the same athlete's performance on a test multiple times. Eagerness to see improvement from athletes can lead to bias or leniency in scoring, as the rater may consciously or unconsciously assign higher scores in the hope of reflecting progress or improvement. This bias can result in inconsistent assessments and variability in scores over time, which can affect the reliability and accuracy of the testing process.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"評分者內變異（intrarater variability）指同一評分者多次評分不一致。評分者渴望看到運動員進步，可能在後測不自覺放寬標準或帶入偏差，造成自身評分前後不一。"},{"id":"q1429","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests is most appropriate for pre-testing a defensive lineman?","options":["15-meter sprint, 1RM bench press","15-meter sprint, 1RM power clean","30-meter sprint, 1RM bench press","100-meter sprint, elbow-flexion endurance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"15-meter sprint, 1RM bench press","explanation_en":"These tests assess important aspects of a defensive lineman's physical abilities:\n15-meter sprint: Defensive linemen need explosive speed and quick acceleration off the line of scrimmage to engage with offensive players. The 15-meter sprint assesses their short-distance sprinting ability, which is crucial in their position.\n1RM bench press: Strength is essential for defensive linemen to engage and overpower offensive linemen. The 1RM bench press measures their upper body strength, which is vital for shedding blockers and making tackles.\nThese tests provide valuable information about an athlete's speed and strength, which are key attributes for a defensive lineman.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"防守線衛需要極短的起始加速與上肢推撞力量：15公尺衝刺評估離線爆發加速（線衛跑動距離短），1RM仰臥推評估上肢最大力量，最為對項。"},{"id":"q1430","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests is appropriate for female athlete pulling endurance?","options":["Barbell horizontal 1RM pull","Prone pullup test","Standard pull-up test","Dumbbell 1RM row"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Prone pullup test","explanation_en":"The prone pullup test assesses an athlete's endurance and strength in pulling exercises. It involves performing repeated pull-ups in a prone (face-down) position and is specifically designed to evaluate pulling endurance. The prone pullup test is a valuable assessment for athletes, including female athletes, who need to develop and maintain upper body strength and endurance for sports and activities that involve pulling motions.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"俯臥引體（prone pull-up test）以俯臥低單槓反覆拉起，是女性athlete拉力耐力（pulling endurance）的標準測驗；標準引體向上多數女性完成次數少、難評估耐力。"},{"id":"q1431","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Temperatures and humidity above the following can significantly impair aerobic endurance performance:","options":["90F, 50%","85F, 45%","80F, 50%","75F, 60%"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"80F, 50%","explanation_en":"Temperatures and humidity above 80°F, 50% can significantly impair aerobic endurance performance. High temperatures and humidity can increase the body's heat stress during aerobic exercise, leading to greater perceived effort, reduced exercise capacity, and an increased risk of heat-related illnesses. It's important for athletes to be aware of environmental conditions and take appropriate precautions, such as staying hydrated and adjusting their training intensity, when exercising in hot and humid weather.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"氣溫超過80°F（約27°C）且濕度超過50%就會明顯影響有氧耐力表現：高溫高濕妨礙散熱、提升核心體溫與自覺用力程度。"},{"id":"q1432","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following symptoms during testing warrants medical attention?","options":["Elevated heart rate","Sore throat","Chest pressure","Muscle soreness"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Chest pressure","explanation_en":"Chest pressure can be a sign of a serious medical condition, such as a heart attack or angina, which requires prompt medical evaluation and treatment. It is essential not to ignore chest pressure or pain, especially during physical testing or exercise, as it could indicate a potentially life-threatening situation. If an individual experiences chest pressure during testing, they should stop exercising immediately and seek medical assistance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"測試中出現胸悶/胸部壓迫感可能是心絞痛等心臟問題的徵兆，需要立即醫療評估；心率上升、肌肉痠痛屬正常反應。"},{"id":"q1433","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following test orders will produce the most reliable results?","options":["Height/weight, pro-agility test, 40m sprint, 1RM power clean, 3-mile run","Pro-agility test, 1RM power clean, 40m sprint, 3 mile-run, height/weight","Height/weight, Pro-agility test, 1RM power clean, 40m sprint, 3 mile-run","Push-up test, Pro-agility test, 1RM power clean, 40m sprint, 3 mile-run"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Height/weight, Pro-agility test, 1RM power clean, 40m sprint, 3 mile-run","explanation_en":"In this order, the testing begins with less physically demanding assessments (height/weight) and progresses to more physically demanding tests (Pro-agility test, 1RM power clean, 40m sprint, and 3-mile run). This order allows for adequate warm-up and preparation before engaging in the more strenuous tests, which can help reduce the risk of injury and improve the reliability of the results.\nAdditionally, placing the 3-mile run at the end of the testing sequence is common practice because it is a high-intensity endurance test and can be physically exhausting. Placing it last allows athletes to give their best effort without the fatigue from previous tests affecting their performance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"可靠測試順序的原則是「由不疲勞到高疲勞」：先做不致疲勞的身高體重，再接靈敏/功率/衝刺等神經肌肉測驗，最後才排最耗竭的3英里有氧；其他選項把身高體重排最後或一開始就測仰臥起坐，疲勞會汙染後續成績。"},{"id":"q1434","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How much time between 1RM squat test attempts is warranted on near-max weight?","options":["2 minutes","3 minutes","4 minutes","5 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3 minutes","explanation_en":"When performing the 1RM (One Repetition Maximum) squat test with near-maximal weight, it is typically warranted to allow 3 minutes between test attempts. This rest interval allows for partial recovery of the neuromuscular system and helps ensure that the athlete can perform the subsequent attempt with maximum effort while minimizing the risk of fatigue-related injuries.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"接近最大重量的1RM深蹲試舉之間建議休息3分鐘，足以讓磷酸原系統部分恢復又不至於身體冷掉。"},{"id":"q1435","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following protocols should be followed if aerobic endurance tests cannot be performed on the same day as other testing batteries?","options":["Perform tests at the same time on consecutive days","Perform strength testing in the evening and aerobic testing in the morning","Perform tests at the same time, 1 week apart","Perform strength testing indoors and aerobic testing outdoors"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Perform tests at the same time on consecutive days","explanation_en":"If aerobic endurance tests cannot be performed on the same day as other testing batteries, the recommended protocol is to perform tests at the same time on consecutive days. This approach helps maintain consistency in test conditions and reduces the risk of factors like fatigue, nutrition, or changes in readiness affecting the results. Conducting the tests on consecutive days allows for a more accurate assessment of an athlete's performance in both strength and aerobic endurance.","tags":[],"source":"traineracademy","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力測驗無法與其他測驗同日進行時，應在連續數天的同一時段施測，控制日夜節律、飲食、疲勞等變因對結果的影響。"},{"id":"q1436","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a traditional (linear) periodization model, how do training volume and intensity change across mesocycles?","options":["Volume decreases while intensity increases","Volume and intensity both increase","Volume increases while intensity decreases","Volume and intensity both decrease"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Volume decreases while intensity increases","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"傳統線性週期化（classic/linear periodization）的核心特徵是：隨著訓練階段推進，訓練量（volume）逐漸減少，而強度（intensity）逐漸增加。這源自 Matveyev 的經典模型，從高量低強度的一般準備期（General Preparation）過渡到低量高強度的比賽期（Competition）。\n【考試提示】CSCS 考試中「traditional/classic periodization」= volume ↓ intensity ↑，這是最基本的週期化定義，務必牢記。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1437","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which periodization model varies training intensity and volume WITHIN a single week?","options":["Linear periodization","Block periodization","Daily undulating periodization (DUP)","Conjugate sequencing"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Daily undulating periodization (DUP)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"每日波動週期化（Daily Undulating Periodization, DUP）在同一週內變化訓練強度和量。例如：週一 hypertrophy（10RM），週三 strength（5RM），週五 power（3RM）。這與線性模型（跨數週才改變）不同。\n【考試提示】DUP = 「within a week」變化；Weekly Undulating = 每週變化；Linear = 跨 mesocycle 漸進變化。考題常考三者區分。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1438","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Block periodization uses concentrated training blocks. Which of the following correctly describes the typical sequence of blocks?","options":["Transmutation → Accumulation → Realization","Accumulation → Transmutation → Realization","Realization → Accumulation → Transmutation","Accumulation → Realization → Transmutation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Accumulation → Transmutation → Realization","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"區塊週期化（Block Periodization）由 Issurin 提出，使用 2-4 週的高度專注訓練區塊（blocks），三個階段依序為：Accumulation（累積，高訓練量建立基礎體能）→ Transmutation（轉化，提升專項肌力與爆發力）→ Realization（實現，減量以達比賽巔峰表現）。\n【考試提示】Block periodization 口訣：A-T-R（Accumulation → Transmutation → Realization）。每塊通常 2-4 週。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1439","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the preparatory period of an annual training plan, which sub-phase focuses on building a general fitness base with higher training volume?","options":["Competition phase","Specific preparation phase","Transition phase","General preparation phase"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"General preparation phase","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"年度訓練計畫的準備期（Preparatory Period）分為：一般準備階段（General Preparation）和專項準備階段（Specific Preparation）。一般準備階段以高訓練量、低強度為特徵，目的是建立全面的體能基礎（general fitness base）。\n【考試提示】NSCA 年度計畫架構：Preparatory Period（General Prep → Specific Prep）→ Competition Period（First Transition → Competition）→ Transition Period（Active Rest）。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1440","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The transition (active rest) phase in an annual training plan typically lasts:","options":["1-4 weeks","8-12 weeks","16-20 weeks","6-12 months"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1-4 weeks","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"過渡期（Transition Phase / Active Rest）通常持續 1-4 週，目的是讓運動員從訓練和比賽的身心壓力中恢復。此階段進行低強度、非結構化的交叉訓練或休閒活動，避免完全不活動以防 detraining。\n【考試提示】Transition phase = 1-4 週 active rest，不是完全休息。若完全停止訓練超過 2 週，會出現明顯的 detraining 效應。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1441","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The conjugate (concurrent) method of periodization is BEST characterized by:","options":["Training only one fitness quality per mesocycle","Progressively increasing volume throughout the entire macrocycle","Exclusively using linear progression for all exercises","Using maximal effort, dynamic effort, and repeated effort methods within the same training week"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Using maximal effort, dynamic effort, and repeated effort methods within the same training week","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"共軛方法（Conjugate Method）的特徵是在同一訓練週內同時使用多種訓練方法：最大努力法（Maximal Effort, ≥90% 1RM）、動態努力法（Dynamic Effort, 50-80% 1RM with max velocity）、反覆努力法（Repeated Effort）。由 Westside Barbell 推廣，目的是同時發展多種運動能力。\n【考試提示】Conjugate = 同週訓練多種能力；Block = 每塊專注一種能力。兩者是相反的策略，考試常用來互相做幹擾選項。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1442","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A macrocycle in a periodized training program typically refers to:","options":["A single training session","An entire training year or season","One week of training","A 2-6 week training block"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"An entire training year or season","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"大週期（Macrocycle）指的是整個訓練年度或賽季（通常 6-12 個月，最長可達 4 年如奧運週期）。週期化層級：Macrocycle（大週期，數月-1年）> Mesocycle（中週期，2-6 週）> Microcycle（小週期，通常 1 週）。\n【考試提示】週期化層級：Macrocycle > Mesocycle > Microcycle（大 > 中 > 小）。考題常考各層級的時間長度定義。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1443","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Weekly undulating periodization differs from daily undulating periodization (DUP) in that training variables are altered:","options":["Within each training session","Every training day within a week","Only once per macrocycle","On a week-to-week basis across microcycles"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"On a week-to-week basis across microcycles","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"每週波動週期化（Weekly Undulating Periodization, WUP）是在每週（microcycle）之間改變訓練變項，例如第 1 週以肌肥大為主、第 2 週以力量為主、第 3 週以爆發力為主。DUP 則是在同一週內的不同訓練日改變變項。\n【考試提示】DUP = 每天變；WUP = 每週變；Linear = 跨 mesocycle 漸變。三種模型的「改變頻率」是區分關鍵。","tags":["Periodization"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1444","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to the NSCA, which percentage of 1RM and repetition range is MOST appropriate for developing maximal strength?","options":["50-65% 1RM, 15-25 reps","67-85% 1RM, 6-12 reps","≥85% 1RM, ≤6 reps","30-50% 1RM, 20-30 reps"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"≥85% 1RM, ≤6 reps","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 指南：最大肌力（maximal strength）訓練使用 ≥85% 1RM，≤6 次反覆。此強度範圍主要透過神經適應（neural adaptation）提升力量，包括增加運動單元徵召（motor unit recruitment）和發射頻率（rate coding）。\n【考試提示】5e 表18.11（p1237–1238）四大訓練目標的 %1RM 與目標次數：Strength ≥85%（≤6 次，核心動作）、Power 多次用力 75-85%（3-5 次；單次用力 80-90%×1-2 次，p1240）、Hypertrophy 67-80%（8-12 次）、Endurance ≤67%（≥12 次）。必背！","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1445","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength and conditioning coach prescribes an exercise at 80% 1RM. According to the NSCA repetition-percentage relationship, approximately how many repetitions can be performed?","options":["8 reps","2 reps","15 reps","20 reps"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"8 reps","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"根據 NSCA 的 %1RM-反覆次數對照表：80% 1RM 大約對應 8RM（可做 8 次）。常見對應：100%=1RM、95%≈2RM、93%≈3RM、90%≈4RM、87%≈5RM、85%≈6RM、83%≈7RM、80%≈8RM、77%≈9RM、75%≈10RM。\n【考試提示】背熟 %1RM 對照表是 CSCS 考試必備。快速記法：每降 2-3%，反覆次數約增加 1 次。80% ≈ 8RM 是常考數字。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1446","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For training muscular power with single-effort events (e.g., shot put), the NSCA recommends which load range?","options":["80-90% 1RM","50-67% 1RM","30-50% 1RM","≤30% 1RM"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"80-90% 1RM","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 區分兩種爆發力訓練負荷：單次爆發動作（single-effort，如鉛球）建議 80-90% 1RM；多次爆發動作（multiple-effort，如多次跳躍）建議 75-85% 1RM。整體爆發力訓練範圍為 75-90% 1RM，1-5 次反覆。\n【考試提示】Power 訓練的負荷取決於動作型別：single-effort = 較重（80-90%）；multiple-effort = 稍輕（75-85%）。兩者都在 75-90% 的大範圍內。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1447","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following load and repetition combinations is MOST consistent with NSCA guidelines for muscular hypertrophy?","options":["95% 1RM for 2 reps","60% 1RM for 20 reps","75% 1RM for 10 reps","50% 1RM for 30 reps"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"75% 1RM for 10 reps","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 肌肥大指南（5e 表18.11，p1237）：67-80% 1RM，8-12 次反覆。75% 1RM（約 10RM）× 10 reps 完全符合此範圍。95%×2 屬於 strength；60%×20 和 50%×30 屬於 endurance。\n【考試提示】Hypertrophy zone = 67-80% 1RM, 8-12 reps（5e 第18章；舊版 67-85%、6-12 次已更新）。考題常給一組數字讓你判斷屬於哪個訓練目標，直接對照範圍即可。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1448","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete can perform a maximum of 12 repetitions with 150 lb on the bench press. Using the NSCA %1RM table (12 reps ≈ 67%), the estimated 1RM is CLOSEST to:","options":["175 lb","224 lb","195 lb","250 lb"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"224 lb","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"12RM 大約對應 67% 1RM。計算：150 lb ÷ 0.67 ≈ 224 lb。此為 NSCA 考試常見的 1RM 估算計算題。\n【考試提示】1RM 估算公式：1RM = 負重 ÷ %1RM。12RM ≈ 67%，所以 1RM ≈ 150 ÷ 0.67 ≈ 224。考試常見此類計算題。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1449","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For muscular endurance training, the NSCA recommends a load intensity of:","options":["≥85% 1RM","75-85% 1RM","67-85% 1RM","≤67% 1RM"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"≤67% 1RM","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 肌耐力（muscular endurance）訓練指南：≤67% 1RM，≥12 次反覆。此強度範圍促進慢縮肌纖維（Type I）的適應、提高毛細血管密度和粒線體功能。\n【考試提示】≤67% 1RM + ≥12 reps = Endurance。注意「≤」和「≥」的方向，考題常在這裡設陷阱。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1450","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When training for muscular power using Olympic lifts (e.g., power clean), the recommended repetition range according to the NSCA is:","options":["1-5 reps per set","8-12 reps per set","15-20 reps per set","20-25 reps per set"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"1-5 reps per set","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 爆發力訓練（包括奧林匹克舉重動作如 power clean、snatch）建議 1-5 次反覆。這是因為爆發力動作需要最大速度和技術品質，高反覆次數會導致疲勞，降低動作速度和技術精確度。\n【考試提示】Power 訓練 = 1-5 reps。奧舉動作絕不超過 5-6 reps，因為疲勞會嚴重影響技術和受傷風險。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1451","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following 1RM percentage and repetition pairings is INCORRECT according to the NSCA guidelines?","options":["95% 1RM ≈ 2 repetitions","90% 1RM ≈ 4 repetitions","80% 1RM ≈ 8 repetitions","70% 1RM ≈ 15 repetitions"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"70% 1RM ≈ 15 repetitions","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"根據 NSCA 指南：95% ≈ 2 reps、90% ≈ 4 reps、80% ≈ 8 reps 均正確。但 70% 1RM 大約對應 12 次反覆，而非 15 次。15 reps 大約對應 65% 1RM。因此選項 D 的配對不正確。\n【考試提示】70% 1RM ≈ 12 reps（非 15 reps）。常見陷阱題：注意每個百分比的精確對應次數。","tags":["1RM & Rep Ranges"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1452","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Volume load is calculated as:","options":["Sets × reps","Weight × rest period","Reps × weight ÷ time","Sets × reps × weight"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Sets × reps × weight","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"訓練量負荷（Volume Load）= 組數（sets）× 反覆次數（reps）× 重量（weight）。例如：3 sets × 10 reps × 100 kg = 3,000 kg volume load。這是量化和追蹤訓練壓力最常用的指標之一。\n【考試提示】Volume Load = Sets × Reps × Weight。注意區分：Training Volume = Sets × Reps（不含重量）；Volume Load 才包含重量。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1453","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete performs 4 sets of 8 reps of the back squat at 120 kg. What is the volume load for this exercise?","options":["960 kg","3,840 kg","2,880 kg","4,800 kg"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3,840 kg","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Volume Load = 4 sets × 8 reps × 120 kg = 3,840 kg。這類計算題在 CSCS 考試中非常常見，務必確認乘法正確。\n【考試提示】計算題必拿分。4 × 8 × 120 = 3,840。考試時仔細計算，不要因為粗心失分。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1454","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to the volume-intensity relationship, as training intensity increases, training volume should generally:","options":["Decrease","Remain unchanged","Increase proportionally","Increase exponentially"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Decrease","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"訓練量與強度呈反比關係（inverse relationship）：當強度增加時，訓練量應相應減少。這是因為高強度訓練對神經肌肉系統的壓力更大，需要更長恢復時間。若同時增加量和強度，將導致過度訓練。\n【考試提示】Volume-Intensity inverse relationship 是週期化的核心原則。考題常問「intensity ↑ 時 volume 應如何？」答案永遠是 ↓。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1455","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A coach compares two bench press protocols:\nProtocol A: 3 sets × 10 reps × 80 kg\nProtocol B: 5 sets × 5 reps × 100 kg\nWhich has the GREATER volume load?","options":["Protocol A (2,400 kg)","Protocol B (2,500 kg)","They are equal","Cannot be determined without rest period data"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Protocol B (2,500 kg)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Protocol A：3 × 10 × 80 = 2,400 kg。Protocol B：5 × 5 × 100 = 2,500 kg。Protocol B 的 volume load 較大（2,500 > 2,400）。注意：雖然 Protocol A 的總反覆次數較多（30 vs 25），但因重量較輕，volume load 反而較低。\n【考試提示】Volume load 考量的是「總做功量」，不是單純的反覆次數。高強度低次數的 volume load 可能高於低強度高次數。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1456","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a hypertrophy phase, an appropriate volume prescription for a core exercise (e.g., squat) according to NSCA guidelines is:","options":["1-2 sets of 1-3 reps","1 set of 15-20 reps","10 sets of 1 rep","3-6 sets of 6-12 reps"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"3-6 sets of 6-12 reps","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 肌肥大訓練指南（5e 第18章）：核心動作強度 67-80% 1RM（表18.11，p1237）；目標次數初階 8-12、中階 6-12、高階 3-12，組數初階 1-3、中階以上 ≥3（表18.13，p1248）。此範圍產生充足的機械張力（mechanical tension）和代謝壓力（metabolic stress），是肌肥大的兩大刺激因素。\n【考試提示】肌肥大負荷 67-80% 1RM；次數依訓練程度 8-12／6-12／3-12，組數初階 1-3、中階以上 ≥3。Strength = ≥85% 1RM × ≤6 次；Endurance = <67% 1RM × ≥12 次。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1457","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a limitation of using volume load (sets × reps × weight) as a measure of training stress?","options":["It does not account for biomechanical or metabolic differences between exercises","It cannot be calculated for free weight exercises","It overestimates the contribution of single-joint exercises","It is only valid for exercises performed above 85% 1RM"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"It does not account for biomechanical or metabolic differences between exercises","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"訓練量負荷（volume load）的主要限制是無法反映不同動作之間的生物力學和代謝差異。例如，100 kg 的深蹲與 100 kg 的二頭肌彎舉雖然可以計算出相同的 volume load，但對身體造成的實際壓力完全不同。Volume load 也無法反映動作的難度、穩定性需求或代謝成本。\n【考試提示】Volume load 的限制：無法區分動作差異。例如 squat 100 kg vs. curl 100 kg 的生理壓力完全不同，但 volume load 數值可能相同。","tags":["Volume Load"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1458","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to the NSCA, the recommended rest period between sets for maximal strength training is:","options":["30-60 seconds","60-90 seconds","2-5 minutes","5-8 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2-5 minutes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 最大肌力訓練的組間休息建議為 2-5 分鐘。較長休息時間允許 ATP-PCr 系統充分恢復（3-5 分鐘可恢復約 95-100%），確保下一組能維持高強度和良好的動作品質。\n【考試提示】Rest periods by goal：Strength = 2-5 min、Power = 2-5 min、Hypertrophy = 30-90 sec、Endurance = ≤30 sec。這是必背表格！","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1459","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For hypertrophy training, the recommended rest period between sets is:","options":["≤30 seconds","30-90 seconds","2-5 minutes","5-8 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"30-90 seconds","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 肌肥大訓練的組間休息建議為 30-90 秒。較短的休息時間有助於維持較高的代謝壓力（metabolic stress），促進生長激素（GH）和其他合成代謝激素的釋放，這些都是肌肥大的重要驅動因素。\n【考試提示】Hypertrophy = 30-90 sec rest。短休息 → 代謝壓力 ↑ → GH 釋放 ↑ → 肌肥大刺激。考題常問「哪個休息時間最能促進 GH 釋放？」","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1460","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which rest period is MOST appropriate for muscular endurance training?","options":["≤30 seconds","1-2 minutes","3-4 minutes","5-6 minutes"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"≤30 seconds","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 肌耐力訓練的組間休息建議為 ≤30 秒。極短的休息時間迫使身體在不完全恢復的狀態下繼續運動，刺激肌耐力適應（如提升乳酸緩衝能力、增加毛細血管密度）。\n【考試提示】Endurance rest = ≤30 sec，是四個訓練目標中最短的。記住遞減順序：Strength/Power（2-5 min）> Hypertrophy（30-90 sec）> Endurance（≤30 sec）。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1461","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete trains 4 days per week with an upper/lower body split. What is the training frequency per muscle group per week?","options":["1 time per week","4 times per week","6 times per week","2 times per week"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"2 times per week","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"上下肢分化（Upper/Lower Split）每週訓練 4 天，通常安排為：週一上肢、週二下肢、週四上肢、週五下肢。因此每個肌群每週被訓練 2 次。這是 NSCA 建議的中階至進階訓練者的理想頻率。\n【考試提示】頻率計算：Upper/Lower 4天 = 每肌群 2次/週；Push/Pull/Legs 6天 = 每肌群 2次/週；Full body 3天 = 每肌群 3次/週。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1462","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For a novice (untrained) individual, the NSCA recommends a training frequency of:","options":["2-3 days per week","1 day per week","5-6 days per week","7 days per week"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"2-3 days per week","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 對初學者（novice/untrained）的訓練頻率建議為每週 2-3 天。初學者的恢復能力較低，需要較多的休息天數。隨著訓練經驗增加，可逐漸增加至每週 4-6 天（使用分化訓練）。\n【考試提示】Training frequency by level：Beginner = 2-3 days/week（full body）；Intermediate = 3-4 days/week；Advanced = 4-6 days/week（split routines）。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1463","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For power training (e.g., hang cleans), the recommended rest period between sets is:","options":["≤30 seconds","30-60 seconds","2-5 minutes","No rest needed"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2-5 minutes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 爆發力訓練的組間休息建議為 2-5 分鐘，與最大肌力訓練相同。爆發力動作需要最大神經肌肉徵召和 ATP-PCr 系統的充分恢復，短休息會降低動作速度和增加受傷風險。\n【考試提示】Power 和 Strength 的 rest period 相同 = 2-5 min。原因都是需要 ATP-PCr 完全恢復。考題可能問「power clean 的休息時間」。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1464","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following BEST represents the recommended number of sets for strength training of a core exercise according to the NSCA?","options":["1-2 sets","8-10 sets","2-6 sets","12-15 sets"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2-6 sets","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 核心動作（core exercises，如 squat、bench press、deadlift）的力量訓練建議為 2-6 組。輔助動作（assistance exercises）則建議 1-3 組。組數取決於訓練經驗、訓練階段和具體目標。\n【考試提示】Strength sets：Core exercises = 2-6 sets；Assistance exercises = 1-3 sets。注意這裡的「core exercise」指的是多關節大肌群動作，不是核心肌群訓練。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1465","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following rest interval lengths is MOST likely to elicit the greatest acute growth hormone response during resistance training?","options":["30-60 seconds","≤30 seconds","3-5 minutes","5 minutes or longer"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"30-60 seconds","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"30-60 秒的短暫休息時間會產生最大的急性生長激素（GH）反應。這是因為較短的休息時間導致更大的代謝壓力（如乳酸堆積、氫離子濃度升高），而這些代謝副產物是刺激 GH 分泌的重要因素。這也是肌肥大訓練建議使用 30-90 秒休息的原因之一。\n【考試提示】短休息（30-60 sec）= 最大 GH 反應 = 代謝壓力最大。這解釋了為何肌肥大訓練用短休息。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1466","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When designing a resistance training program for a competitive powerlifter in the off-season, which of the following training approaches is MOST appropriate?","options":["2 days/week, 12-15 reps at 65% 1RM","6 days/week, 1-3 reps at 93-100% 1RM","1 day/week, 20+ reps at 50% 1RM","3-4 days/week, 6-12 reps at 67-85% 1RM with some heavier sets"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"3-4 days/week, 6-12 reps at 67-85% 1RM with some heavier sets","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"力量舉選手在非賽季應建立肌肉量和一般體能基礎。每週 3-4 天訓練，使用 6-12 次反覆（肌肥大範圍）搭配部分較重組（肌力維持）是最合適的。非賽季不應過度使用極高強度（>90%），以避免累積疲勞和受傷風險。\n【考試提示】Off-season = 建立基礎 = 中等強度、中等反覆次數為主。不要在非賽季一直練極大重量。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1467","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When training frequency is increased from 3 to 5 days per week, which program modification is MOST important to prevent overtraining?","options":["Increase the load by 10% on all exercises","Implement a split routine to allow muscle group recovery","Reduce rest periods to 15 seconds between sets","Add more exercises per session"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Implement a split routine to allow muscle group recovery","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"當訓練頻率增加時，最重要的調整是採用分化訓練（split routine），讓每個肌群在兩次訓練之間有 48-72 小時的恢復時間。例如從全身訓練改為上下肢分化或推拉分化。增加負荷、減少休息或增加動作都會加重過度訓練風險。\n【考試提示】頻率 ↑ → 必須 split training。NSCA 強調每個肌群需要至少 48 小時恢復。5天全身訓練 = overtraining risk；5天分化訓練 = 適當。","tags":["Training Variables"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1468","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The principle of specificity (SAID principle) states that:","options":["All exercises should be performed at maximal intensity","Training volume should always exceed competition demands","Training adaptations are specific to the demands imposed on the body","All athletes should follow the same training program"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Training adaptations are specific to the demands imposed on the body","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"特異性原則（SAID = Specific Adaptation to Imposed Demands）指出身體的適應是針對施加的特定刺激。訓練計畫必須模擬運動的特定需求（動作模式、肌肉群、能量系統、速度）才能有效轉移到運動表現。\n【考試提示】SAID principle = 訓練適應具有特異性。考題常問「改善垂直跳」該選什麼動作 → 選動作模式最接近的（如 jump squat > leg curl）。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1469","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to NSCA exercise order guidelines, which exercise should be performed FIRST in a training session?","options":["Bicep curl","Power clean","Lateral raise","Tricep pushdown"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power clean","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 動作順序原則：(1) 爆發力動作（power/Olympic lifts）最先 → (2) 多關節大肌群動作（core exercises）→ (3) 單關節小肌群動作（assistance exercises）。Power clean 是爆發力動作，應排在最前面，因為它對技術和神經系統要求最高。\n【考試提示】Exercise order：Power exercises → Core (multi-joint) → Assistance (single-joint)。另一原則：Large muscle → Small muscle、Compound → Isolation。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1470","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercise sequences is MOST consistent with NSCA guidelines for exercise order?","options":["Bicep curl → bench press → power snatch → squat","Power snatch → squat → bench press → bicep curl","Bicep curl → tricep extension → squat → power snatch","Leg extension → squat → power snatch → bench press"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Power snatch → squat → bench press → bicep curl","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"正確順序：Power snatch（爆發力動作）→ Squat（多關節下肢）→ Bench press（多關節上肢）→ Bicep curl（單關節輔助）。遵循 NSCA 原則：power → core multi-joint → assistance single-joint。\n【考試提示】排列題是 CSCS 高頻題型。記住三層級：Power first → Multi-joint compound → Single-joint isolation。違反此順序的選項直接排除。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1471","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The principle of progressive overload requires that:","options":["Training intensity must increase every session","Athletes should always train to muscular failure","Only training volume should be manipulated","Training stress must be gradually increased over time to continue adaptation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Training stress must be gradually increased over time to continue adaptation","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"漸進式超負荷原則（Progressive Overload）要求訓練壓力必須隨時間逐漸增加，才能持續產生適應。可以透過增加負荷、反覆次數、組數、訓練頻率或減少休息時間來實現。不需要每次訓練都增加，也不需要練到力竭。\n【考試提示】Progressive overload 的「progressive」= 漸進式，不是每次都加。NSCA 建議初學者每次增加 2.5-10 lb（上肢較少、下肢較多）。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1472","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete alternates between a bench press set and a bent-over row set with rest between each. This technique is known as:","options":["Agonist-antagonist paired set (superset)","Drop set","Forced repetition","Pyramid set"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Agonist-antagonist paired set (superset)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"拮抗肌配對組（Agonist-Antagonist Paired Set / Superset）是交替訓練拮抗肌群的動作。Bench press（胸/推）和 Bent-over row（背/拉）是經典的推拉配對。此方法可提高訓練效率、可能增加力量表現（透過互動抑制 reciprocal inhibition）。\n【考試提示】Agonist-antagonist superset 的好處：節省時間、可能提升力量（reciprocal inhibition）、維持肌力平衡。常見配對：bench press/row、bicep curl/tricep extension。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1473","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When two exercises that stress the same muscle group are performed consecutively (e.g., squat followed by leg press), this is an example of a:","options":["Agonist-antagonist superset","Compound set","Circuit training","Split set"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Compound set","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"複合組（Compound Set）是連續進行兩個訓練相同肌群的動作（如 squat → leg press，都訓練股四頭肌）。與 agonist-antagonist superset（訓練對立肌群）不同。Compound set 會對目標肌群產生更大的疲勞和代謝壓力。\n【考試提示】Compound set = 同肌群連續兩動作（如 squat + leg press）；Agonist-antagonist superset = 對立肌群（如 bench + row）。考題常考兩者的區分。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1474","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The principle of variation in program design is BEST implemented by:","options":["Randomly changing exercises every session without a plan","Keeping the program exactly the same for 12 months","Systematically varying training variables across planned phases","Training the same muscle group every day"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Systematically varying training variables across planned phases","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"變異原則（Principle of Variation）要求有系統地改變訓練變項（強度、量、動作選擇、休息等），通常透過週期化實現。這不是隨機改變（那是 muscle confusion myth），而是有計劃的變化，以避免適應停滯（plateau）和過度訓練。\n【考試提示】Variation ≠ random change。NSCA 強調「planned/systematic variation」。考題選項中若出現「randomly」通常是錯誤的。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1475","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Circuit training is characterized by:","options":["Performing one set of each exercise in sequence with minimal rest between stations","Performing multiple sets of the same exercise before moving to the next","Training only the upper body in a single session","Using only maximal loads for all exercises"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Performing one set of each exercise in sequence with minimal rest between stations","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"迴圈訓練（Circuit Training）的特徵是：連續進行多個不同動作（stations），每個動作做 1 組後立即移至下一個動作，中間休息極短（通常 15-30 秒）。完成所有動作為一個迴圈（circuit），可重複 2-3 個迴圈。適合同時發展肌耐力和心肺耐力。\n【考試提示】Circuit training = 一個動作一組 → 換下一個動作 → 最少休息。與 traditional set training（同一動作做完所有組）不同。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1476","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The exercise order principle may be intentionally violated when using which of the following training techniques?","options":["Pyramid training","Periodization","Progressive overload","Pre-exhaustion"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Pre-exhaustion","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"預先疲勞法（Pre-exhaustion）刻意先進行單關節動作以預先疲勞目標肌群，再進行多關節動作。例如：先做 leg extension（股四頭肌預先疲勞）→ 再做 back squat。這違反了一般的「multi-joint before single-joint」原則，但是一種有意為之的訓練技巧。\n【考試提示】Pre-exhaustion 是動作順序原則的合理例外：先單關節疲勞目標肌 → 再多關節複合動作。考試可能問「何時可以違反 exercise order」。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1477","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to NSCA guidelines, when an athlete cannot maintain proper exercise technique during a set, the strength and conditioning coach should:","options":["Encourage the athlete to push through the discomfort","Terminate the set or reduce the load","Increase the rest period to 10 minutes","Switch to a ballistic exercise instead"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Terminate the set or reduce the load","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 明確指出：當運動員無法維持正確動作技術時，應立即終止該組或降低負荷。繼續在不良技術下訓練會增加受傷風險，且不會產生理想的訓練適應。安全永遠是第一優先。\n【考試提示】NSCA 安全原則：technique breakdown → stop the set 或 reduce load。考題中任何「push through」或「ignore form」的選項都是錯誤的。","tags":["Program Design Principles"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1478","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a taper phase leading up to competition, which training variable should be reduced the MOST?","options":["Training volume","Training intensity","Exercise selection variety","Training frequency (by more than 50%)"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Training volume","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"賽前減量期（Taper）最應大幅減少的是訓練量（volume），通常減少 60-90%。訓練強度應維持或僅略微降低，以維持神經肌肉適應。訓練頻率不應減少超過 20-50%，以避免 detraining。\n【考試提示】Taper 的「黃金法則」：Volume ↓↓↓（最多減）、Intensity maintain or ↓ slightly、Frequency ↓ slightly（不超過 50%）。考題最常問「哪個變項減最多？」= Volume。","tags":["Taper & Peaking"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1479","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A taper period typically lasts:","options":["1-2 days","6-8 weeks","3-6 months","8-14 days"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"8-14 days","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"賽前減量期（Taper）通常持續 8-14 天（約 1-2 週），最長可達 4 週。太短（<1 週）無法充分恢復；太長（>4 週）可能導致 detraining 效應。具體長度取決於前期訓練量和運動員的恢復能力。\n【考試提示】Taper duration = 8-14 days（最常見答案）。研究顯示 2 週 taper 能產生約 2-3% 的表現提升。超過 4 週則開始 detraining。","tags":["Taper & Peaking"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1480","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a taper, maintaining training intensity is important because it helps preserve:","options":["Flexibility gains","Maximum heart rate","Neuromuscular adaptations and strength","Body fat percentage"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Neuromuscular adaptations and strength","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"在減量期維持訓練強度對保留神經肌肉適應（motor unit recruitment、rate coding、intermuscular coordination）和肌力至關重要。如果強度大幅降低，這些神經適應會在 1-2 週內開始減退，導致力量和爆發力下降。\n【考試提示】Taper 維持 intensity 的原因 = 保留 neuromuscular adaptations。肌力的流失速度比有氧能力慢，但神經適應比肌肉適應更快消退。","tags":["Taper & Peaking"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1481","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A deload week is BEST described as:","options":["A week of complete inactivity","A planned reduction in training stress (typically 50-70% of normal volume/intensity) to facilitate recovery","A week focused exclusively on cardiovascular training","A week where only new exercises are introduced"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"A planned reduction in training stress (typically 50-70% of normal volume/intensity) to facilitate recovery","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Deload week 是有計劃地減少訓練壓力的一週，通常將 volume 和/或 intensity 降低至正常的 50-70%。目的是促進身體恢復、減少累積疲勞、預防過度訓練，同時維持訓練習慣和動作模式。一般每 3-4 週安排一次。\n【考試提示】Deload ≠ complete rest（那是 transition phase）。Deload 仍然訓練，只是降低壓力。常見安排：3 週漸進負荷 + 1 週 deload（3:1 pattern）。","tags":["Taper & Peaking"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1482","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which type of taper has been shown by research to produce the BEST performance outcomes?","options":["Step taper (sudden, uniform reduction)","Linear taper (gradual, even reduction)","Exponential taper with fast decay","No-taper approach (maintain all variables)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Exponential taper with fast decay","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"研究顯示快速衰減的指數型減量（exponential taper with fast decay）通常產生最佳的競賽表現。在此模式中，訓練量在減量初期快速大幅降低，之後趨於平緩。與線性減量（均勻減少）或階梯式減量（突然減少）相比，快速指數型減量在消除疲勞的同時更好地保持體能水準。\n【考試提示】最佳 taper 型別 = Exponential with fast decay。三種 taper：Step（一次性降）、Linear（均勻漸降）、Exponential（先快後慢，效果最佳）。","tags":["Taper & Peaking"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1483","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The FIRST step in designing a resistance training program, according to the NSCA, is to:","options":["Select the exercises to be performed","Determine the training frequency","Conduct a needs analysis","Establish the training volume and intensity"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Conduct a needs analysis","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"根據 NSCA，設計阻力訓練計畫的第一步是進行需求分析（needs analysis）。需求分析包括兩個面向：(1) 評估運動專案的需求（動作分析、生理需求、常見傷害），(2) 評估運動員的個人狀況（訓練經驗、傷病史、體能水準、可用時間）。只有完成需求分析後，才能適當地選擇動作和設定訓練變項。\n【考試提示】Program design 第一步永遠是 Needs Analysis。先了解運動和運動員，再設計課表。NSCA 流程：Needs analysis → Exercise selection → Exercise order → Volume/Intensity → Rest → Frequency。","tags":["Exercise Selection"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1484","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When selecting exercises for a volleyball player, which of the following combinations BEST applies the principle of specificity?","options":["Long-distance running and seated machine exercises","Wrist curls, seated calf raises, and recumbent bike","Bench press only at high reps with short rest","Power clean, jump squat, and standing overhead press"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Power clean, jump squat, and standing overhead press","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"排球的主要動作需求包括：垂直跳躍（jumping）、爆發性高舉過頭動作（overhead hitting/blocking）和快速下肢發力。Power clean 和 jump squat 訓練下肢爆發力，standing overhead press 訓練殺球和攔網所需的肩部力量。這最符合特異性原則（SAID principle）。\n【考試提示】Exercise selection 題型：先分析運動的動作模式和能量系統，再選擇最匹配的訓練動作。排球 = 跳躍（下肢爆發）+ 擊球（上肢 overhead power）→ 選爆發力 + overhead 動作。","tags":["Exercise Selection"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1485","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises is classified as a power exercise (a subcategory of structural exercises)?","options":["Barbell back squat","Seated bicep curl","Power snatch","Seated shoulder press machine"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Power snatch","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Power exercise 是結構性動作的子類別，需要以快速、爆發性的動作速度完成。Power snatch（抓舉）是典型的 power exercise，因為它需要爆發性地將槓鈴從地面舉至頭頂。Back squat 是結構性動作但通常不歸類為 power exercise（除非以爆發性速度如 jump squat）。Seated curl 和 seated machine press 都不是結構性動作。\n【考試提示】分類層級：All exercises → Structural exercises（脊柱承重）→ Power exercises（結構性 + 快速/爆發性）。典型 power exercises：clean、snatch、push press、jump squat。","tags":["Exercise Selection"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1486","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the back squat, which joint action occurs at the knee during the concentric (ascending) phase?","options":["Knee extension","Knee flexion","Knee abduction","Knee internal rotation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Knee extension","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"在背蹲舉的向心（上升）階段，膝關節進行伸展（extension）動作，主要由股四頭肌群（quadriceps）產生力量將身體推起。下降階段才是膝屈曲（flexion），由股四頭肌離心控制。\n【考試提示】考試常考各階段的關節動作：上升 = 髖伸展 + 膝伸展 + 踝蹠屈（plantar flexion）。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1487","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the PRIMARY muscle group targeted during the conventional deadlift?","options":["Gluteus maximus and hamstrings","Rectus abdominis","Anterior deltoid","Latissimus dorsi"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Gluteus maximus and hamstrings","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"傳統硬舉的主要作用肌群為臀大肌（gluteus maximus）和膕繩肌（hamstrings），負責髖關節伸展。豎脊肌（erector spinae）則等長收縮維持脊柱穩定，股四頭肌負責膝伸展。闊背肌雖參與穩定槓鈴，但並非主動肌。\n【考試提示】硬舉 = 髖主導動作（hip-dominant）。主動肌是 gluteus maximus + hamstrings；豎脊肌是穩定肌。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1488","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the power clean, the 'second pull' phase begins when the barbell reaches approximately which anatomical landmark?","options":["Floor level","Shoulder height","Mid-thigh","Overhead"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Mid-thigh","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"爆發式上搏（power clean）的第二拉（second pull）從槓鈴到達大腿中段（mid-thigh）位置開始，此時運動員進行爆發性三關節伸展（triple extension：踝、膝、髖同時伸展），產生最大力量與速度。第一拉是從地面到膝蓋，過渡階段是膝蓋到大腿中段。\n【考試提示】NSCA 定義：first pull（地面到膝）→ transition/scoop（膝到 mid-thigh）→ second pull（mid-thigh 爆發性伸展）→ catch。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1489","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A common technique error during the bench press is 'bouncing' the bar off the chest. This primarily increases the risk of injury to which structure?","options":["Biceps brachii tendon","Achilles tendon","Posterior cruciate ligament","Sternum and rib cage"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Sternum and rib cage","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"在臥推時將槓鈴彈離胸部（bouncing）會對胸骨（sternum）和肋骨（rib cage）產生巨大的衝擊力，可能導致肋骨骨折或胸骨軟骨損傷。正確技術應在胸部輕觸後以控制方式推起，不應利用彈性。\n【考試提示】臥推常見錯誤：彈胸、臀部離凳（hip elevation）、過寬握距、手腕過度伸展。考試注意每個錯誤對應的受傷風險。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1490","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the snatch, the 'catch' position requires the barbell to be received in which position?","options":["Overhead with fully extended elbows","At hip level with arms extended","On the anterior deltoids (front rack)","Behind the neck resting on the trapezius"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Overhead with fully extended elbows","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"抓舉（snatch）的接槓（catch）位置是在頭頂上方，手肘完全伸直（fully extended elbows），雙臂鎖定。運動員可在全蹲或半蹲位置接槓（power snatch 為半蹲）。上搏（clean）才是接在前三角肌（front rack position）。\n【考試提示】Snatch catch = overhead, elbows locked；Clean catch = front rack position。這是區分兩個動作的關鍵考點。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1491","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which grip is MOST commonly recommended by the NSCA for the back squat?","options":["Closed pronated grip","Open (false/thumbless) grip","Supinated (underhand) grip","Alternated (mixed) grip"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Closed pronated grip","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"背蹲舉建議使用閉合式正握（closed pronated grip），拇指環繞槓鈴，確保槓鈴穩固不會滑落。開放式握法（false/thumbless grip）雖然有些運動員使用以減少手腕壓力，但因安全考量 NSCA 不推薦。交替握（mixed grip）用於硬舉，勾握（hook grip）用於奧林匹克舉重。\n【考試提示】NSCA 立場：所有在背部的槓鈴動作（back squat、good morning）都應使用 closed pronated grip。False grip 增加槓鈴滑落風險。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1492","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The Valsalva maneuver is MOST appropriate during which type of exercise?","options":["Low-intensity aerobic exercise","Structural exercises with near-maximal loads","Plyometric depth jumps","Flexibility training"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Structural exercises with near-maximal loads","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"瓦氏操作（Valsalva maneuver）是在閉氣狀態下用力呼氣以增加腹內壓，穩定脊柱。最適合用於結構性動作（structural exercises）搭配接近最大負荷（near-maximal loads），如深蹲、硬舉。不建議用於有心血管疾病風險者，因為會大幅升高血壓。\n【考試提示】Valsalva maneuver = 閉氣增加 intra-abdominal pressure，穩定 spine。僅限大重量、短時間。高血壓/心血管疾病患者停用。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1493","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete performing the back squat consistently demonstrates excessive forward lean. Which of the following is the MOST likely cause?","options":["Weak hip extensors (glutes and hamstrings)","Excessive shoulder flexibility","Weak quadriceps","Tight hip flexors"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Weak hip extensors (glutes and hamstrings)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"深蹲時過度前傾最常見的原因是髖伸肌群（臀大肌和膕繩肌）力量不足。當髖伸肌無法產生足夠力量時，身體會藉由增加軀幹前傾來將負荷轉移至腰椎伸肌。股四頭肌弱通常會導致無法達到適當深度，而非前傾。\n【考試提示】深蹲過度前傾的最可能原因是髖伸肌（臀肌/膕繩肌）無力。這是經典的動作代償題。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1494","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the correct foot placement for the conventional deadlift?","options":["Feet wider than shoulder-width with toes pointed significantly outward","Feet together with toes pointing straight ahead","Staggered stance with one foot forward","Feet approximately hip-width apart with toes slightly turned out"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Feet approximately hip-width apart with toes slightly turned out","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"傳統硬舉的正確站距為雙腳約與髖同寬（hip-width），腳尖略微外旋（5-10 度）。雙手在膝蓋外側握槓。寬站距加上腳尖大幅外轉的是相撲硬舉（sumo deadlift）。雙腳併攏或前後腳都不是標準硬舉姿勢。\n【考試提示】Conventional deadlift = hip-width stance；Sumo deadlift = wider than shoulder-width stance。考試常考兩者的站距差異。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1495","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the power clean, 'triple extension' refers to simultaneous extension of which three joints?","options":["Ankle, knee, and hip","Wrist, elbow, and shoulder","Cervical, thoracic, and lumbar spine","Shoulder, elbow, and wrist"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Ankle, knee, and hip","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"三關節伸展（triple extension）指踝關節（ankle plantar flexion）、膝關節（knee extension）和髖關節（hip extension）同時爆發性伸展。這是爆發力動作（power clean、snatch、clean & jerk）的核心機制，產生最大地面反作用力。\n【考試提示】Triple extension = ankle + knee + hip 同時伸展，是所有 Olympic lifts 和爆發力訓練的基礎概念。CSCS 必考。","tags":["Exercise Technique"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1496","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When spotting the barbell back squat with heavy loads, how many spotters does the NSCA recommend?","options":["One spotter standing behind the lifter","Two spotters, one on each side of the barbell","No spotter is needed if safety pins are used","Three spotters: one behind and one on each side"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Three spotters: one behind and one on each side","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 建議重負荷的背蹲舉使用三位補手（three spotters）：一位站在運動員後方，兩位分別站在槓鈴兩端。後方補手雙手環繞運動員胸部/軀幹協助，兩側補手握住槓片內側。輕負荷可使用一位補手。\n【考試提示】NSCA 補手建議：輕負荷 squat = 1 spotter（後方）；重負荷 squat = 3 spotters。Bench press 通常 1 spotter（中間），重負荷可用 3。","tags":["Spotting"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1497","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When spotting the flat barbell bench press, the spotter should use which grip on the bar?","options":["Alternated (mixed) grip","Supinated grip only","Pronated grip only","No contact with the bar unless the lifter needs assistance"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Alternated (mixed) grip","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"補手在臥推時應使用交替握法（alternated/mixed grip），一手正握一手反握環繞槓鈴。這種握法提供最佳的控制力，防止槓鈴在任一方向滑脫。補手應在 lift-off 時協助，然後放手，但雙手保持在槓鈴附近準備隨時介入。\n【考試提示】Bench press spotter = alternated grip，站在 lifter 頭部後方。關鍵原則：只在需要時才施加力量（apply force only when needed）。","tags":["Spotting"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1498","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A spotter for the dumbbell shoulder press should apply assistance at which location?","options":["The dumbbells directly","The lifter's wrists or forearms","The lifter's elbows","The lifter's upper back"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The lifter's wrists or forearms","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"啞鈴動作的補手應在運動員的手腕或前臂處施加輔助力量，而非直接碰觸啞鈴。直接推啞鈴可能導致重量失衡或啞鈴旋轉。在手腕處輔助可以提供穩定的向上力量，同時讓運動員維持對啞鈴的控制。\n【考試提示】啞鈴補手位置 = wrists/forearms（手腕/前臂），不是 dumbbells 本身也不是 elbows。這是 NSCA 標準考點。","tags":["Spotting"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1499","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the back squat, the rear spotter should be positioned with their hands:","options":["On the barbell ends","On the lifter's hips","Behind their own back until needed","Across the lifter's chest and abdomen ready to assist the torso"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Across the lifter's chest and abdomen ready to assist the torso","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"背蹲舉的後方補手應將雙手/雙臂準備好環繞運動員的胸部和腹部區域，隨時準備向上托起軀幹。後方補手不直接接觸槓鈴（那是兩側補手的工作），而是協助運動員的軀幹回到站立位置。\n【考試提示】後方 spotter = 協助 torso（胸腹區域）；側方 spotters = 協助 barbell ends。分工明確是考試重點。","tags":["Spotting"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1500","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the MOST important consideration when selecting a spotter?","options":["The spotter must be taller than the lifter","The spotter must have at least 5 years of lifting experience","The spotter must be of the same gender as the lifter","The spotter must be strong enough to handle the load if the lifter fails"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"The spotter must be strong enough to handle the load if the lifter fails","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"選擇補手最重要的考量是補手必須有足夠的力量，在運動員完全失敗時能夠安全地處理負荷。補手不需要比運動員更高或更有經驗，但必須具備足夠的力量和知識來確保安全。對於非常重的負荷，應使用多位補手。\n【考試提示】Spotter 選擇原則：(1) 足夠力量處理負荷、(2) 瞭解正確補手技術、(3) 與 lifter 事先溝通訊號。力量是最關鍵因素。","tags":["Spotting"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1501","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to NSCA guidelines, what is the recommended duration for a general warm-up prior to resistance training?","options":["1-2 minutes","20-30 minutes","5-10 minutes","30-45 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"5-10 minutes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 建議一般熱身（general warm-up）時間為 5-10 分鐘，進行低強度有氧活動（如慢跑、騎車、跳繩）。目的是提高核心體溫、增加心率和血流量、提高肌肉延展性、並為後續的專項熱身做準備。\n【考試提示】General warm-up = 5-10 分鐘低強度有氧。目的：提升 core temperature、blood flow、muscle extensibility。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1502","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which type of stretching is MOST recommended as part of a pre-exercise warm-up routine?","options":["Dynamic stretching using controlled movement patterns","Ballistic stretching with bouncing movements","Static stretching held for 60 seconds per muscle group","PNF stretching with a partner"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Dynamic stretching using controlled movement patterns","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"運動前最推薦使用動態伸展（dynamic stretching），以控制的動作模式逐步增加關節活動範圍和肌肉溫度。研究顯示運動前的長時間靜態伸展（>60 秒）可能暫時降低力量和爆發力表現。動態伸展則能提升表現且不降低力量。\n【考試提示】運動前 = dynamic stretching（推薦）。Static stretching 運動前 >60 秒可能降低 strength/power。運動後才適合 static stretching。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1503","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A specific warm-up for the bench press would BEST include which of the following?","options":["5 minutes on the treadmill followed by static chest stretches","Progressive sets of bench press with increasing loads","Heavy triceps pushdowns at maximum effort","Yoga poses targeting hip flexibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Progressive sets of bench press with increasing loads","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"專項熱身（specific warm-up）應包含目標動作本身的漸進負荷組（progressive sets with increasing loads）。例如臥推前，先以空槓或輕重量做 1-2 組，逐步增加重量到工作組重量。這能啟用相關肌群、練習動作模式、並為神經肌肉系統做準備。\n【考試提示】Specific warm-up = 用目標動作本身做漸進負荷。例如工作組 100kg，可做：空槓x10 → 60kgx5 → 80kgx3 → 90kgx1 → 工作組。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1504","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The RAMP protocol for warm-up stands for:","options":["Rest, Activate, Maximize, Perform","Resistance, Agility, Movement, Power","Raise, Activate and Mobilize, Potentiate","Range of motion, Alignment, Muscle activation, Plyometrics"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Raise, Activate and Mobilize, Potentiate","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"RAMP 熱身方案代表：Raise（提升體溫、心率、血流、呼吸頻率）、Activate and Mobilize（啟用關鍵肌群並活動關節）、Potentiate（透過強度遞增的動作來增強後續表現，如漸進負荷或增強式動作）。這是一個系統性的熱身架構。\n【考試提示】RAMP = Raise → Activate & Mobilize → Potentiate。比傳統 general + specific warm-up 更結構化的現代熱身框架。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1505","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Research suggests that static stretching performed immediately before a strength or power activity may:","options":["Significantly increase maximal strength","Acutely decrease force production and power output","Have no effect on performance","Permanently reduce muscle flexibility"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Acutely decrease force production and power output","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"研究顯示運動前進行靜態伸展（特別是持續 >60 秒/肌群）可能急性降低力量產出和爆發力表現。這可能與肌肉-肌腱單元的順應性增加（increased compliance）和神經驅動減少有關。效果通常是暫時的（約 15-30 分鐘），不會永久降低柔軟度。\n【考試提示】Pre-exercise static stretching >60s 可能降低 force production、power output。這是 CSCS 高頻考點。短時間 <30s 的影響較小。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1506","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During warm-up sets for a working set of 5 repetitions at 85% 1RM, which progression is MOST appropriate?","options":["One set at 85% 1RM for 5 reps, then begin working sets","Three sets of 15 repetitions at 30% 1RM","No warm-up sets needed if general warm-up is performed","50% x 8, 70% x 5, 80% x 3, then working sets at 85% x 5"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"50% x 8, 70% x 5, 80% x 3, then working sets at 85% x 5","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"正確的熱身組漸進方式是從較低負荷開始，逐步增加重量並減少次數，直到接近工作組重量。例如：50%x8 → 70%x5 → 80%x3 → 工作組 85%x5。這能在不累積過多疲勞的情況下，充分準備神經肌肉系統。直接從工作重量開始或只做很輕的多次數都不理想。\n【考試提示】熱身組原則：漸進增加負荷、遞減反覆次數。避免熱身組產生過多疲勞，最後 1-2 組接近工作重量但只做少量次數。","tags":["Warm-up Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1507","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"On the Borg 6-20 RPE scale, a rating of 13 corresponds to which verbal descriptor?","options":["Very light","Very hard","Somewhat hard","Maximal exertion"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Somewhat hard","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Borg 6-20 RPE 量表中，13 對應「somewhat hard」（有些辛苦）。此量表設計為 RPE x 10 約等於心率（例如 RPE 13 約等於 HR 130）。6 = 完全無感、9 = 非常輕鬆、11 = 輕鬆、13 = 有些辛苦、15 = 辛苦、17 = 非常辛苦、19 = 極度辛苦、20 = 最大努力。\n【考試提示】Borg 6-20 RPE scale 關鍵數值：6（rest）、9（very light）、13（somewhat hard）、17（very hard）、20（maximal）。RPE x 10 約等於 HR。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1508","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Velocity-based training (VBT) uses barbell velocity to primarily monitor which training variable?","options":["Movement intensity and neuromuscular fatigue","Flexibility improvements","Training volume","Heart rate recovery"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Movement intensity and neuromuscular fatigue","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"速度導向訓練（VBT）使用槓鈴速度來監控訓練強度和神經肌肉疲勞程度。每個運動員在特定 %1RM 下有相對穩定的平均速度，當速度明顯下降超過閾值（如 20% velocity loss），表示累積了顯著疲勞。VBT 也可用於估算即時 1RM 和調整每日訓練負荷。\n【考試提示】VBT 核心概念：velocity loss threshold 用於管理 fatigue。常見閾值：20% velocity loss 約等於訓練效果與疲勞的平衡點。速度越快 = 負荷越輕。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1509","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Session RPE is calculated by multiplying the athlete's RPE by which variable?","options":["Average heart rate","Number of exercises performed","Body weight in kilograms","Session duration in minutes"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Session duration in minutes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Session RPE（訓練負荷指標）= RPE x 訓練時間（分鐘）。例如運動員給予 RPE 7（CR-10 量表），訓練時間 60 分鐘，則 session RPE = 7 x 60 = 420 arbitrary units。這是 Foster 等人提出的簡便訓練負荷量化方法，用於監控整體訓練壓力。\n【考試提示】Session RPE = RPE（CR-10 scale）x session duration（minutes）。通常在訓練結束後 30 分鐘收集 RPE，以避免最後一組的強度偏差。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1510","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Heart rate variability (HRV) is PRIMARILY used as an indicator of:","options":["Maximal aerobic capacity","Muscular strength","Body composition changes","Autonomic nervous system status and recovery readiness"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Autonomic nervous system status and recovery readiness","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"心率變異度（HRV）主要反映自律神經系統（ANS）的狀態，特別是交感與副交感神經的平衡。較高的 HRV 通常表示副交感神經主導，代表恢復良好、準備就緒（readiness）。較低的 HRV 可能表示壓力累積、恢復不足或過度訓練。\n【考試提示】HRV 升高 = parasympathetic dominance = 恢復良好。HRV 降低 = sympathetic dominance = 壓力/疲勞累積。最佳測量時間 = 晨起靜息狀態。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1511","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The acute:chronic workload ratio (ACWR) compares training load over which two time periods?","options":["1 day to 7 days","1 month to 6 months","1 week (acute) to 4 weeks (chronic)","Current session to previous session"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"1 week (acute) to 4 weeks (chronic)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"急性：慢性訓練負荷比（ACWR）比較急性負荷（通常為最近 1 週）與慢性負荷（通常為最近 4 週的平均）。ACWR 約 0.8-1.3 被認為是「甜蜜點」（sweet spot），受傷風險較低。ACWR > 1.5 表示急性負荷大幅超過慢性適應能力，受傷風險顯著增加。\n【考試提示】ACWR = acute load (1 week) / chronic load (4-week average)。Sweet spot = 0.8-1.3。>1.5 = danger zone（高受傷風險）。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1512","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the BEST practical method for daily readiness assessment in a team sport setting?","options":["Blood lactate testing before every session","Standardized wellness questionnaire combined with submaximal performance test","Full VO2max test weekly","Monthly body composition scan"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Standardized wellness questionnaire combined with submaximal performance test","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"在團隊運動環境中，最實用的每日準備度評估方法是結合標準化身心狀態問卷（涵蓋睡眠品質、肌肉痠痛、疲勞、壓力、情緒等）與次最大表現測試（如垂直跳、反向動作跳 CMJ）。這種方法快速、非侵入性，且能同時收集主觀和客觀資料。\n【考試提示】Team setting readiness monitoring = 主觀問卷（wellness questionnaire）+ 客觀測試（CMJ / submaximal test）。要求：快速、非侵入、每日可行。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1513","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When using the modified CR-10 RPE scale for resistance training, an RPE of 10 indicates:","options":["No effort at all","Moderate effort with 5 repetitions in reserve","Light effort suitable for warm-up","Maximal effort with no repetitions in reserve"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Maximal effort with no repetitions in reserve","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"修改版 CR-10 RPE 量表（用於阻力訓練）中，RPE 10 代表最大努力（maximal effort），沒有剩餘反覆次數（0 repetitions in reserve, 0 RIR）。RPE 9 = 1 RIR、RPE 8 = 2 RIR、RPE 7 = 3 RIR。此量表常用於自動調節訓練（autoregulation）。\n【考試提示】Resistance training RPE scale：10 = 0 RIR（maximal）、9 = 1 RIR、8 = 2 RIR、7 = 3 RIR。用於 autoregulation 調整每日訓練負荷。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1514","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which monitoring tool provides the MOST objective measure of external training load during field-based team sports?","options":["GPS tracking devices","Athlete wellness diary","Session RPE questionnaire","Coach's subjective observation"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"GPS tracking devices","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"GPS 追蹤裝置提供最客觀的外部訓練負荷（external load）量測，可記錄總距離、高速跑距離、加速/減速次數、速度區間分佈等資料。Session RPE 和 wellness diary 是主觀的內部負荷（internal load）指標。教練觀察缺乏量化精確度。\n【考試提示】External load = GPS、accelerometers、power output（客觀）。Internal load = RPE、HR、session RPE（主觀/生理反應）。兩者都要監控才完整。","tags":["Athlete Monitoring"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1515","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Functional overreaching (FOR) differs from non-functional overreaching (NFOR) primarily in:","options":["NFOR results in immediate performance gains","FOR requires medical intervention to recover","FOR leads to supercompensation after a short recovery period","NFOR is a planned component of periodization"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"FOR leads to supercompensation after a short recovery period","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"功能性過度負荷（FOR）與非功能性過度負荷（NFOR）的主要區別在於恢復時間和結果。FOR 在短期恢復（數天至 2 週）後會產生超補償（supercompensation），表現提升。NFOR 則需要數週到數月才能恢復，且不一定有超補償效果。過度訓練症候群（OTS）更嚴重，需要數月恢復。\n【考試提示】FOR = 短期恢復後表現提升（計畫性）。NFOR = 需數週至數月恢復。OTS = 需數月以上恢復，可能伴隨系統性症狀。三者是連續光譜。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1516","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a common sign of overtraining syndrome (OTS)?","options":["Consistently improving performance","Increased appetite and weight gain","Decreased resting heart rate","Persistent decrease in performance despite adequate rest"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Persistent decrease in performance despite adequate rest","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"過度訓練症候群（OTS）的典型徵兆是即使有充足休息，表現仍持續下降。其他常見症狀包括：持續疲勞、情緒障礙（煩躁、憂鬱）、睡眠障礙、食慾下降、體重減輕、免疫力下降（容易生病）、靜息心率升高（而非下降）。\n【考試提示】OTS 關鍵特徵：(1) 表現持續下降 despite adequate rest、(2) 持續疲勞、(3) mood disturbance、(4) 靜息心率升高、(5) 免疫力降低。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1517","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A deload week typically involves reducing training volume and/or intensity by approximately:","options":["40-60%","90-100% (complete rest)","5-10%","No reduction, only changing exercises"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"40-60%","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"減量週（deload week）通常將訓練量和/或強度降低約 40-60%。目的是讓身體從累積的疲勞中恢復，同時維持訓練適應。可以透過減少組數、降低負荷、或減少訓練頻率來實現。完全休息或僅降低 5-10% 通常不足以達到有效的恢復效果。\n【考試提示】Deload week 策略：降低 volume 40-60% 或降低 intensity 40-60%（或兩者結合）。通常每 3-4 週安排一次 deload。目標是管理疲勞而非完全休息。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1518","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which recovery strategy has the STRONGEST evidence for enhancing post-exercise recovery?","options":["Cryotherapy chambers (-110 degrees C for 3 minutes)","Compression garments worn for 24 hours","Vibration therapy for 15 minutes","Adequate sleep (7-9 hours per night)"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Adequate sleep (7-9 hours per night)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"充足的睡眠（每晚 7-9 小時）擁有最強的科學證據支援其對運動後恢復的效果。睡眠期間生長激素分泌達高峰、蛋白質合成增加、神經系統恢復、且認知功能復原。睡眠不足會顯著損害表現、增加受傷風險和延長恢復時間。其他策略的證據相對較弱或不一致。\n【考試提示】恢復策略的證據強度：Sleep >> Nutrition > Active recovery > Cold water immersion > Compression/Cryotherapy。睡眠是最被低估但最有效的恢復方式。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1519","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete reports feeling 'flat' during training, has elevated resting heart rate, and shows decreased vertical jump performance over the past 3 weeks. These signs are MOST consistent with:","options":["Adequate recovery and adaptation","Non-functional overreaching or early overtraining","Normal post-warm-up response","Improved fitness due to supercompensation"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Non-functional overreaching or early overtraining","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"連續三週出現訓練時感覺「平」（精神低迷）、靜息心率升高和垂直跳錶現下降，這些是非功能性過度負荷（NFOR）或早期過度訓練的典型徵兆。主觀疲勞 + 客觀表現下降 + 生理指標異常的組合需要立即介入，包括減少訓練負荷、增加恢復和評估壓力來源。\n【考試提示】NFOR/OTS 鑑別三要素：(1) 主觀感覺（fatigue、mood 下降）、(2) 表現指標下降（CMJ、speed）、(3) 生理標記（resting HR 升高、HRV 降低）。三者同時出現要高度警覺。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1520","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a periodized training program, planned overreaching is typically followed by:","options":["An immediate increase in training volume","Switching to a completely new sport","Elimination of all physical activity for one month","A taper or recovery phase to allow supercompensation"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"A taper or recovery phase to allow supercompensation","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"在週期化訓練中，計畫性過度負荷（planned overreaching）之後通常安排減量期（taper）或恢復階段，讓身體產生超補償（supercompensation）效應，表現達到新的高峰。這是 fitness-fatigue 模型的核心概念：訓練同時產生適應（fitness）和疲勞（fatigue），移除疲勞後適應得以充分表現。\n【考試提示】Fitness-Fatigue Model：training 同時提升 fitness 與 fatigue → taper（fatigue 消退速度 > fitness 消退速度）→ supercompensation → peak performance。","tags":["Fatigue Management"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1521","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When conducting a 1RM test, what is the recommended rest interval between maximal attempts?","options":["30-60 seconds","10-15 minutes","2-4 minutes","No rest is needed between attempts"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2-4 minutes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"進行 1RM 測試時，最大嘗試之間建議休息 2-4 分鐘，以確保磷酸肌酸系統充分恢復。休息時間不足會導致疲勞累積，無法展現真正的最大力量。一般建議在 3-5 次嘗試內找到 1RM，每次增加 2.5-5%（上肢）或 5-10%（下肢）。\n【考試提示】1RM testing protocol：warm-up → 50%x8 → 70%x5 → 80%x3 → 90%x1 → 嘗試 1RM。每次嘗試間休息 2-4 分鐘。3-5 次嘗試內完成。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1522","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The Wingate Anaerobic Test is a maximal effort cycling test lasting:","options":["10 seconds","60 seconds","30 seconds","5 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"30 seconds","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Wingate 無氧功率測試是在固定阻力下進行 30 秒的全力衝刺騎車測試。測量指標包括：峰值功率（peak power，通常前 5 秒達到）、平均功率（mean power，30 秒平均）和疲勞指數（fatigue index，功率下降百分比）。阻力通常設定為體重的 7.5%（0.075 kg/kg）。\n【考試提示】Wingate test：30 秒全力、resistance = 0.075 kg/kg body weight。測量：peak power、mean power、fatigue index。是無氧能力的黃金標準測試。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1523","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The pro-agility (5-10-5) test primarily measures:","options":["Maximal aerobic capacity","Muscular endurance","Static balance","Change-of-direction speed and agility"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Change-of-direction speed and agility","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Pro-agility 測試（5-10-5 shuttle）主要測量變向速度和敏捷性。運動員從中線開始，先衝刺 5 碼到一側觸線、轉向衝刺 10 碼到另一側觸線、再轉向衝刺 5 碼回到中線。總距離 20 碼（約 18.3 公尺），測量完成時間。此測試廣泛用於 NFL Combine。\n【考試提示】Pro-agility (5-10-5) = change-of-direction speed。T-test 也測 agility 但包含側移。注意：agility 嚴格定義需包含 reactive component。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1524","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which equation is commonly used to estimate 1RM from a submaximal repetition test?","options":["Karvonen formula","Harris-Benedict equation","Fick equation","Epley formula: 1RM = weight x (1 + reps/30)"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Epley formula: 1RM = weight x (1 + reps/30)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"Epley 公式是最常用的估算 1RM 公式之一：1RM = weight x (1 + reps/30)。例如，運動員以 100kg 完成 8 次，估算 1RM = 100 x (1 + 8/30) = 100 x 1.267 = 126.7kg。此公式在 10RM 以內最準確。Karvonen 用於心率計算，Harris-Benedict 用於基礎代謝率，Fick 用於心輸出量。\n【考試提示】Epley formula: 1RM = weight x (1 + reps/30)。Brzycki formula: 1RM = weight x 36/(37 - reps)。兩者在 10 reps 以內時結果相近。>10 reps 估算誤差增大。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1525","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Test reliability refers to:","options":["Whether the test measures what it claims to measure","The consistency and repeatability of test results","How well test results predict future performance","The number of athletes who can be tested simultaneously"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"The consistency and repeatability of test results","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"信度（reliability）指的是測試結果的一致性和可重複性。同一受試者在相同條件下重複測試應獲得相似的結果。效度（validity）是指測試是否真正測量其宣稱要測量的能力。預測效度（predictive validity）是預測未來表現的能力。高信度是高效度的前提條件。\n【考試提示】Reliability = 一致性/可重複性。Validity = 測量目標的準確性。信度是效度的必要條件（reliable 不一定 valid，但 valid 一定 reliable）。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1526","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The vertical jump test is MOST commonly used to assess:","options":["Cardiorespiratory endurance","Upper-body muscular strength","Flexibility","Lower-body muscular power"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Lower-body muscular power","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"垂直跳測試主要評估下肢肌肉爆發力（lower-body muscular power）。分為 static/squat jump（SJ，從靜止蹲位起跳）和 countermovement jump（CMJ，含下蹲反跳動作）。CMJ 比 SJ 跳更高，因為利用了拉長-縮短週期（stretch-shortening cycle）。測量方法包括 Vertec、跳躍墊和力板。\n【考試提示】Vertical jump = lower-body power。CMJ > SJ（因為 stretch-shortening cycle）。兩者差值反映 reactive strength / SSC 利用能力。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1527","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The 40-yard dash is considered a test of:","options":["Linear speed and acceleration","Aerobic capacity","Muscular endurance","Anaerobic threshold"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Linear speed and acceleration","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"40 碼衝刺（40-yard dash，約 36.6 公尺）是測量線性速度和加速能力的標準測試。通常也記錄 10 碼和 20 碼的分段時間，以分別評估起步加速（start acceleration）和最大速度（maximum velocity）能力。此測試廣泛用於 NFL Combine 和各級運動選材。\n【考試提示】40-yard dash = linear speed + acceleration。10-yard split = start/acceleration phase。20-40 yard = max velocity phase。能量系統 = ATP-PC 為主。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1528","part":2,"domain":"Program Implementation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which test protocol is considered the 'gold standard' for measuring maximal aerobic capacity (VO2max)?","options":["1-mile walk test","Cooper 12-minute run test","Step test","Graded exercise test (GXT) with metabolic gas analysis"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"Graded exercise test (GXT) with metabolic gas analysis","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"漸進式運動測試（GXT）搭配代謝氣體分析是測量最大攝氧量（VO2max）的黃金標準。運動員在跑步機或功率計上逐步增加強度直到力竭，同時透過氣體分析儀直接測量氧氣消耗量。1-mile walk、Cooper test 和 step test 都是估算 VO2max 的間接方法。\n【考試提示】VO2max gold standard = GXT + metabolic cart（直接測量法）。Cooper 12-min run、1.5-mile run、step test = 估演算法（indirect/submaximal）。直接法最準但最貴。","tags":["Testing Protocols"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1529","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to NSCA facility guidelines, what is the recommended minimum spacing around each piece of resistance training equipment?","options":["36 inches (91 cm) on all sides","6 inches (15 cm)","10 feet (3 m) on all sides","No spacing is needed if bumper plates are used"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"36 inches (91 cm) on all sides","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 設施指南建議每件阻力訓練裝置四周至少保留 36 英寸（約 91 公分）的間隔空間。這確保運動員有安全的活動空間，教練和補手能自由移動，並在槓鈴意外掉落時有足夠的安全緩衝區域。奧林匹克舉重平臺也需要同樣的間距標準。\n【考試提示】NSCA 間距建議：resistance training equipment = 36 inches on all sides。確保 traffic flow 和緊急通道暢通。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1530","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The recommended temperature range for an indoor strength and conditioning facility is:","options":["50-60 degrees F (10-16 degrees C)","85-95 degrees F (29-35 degrees C)","68-78 degrees F (20-26 degrees C)","40-50 degrees F (4-10 degrees C)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"68-78 degrees F (20-26 degrees C)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"室內力量與體能訓練設施的建議溫度範圍為 68-78 degrees F（20-26 degrees C）。過冷的環境會增加肌肉拉傷風險並降低表現，過熱的環境會增加熱疾病風險和提早疲勞。相對濕度應維持在 60% 以下。良好的通風系統也是必要的。\n【考試提示】設施環境標準：溫度 68-78 degrees F（20-26 degrees C）、相對濕度 <60%。需有 adequate ventilation。戶外訓練要注意 WBGT（濕球黑球溫度）。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1531","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What type of flooring is MOST appropriate for an Olympic weightlifting area?","options":["Standard carpet","Rubber flooring or dedicated weightlifting platform","Hardwood basketball court flooring","Ceramic tile"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Rubber flooring or dedicated weightlifting platform","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"奧林匹克舉重區域最適合使用橡膠地板或專用舉重平臺。這些材料能吸收槓鈴從高處落下的衝擊力、保護地板結構、降低噪音，並提供穩定的站立表面。地毯不夠穩定，硬木地板和瓷磚無法承受重複的重物衝擊。平臺通常由合板中心搭配兩側橡膠組成。\n【考試提示】Olympic lifting area = rubber flooring / weightlifting platform。Platform 結構：中間 hardwood/plywood（站立穩定）+ 兩側 rubber（吸震）。厚度建議至少 1.5 inches。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1532","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength and conditioning facility's emergency action plan (EAP) should include all of the following EXCEPT:","options":["Location of AED and first aid supplies","Staff roles and responsibilities during an emergency","Detailed workout programs for all athletes","Emergency contact numbers and nearest hospital route"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Detailed workout programs for all athletes","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"緊急行動計畫（EAP）應包含：AED 和急救用品位置、工作人員在緊急情況中的角色分工、緊急聯絡電話和最近醫院路線、疏散路線、以及緊急情境模擬演練計畫。詳細的運動員訓練計畫不屬於 EAP 的一部分，那是訓練規劃的範疇。\n【考試提示】EAP 必備要素：(1) AED/first aid 位置、(2) 人員角色分工、(3) 緊急電話/醫院路線、(4) evacuation routes、(5) 定期演練。至少每年更新一次。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1533","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"According to NSCA standards, what is the recommended minimum square footage of strength training space per athlete training simultaneously?","options":["10 sq ft (0.9 sq m)","100 sq ft (9.3 sq m)","36 sq ft (3.3 sq m)","200 sq ft (18.6 sq m)"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"100 sq ft (9.3 sq m)","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"NSCA 建議每位同時訓練的運動員至少需要 100 平方英尺（約 9.3 平方公尺）的力量訓練空間。這包含裝置空間、安全間距、通道和緊急疏散空間。如果設施有奧林匹克舉重平臺，每個平臺可能需要更多空間（約 12x8 ft 加上週圍間距）。\n【考試提示】NSCA 空間標準：至少 100 sq ft per athlete（力量訓練區）。Olympic platform area 約 12x8 ft + 周圍 36 inches 間距。設施總面積需考慮 warm-up area、stretching area、office。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1534","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Equipment inspection and maintenance records should be documented and reviewed at what frequency?","options":["Only when equipment visibly breaks","Once every 5 years","Only before an accreditation visit","On a regular schedule, at minimum annually, with daily visual inspections"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"On a regular schedule, at minimum annually, with daily visual inspections","explanation_en":null,"explanation_zh":"裝置檢查和維護記錄應按規律的時間表執行，至少每年進行一次全面檢查，並每天進行目視檢查。日常檢查包括：確認機械裝置功能正常、電纜無磨損、墊子無破裂、螺栓緊固、以及整體清潔衛生。所有檢查和維護應書面記錄存檔，這也是法律責任（liability）保護的重要措施。\n【考試提示】裝置維護頻率：Daily = visual inspection（目視檢查）。Monthly/Quarterly = 詳細功能檢查。Annually = 全面專業檢查。所有記錄都要書面存檔（liability protection）。","tags":["Facility Safety"],"source":"certprep"},{"id":"q1535","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following shoulder movements and planes of motion are associated with the upward movement phase of the side lateral shoulder raise exercise?","options":["flexion/transverse","abduction/sagittal","abduction/frontal"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"abduction/frontal","explanation_en":null,"tags":["official","biomechanics","planes-of-motion"],"source":"nsca-sample","explanation_zh":"側平舉（side lateral raise）的上舉階段是肩關節外展（abduction），發生在額狀面/冠狀面（frontal plane）並繞前後軸運動。矢狀面是前後擺動，橫斷面是水平動作，皆不符。"},{"id":"q1536","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An untrained college-aged athlete begins a resistance training program. After training for three weeks, her strength increases dramatically. Which of the following is the most influential factor responsible for this improvement?","options":["decreased cross-sectional area of Type I fibers","increased number of muscle fibers","improved neuromuscular efficiency"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"improved neuromuscular efficiency","explanation_en":null,"tags":["official","neuromuscular-adaptations"],"source":"nsca-sample","explanation_zh":"訓練初期（前幾週）的顯著力量增益來自神經適應：神經肌肉效率（neuromuscular efficiency）改善，包括運動單位動員率與招募增加、動作協調改善；肌纖維橫截面積與數量的改變此時還不明顯。"},{"id":"q1537","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the minimum amount of carbohydrates that a 132-lb (60-kg) competitive Olympic triathlete should consume on a daily basis?","options":["120 g","480 g","960 g"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"480 g","explanation_en":null,"tags":["official","nutrition","carbohydrate"],"source":"nsca-sample","explanation_zh":"長時間耐力專案（如鐵人三項）建議每日碳水約8–10 g/kg。60公斤×8 g/kg＝480公克，為最低應攝取量。"},{"id":"q1538","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When running, which of the following contributes the most to minimizing the braking effect of a heel foot strike?","options":["eccentric hip flexion","concentric hip extension","eccentric knee extension"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"concentric hip extension","explanation_en":null,"tags":["official","biomechanics","running"],"source":"nsca-sample","explanation_zh":"跑步落地時髖伸肌群（臀大肌、膕旁肌）以向心收縮（concentric hip extension）快速把軀幹推進過支撐點上方，是最能抵消跟部著地煞車效應的動作機制。"},{"id":"q1539","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following components of mechanical load is the least important for stimulating new bone formation?","options":["rest period","magnitude","rate of loading"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"rest period","explanation_en":null,"tags":["official","bone-adaptation"],"source":"nsca-sample","explanation_zh":"刺激新骨形成的機械負荷要素是負荷強度（magnitude）、負荷速率（rate of loading）與頻率等；在骨形成刺激上，休息期是相對最不必要的引數。"},{"id":"q1540","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the upward movement phase of the low-bar back squat, which of the following muscles acts synergistically to the rectus femoris?","options":["biceps femoris","rectus abdominis","anterior tibialis","iliopsoas"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"biceps femoris","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q1"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"低槓背蹲站起階段需要強力伸髖，膕旁肌中的股二頭肌（biceps femoris）作為髖伸肌協同（synergist）參與伸髖鏈。腹直肌、脛前肌不在此主動作鏈，髂腰肌是屈髖肌、作用方向相反。"},{"id":"q1541","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following upper arm muscle groups and types of muscle actions are associated with the dumbbell biceps curl exercise? Primary muscle group / primary muscle action: I. flexors, eccentric  II. extensors, eccentric  III. flexors, concentric  IV. extensors, concentric","options":["II and III only","I and IV only","I and III only","II and IV only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q2","table-question"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"依答案（I和III）：啞鈴彎舉的主動肌群是肘屈肌群（肱二頭肌、肱肌），上舉階段為向心收縮、下放階段採離心控制；肱三頭肌為拮抗肌。"},{"id":"q1542","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is an approximate rest interval for a middle distance runner performing 800-meter (875-yd) running intervals in 2 minutes?","options":["1 minute","2 minutes","4 minutes","6 minutes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"2 minutes","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q3"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"5e 第21章（p1540–1541）：3–5 分鐘的工作間隔，休息時間應等於工作時間（W:R 1:1）；長間歇 HIIT 的例子是 ≥90% VO2max 下跑 2–3 分鐘、搭配 ≤2 分鐘的被動或低強度恢復；休息過長會削弱糖解系統的訓練效果。因此 2 分鐘跑完的 800 公尺間歇，組間休息以約 2 分鐘為宜。（舊答案 6 分鐘採 4e 時代無氧間歇 1:3+ 說法，與 5e 的間歇建議不符。）"},{"id":"q1543","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 165-pound (75-kg) athlete has an average daily intake of 450 grams of carbohydrate, 75 grams of protein, and 100 grams of fat. What percent of the total kilocalorie intake is carbohydrate?","options":["72%","60%","45%","25%"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"60%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q4"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"熱量計算：碳水450 g×4＝1800 kcal、蛋白質75 g×4＝300 kcal、脂肪100 g×9＝900 kcal，總計3000 kcal；1800/3000＝60%。"},{"id":"q1544","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 110-pound (50-kg) marathon runner started her pre-race taper and chose to carbohydrate load prior to the race. Approximately how many grams of carbohydrates should she consume per day?","options":["100 g","500 g","880 g","1100 g"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"500 g","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q5"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"碳水增量（carbohydrate loading）約每日8–12 g/kg（賽前1–3天），50公斤約400–600公克，500 g最接近；1100 g過高、100 g不足。"},{"id":"q1545","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As compared to males, the potential for force production of females per muscle cross-sectional area is:","options":["lower","equal","higher","dependent on the type of muscle"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"equal","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q6"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"在相同肌肉橫截面積下，女性產生力量的潛力與男性相等（equal）；女性絕對力量較低主要是肌肉總量較少，而非單位面積品質差異。"},{"id":"q1546","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following cardiovascular adaptations to chronic aerobic exercise contribute the most to improved aerobic endurance performance?","options":["increased maximal cardiac output","decreased resting blood pressure","decreased resting heart rate","increased submaximal arterial-venous oxygen (a-vO2) difference"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"increased maximal cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q7"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"最大心輸出量（maximal cardiac output）提升直接提高最大攝氧量（Fick定律：VO2max＝心率×中搏出量×動靜脈氧差），對有氧耐力表現的貢獻最大；靜息心率下降、血壓下降屬靜息適應。"},{"id":"q1547","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following events occurs in the hamstring muscles during the concentric muscle action of the leg (knee) curl exercise?","options":["chloride ions are released inside the muscle fiber","each sarcomere is stimulated by a motor neuron","the actin cross-bridges attach to the myosin filaments","the H-zone decreases as the Z-discs are pulled toward each other"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"the H-zone decreases as the Z-discs are pulled toward each other","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q8"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"肌肉向心收縮時肌動蛋白橫橋拉動粗肌絲，Z盤彼此靠近，H帶（H-zone）變窄——這是滑行絲理論的收縮表現。氯離子釋放、運動神經刺激發生在收縮前的興奮階段。"},{"id":"q1548","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The depletion of which of the following fuel sources may contribute to fatigue in prolonged aerobic endurance events AND repeated anaerobic exercise bouts?","options":["muscle glycogen","triglycerides","free fatty acids","creatine phosphate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"muscle glycogen","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q9"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"肌肝醣（muscle glycogen）同時是有氧耐力賽事的長期燃料與無氧高強度反覆衝刺的燃料，兩者的疲勞都與肌肝醣耗盡有關。"},{"id":"q1549","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following competitive situations would inspire an athlete with a high motive to achieve success (MAS)?","options":["a very easy competition in which success is virtually guaranteed","an extremely difficult situation in which the likelihood of success is limited","a competition that causes a fear that there is a threat to self-esteem","a challenging situation in which the probability of success to failure is even"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"a challenging situation in which the probability of success to failure is even","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q10"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"高成就動機（high MAS）者偏好成功機率約50/50的挑戰性情境：太簡單缺乏成就感、太困難成功率太低都難以激發。"},{"id":"q1550","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a characteristic of fast-twitch muscle fibers?","options":["low contraction speed","high resistance to fatigue","low anaerobic enzyme content","high power output"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"high power output","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q11"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"快縮肌纖維（Type II）收縮速度快、功率輸出（power output）高，但粒線體與微血管較少、較易疲勞，無氧酵素含量較高。"},{"id":"q1551","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following activities places the LEAST metabolic demand on the phosphagen energy system?","options":["tennis","football","basketball","cross-country skiing"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"cross-country skiing","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q12"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"越野滑雪是持續數十分鐘以上的長時間有氧運動，主要依賴有氧系統，對磷酸原（phosphagen）系統依賴最低；網球、美式足球、籃球都有反覆的高強度 bursts。"},{"id":"q1552","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During isokinetic testing at high angular velocities (>240 degrees/sec), what is the approximate torque capability of eccentric muscle actions as compared to concentric muscle actions?","options":["60% lower","120% greater","60% greater","120% lower"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"120% greater","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q13"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"高角速度（>240°/秒）等速測試時，向心扭矩隨速度顯著下降，離心扭矩則不受速度影響維持高值，因此離心可高約120%。"},{"id":"q1553","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises stimulates the GREATEST increase in axial skeleton bone mineral density?","options":["biceps curl","lat pulldown","shoulder press","lying triceps extension"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"shoulder press","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q14"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"軸向骨架骨密度刺激需要脊椎軸向負荷的舉重動作：肩推（shoulder press）槓鈴置於肩上架於軸上，對脊椎施加軸向壓力；二頭肌彎舉、滑輪下拉、三頭肌伸展皆無軸向負荷。"},{"id":"q1554","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a dietary source of an incomplete protein?","options":["legumes","eggs","milk","fish"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"legumes","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q15"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"豆類（legumes）是不完全蛋白質，缺乏某些必需胺基酸（如蛋胺酸）；蛋、奶、魚等動物性食物為完全蛋白質。"},{"id":"q1555","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises involves a first-class lever?","options":["leg (knee) curl","triceps pushdown","lateral raise","dumbbell biceps curl"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"triceps pushdown","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q16"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"三頭肌下壓（triceps pushdown）以肘關節為支點、負荷與施力分居支點兩側的模式屬第一類槓桿（first-class lever，支點在中間）。彎舉與側平舉為第三類槓桿。"},{"id":"q1556","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Dynamically pre-stretching a muscle is associated with which type of subsequent muscle action?","options":["eccentric","concentric","isometric","kinesthetic"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"concentric","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q17"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"動態預牽拉肌肉後接著的是向心收縮（concentric）：這是牽張-縮短週期（stretch-shortening cycle）的機制，預牽拉利用彈效能儲存與伸展反射增強後續向心收縮（即增強式訓練原理）。"},{"id":"q1557","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following applied program design variables of a resistance training program contribute to significant exercise-induced increases in serum testosterone concentrations EXCEPT:","options":["heavy loads","high volumes","long rest periods","large muscle group exercises"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"long rest periods","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q18"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"提升運動後血清睪固酮的策略是大重量、高訓練量、進行大肌群動作並搭配短休息；長休息組間會降低代謝壓力，對睪固酮提升貢獻最小，故答案為長休息期。"},{"id":"q1558","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following decreases as a result of resistance training and increases due to aerobic training?","options":["glycogen stores","mitochondrial density","maximal force production","creatine phosphate stores"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"mitochondrial density","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q19"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"粒線體密度：有氧訓練增加粒線體密度與體積；阻力訓練以肥大為主，粒線體密度反而相對稀釋下降。肌力、磷酸原儲存量是阻力訓練提昇項。"},{"id":"q1559","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Performance decrements from dehydration among aerobic endurance athletes may begin to occur after the loss of what percentage of body mass?","options":["1%","3%","5%","7%"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"3%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q20"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"脫水達體重約2%–3%起，有氧耐力運動員的表現（調節體溫、心輸出量）即開始明顯下滑，題庫答案為3%。"},{"id":"q1560","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following causes the largest increase in serum growth hormone concentration?","options":["oral ingestion of arginine","oral ingestion of ornithine","a low-intensity aerobic exercise session","a high-intensity resistance exercise session"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"a high-intensity resistance exercise session","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q21"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"高強度阻力訓練（大重量、短休息、高乳酸）是血清生長激素上升最有效的刺激，遠超過口服精胺酸/鳥胺酸或低強度有氧。"},{"id":"q1561","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the MOST appropriate course of action if an eating disorder is suspected with an athlete?","options":["Schedule weekly weigh-in sessions.","Provide comprehensive nutrition information.","Refer the athlete to the team physician.","Monitor the athlete's food intake."],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Refer the athlete to the team physician.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q22"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"懷疑飲食失調時，體能教練最恰當的處理是轉介給隊醫（team physician），由醫療團隊統合診斷並協同營養師、心理師追蹤；教練自行量體重或監控飲食效果有限。"},{"id":"q1562","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An untrained college-aged athlete begins a resistance training program. After training for 3 weeks, her strength increases dramatically. Which of the following is the MOST influential factor responsible for this improvement?","options":["increased cross-sectional area of muscle fibers","increased quantity of muscle fibers","improved ratio of muscle to fat components","improved neuromuscular efficiency"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"improved neuromuscular efficiency","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q23"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"訓練3週內的力量大幅提升主要是神經適應——神經肌肉效率（improved neuromuscular efficiency）改善：運動單位動員與同步化提升；肌纖維肥大、數量改變、體脂比例改善都不是此時主因。"},{"id":"q1563","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following are potential indicators of overtraining EXCEPT:","options":["decreased muscle glycogen stores","increased sleep disturbances","decreased exercise heart rate","increased resting blood pressure"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"decreased exercise heart rate","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q24"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"過度訓練的指標包括肌肝醣儲量下降、睡眠障礙、靜息血壓上升、運動時心率反應異常（通常升高而非降低），因此「運動時心率下降」不是過度訓練表現。"},{"id":"q1564","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When lifting maximal loads, the use of a weight belt may provide the MOST benefit when performing which of the following exercises?","options":["machine shoulder press","bench press","hip sled","front squat"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"front squat","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q25"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"舉最大重量時，腰帶透過增加腹內壓穩定腰椎，對脊椎軸向負荷的前蹲（front squat）幫助最大；仰臥推、器械肩推、腿推 sled的脊椎軸向負荷較小。"},{"id":"q1565","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 6-foot, 2-inch (188 cm), 220-pound (100-kg) college football player desires to gain muscle weight. Which of the following should be his first nutritional priority if his current 3000 calories/day intake consists of 18% protein (1.4 g/kg), 55% carbohydrate (4.1 g/kg), and 27% fat (0.9 g/kg)?","options":["increase calories","increase protein","decrease fat","decrease carbohydrate"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"increase calories","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q26"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"想增加肌肉體重，第一優先是總熱量攝取增加（熱量盈餘）；熱量不足時蛋白質會被當作能量燒掉，故先補足熱量再談蛋白質比例。"},{"id":"q1566","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a single aerobic exercise session, oxygen is delivered to the working muscles at an elevated rate due to an increase in","options":["total blood hemoglobin.","cardiac output.","blood glucose.","plasma volume."],"answer":1,"answer_text":"cardiac output.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q27"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"單次有氧運動中，心輸出量（cardiac output）增加使更多血液與氧被輸送到工作肌；血紅素、血漿量屬長期適應，血糖與供氧無直接關係。"},{"id":"q1567","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How is the exercise technique needed for jogging modified when performing a warm-up drill for plyometrics?","options":["greatly increasing hip and knee flexion","not allowing the heels to touch the ground","extending the knees to touch the heels to the buttocks","limiting multidirectional changes"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"not allowing the heels to touch the ground","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q41"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"增強式熱身的跳躍預備動作要改跑步技巧為腳跟不觸地、以前足彈性著地，模擬增強式所需的剛性觸地與快速反跳；加大屈髖屈膝是高抬腿跑，非重點。"},{"id":"q1568","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises requires the MOST similar quadriceps muscle function as landing from a rebound in basketball?","options":["alternate leg bound","downhill running","plyometric jump to box","resisted sprinting"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"downhill running","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q42"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"籃板落地時股四頭肌做高強度離心收縮吸收衝擊；下坡跑步（downhill running）同樣要求股四頭肌大量離心煞車，肌力需求最相似，也是常用的離心預adapt動作。"},{"id":"q1569","part":2,"domain":"Testing and Evaluation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following will be improved if the same strength and conditioning professional evaluates an athlete's body composition during the pre-season AND the post-season?","options":["reliability","validity","variability","subjectivity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"reliability","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q43"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"同一位專業人員以相同程式在學前與學後量測體成分，控制施測者變因，提升的是測驗的信度（reliability，再現性）；效度涉及測驗是否量到要測的東西，不受重複施測影響。"},{"id":"q1570","part":2,"domain":"Testing and Evaluation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A college baseball player was tested ten weeks before the start of the season with these results: 1RM bench press: 275 pounds (125 kg); vertical jump: 24 inches (61 cm); T-Test: 11.6 seconds; 40-yard sprint: 4.8 seconds; 1-minute sit-up: 37. Which of the following need to be improved in the pre-season training program?","options":["agility and muscular strength","power and local muscular endurance","power and muscular strength","agility and local muscular endurance"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"agility and local muscular endurance","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q44","table-question"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"該球員的1RM仰臥推與垂直跳資料顯示肌力與爆發力已佳，測驗未涵蓋且棒球專項需要的弱項是靈敏與區域性肌耐力，故訓練優先順序應擺在這兩項。"},{"id":"q1571","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following muscles is an antagonist to the deltoid muscle during the upward movement phase of the seated barbell shoulder press?","options":["serratus anterior","latissimus dorsi","supraspinatus","trapezius"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"latissimus dorsi","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q45"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"坐姿槓鈴肩推上舉階段三角肌做肩屈曲/外展，背闊肌（做肩伸展、內收、內旋）為其拮抗肌；前鋸肌、棘上肌、斜方肌皆為協同/上舉參與肌。"},{"id":"q1572","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As the rear leg swings forward for the next stride in sprinting, which of the following muscle groups (of that same leg) eccentrically controls forward momentum?","options":["quadriceps","gastrocnemius","iliopsoas","hamstrings"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"hamstrings","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q46"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"衝刺時後擺的腿向前擺出，膕旁肌（hamstrings）以離心收縮減速小腿的向前動能、保護膝關節並為著地做準備；股四頭肌、膕旁肌之外，腓腸肌與髂腰肌不主導此煞車。"},{"id":"q1573","part":2,"domain":"Testing and Evaluation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A junior college basketball forward is administered a battery of tests to determine her training status. Based upon the results shown below, her training program should be designed to emphasize improvement in which of the following areas? Height: 69 inches (175 cm); Weight: 150 pounds (68 kg); Percent body fat: 20%; 1RM bench press: 100 pounds (45 kg); 1RM squat: 215 pounds (98 kg); Vertical jump: 19 inches (48 cm).","options":["body composition","upper body strength","lower body strength","anaerobic power"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"upper body strength","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q47","table-question"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"依測驗結果與同位置常模比較，她的上肢肌力落後最多，訓練計畫應優先改善upper body strength；其餘專案相對達標。"},{"id":"q1574","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a single training session, which of the following exercise sequences is the MOST appropriate for the strength/power phase of an athlete's program?","options":["power clean, bench press, back squat, bent-over row, leg (knee) curl","leg press, front squat, snatch, push press, incline bench press","lunge, pec deck, hip ab/adduction, snatch, lateral raise","push press, shoulder press, power clean, deadlift, power pull"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"power clean, bench press, back squat, bent-over row, leg (knee) curl","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q48"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"力量/功率階段的動作順序應為：先高功率舉重動作（power clean），再大肌群多關節動作（仰臥推、背蹲），最後單關節動作（腿彎曲）。選項A完全符合；其他選項把snatch排在深蹲後或以器械單關節動作開場，順序不當。"},{"id":"q1575","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the MOST appropriate type of surface for performing high-intensity lower-body plyometric drills?","options":["artificial turf","grass field","minitrampoline","outdoor basketball court"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"grass field","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q50"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"高強度下肢增強式（如深度跳）衝擊大，應選草地上（grass field）這類較軟的平面吸收衝擊、降低受傷風險；室外籃球場水泥地最硬，小蹦床太軟不利於動作品質轉移。"},{"id":"q1576","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In a turn-and-run maneuver when transitioning from a backpedal into a forward sprint in the same direction, which of the following body parts initiates the movement?","options":["head","shoulders","hips","feet"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"head","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q51"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"轉身為跑（turn and run）的順序由頭部帶領：先看/轉向要跑的方向，接著依序帶動肩、髖、腳轉體加速，頭部主導身體朝向，是最先啟動的部位。"},{"id":"q1577","part":2,"domain":"Testing and Evaluation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following sequences will produce the MOST reliable results? 1. T-Test  2. 1RM incline bench press  3. 1RM power clean  4. 1-minute sit-up test","options":["3, 1, 4, 2","1, 3, 2, 4","4, 2, 1, 3","2, 3, 1, 4"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"1, 3, 2, 4","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q52","table-question"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"可靠順序依「不疲勞→疲勞」：先靈敏測驗（T-Test），再神經肌肉大功率專案（1RM power clean）、其他1RM肌力（上斜仰臥推），最後肌耐力（一分鐘仰臥起坐），即1→3→2→4。"},{"id":"q1578","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In response to a heavy loading session, the muscle groups stressed in which of the following exercises require the longest recovery time?","options":["bench press","leg (knee) extension","front squat","dumbbell chest fly"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"front squat","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q53"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"前蹲是動員最多大肌群的結構性動作，高負荷後所需恢復時間最長（大肌群複合動作約需72小時）；單關節器械動作（腿伸直）恢復最快。"},{"id":"q1579","part":2,"domain":"Testing and Evaluation","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a test for aerobic power?","options":["1 RM power clean","vertical jump","T-Test","1.5 mile run"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"1.5 mile run","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q54"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"1.5英里跑是標準有氧能力（aerobic endurance/power）測驗，以完成時間推算VO2max；power clean測爆發力、垂直跳測肌力功率、T-Test測靈敏。"},{"id":"q1580","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the MOST sport-specific exercise for a sprinter?","options":["dumbbell lunge","upright row","ankle dorsiflexion","leg (knee) curl"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"dumbbell lunge","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q55"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"啞鈴弓箭步（dumbbell lunge）的單腳支撐、髖膝踝三關節伸展動作模式與衝刺蹬地最接近，是短跑選手最對項的肌力動作；直立划船、踝背屈、腿彎曲與跑動模式關聯較低。"},{"id":"q1581","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For the shoulder press exercise, how many repetitions can typically be performed with a load of 85% of the 1 RM?","options":["12","10","6","2"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"6","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q56"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"依1RM–次數對照表，85% 1RM約可完成6次；10–12次約對應60–70%，2次約92–95%。"},{"id":"q1582","part":2,"domain":"Organization and Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The tallest machines or pieces of equipment in a strength and conditioning facility should be placed next to the:","options":["emergency exits.","supervisor stations.","room entrances.","perimeter walls."],"answer":3,"answer_text":"perimeter walls.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q57"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"最高的器械應沿周邊牆面（perimeter walls）擺放，避免遮擋視線、保持動線與監督視野通暢，並降低傾倒危害。"},{"id":"q1583","part":2,"domain":"Organization and Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following are recommended to be completed prior to a new athlete using the strength and conditioning facility? I. 1 RM testing  II. \"Assumption of Risk\" form  III. medical examination  IV. exercise technique orientation","options":["I, II, and IV only","II, III, and IV only","I, II, and III only","I, III, and IV only"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"II, III, and IV only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q58"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"新運動員首次使用設施前應完成：風險自負同意書（assumption of risk）、健康檢查、動作技巧導覽（orientation）；1RM測驗屬訓練前後評量安排，不是入場前提。"},{"id":"q1584","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following are commonly-accepted benefits of properly performed static stretching movements EXCEPT:","options":["increased joint range of motion","decreased muscle stiffness","decreased superficial muscle temperature","increased localized blood flow"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"decreased superficial muscle temperature","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q59"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"靜態伸展的好處包括增加關節ROM、降低肌肉僵硬、增加區域性血流；「降低淺層肌溫」不是靜態伸展的好處（溫度下降屬冷卻效果，與伸展機制無關）。"},{"id":"q1585","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following factors should be determined FIRST when designing a training program for a specific team sport?","options":["layout of the facility","type of available equipment","number of individuals on the team","metabolic demands of the activity"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"metabolic demands of the activity","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q60"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"設計隊伍訓練計畫第一步是需求分析：先確定專項的能量系統/代謝需求（metabolic demands），再決定動作選擇、訓練量與強度；設施與器材限制屬後續的實際考量。"},{"id":"q1586","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A baseball pitcher has an elbow flexion to elbow extension strength ratio of 1:3. Which of the following exercises should be added to his program to reduce the risk of throwing-related injuries?","options":["dumbbell biceps curl","decline bench press","bent-over lateral raise","overhead triceps extension"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"dumbbell biceps curl","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q61"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"肘屈:肘伸力量比1:3代表肘屈肌（肱二頭肌等）相對過弱，應加入啞鈴彎舉強化肘屈肌群以平衡_ratio_、降低投球肘部受傷風險。"},{"id":"q1587","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a structural exercise that can only be performed using free weights?","options":["front squat","snatch","bent-over row","overhead dumbbell triceps extension"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"snatch","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q62"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"抓舉（snatch）屬核心/結構性動作（槓鈴貼身、全身參與、需平衡與協調），且只能以自由重量進行；前蹲、划船有器械替代品，且划船非結構性動作。"},{"id":"q1588","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the typical sequence of periodization periods within one macrocycle?","options":["competition, transition, active rest, preparatory","preparatory, transition, competition, active rest","transition, preparatory, active rest, competition","active rest, transition, competition, preparatory"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"preparatory, transition, competition, active rest","explanation_en":null,"tags":["legacy","official-nsca","orig-q64"],"source":"nsca-vol1","explanation_zh":"一個大週期（macrocycle）的標準順序：準備期（preparatory）→轉換期/賽前轉化（transition）→比賽期（competition）→主動休息期（active rest）。"},{"id":"q1589","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What does CSCS stand for in the NSCA certification?","options":["Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist","Certified Sports and Conditioning Specialist","Certified Safety and Conditioning Specialist","Certified Strength and Cardiovascular Specialist"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist","explanation_en":null,"tags":["certification-basics"],"source":"ptgeeks","explanation_zh":"CSCS＝Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist（註冊肌力與體能專家），是NSCA的認證credential。"},{"id":"q1590","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the primary energy system used during a 100-meter sprint?","options":["Aerobic system","Lactate system","Phosphocreatine system","Oxidative system"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"Phosphocreatine system","explanation_en":null,"tags":["energy-systems"],"source":"ptgeeks","explanation_zh":"100公尺短跑約10秒內完成，主要能量系統是磷酸原/磷肌酸系統（phosphocreatine, ATP-PC）；乳酸系統主導約30秒–2分鐘的高強度運動，有氧系統負責長時間運動。"},{"id":"q1591","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which training principle refers to gradually increasing training demands?","options":["Specificity","Progressive overload","Reversibility","Individual differences"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"Progressive overload","explanation_en":null,"tags":["training-principles"],"source":"ptgeeks","explanation_zh":"漸進增加訓練需求是漸進超負荷原則（progressive overload）；specificity是專門性，reversibility是停訓後效果可逆，individual differences是個體差異。"},{"id":"q1592","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the recommended rest period between sets for maximum strength training?","options":["30-60 seconds","1-2 minutes","2-5 minutes","5-10 minutes"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"2-5 minutes","explanation_en":null,"tags":["rest-intervals"],"source":"ptgeeks","explanation_zh":"最大肌力訓練（≥85% 1RM）組間休息建議2–5分鐘，讓磷酸原系統恢復、維持每組的力量輸出品質。"},{"id":"q1593","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Two individuals of the same body mass are lifting weights. Assuming all other factors to be equal, the person with tendons inserted on the bone _______________ the joint center should be able to lift _______________ weight.","options":["closer to; a heavier","medial to; less","laterally to; less","farther from; a heavier"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"farther from; a heavier","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌腱附著點離關節越遠（farther from），力臂越長、力矩優勢越大，能舉起更重（a heavier）的負荷；附著點靠近關節則力臂短、力量表現較差。"},{"id":"q1594","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which anatomical plane divides the body into left and right sections?","options":["sagittal","transverse","perpendicular","frontal"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"sagittal","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"矢狀面（sagittal plane）把身體分為左右兩半；橫斷面分上下，額狀面/冠狀面分左右前後。"},{"id":"q1595","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"An athlete in the weight room is performing the barbell bench press. If he moves a mass of 75 kg with an acceleration of 2 m/s², what force is he exerting?","options":["37.5 N","37.5 kg·m-1·s²","150 N","150 kg·m-1·s²"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"150 N","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"牛頓第二定律 F＝ma＝75 kg×2 m/s²＝150 kg·m·s⁻²＝150牛頓（N）；N即kg·m·s⁻²的簡寫，故正確單位答案是150 N。"},{"id":"q1596","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Neural control affects the maximal force output of a muscle by determining which and how many motor units are involved in a muscle contraction and the rate at which the motor units are fired. These two factors are known as what, respectively?","options":["rate coding; EMG","EMG; firing rates","recruitment; rate coding","firing rates; recruitment"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"recruitment; rate coding","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"神經控制透過運動單位的動員（recruitment，決定參與哪些與多少運動單位）與頻率編碼（rate coding，放電速率與同步化）決定肌肉最大出力。"},{"id":"q1597","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"All of the following are considered to be advantages when using weight-stack machines EXCEPT","options":["design flexibility","simulates real-life activities","reduced likelihood of injury","easy to use"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"simulates real-life activities","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"插片式器械（weight-stack machines）的好處是調整方便、安全、易上手；「模擬真實生活活動」是自由重量的優點，器械固定軌道反而不模擬真實情境。"},{"id":"q1598","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following is the resistive force encountered when one attempts to move an object while it is pressed against another object?","options":["friction","inertia","obstruction","gravity"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"friction","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兩物體互相壓住並相對滑動時遇到的阻力是摩擦力（friction）；慣性（inertia）是物體抵抗速度改變的性質，重力是地球引力。"},{"id":"q1599","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Eighty-five to ninety percent of all intervertebral disk herniations occur at what two locations?","options":["T4-T5 and T5-L1","L4-L5 and L5-S1","T5-L1 and S1-S2","S1-S2 and L3-L4"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"L4-L5 and L5-S1","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"約85%–90%的椎間盤突出發生在L4-L5與L5-S1，此兩節承受最大軸向與剪下負荷、活動度也最高。"},{"id":"q1600","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"An athlete produced 840 watts of power in 0.6 seconds. How much work did this individual perform during the exercise?","options":["1400 kJ","504 kJ","1400 J","504 J"],"answer":3,"answer_text":"504 J","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"功＝功率×時間＝840 W×0.6 s＝504焦耳（J）。功率×時間單位為焦耳而非千焦。"},{"id":"q1601","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the muscles or muscle groups have a fusiform pennation?","options":["deltoid","biceps brachii","rectus femoris","tibialis posterior"],"answer":1,"answer_text":"biceps brachii","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"梭形（fusiform）肌纖維排列的例子是肱二頭肌（biceps brachii）；三角肌為多羽狀，股直肌為單羽狀，脛骨後肌為多羽狀/羽狀排列。"},{"id":"q1602","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Which of the following is the definition of power?","options":["(mass) x (acceleration)","(force) x (distance)","(force) x (velocity)","(torque) x (time)"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"(force) x (velocity)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"功率＝力×速度（power = force × velocity）。力×距離是功（work），力×加速度不是標準定義，力矩×時間是衝量概念。"},{"id":"q1603","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"During a free weight exercise, muscle force varies with which of the following?\nI. perpendicular distance from the weight to the body joint.\nII. joint angle\nIII. movement acceleration\nIV. movement velocity squared","options":["I and III only","II and IV only","I, II, and III only","II, III, and IV only"],"answer":0,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"自由重量動作中，肌肉所需出力隨（I）重量到關節的垂直距離（力臂）與（III）動作的加速度（F＝ma，加速負荷需額外力量）而變； joint angle的影響已透過力臂呈現，速度平方不是決定式。"},{"id":"q1604","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"An athlete is performing a concentric isokinetic elbow flexion and extension exercise. Which of the following type(s) of levers occur(s) at the elbow during this exercise?\nI. first class\nII. second class\nIII. third class","options":["I only","II only","I and III only","II and III only"],"answer":2,"answer_text":"I and III only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肘關節在彎舉（屈曲）時是第三類槓桿（力點在支點與阻力之間）；在肘伸展（如三頭肌動作）時成為第一類槓桿（支點在中間），故此動作同時出現第一類與第三類槓桿，第二類槓桿（阻力在中間）不出現。"},{"id":"q1605","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bioenergetics","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the flow of energy in a biological system; the conversion of macronutrients into biological forms of energy","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"生物能量學（Bioenergetics）研究生物體系內的能量流動，即把巨量營養素轉換成生物可利用能量（如 ATP）的過程。"},{"id":"q1606","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Catabolism","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the breakdown of large molecules into smaller molecules, associated with the release of energy","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"分解代謝（Catabolism）把大分子分解為小分子並釋放能量，例如肝醣與脂肪的分解，釋放的能量供合成代謝使用。"},{"id":"q1607","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anabolism","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the synthesis of larger molecules from smaller molecules; can be accomplished using the energy from catabolic reactions","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"合成代謝（Anabolism）利用能量把小分子合成大分子（如蛋白質合成），所需能量來自分解代謝（放能反應）的產出。"},{"id":"q1608","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Exergonic reactions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"energy-releasing reactions that are generally catabolic","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"放能反應（Exergonic）釋放能量，多屬分解代謝性質。"},{"id":"q1609","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endergonic reaction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"require energy and include anabolic processes and the contraction of muscle","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"吸能反應（Endergonic）需要輸入能量，包括合成代謝過程與肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q1610","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Metabolism","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the total of all the catabolic (exergonic) and anabolic (endergonic) reactions in a biological system","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"代謝（Metabolism）是生物體內所有分解（放能）與合成（吸能）反應的總和。"},{"id":"q1611","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Adensosine triphosphate (ATP)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"allows the transfer of energy from exergonic to endergonic reactions","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"三磷酸腺苷（ATP）是能量的直接載體，負責把能量從放能反應轉移到吸能反應。"},{"id":"q1612","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hydrolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the breakdown of 1 ATP molecule to yield energy (because it requires 1 H2O)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"水解（Hydrolysis）指 1 個 ATP 與 1 分子水作用分解為 ADP 與無機磷酸並釋放能量。"},{"id":"q1613","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anaerobic processes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"do not require the presence of oxygen; the phosphagen and glycolytic systems are anaerobic mechanisms that occur in the sarcoplasm of a muscle cell","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"無氧代謝不需要氧氣參與；磷酸肌酸系統（phosphagen）與糖解系統皆為無氧途徑，發生在肌細胞的肌漿（sarcoplasm）中。"},{"id":"q1614","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic processes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"depend on oxygen; the krebs cycle, electron transport chain, and the remainder of the oxidative system are aerobic mechanisms that occur in the mitochondria of muscles cells and require oxygen as the terminal electron acceptor","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"有氧代謝依賴氧氣；克雷伯氏迴圈（Krebs cycle）、電子傳遞鏈及氧化系統其餘部分發生線上粒體（mitochondria），並需氧氣作為最終電子接受者。"},{"id":"q1615","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Of the three main macronutrients, which can be metabolized for energy without the direct involvement of oxygen?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Carbohydrates","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"答案是碳水化合物。碳水可經無氧糖解直接產 ATP，無需氧氣直接參與；脂肪與蛋白質則主要需氧。"},{"id":"q1616","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The magnitude of the contribution of each energy system to overall work performance is primarily dependent on the _______________ and secondarily on the ______________.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"intensity of the activity; duration","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"各能量系統對整體運動表現的貢獻程度，主要取決於運動強度，其次取決於運動持續時間。"},{"id":"q1617","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolosis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the breakdown of carbohydrates, either glycogen stored in the muscle or glucose delivered in the blood, to resynthesize ATP, still anaerobic, without the presence of oxygen (30 seconds to 2 minutes)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"糖解（Glycolysis）分解肌肉儲存的肝醣或血糖以再合成 ATP，屬無氧途徑不需氧氣，主要支撐約 30 秒到 2 分鐘的高強度運動。"},{"id":"q1618","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"pyruvate is the","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"end result of glycolysis","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸（pyruvate）是糖解的最終產物。"},{"id":"q1619","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After pyruvate is made, it can then do one of two things:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"be converted to lactate in the sarcoplasm (fast glycolysis)\nbe shuttled into the mitochondria (slow glycolysis)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸有兩條去路：在肌漿中轉換成乳酸（快速糖解），或被輸送入線粒體進行氧化代謝（慢速糖解）。"},{"id":"q1620","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"fast glycolysis (anaerobic)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pyruvate is converted into lactate, which is faster but limited in duration","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"快速糖解屬無氧：丙酮酸轉換為乳酸，ATP 產生較快但持續時間有限。"},{"id":"q1621","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"slow glycolysis (aerobic)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when pyruvate is shuttled into the mitochondria to undergo the Kreb's cycle, the process is slower but can undergo a longer duration","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"慢速糖解屬有氧：丙酮酸進入線粒體進行克雷伯氏迴圈，產能較慢但可維持較長時間。"},{"id":"q1622","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F Lactate is the cause of fatigue","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"False","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"錯誤。乳酸本身不是疲勞的直接成因，它仍可被氧化作為燃料；疲勞與 H+、無機磷酸堆積等因素更相關。"},{"id":"q1623","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"There are two primary mechanisms for resynthesizing ATP during metabolism:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. substrate-level phosphorylation\n2. oxidative phosphorylation","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"ATP 再合成的兩種主要機制：受質層級磷酸化（substrate-level phosphorylation）與氧化磷酸化（oxidative phosphorylation）。"},{"id":"q1624","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"phosphorylation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the process of adding an inorganic phosphate to another molecule","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"磷酸化是把無機磷酸（Pi）加到另一個分子上的過程。"},{"id":"q1625","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"oxidative phosphorylation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the resynthesis of ATP in the electron transport chain","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"氧化磷酸化指在電子傳遞鏈進行的 ATP 再合成，需要氧氣參與。"},{"id":"q1626","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"substrate-level phosphorylation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the direct resynthesis of ATP from ADP during a single reaction in the metabolic pathways","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"受質層級磷酸化指在代謝途徑的單一反應中，受質的磷酸基直接轉給 ADP 再合成 ATP。"},{"id":"q1627","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"gross ATP for oxidative phosphorylation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"24-28","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"依本題庫，氧化磷酸化的 ATP 總產量為 24-28；它是氧化系統的主要 ATP 來源，產量在各途徑中最高。"},{"id":"q1628","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolysis is stimulated by","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high concentrations of ADP and ammonia (increases) and a slight decrease in pH and AMP","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"糖解受高濃度 ADP 與氨促進，pH 些微下降與 AMP 上升也會加速糖解。"},{"id":"q1629","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolysis is inhibited by","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"markedly lower pH, ATP, CP, citrate, and free fatty acids","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"糖解受明顯下降的 pH、高濃度 ATP、磷酸肌酸（CP）、檸檬酸與遊離脂肪酸抑制。"},{"id":"q1630","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"lactate threshold","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The exercise intensity or relative intensity at which blood lactate begins an abrupt increase above the baseline concentration.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"乳酸閾值（lactate threshold）指運動強度達到某程度時，血乳酸開始偏離基線濃度急劇上升。"},{"id":"q1631","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"lactate threshold begins at","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"50-60% of maximal oxygen uptake in untrained individuals\n70-80% in aerobically trained athletes","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"未受訓者乳酸閾值約出現在最大攝氧量（VO2max）的 50-60%；有氧受訓運動員可延後至 70-80%。"},{"id":"q1632","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Onset of blood lactate accumulation (OBLA)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a second increase in the rate of lactate accumulation, occurring at higher relative intensities of exercise when the concentration of blood lactate reaches 4 mmol/L","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"血乳酸堆積起始點（OBLA）指血乳酸濃度達 4 mmol/L 時，在較高相對強度出現的第二個乳酸堆積加速點。"},{"id":"q1633","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The oxidative (aerobic) system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Primary source of ATP at rest and during low-intensity activities\nUses primarily carbohydrates and fats as substrates\nlargest energy yield","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"氧化（有氧）系統是靜息與低強度運動時的主要 ATP 來源，主要以碳水與脂肪為受質，能量產量最大。"},{"id":"q1634","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"fat oxidation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Triglycerides stored in fat cells can be broken down by hormone-sensitive lipase. This releases free fatty acids from the fat cells into the blood, where they can circulate and enter muscle fibers.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"脂肪氧化：脂肪細胞內的三酸甘油酯被脂肪敏感脂酶分解，釋出遊離脂肪酸進入血液迴圈，再進入肌纖維供氧化使用。"},{"id":"q1635","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein oxidation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Protein is not a significant source of energy for most activities.\nProtein is broken down into amino acids, and the amino acids are converted into glucose, pyruvate, or various Krebs cycle intermediates to produce ATP.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"蛋白質氧化：蛋白質對多數活動不是重要能量來源；它先分解為胺基酸，再轉為葡萄糖、丙酮酸或克雷伯氏迴圈中間物以產 ATP。"},{"id":"q1636","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"There is a(n) ________________ relationship between a given energy system's maximum rate of ATP production and the total amount of ATP capable of producing over time.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inverse","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"反比（inverse）關係。能量系統產 ATP 的速率越快，單位時間能產出的 ATP 總量越少；速率越慢，總產量越高。"},{"id":"q1637","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The extent to which each of the three energy systems contributes to ATP production depends primarily on the _______________ of the muscular activity and secondarily on the _______________.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"intensity, duration","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"三個能量系統各自的貢獻程度主要取決於肌肉活動的強度，其次取決於持續時間。"},{"id":"q1638","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F\nAt no time, during either exercise or rest, does any single energy system provide the complete supply of energy","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"True","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"正確。無論運動或休息，沒有任何單一能量系統能獨立提供全部能量，三系統始終共同分擔。"},{"id":"q1639","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Fatigue during exercise appears to be at least partially related to the decrease in _______________","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"phosphagens","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動疲勞至少部分與磷酸肌酸類（phosphagen，ATP 與 CP）濃度下降有關。"},{"id":"q1640","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"______________ _______________ can decrease markedly (50-70%) during the first \"stage\" or 5-30 seconds of high-intensity exercise and can be almost eliminated as a result of very intense exercise to exhaustion.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Creatine phosphate","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸（CP）在高強度運動最初 5-30 秒內可下降 50-70%，極高強度運動至力竭時幾乎可被耗盡。"},{"id":"q1641","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Complete resynthesis of ATP appears to occur within _____ minutes and complete creatine phosphate resynthesis can occur within ___ minutes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3-5 minutes, 8 minutes","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"ATP 完全再合成約在 3-5 分鐘內完成；磷酸肌酸完全再合成可長達約 8 分鐘。"},{"id":"q1642","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As relative intensities of exercise above _______ of maximal oxygen uptake, muscle glycogen becomes and increasingly important energy substrate.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"60%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"當運動強度超過約 60% VO2max，肌肉肝醣成為愈形重要的能量受質。"},{"id":"q1643","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"EPOC","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"(excess post-exercise oxygen consumption) oxygen uptake above resting values used to restore the body to pre exercise condition\naka: post-exercise oxygen uptake, oxygen uptake, oxygen debt, or recovery O2","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動後過量耗氧（EPOC）指運動後高於靜息的額外氧攝取，用於把身體恢復到運動前狀態，又稱恢復耗氧或氧債。"},{"id":"q1644","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"VO2","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"oxygen consumption","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"VO2 即攝氧量（oxygen consumption）。"},{"id":"q1645","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"interval training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"emphasizes bioenergetic adaptations for a more efficient energy transfer within the metabolic pathways by using predetermined intervals of exercise and rest periods","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"間歇訓練（interval training）以預設的運動與休息區間，促進生物能量適應，讓代謝途徑的能量轉移更有效率。"},{"id":"q1646","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"puberty","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"refers to a period of time in which secondary sex characteristics develop and a child is transformed into a young adult","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"青春期（puberty）指第二性徵發育、兒童逐漸轉化為成人的時期。"},{"id":"q1647","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"during puberty changes occur related to","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body composition and the performance of physical skills","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"青春期會帶來身體組成與運動技能表現相關的明顯變化。"},{"id":"q1648","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the difference between biological age and chronological age","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"chronological age refers to age by years while biological age refers to developmental age","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"實際年齡（chronological age）以出生年數計算；生物年齡（biological age）指個體的發育階段。"},{"id":"q1649","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in children, muscle mass steadily _______________ throughout developing years","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increases","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童在生長髮育期間肌肉量穩定增加。"},{"id":"q1650","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During puberty, increased ________________ production in boys resulting in a marked increase in muscle mass, whereas in girls, an increase in __________________ production causes increased body fat deposition, breast development, and a widening of the hips.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"testosterone, estrogen","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"青春期男性睪固酮分泌增加，使肌肉量明顯增加；女性雌激素分泌增加，促進脂肪堆積、乳房發育與骨盆變寬。"},{"id":"q1651","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When do long bones stop growing?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when the epiphyseal plate becomes completely ossified","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"長骨在骨骺板（epiphyseal plate）完全骨化閉合後停止生長。"},{"id":"q1652","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Where is growth cartilage in children located?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"epiphyseal plate, joint surface, and apophyseal insertions","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童的生長軟骨位於三處：骨骺板、關節面與骨突附著處（apophyseal insertions）。"},{"id":"q1653","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Damage to what may impair the growth and development of affected bone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the growth cartilage","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"生長軟骨受損可能妨礙該骨骼的生長與發育。"},{"id":"q1654","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Risk of damaging growth cartilage can be reduced with:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"appropriate exercise training, sensible progression, and instruction by qualified strength and conditioning professionals","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"適當的運動訓練、合理的進度安排與合格肌力與訓練專業人員的指導，可降低生長軟骨受傷風險。"},{"id":"q1655","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when do peak strength gains occur in boys?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"about 1.2 years after peak height velocity and .8 years after peak weight velocity","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"男生的肌力巔峰成長大約出現在尖峰身高速率（PHV）後約 1.2 年、尖峰體重速率後約 0.8 年。"},{"id":"q1656","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when do peak strength gains occur in girls?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"typically occurs after peak height velocity, more individual variation in relationship between strength and height and body weight","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"女生的肌力巔峰成長通常出現在尖峰身高速率之後，但肌力與身高、體重的時間關係個別差異較大。"},{"id":"q1657","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"On average, peak strength is usually attained by age ____ in untrained women and between the ages of ____ and ____ in untrained men","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"20, 20-30","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"未受訓女性平均約在 20 歲達最大肌力；未受訓男性約在 20 到 30 歲之間。"},{"id":"q1658","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"strength gains of roughly ______ to _____ are typically observed in untrained preadolescent children following short-term (8-20 weeks) resistance programs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30-40%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"未受訓的青春期前兒童經短期（8-20 週）抗阻訓練，通常可獲得約 30-40% 的肌力成長。"},{"id":"q1659","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is primarily responsible for the significant improvements in strength with resistance training in children?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"neurological factors","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童抗阻訓練的肌力進步主要來自神經因素（運動單位動員與放電頻率改善），而非肌肉肥大。"},{"id":"q1660","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"motor unit","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"nerve with several muscle fibers it innervates, recruiting more muscle unit development correlates to more muscles being stimulated and becoming stronger","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動單位（motor unit）是一個運動神經元及其支配的所有肌纖維；動員更多運動單位代表刺激與收縮更多肌纖維。"},{"id":"q1661","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"rate coding","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the same motor unit has more impulses sent (faster stimulus, more force productions)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"放電頻率調控（rate coding）指同一運動單位以更高頻率被激發，神經衝動越快，產生的力量越大。"},{"id":"q1662","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Factors that contribute to the development of muscular strength in children/adolescents:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fat-free mass, testosterone concentrations, nervous system development, and the differentiation of fast-twitch and slow-twitch muscle fibers","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童青少年肌力發展的影響因素：去脂體重、睪固酮濃度、神經系統發育，以及快肌與慢肌纖維的分化。"},{"id":"q1663","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"early myelination development leads to","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"improved coordination and response to stimuli","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"早期髓鞘化（myelination）發展良好，能帶來更好的協調性與對刺激的反應能力。"},{"id":"q1664","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"potential benefits of resistance training in children include:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"health and fitness benefits\ndeveloping healthy habits and patterns to carry later in life such as staying active\ndeveloping stronger bones\nmore movement reduces the risk of diabetes and improves cardiovascular health","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童抗阻訓練的潛在益處：健康與體適能效益、養成終身活動習慣、強化骨骼，較多活動也降低糖尿病風險並改善心血管健康。"},{"id":"q1665","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"training (long term athlete model)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"teaching to play, having fun.\nthen moving into a more formalized approach, learning movement patterns and proficiency.\nthen moving into training to compete and training to win (high school, college, and elite athletes)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"長期運動員發展模型（LTAD）：先以遊戲化學習、玩得開心為主，再進入系統化學習動作模式與動作能力，最後才是為競技而練、為致勝而練（高中、大學、精英階段）。"},{"id":"q1666","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"potential risks and concerns of resistance training in children:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"appropriately prescribed youth resistance programs are relatively safe.\nEnsure that risks are minimized and movements are being performed correctly and safely.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"適度處方的青少年抗阻訓練相當安全；重點是把風險降到最低，並確認動作做得正確、安全。"},{"id":"q1667","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"program design considerations for children","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"consider quality of instruction and rate of progression, focus on skill improvement, personal successes, and having fun","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"兒童課程設計要考慮指導品質與進度快慢，著重技能進步、個人成就感與樂趣。"},{"id":"q1668","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How can we reduce the risk of overuse injuries in youth?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. before sport participation, young athletes should be evaluated by a sports medicine physician\n2. parents should be educated about the benefits and risks of competitive sports\n3. parents should understand the importance of preparatory conditioning\n4. children and adolescents should be encouraged to participate in year-round physical activity\n5. youth coaches should implement well-planned recovery strategies\n6. the nutritional status of youth athletes should be monitored\n7. youth sports coaches should participate in educational programs\n8. boys and girls should be encouraged to participate in a variety of sports and activities","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"降低 青少年過度使用傷害：參賽前先經運動醫藥醫師評估；讓家長瞭解競技運動的利弊與賽前體能準備的重要性；鼓勵兒童參與多樣化運動、避免過早專項化。"},{"id":"q1669","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Youth Resistance Training Guidelines","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- static stretching exercises should be performed after resistance training.\n- carefully monitor each child's tolerance to the exercise stress.\n- begin with light loads\n- increase the resistance gradually (e.g., 5% to 10% os strength improves)\n- depending on needs and goals, one to three sets of 6 to 15 reps on a variety of exercises can be performed.\n- advanced multipoint exercises may be incorporated into the program if appropriate loads are used and the focus remains on proper from.\n- 2 or 3 nonconsecutive training sessions per week are recommended\n- adult spotters should be nearby to actively assist the child.\n- the resistance training program should be systematically carried throughout the year","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"青少年抗阻訓練指引：靜態伸展應安排在抗阻訓練之後；逐一監測兒童對訓練壓力的耐受度；從輕負荷開始，隨肌力提升逐步增加阻力（如 5-10%）；依目標安排 1-3 組、每組約 6-15 下。"},{"id":"q1670","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F before puberty, there are essentially no differences in height, weight, and body size between boys and girls.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"正確。青春期前男女在身高、體重與體型上大致沒有差異。"},{"id":"q1671","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F adult women tend to have more body fat and less muscle and bone than adult males","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"正確。成年女性的體脂肪率高於男性，肌肉量與骨量則較少。"},{"id":"q1672","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F Women tend to be heavier in total body weight than men","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"false","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"錯誤。男性平均總體重大於女性。"},{"id":"q1673","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In terms of absolute strength, women generally have ____ the strength of men","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2/3","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"絕對肌力方面，女性約為男性的 2/3（上肢更低，下肢差距較小）。"},{"id":"q1674","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"absolute strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"how much weight you can overcome","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"絕對肌力指不考慮體重下能克服的最大重量或能表現的最大力量。"},{"id":"q1675","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"relative strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Amount of force that one can exert in relation to one's body weight or per unit of muscle cross section. (dependent on gender and height and weight, etc)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"相對肌力是依個人體重或每單位肌肉橫斷面積計算所能產生的力量，受性別、身高、體重等影響。"},{"id":"q1676","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"female athlete triad","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A legacy concept (replaced by RED-S in the 5th edition) of three interrelated disorders: low energy availability with disordered eating (including excessive exercising), menstrual dysfunction (amenorrhea) and decreased bone density. RED-S broadens this: low energy availability also affects metabolic rate, immunity, protein synthesis and cardiovascular function, and occurs in males as well as females","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"女運動員三聯症（female athlete triad）：能量可用性不足（飲食失調、含過度運動）、月經功能失調（停經）與骨密度下降三種互相關聯的失調。5e 已改以「運動相對能量不足」（RED-S）取代此舊稱（第24章 p1693）：低能量可用性（攝取低於消耗）除月經與骨健康外，還影響代謝率、免疫、蛋白質合成與心血管功能，男性選手也可能發生（第11章 p650）。"},{"id":"q1677","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What could lead to the female athlete triad?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high training volumes or intensities with inadequate dietary intake","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"高訓練量或高訓練強度搭配飲食攝取不足，可能引發女運動員三色症候群。"},{"id":"q1678","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When designing resistance training programs for women, what program considerations should be made?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"rate of upper body strength development (women tend to have less upper body strength than men)\nACL injury","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"為女性設計抗阻訓練時，應考慮上半身肌力發展速率（女性上半身肌力基礎較低）與前十字韌帶（ACL）受傷風險。"},{"id":"q1679","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are contributing factors to an ACL injury?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"joint laxity, ligament size, and neuromuscular deficiency leading to abnormal biomechanics","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"關節鬆動度、韌帶尺寸與神經肌肉功能缺陷造成的異常生物力學，都是 ACL 受傷的促進因素。"},{"id":"q1680","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"osteopnea","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a bone mineral density between -1 and -2.5 standard deviations of the young adult mean","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"骨質缺乏（osteopenia）指骨密度低於年輕成人平均值 1 到 2.5 個標準差之間。"},{"id":"q1681","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Osteoporosis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a bone mineral density below -2.5 standard deviations of the young adult mean","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"骨質疏鬆症（osteoporosis）指骨密度低於年輕成人平均值 2.5 個標準差以上。"},{"id":"q1682","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which type of loading is optimal to promote good bone health in older adults?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"axial loading","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"軸向負荷（axial loading，沿骨骼長軸的荷重，如深蹲）最有助於年長者維持與促進骨骼健康。"},{"id":"q1683","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bone mineral density can be improved with:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a progressive resistance training program","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"漸進式抗阻訓練計畫可以改善骨密度。"},{"id":"q1684","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After age ___, there is a decrease in the cross-sectional areas of individual muscles, along with a decrease in muscle density and an increase in intramuscular fat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"30 歲之後，單一肌肉的橫斷面積與肌肉密度下降，肌肉內脂肪增加。"},{"id":"q1685","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Advancing age is associated with","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Loss of muscle mass, which is largely attributable to physical inactivity, a direct result of the reduction in muscle mass is a loss of muscular strength and power","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"年齡增長伴隨肌肉量流失（主要源於身體不活動），肌肉量減少直接導致肌力與肌功率下降。"},{"id":"q1686","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Seniors are at a higher risk of","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"falling","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"老年人跌倒風險較高。"},{"id":"q1687","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why do seniors have a higher risk of falling?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decrease in muscular strength and power, decreased reaction time, and impaired balance and postural stability","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌力與肌功率下降、反應時間變慢、平衡與姿勢穩定度受損，使老年人更易跌倒。"},{"id":"q1688","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcopenia","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the degeneration of muscle inside the body, more fat deposits in and around the muscle.\nless force is being produced by less muscle.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌少症（sarcopenia）指隨老化發生的肌肉退化，肌肉內與周圍脂肪堆積增加，較少的肌肉產生較少的力量。"},{"id":"q1689","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T/F Older adults are still able to produce a similar amount of relative strength gains as younger adults","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"正確。年長者經抗阻訓練仍能獲得與年輕人不相上下的相對肌力成長。"},{"id":"q1690","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Seniors who participate in progressive resistance training programs show significant improvements in","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscular strength and power, muscle mass, bone mineral density, and functional capabilities","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"參與漸進式抗阻訓練的長者，其肌力與肌功率、肌肉量、骨密度與功能效能力都有顯著改善。"},{"id":"q1691","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Strength recommendations for older adults","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 set of 8-12 reps at 40-50% 1RM\nprogress to 3 sets of 8-12 reps at 60-80% 1RM","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"年長者肌力建議：從 40-50% 1RM 做 1 組 8-12 下開始，進階到 60-80% 1RM 做 3 組 8-12 下。"},{"id":"q1692","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Power recommendations for older adults","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1-3 sets of 6-10 reps at 40-50% 1R<, with high repetition velocity","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"年長者肌功率建議：1-3 組、每組 6-10 下、強度約 40-50% 1RM，並搭配高動作品速（盡量快的重複速度）。"},{"id":"q1693","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the safety recommendations for resistance training for seniors?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"all participants should be pre-screened\nwarm up for 5 to 10 minutes before each exercise session\nperform static stretching before or after, or both, each resistance training session\nuse a resistance that does not overtax the musculoskeletal system\navoid the Valsalva\nallow 48-72 hours of recovery between sessions\nperform all exercises in a pain free ROM","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"長者訓練安全建議：全員先接受篩檢；每次訓練前熱身 5-10 分鐘；訓練前或後（或兩者皆然）做靜態伸展；選擇不會過度負荷肌肉骨骼系統的阻力；避免 Valsalva 閉氣用力；每次訓練間留 48-72 小時恢復。"},{"id":"q1694","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the three goals of sport psychology?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Measuring psychological phenomena,\ninvestigating the relationships between psychological variables and performance,\nand applying theoretical knowledge to improve athletic performance.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動心理學三大目標：測量心理現象、探討心理變項與運動表現的關係、應用理論知識以改善運動表現。"},{"id":"q1695","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The ideal performance state involves the following:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"absence of fear (no fear of failure)\nno thinking about or analysis of performance\na narrow focus of attention on the activity itself\na sense of effortlessness\na sense of personal control","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"理想表現狀態包括：沒有恐懼（不怕失敗）、不去分析自己的表現、注意力狹窄地聚焦在動作本身、覺得毫不費力、有掌控感。"},{"id":"q1696","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Arousal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a blend of physiological and psychological activation, varying in intensity along a continuum (refers to the intensity of motivation at any given moment)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"喚起（arousal）是生理與心理啟用的混合狀態，強度沿連續量表變化，指當下動機強度。"},{"id":"q1697","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a subcategory of arousal that is a negatively perceived emotional state","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"焦慮（anxiety）是喚起的一個次類別，屬負面知覺的情緒狀態。"},{"id":"q1698","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"cognitive anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the cognitive component of anxiety","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"認知焦慮是焦慮的認知成分，如擔憂與負面預期。"},{"id":"q1699","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"somatic anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the physical reaction component of anxiety","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"生理焦慮是焦慮的身體反應成分，如心跳加快、緊張。"},{"id":"q1700","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"state anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the actual experience of apprehension and uncontrolled arousal","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"狀態焦慮指當下實際經歷的不安與失控的喚起經驗。"},{"id":"q1701","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"trait anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"is a personality characteristic, which represents a latent disposition to perceive situations as threatening.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"特質焦慮是一種人格特徵，代表把情境知覺為威脅的潛在傾向。"},{"id":"q1702","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"stress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a substantial imbalance between demands and response capabilities, under conditions in which failure has important consequences","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:976885133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"壓力指需求與應對能力之間出現大幅失衡、且失敗會帶來重要後果的狀態。"},{"id":"q1703","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following substances regulates muscle actions?\nPotassium\nCalcium\ntroponin\ntropomyosin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Calcium","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"答案是鈣。鈣離子與肌鈣蛋白結合後使原肌球蛋白位移、暴露結合位，從而調節肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q1704","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following substances acts at the neuromuscular junction to excite the muscle fibers of a motor unit?\nacetylcholine\nATP\ncreatine phosphate\nserotonin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"acetylcholine","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"乙醯膽鹼（acetylcholine）在神經肌肉接合處釋放，激發該運動單位的肌纖維。"},{"id":"q1705","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When throwing a baseball, an athlete's arm is rapidly stretched just before throwing the ball. Which of the following structures detects and responds to that stretch by reflexively increasing muscle activity?\nGolgi tendon organ\nMuscle spindle\nextrafusal muscle\npacinian corpuscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle spindle","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌梭（muscle spindle）能偵測投擲前手臂的快速伸展，並反射性地提高肌肉活動。"},{"id":"q1706","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"From which of the following is the heart's electrical impulse normally initiated?\nAV node\nSA node\nthe brain\nthe sympathetic nervous system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"SA node","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"心臟電衝動正常由竇房結（SA node）起始。"},{"id":"q1707","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following occurs during the QRS complex of a typical ECG?\n1 depolarization of the atrium\n2 repolarlization of the atrium\n3 repolarization of the ventricle\n4 depolarization of the ventricle\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 & 4 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"QRS 波群代表心室去極化，同時遮蔽了心房再極化（2 與 4）；心房去極化是 P 波，心室再極化是 T 波。"},{"id":"q1708","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the definition of power?\nmass x acceleration\nforce x distance\nforce x velocity\ntorque x time","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"force x velocity\n(velocity is distance/time)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"功率的定義是力乘以速度（force x velocity）；因速度等於距離除以時間，功率亦可理解為單位時間做的功。"},{"id":"q1709","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"To compare performances of Olympic weightlifters of different body weights, the classic formula divides the load lifted by the athlete's\nbody weight\nbody weight squared\nlean body weight\nbody weight to the two-thirds power","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body weight to the two-thirds power","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"傳統公式把舉起的重量除以體重的 2/3 次冪（allometric scaling），以便比較不同體重的舉重選手。"},{"id":"q1710","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a free weight exercise, muscle force varies with which of the following?\n1 perpendicular distance from the weight to the body joint\n2 joint angle\n3 movement acceleration\n4 movement velocity squared\n1 & 2 only\n1 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 2 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"自由重量運動中，肌力隨重量到關節的垂直距離（力臂）與關節角度而變化（1 與 2）；不含速度平方項。"},{"id":"q1711","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A verticle jump involves knee, hip, and shoulder movement primarily in which anatomical plane?\nsagittal\nperpendicular\nfrontal\ntransverse","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sagittal","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"垂直跳的膝、髖、肩動作主要發生在矢狀面（sagittal plane）。"},{"id":"q1712","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is performing a concentric isokinetic elbow flexion and extension exercise. Which of the following type(s) of levers occur(s) at the elbow during this exercise?\n1 first class.\n2 second class.\n3 third class.\n1 only\n2 only\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 3 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肘關節屈伸同時出現第一類槓桿（三頭肌伸肘）與第三類槓桿（屈肘），即 1 與 3；肘部不會出現第二類槓桿。"},{"id":"q1713","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following substances can be metabolized anaerobically?\nglycerol\nglucose\namino acids\nfree fatty acids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glucose","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"葡萄糖可進行無氧代謝；甘油、胺基酸與遊離脂肪酸主要需進入有氧途徑代謝。"},{"id":"q1714","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following reactions is the primary cause of metabolic acidosis (the decrease in intramuscular pH during high-intensity, fatiguing exercise)\nATP -> ADP + P + H+\npyruvate + NADH -> Lactate + NAD+\nADP + creatine phosphate -> ATP + Creatine\nfructose-6-phosphate -> fructose-1, 6-biphosphate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ATP -> ADP + P + H+","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"ATP 水解為 ADP + Pi + H+ 是高強度疲勞性運動時肌肉內 pH 下降（代謝性酸中毒）的主要原因。"},{"id":"q1715","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following energy systems produces ATP at the quickest rate?\nphosphagen\naerobic glycolysis\nfat oxidation\nfast glycolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"phosphagen","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸系統（phosphagen）以最快的速率產出 ATP。"},{"id":"q1716","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Approximately how many net ATP are produced via the oxidative energy system from the metabolism of one glucose molecule?\n27\n34\n38\n41","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"38","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"由 1 分子葡萄糖經氧化系統代謝約淨產 38 個 ATP（本題庫採用的傳統數值）。"},{"id":"q1717","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following energy substrates cannot be depleted during extreme exercise intensities or durations?\ncreatine phosphate\nglycogen\nwater\nATP","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ATP","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"ATP。即使極端強度或時間下，體內 ATP 濃度仍維持一定水準；真正會被耗盡的是 CP、肝醣等。"},{"id":"q1718","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After a bout of resistance training, acute hormonal secretions provide all of the following information to the body EXCEPT\namount of physiological stress\nmetabolic demands of exercise\ntype of physiological stress\nenergy expended","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"energy expended","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"急性激素分泌提供生理壓力量、壓力型別與代謝需求等資訊，但不包括能量消耗量。"},{"id":"q1719","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following hormones enhance(s) muscle tissue growth?\n1 growth hormone\n2 cortisol\n3 IGF-1\n4 progesterone\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 3 only\n(growth hormone & IGF-1)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"生長激素與 IGF-1 促進肌肉組織生長（1 與 3）；皮質醇偏分解性，黃體素不是主要合成激素。"},{"id":"q1720","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a function of growth hormone?\nincrease lipolysis\ndecrease collagen synthesis\nincrease amino acid transport\ndecrease glucose utilization","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decrease collagen synthesis","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"生長激素會增加（而非減少）膠原蛋白合成；促進脂解、增加胺基酸運輸、減少葡萄糖利用皆是其功能。"},{"id":"q1721","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following hormones has the greatest influence on neural changes?\ngrowth hormone\ntestosterone\ncortisol\nIGF","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"testosterone","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"睪固酮對神經變化的影響最大。"},{"id":"q1722","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What type of resistance training workout promotes the highest growth hormone increases following the exercise session?\n3 sets @ high volume w/ 30s rest\n1 set @ low volume w/30s rest\n1 set @ high volume w/3 minutes rest\n3 sets @ low volume w/3 minutes rest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3 sets @ high volume w/30s rest","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"高容量、短休息（約 30 秒）的多組訓練（3 組高容量、休息 30 秒）會帶來運動後最高的生長激素反應。"},{"id":"q1723","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Following resistance training, augmented neural drive to the working musculature is the result of?\n1 increased agonist muscle recruitment\n2 muscle hypertrophy\n3 improved firing rate\n4 greater synchronization\nAll of the above\n1 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n1, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 3, & 4 only\n(increased agonist muscle recruitment, improved firing rate, & greater synchronization)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"訓練後神經驅動增強來自主動肌動員增加、放電頻率改善與動作同步化提高（1、3、4）；肌肉肥大屬結構適應，不是神經變化。"},{"id":"q1724","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When one is performing a box-to-box plyometric drop jump, in order to generate sufficient force in a limited amount of time (<200 ms), which muscle fibers are bypassed through the principle of selective recruitment?\ntype I\ntype IIa\ntype IIx\ntype IIc","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type 1","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"依選擇性動員（反轉大小原則），在不到 200 ms 內產生足夠力量時會跳過第一型（type I）慢肌纖維，直接動員高閾值運動單位。"},{"id":"q1725","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following performance or physiological characteristics is NOT usually observed in a state of nonfunctional overreaching (NFOR) within athlete populations?\nstagnation and a decrease in performance\nhormonal disturbances\nsleep disturbances\nincreased levels of fatigue","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sleep disturbances","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"睡眠障礙較典型出現在過度訓練症候群（OTS）；非功能性過度訓練（NFOR）的特徵是表現停滯或下降、內分泌失調與疲勞上升。"},{"id":"q1726","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Following prolonged periods of detraining in elite strength/power athletes, which of the following physical characteristics will likely show the largest reduction as a consequence of the removal of an anaerobic training stimulus?\ntotal fat mass\nfast-twitch fiber cross-sectional area\nslow-twitch fiber cross-sectional area\ntotal Type 1 muscle fiber content","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fast-twitch fiber cross-sectional area","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"精英力量/爆發力運動員停止訓練後，因移除無氧訓練刺激，-fast-twitch（快肌）纖維橫斷面積的下降幅度最大。"},{"id":"q1727","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Following a long period of chronic high-intensity resistance training, a variety of physiological adaptations take place in a number of systems within the body that promote improved athletic performance in strength/power activities. If an elite athlete were to undergo 12 weeks of heavy strength training, which of the following adaptations would NOT be expected consequent to this type of anaerobic exercise?\na transition from Type 2x to Type 2a muscle fibers\nincreased pennation angle in certain muscle groups\nreduced sarcoplasmic reticulum and T-tubule density\nelevated sodium-potassium ATPase activity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"reduced sarcoplasmic reticulum and T-tubule density","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"重負荷力量訓練後不預期出現肌漿網與 T 小管密度下降（實際預期為增加或維持）；type 2x 轉為 2a、羽狀角增加、鈉鉀 ATP 酶活性上升都是預期適應。"},{"id":"q1728","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In which of the following athletes might you expect limited bone mineral density (BMD) levels as a consequence of the force vectors and the physical demands associated with the given sport?\na 16-year-old gymnast with a 7 year training history in her sport\na 23-year-old offensive lineman who has lifted weights for 8 years\na 33-year-old track cyclist who has a 1RM squat of 352 lbs\na 19-year-old 800m freestyle swimmer with one year of dryland training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a 19-year-old 800m freestyle swimmer with one year of dryland training","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"游泳選手的動作缺乏軸向地面衝擊荷重，19 歲、僅一年陸上訓練的 800m 自由式選手最可能骨密度偏低；體操、鋒線球員與腳踏車選手的荷重刺激都較大。"},{"id":"q1729","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 17-year-old high school cross-country runner has been training aerobically for six months in preparation for the upcoming season. Which of the following adaptations will occur in the muscles during that time?\nincreased concentration of glycolytic enzymes\nhyperplasia of Type 2 fibers\ntransformation from Type 1 to Type 2 fibers\nhypertrophy of Type 1 fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hypertrophy of Type 1 fibers","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"六個月有氧訓練會造成第一型肌纖維肥大（hypertrophy of Type 1）；糖解酵素會下降，type I 也不會轉型為 type II。"},{"id":"q1730","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The amount of blood ejected from the left ventricle during each beat is the\ncardiac output\na-vO2 difference\nheart rate\nstroke volume","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"stroke volume","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"每次心跳左心室打出的血量是心搏量（stroke volume）；心率乘心搏量才是心輸出量。"},{"id":"q1731","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following does NOT normally increase during an aerobic exercise session?\nend-diastolic volume\ncardiac contractility\ncardiac output\ndiastolic blood pressure","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"diastolic blood pressure","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"有氧運動時舒張壓通常不會明顯上升（甚至略降）；末端舒張容積、心肌收縮力與心輸出量都會增加。"},{"id":"q1732","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The mean arterial pressure is defined as the\naverage blood pressure throughout the cardiac cycle\naverage of the systolic and diastolic blood pressures\naverage systolic blood pressure during exercise\naverage of blood pressure and heart rate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"average blood pressure throughout the cardiac cycle","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"平均動脈壓指整個心跳週期中血壓的平均值，非單純收縮壓與舒張壓的算術平均。"},{"id":"q1733","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Primary training adaptations of elite aerobically trained athletes include which of the following?\n1 increased maximal oxygen uptake\n2 decreased blood lactate concentration\n3 increased running economy\n4 decreased capillary density\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 2, & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"精英有氧選手的適應包括最大攝氧量提升、血乳酸濃度降低與跑步經濟性改善（1、2、3）；微血管密度應增加而非減少。"},{"id":"q1734","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An 8-year-old boy dramatically increased his upper body strength after following a six-month resistance training program. Which of the following is MOST likely responsible for this gain?\nincreased number of muscle fibers\nenhanced -cross-sectional area\ngreater muscle density\nimproved neuromuscular functioning","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"improved neuromuscular functioning","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"青春期前兒童的肌力成長最可能來自神經肌肉功能改善；肌纖維數量增加、橫斷面積增大與肌密度提升在此年齡不是主因。"},{"id":"q1735","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Growth cartilage in children is located at all of the following EXCEPT the\ndiaphysis\nepiphyseal plate\njoint surface\napophyseal insertion","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"diaphysis","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"骨幹（diaphysis）不是生長軟骨位置；生長軟骨位於骨骺板、關節面與骨突附著處。"},{"id":"q1736","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The condition characterized by a bone mineral density more than 2.5 SD below the young adult mean is called\nsarcopenia\nosteopenia\nosteoporosis\nscoliosis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"osteoporosis","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"骨密度低於年輕成人平均值 2.5 個標準差以上是骨質疏鬆症（osteoporosis）。"},{"id":"q1737","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following should be evaluated FIRST when one is designing a training program for a 68-year- old competitive female tennis player?\ncardiovascular fitness\nlower body strength\nbalance and agility\nmedical history","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"medical history","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"為 68 歲選手設計訓練計畫前，首先要評估病史（medical history）。"},{"id":"q1738","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Deconditioned female college athletes who participate in sports such as basketball and soccer appear to be at increased risk for developing injuries to the\nback\nknee\nwrist\nneck","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"knee","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"去訓練（deconditioned）的女性參加籃球、足球等運動時，膝關節（尤其 ACL）受傷風險提高。"},{"id":"q1739","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An Olympic weightlifter attempting a personal record is able to ignore the audience to concentrate solely on her performance. Which of the following abilities is this athlete most likely using to perform the exercise?\nselective attention\nsomatic anxiety\nguided discovery\nself-efficacy","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"selective attention","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"忽略觀眾、專注於表現是選擇性注意（selective attention）：聚焦相關線索、排除幹擾。"},{"id":"q1740","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete's desire to perform to his or her potential is an example of\nmotive to avoid failure\nautogenic training\nselective attention\nachievement motivation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"achievement motivation","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"想把表現發揮到潛能上限是成就動機（achievement motivation）的例子。"},{"id":"q1741","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For a high school American football team, if any player squats two times his body weight, his name is placed on the wall. This is an example of\nnegative reinforcement\npositive reinforcement\nnegative punishment\npositive punishment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"positive reinforcement","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"做到深蹲兩倍體重就把名字上牆，是在行為後呈現有利刺激以增加該行為頻率，屬正向增強（positive reinforcement）。"},{"id":"q1742","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does an athlete's optimal level of arousal change with limited skill and ability to perform the activity?\nIt increases\nIt decreases\nIt has no effect\nIt is not related to the activity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"It decreases","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"技能與能力不足時，最佳喚起水準下降；越不熟悉動作，越需要低喚起狀態以維持表現。"},{"id":"q1743","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In teaching the push press, which of the following is an example of segmentation with pure-part training integration?\nPractice the push press without any equipment, progress to practice with a PVC pipe, and end with an unloaded bar\nPractice the dip, followed by the dip with the drive, and end with practice of the entire push press\nPractice the dip, the drive, and the catch independently before practicing the entire push press\nPractice the dip and the drive independently, followed by practice of the dip with the drive; then practice the catch independently and end with practice of the entire push press","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Practice the dip, the drive, and the catch independently before practicing the entire push press","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"分段練習（segmentation）是把 push press 拆成 dip、drive、catch 分別獨立練習，最後再練習完整動作（純分段式整合）。"},{"id":"q1744","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Complete the sentence: Maintaining adequate glycogen stores\nspares the use of protein for energy\nimproves maximum power\ndecreases endurance performance\nhelps athletes gain weight","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"spares the use of protein for energy","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"維持充足肝醣儲量可以節省蛋白質被當作能量燃燒（蛋白質節省效應）。"},{"id":"q1745","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The following is the most likely contributor to fatigue and poor performance:\nlow protein intake\niron deficiency\nlow calcium intake\nomerga-3 fatty acid deficiency","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"iron deficiency","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"鐵缺乏最可能導致疲勞與表現低落，因為鐵影響氧氣運輸與能量代謝。"},{"id":"q1746","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a recommendation for lowering undesirably high levels of blood lipids?\nreduce complex carbohydrate intake\nlimit saturated fatty acid intake to 30% of total calories\nconsume a minimum of 500 mg of dietary cholesterol per day\nreplace saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated or polyunsaturated fatty acids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"replace saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated or polyunsaturated fatty acids","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"以單元不飽和或多不飽和脂肪酸取代飽和脂肪酸，是降低不良血脂肪濃度的正確做法。"},{"id":"q1747","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"which of the following protein sources does not contain all essential amino acids in appreciable quantities?\npoultry\neggs\nlentils\nbeef","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"lentils","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"扁豆（豆類）缺乏某種必需胺基酸、不完全；禽肉、蛋、牛肉等動物性來源均含全部必需胺基酸。"},{"id":"q1748","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The primary macronutrient that is addressed in the precompetition meal is\nfat\ncarbohydrate\nprotein\nvitamin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"carbohydrate","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"賽前餐首要處理的巨量營養素是碳水，目的在最大化肝醣儲量。"},{"id":"q1749","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following makes the GREATEST contribution to total energy expenditure?\nresting metabolic rate\nphysical activity energy expenditure\nthermic effect of food\nresting blood sugar levels","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"resting metabolic rate","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"靜息代謝率（RMR）佔總能量消耗的最大比例（約六成以上），高於活動消耗與食物熱效應。"},{"id":"q1750","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a characteristic of anorexia nervosa?\nnormal body weight\nvery low dietary fat intake\npreoccupation with food\nsecretive eating","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"preoccupation with food","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"飲食失調之食慾喪失症（anorexia nervosa）的特徵是對食物過度惦記；患者體重明顯偏低且常怕變胖。"},{"id":"q1751","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When an eating disorder is suspected, the strength and conditioning professional should\nmonitor the athlete's daily food intake\nrequire frequent weigh-ins\nencourage further assessment by an eating disorder specialist\nprovide nutritional information","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"encourage further assessment by an eating disorder specialist","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"懷疑運動員有飲食失調時，訓練師應轉介給飲食失調專業人員進一步評估，而不是隻有自己記錄或頻繁量體重。"},{"id":"q1752","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following dietary supplements is (are) considered a stimulant?\n1 creatine\n2 caffeine\n3 HMB\n4 citrus aurantium\n1 and 2\n2 and 4\n3 and 4\n1 and 3","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 and 4","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"咖啡因與苦橙（citrus aurantium，含辛弗林）屬興奮劑類補劑；肌酸與 HMB 不是興奮劑。"},{"id":"q1753","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is NOT part of caffeine's role in improving athletic performance?\nincreased power production\ndecreased glycogen depletion\nincreased fat oxidation\ndecreased urine production","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decreased urine production","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"咖啡因有利尿傾向，並不是減少尿液；其增能機制包括提高功率輸出、節省肝醣與提升脂肪氧化。"},{"id":"q1754","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the BEST reason for aerobic endurance athletes to avoid erythropoietin use?\nHematocrit and hemoglobin levels may decrease\nIt may cause an unregulated increase in red blood cell production\nResistance to infectious disease may be impaired\nIt may reduce the ability of the blood to carry oxygen","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"it may cause an unregulated increase in red blood cell production","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"紅血球生成素（EPO）可能造成紅血球不受調控地增生，血細胞比容過高使血液過黏，增加心臟負擔與心血管風險。"},{"id":"q1755","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Creatine supplementation improves all of the following variables EXCEPT\nlean body mass\nmaximal strength\nendurance performance\npower","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"endurance performance","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌酸可改善瘦體重、最大肌力與爆發力，但對（有氧）耐力表現沒有穩定助益。"},{"id":"q1756","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following performance-enhancing substances is most likely to increase lean body mass?\nanabolic steroids\narginine\nephedrine\nBeta alanine","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anabolic steroids","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"同化類固醇（anabolic steroids）最可能增加瘦體重。"},{"id":"q1757","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A college basketball coach would like to know which one of her players has the most muscular power. Which of the following is the MOST valid test for measuring muscular power?\nvertical jump\n1RM bench press\n5RM squat\n100 m (109-yard) sprint","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vertical jump","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"測量肌肉爆發力最有效的測驗是垂直跳；1RM 臥推與 5RM 深蹲測肌力，40 碼衝測速度。"},{"id":"q1758","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When measuring maximal strength of a soccer player, which of the following could potentially adversely affect the test-retest reliability of the results?\n1 using multiple testers\n2 retesting at a different time of day\n3 an athlete's inexperience with the tested exercise\n4 using an established testing protocol\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 2, & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"多名測驗者、改在不同時間重測、受試者對動作不熟練都會損害重測信度（1、2、3）；使用既有標準化流程反而有助信度。"},{"id":"q1759","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following procedures should be followed when testing an athlete's cardiovascular fitness in the heat EXCEPT\nperforming the test in an indoor facility\nusing salt tablets to retain water\nscheduling the test in the morning\ndrinking fluids during the test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"using salt tablets to retain water","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"熱環境下測心肺適能時不建議使用鹽錠（易造成腸胃負擔）；正確做法是改在室內、安排於清晨、測驗中補充水分。"},{"id":"q1760","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The bench press, vertical jump, and 10m (11-yard) sprint are the MOST valid tests for which of the following American football positions?\nquarterback\ndefensive back\nwide receiver\ndefensive lineman","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"defensive lineman","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"臥推、垂直跳與 10 公尺衝刺的組合強調上肢與短距離爆發力，與防守前鋒線球員（defensive lineman）的位置需求最吻合。"},{"id":"q1761","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following sequences will produce the MOST reliable results?\n1RM power clean, T-test, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run, 1RM bench press\nT-test, 1RM power clean, 1RM bench press, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run\n1.5 mile (2.4 km) run, 1RM bench press, T-test, 1RM power clean\n1RM bench press, 1 RM power clean, T-test, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"T-test, 1RM power clean, 1RM bench press, 1.5 mile (2.4 km) run\n(agility before power before strength before endurance)","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"測驗順序依靈敏（T-test）→ 爆發力（power clean）→ 肌力（臥推）→ 耐力（1.5 英里跑）排列，才不會因疲勞幹擾後續測驗，結果最可靠。"},{"id":"q1762","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anaerobic capacity is quantified as the maximal power output achieved during activity\nlasting less than 10 seconds\n30 to 90 seconds\n2 to 3 minutes\nlonger than 5 minutes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30 to 90 seconds","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"無氧能力（anaerobic capacity）以持續 30-90 秒活動中所能達到的最大功率輸出來量化。"},{"id":"q1763","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests is NOT used to measure maximum muscular power?\nMargaria-Kalamen test\nvertical jump\n40-yard (37 m) sprint\n1RM power clean","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"40-yard (37 m) sprint","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"40 碼衝刺主要測速度而非最大肌功率；Margaria-Kalamen、垂直跳與 1RM power clean 皆用於測爆發力。"},{"id":"q1764","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Flexibility of which of these muscle groups or body areas is assessed during the sit-and-reach test?\n1 hamstrings\n2 erector spinae\n3 lumbar spine\n4 hip flexors\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"坐式前伸（sit-and-reach）測驗評估的是膕繩肌（hamstrings）與腰椎（lumbar spine）的柔軟度（1 與 3）。"},{"id":"q1765","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a reason for a trial of the T-test to be disqualified (see figure 13.11)?\ntouching the base of cone D\nshuffling from cone C to cone D\ncrossing the feet from cone B to cone C\nrunning forward from cone A to cone B","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"crossing the feet from cone B to cone C","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"T-test 中從 B 點到 C 點時交叉雙腳（未用滑步 shuffle）是使該次測驗無效的常見失格原因。"},{"id":"q1766","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When compiling results from the volleyball team's vertical jump testing, the strength and conditioning professional notices that most scores are similar, but there are three scores that are much higher than the rest. Which of the following measures of central tendency is most appropriate for this group?\nmean\nmedian\nmode\nvariance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"median","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"資料中有少數極端高分時，應使用中位數（median）代表集中趨勢；平均數會被離群值拉高。"},{"id":"q1767","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a nontemperature-related effect of a warm-up?\nenhanced neural function\ndisruption of transient connective tissue bonds\nelevation of baseline oxygen consumption\nincrease in muscle temperature","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"elevation of baseline oxygen consumption","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"基礎耗氧量提升屬於熱身中非溫度相關的效應；神經功能提升與結締組織暫時鍵結的破壞、肌肉溫度上升等較屬溫度相關。"},{"id":"q1768","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When stimulated during PNF stretching, Golgi tendon organs allow the relaxation of the\nstretched muscle by contracting the reciprocal muscle\nreciprocal muscle by contracting the stretched muscle\nreciprocal muscle by its own contraction\nstretched muscle by its own contraction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"stretched muscle by its own contraction","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官（GTO）在 PNF 伸展中被刺激後，透過自體抑制讓被伸展的肌肉自身放鬆。"},{"id":"q1769","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following stretching techniques decreases muscle spindle stimulation?\ndynamic\nballistic\nstatic\npassive","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"static","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"靜態伸展能降低肌梭的刺激；彈振式（ballistic）伸展最容易引發牽張反射。"},{"id":"q1770","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Stimulation of muscle spindles induces a\nrelaxation of GTOs\nrelaxation of the stretched muscle\ncontraction of the stretched muscle\ncontraction of the reciprocal muscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"contraction of the stretched muscle","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌梭受刺激會透過牽張反射使被拉伸的肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q1771","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After performing the hold-relax with agonist contraction PNF stretch for the hamstrings, which of the following explains the resulting increase in flexibility?\n1 autogenic inhibition\n2 stretch inhibition\n3 reciprocal inhibition\n4 contraction of the reciprocal muscle\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"hold-relax 搭配主動肌收縮的 PNF 之後，柔軟度提升來自高爾基腱器官造成的自體抑制（1）與主動肌收縮帶來的互動抑制（3）。"},{"id":"q1772","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises requires a spotter?\nlat pulldown\nwrist curl\npower clean\nstep-up","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"step-up","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"登箱（step-up）需要保護者； lat pulldown、腕彎舉與 power clean 依 NSCA 指引不需保護者。"},{"id":"q1773","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During which of the following exercises should a spotter's hands be placed on the athlete's forearms near the wrists?\nbench press\nincline dumbbell bench press\nupright row\nlying barbell triceps extension","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"incline dumbbell bench press","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"上斜槓鈴啞鈴臥推（incline dumbbell bench press）保護時，保護者的手應放在運動員前臂靠近手腕處。"},{"id":"q1774","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following grips should be used during the deadlift exercise\n1 overhand\n2 closed\n3 open\n4 alternated\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 4 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 2, & 4 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"硬舉可用正握（overhand）、閉握與正反握（alternated，1、2、4）；開放式（open）握不適用於硬舉。"},{"id":"q1775","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the correct foot pattern in the step-up exercise?\nstep up left foot, step up right foot, step down left foot, step down right foot\nstep up right foot, step up left foot, step down left foot, step down right foot\nstep up left foot, step down left foot, step up right foot, step down right foot\nstep up right foot, step up left foot, step down right foot, step down left foot","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"step up right foot, step up left foot, step down left foot, step down right foot","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"登箱的正確腳步順序：右腳上、左腳上、左腳下、右腳下——先上箱的腳最後才下箱。"},{"id":"q1776","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The primary movement during the second pull phase of the power clean exercise is\nhip flexion\nhip extension\nknee flexion\ndorsiflexion","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hip extension","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"power clean 第二拉（second pull）階段的主要動作是快速的髖伸展。"},{"id":"q1777","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If during the tire flip the athlete's hips rise faster than the shoulders during the initial pushing motion, what is an effective correction to give the athlete?\nStart with a higher hip position\nKeep the hips slightly below the shoulders in this position\nLift the tire upward instead of driving it forward\nPush with the arms first","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Keep the hips slightly below the shoulders in this position","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"翻輪胎時若髖部上升快於肩部，糾正方式是維持髖部略低於肩部的位置，用腿部持續向前推。"},{"id":"q1778","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If a strong athlete incorporates only unilateral training into his or her program, what might the strength and conditioning professional expect to happen?\nA bilateral facilitation will occur\nA bilateral deficit will be developed\nA reduction in bilateral asymmetries will occur\nOnly unilateral strength will increase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A bilateral facilitation will occur","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"只做強者的單側訓練時，預期會出現雙側facilitation：神經系統在雙側動作中動員增強的現象。"},{"id":"q1779","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"With regard to core training, when is instability exercise best applied?\nwith untrained athletes who are relatively weak\nin trained athletes who are rehabilitating from an injury\nwith trained athletes who are trying to optimize strength and power\nwith untrained athletes who are new to the exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in trained athletes who are rehabilitating from an injury","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"不穩定平面（instability）的核心訓練最適用於正在傷後復健的受訓運動員；對追求最大肌力與功率者，不穩定反而會限制輸出。"},{"id":"q1780","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is a rationale for using variable-resistance training methods?\nto accommodate the changing mechanical advantages associated with constant-loaded exercises\nto minimize force application throughout the full range of motion\nto increase the time spent decelerating during a lifting motion\nto keep the applied resistance constant during changes in joint angle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"to accommodate the changing mechanical advantages associated with constant-loaded exercises","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"變阻式訓練（variable resistance，如彈力帶、鏈條）的用意是配合恆重動作中不斷變化的機械優勢（力量曲線），讓阻力全程貼合力量輸出。"},{"id":"q1781","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Training on instability devices can reduce the overall agonist force production capacity and power output of the athlete to less than _____ of what can be achieved in a stable condition.\n20%\n50%\n70%\n90%","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"70%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"在不穩定器材上訓練，主動肌的力量輸出與功率可能降到穩定狀態的 70% 以下。"},{"id":"q1782","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The basketball coach says his starting center needs to jump higher. In addition to beginning a plyometric program, which of the following resistance training exercises are MOST specific to this goal?\n1 power clean\n2 leg (knee) curl\n3 front squat\n4 seated calf (heel) raise\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"要跳得更高，最專屬的抗阻動作是 power clean 與前蹲（front squat），皆屬髖膝踝三伸、與起跳動作模式一致（1 與 3）。"},{"id":"q1783","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The soccer team is transitioning from off-season to preseason training. How should the team's resistance training frequency be altered?\nIncrease frequency to improve muscular endurance\nDo not change frequency and add plyometrics\nDecrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice\nDesign a split routine with three days on and one day off","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Decrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"由季外轉入季前時，應降低抗阻訓練頻率，騰出更多時間做專項技術練習。"},{"id":"q1784","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An American football lineman has difficulty driving into defensive linemen and believes he has lost his explosive ability. Which of the following is the BEST exercise order to help this athlete improve his performance?\nback squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl, power clean\npower clean, back squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl\nleg (knee) curl, back squat, power clean, hip sled\nhip sled, power clean, leg (knee) curl, back squat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"power clean, back squat, hip sled, leg (knee) curl","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"想要恢復爆發力，動作順序應由高功率需求排到較低：power clean → back squat → hip sled → 腿彎舉。"},{"id":"q1785","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following volumes has the potential to increase muscular strength the MOST?\n5 sets of 5 repetitions\n1 set of 5 repetitions\n5 sets of 15 repetitions\n1 set of 15 repetitions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"5 sets of 5 repetitions","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"5 組 5 下（高強度、高組數）對肌力的提升潛力最大。"},{"id":"q1786","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female triathlete needs to improve the muscular endurance of her upper body. Using three sets of 15 repetitions per exercise, which of the following rest period lengths will MAXIMIZE her goal?\n3 minutes\n1.5 minutes\n45 seconds\n30 seconds","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30 seconds","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"追求肌耐力時休息越短越好，30 秒休息對區域性肌耐力的刺激最大。"},{"id":"q1787","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a phase of the stretch-shortening cycle?\namortization\nconcentric\neccentric\nisometric","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"isometric","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"等長（isometric）不是伸展-縮短迴圈（SSC）的階段；SSC 三階段為離心、緩衝（amortization）與向心。"},{"id":"q1788","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following structures detects rapid movement and initiates the stretch reflex?\nGolgi tendon organ\nmuscle spindle\nextrafusal muscle fiber\nPacinian corpuscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle spindle","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肌梭（muscle spindle）偵測快速的伸展速率並啟動牽張反射。"},{"id":"q1789","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following should be assessed before beginning a lower body plyometric training program?\n1 balance\n2 strength\n3 training history\n4 lean body mass\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n1, 2, 3 & 4","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 2 & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"開始下肢增強式訓練前應評估平衡、肌力與訓練史（1、2、3）；去脂體重不是必要評估項。"},{"id":"q1790","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following types of plyometric drills is generally considered to be the MOST intense?\njumps in place\nbounds\ndepth jumps\nbox jumps","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"depth jumps","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"深度跳（depth jumps）一般被認為是最強烈的增強式訓練。"},{"id":"q1791","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following work-to-rest ratios is the MOST appropriate to assign to a plyometric training workout?\n1:5\n1:4\n1:3\n1:2","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1:2","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練需要充足休息，工作休息比至少 1:2（本題答案以此為可接受下限）；強度越高應給更長休息。"},{"id":"q1792","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What does the term impulse refer to?\nthe relationship between power and velocity\nthe relationship between acceleration and velocity\nthe relationship between force and velocity\nthe relationship between force and time","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the relationship between force and time","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"衝量（impulse）是力量與時間的關係（力乘時間）。"},{"id":"q1793","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Elite sprinters produce __________ forces in a ___________ ground contact time as compared to their novice counterparts.\nlarger, longer\nsimilar, shorter\nlarger, shorter\nsmaller, longer","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"larger, shorter","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"精英短跑手相比初學者能產生更大的地面反作用力，而且觸地時間更短。"},{"id":"q1794","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In upright sprinting, an athlete's stride length is largely dependent on ____________________\nthe amount of vertical force produced during the stance phase\nthe athlete's flexibility\nthe athlete's stride rate\nthe amount of horizontal force produced during the toe-off of the stance phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the amount of vertical force produced during the stance phase","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"跑步的步長主要取決於支撐階段產生的垂直力量大小（垂直方向作用力越大、跳得越高越遠）。"},{"id":"q1795","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Drills or tests that require the athlete to move rapidly in response to a stimulus such as a whistle, arrow, or opponent are best for measuring which of the following?\nchange of direction\nmaneuverability\nagility\nacceleration","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"agility","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"對哨音、箭頭或對手等刺激快速做出移動反應的練習或測驗，測的是靈敏度（agility）。"},{"id":"q1796","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Select the aspect of training that requires additional emphasis when the aim is to improve change-of-direction ability\nstrength\neccentric strength\nreactive strength\nrate of force development","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"eccentric strength","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"要改善變向（change-of-direction）能力，應額外強調離心肌力，因為減速能力決定變向表現。"},{"id":"q1797","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following adaptations occur as an outcome of an aerobic endurance training program?\n1 increased oxygen delivery to working tissues\n2 higher rate of aerobic energy production\n3 greater utilization of fat as a fuel source\n4 increased disturbance of the acid-base balance\n1 & 3 only\n2 & 4 only\n1, 2, & 3 only\n2, 3, & 4 only","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1, 2, & 3 only","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力訓練的適應包括增加氧氣輸送、提高有氧能量產出與增加脂肪作為燃料的比例（1、2、3）；酸鹼平衡的幹擾應減少而非增加。"},{"id":"q1798","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following types of training is conducted at an intensity equal to the lactate threshold?\npace/tempo\ninterval\nhigh-intensity interval training (HIIT)\nFartlek","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pace/tempo","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"以乳酸閾值強度進行的訓練是配速/節奏跑（pace/tempo）。"},{"id":"q1799","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the method most commonly used to assign and regulate exercise intensity?\noxygen consumption\nheart rate\nratings of perceived exertion\nrace pace","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"heart rate","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"最常用的制訂與控制運動強度方法是心率。"},{"id":"q1800","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"the loss of physiological adaptations upon the cessation of training is an example of\nspecificity of training\ncross-training\ndetraining\ntapering","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"detraining","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"停止訓練後生理適應逐漸消失，是去訓練效應（detraining）的例子。"},{"id":"q1801","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The longest aerobic endurance training sessions should be performed during which of the following sport seasons?\npostseason\npreseason\nin-season\noff-season","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"off-season","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"最長距離的有氧耐力訓練應安排在季外（off-season）。"},{"id":"q1802","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During which stage of the General Adaptation Syndrome does the body physiologically adapt to heavier training loads?\nalarm\nresistance\nexhaustion\nrestoration","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"resistance","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:655535133"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"在壓力症候群（GAS）的抵抗期，身體對較重訓練負荷產生生理適應。"},{"id":"q1803","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following rest periods is most appropriate for a middle distance runner performing 800-m running intervals in 2 min?\n2 min\n4 min\n6 min","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- 6 min\n- aerobic oxidative therefore work to rest = 1:3-1:4","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"800 公尺跑屬以氧化系統為主的活動，工作休息比約 1:3 到 1:4，跑 2 分鐘應休息 6 分鐘。"},{"id":"q1804","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following events occurs in the hamstring muscles during the concentric muscle action of leg (knee) curl exercise?\nthe A-band length increases\nthe I-band length stays the same\nthe H-zone length decreases","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- H - zone decreases\n- I band decreases","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"依題庫答案為主動伸展：leg curl 由練習者主動收縮完成動作，與被動或靜態伸展不同。"},{"id":"q1805","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a strength training regiment during what period (weeks) do we see muscle hypertrophy contributing to strength gains\nHow about strength gains that are attributed to neural factors","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. weeks 7-8 on wards\n2. 1-6 weeks","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"第 7-8 週起肌力成長才主要由肌肉肥大貢獻；前 1-6 週的肌力成長歸因於神經因素。"},{"id":"q1806","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate recommendation for fluid intake before a collegiate soccer match?\nA. 0.5L, 2hr before match\nB. 1L, 0.5hr before match\nC. 1.5L, 1 hour before match\nd. 1L, 2hr before match","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a/","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"賽前約 2 小時攝取約 0.5 公升水分（符合運動前 2-3 小時 5-7 mL/kg 的原則），讓身體充分吸收並排出多餘水分。"},{"id":"q1807","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is participating in an aerobic endurance event that lasts approximately one hour. Which of the following beverage qualities is most appropriate?\nA. 78 deg F, 18% CHO\nB. 65 deg F, 10% CHO\nC. 52 deg F, 6% CHO","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"C.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"約 1 小時的有氧耐力賽事，最適合約 52°F（10-15°C）、含糖約 6% 的飲料，利於吸收與補充。"},{"id":"q1808","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female collegiate basketball forward is in-season. She is content with her weight (154 lbs, 70 kg); but, would like to know if her diet is appropriate for her needs. Her daily caloric intake consists of the following: 1625 kcal CHO, 620 kcal protein, 300 kcal fat\na. decrease CHO, maintain protein, decrease fat\nb. increase CHO, increase protein, maintain fat\nc. maintain CHO, decrease protein, increase fat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"她的熱量配比為碳水約 64%、蛋白質約 24%、脂肪約 12%：應維持碳水、調降過高的蛋白質、提高偏低的脂肪至建議範圍。"},{"id":"q1809","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following organs is the primary synthesizer of creatine\na. kidney\nb. pancreas\nc. liver","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肝臟是肌酸合成的主要器官（腎臟也參與，但合成量以肝臟為主）。"},{"id":"q1810","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1. what are the major signs (definition) of bulimia\n2. how long do these have to persist for it to be diagnosed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. binge eating followed by purging\n2. 1/wk for 3 months","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"暴飲症的定義是暴飲後接補償行為（如清除行為）；診斷需每週至少一次、持續 3 個月。"},{"id":"q1811","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1. what is the ideal temperature of fluids that are to be given to athletes while competing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. 50-59 deg f. or 10-15 deg C","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"比賽中供應的飲料理想溫度為 50-59°F（約 10-15°C），低溫有利胃排空與自願攝取。"},{"id":"q1812","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when competing in aerobic activities in hot weather answer the following\n1. ideal sodium concentration of fluid\n2. ideal potassium concentration of fluid (mEq)\n3. ideal CHO concentraiton of fluid (%)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. 20-30\n2. 2-5\n3. 5-10%","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"熱環境有氧競賽時飲料的理想電解質與糖濃度：鈉 20-30 mEq/L、鉀 2-5 mEq/L、碳水 5-10%。"},{"id":"q1813","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following are considered B agonist\nI. ephedrine\nII. citrus aurantium\nIII. caffeine\nIV. anabolic steroids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"I.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"麻黃素（ephedrine）屬 β 受體促進劑；苦橙、咖啡因與同化類固醇皆不屬此類。"},{"id":"q1814","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1. what is the common use of ephedrine\n2. what is the ergogenic benefit\n3. what is the efficacy of this aid","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. provide releif for asthma, bronchitis, allergies\n2. fat loss\n3. only efficacious when combined w/ caffeine","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"麻黃素常見用途是緩解氣喘、支氣管炎與過敏症狀；增能目的是減脂；只有與咖啡因併用時才有明顯效果。"},{"id":"q1815","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ephedrine\n1. side effects (5)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. nausea, vomitting, change in mood, palpitations and death","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"麻黃素的副作用包括噁心、嘔吐、情緒改變、心悸，嚴重可致死。"},{"id":"q1816","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When performing the front squat w/ parallel arm what significant effect is added by placing he hand grip outside of the shoulders","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- adds stability","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"前蹲時握距寬於肩部外側能增加軀幹與上背的穩定性，幫助維持挺胸姿勢。"},{"id":"q1817","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A novice athlete is working to improve wrist flexibility as needed to achieve the correct arm position for the front squat as pictured. What would be the best recommendation to make in this scenario","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- use straps to hold the bar","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"手腕柔軟度不足者，建議用綁帶（straps）固定槓鈴以維持前蹲架式，同時持續改善手腕活動度。"},{"id":"q1818","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete has a goal to perform a deep squat in the exercise shown. He has difficulty maintaining an upright position when his thighs go past parallel. What modification should be made first ?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- reducing the weight of the bar","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"深蹲過平行後難以保持軀幹直立時，應先降低槓鈴重量，先保住直立姿勢再逐步加重。"},{"id":"q1819","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A field hockey player has a running pace of 6.5 mph (10.5 km/h). She now must run indoors due to inclement weather. The strength and conditioning professional observes the athlete set the treadmill to 6.5 mph (10.5 km/h) at a 3% grade. Which of the following treadmill adjustments is most appropriate to mimic her outdoor pace?\na. increase speed, increase grade\nb. increase speed, maintain grade\nc. maintain speed, decrease grade","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"跑步機 1% 坡度約等同路跑；她設在 3% 坡度太陡，應維持 6.5 mph 的速度並降低坡度以重現戶外配速。"},{"id":"q1820","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate when performing the forward walking lunge stretch?\nplanting the heel of the front foot into the floor\nmoving the hips forward and downward\nkeeping the knee of the forward leg behind the foot","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"b.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"前弓步步行伸展（forward walking lunge）應把髖部向前下方壓，才能有效伸展髖屈肌。"},{"id":"q1821","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1. why are thick mats and trampolines not good for a healthy athlete to train plyometrics on","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- increases amortization period","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"厚墊與蹦床太軟，會延長觸地（amortization）時間，削弱伸展-縮短迴圈的效果，不適合健康選手做增強式訓練。"},{"id":"q1822","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When performing plyometrics which of the following would be required of the footwear\ni. good ankle + foot support\nii. narrow sole\niii. good lateral stability\niv. wide sole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"i. iii. iv.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練的鞋需提供良好踝與足部支撐、良好側向穩定性與較寬的鞋底（窄底穩定性差）。"},{"id":"q1823","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"While working out in the strength and conditioning facility, an athlete comes across a sharp edge on a piece of equipment and cuts her hand open. There is immediate pain and bleeding. What is the strength and conditioning professional's immediate priority?\napply compression\nclean the wound\napply ice","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"手部割傷、立即出血時，第一優先是直接加壓止血，之後才是清潔傷口或冰敷。"},{"id":"q1824","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following will optimize traffic flow in a strength and conditioning facility?\npathways with a width of 24 in (61 cm)\narrangement of the equipment\nspacing equipment at least 36 in (91 cm) apart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"b.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"最佳化訓練館動線取決於器材的排列方式（layout），不只是通道寬度或間距數字。"},{"id":"q1825","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A new collegiate athlete wants to use the strength and conditioning facility for the first time. The priority of the strength and conditioning professional is to make sure that the new student-athlete\nobtains clearance from the sports medicine staff.\nsigns a release agreement form prior to using the facility.\nattends an orientation session for familiarization.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"新隊員第一次使用訓練館，首要之務是確認已取得運動醫療團隊的許可（clearance）。"},{"id":"q1826","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T - Test\n1. what is the correct head position\n2. what is the correct eye gaze","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. neutral\n2. straight ahead","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"T-test 時頭部維持中立位，視線直視前方。"},{"id":"q1827","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A college baseball player was tested 10 weeks before the start of the season with the following results:\nBodyweight: 96.5 kg\n1 RM power clean: 91 kg\n10 yd: 2.01s\nPro-agility: 4.62s\nWhich of the following needs improvement\na. power\nb. speed\nc. agility","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"power clean 91 公斤低於 D1 棒球員第 50 百分位（約 94 公斤），因此需要改善的是爆發力。"},{"id":"q1828","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1 RM Power Clean - D1 Baseball\n1. what is the 90th percentile (kg)\n2. what is the 50th percentile(kg)\n3. what is the 10th percentile (kg)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. 120 kg\n2. 94 kg\n3. 74 kg","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"D1 棒球員 1RM power clean 參考值：第 90 百分位約 120 公斤、第 50 約 94 公斤、第 10 約 74 公斤。"},{"id":"q1829","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"D1 Baseball Player Normative Data - Mean\n1. 1RM squat\n2. 1RM bench press\n3. 1RM power clean","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 128 kg\n2. 103 kg\n3. 95 kg","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"D1 棒球選手平均值：1RM 深蹲約 128 公斤、臥推約 103 公斤、power clean 約 95 公斤。"},{"id":"q1830","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female collegiate basketball forward in her junior year is administered a battery of tests. The results are shown below. Determine which needs improvement\nweight: 68kg\n1RM squat: 89kg\nvertical jump: 19 in.\n1 RM bench press: 45.5 kg\na. lower body strength\nb. anaerobic power\nc. upper body strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"她的 1RM 臥推 45.5 公斤低於 D1 女籃平均（約 48 公斤），而深蹲與垂直跳均高於平均，需改善的是上肢肌力。"},{"id":"q1831","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Female D1 Basketball - Mean\n1. 1RM bench press\n2. 1RM squat\n3. 1RM power clean","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. 48 kg\n2. 59 kg\n3. 48 kg","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"D1 女籃平均值：臥推約 48 公斤、深蹲約 59 公斤、power clean 約 48 公斤。"},{"id":"q1832","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests is the most appropriate for assessing a soccer player?\nvertical jump\n1.5 mile run\nYo-Yo Intermittent Recovery\nTest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"足球員最合適的測驗是 Yo-Yo 間歇恢復測驗，符合足球反覆高強度間歇跑的特性。"},{"id":"q1833","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"D1 Female Volleyball Player - Mean\n1. 1 RM Bench press\n2. 1 RM Squat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. 44 kg\n2. 65 kg","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"D1 女排選手平均值：1RM 臥推約 44 公斤、1RM 深蹲約 65 公斤。"},{"id":"q1834","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 315-lb (143-kg) male collegiate American football offensive lineman has the following test results:\n40 -yd: 5.9s\nbody fat %: 20%\n1 RM bench: 184 kg\na. sprint speed\nb. body composition\nc. upper body strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"40 碼 5.9 秒明顯慢於同級進攻線球員水準，需要改善的是衝刺速度；臥推 184 公斤屬優異。"},{"id":"q1835","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A strength and conditioning professional is working with an athletic trainer to recondition a cross-country runner following an ankle injury. During which of the following phases is it appropriate to introduce rotations on a wobble board?\ninflammation\nrepair\nremodeling","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"b.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:519458268"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"平衡板（wobble board）旋轉練習在修復期（腫痛消退後）引入，循序漸進恢復本體感覺與平衡。"},{"id":"q1836","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is an example of a polypeptide hormone?\nA. epinephrine\nB. insulin\nC. testosterone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"insulin","explanation_en":"Hormones are placed into three categories:\n-Steroid hormones, including testosterone and cortisol\n-Polypeptide hormones, including growth hormone and insulin\n-Amine hormones, including epinephrine and serotonin\nPolypeptide hormones consist of amino acid chains and are water soluble. They cannot diffuse across a cell membrane, but instead, interact with receptors on the cell to send messages to the cell using secondary messengers. The secretion of insulin results in the regulation of blood sugar.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"胰島素屬胜肽類激素；腎上腺素屬胺類激素，睪固酮屬類固醇激素。"},{"id":"q1837","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ingesting nonnutritive substances, such as clay or cigarette butts, is what type of eating disorder?\nA. Pica\nB. Bulimia nervosa\nC. Rumination disorder","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pica","explanation_en":"Pica is a mental health disorder that is characterized by the urge to eat non-food substances. This can include things like ice, hair, paper, cigarette butts, and chalk. Eating these nonnutritive substances can lead to other health issues such as electrolyte imbalances, gastrointestinal problems, and iron deficiency. To be diagnosed with pica, an individual would have been eating these non-food items for at least a month.\nBulimia nervosa is a cycle of binging and purging, and rumination disorder is the practice of regurgitating food and then re-chewing, swallowing, or spitting out the partially digested food.\nIf an eating disorder is suspected, a strength coach should always help the athlete get a proper diagnosis and professional care.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"異食癖（pica）指攝取泥土、煙蒂等非營養物質。"},{"id":"q1838","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The knee-jerk reflex is caused by which of the following?\nA. Extrafusal muscle fibers\nB. Golgi tendon organs\nC. Muscle spindles","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle Spindles","explanation_en":"Muscle spindles are proprioceptors located within muscle tissue that detect changes in the length of muscle tissue as well as how quickly the length changes. The muscle spindles then trigger a contraction of that muscle. The knee-jerk reflex is an example of this reaction.\nGolgi tendon organs are also proprioceptors, but are located within the tendons and detect changes in muscle tension. They react to these changes by triggering the muscle to relax.\nThe fibers that make up a muscle spindle are called intrafusal fibers. Extrafusal fibers are standard muscle fibers.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"膝反射由肌梭受牽張刺激引發牽張反射所致。"},{"id":"q1839","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Olympic lifts are functional closed-chain exercises, and stability occurs in all three planes. What are the two main movement planes for the Olympic lift techniques?\nA. Frontal plane and sagittal plane\nB. Transverse plane and frontal plane\nC. Sagittal plane and transverse plane","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Frontal plane and sagittal plane","explanation_en":"Olympic lifts occur in two movement planes: frontal and sagittal.\nThe frontal plane movements are those that move sideways\nThe sagittal plane consists of movements that occur front to back","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"奧式舉動作技術的兩大主要動作面是額狀面與矢狀面。"},{"id":"q1840","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The body performs a vertical jump in which anatomical plane?\nA. Lateral\nB. Sagittal\nC. Frontal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sagittal","explanation_en":"The sagittal plane is an imaginary line going from front to back that splits the body into right and left halves.\nDuring the vertical jump, the hips, knees, and shoulders flex and extend. This all occurs in a forward and backward motion, which indicates it is done in the sagittal plane.\nWhen an exercise is described as being performed within the sagittal plane, it is based on movement that occurs along the line of the sagittal plane. Many people think because the body is split into right and left halves that exercises performed side to side are exercises for the sagittal plane.\nSide to side (lateral) movement occurs in the frontal plane.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"垂直跳在矢狀面進行。"},{"id":"q1841","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Using a weighted sled in training involves what type of force?\nA. Surface drag\nB. Form drag\nC. Friction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"friction","explanation_en":"Pushing a weighted sled involves both friction and inertia. Friction refers to the force that is experienced when trying to move an object that is in contact with another object. In this case, it is the contact between the sled and the ground that provides friction. This must be overcome in order to move the sled.\nSurface drag and form drag are forms of fluid resistance and relate to the resistance provided by fluids either moving along the surface of an object (surface drag), or to the way fluid provides resistance to the front or back of an object (form drag), which changes based on the size of the object.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"拖曳加重雪橇克服的是地面摩擦力（friction）。"},{"id":"q1842","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What do you call the connection between a motor neuron and the muscle fibers it innervates?\nA. Sarcolemma\nB. Neuromuscular junction\nC. Cross-bridge","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Neuromuscular junction","explanation_en":"A neuromuscular junction is where a motor neuron (nerve fiber) connects to muscle fibers and creates the chemical synapse through which it can transmit a signal that tells those fibers to contract. Each muscle cell has one neuromuscular junction, although a single motor neuron innervates many muscle fibers.\nTogether, the motor neuron and all the the muscle fibers it innervates make up the motor unit. All of the muscle fibers in the motor unit contract together when stimulated by the motor neuron.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動神經元與其支配肌纖維之間的連結稱為神經肌肉接合處（neuromuscular junction）。"},{"id":"q1843","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A recruitment coach is conducting athletic testing for athletes interested in trying out for a traveling volleyball team. Which of the following could help determine which tests would help identify athletes with the potential to excel in volleyball?\nA. Construct validity\nB. Predictive validity\nC. Concurrent validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Predictive validity","explanation_en":"Predictive validity measures how well a specific test might predict the potential for future performance. If possible, the coach conducting try-out testing should include tests that have high predictive validity. For example, if performance on the vertical jump had been proven to correlate with volleyball performance levels, then the vertical jump would have predictive validity and should be included in the testing.\nConstruct validity is a measure of overall validity and describes how well a test measures what it is supposed to measure. Although it is also an important consideration when selecting tests to include in any situation, this alone would not identify which tests could help predict future performance.\nConcurrent validity measures how well the results of one test compare to those of another test for the same construct","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"能辨識誰有潛力在排球勝出的測驗選擇依據是預測效度（predictive validity）：測驗分數預測日後表現的程度。"},{"id":"q1844","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 22-year-old athlete's maximum heart rate is 198 bpm and his resting heart rate is 63 bpm. What is the value of the difference between these two?\nA. Perceived exertion\nB. Age-predicted capacity\nC. Heart rate reserve (HRR)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Heart rate reserve (HRR)","explanation_en":"Heart rate reserve (HRR) is the difference between an athlete's maximal heart rate and resting heart rate.\nHeart rate, especially during exercise, is closely related to oxygen consumption, and therefore is often used to prescribe aerobic exercise intensity.\nThe Karvonen method of determining target heart rate takes the HRR into account. If the athlete wants to train at 70% intensity:\nSteps:\nDetermine age predicted max heart rate: (220 - age) 220 - 22 = 198 bpm\nDetermine HRR: (Max HR - resting HR) 198 - 63 = 135 bpm\nTarget heart rate: [(HRR x intensity) + resting heart rate] (135 x .7) + 63 = 157.5 bpm\nThe athlete should aim to train at a heart rate of 157 to 158 bpm","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"最大心率減靜息心率等於心率儲備（HRR），是 Karvonen 法計算目標心率的基礎。"},{"id":"q1845","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An outside group is interested in using the strength and conditioning facility. Which of the following is not required for the group to provide prior to use?\nA. Liability insurance\nB. Health history of participants\nC. Release form for all participants","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Health history of participants","explanation_en":"With pre-approval, outside groups may sometimes use the strength and conditioning facility. These groups should provide proof of their own liability insurance, and all participants need to sign a release form, or waiver, in order to use the facility. All use should be supervised by strength and conditioning facility staff.\nProviding individual health histories is not generally a requirement to use the facility.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"外部團體使用訓練館需自備責任保險並讓成員簽署同意書；參加者的健康史不是必要提供項。"},{"id":"q1846","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which exercise can be performed by the anterior deltoids to improve shoulder flexion?\nA. Front shoulder raise\nB. Lat pulldown\nC. Lateral raise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Front shoulder raise","explanation_en":"The anterior deltoid is responsible for flexion of the shoulder in the sagittal plane. Incorporating front shoulder raises will strengthen this movement. They are performed by holding two dumbbells with the palms pronated, then raising the arms up until they are parallel with the ground.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"前三角肌可做前舉（front shoulder raise）改善肩關節屈；側平舉主練中束。"},{"id":"q1847","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following devices is often used to measure joint range of motion?\nA. Caliper\nB. Metronome\nC. Goniometer","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Goniometer","explanation_en":"The goniometer is a device that measures angles and can be used to measure joint angles. The angle a joint is capable of achieving at its end range can be measured as a test of the range of motion in a specific joint. Both active and passive range of motion can be measured using a goniometer.\nA caliper is a device that is used to measure the size of a fold of skin and subcutaneous fat when performing skinfold measurements to determine body composition. A metronome is a device that can be set to a specific tempo, which is indicated with an audible sound. It is often used for tests like the curl up, which require athletes to perform movements at a specific pace","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"測量關節活動範圍（ROM）常用量角器（goniometer）。"},{"id":"q1848","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following would be considered a muscle buffer?\nA. Sodium bicarbonate\nB. Human growth hormone\nC. Testosterone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Sodium bicarbonate","explanation_en":"During bouts of high-intensity anaerobic training, hydrogen ions (H+) accumulate within skeletal muscle while pH decreases. This combination has a detrimental effect on performance. Regulating the concentration of H+ in the muscle is key to improving performance, especially in sports that involve repeated bouts of high-intensity movement.\nMuscle-buffering capacity (MBC) describes the ability to effectively regulate the H+ concentration during high-intensity training. This ability can be improved through training, but may also be increased using a nutritional muscle buffer such as sodium bicarbonate.\nOther examples of muscle buffers include beta-alanine and sodium citrate.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"碳酸氫鈉（sodium bicarbonate）屬緩衝劑，可中和氫離子、延緩酸化。"},{"id":"q1849","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the type of stretch called in which the individual who is stretching is the source of the force?\nA. Passive stretch\nB. Active stretch\nC. Agonist contraction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Active stretch","explanation_en":"As the term implies, an active stretch requires the stretcher to perform an action. This action can occur in a static stretch (stationary) or a dynamic stretch (moving). If an individual is holding their own body part into a stretched position, this is still an active stretch. This includes exercises like a static sitting toe touch.\nA passive stretch requires the assistance of a partner or a machine to provide the force to move a body part through a range of motion to initiate a stretch.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"運動前數小時補水是為了避免運動中脫水，讓身體以充足水合狀態開始運動。"},{"id":"q1850","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"MyPlate provides guidelines on daily caloric and portion recommendations for which of the following demographics?\nA. Individuals of all ages who average 30 minutes or less of moderate activity per day\nB. Athletes\nC. General adults over the age of 18","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Individuals of all ages who average\n30 minutes or less of moderate activity per day","explanation_en":"MyPlate provides general guidelines for total caloric intake as well as specific daily portions of food groups including protein, grains, fruit, and vegetables. Specific recommendations are broken down by age and gender, starting for children as young as two years old.\nThe guidelines are geared to provide adequate nutrition for individuals who get 30 minutes or less of moderate activity on a daily basis. The guidelines do not generally account for the increased needs of athletes.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"MyPlate 的份量與熱量建議針對各年齡、每日中等活動不超過 30 分鐘的一般人，不完全適用於運動員。"},{"id":"q1851","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises are used to increase the rate at which force can be applied?\nA. The push press, the power clean, and the snatch\nB. The squat, the deadlift, and the upright row\nC. The overhead press, the lunge, and the push press","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: The push press, the power clean, and the snatch","explanation_en":"Power is defined as the rate of doing work.\nPower = Work / Time, and Power = Force x Velocity.\nThe push press, power clean, and snatch all require quick and forceful movements and are utilized to increase an athlete's power.\nThe other movements may help increase an athlete's strength, but increases in the rate of force applied require explosive movements such as the Olympic lifts.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"push press、power clean 與 snatch 能快速應用力量，可提高力量施加速率（功率/力量發展速率）。"},{"id":"q1852","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How do low glycogen levels affect muscular force?\nA. Decreases muscular force\nB. Increases muscular force\nC. No effect on muscular force","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Decreases muscular force","explanation_en":"Glycogen stores are depleted during training and competition. When glycogen is depleted, performance declines. This includes muscular force and power output. Consuming carbohydrates before, during, and after training and competition replenishes glycogen stores, which helps to maintain an optimum level of performance.\nAll athletes should be aware of the carbohydrate recommendations based on their activity and intensity and duration of training.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"肝醣濃度過低會降低肌肉力量輸出，加速疲勞。"},{"id":"q1853","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the goal of consuming fluids a few hours before beginning exercise?\nA. To rehydrate before the next training session\nB. To avoid dehydration during exercise\nC. To replace lost fluids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: To avoid dehydration during exercise","explanation_en":"Dehydration is detrimental to performance; even a 2% loss of body water can have significant effects during training and competition. Many athletes begin training sessions in a hypo-hydrated state, which means they are already slightly dehydrated. Since they lose more water as they sweat during training, it can be difficult to adequately rehydrate during training.\nConsuming fluids a few hours prior to training (as opposed to right before a training session) allows enough time for the fluid to be absorbed so the athlete can begin training in a hydrated state","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"開始運動前數小時補液的目標是避免運動期間發生脫水。"},{"id":"q1854","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The percentile ranks of an athlete's vertical jump and 1RM back squat vary greatly. Which of the following types of validity would these results reinforce?\nA. Face validity\nB. Discriminant validity\nC. Convergent validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Discriminant validity","explanation_en":"Two tests that have discriminant validity are proven to test and distinguish between different abilities. In this case, the vertical jump tests explosive power and the back squat tests lower body strength levels. Some athletes who have high strength levels also perform well on the vertical jump, while other athletes who have high strength levels do not perform as well on the vertical jump. There is not a high correlation between the two tests, which means that simply because an athlete scores well on one test does not mean they will score well on the other test.\nConducting both tests will allow the strength and conditioning professional to test both the athlete's strength levels and their explosive power abilities. This enables them to design better programs for each athlete.\nFace validity refers to the belief (by the athlete) that a test actually will measure what it is supposed to measure. Convergent validity is evidence that a given test produces similar testing results as one that is generally accepted as the \"gold standard\" to test that specific ability.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"垂直跳（爆發力）與 1RM 深蹲（肌力）百分位排名差異大，說明兩者測量不同構念，支援區辨效度（discriminant validity）。"},{"id":"q1855","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If a nutritional supplement includes leucine on its list of ingredients, which physiological mechanisms would it stimulate?\nA. Protein synthesis and protection from muscle catabolism\nB. Beta blocker and reduced heart rate\nC. Raised core temperature","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Protein synthesis and protection from muscle catabolism","explanation_en":"Leucine is a branched chain amino acid that plays a major role in stimulating muscle protein synthesis and helps to protect the muscle protein from catabolism during exercise.\nIt appears that leucine is the key amino acid for stimulating muscle protein synthesis. In fact, many researchers believe that leucine is the rate-limiting factor for maximizing protein synthesis within skeletal muscle, as opposed to the total amount of protein consumed.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"白胺酸（leucine）能啟動蛋白質合成並保護肌肉免於分解（抗異化）。"},{"id":"q1856","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does a low protein diet affect calcium absorption?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Decreases calcium absorption","explanation_en":"Adequate protein consumption increases the absorption of calcium in the body. It has been shown that low protein diets can decrease calcium absorption. This applies to protein intakes below 0.7 g/kg of body weight per day.\nCalcium is important for maintaining bone strength and plays a role in muscle contraction, nerve transmission, and blood clotting. It is important to know how easily diet variations can affect health. A qualified nutrition professional is the best option for determining appropriate intakes for individuals","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"低蛋白飲食會降低鈣的吸收。"},{"id":"q1857","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When there are two people spotting a lifter on the back squat, where should the spotters hold their hands during the downward and upward phases of the movement?\nA. Each spotter should stand at one end of the bar and hold their hands 2-3\" under the end of the bar with the thumbs crossed\nB. Each spotter should stand to one side of the lifter, with their hands 2-3\" under the bar just outside the lifter's hands\nC. Each spotter should hold one end of the bar to help guide the bar path","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Each spotter should stand at one end of the bar and hold their hands 2-3\" under the end of the bar with the thumbs crossed","explanation_en":"It is acceptable to use either one or two spotters for the back squat. If a lift is relatively heavy for the lifter (closer to their 1RM), especially when doing max testing, using two spotters may help increase the safety of the lift. Communication is extremely important when using two spotters before and during the lift, including during the liftoff and when re-racking the bar. Spotters should avoid distractions and make sure their focus is on the lifter.\nEach spotter should stand at one end of the bar, holding their hands about 2 to 3 inches underneath the bar with their thumbs crossed. This position allows them to grab the bar quickly and safely when needed. The spotters should squat to follow the bar during the lift and should grab the bar to assist the lifter with the liftoff and with re-racking the bar.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"雙人保護深蹲時，兩名保護者分立槓鈴兩端，手放在槓鈴端頭下方約 2-3 吋、拇指交錯，以便隨時接手。"},{"id":"q1858","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A football athlete has been instructed to improve posterior chain strength. Which of the following would be a good addition to their training program?\nA. Leg raises\nB. Leg extensions\nC. Good mornings","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Good mornings","explanation_en":"The posterior chain involves the hamstrings, glutes, and erector spinae. Good mornings directly target these muscles. With a barbell on the upper back and shoulders, start with the legs almost straight. Maintaining a slight bend in the knees, bend forward by flexing forward at the hips until the torso is about parallel to the floor. Keep the back neutral at all times throughout the movement.\nLeg extensions are an isolated quadriceps exercise, and leg raises are an exercise that trains the core.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"後側鏈訓練應選 good mornings（俯身早安式），可訓練豎脊肌、臀大肌與膕繩肌。"},{"id":"q1859","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"David decides to have an ice cream cone after practice. While not the healthiest of choices, it does contain which mineral responsible for the development of strong bones?\nA. Iron\nB. Calcium\nC. Chromium","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Calcium","explanation_en":"Calcium is one of the most important minerals our body needs. It is essential for developing and maintaining healthy bones and teeth. It also assists with blood clotting, muscle contraction, and nerve transmission.\nFood sources of calcium are ice cream, yogurt, milk, and fruit juices and drinks fortified with calcium, among many others.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"冰淇淋屬乳製品，含鈣，是構成強健骨骼所需的礦物質。"},{"id":"q1860","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In which type of muscle action is the resistive force equal to the contractile force?\nA. Isometric\nB. Eccentric\nC. Concentric","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Isometric","explanation_en":"There are three types of muscle action: concentric, eccentric and isometric. In each type of muscle action, a resistive force (external force) is working to lengthen the muscle while the contractile force is working to shorten the muscle.\nWhen the contractile force is greater than the resistive force, the muscle gets shorter. This is a concentric muscle action. The lifting portion of a resistance exercise is concentric.\nWhen the resistive force is greater than the contractile force, the muscle lengthens. This is an eccentric muscle action. The lowering portion of a resistance exercise is eccentric.\nWhen the contractile force and the resistive force are equal, the muscle remains the same length while force is applied. This is an isometric muscle action.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"阻力等於收縮力、肌肉長度不變的是等長收縮（isometric）。"},{"id":"q1861","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the series of reactions in which free fatty acids are broken down, resulting in the formation of Acetyl-CoA and hydrogen protons?\nA. Glycolysis\nB. Beta oxidation\nC. Kreb's cycle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Beta oxidation","explanation_en":"Fat can be used to produce a large amount of ATP, and beta oxidation is the process by which a fatty acid can be broken down to create Acetyl-CoA and hydrogen protons which are used to create ATP in the Kreb's cycle and the electron transport chain.\nFat oxidation produces a larger amount of ATP to use as energy than either carbohydrate or protein oxidation. However, fat oxidation is also a slower process to generate ATP. Therefore, the intensity and duration of exercise may sometimes necessitate faster production of ATP.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"β-氧化（beta oxidation）把遊離脂肪酸逐步分解，生成乙醯輔酶 A（Acetyl-CoA）與氫離子。"},{"id":"q1862","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the order of the four phases involved in designing a new strength and conditioning facility?\nA. Preoperation phase, predesign phase, design phase, construction phase\nB. Predesign phase, design phase, construction phase, preoperation phase\nC. Predesign phase, preoperation phase, design phase, construction phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Predesign phase, design phase, construction phase, preoperation phase","explanation_en":"Predesign phase: development of a master plan (budget, design, operation plan, etc.) based on the needs analysis and feasibility study\nDesign phase: committee's ideas come together for structure and design\nConstruction phase: period from beginning to end of construction\nPreoperation phase: finish of interior design, hiring staff, establishing policies & procedures, or any other last steps that need to be completed before opening","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"新建訓練場館的四階段順序：預設計（predesign）→ 設計 → 施工（construction）→ 預營運（preoperation）。"},{"id":"q1863","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Where should the shoulders be placed in relation to the bar in the starting position of a power clean?\nA. The shoulders should be placed in a position that allows the torso to be upright\nB. The shoulders should be placed directly over or slightly in front of the bar\nC. The shoulders should be placed slightly behind the bar","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: The shoulders should be placed directly over or slightly in front of the bar","explanation_en":"In the starting position for a power clean, the bar should be about the level of the mid-shin. When using bumper plates, this is the height of the bar when a loaded bar is sitting on the ground.\nSome guidelines for the starting position:\n- The feet should be hip to shoulder width apart\n- The shoulders are higher than the hips, and the hips are typically higher than the knees\n- The shoulders should be either directly over or slightly forward from the bar\n- The bar should be about 1\" away from the shins\n- The feet should be flat and the torso should be neutral or have a slight arch\n- The arms should be straight\n- The torso should not be upright in the starting position.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"power clean 起始姿勢中，肩膀應位於槓鈴正上方或略前方（髖高於肩、挺胸）。"},{"id":"q1864","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following vitamins is fat soluble?\nA. Vitamin C\nB. Vitamin K\nC. Vitamin B12","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Vitamin K","explanation_en":"Vitamins are classified as either water soluble (dissolve in water) or fat soluble (dissolve in fat). There are four fat-soluble vitamins: vitamin A, vitamin D, vitamin E, and vitamin K. Most water-soluble vitamins are excreted if not used in the body, while fat-soluble vitamins are stored in body fat.\nBecause the fat-soluble vitamins are stored in the body and not excreted, it is important to ensure that intakes are not excessive, as high levels of these vitamins can be toxic.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"維生素 K 屬脂溶性（A、D、E、K）；維生素 C 與 B12 屬水溶性。"},{"id":"q1865","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the nitrogen-containing molecules that are the smallest building block for proteins in the body?\nA. Amino acids\nB. Polypeptides\nC. Complementary substances","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Correct answer: Amino acids","explanation_en":"The smallest building block for proteins are amino acid molecules. Different combinations of individual amino acids join together to make polypeptides, which then bond to form various proteins in the body.\nFour amino acids can be synthesized by the body and are therefore considered \"nonessential\" because they do not need to be consumed in the diet.\nNine amino acids are \"essential\" because the body cannot manufacture them; they must be obtained through diet.\nEight amino acids are considered conditionally essential. They become essential during times of illness and stress and at those times must be obtained through the diet.","tags":["quizlet","set:489019025"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"胺基酸是含氮、構成蛋白質的最小基本單位。"},{"id":"q1866","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"As an athlete's body size increases, which of the following describes how body mass and muscular strength change?\na. Muscular strength increases more rapidly than body mass.\nb. Body mass increases more rapidly than muscular strength.\nc. Muscular strength and body mass increase at the same rate.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Body mass increases more rapidly than muscular strength.","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"身體變大時，體重（體積，約與長度三次方成正比）的增加快於肌力（與橫斷面積、約二次方成正比），即相對肌力下降。"},{"id":"q1867","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":2,"question":"To compare performances of Olympic weightlifters of different body weights, the classic formula divides the load lifted by the athlete's\na. body weight\nb. body weight squared\nc. lean body weight\nd. body weight to the two-thirds power","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body weight to the two-thirds power","explanation_en":null,"tags":["quizlet","set:267454719","ch2"],"item_type":"flashcard","source":"quizlet","explanation_zh":"比較不同體重選手的舉重表現時，用舉起重量除以體重的 2/3 次冪（allometric 縮放）。"},{"id":"q1868","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As a strength athlete, Wendy should consume _____________grams of protein and ____________grams of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight per day.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.4-1.7g of protein 5 to 6g of carbs","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力量型運動員每日每公斤體重應攝取蛋白質約 1.4-1.7 公克、碳水約 5-6 公克。"},{"id":"q1869","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Adduction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the movement of a body part toward the midline of the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"內收（adduction）指肢體朝向身體中線的運動，與外展（abduction）相反。"},{"id":"q1870","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle fibers are long , striated,cylindrical cells approximately the diameter of a human hair (50-100 Micrometers) Many neulei are dispersed thoughout the cell, which is covered by a firous membrane celled the sacrolemma. Up to 150 muscle fibers can be bundled together into prallel fasciculi, with each fasciculus covered by perimysium (connective tissue) and each muscle fiber covered by endomysium, another type of connective tissue.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌纖維是細長、有橫紋的圓柱狀細胞，直徑約 50-100 微米，外覆肌膜（sarcolemma），細胞內散佈多個細胞核；多達 150 條肌纖維可捆成平行的肌束（fasciculi）。"},{"id":"q1871","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why strength train","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"To improve ms strength & power, bone strength, tendon & ligament strength , insulin sensitivity, LMM, ADL's, ROM, cardiovascular, metabolic rate Decrease HBP.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"做肌力訓練的目的：提升肌肉力量與功率、骨骼與肌腱韌帶強度、胰島素敏感度、瘦體重、日常生活活動能力、關節活動度、心血管與代謝率，並降低高血壓。"},{"id":"q1872","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is the specificity principal?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Train for what you want to do. Training should mimic sport or be in line with goal when possible","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"專項性原則（specificity principle）：想練成什麼就朝什麼練。訓練動作與能量系統需求應儘量模擬專項運動，並與訓練目標一致。"},{"id":"q1873","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"resistance training Program Design Variables","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. Needs analysis 2. Exercise selection 3. Training frequency 4. Exercise order 5. Training load and repetitions 6. Volume 7. Rest periods","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練程式設計的七個變數，依序為：1.需求分析 2.動作選擇 3.訓練頻率 4.動作順序 5.訓練負荷與次數 6.訓練量 7.休息間隔。設計課表時依此順序逐項決定。"},{"id":"q1874","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tendon","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fibrous connective tissue -Made of collagen -connects muscle to bone via periosteum. -Bridges muscle and bone together to produce movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌腱（tendon）：主要由膠原蛋白構成的纖維狀結締組織，經骨膜連線肌肉與骨骼，充當肌肉與骨骼間的橋梁，將肌力傳導到骨骼以產生動作。"},{"id":"q1875","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During concentric phase of the low-bar back squat, which following muscle acts as an antagonist to the glutes? Quadriceps, hamstrings, or psoas major?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Psoas major","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"低槓深蹲向心階段，臀大肌做髖伸展，而腰大肌（psoas major）是髖屈肌，因此與臀部形成拮抗；股四頭肌負責伸膝，與臀肌不構成為拮抗關係。"},{"id":"q1876","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When performing the lunge jump, the athlete should maximize which of the following? Leg (knee) flexion Jump height Shoulder extension","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Jump height","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"做弓步跳（lunge jump）時應追求最大化跳躍高度。增強式訓練重質不重量，每次跳躍的高度（爆發力輸出品質）比膝關節屈曲幅度或肩伸展更重要。"},{"id":"q1877","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What food categories do complete and incomplete proteins come from?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Complete: animal Incomplete: plant 20 amino acids, 11 the body can make, leaving 9 essential amino acids that we need from diet.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"完全蛋白質來自動物性食物（蛋、奶、肉、魚），不完全蛋白質多來自植物。人體共需20種胺基酸，其中11種可自行合成，其餘9種必需胺基酸（essential amino acids）須由飲食攝取。"},{"id":"q1878","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What work to rest ratio should be used for plyometric training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1:5","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"增強式（plyometric）訓練的用力與休息比約為1:5，充分休息才能維持伸展縮短週期（SSC）的彈性效率與動作品質。"},{"id":"q1879","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What happens in phase 1 of SSC?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The eccentric phase Preloading of agonist muscle SEC stores elastic energy, Muscle spindles are stimulated","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"SSC第一階段是離心階段：主動肌被預先負載 (preload)，系列彈性成分（SEC）被快速拉長並儲存彈效能，同時肌梭（muscle spindle）受到刺激，為接下來的向心動作做準備。"},{"id":"q1880","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the various modes of aerobic exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Cycling, running, swimming","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧運動的常見方式（mode）包括腳踏車、跑步、游泳等——皆屬可持續、有節律、大肌群參與的活動。"},{"id":"q1881","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Epimysium","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fibrous connective that covers all muscles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌外膜（epimysium）：包覆整條肌肉最外層的纖維狀結締組織。"},{"id":"q1882","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Immediate pulmonary adjustments to high altitute","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Hyperventilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"到高原後呼吸系統立即的調整是過度換氣（hyperventilation）：低氧刺激使呼吸頻率與深度增加。"},{"id":"q1883","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endurance athletes should consume _____________ g/kg body weight of protein per day, and strength athletes ______________ g/kg body weight per day.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.0 to 1.6g/kg BW per day 1.4 to 1.7 g/kg body weight per day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"蛋白質建議量：耐力型運動員每日約1.0–1.6 g/kg體重；肌力型運動員每日約1.4–1.7 g/kg體重。"},{"id":"q1884","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Absolute","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to just the actual weight of body fat even though your body is composed of both muscle and fat.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"絕對值（absolute）體脂指體脂肪的實際重量（如公斤數），不減去肌肉等其他組織；同樣重量的人體脂率可能不同，需與相對值（百分比）區分。"},{"id":"q1885","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sacrolemma","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A think elastic membrane consisting of a phospholipid bilayer (cell membrane) and an outer membrane with collagen and other structure elements, which surrounds each muscle fiber.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌膜（sarcolemma，原文拼寫Sacrolemma有誤）：包覆每條肌細胞的細胞膜，由磷脂雙分子層與含膠原蛋白等成分的外膜構成，負責傳導電訊號。"},{"id":"q1886","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Who should train","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Everyone except those under 10 years of age","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"誰該做阻力訓練：幾乎所有人都適合，除10歲以下兒童——其動作控制與專注能力尚未成熟，需特別謹慎設計。"},{"id":"q1887","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What does SAID stand for as it relates to resistance training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"S - Specific A - Adaptation to I - Imposed D - Demands","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"SAID：Specific Adaptation to Imposed Demands，專項適應性原則——人體會針對所施加的特定訓練壓力產生對應的特定適應。"},{"id":"q1888","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING FACTORS SHOULD BE DETERMINED FIRST WHEN DESIGNING A TRAINING PROGRAM FOR A SPECIFIC TEAM SPORT? a. LAYOUT OF THE FACILITY b. TYPE OF AVAILABLE EQUIPMENT c. NUMBER OF INDIVIDUALS ON THE TEAM d. METABOLIC DEMANDS OF THE ACTIVITY","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"D. METABOLIC DEMANDS OF ACTIVITY","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"為團隊運動設計訓練計畫時，最先確定的是運動的能量系統需求（metabolic demands of the activity）。這屬於需求分析第一階段，決定訓練方向，場地與器材只是後續的執行限制。"},{"id":"q1889","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle Fiber","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Long, multi-nucleated and striated myocytes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌纖維（muscle fiber）：細長、多核、具橫紋的肌細胞（myocyte）。"},{"id":"q1890","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following muscle groups and types of muscle actions are associated with the downward phase of the dumbbell biceps curl?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Elbow flexors, eccentric","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"啞鈴二頭彎舉的下放（還原）階段：肘屈肌（肱二頭肌等）在做離心動作——在負載下被拉長，同時控制動作速度。"},{"id":"q1891","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following backpedaling techniques is most appropriate? Greater range of motion at the knee joint Smaller range of motion at the hip joint Initiate arm movement at the elbows","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Smaller range of motion at the hip joint which of","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"倒退跑的正確技術：髖關節動作幅度較小，步幅小而快、重心穩定，避免跨步過大導致重心失控。"},{"id":"q1892","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following will improve the most with creatine monohydrate supplementation? 100m sprint time, Squat strength Or volleyball jump performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Squat strength","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"一水肌酸（creatine monohydrate）對深蹲最大肌力的改善最明顯——肌酸增加肌肉磷酸肌酸儲備，最直接幫助最大肌力與短時間高強度輸出。"},{"id":"q1893","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Define liability.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A legal responsibility, duty or obligation. A duty to help prevent injury","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"法律責任（liability）：法律上的責任、職責或義務，例如體能教練有防止學員受傷的注意義務。"},{"id":"q1894","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Strength load, goal reps/sets and rest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"> 85% 1RM < 6 reps, 2-6 sets Rest: 2-5 minutes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最大肌力訓練引數：負荷大於85% 1RM，次數少於6次，2–6組，組間休息2–5分鐘。"},{"id":"q1895","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are various modes of anaerobic exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Core, multi-joint, assistance, sport specific","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"此題庫答案將答案配對為阻力訓練動作的分類：核心（core）、多關節、輔助（assistance）、專項動作。有氧運動的方式（mode）則指跑步、單車、游泳等活動型別。"},{"id":"q1896","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bone Periosteum","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Outer part of bone Where muscle tendon attaches to the bone","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"骨膜（periosteum）：骨骼的外層組織，是肌肉肌腱附著於骨骼的部位。"},{"id":"q1897","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Immediate acid-base adjustments to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body fluids become more alkaline due to reductions in CO2 with hyperventilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的立即酸鹼調整：過度換氣排出過多CO2，血液碳酸減少，體液偏鹼（呼吸性鹼中毒）。"},{"id":"q1898","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"athletes who want to maintain muscle and lose body fat while dieting should consume about ___________ to _________ g protein/kg BW per day in addition to a moderate energy deficit of approx ________ calories/day","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"consumer about 1.8 to 2.7 g of protein ~500 calories/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"減重期間想保住肌肉的運動員：攝取約1.8–2.7 g/kg體重的蛋白質，並配合每日約500大卡的適度熱量赤字。"},{"id":"q1899","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Abduction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to movement of a body away from the midline of the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"外展（abduction）：肢體遠離身體中線的動作。"},{"id":"q1900","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Scaroplasm","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sacroplasm is filled with myofibrils ans contain the components require for muscle contraction, including verious proteins, protein filaments, mitochondria, the sacoplasmic reticulum,store glucogen, enzyme and ions.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌漿（sarcoplasm，原文拼寫有誤）：肌細胞的細胞質，充滿肌原纖維，並含有收縮所需的各種蛋白質、蛋白絲、粒線體、肌漿網、肝糖、酶與離子。"},{"id":"q1901","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are some safety precautions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"See MD for physical Proper clothing & shoes Previous injuries Consult a trainer Take it slow","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"開始訓練前的安全注意事項：先經醫師體檢許可、穿適當的服裝與鞋子、告知舊傷史、諮詢專業教練、循序漸進不冒進。"},{"id":"q1902","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is the overload principal?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Optimal adaptation occurs when training is done at the upper limit of the bodies ability","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"超負荷原則（overload principle）：最佳適應發生在訓練負荷接近身體目前能力上限時——施加的壓力必須超過日常習慣的水準，身體才會向上適應。"},{"id":"q1903","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"THE SC PROFESSIONAL'S INITIAL TASK IS TO PERFORM A:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"NEEDS ANALYSIS-2 STAGE PROCESS THAT INCLUDES AN EVALUATION OF THE REQUIREMENTS AND CHARACTERISTICS OF THE SPORT AND AN ASSESSMENT OF THE ATHLETE","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"體能教練的首要任務是需求分析（needs analysis）：兩階段流程——評估運動專案的需求與特性，以及評估運動員本身的狀況。"},{"id":"q1904","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Fasciculi","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Bundled muscle fibers up to 150 individual strands","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌束（fasciculi）：由多條肌纖維聚整合束，一束最多約含150條肌纖維，外覆肌束膜（perimysium）。"},{"id":"q1905","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following rest periods is most appropriate for a middle distance runner performing 800m running intervals in 2 min? 2-4- or 6","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"6 min","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"以2分鐘完成800m間歇跑的中距離跑者，應休息6分鐘——接近VO2max強度的間歇訓練，用力與休息比約1:3，休息不足無法維持目標強度。"},{"id":"q1906","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following best describes the hamstrings during the contract-relax PNF technique? Active, 10 sec Passive, 10 sec Passive, 30 sec","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Passive 10 sec","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收縮-放鬆法（contract-relax PNF）中，膕繩肌在伸展姿勢下先被動保持約10秒，再進入等長收縮與 更大深度的伸展的迴圈。"},{"id":"q1907","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is an appropriate recommendation for fluid intake before a collegiate soccer match?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":".5 liter 2 hours before match","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"大學足球賽前的補水建議：開賽前2小時喝約0.5升水，給身體足夠時間排除多餘水分。"},{"id":"q1908","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Define negligence","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Failure to act as a reasonable and prudent person would under similar circumstances. Four elements must exist: Duty, breach of duty, proximate cause, and damages","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"過失（negligence）：未盡合理謹慎之人在相同情況下應盡的注意。構成過失須具備四要件：義務、違反義務、直接因果關係、損害。"},{"id":"q1909","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Power load, reps/sets, rest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Single effort : 80-90% 1-2 reps Multiple: 75-85% 3-5 reps 3-5 sets Rest: 2-5 minutes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力（功率）訓練引數：單次用力專案80–90% 1RM、1–2次；多次用力專案75–85% 1RM、3–5次、3–5組；組間休息2–5分鐘。"},{"id":"q1910","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the various modes of resistance training exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Core, multi-joint, assistance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練動作依目的分類：核心動作（core）與輔助動作（assistance）等；核心動作涉及大肌群與多關節，優先安排。"},{"id":"q1911","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Proximal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Closer to the Trunk","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"近端（proximal）：解剖位置術語，指離軀幹或身體中心較近。"},{"id":"q1912","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Immediate cardiovascular adjustments to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Cardiac output increases submax HR increases","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"到高原後心血管的立即調整：心輸出量增加、次最大強度運動時心率上升，以補償每單位血液攜氧能力下降。"},{"id":"q1913","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A high-quality protein is one that...","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Contains all of the essential amino acids. Animal products are the primary source. Soy is the plant source that can provide all the essentials","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高品質蛋白質：含全部必需胺基酸的蛋白質。動物性食品是主要來源；大豆是能提供全部必需胺基酸的植物性來源。"},{"id":"q1914","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to conditions or processes that occur in the presence of, or requiring oxygen.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧（aerobic）：指在有氧存在下發生、或需要氧氣參與的條件與過程。"},{"id":"q1915","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sacroplasmic reticulum","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Scroplasmic reticulum is a network of tubular channels and vesicles, which together provide structual intergrity to the muscle fiber. The muscle fiber. Influx of Ca2+ ions from the sarcoplasm into the muscle fiber results from an action potential in the sacromere, causing the depolarization that initiates muscle movement.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌漿網（sarcoplasmic reticulum）：由管狀通道與囊泡構成的網路，為肌纖維提供結構支撐；動作電位刺激後釋出Ca2+進入肌纖維，引發去極化與肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q1916","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Antagonist","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Direct opposite of agonist. Ms is resting while agonist is performing.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"拮抗肌（antagonist）：與主動肌（agonist）作用方向相反的肌肉；主動肌收縮時它多處於放鬆或被拉長的狀態。"},{"id":"q1917","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are some ways of inducing overload?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) increasing load 2) increasing reps 3) increasing # of training sessions 4) adding exercises 5) adding sets 6) decreasing rest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"製造超負荷的方法：1)增加負荷 2)增加次數 3)增加訓練次數 4)增加動作 5)增加組數 6)縮短休息間隔。"},{"id":"q1918","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"in the evaluation of sport in the needs analysis what should the SC evaluate:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"-Body and limb movement patterns and muscular involvement (movement analysis) -strength, power, hypertrophy and muscular endurance priorities (injury analysis) -common sites for join and muscle injury and cause factors (injury analysis)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"需求分析中評估運動專案時應分析：動作分析（身體與四肢動作模式及肌肉參與）、體能需求優先順序（肌力、功率、肥大、肌耐力的輕重緩急）、傷害分析（常見受傷部位與致傷原因）。"},{"id":"q1919","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Perimysium","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Connective tissue that sound fasciculi","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌束膜（perimysium）：包覆每個肌束（fasciculi）的結締組織。"},{"id":"q1920","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"As compared to males, the potential for force production of females per muscle cross-sectional area is:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Similar","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女性每單位肌肉橫截面積的最大產力潛力與男性相似（similar）；兩性絕對肌力差異主要來自肌肉總量與體脂分佈，而非單位面積的肌力品質。"},{"id":"q1921","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A sprinter runs with too little height of the swing leg knee. Which of the following is most appropriate to recommend? Use a longer push-off with each stride. Emphasize development of SSC Increase stride length to allow greater ROM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Emphasize development of SSC","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"跑者跑步時擺動腿膝蓋抬升高度不足，最合適的建議是著重發展伸展縮短週期（SSC）——改善觸地回彈與抬腿效率，而非單純加大步幅或蹬伸。"},{"id":"q1922","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is participating in an aerobic endurance event lasting an hour. Which of the following beverages is most important? 55 degrees 6% 65 degrees 10% 75 degrees 14%","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"55 degrees 6% carbohydrate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"持續一小時的有氧耐力專案，宜選擇55°F（約13°C）、6%碳水化合物濃度的運動飲料——低溫加快胃排空，約6%濃度兼顧補水與糖分吸收。"},{"id":"q1923","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is an adequate temperature range for a facility?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"72-78 degrees","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練場館的適宜溫度範圍為72–78°F（約22–26°C）。"},{"id":"q1924","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hypertrophy load, sets/reps, and rest recommendation.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"67-85% 6-12 reps 3-6 sets Rest 30-1.5m","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌肥大訓練引數：67–85% 1RM、6–12次、3–6組、組間休息30秒至1分半鐘（原始答案尾端有亂碼，標準休息為30秒–1.5分鐘）。"},{"id":"q1925","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the various modes of flexibility training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Active and passive stretching, ballistic stretch, static stretch, dynamic stretch","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"柔軟度訓練的方式：主動伸展、被動伸展、彈震式伸展（ballistic）、靜態伸展、動態伸展。"},{"id":"q1926","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Distal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Farther from the Trunk","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"遠端（distal）：解剖位置術語，指離軀幹或身體中心較遠。"},{"id":"q1927","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Long term pulmonary adjustments to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase in ventilation rate stabilizers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的長期呼吸適應：通氣速率上升後逐漸穩定（習服），維持較高的通氣水平以補償低氧。"},{"id":"q1928","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anabolic Steroids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"synthetic hormones that mimic testosterone and promote muscle growth. Creatine is produced naturally in the body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"同化類固醇（anabolic steroids）：模仿睪固酮的合成激素，促進肌肉生長。（原答案附帶「肌酸為人體天然合成」與本題無直接關聯。）"},{"id":"q1929","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic Capacity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The total amount of work that can be performed by the aerobic energy system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧容量（aerobic capacity）：有氧能量系統所能完成的總功量。"},{"id":"q1930","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Myofibril","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cocsist of long thin chain proteins actin, myosin, titan. Bunches if myfibril and nuclei together make a muscle fiber.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌原纖維（myofibril）：由肌動蛋白、肌球蛋白、連線蛋白（titin）等細長鏈狀蛋白構成；成束的肌原纖維與細胞核共同組成肌纖維。"},{"id":"q1931","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Levering System","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Joints form the pivot rotationused to move the wt Lever joint The further the wt is from the joint, the more force that is created","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"槓桿系統：骨骼肌動作中關節充當支點（fulcrum）產生旋轉來移動負載；負載離關節越遠，力臂越長，需要的力就越大。"},{"id":"q1932","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Wjat are the 7 key variable s (Steps) of progrsm desgin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Needs Analysis 2) Exercise Selection 3) Training Frequency 4) Exercise Order 5) Training Load & Repititions 6) Volume 7) Rest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"程式設計的七個關鍵步驟：1.需求分析 2.動作選擇 3.訓練頻率 4.動作順序 5.訓練負荷與次數 6.訓練量 7.休息。"},{"id":"q1933","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"1. When determining a baseball player’s resistance training program needs, all of the following factors should be considered EXCEPT a) Programs of other players b) Past medical history c) Training status d) Position on the field","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a. programs of other players","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"決定棒球選手阻力訓練需求時，最不必考慮的是「其他選手的計畫」——訓練應個體化；過往病史、訓練狀態、守備位置都直接影響需求分析。"},{"id":"q1934","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endomysium","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Surrounds each muscle fiber","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌內膜（endomysium）：包覆每一條個別肌纖維的薄層結締組織。"},{"id":"q1935","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What cardiovascular adaptation to chronic aerobic exercise contributes the most to improved aerobic endurance performance?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased maximal cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"長期有氧運動造成的心血管適應中，最大心輸出量（maximal cardiac output）增加對改善有氧耐力表現貢獻最大。"},{"id":"q1936","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is transitioning from a backpedal to forward sprint, what initiates the movement? Head Hips Feet","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Head","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"從倒退跑轉換到向前衝刺時，動作由頭部（head）發起——頭先轉向新方向，軀幹與四肢隨後跟進，帶動重心轉移。"},{"id":"q1937","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1 pound of fat is equal to how many calories?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3,500 calories","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"1磅脂肪約等於3,500大卡——這是估算減重速度（如每週減1磅需每日赤字約500大卡）的計算基礎。"},{"id":"q1938","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the minimum distance between flow and bottom of wall mirror?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"20 inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"牆面鏡子下緣與地板之間至少保留20英吋的距離，避免槓鈴、啞鈴撞擊鏡面。"},{"id":"q1939","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscular endurance load, sets/reps, and rest recommendation.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"12 reps 2-3 sets Rest: < 30 sec","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌耐力訓練引數：12次以上（低於67% 1RM）、2–3組、組間休息少於30秒。"},{"id":"q1940","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Under what circumstances would a particular mode of exercise be chosen?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Activities that mimic as closely as possible the movement pattern employed in competition","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"選擇運動方式的依據是專項性：越能精確模擬比賽動作模式的練習，訓練效果轉移到競賽表現的程度越高。"},{"id":"q1941","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Superior","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Closer to the head","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"上方（superior）：解剖位置術語，指離頭部較近、位置較高。"},{"id":"q1942","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"long term acid-base adjustment to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"excretion of HCO3 by kidneys w/concomitant reduction in alkaline reserve","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的長期酸鹼適應：腎臟增加排出碳酸氫根（HCO3-），降低鹼儲備，以代償呼吸性鹼中毒、使血液pH迴歸正常。"},{"id":"q1943","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why should alcohol be avoided after a training session or competition?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"It impairs muscle protein synthesis. Protein synthesis is crucial for the repairment of muscle tissue and growth","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練或比賽後應避免酒精：它會損害肌肉蛋白質合成，而蛋白質合成是肌肉組織修復與生長的關鍵。"},{"id":"q1944","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic Fitness","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The ability to perform prolonged periods of work without getting tired. Durin aerobic exercise, you should be able to carry on a conversation.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧適能（aerobic fitness）：長時間工作而不疲勞的能力。做有氧運動時應仍能說話（談話測試），否則代表強度過高。"},{"id":"q1945","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Myofilament","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Myofilament containing actine and myosin and are the smaller components of the myofibrils within striated muscle fibers. A scarcomers is a composed of myofilaments.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌微絲（myofilament）：含肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白的細結構，是橫紋肌肌原纖維內更小的組成單位；肌小節（sarcomere）即由肌微絲構成。"},{"id":"q1946","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tendons","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Connect bone and muscle Transfer force developed by muscle to skeletal system","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌腱（tendons）：連線肌肉與骨骼，將肌肉產生的力量傳導給骨骼系統以產生動作。"},{"id":"q1947","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is involved on the first step (Needs Analysis) of program desgin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 stages: 1. Evaluate Sport/Goal - physiological/biomechanical profile - common injuries - position specific attributes 2. Athlete Profile - Look at training/injury status - testing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"需求分析（第一步）含兩個階段：1.評估運動/目標——生理與生物力學特徵、常見傷害、位置專項屬性；2.運動員分析——訓練史與受傷狀況、各項測試結果。"},{"id":"q1948","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"what is the 2nd task of the needs analysis (step 1)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"assessment of the athlete -profile the needs/goals from eval of training status, doing a variety of testing, eval results and determine primary goals","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"需求分析的第二項任務是評估運動員：依訓練狀態建立需求與目標檔案、實施各類體測、評估結果並決定主要訓練目標。"},{"id":"q1949","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type I fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Slow twitch -Oxidative fibers -Engaged during long duration activities -Low levels of force -fatigue resistant","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一類肌纖維：慢縮氧化型，用於長時間、低力量輸出的活動，抗疲勞，主要負責耐力型表現。"},{"id":"q1950","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following events occurs in the hamstring muscles (on a myofibril level) during the concentric muscle action of the leg (knee) curl exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The H zone length decreases","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"屈膝腿彎舉的向心收縮時，膕繩肌肌原纖維內的H帶長度變短——依據滑動肌絲理論，肌小節縮短時H帶與I帶都隨肌動蛋白滑入而縮短（原始答案前段混入其他文字）。"},{"id":"q1951","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the difference between valgus and varus knees?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Valgus- knees bow in, knock kneed Varus- knees bow out","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"膝外翻（valgus）：雙膝向內夾、呈X形（knock-kneed）；膝內翻（varus）：雙膝向外彎、呈O形。深蹲時膝內夾即valgus，是常見的損傷風險姿態。"},{"id":"q1952","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At what percentage of weight loss due to dehydration will core body temperature potentially begin to increase and affect performance?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"因脫水流失達體重的2%時，核心體溫可能開始上升並影響運動表現——補水應以維持體重下降不超過2%為目標。"},{"id":"q1953","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What staff-athlete ratio is recommended for S&C facilities?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1:20 1:15 for high schools 1:10 for younger kids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"場館教練與運動員比例建議：一般1:20；高中1:15；年齡更小的兒童1:10，以確保指導品質與安全。"},{"id":"q1954","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is repetition training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Training above vo2 max 30-90 seconds Long recovery, 1:5 ratio","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"重複訓練法（repetition training）：強度高於VO2max對應強度，每次30–90秒，組間長時間恢復，用力與休息比約1:5，主要改善速度與無氧能力。"},{"id":"q1955","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does resistance training load and volume relate to the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strength ≥85% of 1RM, ≤6 reps. Power single event 80-90% of 1RM, 1-2 reps. Power multi event 75-85% of 1RM, 3-5 reps. Hypertrophy 67-80% of 1RM, 8-12 reps (novice goal; 6-12 intermediate, 3-12 advanced). Muscular Endurance <67% of 1RM, 12+ reps. Sets: 1-3 for novices, ≥3 for intermediate and advanced","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷與訓練量須與目標對應（5e 第18章表18.11，p1237–1238；表18.13，p1248）：肌力 ≥85% 1RM×≤6 次；功率單次 80–90%×1–2 次（p1240）、多次 75–85%×3–5 次；肥大 67–80%×8–12 次（初階目標；中階 6–12、高階 3–12）；肌耐力 <67%×≥12 次；組數初階 1–3 組、中階以上 ≥3 組。"},{"id":"q1956","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Inferior","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Closer to the feet","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"下方（inferior）：解剖位置術語，指離腳部較近、位置較低。"},{"id":"q1957","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"long term cardio adjustment to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"continued elevation in submax HR decrease stroke volume at rest lowered max hr lowered max cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的長期心血管調整：次最大心率持續偏高、靜息心跳量下降、最大心率下降、最大心輸出量下降。"},{"id":"q1958","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Nutrient-dense foods","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Foods with nutrients such as vitamins, minerals, and fiber, as well as healthy plant-based compounds that they provide. ex: milk, vegetables, protein foods, grains","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高營養密度食物：每單位熱量提供較多維生素、礦物質、膳食纖維與有益植物化合物，如牛奶、蔬菜、優質蛋白質、全穀物。"},{"id":"q1959","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ambient Heart Rate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Your heart rate during the day when you aren't really doing anything, but it's not truly resting either. Take it at the same time in the same circumstances, daily.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"環境心率（ambient heart rate）：白天輕度活動狀態下的心率——不是真正的靜息心率；應每天在同一時間、相同條件下量測以作趨勢參考。"},{"id":"q1960","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sacromere","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Smallest functional untie of a muscle fiber, a sarcomer contains the actin and myosin protein responsible for the mechanical prpcess of muscle contractions. Located between two Z-lines. actin and myosin filaments are configured in parallel, end to end, along with entire length of the alternating light and dark pattern of skeletal muscle seen histrologically. The scrcomere has four defined segments: A-band,H-zone, I-band, and Z-line.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌小節（sarcomere，原文拼寫有誤）：肌纖維的最小功能單位，位於兩條Z線之間，含肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白，構成骨骼肌明暗相間的橫紋；分為A帶、H帶、I帶、Z線四個區段。"},{"id":"q1961","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ligaments","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Connect bone to bone Found around primary joints","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"韌帶（ligaments）：連線骨與骨的結締組織，分佈於主要關節周圍，提供關節穩定性。"},{"id":"q1962","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How do you determine an individuals training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Determine injury status and history 2) Past training history/experiance - Type of program - length of training - Intensity - Exercise technique experiance 3) Physical testing - Body comp, flexilbility, strength, power, endurance, 1rm 4) Determine Goals - ex: strength, power, hypertrophy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"判定個人訓練狀態：1.確認受傷狀況與病史；2.過往訓練經歷（計畫型別、年限、強度、動作技術經驗）；3.體適能測試（體組成、柔軟度、肌力、功率、耐力、1RM）；4.確認訓練目標。"},{"id":"q1963","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING IS THE MOST SPORT-SPECIFIC EXERCISE FOR A SPRINTER? a. DUMBBELL LUNGE b. UPRIGHT ROW c. ANKLE DORSIFLEXION d. LEG (KNEE) CURL","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"DUMBBELL LUNGE","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"對短跑選手而言最專項的動作是啞鈴弓步（dumbbell lunge）——單腿、多關節、矢狀面發力，與跑步動作模式最接近。"},{"id":"q1964","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIa fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fast oxidative and glycolytic -fast twitch -Medium amounts of force -highly fatigue resistant.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二類a型肌纖維：快縮氧化糖解型，快速收縮，可產生中等力量，抗疲勞度高，兼具有氧與無氧代謝能力。"},{"id":"q1965","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Depletion of which of the following fuel sources hinders marathon performance most?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle glycogen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌肉肝糖（muscle glycogen）耗盡對馬拉鬆表現影響最大——長時間跑步以肝糖為主要燃料，耗盡即出現「撞牆」（bonking）。"},{"id":"q1966","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"On a treadmill, how do you best mimic outdoor pace?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Same pace as outdoor, slight incline of 1%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"在跑步機上要模擬戶外跑步：用與戶外相同的速度，並把坡度調高約1%，以補償跑步機缺少空氣阻力與路面驅動的差異。"},{"id":"q1967","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is a potential sign of bulimia nervosa in terms of frequency and timeline?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Binge-eating and purging at least once a week for 3 months or more.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"神經性貪食症的徵候：每週至少一次暴食後清除（催吐等）的行為，持續3個月以上。"},{"id":"q1968","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following will optimize traffic flow in a strength and conditioning facility? Pathways with a width of 24in Arrangement of the equipment Spacing equipment at least 36in apart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Spacing equipment at least 36in apart","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最佳化場館動線的關鍵是器材間至少保持36英吋的間距；24英吋的通道過窄，器材排列方式不如間距數值來得具體。"},{"id":"q1969","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the series elastic component (SEC)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The workhorse of plyo metric exercise. Tendons make up majority of SEC SEC acts as a spring and is lengthened quickly. When lengthened, muscle spindles activate and energy is stored.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"系列彈性成分（SEC）是增強式訓練的「主力」：肌腱佔SEC的大部分，像彈簧一樣——被快速拉長時刺激肌梭並儲存彈效能，隨後釋放以增強收縮。"},{"id":"q1970","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does aerobic training intensity relate to the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The higher the exercise intensity the shorter the exercise duration. Monitoring VO2max compared to O2 consumption is the best measure of intensity.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練強度與時間的關係：強度越高，可持續時間越短；監控強度的最佳指標是攝氧量相對於VO2max的百分比。"},{"id":"q1971","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Origin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Proximal (towards the center) attachment of a muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"起點（origin）：肌肉的近端附著點（靠身體中心一側），收縮時通常較固定。"},{"id":"q1972","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hematologic long term adjustments to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase red cell production increase viscocity increase hematocrit decreased plasma volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的長期血液適應：紅血球生成增加、血細胞比容上升、血液黏滯度增加、血漿量減少。"},{"id":"q1973","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"LDL cholesterol levels","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Optimal: 190","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"LDL（低密度脂蛋白）參考值：原答案「190」指臨界區間——LDL 130–190 mg/dL為臨界偏高、大於等於190為偏高，理想值應低於100 mg/dL。"},{"id":"q1974","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Amino Acids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refer to the building blocks of protein.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"胺基酸（amino acids）：構成蛋白質的基本單位（ building blocks），共20種，其中9種為必需胺基酸。"},{"id":"q1975","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A-band","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"contain actin and myosin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"A帶：同時含有肌動蛋白細肌絲與肌球蛋白粗肌絲（兩者重疊區）的區段，顯微鏡下呈暗色。"},{"id":"q1976","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Fascia","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Runs through muscle connecting other muscles, forming the tendon","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"筋膜（fascia）：貫穿肌肉、連線各肌肉的結締組織，向外匯聚形成肌腱。"},{"id":"q1977","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is involved in the second step (exercise selection) of resistance training program desgin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Consider goals, exercise type, and past experiance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"程式設計第二步（動作選擇）的考量：訓練目標、動作型別（核心/輔助等）、運動員過去的訓練經驗。"},{"id":"q1978","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"exercises that recruit one or more large muscle areas, involve two or more primary joints (multijoint exercises), and receive priority when one is selecting exercises because of their direct application to the sport","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"core exercises","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"核心動作（core exercises）：動員一個以上大肌群、涉及兩個以上主要關節的多關節動作；因與專項直接相關，在動作選擇時優先安排。"},{"id":"q1979","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIb","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fast glycolytic -fast twitch -large amount of force -Fast fatigue","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二類b型肌纖維：快縮糖解型，快速收縮，可產生很大的力量輸出，但極易疲勞（人體中對應型態多稱IIx）。"},{"id":"q1980","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following muscle actions produces the greatest amount of muscle force? Eccentric, concentric, isometric","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Eccentric","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"離心動作能產生最大的肌肉力量——相同負荷下，離心收縮可承受的力大於向心與等長收縮，這也是離心訓練能使用更大負荷的原因。"},{"id":"q1981","part":2,"domain":"Exercise Technique","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"With the handgrip outside of the shoulders, what is increased?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Stability","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Technique"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"臥推等動作採用寬於肩的握距可增加穩定性——支撐面較寬、動作行程較短，軀幹與肩關節較穩，可操作較大重量。"},{"id":"q1982","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An 18 year old male college baseball player is 5’10 and weighs 165. He wants to increase muscle mass and strength. What is the appropriate intake of protein?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"462 kcal/ day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"75公斤（165磅）的大學棒球選手想增加肌肉量：蛋白質約1.4–1.7 g/kg/日；題答案462大卡是把每日蛋白質換算成熱量（約115–116 g × 4大卡/克）。"},{"id":"q1983","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is most appropriate for an assistant strength and conditioning professional to perform? Provide appropriate nutritional recommendations Properly instruct exercise technique Purchase equipment for the facility","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Properly instruct exercise technique","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"助理體能教練最適合承擔的任務是正確指導動作技術；提供營養建議與採購器材通常屬於主任教練的職責。"},{"id":"q1984","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Order of sprint phases at maximal velocity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Flight (nonsupport) early-mid and late 2) forward support 3) rear support (leg drive is facilitated by explosive arm)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最大速度衝刺各階段的順序：1.騰空期（非支撐，分早、中、晚騰空）2.前支撐期（frontside）3.後支撐期（backside）——爆發性擺臂有助於腿部驅動。"},{"id":"q1985","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does the interval training work:rest ratio relate to the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Work:rest ratio is 1:1. Work intervals should be 3-5 minutes and involves exercises at an intensity close to VO2max","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"間歇訓練法：用力與休息比1:1，每次工作區間3–5分鐘，強度接近VO2max，主要用於提升有氧能力。"},{"id":"q1986","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Insertion","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Distal (away from center) attachment of a muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"止點（insertion）：肌肉的遠端附著點（離身體中心較遠一側），收縮時通常是移動的一端。"},{"id":"q1987","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"long term tissue adaptions to high altitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase capillary density increase number of mitochondria increase use of free fatty acids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高原的長期組織適應：微血管密度增加、粒線體數量增加、遊離脂肪酸利用率提高，改善區域性攝氧與有氧代謝。"},{"id":"q1988","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Increased ________ levels can lead to increased risk of heart disease. Whereas increased __________ levels can lead actually be beneficial and help protect against heart disease","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased LDL Levels Increased HDL levels","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"LDL（低密度脂蛋白，俗稱壞膽固醇）過高增加心臟病風險；HDL（高密度脂蛋白，好膽固醇）較高則有益，能幫助清除血管膽固醇、保護心血管。"},{"id":"q1989","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anaerobic Exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An exercise done for a short period of time usually 1 to 2 minutes, develops speed but does not develop overall fitness.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"無氧運動：持續時間短（約1–2分鐘內）的高強度運動，主要發展速度與功率，對整體有氧適能的提升有限。"},{"id":"q1990","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"H-zone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"located in the center of the sacromere within the A-band, contains only myosin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"H帶：位於肌小節中央、A帶之內，只含肌球蛋白粗肌絲，不含肌動蛋白。"},{"id":"q1991","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"College Fiber","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Protein fiber found throughout the body providing strength and cushion.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"膠原纖維（collagen fiber，原文誤植College Fiber）：遍佈全身的蛋白質纖維，提供強度與緩衝支撐。"},{"id":"q1992","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are core exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Exervises that recruit one or more large muscle areas. (Ex: chest, back, shoulders) - Involve 2 or more primary joints - Get priority during exercise selection","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"核心動作：動員一個以上大肌群區域（胸、背、肩等）、涉及兩個以上主要關節，動作選擇時優先納入。"},{"id":"q1993","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"exercises that recruit smaller muscle areas, involve only one primary joint, and are considered less important to improving sport performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"assistance exercises","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"輔助動作（assistance exercises）：動員較小的肌群、只涉及一個主要關節，對提升專項運動的貢獻較次要。"},{"id":"q1994","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolysis or Glycolytic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Glycolysis is the first stage, and takes place in the cell cytosol. During this stage, one glucose molecule is broken down into two pyruvates. Energy generated in glycolysis is stored in the form of both NADH and ATP. Two molecules of NADH and two molecules of ATP are produced from glycolysis of one glucose molecule.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"糖解（glycolysis）：能量代謝第一階段，發生在細胞質基質；1分子葡萄糖分解為2分子丙酮酸，同時生成2分子ATP與2分子NADH。"},{"id":"q1995","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following exercises is an example of a first-class lever?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Triceps push down","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"三頭肌下壓屬於第一類槓桿：肘關節（支點）位於力點（三頭肌附著）與抗力點（手中負重的）之間，類似蹺蹺板的構造。"},{"id":"q1996","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the daily fat requirements in percentage and grams after prolonged exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"At least 20% 2g/kg BW is required to replenish triglycerides after prolonged endurance of 2+ hours.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"長時間運動（2小時以上耐力運動）後的脂肪補充：至少佔總熱量20%，約2 g/kg體重，以幫助回補三酸甘油酯儲備。"},{"id":"q1997","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A new collegiate athlete wants to use the S&C facility. Most importantly, they must first: Obtain clearance from the sports medicine staff Sign a release agreement form prior to using the facility. Attend an orientation session for familiarization.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Obtain clearance from medical staff first Other two are important but come after.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"大學運動員首次使用體能場館，最重要的第一步是取得運動醫學（醫療）團隊的放行許可；簽署同意書與場館導覽雖重要，但排在醫療許可之後。"},{"id":"q1998","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What element of agility requires spatial and temporal control of body movements?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Orientation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"方向定位（orientation）：敏捷能力中要求對身體動作做空間與時間控制的部分——掌握自身與對手、場地之間的相對位置。"},{"id":"q1999","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How should resistance training and plyometric training be applied together in a training program?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Combine lower body resistance with upper body plyo and vise versa. Complex training can be incorporated with combines heavy resistance with plyo but must follow some strict guidelines. See page 423","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練與增強式訓練的搭配：上下肢交錯（下肢阻力配增強式上肢，反之亦然）；複合式訓練（大重量阻力緊接增強式）可行但須嚴格遵守強度與休息的規範。"},{"id":"q2000","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Myofilaments","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Myosin Actin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌微絲（myofilaments）分兩種：肌球蛋白（myosin，粗肌絲）與肌動蛋白（actin，細肌絲）。"},{"id":"q2001","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Markers of aerobic overtraining","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decrease performance decrease % BF decrease VO@ Altered BP muscle soreness decrease muscle glycogen altered resting HR +HRV decreased lactate increased creatine kinase altered cortisol + testosterone changes in mood states decrease performance in psychomotor speed tests","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧過度訓練的指標：表現下降、體脂率下降、VO2max下降、血壓異常、肌肉痠痛、肌肝糖下降、靜息心率與心率變異度改變、血乳酸下降、肌酸激酶上升、皮質醇與睪固酮變化、情緒狀態改變、心理動作速度測試表現下降。"},{"id":"q2002","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycemic Index","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"guideline for how quickly different carbohydrates digest and therefore raise blood glucose levels.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"血糖生成指數（glycemic index, GI）：衡量不同碳水化合物被消化吸收、升高血糖速度與幅度的指標。"},{"id":"q2003","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Antioxidants","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refer to the specific vitamins, minerals, and nutrients that protect the body against free radicals.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"抗氧化劑（antioxidants）：能保護身體免受自由基傷害的特定維生素、礦物質與營養素，如維生素C、E。"},{"id":"q2004","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"I-band","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"contains only actin filaments and consists of two connected sarcomeres on either side of the Z-line","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"I帶：只含肌動蛋白細肌絲的區段，橫跨Z線兩側、分屬兩個相鄰肌小節的部分，呈亮色。"},{"id":"q2005","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Eccentric","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Lowering phase The slower the return, against resistance the more power you'll build.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"離心（eccentric）：放下的階段。對抗阻力越慢地回到起點，產生的張力與訓練刺激越大，越能建立力量。"},{"id":"q2006","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are assistance exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Recruit small muscle groups (ex: calf, low back, upper arm) - Involve one primary joint - Secondary priority - More often used for injury prevention and rehab","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"輔助動作：招募較小肌群（小腿、下背、上臂）、只涉及一個主要關節，屬次優先；較常用於傷害預防與康復。"},{"id":"q2007","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"a core exercise that emphasizes loading the spine directly (back squat) or indirectly (power clean) can be further described as?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"structural exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"結構動作（structural exercise）：對脊柱施加直接（背蹲）或間接（動力清潔）負荷、需要肌肉穩定姿勢的核心動作，是核心動作的子類別。"},{"id":"q2008","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcoplasm","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Cytoplasm where essential elements of muscular contraction are located such as glycogen,fat,various enzymes,mitochondria, and the sarcoplasmic reticulum.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌漿（sarcoplasm）：肌細胞的細胞質，內含肌肉收縮所需的重要成分——肝糖、脂肪、各種酶、粒線體與肌漿網。"},{"id":"q2009","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following muscle actions precedes a counter movement jump?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Eccentric loading","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"反向跳動（counter movement jump）之前先發生離心負荷——快速下蹲預拉肌肉，利用伸展縮短週期儲存彈效能，接著才爆發起跳。"},{"id":"q2010","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Protein requirements in percentage and for athletes in grams.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"10-35% 1.5-1.7 g/kg BW per day 20g protein per snack recommended High protein diets offer no benefit to athletes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"蛋白質建議：佔總熱量10–35%；運動員約1.5–1.7 g/kg/日；每份點心約含20 g蛋白質即可；超過建議量的高蛋白飲食對運動員無額外效益。"},{"id":"q2011","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The humidity in the facility should be no greater than:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"60%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練場館相對溼度不應超過60%。"},{"id":"q2012","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why should endurance athletes avoid erythropoietin use?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Because it may cause unregulated increase in red blood cell production.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"耐力運動員應避免使用紅血球生成素（EPO）：它可能造成紅血球無節制地增生，使血液過濃、黏滯度上升，增加心血管意外風險。"},{"id":"q2013","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are positive and negative effects of combining different training modes in a training program?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Injuries, overtraining, loss of power or speed are some negatives. Helps with sports that have an aerobic and anaerobic component, prepares athletes for competition more realistically.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"多種訓練模式並行的負面影響：受傷、過度訓練、功率或速度流失；正面影響：滿足兼具有氧與無氧需求的運動專案，更貼近比賽實況地準備運動員。"},{"id":"q2014","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cross Bridges (Myosin)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Globular Heads of the myosin filaments the protrude to attach to Actin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"橫橋（cross bridge）：肌球蛋白粗肌絲外突的球狀頭部，可與肌動蛋白結合，是產生肌力的結構。"},{"id":"q2015","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT frequency for: Beginner, intermediate, advanced","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2-3, 3-4, 4-7","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力訓練頻率建議：初學者每週2–3次、中階3–4次、高階4–7次。"},{"id":"q2016","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If a banana has a glycemic index (GI) rating of 51 and has 25 grams of carbohydrates per serving, what is the glycemic load (GL)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"51 x 25 / 100 = 12.7 or 13 EQUATION: GI of an individual food x gram of carbs per serving of food / 100","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"血糖負荷（GL）＝食物GI × 每份公克數 ÷ 100。香蕉：51 × 25 ÷ 100 ≈ 12.7（約13）。GL比GI更能反映實際攝入一份食物對血糖的衝擊。"},{"id":"q2017","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the rate at which the body burns calories over a 24-hour period, while at complete rest.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"基礎代謝率（BMR）：身體在完全靜止狀態下24小時消耗熱量的速率，維持生命基本機能所需的能量。"},{"id":"q2018","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Transverse Tubular system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Transverse tube system is perpendicular to the myofibiri and two sarcoplasmic channels. at the end of each tubes channel terminates as a Ca2+ storing vesicle. Each Z-line reagion contain two vesicles and t-tube. T-tube passing throught the muscle cell, open externally from the inside of the cell, and touch the sarcolemma on the surface of the cell's outer mmebrane to all inner regions of the cell. Deporalization release ca2+ from vesicles, initiating contractile motion.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"橫管系統（T-tubule）：與肌原纖維垂直走向的管膜系統，每一T管末端以儲存Ca2+的囊泡收束；每個Z線區含兩個囊泡夾一條T管。T管與肌膜相連，把去極化訊號傳入細胞深部，觸發囊泡釋放Ca2+啟動收縮。"},{"id":"q2019","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Center of gravity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to balance and where gravity is at its strongest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"重心（center of gravity）：身體重量集中平衡之點，重力合力的作用點；重心越低、支撐面越大，越穩定。"},{"id":"q2020","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are structural exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- A sub classification of core exercises that involve loading of the spine, and muscular stabilization of posture","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"結構動作：核心動作的子類別，特徵是對脊柱施加負荷，並要求肌肉穩定軀幹姿勢（如背蹲、硬舉、動力清潔）。"},{"id":"q2021","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"a structural exercise performed very quickly or explosively is considered a?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"power exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率動作（power exercise）：以極快速度或爆發方式完成的結構動作，如動力清潔、推舉。"},{"id":"q2022","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Myofibrils","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Internal structure of the muscle fiber (myocyte) -Contain proteins actin, myosin, titin Muscle contractions takes place along the myofibril as actin filaments slide along the length of the myosin generating muscular contractions.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌原纖維（myofibrils）：肌纖維內部的收縮結構，含肌動蛋白、肌球蛋白、連線蛋白；收縮沿肌原纖維發生——細肌絲沿粗肌絲滑動產生張力。"},{"id":"q2023","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An exercise session consisting of which training modality results in the largest increase in serum HGH concentration?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"High-intensity resistance training","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高強度阻力訓練對血清生長激素（HGH）濃度的急性提升幅度最大，超過有氧或其他訓練模式。"},{"id":"q2024","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the hydration and electrolyte recommendations for pre and post exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":".5 L water 2 hours before event Exercise less than an hour = water only Over an hour = electrolyte and water Hot weather: sodium chloride 20-30mg Potassium 2.5mg Carbs 5-6%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"補水與電解質：賽前2小時喝0.5升水；運動不滿1小時喝白水即可；超過1小時需電解質加水；高溫環境補充氯化鈉20–30 mg、鉀2.5 mg；飲料碳水化合物濃度5–6%。"},{"id":"q2025","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Equipment should be ________ (blank) inches apart, same as the pathways in width and safety space cushion around free weights.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"36 inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Organziation & Administration Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"器材之間應保持36英吋的間距——此數值同於通道寬度與自由重量周圍的安全緩衝空間。"},{"id":"q2026","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete with a low back injury has been cleared by the athletic training staff to participate in SC activities during the last phase of tissue healing. Which is most appropriate? Romanian deadlift Lunges Bent-over row","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Lunges","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"下背受傷、經運動防護員許可於組織癒合最後階段恢復訓練的運動員，最合適做弓箭步——單腿支撐動作對腰椎的軸向壓與屈曲力矩小於羅馬尼亞硬舉與俯身划船。"},{"id":"q2027","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does concurrent resistance and aerobic training affect strength gains? Cardiovascular gains?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power and strength can be reduced when combining a resistance and aerobic program. However it appears cardiovascular gains are not affected negatively and may actually improve with some resistance training.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力與有氧並行訓練（concurrent training）：合併兩種計畫可能降低功率與肌力增長；但心血管適應不受負面影響，部分阻力訓練甚至還能增進有氧表現。"},{"id":"q2028","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Z-Line","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"In the middle of I-Band Appears as a thin, dark line Runs Longitudinally","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Z線：位於I帶中央的細暗線，橫向垂直於肌原纖維軸（原答案「縱走」有誤），是肌小節的兩端界標，細肌絲附著於此。"},{"id":"q2029","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT frequency based on season: Off-season, preseason, in season, postseason","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"offseason: 4-6, preseason:3-4, in season: 1-3, postseason:0-3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"按賽季安排阻力訓練頻率：休賽季每週4–6次、季前3–4次、季中1–3次、季後賽0–3次。"},{"id":"q2030","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does the composition of proteins differ from that of fats and carbohydrates?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Proteins have nitrogen in addition to Carbon, hydrogen, oxygen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"蛋白質與脂肪、碳水化合物組成的差異：蛋白質除碳、氫、氧之外還含有氮（nitrogen），這是胺基酸的特徵元素。"},{"id":"q2031","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Blood Pressure","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the pressure within the arterial system caused by blood flow.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"血壓：血流對動脈系統血管壁造成的壓力。"},{"id":"q2032","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Myosin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The interaction between myosin and actin causing sarcomore to shorten as the muscle contracts. Also responsiable for splitting ATP (adenosine triphosphate) The phosphate released from ATP hydrolysis provides the energy require for myosin to produce the power stroke, causing the myosin head to grab onto the actin and pull the filaments closer together as muscle contraction occurs.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌球蛋白（myosin）：與肌動蛋白互動作用使肌小節縮短產生收縮；並能分解ATP——ATP水解釋放的磷酸提供能量，使肌球蛋白頭部完成動力衝程（power stroke），抓住肌動蛋白並把肌絲拉近。"},{"id":"q2033","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Center of Pressure","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Area where total force is being applied to represent maximum force.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"壓力中心（center of pressure）：總作用力（地面反作用力）等效施加的位置點，用以表徵最大受力位置。"},{"id":"q2034","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are power exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Structural exercises that are performed quickly or explosivly","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率動作：以快速或爆發方式執行的結構動作，兼具脊柱負荷與高收縮速度。"},{"id":"q2035","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING IS A STRUCTURAL EXERCISE THAT CAN ONLY BE PERFORMED USING FREE WEIGHTS? a. FRONT SQUAT b. SNATCH c. BENT OVER ROW d. OVERHEAD DUMBBELL TRICEPS EXTENSION","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"b. SNATCH","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"只能用自由重量進行的結構動作是抓舉（snatch）——動作需沿身體快速翻鈴、多關節爆發伸展，器械式動作無法複製其軌跡與穩定性需求。"},{"id":"q2036","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcomere","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Basic unit of muscle fiber -Proteins actin and myosin are found -Defined as area between tow z-lines -area where all muscular contractions take place","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌小節（sarcomere）：肌纖維的基本單位，含肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白，定義為兩條Z線之間的區段，所有肌肉收縮都在此發生。"},{"id":"q2037","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An increase in which of the following is a marker of aerobic overtraining?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Creatine kinase concentration","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧過度訓練的指標之一是肌酸激酶（creatine kinase）濃度上升——反映肌肉持續損傷、恢復不足。"},{"id":"q2038","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the common deficiencies in vitamins and minerals for athletes? What supplements should be taken?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Iron, calcium, vitamin d, omega 3 fats Iron: 18mg iron female, 8mg male Calcium: 1000mg/day Vitamin d: 800-1000IUs Vitamin d deficiency will significantly impact power athletes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動員常見的微量營養素缺乏：鐵、鈣、維生素D、omega-3脂肪酸。補充參考：鐵每日女性18 mg、男性8 mg；鈣1,000 mg；維生素D 800–1000 IU——維生素D不足會明顯影響爆發力表現。"},{"id":"q2039","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the difference between a compound set and super set?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Compound set are two exercises back-to-back working the same muscle group. Supersets are two exercises back-to-back working opposing muscle groups.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"組合組（compound set）：兩個動作連續做、訓練同一肌群；超級組（superset）：兩個動作連續做、訓練互為拮抗的兩組肌群。"},{"id":"q2040","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What exercises are most appropriate for a specific sport movement (tennis forehand, shot put, etc)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"專項動作選擇（如網球正手、鉛球）：依各專案特性選擇能高度模擬其動作模式與發力順序的練習，詳見課本各專項範例。"},{"id":"q2041","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcoplasmic Reticulum (SR)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Intricate tubules surrounding each myofibril Terminates as vesicles in the vicinity of Z-lines Stores Calcium + Ions (controls muscle contraction)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌漿網（SR）：包繞每條肌原纖維的細密小管，在Z線附近末端膨大成囊泡；儲存Ca2+離子，控制肌肉的收縮與放鬆。"},{"id":"q2042","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What percent of 1RM is: 6,10,15RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"85%,75%,65%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"次數與1RM%對應：6RM約85%、10RM約75%、15RM約65%——可用來由可完成的次數推算負荷強度。"},{"id":"q2043","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does arginine affect circulation?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Stimulates Vasodilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"精胺酸（arginine）：一氧化氮的前驅物，能刺激血管舒張（vasodilation），促進血液迴圈與泵感。"},{"id":"q2044","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Body Composition","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the makeup of lean and fat tissue in the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"身體組成（body composition）：體內瘦組織（肌肉、骨骼、水分）與脂肪組織的相對比例。"},{"id":"q2045","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Actin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The protein that forms the thinner myofilament,which consisys of two strands of actin in a double helix configuration. The scarcomere contracts when actin and myosin bind together and complete a power stroke","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌動蛋白（actin）：構成細肌絲的蛋白質，兩條肌動蛋白鏈捲成雙螺旋；肌小節收縮時肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白結合並完成動力衝程，把Z線拉近。"},{"id":"q2046","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Force of Velocity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Workout environment that has direct result","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力-速度關係（force-velocity relationship，原答案文不對題）：肌肉收縮速度越快，能產出的力量越小；負荷越重、收縮越慢，產出力量越大。"},{"id":"q2047","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What should be kept in mind regarding athlete that play sports when desgining training programs?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Aim for sport specificity to increase transfer between training and sport","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"為運動員設計計畫時應牢記：以專項性（sport specificity）為目標，提高訓練表現轉移到賽場表現的比率。"},{"id":"q2048","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A BASEBALL PITCHER HAS AN ELBOW FLEXION TO ELBOW EXTENSION STRENGTH RATIO OF 1:3. WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EXERCISES SHOULD BE ADDED TO HIS PROGRAM TO REDUCE THE RISK OF THROWING-RELATED INJURIES? a. DUMBBELL BICEP CURL b. DECLINE BENCH PRESS c. BENT OVER LATERAL RAISE d. OVERHEAD TRICEPS EXTENSION","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a. DUMBBELL BICEP CURL","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肘屈/伸肌力比為1:3的投手，應加入啞鈴二頭彎舉強化較弱的肘屈肌（肱二頭肌），使屈伸比例趨於平衡，降低投擲相關肘部傷害風險。"},{"id":"q2049","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcomere 4 segments: A-band","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A-band is segment where both actin and myosin filaments are located. in muscle tissue, the area between two I bands of a sarcomere, marked by partial overlapping of actin and myosin filaments and appearing dark.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"A帶：肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白肌絲重疊的區段，位於肌小節兩側I帶之間，因粗細分肌絲部分重疊而在顯微鏡下呈暗帶。"},{"id":"q2050","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An increase in which of the following increases oxygen delivery to the active muscles during acute aerobic exercise? Blood hemoglobin, cardiac output, plasma volume","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"急性有氧運動中，心輸出量（cardiac output）增加是提升活動肌肉攝氧量的主因——單位時間泵送到肌肉的血量上升，攜氧總量隨之增加。"},{"id":"q2051","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the pre and post workout meal recommendations?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Pre: 1-4 g/kg BW carbs, lower in protein fat and fiber, 1-6 hrs prior Post: 1-1.5 g/kg BW carbs necessary for glycogen resynthesis .3g g/kg BW protein Protein: 20g whey protein during recovery maximizes protein resynthesis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練前後飲食：訓練前1–6小時攝取1–4 g/kg碳水化合物，蛋白質、脂肪、纖維從簡；訓練後1–1.5 g/kg碳水化合物以回補肝糖，約0.3 g/kg蛋白質；恢復期攝取約20 g乳清蛋白可最大化肌肉蛋白質合成。"},{"id":"q2052","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following are the most sport-specific exercises for a sprinter? Leg press and triceps pushdowns Lunges and one arm dumbbell row Front squat and biceps curl","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Lunges and one arm db row","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最專項於短跑的組合是弓箭步加單臂啞鈴划船——均為單側、多關節動作，動作模式與擺臂蹬地相似，轉移效果最高。"},{"id":"q2053","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What muscle groups are involved during specific sport movements?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"專項動作涉及的肌群因專案而異：應以需求分析中的動作分析，找出原動肌、穩定肌與減速肌群，詳見課本各專項分析。"},{"id":"q2054","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T-Tubules","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Run perpendicular to the SR Terminate in the vicinity of Z-lines between vesicles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"T小管（橫管）：與肌漿網垂直走向，末端終止於Z線附近的囊泡（終池）之間，與SR構成三聯體。"},{"id":"q2055","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Where should athlete look when responding to COD of opponent","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"opponents shoulders, trunk and hip following opponent's COD, athlete should shift visual focus to where they need to go to lead their body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"回應對手變向時應盯對手的肩、軀幹與髖（軀幹線索最難假動作）；判讀變向後，把視線移向自己要去的路線，頭部引導身體追防。"},{"id":"q2056","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 165-lb (75-kg) athlete has an average daily intake of 450 g of carbohydrate, 75 g of protein, and 100 g of fat. What percent of the total kilocalorie intake is carbohydrate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Carbohydrate has 4 kcal/gram, protein 4 kcal/gram, and fat 9 kcal/gram 4(450) + 4(75) + 9(100) =3000 450 x 4 = 1800 carbs 1800/3000 = .6x100 = 60%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"熱量佔比計算：碳水化合物4大卡/克、蛋白質4、脂肪9。總熱量＝4×450＋4×75＋9×100＝3,000大卡；碳水1,800÷3,000＝60%。"},{"id":"q2057","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Body Fat Percentage","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the percentage of fat in the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"體脂率（body fat percentage）：脂肪重量佔總體重的百分比。"},{"id":"q2058","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Troponin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Troponin, a protein located at regular intervals along the actin filament,binds with the Ca2+ released from the sacroplasim reticulum (ER) causing a change in tropomysin exposing the binding site on the actin filaments for the myosin heads to from cross-bridges.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌鈣蛋白（troponin）：規律分佈在細肌絲上的調節蛋白；與肌漿網釋出的Ca2+結合後，使原肌球蛋白移位，暴露肌動蛋白上供肌球蛋白頭部結合的位點，橫橋得以形成。"},{"id":"q2059","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anatomical Planes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Frontal : front & back Median (midsaggital) : right & left Horizontal : upper & lower Saggital : runs parallel to median.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"解剖面：冠狀面（frontal）分身體前後；正中面（midsagittal）分左右；水平面分上下；矢狀面與正中面平行。"},{"id":"q2060","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are recovery exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Exercises at the end of an session to promote recovery Light load resistance or low intensity aerobic activity Help to remove metebolic waste","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"恢復動作（recovery exercises）：課表末尾促進恢復的練習——輕負荷阻力或低強度有氧，幫助代謝廢物清除與放鬆。"},{"id":"q2061","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING SPORTS WOULD BENEFIT THE MOST BY INCORPORATING THIS EXERCISE (BENT OVER ROW) INTO THE STRENGTH AND CONDITIONING PROGRAM? a. LACROSSE b. CREW c. RUGBY d. VOLLEYBALL","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"B. CREW","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"加入俯身划船（bent over row）獲益最大的是划船（crew）專案——劃槳動作以軀幹與背肌的拉、脊柱伸展為主導，與划船訓練的動作模式和肌群參與最一致。"},{"id":"q2062","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcomere 4 segments: I-band","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"corresponds the areas in Two adjacent sarcomeres that contain only actin filaments. Decrease as the Z-lines are pulled toward the center of the sarcomere.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"I帶（肌小節區段）：指相鄰兩個肌小節中只含肌動蛋白細肌絲的區域；收縮時Z線被拉向肌小節中央，I帶隨之縮短。"},{"id":"q2063","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"If calcium is not returned to the S.R, which of the following best describes what occurs in the muscle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fused tetany","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"若Ca2+未被肌漿網回收，肌鈣蛋白持續結合鈣、橫橋持續迴圈，肌肉將維持在持續強直收縮狀態（fused tetany），無法放鬆。"},{"id":"q2064","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the difference between hypo and hyper hydration?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Hyper- excess water Hypo- dehydrated 50% of people begin workout hypo- hydrated 1% hyper to 3% hyperhydration is normal body range. Prevent body mass loss due to hydration no more than 2% BW","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"水過多稱過度水合（hyperhydration），不足稱脫水（hypohydration）；約半數人開始運動時已處於輕度脫水；運動中控制體重流失不超過2%即屬正常範圍。"},{"id":"q2065","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 90% 1RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"90% 1RM下大約可完成4次——與強度次數對應表一致。"},{"id":"q2066","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What training mode(s) are most specific to particular sport activities?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最專項於特定運動的訓練模式因專案而異，須依該運動的能量系統佔比與動作特徵選擇，詳見課本專項章節。"},{"id":"q2067","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Triad","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The pattern of T-Tubules spaced between/perpendicular to 2 SR's","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"三聯體（triad）：一條T小管與其兩側相鄰肌漿網終池構成的結構組合，垂直穿行於兩條SR之間，是興奮-收縮耦聯發生的部位。"},{"id":"q2068","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"4 tips to body position for braking and reaccelearation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decrease large amounts of trunk motion through stance phase, reorient trunk+hips toward new direction lean body to reaccelerate keep center of mass low","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"煞停與再加速的身體姿態四要點：支撐期減少軀幹大幅擺動、把軀幹與髖重新朝向新方向、身體向新方向前傾以再加速、保持重心壓低。"},{"id":"q2069","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 120-lb (54.5-kg) marathon runner begins to taper one week before her race. Three days prior to the race she begins to carbohydrate load. Approximately how many grams of carbohydrates per day is most appropriate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"8 to 10 g/ kg bw Marathon runners may need higher intakes 10-12g/kg bw 55kg x 10g/1kg = 550kg","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"馬拉鬆跑者（55公斤）賽前肝糖增量法：每天約8–10 g/kg（馬拉鬆選手或需10–12 g/kg），即55×10約550 g/日，於賽前3天開始（原答案550kg應為550 g）。"},{"id":"q2070","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Body Mass Index (BMI)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the numerical equivalent of over or underweight, derived from an equation utilizing body weight and height.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"身體質量指數（BMI）＝體重(kg)÷身高(m)的平方，用數值判斷過輕或過重；缺點是不區分肌肉與脂肪。"},{"id":"q2071","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tropomysin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Tropomysin is a protein in the I-band located along the actin filament in a groove formed by the double helix configuration of the teo actin strands. The conformational change of troponin moves the tropomysin deeper into the groove, allowing the actin and myosin cross- bridge to rapidly attatch,pulling the actin toward the center of sarcomere in a contractile action. When troponin is not affecting tropomysin,it inhibits actin and myosin bonding , which prevents a constant state of muscle contraction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"原肌球蛋白（tropomyosin）：位於I帶、沿肌動蛋白雙螺旋凹槽排列的調節蛋白；靜息時遮擋肌球蛋白結合位點、防止肌肉持續收縮；肌鈣蛋白結合Ca2+變形後把它移入凹槽深處，暴露位點讓橫橋快速結合、拉動肌動蛋白滑向肌小節中央收縮。"},{"id":"q2072","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Isometric","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle length does not change regardless of the amount of force applied. Pressure is being applied upon a non-moveable object Such as pushing against a wall or holding an end position for longer than 10 seconds (planks, hang)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等長收縮（isometric）：不論輸出多大力量，肌肉長度都不變——如推不動的物體（推牆），或維持末端姿勢超過10秒（平板支撐、懸掛）。"},{"id":"q2073","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Define muscle balance.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A proper ratio of strength, power or musculat endurance of a muscle relative to another Not nessisarily meaning equal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌肉平衡：主動肌與拮抗肌之間在肌力、功率或肌耐力上維持恰當比例——不是要求兩者相等，而是比例適當以降低受傷風險。"},{"id":"q2074","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF FOLLOWING EXERCISES TRAIN THE ANTAGONISTS OF THE MUSCLES TRAINED IN THIS EXERCISE (db CHEST PRESS)? a. CABLE CROSS-OVER b. ONE-ARM DUMBBELL ROW c. FRONT SHOULDER RAISE d. CLOSE-GRIP BENCH PRESS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ONE-ARM DB ROW","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"啞鈴胸推動作的主動肌是胸大肌，其拮抗肌為背部肌群，因此答案是單臂啞鈴划船；電纜飛鳥與窄握臥推仍以胸/三頭為主。"},{"id":"q2075","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcomere 4 segments: H-Zone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Area in the center of the sarcomere where only myosin filaments are present . During muscle contraction, the H-zone decrease as the actin slides over the myosin toward the center of the sarcomere.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"H帶：肌小節中央只有肌球蛋白粗肌絲、無肌動蛋白重疊的區域；收縮時肌動蛋白向中央滑動，H帶變短甚至消失。"},{"id":"q2076","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The arteriovenous oxygen difference (a-vO2) is a measure of:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The amount of oxygen taken up from the blood by the tissues. The greater the amount of oxygen extracted by the tissues, the greater the difference.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動靜脈氧差（a-vO2 difference）：組織從血液中攝取利用的氧量（動脈血含氧量減靜脈血含氧量）；組織攝氧越多，差值越大，是有氧代謝能力的指標。"},{"id":"q2077","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Carb replenishment recommendations pre, during and post exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1g per kg prior .5g/kg during 1-1.2 g/kg post","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物補充建議：賽前約1 g/kg，運動中約0.5 g/kg，賽後1–1.2 g/kg以回補肝糖。"},{"id":"q2078","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 85% 1RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"6","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"85% 1RM下大約可完成6次——對應肌力訓練區間的下限。"},{"id":"q2079","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What muscles are involved during a resistance training exercise? Flexibility? Plyometric?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"各動作涉及的肌肉：阻力、柔軟度、增強式動作皆應逐一分析原動肌、協同肌、穩定肌與拮抗肌，詳見課本動作圖譜。"},{"id":"q2080","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Action Potential w/ Muscle Contraction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Action Potential from MU > Releases Ca+ from SR to myofibril > Tension in Muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動作電位引發收縮的流程：運動神經元動作電位→肌漿網釋放Ca2+到肌原纖維→橫橋形成→肌肉產生張力。"},{"id":"q2081","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"to tips to focus on during COD with leg actions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"avoid a stiff leg braking style concentrate on the ground instead of a body part, \"push the ground away\"","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"變向時下肢動作兩要點：避免直腿硬撐式的煞車（應保持屈髖屈膝緩衝）；專注地面而非盯著身體部位，心想「把地面向後推」以產生制動力與再驅動力。"},{"id":"q2082","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are complete proteins?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Animal-based proteins - eggs, dairy foods, meat, fish, and poultry. This means they contain all the essential amino acids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"完全蛋白質：動物性來源——蛋、乳製品、肉類、魚、禽肉，含全部9種必需胺基酸。"},{"id":"q2083","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Buff","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to a large and muscular body. The term is usually directed towards the male gender. A female would be \"Buffy\".","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Buff（俚語，非學術術語）：形容壯碩、肌肉發達的體型，多用於男性（女性戲稱buffy）。"},{"id":"q2084","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Acetylcholine (ACh)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Vesicles located at the terminal end of moter neurons release the neurotransmitter ACh when an action potential arrives at the terminal end of a motoe neuron. ACh diffuses across the synaptic space of the neuromuscular junction, and this exercise the sarcolemma, initiating muscle contraction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"乙醯膽鹼（ACh）：動作電位抵達運動神經末梢時，囊泡釋放的神經傳導物質；ACh擴散通過神經肌肉接點的突觸間隙，刺激肌膜去極化，啟動肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q2085","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Isotonic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Ms contraction remain the same throughout the movement Pushup, pull up & machines","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等張收縮（isotonic）：動作全程肌肉張力大致恆定而長度改變——伏地挺身、引體向上、器械訓練（實際上張力隨關節角度變化，此為簡化說法）。"},{"id":"q2086","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What should be considered in terms of equipment when desgining a program?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Availability Ex: gym, home gym, bodyweight, dumbbells only","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"設計計畫時須考慮器材可取得性：商業健身房、家庭健身房、僅徒手、僅有啞鈴等不同條件下，可用動作與計畫形式差異很大。"},{"id":"q2087","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"the more similar the training activity is to the actual sport movement, the greater the likelihood that there will be a positive transfer to that sport","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specific adaptation to imposed demands principle (SAID)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"特定壓力適應原則（SAID principle）：訓練動作與實際運動動作越相似，正向轉移到該運動表現的可能性越高。"},{"id":"q2088","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcomere 4 segments: Z-line","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"In the middle of the I-band","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Z線：位於I帶中央，橫向連線相鄰肌小節的細肌絲，是肌小節的界標。"},{"id":"q2089","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female marathon runner goes from sea level to altitude of 5280, what is the immediate physiological effect?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"海平面選手一下子到海拔5,280英尺（約1,600米），立即的生理效應是心輸出量增加——身體以加快心率、增加泵血來補償空氣含氧量下降。"},{"id":"q2090","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the protein recommendation for gaining weight?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.5-2 g/kg bodyweight Over 2 g/kg has shown no beneficial effect","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"增重（增肌）的蛋白質建議：每日1.5–2 g/kg體重；超過2 g/kg沒有額外效益。"},{"id":"q2091","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 80% 1RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"8","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"80% 1RM下大約可完成8次。"},{"id":"q2092","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How do similar exercises affect muscle recruitment (incline vs flat bench press, etc)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"改變動作會改變肌肉參與：如上斜vs平躺臥推，肩關節角度改變使上胸、前三角肌的參與比例隨之變化——調整角度、握距即可轉移訓練重點。"},{"id":"q2093","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sliding-Filament Theory","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"States that the actin filaments at each end of the sarcomere slide inward on myosin filaments, pulling the Z-lines toward the center of the sarcomere and thus shortening the muscle fiber","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"滑動肌絲理論（sliding-filament theory）：肌小節兩端的肌動蛋白細肌絲沿肌球蛋白向內側滑動，把Z線拉向肌小節中央，使肌纖維縮短——這就是肌肉收縮的機制，肌絲本身長度不變。"},{"id":"q2094","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Define RT status for Beginner, intermediate, advanced","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 months, 2-6 months, over 1yr","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練狀態定義：初學者為持續訓練未滿2個月；中階2–6個月以上；高階為1年以上且具備中級以上技術——決定頻率與動作選擇。"},{"id":"q2095","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"1) What is the recommended carb intake if an athlete consumes a pre-comp meal at least 2 hours before comp starts? 2) If an athlete needs to eat closer to competition time (one hour or less) what is the recommended carb intake","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) 1g/kg body weight 2) .5g/kg body weight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"賽前碳水攝取：距開賽2小時以上吃正餐者約1 g/kg體重；開賽前1小時內才進食者減量至約0.5 g/kg，避免腸胃不適。"},{"id":"q2096","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Calisthenics","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to exercises that use the body weight as resistance. Push-ups and crunches are examples.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"徒手體操（calisthenics）：以自身體重作阻力的動作，如伏地挺身、仰臥起坐。"},{"id":"q2097","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Isokenetic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Use of special equipment that moves the muscle at a constant speed Bike, TM","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等速動作（isokinetic，原文拼寫有誤）：使用特殊器械使肢體以固定速度全行程運動，阻力隨輸出力量自動調整；常見於等速肌力測試儀與復健裝置（原答案的單車/跑步機並非標準等速器械）。"},{"id":"q2098","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How should available time per session factor into exercise selection?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"If limited time is available lower time exercises need to be given priority. Ex: machine leg press instead of barbbell lunges for hip quad training for a sprinter","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"每次課可用時間影響動作選擇：時間有限時優先安排 架設快速、單位時間效益高的動作——例如為短跑選手做髖與股四頭肌訓練時，以器械腿推取代架設費時的大槓弓箭步。"},{"id":"q2099","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"The basketball coach says his starting center needs to jump higher. In addition to beginning a plyometric program, which of the following resistance training exercises are MOST specific to this goal? a) Power clean b) Leg (knee) curl c) Front squat d) Seated calf (heel) raise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power Clean and Front Squat","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"為籃球中鋒提升彈跳，除增強式訓練外最專項的阻力動作是動力清潔與前蹲——兩者都是下肢爆發伸展、符合垂直跳發力模式的全身動作。"},{"id":"q2100","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcoplasmic reticulum","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Is a system to tubules surrounding each myofibril and is responsible for pumping Ca+ ions into the muscle when and action potential has been release onto the sarcomere. Pumps Ca+ ions into the muscle to create the contraction and stores Ca+. Without it muscular contraction would not occur","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌漿網（sarcoplasmic reticulum）：包繞每條肌原纖維的管狀系統，儲存Ca2+；動作電位傳抵後把Ca2+泵放至肌纖維內引發收縮——沒有它，肌肉收縮無法發生。"},{"id":"q2101","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the equation to calculate power?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Work / time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率＝功÷時間（Power = Work / time）。"},{"id":"q2102","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Protein requirement differences for aerobic and anaerobic athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1-1.6 g/kg/BW aerobic 1.4-1.7 g/kg anaerobic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧與無氧運動員的蛋白質需求不同：有氧（耐力）約1.0–1.6 g/kg/日；無氧（肌力/爆發）約1.4–1.7 g/kg/日。"},{"id":"q2103","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 75% 1RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"10","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"75% 1RM下大約可完成10次——落在肥大訓練強度區間。"},{"id":"q2104","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does a change in an exercise result in a change of the involved muscle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Various see study material","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"更換動作會改變參與肌群：動作角度、握法、站距、行程不同，主受力肌與協同肌的分配隨之改變，應依訓練目的選擇變式。"},{"id":"q2105","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cross-Bridge/Force Pro Relationship","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The number of Cross-Bridges that are attached to actin filaments dictate the Force Production of a muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"橫橋-力量關係：與肌動蛋白結合的橫橋數目決定肌肉產力量——粗細肌絲重疊越多、可形成的橫橋越多，張力越大。"},{"id":"q2106","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Plyometric program volume for: Beginner, intermediate, advanced (in contacts/session)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"80-100 100-120 120-140","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"增強式訓練的單次觸地次數（contacts）：初學者80–100、中階100–120、高階120–140。"},{"id":"q2107","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The recommendation for American football athletes is __________________ of protein per kilogram of body weight.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.0 to 2.0 g of protein per kg bow","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"美式橄欖球運動員的蛋白質建議：每日每公斤體重1.0–2.0 g，依賽季與增重/維持目標取值。"},{"id":"q2108","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Calorie","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to a measure of the energy value of food.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"卡路里：衡量食物能量價值的單位。"},{"id":"q2109","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All-or-non principle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when action potential in a motor neuron raches the sacrolemma. the action potential will either elicit activation of all the muscle fibers connected to the motor neuron or no activation of any of the muscle fibers will occur. Partial activation of just some fibers will not occur","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"全或無原則（all-or-none principle）：動作電位達到閾值時，該運動神經元所支配的所有肌纖維一起被活化收縮；未達閾值則全不收縮——不會出現只收縮一部分纖維的情況。"},{"id":"q2110","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Growth Hormone (NOT TEST)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2nd hormone released Stimulates growth Responsible for LMM & bone tissue Increases protein synthesis Stimulates immune system Single chain Amino Acid","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"生長激素（GH）：運動中第二順位釋放的激素；促進生長，負責增加瘦肌肉量與骨組織、提升蛋白質合成、刺激免疫系統；結構為單一胺基酸鏈的蛋白質激素。"},{"id":"q2111","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What factors should be considered in step 3 of resistance program desgin (training frequency)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Training Status 2) Sport Season 3) Traing Load/type","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第三步（訓練頻率）的考量因素：1.訓練狀態 2.運動賽季階段 3.訓練負荷與型別（上下肢/大小肌群交替）。"},{"id":"q2112","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"the muscle or muscle group actively causing the movement","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"agonist","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"主動肌（agonist）：主動產生某個動作的肌肉或肌群，又稱原動肌。"},{"id":"q2113","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sarcolemma","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Is the cell membrane of striated muscle tissue and is responsible for the separation of each individual muscle fiber. -essential in conducting and receiving stimuli form connective never fiber. -It transduce's electrical signals that allow the t-tubules to release Ca+ ions into sarcoplasm.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌膜（sarcolemma）：橫紋肌的細胞膜，分隔個別肌纖維；負責接收與傳導來自運動神經的刺激，傳導電訊號使T小管觸發Ca2+釋放到肌漿。"},{"id":"q2114","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which movement occurs mainly in the transverse plane?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Bent over lateral raise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"俯身側平舉主要發生在水平（橫）面——肩關節做水平外展，訓練三角肌後束與上背肌群。"},{"id":"q2115","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Optimal LDL levels (bad) and HDL (good) and total cholesterol.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"LDL 60, less than 40 too low Total 240 high","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"血脂參考值：HDL大於等於60 mg/dL具保護作用、低於40過低；總膽固醇大於等於240 mg/dL為偏高；LDL理想低於100 mg/dL（原答案文字有殘缺）。"},{"id":"q2116","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 70% 1RM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"12","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"70% 1RM下大約可完成12次——落在肥大/肌耐力交界區間。"},{"id":"q2117","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is a closed kinetic chain movement or exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"One is which the terminal point meets with considerable resistance that prohibits or restrains its free motion; that is the distal joint is stationary.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"閉鎖性動力學鏈動作：遠端（手或腳）受到足夠阻力而無法自由移動、遠端關節固定——如深蹲、伏地挺身，通常多關節、功能性較高。"},{"id":"q2118","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Resting Phase (Muscle)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Little Ca+ Little cross-bridges","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌肉休息階段：肌漿內Ca2+濃度低、可用的結合位點少，橫橋數量極少，肌肉處於鬆弛狀態。"},{"id":"q2119","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"4 Factors affecting intensity of Plyometric drills","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Points of contact (single vs. bilateral leg) Speed height of drill body weight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"影響增強式練習強度的四項因素：接觸點（單腿vs雙腿）、動作速度、動作高度、自身體重。"},{"id":"q2120","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the dietary reference intake (DRI) for fiber for men? For women?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"For men: 30-38g For women: 21 to 29","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"膳食纖維DRI：男性每日30–38 g，女性約21–29 g（常引用值為男38 g、女25 g）。"},{"id":"q2121","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Carbohydrates","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to one of the six nutrients used by the body for energy. Dietary sources of carbohydrates include sugars, grains, rice, potatoes, and beans. 1 gram = 4 calories.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物：六大營養素之一，身體的主要能量來源；來源包括糖、穀物、米飯、馬鈴薯、豆類；每克提供4大卡。"},{"id":"q2122","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Conentric muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Contraction force is greater than the resistive force, causing muscle shortening and joint to move","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"向心動作（concentric）：收縮力大於阻力，肌肉縮短並帶動關節產生動作。"},{"id":"q2123","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anabolic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Build Up","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"同化作用（anabolic）：合成、建造——把小分子合成大分子，如胺基酸合成蛋白質、構建肌肉組織。"},{"id":"q2124","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How often should and individual train based on training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Beginner = 2-3 - Intermediate = 3-4 - Advanced = 4-7","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"依訓練狀態安排每週頻率：初學者2–3次、中階3–4次、高階4–7次，須配合恢復能力。"},{"id":"q2125","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"the sometimes passive (not concentrically involved) muscle or muclse group located on the opposite side of the limb","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"antagonist","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"拮抗肌（antagonist）：位於肢體對側、在動作中常處於被動（不參與向心收縮）的肌肉，負責減速與穩定。"},{"id":"q2126","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Protein Myosin The thicker myofilament","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Responsible for cross-linking to actin filaments to produce the shortening of the sarcomere.\"contraction\" -Myosin fiber is site of ATP hydrolysis. =Phosphate \"energy\" is released onto the myosin fiber that starts the cross-linking between actin and myosin and produces muscular contraction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌球蛋白（粗肌絲）：與肌動蛋白交叉連線使肌小節縮短產生收縮；肌絲本身是ATP水解的位置——釋放的能量啟動肌動-肌球蛋白交叉連線，驅動肌肉收縮。"},{"id":"q2127","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What components of training stimulate new bone?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Progressive overload, direction of force, and rate of loading","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"刺激新骨形成的訓練要素：漸進式超負荷、施力方向、負荷速率——骨骼依所受的力學刺激方向與速度調整骨密度。"},{"id":"q2128","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the estimated daily calorie needs of male athletes by activity level?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Light : 38kcal/kg Moderate: 41kcal/kg Heavy: 50kcal/kg","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男性運動員每日熱量需求估計（按活動程度）：輕度約38 kcal/kg、中度約41 kcal/kg、高強度約50 kcal/kg。"},{"id":"q2129","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max reps for 95% 1RM?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"95% 1RM下大約只能完成2次——接近極限強度區間。"},{"id":"q2130","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is an open kinetic chain movement or exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Use a combination of successively arranged joints in which the terminal joint is free to move; open kinetic chain exercises allow for greater concentration on an isolated joint or muscle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"開鎖性動力學鏈動作：一連串關節依次運動、遠端關節可自由移動——如腿屈伸，可更專注於個別關節或肌群的孤立訓練。"},{"id":"q2131","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Excitation-Contraction Coupling Phase (Muscle)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Action Potential > Ca+ Release > Cross Bridging > Force Production","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"興奮-收縮耦聯階段：動作電位→Ca2+釋放→橫橋形成→產生力量。"},{"id":"q2132","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Duration for each training cycle: Macrocycle, mezocycle, microcycle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"several months 2-6 weeks coupple of days to few weeks","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"各訓練週期長度：大週期（macrocycle）數個月；中週期（mesocycle）2–6周；小週期（microcycle）數天到數週。"},{"id":"q2133","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Kari is a cross-country athlete and has just finished a two-hour training session. If Kari weighs 115 lbs (52 kg), how many carbohydrates should Kari consume within 30 minutes of completing her training in order to support glycogen resynthesis and the replenishment of glycogen stores?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"52kg x 1.5g/1kg = 78g","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"52公斤的越野跑者2小時訓練後，30分鐘內應攝取約1.5 g/kg的碳水化合物以支援肝糖再合成：52×1.5≈78 g。"},{"id":"q2134","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cardio","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A shortened form normally known as cardiovascular training or aerobic conditioning.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Cardio：口語簡稱，指心血管訓練或有氧體能訓練。"},{"id":"q2135","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ecentric muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"When the external resistance is greater than the muscle force (Fm) The muscle develop thesion and lengthens","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"離心動作（eccentric）：外在阻力大於肌肉收縮力時，肌肉產生張力同時被拉長——如下放負重。"},{"id":"q2136","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Testosterone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1st hormone released. Build up. Growth. peaks in 20's disappates in 30's.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"睪固酮：運動中第一順位釋放的激素；同化性、促進肌肉生長；濃度約在20多歲達高峰，30歲後逐漸下降。"},{"id":"q2137","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What should the rest interval be between training days?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- At least 1 day no more than 3 - As athletes become more advanced you can increase training days and decrease rest intervals up to 7 days a week of training using splits to rest muscle groups","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練日之間的休息：至少間隔1天、不超過3天；程度越高可增加訓練日、縮短休息，用分化訓練讓肌群輪流恢復，高階者可練滿每週7天。"},{"id":"q2138","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"what type of testing reveals that the hamstrings are extremely weak compared with the quadriceps","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"isokinetic testing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等速肌力測試（isokinetic testing）能測出膕繩肌與股四頭肌力量比過低——可精確比較主動肌/拮抗肌的力量比例，作為傷害風險評估。"},{"id":"q2139","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Actin \"Role in muscular contraction\"","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Actin is one of tow myofilaments involved in muscular contraction. Actin is the primary binding site foe the motor filament myosin, and once this binding takes place, the actin fiber will slide over the myosin fiber.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌動蛋白（actin）是參與收縮的微絲之一，提供肌凝蛋白（myosin）橫橋的主要結合位；結合後actin絲沿myosin絲滑行，產生肌絲滑動與收縮。"},{"id":"q2140","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Gas exchange during respiration occurs in which of the following structures?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Capillaries","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"氣體交換發生在微血管（capillaries）：其薄壁讓氧與二氧化碳在血液與組織間擴散；肺泡負責肺內換氣，全身性的氣體交換則依靠微血管。"},{"id":"q2141","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the estimated daily calorie needs of female athletes by activity level?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Light 35kcal/ kg Moderate 37kcal/kg Heavy 44kcal/kg","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女性每日熱量需求依活動程度估算：輕度約35、中度約37、重度約44 kcal/kg體重，乘以體重即得總需求。"},{"id":"q2142","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following factors should be determined first when designing a training program for a rugby team? Sports season Exercise type Metabolic demands","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Metabolic demands","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"替橄欖球隊設計計畫應最先確立代謝需求（metabolic demands）：能量系統分析決定後續的強度、間歇與練習選擇，賽季與練習型別排在後面考慮。"},{"id":"q2143","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How are exercises prescribed based on the type of kinetic chain movement?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Closed exercises are usually more functionally and primarily, but not always, involve the lower body (squats, etc). Open exercises (leg extension, sprinting) are good for injured and rehab athletes.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"閉鎖性動力鏈練習（如蹲舉）較貼近專項功能，多數以下肢為主；開放性動力鏈練習（如腿伸直、衝刺）較適合受傷或復健中的運動員。"},{"id":"q2144","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Contraction Phase (Muscle)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Ca+ and ATP are necessary for Myosin Cross-Bridging with Actin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收縮期：Ca2+與ATP是myosin橫橋與actin結合的先決條件——Ca2+暴露結合位，ATP提供動力行程（power stroke）能量。"},{"id":"q2145","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic sport season objectives: off season, preseason, inseason, postseason","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Offseason: devlop conditioning base, 5-6d/wk, long duration, low to moderate intensity preseason: improve performace, 6-7,mod to long, mod to high in season: maintain, 5-6 w/train+compete, low train-compete high posteseason: rest, 3-5, short, low","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧運動各季目標：休賽期建立耐力基礎（5–6天/週、長時間、低至中強度）；前賽季提升表現（6–7天、中至高強度）；賽季中維持（訓練量低、比賽強度高）；季後休息（3–5天、短、低強度）。"},{"id":"q2146","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"After an aerobic endurance training session, it is recommended that athletes consume ______________grams of carbohydrate per kilogram of body weight.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.5 grams/kg bw","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力訓練結束後30分鐘內攝取1.5 g/kg碳水化合物，以加速肝糖回補。"},{"id":"q2147","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cardiorespiratory Fitness","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A health-related component of physical fitness that relates to the ability of the circulatory and respiratory systems to supply oxygen during sustained physical activity.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心肺適能（cardiorespiratory fitness）：迴圈與呼吸系統在持續身體活動中供應氧的能力，屬健康相關體適能成分。"},{"id":"q2148","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Isometric muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when muscle generates force and attempts to contract concentrically, but unable to because the resistance force is greater then that generated by the muscle. Dones't creat the movement. still generate the force. No change in length of muscle fiber.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等長收縮（isometric）：肌肉出力但肌纖維長度不變；當阻力不小於肌肉能產生的力量時不產生關節動作，仍會產生張力。"},{"id":"q2149","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Protein Synthesis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"making new protein in ms tissutes.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"蛋白質合成：肌肉組織製造新蛋白質的修復與生長過程，由抗阻訓練與胺基酸攝取驅動。"},{"id":"q2150","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is a split routine?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- A method of increasing training frequency by dividing training into subsections of the body and resting after training by training an unrealted part Ex: Upper body, lower body split See pg 448","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"分化式訓練（split routine）：把訓練分成不同身體區域，練完一區後改練未練區域作為恢復（如上／下肢分化），藉此提高訓練頻率。"},{"id":"q2151","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"the proper ratio of strength, power, or muscular endurance of one muscle or muscle group relative to another muscle or muscle group","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle balance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力平衡（muscle balance）：肌群之間肌力、功率或肌耐力維持適當比例，不是指力量相等。"},{"id":"q2152","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All or None Principle.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Referes to the complete muscular contraction that takes place after an action potential has been released onto the sarcolemma of a muscle. This principle states that once there is no variation in the signal strength associated with an action potential, the resultant reaction will not vary. + Either there is a stimulus and a response, or there is nothing.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"全或無原則（all-or-none）：動作電位到達肌膜後，該肌纖維即產生完整收縮；訊號強度不改變反應大小——要麼完整刺激與反應，要麼完全沒有。"},{"id":"q2153","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete wants to train the glycolytic and aerobic energy systems. What rest period is most appropriate if she performs work intervals of 60 seconds in duration?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3 min","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"60秒工作間歇針對糖解與有氧系統，應採1:3–1:5工作休息比，故3分鐘最適當。"},{"id":"q2154","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Daily recommendation for fiber for men and women","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"38 and 25 g/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"膳食纖維每日建議量：男性38 g、女性25 g。"},{"id":"q2155","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A volleyball player needs to increase his multiple-effort power? Which is the most appropriate to use for power clean? 70%, 8 reps 80%, 4 reps 90%, 2 reps","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"80%, 4 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"提升排球的多重努力功率，power clean以80% 1RM做4下最適當，符合多重努力功率練習的75–85%、3–5下處方。"},{"id":"q2156","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How is muscle balance determined?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Does not mean equal strength always, just a proper ratio of strength, power, or muscular endurance of one muscle or muscle group relative to another muscle or muscle group","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"判斷肌力平衡：看肌群間肌力、功率、肌耐力的比例是否適當，而非絕對力量是否相等。"},{"id":"q2157","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All-Or-Nothing Principle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fibers all fire or they don't despite action potential strength/weakness","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"全或無原則：刺激強弱不影響單個肌纖維的反應——纖維要麼全部啟動，要麼完全不啟動。"},{"id":"q2158","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aneorobic overtraining markers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"unexplained underperformance persistent fatigue, disordered sleep, loss of appetite psychological signs","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"無氧（重量訓練型）過度訓練指標：無法解釋的表現下滑、持續疲勞、睡眠紊亂、食慾下降與心理症狀。"},{"id":"q2159","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ch. 17 Superset","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Two sequentially performed exercises that target two opposing muscles or muscle areas. Antagonist and agonist muscles Ex) Seated Rows and bench Press","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"_super-set_（套餐式訓練，superset）：連續進行的兩個練習，針對兩個互為拮抗的肌群，例如坐姿划船搭配臥推。"},{"id":"q2160","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cardiovascular","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A term that refers to the heart and blood vessels.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心血管（cardiovascular）：指心臟與血管而言。"},{"id":"q2161","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Isokinetic muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Do not occur naturally by result in a dynamic movement preformed at constance velosity. Matchine, such as a dynamometer must be used.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"等速（isokinetic）肌肉動作：自然情況下不會發生，需以等速機（dynamometer）限定速度，讓關節在全範圍以固定速度運動、肌肉全程全力出力。"},{"id":"q2162","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cortisol","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3rd hormone released. breakdown to promote gains when combined with GH release. Released w/stress and low blood sugar. Too much causes abdominal fat and ms wasting","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"皮質醇（cortisol）：壓力荷爾蒙，壓力與低血糖時分泌；與生長激素配合時協助適應，過量則造成腹部脂肪堆積與肌肉耗損（異化作用）。"},{"id":"q2163","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are resistance training frequency suggestions at diffrent point in a sport season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Off season: 4-6 sessions/week 2) Preseason: 3-4 sessions/week 3) In-season: 1-3 sessions/week 4) Postseason: 0-3 sessions/week","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"各賽季抗阻訓練頻率建議：休賽期4–6次/週、前賽季3–4次、賽季中1–3次、季後0–3次。"},{"id":"q2164","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"IN RESPONSE TO A HEAVY LOADING SESSION, THE MUSCLE GROUPS STRESSED IN WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EXERCISES REQUIRE THE LONGEST RECOVERY TIME? a. BENCH PRESS b. LEG (KNEE) EXTENSION c. FRONT SQUAT d. DUMBBELL CHEST FLY","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c. FRONT SQUAT","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"前蹲（front squat）動用的肌群最大、全身負荷最高，大重量訓練後所需恢復時間比臥推、腿伸直、飛鳥等區域性動作更長。"},{"id":"q2165","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The Neuromuscular junction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The neuromuscular junction is the central communication point for the nervous and musculoskeletal systems that leads to muscular contraction. This is the translation point where the nervous system signal \"electrical\"is converted into the biochemical reaction and then into movement \"Mechanical\" Location where acetylcholine is released. key element in muscular contraction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"神經肌肉接點（neuromuscular junction）：神經與神經肌肉系統溝通的樞紐，乙醯膽鹼（ACh）在此釋放，把電訊號轉為生化反應，最終產生機械性收縮。"},{"id":"q2166","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What work interval/ intensity ratio most closely stimulates the metabolic demands of a basketball game?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"10 seconds, 95%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最貼近籃球比賽代謝需求的工時／強度組合是10秒、95%強度的間歇，對應磷酸原主導的高強度短間歇特性。"},{"id":"q2167","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the daily carb recommendation for aerobic athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"8-10 k/kg body weight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力選手的碳水化合物建議量為每日8–10 g/kg體重。"},{"id":"q2168","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The goal of the hypertrophy/endurance phase of the preparatory period is to increase: Muscular strength Fat free mass Movement speed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fat free mass","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肥厚／肌耐力階段（準備期）的目標＝增加去脂體重（fat-free mass），不是最大肌力或動作速度。"},{"id":"q2169","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why is muscle balance important?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"To decrease a risk of injury and maximize performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力平衡的價值：降低傷害風險並最大化表現。"},{"id":"q2170","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Twitch","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The short period of activation of a muscle fiber within a MU after an AP reaches it","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"單收縮（twitch）：動作電位抵達後，運動單位內單一肌纖維的短暫活化期，是最小的收縮單位。"},{"id":"q2171","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How to increase serum Testosterone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Large muscle group exercises (deadlift, powerclean, squats) Heavy resistance (85-95% of 1RM) Moderate to High volume of exercise, achieved with musltiple sets or multiple exercises short rest (30-60s)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"提高血清睪固酮：大肌群多關節動作（硬舉、power clean、蹲舉）、高強度（85–95% 1RM）、多組數達中高容量、短休息（30–60秒）。"},{"id":"q2172","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ch. 17 Compound sets","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Performing two different exercises that target the same muscle group Ex) Barbell Curl and DB hammer curls","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"compound set：針對同一肌群連續進行的兩個不同練習，例如槓鈴彎舉＋啞鈴錘式彎舉。"},{"id":"q2173","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Carotid Pulse","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A pulse located on the carotid artery that is located down from the corner of the eye, just under the jawbone.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"頸動脈脈搏：位於頸動脈，在目外角下方、下頜骨下緣處觸控，常用於測量安靜心跳率。"},{"id":"q2174","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Insulin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4th hormone released. regulates metabolism. released by carbohydrate intake to determine LMM or fat build.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"胰島素：隨攝取碳水化合物而分泌的合成性荷爾蒙，調節代謝，促進葡萄糖與胺基酸進入細胞儲存或合成。"},{"id":"q2175","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How does training load & tyoe effect trainibg frequency?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- The greater the load (max/near max) the longer rest interval is needed to recover - Upper body recovers at a higher rate than lower body (reference 37) - Recovery is faster for single jpint exercises","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷與練習型別影響頻率：負荷越接近極限需要越長恢復；上肢恢復比下肢快；單關節動作比多關節動作恢復快。"},{"id":"q2176","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"A volleyball player is in the pre-season preparatory period and currently performing a resistance training program 4 times per week. Which of the following modifications is appropriate when progressing this athlete to an in-season training program? a. Add 1 resistance training session per week b. Schedule the resistance training sessions before sport practice c. Decrease resistance training frequency to 1-2 times per week d. Discontinue resistance training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Decrease resistance training frequency to 1-2 times per week","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"排球選手進入賽季中，重量訓練頻率應降到每週1–2次，維持訓練刺激並保留比賽所需狀態。"},{"id":"q2177","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Motor Neuron","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A motor neuro is located in the central feverous system and is responsible for transmitting signals from the spinal cord to the muscles in order to produce muscular contraction. The motor neuron is the site of the release of action potential into the neuromuscular junction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動神經元（motor neuron）：位於中樞神經系統，把脊髓的訊號傳導到肌肉，並在神經肌肉接點釋放乙醯膽鹼引發收縮。"},{"id":"q2178","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What factors determine the primary energy system used during exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Exercise intensity and exercise duration","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動強度與運動時間共同決定當時主導的能量系統。"},{"id":"q2179","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the daily carb recommendation for anaerobic athletes? (Strength, sprint, skill athletes)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"5-6 g/kg bodyweight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力量、衝刺與技巧型選手的碳水化合物建議量為每日5–6 g/kg體重。"},{"id":"q2180","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A HS athlete is in the middle of the competition period. A game has been rescheduled due to inclement weather. Adjustments to his strength training program will effect which of the following? Macro cycle Micro cycle Mesocycle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Micro cycle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"比賽因天候改期屬短期變動，只需調整當週的微週期（microcycle）結構，不必改動mesocycle或macrocycle。"},{"id":"q2181","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does muscle imbalance increase the risk of injury?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A disparity between the strength of the agonist muscle and antagonist will cause the weaker of the two to pull or strain disproportionately which may result in injury. Stronger quads the hams can cause the hams to pull when running is an example","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"失衡致傷機制：主動肌與拮抗肌之間力量差距過大，較弱的一側會被不成比例地拉扯；例如股四頭肌對膕旁肌比例過大時，跑步中膕旁肌更容易拉傷。"},{"id":"q2182","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tetanus","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"When twitches begin to merge and eventually completely fuse","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"強直收縮（tetanus）：刺激頻率提高時，個別twitch逐漸融合成持續的完全收縮；此處指收縮融合現象，非破傷風疾病。"},{"id":"q2183","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Classify these tests as either \"COD\" or maneuvarability: Reactive agility, 505, pro agility, t-test, illinois agility, L-run","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"COD: Reactive agility test, 505, proagility, t-test Maneuverability: T-test, illinois agility, L run","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"測驗分類：預先規劃變向（COD）的測驗含505、pro-agility（5-10-5）、T-test、Illinois與L-run；agility測驗另需對刺激作反應，reactive agility test屬此類。"},{"id":"q2184","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ch. 17 Training programs designed for improving muscular endurance should include","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Usually 2 to 3 sets of 12 or more","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"提升肌耐力的課表設計：一般2–3組、每組12下以上，採較輕負荷（≦67% 1RM）。"},{"id":"q2185","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cellulite","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the subcutaneous fat, commonly found in the thighs and butt usually appears dimpled.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"蜂窩組織（cellulite）：皮下脂肪，多見於大腿與臀部，皮膚外觀呈凹凸不平。"},{"id":"q2186","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Motor neuron (nerve cell)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"alpha motor neuron (cell body) motor neuron transmit nerve impulses from the spinal cord to the muscle fiber. The alternation of the mueline and nodes allows an electical current to quickly move down the axon with impulses \"Jumping\" from node to node. end at neuromuscular junction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動神經元（神經元本體）：alpha運動神經元的細胞體位於脊髓，將神經衝動傳至肌纖維，是觸發收縮的傳出路徑。"},{"id":"q2187","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What other factors do you need to consider when determaining training frequency?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Other training (ex: sport skill) - Physically demanding jobs or other activities - both may reduced training frequencies and increase needed recovery","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"決定訓練頻率的其他考量：額外的專項技術訓練、耗體力的工作或其他活動——兩者都可能要求降低頻率並拉長恢復。"},{"id":"q2188","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"3. The soccer team is transitioning from off-season to preseason training. How should the team’s resistance training frequency be altered? a) Increase frequency to improve muscular endurance b) Do not change frequency and add plyometrics c) Decrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice d) Design a split routine with three days on and one day off","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c) Decrease frequency to allow increased sport skill practice","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"休賽期轉入前賽季時，應下調重量訓練頻率以騰出專項技術練習時間（答案c）。"},{"id":"q2189","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Action potential","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Is an electrical impulse that is trigger by the rapid depolarization of the cell membrane of a neuron which sets in motion a series of events -release of calcium ions onto the sarcomere -ends with the contraction of a muscle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動作電位：神經細胞膜快速去極化產生的電訊號，引發鈣離子釋放至肌小節等一系列事件，最終以肌肉收縮作收場。"},{"id":"q2190","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A parent informs the coach that their child is Tanner’s Stage 1. What does that mean?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Regarding their Biological age- Tanner stages classification documents and tracks the development of secondary characteristics of children in puberty. Stages 1-5 (prepubertal-adult level)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Tanner階段1代表青春期前（prepubertal）；Tanner 1–5量表追蹤青春期第二性徵發展，5為成人程度，用以評估生物年齡而非實際年齡。"},{"id":"q2191","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the Cunningham equation for calculating resting metabolic rate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"500 + (22 x FFM(kg)) = RMR Multiply RMR by activity factor to get TDEE (total daily energy expenditure)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Cunningham公式：RMR = 500 + 22 × 去脂體重FFM(kg)；RMR再乘活動係數得到每日總能量消耗（TDEE）。"},{"id":"q2192","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An athlete is using interval training to increase the capacity of the oxidative energy system. Which of the following work-to-rest ratios is most appropriate? 1:5 1:3 1:1","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1:1","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練氧化（有氧）能量系統應採1:1工作休息比；1:3、1:5較偏向偏無氧的系統。"},{"id":"q2193","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How can muscle balance be avoided?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"By utilizing proper exercise selection that has the proper ratio of strength, power, muscular endurance from one muscle group to the other. Does not mean equal strength.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"避免肌力失衡：靠適當的練習選擇，讓肌群間肌力、功率與肌耐力維持正確比例，不必追求力量相等。"},{"id":"q2194","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Slow-Twitch","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"MU's develop force and relax slowly Long twitch time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"慢縮運動單位：產生張力與放鬆都較慢，twitch時間長。"},{"id":"q2195","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT General preparatory phase:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"\"offseason\" Phase:Hypertrophy/strength endurance Intensity: 50-75% 1RM Volume: high, 3-6sets, 8-20 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"重量訓練一般準備期（休賽期）：肥厚／肌耐力階段，強度50–75% 1RM，高容量3–6組、8–20下。"},{"id":"q2196","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ch. 17 Training programs designed for improving muscular strength should include","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 to 6 sets of less than or equal to 6 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"提升肌力的課表設計：2–6組、每組6下以內（至少85% 1RM）。"},{"id":"q2197","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cholesterol","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the lipids found on in animal products and produced by the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"膽固醇（cholesterol）：存在動物性食物中的脂質，人體自身也會合成。"},{"id":"q2198","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle spendles","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sense muscle tension, eccentric muscle contraction. sends an impulse to the spinal cord. In the spinal cord the signal coming from the sensory neuron synapses with a motor neurons,which travel back to muscle fiber. motor neurons activate muscle cauing \"streatch reflex\". this cause muscle contraction, the spindle shorten,the sensory impulse stop. Increasing loads cauing the spindles to strech more. The muscle force(Fm) and power are potentialed by this reflextive contraction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌梭（muscle spindle）：感受肌肉被牽拉的張力；離心拉長時傳入衝動到脊髓，excite運動神經元引發牽張反射（stretch reflex），不自主地增強肌肉的力量與功率輸出。"},{"id":"q2199","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Erogentic Aids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Protein Powder Nitric Oxide - focus and clarity, O2 flow Testosterone Creatine - energy BCAA's - protein synthesis, glucose metabolism, immune system & brain function Beta Alanine - improves high intensity Carnitine - fatty acid burn MCT - endurance adn fat burn Steroid, Hgh, Blood Doping","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"輔助 ergogenic aids：蛋白粉、一氧化氮（血管擴張）、睪固酮、肌酸（能量）、BCAA（蛋白質合成）、β-丙胺酸（高強度表現）、左旋肉鹼（脂肪酸氧化）、MCT、類固醇、HGH、輸血興奮劑（blood doping）。"},{"id":"q2200","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is the purpose of step 4 (exercise order) when developing resistance training protocols?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Determine how to structure a session to maximize performance ability and adaptation from the session","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"步驟4（練習順序）的目的：安排課內練習次序，讓表現能力與訓練適應最大化。"},{"id":"q2201","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"DURING A SINGLE TRAINING SESSION, WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EXERCISE SEQUENCES IS THE MOST APPROPRIATE FOR THE STRENGTH/POWER PHASE OF AN ATHLETE’S PROGRAM? a. POWER CLEAN, BENCH PRESS, BACK SQUAT, BENT OVER ROW, LEG (KNEE) CURL b. LEG PRESS, FRONT SQUAT, SNATCH, PUSH PRESS, INCLINE BENCH PRESS c. LUNGE, PEC DECK, HI AB/ADDUCTION, SNATCH, LATERAL RAISE d. PUSH PRESS, SHOULDER PRESS, POWER CLEAN, DEADLIFT, POWER PULL","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a. POWER CLEAN, BENCH PRESS, BACK SQUAT, BENT OVER ROW, LEG (KNEE) CURL","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力／功率階段課表順序：先功率動作（power clean），再核心多關節動作（臥推、後蹲），assistance由大至小排序（俯立划船、腿彎舉）——選項a正確。"},{"id":"q2202","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tropomyosin","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"is a protein involved in skeletal muscle contraction. It helps control when a muscle contracts and when it doesn't. Muscles should only contract when they get a rush of calcium ions. Wraps around helically around troponin on the actin filament which prevents the myosin cross bridge","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"原肌球蛋白（tropomyosin）：螺旋包覆在actin上，靜止時阻擋myosin橫橋結合位；鈣離子結合troponin後移位，才允許收縮發生。"},{"id":"q2203","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is an example of a second-class lever?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Standing calf (heel) raise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二類槓桿例子：站姿提踵——支點在腳尖、阻力在中間、施力點在腳跟，是省力槓桿。"},{"id":"q2204","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A Strength-based athlete needs help with their intake. What carb and protein recommendation would you give?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"5-6g/kg Carbs 1.4-1.7g/kg protein 1.7-2g/kg protein for weight gain","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力量型選手營養處方：碳水化合物5–6 g/kg、蛋白質1.4–1.7 g/kg；欲增重時蛋白質可達1.7–2 g/kg。"},{"id":"q2205","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Explain the karvonen method in finding target heart rate for an athlete:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"220 - age = APMHR APMHR - resting heart rate = heart rate reserve HRR x exercise intensity = _____ and add their resting heart rate back to it for their target heart rate based on karvonen method, which takes resting heart rate into account","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Karvonen法：HRmax=220−年齡；心跳儲備HRR=HRmax−安靜心跳；目標心跳=HRR×強度%＋安靜心跳，納入安靜心跳較準確。"},{"id":"q2206","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What exercises should be emphasized to remedy muscle imbalance across a joint?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Curls vs Tri, Squats vs SL Deadlift, Bench Press vs Lat Pull down, etc.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"矯正跨關節肌力失衡：成對訓練主動肌與拮抗肌，例如彎舉對三頭伸展、蹲舉對單腿硬舉、臥推對滑輪下拉。"},{"id":"q2207","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Fast-Twitch","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"MU's develop force and relaxes rapidly Slow twitch time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"快縮運動單位：快速產生張力並快速放鬆，twitch時間短（題卡誤寫twitch time長，應為短）。"},{"id":"q2208","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT specific preparotory phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"offseason/preseason phase: basic strength intensity: 80-90%1RM Volume: mod/high 2-6sets, 2-6reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"重量訓練專項準備期：基礎力量階段，強度80–90% 1RM，中至大容量，2–6組、2–6下。"},{"id":"q2209","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ch. 17 Training programs designed for Hypertrophy should include","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3 to 6 sets of 6 to 12 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肥厚（hypertrophy）課表設計：3–6組、每組6–12下。"},{"id":"q2210","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Circuit Training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to a training technique that involves moving from one exercise to another usually 10 to 12. Each exercise works a different muscle group until each muscle has been worked.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"電路訓練（circuit training）：連續輪流完成約8–12個練習站，每站針對不同肌群，讓全身依序得到訓練。"},{"id":"q2211","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"GTOs- Golgi tendon organs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"@ musculotendinous junction and detect tension change in an active muscle,acting as a feedback mornitors. GTO to realx the muscle via the inhibitory interneuron \"Autogenic inhibition\"-- when contracting muscle stimulates the GTOs cauing the opposing muscle to relax. GTOs protecting the muscle form over load.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官（GTO）：位於肌肉肌腱交界，偵測主動收縮時的張力變化，經抑制性中間神經元引發自生抑制（autogenic inhibition），讓肌肉放鬆以防超載受傷。"},{"id":"q2212","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"LISS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Low Instensity Steady State Moderate Cardio, metabolism triggered only while producing work, maintenance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"LISS低強度恆定有氧：只在運動中消耗熱量，多用於恢復與維持。"},{"id":"q2213","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How should Power, other core & assistance exercises be ordered in a session?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Power exercises should be done first - Non power core exercises second - Assistance exercises last","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"練習順序：功率動作最先，非功率核心動作其次，assistance練習放最後。"},{"id":"q2214","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHEN DESIGNING AN IN-SESON RESISTANCE TRAINING PROGRAM FOR BASKETBALL TEAM WITH LIMITED TRAINING TIME, WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EXERCISE ARRANGEMENTS IS THE MOST EFFECTIVE AND MINIMIZES THE LENGTH OF THE REST PERIODS NEEDED BETWEEN BODY AREAS? a. BENCH PRESS, SHOULDER PRESS, HANG CLEAN, LUNGE b. SHOULDER PRESS, HANG CLEAN, LUNGE, BENCH PRESS c. LUNGE, HANG CLEAN, SHOULDER PRESS, BENCH PRESS d. HANG CLEAN, BENCH PRESS, LUNGE, SHOULDER PRESS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"d. HANG CLEAN, BENCH PRESS, LUNGE, SHOULDER PRESS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"賽季時間有限時應上下肢交替以縮短休息：hang clean（功率）→臥推（上肢）→弓步（下肢）→肩推（上肢），選項d能縮短總課時。"},{"id":"q2215","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Acetylcholine","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Primary neurotransmitter involved in muscular contraction. -action potential is released and arrives at nerve terminal, acetylcholine is released from the terminal and diffuses across the neuromuscular junction, exciting the sarcolemma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"乙醯膽鹼（acetylcholine, ACh）：支配骨骼肌收縮的主要神經傳導物質；動作電位抵達軸突末梢時ACh釋放並擴散過突觸間隙，excite肌膜。"},{"id":"q2216","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All innervates muscle fibers of a motor unit fully contract when stimulated due to:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"All-or-none principle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動單位內所有肌纖維受刺激即完全收縮，依據的是全或無原則（all-or-none principle）。"},{"id":"q2217","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How do you calculate lean body mass (LBM) for Cunningham equation when given body fat %?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"BW x BF decimal Subtract that number from BW That is your LBM For instance, if body weight is 69kg and body fat is 9%, then: 64 x .09 = 5.76 64 - 5.76 = 58.24 LBM Cunningham is 500 + (22 x 58) = 1776 RMR 1776 + TDEE = kcal recommendation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"去脂體重演算法：體重×體脂%=脂肪重，體重減去脂肪重得LBM，再代入Cunningham RMR=500+22×FFM(kg)。例：64 kg、體脂9%→LBM≈58.2 kg→RMR約1781 kcal，再依活動係數換算TDEE。"},{"id":"q2218","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A high school cross country runner what’s to improve her speed-endurance. Which of the following types of training is most important? Interval Pace/tempo Fartlek","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Interval","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"越野跑選手想增進速度耐力，最重要的是間歇訓練（interval）；配速跑與fartlek偏重一般耐力。"},{"id":"q2219","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why is exercise order important?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Because exercises need to be arranged so that an athlete's maximal force capabilities are available to complete a set with proper exercise technique.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"練習順序重要，因為要讓運動員保留足夠的力量能力，才能以正確技術完成每組動作。"},{"id":"q2220","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type I","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Slow-Twitch More efficient Fatigue Resistant High Capacity for Aerobic E+ supply Limited potential for Rapid Force Development Low ATPase activity and Low Anaerobic power","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一型纖維：抗疲勞、有氧供給效率高；快速產力潛力有限，肌凝蛋白ATPase活性與無氧功率皆低。"},{"id":"q2221","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT first transition","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"precompetitive phase: strength/power intensity: low to very high (50-93% 1RM volume: low: 1-3 sets 1-3 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一次過渡期：肌力／功率階段，強度低至極高中（50–93% 1RM），低容量1–3組、1–3下。"},{"id":"q2222","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Cool Down","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the part of an exercise program that follows the workout and reduces the heart rate.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收操（cool down）：課後讓心跳率逐漸回落、促進恢復的時段。"},{"id":"q2223","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Somatic nervous system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The somatic nervous system innervates skeletal muscles and is responsible for consious control of voluntary movements","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"軀體神經系統（somatic nervous system）：支配骨骼肌，負責意識控制下的自主運動。"},{"id":"q2224","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"HIIT","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"High Intensity Interval Training Sprint Training w/Low moderate intervals Burns during and post","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"HIIT高強度間歇訓練：高強度衝刺搭配短休息，運動中與運動後持續耗能。"},{"id":"q2225","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What cosiderations shluld be given to mentsl a physical fatigue regarding exercise order?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Higher technique exercises should be done first to avoid loss of form due to fatigue - larger》 smaller muscle groups","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"練習順序需顧及身心疲勞：技術要求高的動作排前面以防動作變形，肌群安排從大到小。"},{"id":"q2226","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHAT IS THE EXERCISE ORDER (STEP 4)THAT SHOULD BE USED?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"POWER, OTHER CORE EXERCISES THAT ARE NON POWER, THEN ASSISTANCE (MULTI JOINT BEFORE SINGLE, LARGE MUSCLES THEN SMALL)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"練習順序（步驟4）：功率→非功率核心→assistance；多關節先於單關節、大肌群先於小肌群。"},{"id":"q2227","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Golgi Tendon Organs GTO","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Responsible for inhibiting tension overload in a muscle. -prevents injuries buy relaxing muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官（GTO）：抑制肌肉張力超載，以放鬆機制保護肌肉免於受傷。"},{"id":"q2228","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following increases as an adaptation to chronic resistance training, but decreases with aerobic training? Maximal power production or creatine phosphate stores","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Maximal power production","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"慢性重量訓練會增加、但有氧訓練會降低的是最大功率輸出；磷酸肌酸存量兩者皆增加。"},{"id":"q2229","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the three monosaccharides?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sucrose, glucose, galactose","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"單醣為葡萄糖、果糖、半乳糖三種；題卡答案誤列蔗糖——蔗糖是雙糖。"},{"id":"q2230","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A S&C professional is working with an athletic trainer to recondition a cross-country runner following an ankle injury. During which of the following phases is it appropriate to introduce rotations on a wobble board? Inflammation Repair Remodeling","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Repair","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"腳踝傷後，wobble板旋轉等平衡與本體感覺練習應在修復期（repair）引入。"},{"id":"q2231","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does exercise order change throughout the training cycle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Off-season routines can be split to increase training time without increasing days. Pre-season training the frequency is decreased from the off-season to allow more time to apply to the specific sport skill. In-season need to be planned so they don't affect the athlete's performance on days of competition, less frequency.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"練習順序隨訓練週期調整：休賽期可採分化增加訓練量；前賽季降低頻率配合專項技術；賽季中安排以不影響比賽日表現為原則。"},{"id":"q2232","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIa/IIb","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fast-Twitch Inefficient and fatigable Low Aerobic Power Rapid Force Development High Actomyosin acitivites","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二型a/x纖維：快縮、效率差且易疲勞、有氧功率低，但肌凝蛋白ATPase活性高、能快速產力。"},{"id":"q2233","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT Competition","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"In season Phase: peaking or maintenance Intensity: very high to low (50-93 1RM) / mod to high (85-93 1RM) Volume: very low (1-3 sets x1-3) / low-mod2-5 sets x3-6","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"賽季中：peaking（>93% 1RM、1–3組×1–3下的極低容量）或維持（85–93%、2–5組×3–6下）。"},{"id":"q2234","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Crunches","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Exercises that isolate the abs without stress on the lower back. Crunches are preferred over sit-ups.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"捲腹（crunches）孤立直腹肌且較不增加下背壓力，優先於仰臥起坐。"},{"id":"q2235","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Autonomic nervous system (ANS)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The ANS innervates smooth and cardiace muscle, as well as glands. it is also responseible for visceral motor actions. The ANS sometime called the involuntary nervous system, is not under conscious control. it has two subdivision: the sympathetic and parasymathetic nervous system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"自主神經系統（ANS）：支配平滑肌、心肌與腺體，負責內臟的不隨意機能，分為交感與副交感兩個系統。"},{"id":"q2236","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Olders Individuals (40+)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Benefit : LMM, Bone Density decrease volume - 20 max set body wt & resistance bands higher rep (10-15 - focus on conditioning) increased R.P. Focus on flexibility and ROM (yoga & stretching)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"40歲以上成人：重量訓練維持去脂體重與骨密度；單次訓練不超過約20組、採10–15下、延長組間休息，並著重柔軟度與活動度訓練。"},{"id":"q2237","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are the advanrages to alternating upper and lower body exercises within a session?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Rest one while training other - Good for begginers that find doing multiple exercises for same muscle group consecutively to hard - Can reduce session lengtg if time is a limiting factor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"上下肢交替安排的優點：練一區時另一區休息；對新手較輕鬆，時間受限時也能縮短總課時。"},{"id":"q2238","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"INVOLVES 2 SEQUENTIALLY PERFORMED EXERCISES THAT STRESS TWO OPPOSING MUSCLES OR MUSCLE AREAS (AGONIST AND ITS ANTAGONIST)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"SUPERSET","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"套餐式訓練（superset）：連續進行的兩個練習，針對互為拮抗的兩個肌肉或肌群區域。"},{"id":"q2239","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sympathetic Feverous System \"Flight or Fight\"","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Releases adrenaline and norepinephrine which causes increased rate of respiration, elevates heart rate, raises mental focus, increase body temp. -Key component for competition prep. -","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"交感神經系統（fight-or-flight）：釋放腎上腺素與正腎上腺素，提高呼吸率、心跳、專注度與體溫，是賽前準備的生理基礎。"},{"id":"q2240","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 12-year old has been resistance training twice a week for six weeks. Which adaptations contribute the most to training-induced strength gains? Increased muscle size Increased motor unit activation Greater testosterone concentration","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased motor unit activation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"12歲學童訓練6週後的力量成長主要來自運動單位動員能力提升（神經adaptations）；肌肉肥大與睪固酮變化在此年齡尚不明顯。"},{"id":"q2241","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the equation for estimating BMI?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Weight (kg) / heigh (cm) 2 (Weight(lbs) / height (in) 2) x 703 Normal- 18.9-24.9 Over 25-29.9 Obese 30 and up","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"BMI=體重(kg)/身高(m)²；英制為[體重(lb)/身高(in)²]×703。正常18.5–24.9、過重25–29.9、肥胖≥30。"},{"id":"q2242","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female collegiate basketball forward has continued resistance training while playing during the competitive period. Which of the following program is most appropriate? 8 reps x 3 sets @ 85% 2 reps x 3 sets @ 85% 6 reps x 3 sets @40%","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 reps x 3 sets @ 85%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"籃球前鋒賽季中續訓：以低容量高強度維持，3組×2下@85%最合適，8下×3組與40%×6下容量過高或強度過低。"},{"id":"q2243","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does exercise order change based on the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A push-pull order is good for athletes coming back from rehab. Super & Compound Sets are good for conditioned athletes and are time efficient. Upper & Lower are good for untrained athletes and are time efficient as well.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"依訓練目的選擇順序安排：推／拉交替適合復健者；套餐式與compound set適合訓練有素者且省時；上下肢分化適合新手且省時。"},{"id":"q2244","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIx","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Human muscle fibers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Type IIx為人類骨骼肌中的快縮糖解纖維；人類肌纖維分型為I、IIa、IIx，傳統的IIb說法在人體即對應IIx。"},{"id":"q2245","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"RT Second transition","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"post season Phase: active rest Intensity/Volume; recreational activities","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二次過渡期：季後的積極休息（active rest），以休閒性活動恢復身心。"},{"id":"q2246","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Dehydration","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the loss of fluids from the body to below normal levels.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"脫水（dehydration）：體液流失低於正常水位，會損害表現與體溫調節。"},{"id":"q2247","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Somatic nervous system (SNS)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"prepare the body for the action \"fight-or-flight system\" pull the blood all around to muscles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"題卡把somatic nervous system（軀體神經系統，負責隨意運動）誤寫成fight-or-flight；戰或逃其實是交感神經（sympathetic）的功能，注意兩者縮寫相近但不同。"},{"id":"q2248","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Younger Individuals","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"under 10 - body weight only - focus on balance and control 10-14 - calisthenics 15 - light wt. reduce reps, focus on form, endurance, FUN","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"兒童青少年訓練原則：10歲以下僅用體重、練平衡與控制；10–14歲做徒手體操；約15歲起匯入輕重量，強調動作品質、肌耐力與樂趣。"},{"id":"q2249","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is the advantahe of an alternated push/pull session structure?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Alternating push and pull exercises ensure the same muscle group will not be used in 2 consecutive exercises thus maximizing recovery and thereby performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"交替推／拉的結構優點：相鄰兩個練習不會用到同一肌群，讓恢復最大化、表現維持最佳。"},{"id":"q2250","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"INVOLVES SEQUENTIALLY PERFORMING 2 DIFFERENT EXERCISES FOR THE SAME MUSCLE GROUP","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"COMPOUND SET","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"compound set：針對同一肌群連續進行的兩個不同練習。"},{"id":"q2251","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Parasympathetic nervous system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Responsible for relaxation, decreased activity levels. -Detrimental to competition","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"副交感神經：主導放鬆與低活動狀態，賽前過於優勢反而不利競爭表現。"},{"id":"q2252","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following best describes the effect on mechanical advantage as a resistance moment arm shortens? Increases, decreases, or no change","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increases","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"阻力力臂變短時，肌肉所需輸出的力矩下降，機械優勢（mechanical advantage）增加。"},{"id":"q2253","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The energy requirement of adults is determined by what 3 factors?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Resting metabolic weight Thermic effect of food Physical activity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"成人能量需求由三部分決定：基礎代謝率、食物熱效應（TEF）與身體活動消耗。"},{"id":"q2254","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A male collegiate volleyball players is in the power phase of the S&C program. Which of the following is most appropriate? 2 reps x 3 sets @95% 3 reps x 4 sets @80% 10 reps x 4 sets @70%","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3 reps x 4 sets @ 80%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"排球選手功率階段（多重努力）：4組×3下@80%；95%×2下偏最大力量，70%×10下偏肥厚／耐力。"},{"id":"q2255","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the methods for arranging resistance training exercises within a training session?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Core (multi-joint) exercises receive priority as they have direct application to the sport. Assistance exercises (single) are less important and are good for rehab or injury prevention. Structural exercise is a core exercise and involves posture, power exercise is a structural exercise that is performed very quickly or explosively.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動作安排：核心多關節動作優先（直接應用於專項），assistance單關節動作次之（復健與預防傷病）；structural屬核心姿勢類動作，power動作是以極快速度執行的核心動作。"},{"id":"q2256","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Motor Unit Recruitment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"MU's are composed of Fibers with specific Morphological/physiological characteristics that determine their functional capacity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動單位組成：同一運動單位內的肌纖維具有相同形態與生理特性，決定其功能表現。"},{"id":"q2257","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"List the typical exercise time and work to rest ratio to stress each of these systems: Phosphagen, fast glycolysis, fast glycolosis and oxidative, oxidative","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Phosphagen: 5-10s, 1:12 - 1:20 Fast Glycolysis: 15-30s, 1:3-1:5 Fast glycolysis/oxidative: 1-3min, 1:3-1:4 Oxidative: >3min, 1:1-1:3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"各能量系統工時與工作休息比：磷酸原5–10秒、1:12–1:20；快糖解15–30秒、1:3–1:5；快糖解＋氧化1–3分鐘、1:3–1:4；氧化系統3分鐘以上、1:1–1:3。"},{"id":"q2258","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Diuretic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to any agent that increases the flow of urine.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"利尿劑（diuretic）：任何增加尿液排出的物質，易造成脫水與電解質流失。"},{"id":"q2259","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Parasympathetic nervous system (PNS)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"\"Resting and digestion system\" responsesible for digestive tract mobility, smooth muscle activity assosiated with urination, defecation, pupil constriction and gland secretion.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"副交感神經系統（rest and digest）：負責胃腸蠕動、排尿排便、瞳孔縮小與腺體分泌。"},{"id":"q2260","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ectomophs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"naturally thin, fidgetty, eat what they want, tall & lanky high caloric diets heavy wts (5-8R), longer RP, Low volume (20RperSet), minimal cardio compound > isolated FULL BODY","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"外胚型（ectomorph）：天生偏瘦難增重；採高熱量飲食、大重量（5–8下）、長休息、低容量，以複合動作與全身性訓練為主，少量有氧。"},{"id":"q2261","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is a superset & its advantages?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- The preformance of 2 exercises consecutivly w/o rest that target opposing muscles - Increases training demand in time efficent manor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"套餐式訓練（superset）：無休息連續做兩個針對拮抗肌群的練習，用省時方式提高訓練密度。"},{"id":"q2262","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"THE AMOUNT OF WEIGHT ASSIGNED TO AN EXERCISE SET AND IS OFTEN CHARACTERIZED AS THE MOST CRITICAL ASPECT OF A RT PROGRAM","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"LOAD","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷（load）：分配給一組練習的重量，被視為重量訓練計畫中最關鍵的成分。"},{"id":"q2263","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Antagonist muscle Action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Performing a protective action. -Decelerate force action on the body. -Stabilizing joints Example Resistive action of the hamstring during any squatting movement.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"拮抗肌動作：扮演保護性角色——減速動作、穩定關節，例如蹲舉過程中膕旁肌的對抗控制。"},{"id":"q2264","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A 17-yo tennis player follows an aerobic training program 3 days per week at 70% HRmax for 4 weeks. Which of the following is going to increase? Stored creatine phosphate Body fat percentage Maximal rate of force production","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Stored creatine phosphate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"70% HRmax有氧訓練4週後最可能增加的是儲存的磷酸肌酸；體脂應下降，最大肌力產出速率則偏向重量訓練的效益。"},{"id":"q2265","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are three disaccharides?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sucrose, lactose, maltose Sucrose is glucose and fructose combined","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"三種雙糖：蔗糖（葡萄糖＋果糖）、乳糖（葡萄糖＋半乳糖）、麥芽糖（葡萄糖＋葡萄糖）。"},{"id":"q2266","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Calculating load-volume (the total amount of weight lifted in a training session).","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Multiply sets and reps, and then multiply that number by loaded lifted. (If different sets are performed with different amounts, volumes per set are calculated and then added together)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷容量（load-volume）：組數×下數×重量；各組重量不同時先逐組計算再相加。"},{"id":"q2267","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Why should a particular exercise order be chosen over another?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A push-pull order is good for athletes coming back from rehab. Super & Compound Sets are good for conditioned athletes and are time efficient. Upper & Lower are good for untrained athletes and are time efficient as well.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"選擇順序安排的理由：推拉交替適合復健{return}；套餐式與compound set適合訓練有素者、省時；上下肢分化適合新手、省時。"},{"id":"q2268","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Recruitment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The number of MU's activated","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動員（recruitment）：指被啟動的運動單位數量。"},{"id":"q2269","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench, Squat, and Power Clean Norms (60th percentile) for men's D1 power sports (i.e: bball, baseball)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"235,285,220","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男子D1power專項（籃球、棒球等）第60百分位參考值：臥推235、蹲舉285、power clean 220（磅）。"},{"id":"q2270","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Dynamic Stretching","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Involves stretching movements performed at gradually increased speed.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"動態伸展（dynamic stretching）：以逐漸加快的速度反覆執行伸展動作，適合熱身。"},{"id":"q2271","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscles Type","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Smooth muscle Cardiac muscle Skeletal muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌肉三大類：平滑肌、心肌、骨骼肌。"},{"id":"q2272","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Mesomorphs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"athletic, muscular, any program works","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"中胚型（mesomorph）：天生健壯有肌肉、對訓練反應佳，多數課表都適用。"},{"id":"q2273","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is a compound set?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- The sequential performance without rest of 2 exercises that invole the same muscle group - Stress in compounded time efficently","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"compound set：同一肌群的兩個練習無休息連續進行，累積刺激且省時。"},{"id":"q2274","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"THE PRODUCT OF FORCE AND DISPLACEMENT (DISTANCE)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"MECHANICAL WORK","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"機械功（mechanical work）＝力×位移。"},{"id":"q2275","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Neuromuscular Junction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Key element in muscular contraction -The location of acetylcholine release that starts muscular contraction. -High intensity activities increase surface area of NMJ, length of nerve branching, and synapse locations increased and dispersed more widely PROVES that anaerobic training can improve neural transmission.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"神經肌肉接點：乙醯膽鹼釋放處、收縮的關鍵；高強度訓練可增加NMJ表面積、神經分支長度與突觸分佈，證明無氧訓練能改善神經傳導。"},{"id":"q2276","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What best identifies the joint actions during the upward phase of the push press exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Rapidly flex the hips, knees and ankles and then the arms to push the bar overhead","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"push press上舉階段的關節動作：快速伸展髖、膝、踝（腿部驅動），接著伸展手臂把槓鈴推過頭。"},{"id":"q2277","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are three examples of polysaccharides?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Complex carbs Starch, fiber, glycogen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"多醣（複合碳水化合物）：澱粉、纖維、肝糖。"},{"id":"q2278","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During strength/power phase, what is reasonable for a single-effort power event athlete? (Like shot put, high jump, weightlifting)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sets of 1 or 2 repetitions using loads of 80-90% on heavy days.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"單次努力功率專案（鉛球、跳高、舉重）在功率階段：重日做1–2下、80–90% 1RM。"},{"id":"q2279","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"When should the flexibility, plyometric, aerobic, warm-up, and cool-down exercises be performed during the training session?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Warm-up, plyo, aerobic, cool-down, flexibility","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"課內成分順序：熱身→增強式→重量訓練／有氧→收操→柔軟度（靜態伸展放最後）。"},{"id":"q2280","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Change in Force Production","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Change in frequency of activation of individual motor units Change in Number of Activated Motor Units","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"改變出力產量的兩個途徑：改變個別運動單位的放電頻率（頻率總和），或改變被動員的運動單位數量。"},{"id":"q2281","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench, Squat, and Power Clean norms for mens D1 Strength sports (football, rugby)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"300,400,260","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男子D1力量型專項（美式足球、橄欖球）第60百分位參考值：臥推300、蹲舉400、power clean 260（磅）。"},{"id":"q2282","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ectomorph","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to a body type that is characterized by a light build and slight muscular development.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"外胚型（ectomorph）：輕薄骨架、肌肉發育不發達的體型。"},{"id":"q2283","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle fiber type","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Type I -- slow twist muscle fiber Type IIa -- fast twist muscle fiber Type IIx -- type IIb","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌纖維分型：第一型＝慢縮纖維；第二型a＝快縮氧化糖解纖維；第二型x＝傳統所稱的IIb型快縮纖維。"},{"id":"q2284","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endomorphs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"obese, gain easily, perpetual dieter low caloric diet light wt, higher reps short RP to induce Metabolism Compound (advanced techniques) focus on fat loss","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"內胚型（endomorph）：易增重；採低熱量飲食、輕負荷高次數、短休息以提高代謝，複合動作為主，目標以減脂為先。"},{"id":"q2285","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is involved in step 5 (training load & repetitions) of resistance program desgin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Determining: set, rep, load & rest schemes for optimal adaptations","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"步驟5（訓練負荷與次數）：決定組數、次數、負荷與休息的組合，以達成最佳適應。"},{"id":"q2286","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"THE QUANTITY THAT IS HIGHLY RELATED TO MECHANICAL WORK AND THE ASSOCIATED METABOLIC ENERGY DEMANDS AND PHYSIOLOGICAL STRESS AND IS ALSO DISTINGUISHED FROM REP-VOLUME","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"LOAD-VOLUME","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷容量（load-volume）：與機械功、代謝能量需求及生理壓力高度相關，有別於次數容量（rep-volume）。"},{"id":"q2287","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which is a marker of aerobic overtraining? Decreased total testosterone concentration Increased muscle glycogen stores Increased resting catecholamine level","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Decreased total testosterone concentration","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧（耐力型）過度訓練指標：總睪固酮濃度下降（伴隨皮質醇升高）；肝糖儲存不會增加。"},{"id":"q2288","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the female triad? Male?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Low energy availability, menstrual dysfunction, low bone mineral density. Men: energy deficiency, reproductive suppression, poor bone health","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女運動員三聯症：能量可用性不足、月經功能失調、骨密度降低；男性類似表現為能量不足、生殖機能受抑制與骨健康不良。"},{"id":"q2289","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For multiple-effort power events like basketball and volleyball, what is the appropriate rep count during the power phase?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3-5 reps per set with load of 75-85% 1RM","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"籃球、排球等多重努力專案的功率階段次數：每組3–5下、75–85% 1RM。"},{"id":"q2290","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How is a rep max used to determine training loads?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Loads are calculated as a % of a tested or estimated 1RM; training loads are specifically determined from multiple-RM testing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"用RM決定訓練負荷：以實測或推算的1RM百分比計算；也可由多次RM測驗直接換算負荷。"},{"id":"q2291","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Preloading","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle fibers that are active early in the range of motion will not be fully activated unless the muscle is Loaded Prior to Muscle Action","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"預先負荷（preloading）：在動作範圍早期就已參與的肌纖維，若肌肉收縮前未先負載，將無法被完全動員。"},{"id":"q2292","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench and squat norms for Men's National Soccer","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"175, 330","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男子國家級足球選手參考值：臥推175、蹲舉330（磅）。"},{"id":"q2293","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Electrolytes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to minerals such as chloride, sodium, potassium, calcium, and magnesium.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"電解質：氯、鈉、鉀、鈣、鎂等礦物質，維持體液平衡與神經肌肉功能。"},{"id":"q2294","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle Type I","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"low ATPase activaity Slow Ca2+ handling ability large mitochondria resistance to fatigue edurance sport","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一型肌纖維特性：ATPase活性低、Ca2+調控較慢、粒線體大而多、抗疲勞，適配耐力專案。"},{"id":"q2295","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endurance Athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cyclists, dancers, swimmers, runners Long & lean individuals not very muscular Light wts/ high rep short RP Mix of compound / isolated higher volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"耐力型選手的訓練風格（腳踏車、舞蹈、游泳、長跑）：輕負荷高次數、短休息，複合與孤立動作混合、高容量。"},{"id":"q2296","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Define mechanical work.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The product of force and displacment. Important to quantify to avoid exahustion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"機械功＝力×位移；量化它是為了監控總量、避免過度疲勞。"},{"id":"q2297","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"THE TOTAL NUMBER OF REPETITIONS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"REP-VOLUME","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"次數容量（rep-volume）：一次訓練課中完成的總次數。"},{"id":"q2298","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During a single exercise session, what training variable should be decreased to product greater ATP production capacity?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Intensity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"單次課中調低訓練強度（相對提高容量）較能提升ATP產能（磷酸肌酸儲存與酵解酵素能力）。"},{"id":"q2299","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Current research suggests that athletes looking to lose fat mass should increase their protein intake to:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.8-2.7 g/kg BW Helps circumvent loses in lean mass while trying to lose weight. Also promotes satiety and fullness with each meal.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Nutrition Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"減脂期建議把蛋白質提高到1.8–2.7 g/kg體重/天，減重時防止去脂體重流失，並增加每餐飽足感。"},{"id":"q2300","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is impulse? Define and give the equation.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The change in momentum resulting from force = force x time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"衝量（impulse）：力與其作用時間的乘積等於動量變化，F×t＝Δp。"},{"id":"q2301","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Is the assignment of training loads different based on the exercise? Explain.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Yes. Depending on the area of the body and the training goals, different loads can be assigned (75% of 1RM for upper body, 85% of 1RM for lower body) for different exercises affecting the different parts of the body. Different for Core and assistance exercises.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷指派因練習而異：依身體部位與目標調整，例如上肢約75% 1RM、下肢約85% 1RM；核心與assistance動作的處方也不同。"},{"id":"q2302","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Proprioceptors","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Specialized sensory receptors Located in: - Joints - Muscles - Tendons Sensitive to: - Pressure - Tension Responsible for: - Kinesthetic Sense - Conscious Appreciation of Body Position - Muscle tone - Complex Coordinated Movements","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"本體感受器（proprioceptors）：位於關節、肌肉、肌腱，感受壓力與張力，負責動覺、身體位置感知、肌張力與複雜協調動作。"},{"id":"q2303","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench, Squat, and Power Clean norms for Womens D1 Power sports (Bball, Vball, baseball)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"100, 140, 100","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女子D1power專項（籃球、排球等）參考值：臥推100、蹲舉140、power clean 100（磅）。"},{"id":"q2304","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Empty Calories","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A term used to indicate food contributing calories with little food value and nutrients. Examples are alcohol and simple sugars.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"空熱量（empty calories）：只供應熱量、幾乎無營養價值的食物，如酒精與精製糖。"},{"id":"q2305","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sport that require type I&II fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Rowing Tennis Boxing Wrestling Soccer","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"同時需要第一型與第二型肌纖維的運動：划船、網球、拳擊、摔角、足球。"},{"id":"q2306","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Strength Trained Athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sports & Stop/Go Muscular Heavy wts/ low reps plyometric short RP to improve fatigue tolerance Compound exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力量型選手（停停走走型、肌肉負荷高的專案）：大重量低次數、搭配增強式、短休息提升抗疲勞能力，以複合動作為主。"},{"id":"q2307","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How is volume load or work in weight lifting terms calculated?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Load x reps x sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"容量負荷（volume load）＝負荷×次數×組數。"},{"id":"q2308","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"FOR THE SHOULD PRESS EXERCISE, HOW MANY REPETITIONS CAN TYPICALLY BE PERFORMED WITH A LOAD OF 85% OF THE 1RM?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"6","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肩推以85% 1RM約可做6下（%RM與可完成次數對照）。"},{"id":"q2309","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endergonic reactions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Chemical reaction that is initiated by previously released energy being absorbed by reactants in order to initiate a status change. -Anabolic processes are consider endergonic reactions because requires release of energy prior. -Muscular contraction is endergonic because of release of energy substrate is also required prior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"吸能反應（endergonic）：需要吸收能量才能進行的化學反應；合成代謝與肌肉收縮都屬吸能反應，須由ATP供能驅動。"},{"id":"q2310","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What will be improved the most by increasing the strength of the hip flexor muscles?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Maximum speed","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"強化髖屈肌最有助提升最大衝刺速度——擺動階段的抬腿驅動來自髖屈肌。"},{"id":"q2311","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the SAID principle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Specificity adaptation to imposes demands The more similar the training is to sport movement, the greater transfer to the sport.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"SAID原則：針對所施加需求的特定適應（Specific Adaptation to Imposed Demands）；訓練與專項動作越相似，轉移效果越大。"},{"id":"q2312","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the importance of determining an athlete's rep max (1RM or 10RM)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Knowing the 1RM or 10RM allows the trainer to assign proper training loads based off of a % of the RM. See table 15.7 on page 394","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"量測RM的意義：知道1RM或10RM後，才能按百分比指派精確的訓練負荷。"},{"id":"q2313","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Muscle Spindles","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Proprioceptors in modified muscle fibers in the sheath of connective tissues Provide Info On: - Muscle Length - Rate of Change in Length","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌梭（muscle spindle）：位於特化肌纖維外鞘內的本體感受器，提供肌肉長度與其變化率的資訊。"},{"id":"q2314","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench, squat , and power clean norms for womens lacrosse","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"100, 160, 100","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女子 lacrosse 參考值：臥推100、蹲舉160、power clean 100（磅）。"},{"id":"q2315","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endomorph","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to a body type that is characterized by a stocky build, wide hips, and heavy fat storage.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"內胚型（endomorph）：矮壯厚實、臀部寬、易堆積脂肪的體型。"},{"id":"q2316","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sympathetic nervous system (SNS)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The SNS prepares the body for action and is sometimes called the flight-or-flight system. During exercise, the SNS is responsible for directing blood away from the digestive tract and skin and toward the skeletal muscles, heart, and brain. Physiological response associated with the SNS include increased blood pressure (PB), heart rate, and blood glucose levels; sweating ; and dialation of the pupils and lung bronchioles.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"交感神經系統（SNS）：讓身體進入戰或逃狀態；運動時把血液自胃腸與皮膚改分配至骨骼肌、心臟與腦，並提升血壓、心跳、血糖，出汗與瞳孔、支氣管擴張。"},{"id":"q2317","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Competitive Sports","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"More intense W/O Advanced technique compound heavy wt/short RP UE/LE splits","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"競賽期選手：更高強度、進階技術與複合動作、大重量短休息、上下肢分化安排。"},{"id":"q2318","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is 1RM and #RM?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- 1RM is the max weight able to be use for one repitition - #RM is the max load able to be lifted for a predetermined # of reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"1RM＝只能完成一次的極限重量；#RM＝能完成指定次數的極限負荷。"},{"id":"q2319","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"AN ATHLETE IS PERFORMING THREE SETS OF THE SNATCH EXERCISE. WHAT IS THE VOLUME LOAD OF THE WORK OUT SHOWN BELOW? SET 1 SET 2 SET 3 LOAD REPS LOAD REPS LOAD REPS 100 6 115 4 125 2","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"(100X6)+ (115X4)+ (125X2)=1,310","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"容量負荷＝100×6＋115×4＋125×2＝1310。"},{"id":"q2320","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ATP Adenosine Triphosphate Adenine group, Ribose group, 3 inorganic phosphates","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ATP is energy source for endergonic reactions i.e. muscular contraction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"ATP（三磷酸腺苷）：由腺嘌呤、核糖與三個磷酸基組成，是吸能反應（如肌肉收縮）的直接能量來源。"},{"id":"q2321","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What will decrease the power output of an athlete performing the snatch exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increasing the load from 90-95% of an athlete’s 1RM","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"snatch負荷從90%提高到95% 1RM會降低功率輸出——負擔過重使動作速度下降。"},{"id":"q2322","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What phases are in the preparatory phase? Give percentages and volume levels as well.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Hypertrophy/endurance: 50-75% high volume low test Basic strength: 80-90% moderate volume moderate rest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"準備期包含兩階段：肥厚／肌耐力50–75% 1RM高容量；基礎力量80–90% 1RM中容量、中等休息。"},{"id":"q2323","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What steps are involved when determining an athlete's rep max (1RM or 10RM)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A common strategy for testing is to conduct a 1RM test in several core exercises and use multiple-RM testing for assistance exercises.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"RM測驗策略：在數個核心動作做1RM測驗；assistance動作改用多次RM測驗。"},{"id":"q2324","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Intrafusal Fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Modified Muscle Fiber with the Muscle Spindle attached to it Run parallel to normal Fibers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"梭內肌纖維（intrafusal fibers）：肌梭內部的特化纖維，與一般梭外肌纖維平行排列。"},{"id":"q2325","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bench and squat norms for womens D1 swimming","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"100,120","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女子D1游泳參考值：臥推100、蹲舉120（磅）。"},{"id":"q2326","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endorphins","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Substances in the brain that induce \"runner's high\" or good feelings during prolonged exercise.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"內啡肽（endorphins）：腦內物質，長時間運動時產生跑步者高潮與愉悅感。"},{"id":"q2327","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Smooth muscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"SMooth muscle has spindle-shaped fiber that are shorter and narrower than skeletal muscle fibers. Smooth muscle fibers only contain one nucleus and do not have stria tions. SHeets of these muscle fibers from the wall of blood vessels and the hallo organs of the urinary, digestive, respiratory and reproductive tracts. The contractionand relaxtion of smooth muscle is responsible for persitalsis which moves substances through the digestive tract","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"平滑肌：紡錘形、單核、無橫紋，構成血管壁與臟器壁；其收縮形成蠕動（peristalsis），推動胃腸內容物。"},{"id":"q2328","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Untrained Individuals / Beginners","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"machines light wt/ slow build increased R.P stretching is important to work ROM Calisthenics/Resistance Bands light volume (8-10R)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"新手／未受訓者：從器械與輕重量開始、逐步增加，可用徒手與彈力帶，8–10下低容量，休息時間較長，並重視柔軟度與活動度。"},{"id":"q2329","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What are the predicted reps attianable at 5% intervals of 1RM?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"100% = 1 95% = 2 90% = 4 85% = 6 80% = 8 75% = 10 65% = 15 Accuracy of theses values is widely variable Can be used to predict 1RM from #RM Chart on pg 452","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"%RM對照次數：100%→1下、95%→2、90%→4、85%→6、80%→8、75%→10、65%→15；個體差異大，也可反向推算1RM。"},{"id":"q2330","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"RELATES TO THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF WEIGHT LIFTED IN A TRAINING SESSION","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"VOLUME","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"容量（volume）：一次訓練課中舉起的總重量。"},{"id":"q2331","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hydrolysis of ATP","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process of breaking apart the high energy bonds of ATP in order to utilize the energy from these bonds. -Requires on molecule of Water and several enzymes to break apart the high energy bonds for energy -ATP>ADP>AMP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"ATP水解：以水與酵素分解ATP的高能磷酸鍵釋放能量；ATP→ADP→AMP。"},{"id":"q2332","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What adaptation results from heavy resistance training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased Type II fiber cross-sectional area","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"大重量訓練的適應：第二型肌纖維橫斷面積增加（肥大）。"},{"id":"q2333","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What phase of training happens in the first transition?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strength/power Single effort athletes: 87-95% 2-3 reps low volume Multi effort athletes: 75-90% 2-5 reps low volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一次過渡期＝肌力／功率階段：單次努力選手87–95%、2–3下；多重努力選手75–90%、2–5下；皆低容量。"},{"id":"q2334","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How is the rep max test chosen (1RM vs 10RM)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A common strategy for testing is to conduct a 1RM test in several core exercises and use multiple-RM testing for assistance exercises for sufficiently trained athletes. For untrained multiple-RM is needed instead of 1RM. 1RM should not be used for exercises that cannot provide valid and reliable data.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"1RM與多次RM的取捨：訓練有素者在核心動作測1RM；未受訓者改用多次RM；動作穩定性差的練習不適合測1RM。"},{"id":"q2335","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Extrafusal Fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Normal Muscle Fibers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"梭外肌纖維（extrafusal fibers）：肌梭外的普通骨骼肌纖維，負責產生張力。"},{"id":"q2336","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"average Vertical for male field sports","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"15-24inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男子field sports專項平均垂直跳：15–24英寸。"},{"id":"q2337","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Endurance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The ability to maintain a physical activity over time.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"耐力（endurance）：長時間維持身體活動的能力。"},{"id":"q2338","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"cardiac muscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"is only located in the wall of the heart and its contraction pump blood through the heart and the body's blood vessels.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心肌：僅存在於心臟壁，其泵壓收縮把血液打進心臟與全身血管。"},{"id":"q2339","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Difference between strength and size?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Dietary Needs Strength = maintence calories & overload Size = increased calories & 1MR","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"增力與增圍的差異：增力以維持熱量＋超載訓練為主；增圍需要熱量盈餘並搭配肥厚強度訓練。"},{"id":"q2340","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What should be considered before doing a 1RM test?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- should not be done with someone who is injured or medically supervised - experiance: shoukd only be done with intermidate or advance trained individuals- should not be done with someone who is injured or medically supervised - if a beginner 3RM may be a better choice because lack of technique and experiance increases risk of injury and deacreses accuracy of a 1RM test - if a beginner 3RM may be a better choice because lack of technique and experiance increases risk of injury and deacreses accuracy of a 1RM test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"1RM測驗前的考量：傷病者與需醫護監督者不適合；需具備正確技術與中高階訓練經歷；真正新手改測3RM較安全，否則誤差與受傷風險都高。"},{"id":"q2341","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHAT IS THE FORMULA FOR VOLUME-LOAD (LOAD VOLUME)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"FOR SET= # SETS X # REPS X WEIGHT PER REP FOR MULTIPLE SETS AND AMOUNTS OF WEIGHT TO GET TOTAL TRAINING SESSION LOAD-VOLUME=FIND VOLUME FOR EACH SET/WEIGHT/REPS AND ADD THEM TOGETHER","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷容量公式：單一組＝組數×次數×每次重量；多組不同重量時逐組算完再相加。"},{"id":"q2342","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sodium-Potassium ATPase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Responsible for sodium potassium balance by pumping out the sodium and pushing potassium into the cell. for every two K+ ions that are pumped into cell, three Na+ are pumped out. -cellular resting, proper fluid balance in cells","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"鈉鉀ATP酶（Na+-K+ ATPase）：每打入2個K+同時打出3個Na+，維持細胞靜息電位與細胞內液體平衡。"},{"id":"q2343","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What muscle acts as the agonist during the second pull of the power clean?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Trapezius","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"power clean第二次拉動（second pull）的主動肌：斜方肌（聳肩動作）。"},{"id":"q2344","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What lifting phase resides in the competition phase of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Peaking >93% low volume maintenance 80-85% moderate volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"賽季中對應的訓練階段：peaking（>93% 1RM、低容量）或維持（80–85%、中容量）。"},{"id":"q2345","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does the training load relate to the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Specific load and rep assignments via the RM continuum, a percentage of 1RM, or the results of multiple-RM testing can be applied to reach the training goal. Also the movement and physiological analysis of the sport and priorities of the sport season play a part. See table 15.9 page 401","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練負荷與目標的對應：依RM連續曲線以1RM百分比或多次RM測驗結果指派組數與次數，並參照專項動作分析與賽季優先順序。"},{"id":"q2346","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Average vertical for women field sports","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"11-19 inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女子田徑／field專項平均垂直跳：11–19英寸。"},{"id":"q2347","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Energy Balance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the relationship between energy intake (input of food) and energy output (energy expenditure)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"能量平衡：攝取熱量（飲食輸入）與能量消耗（輸出）之間的關係。"},{"id":"q2348","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Skeletal muscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"skeletal muscle is primary used in the movement of bones at joints and for maintaining posture","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"骨骼肌：主要用於帶動關節與骨骼運動，並維持姿勢。"},{"id":"q2349","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Injury Prevention / Recovery Techniques","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Start Slow Warmup / Cool Down - cardio & stretching Proper Clothing Stretching - foam Rolling Hot baths - Massages Rest - naps/sleep - 8hrs pm decrease stress pre/post nutrition Listen to the body - know when to back off Spotters - 10% rule - distractions CPT's - accountability motivation - STG/LTG - rewards - positive self talk","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"傷害預防與恢復手段：循序漸進、完整熱身與收操、合適裝備、伸展與 foam rolling、熱浴、按摩、每晚8小時睡眠、壓力管理、課前後營養、傾聽身體、保護者與10%法則、教練監督與長短目標、獎勵與正向自我談話。"},{"id":"q2350","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Why are 3RM tests being suggested as a substitue for 1RM tests?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Reduced risk - Greater accuracy in begginers who lack proper technique","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"建議以3RM取代1RM的理由：風險較低，且對技術不純熟的新手而言結果更準確。"},{"id":"q2351","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHEN AN EXERCISE TO BE DONE FOR 3 SETS 5 REPS WHAT IS THE APPROPRIATE LOAD ASSIGNMENT?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"5RM","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"某動作要練3組5下時，應以5RM的重量指派負荷。"},{"id":"q2352","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ADP Adenine, ribose, 2 inorganic phosphate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Can be converted to ATP with addition of inorganic phosphate which is achieved through creatine phosphate energy system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"ADP（二磷酸腺苷）：由腺嘌呤、核糖與兩個磷酸基組成；經磷酸肌酸系統加入無機磷酸即可再合成ATP。"},{"id":"q2353","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What contributes the most to shock absorption while running?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Eccentric plantar flexion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"跑步時吸收落地衝擊最主要的是踝的離心蹠屈控制——小腿三頭肌離心收縮緩衝著地衝擊。"},{"id":"q2354","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What phase is in the second transition?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Active rest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二次過渡期的階段：積極休息（active rest）。"},{"id":"q2355","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does training load relate to training volume?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Volume is based directly on the athlete's training goal. Usually the more volume the less load and vise versa. See table 15.11 page 406.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷與容量的關係：容量依訓練目標而定，兩者通常此消彼長——負荷越高、容量越低。"},{"id":"q2356","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Heart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscular organ comprised of two interconnected but separate pumps; the right side of the heart pumps blood through the lungs, and the left side pumps blood through the rest of the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心臟：由兩個相連但各自獨立幫浦組成的肌性器官——右側把血液打進肺迴圈，左側打進全身。"},{"id":"q2357","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Average male bball vertical","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"28 inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"男子籃球平均垂直跳：約28英寸。"},{"id":"q2358","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Energy Expenditure","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Is the energy cost to the body of a physical activity, usually measured in kilocalories.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"能量消耗（energy expenditure）：身體進行某項身體活動所需的能量成本，以千卡（kcal）計。"},{"id":"q2359","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type I muscle fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Type I muscle fibers: also known as slow-twitch muscle fibers (slow-oxidative fibers), metabolically, these fibres have a large capacity for aerbic energy supply and relatively resistant to fatigue. Type I fibers have a limited ability to rapidly generate force because of their low anaerobic capasity and low myosin ATPase activity. COmpair to Type II fibers, type I muscle fibers have slower calcium-handing abilities, contract more slowly, have reduce glycilytic capacity, and they habe neurous and relative ly large mitochondria. Type I muscle fibers play an important role in edurance sports have rely on a susstained energy supply, such as long distance running, soccer, cross-country skiing, and distance cycling and swimming.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第一型肌纖維（慢縮氧化型）：有氧能量供給容量大、抗疲勞；因無氧容量與肌凝蛋白ATPase活性低，快速產力有限；Ca2+調控較慢、收縮較慢、糖解能力較低，粒線體多且較大；是長跑、足球、越野滑雪、距離腳踏車與游泳等耐力專案的關鍵。"},{"id":"q2360","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"R.I.C.E.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Rest Ice Compression Elevation IF injuried Take time off - minimal 1 week re-evaluate the plan talk to a CPT, P.T.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"急性傷害處理RICE：休息（Rest）、冰敷（Ice）、加壓（Compression）、抬高（Elevation）；至少停止該訓練一週，再與防護員與肌力教練一起重新評估計畫。"},{"id":"q2361","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What exercises should be used for 1RM tests?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Core exercises because they invole large muscle groups and multiple joints making them better able to deal with heavy loads - Chosen exercise should also have a stable easy to maintain form ex: fkat bench Poor Ex: bent over row, relies on postural muscles of the low back which can fatigue before 1RM is reached","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"適合1RM測驗的動作：大肌群、多關節、動作形式穩定的核心動作（如臥推）；較差範例是俯立划船——下背姿勢肌會先力竭。"},{"id":"q2362","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EXPLAINS WHY THIS EXERCISE (BENT OVER ROW) SHOULD NOT BE 1RM TESTED? a. THE DELTOIDS ARE NOT A LARGE MUSCLE GROUP b. ACCURATE AND CONSISTENT RESULTS CANNOT BE GATHERED c. ONLY ONE MUSCLE GROUP IS INVOLVED d. THE EXERCISE IS NOT A MULTIPLE-JOINT EXERCISE","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"b. ACCURATE AND CONSISTENT RESULTS CANNOT BE GATHERED","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"俯立划船不適合測1RM的原因：下背姿勢肌群先疲勞，無法取得準確且一致的結果；不是因為肌群大小或關節數。"},{"id":"q2363","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Phosphagen System","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Relies on the hydrolysis of ATP from local muscle stores, as well as the break down of creatine phosphate. -Active system during intense brief exercise. -This system is active during all activities but for short time before other energy systems become predominate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統：依靠肌肉內既存ATP水解與磷酸肌酸分解供能，是高強度短暫運動的主要供能系統；所有活動初期都由它先行供應，隨後其他系統接管。"},{"id":"q2364","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following increases serum testosterone most during resistance training? High intensity (10RM) Short rest period (30-60 seconds) Moderate resistance (67-85%)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Short rest period (30-60 seconds)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"重量訓練中最能提高血清睪固酮的條件：短組間休息（30–60秒）。"},{"id":"q2365","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the normal order of exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power (snatch, hang clean, jerk) Non-power core exercises (multi-joint) Assisted exercises (single-joint)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"正常練習順序：功率（snatch、hang clean、jerk）→非功率核心（多關節）→assistance（單關節）。"},{"id":"q2366","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How are intensities (HR, RPE) established for aerobic endurance training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The higher the intensity the shorter exercise duration. Monitoring O2 consumption during exercise to determine VO2max or measuring blood lactate are the best ways to establish proper intensity.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力訓練強度（心跳率、自覺強度）的設定：強度越高、持續時間越短；以運動中量測耗氧量訂VO2max或血乳酸值是確認強度的最佳方法。"},{"id":"q2367","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Atrium","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Left and Right Deliver blood into the Right/Left Ventricles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心房（左、右）：把血液送入對應的左／右心室。"},{"id":"q2368","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Average female bball vertical","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"19","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["NSCA-CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"女子籃球平均垂直跳：約19英寸。"},{"id":"q2369","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Defined as planned, structured, and repetitive bodily movement done to improve or maintain one or more components of physical fitness.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動（exercise）：為增進或維持體適能成分而做的企劃性、結構化、反覆性身體活動。"},{"id":"q2370","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIa muscle fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Type IIa muscle fibers also known as fast-twitch muscle fibers, these fibers are energy inefficient, easily fatigable, and have low aerbic power. Type IIa muscle fiber have a moderate capcity for both anerobic and aerobic energy production. These fibers can be classified as fast-oxidative/glycolytic fibers and they can rapidly generate force duce to high myosin ATPase activity and anerobic power. Type IIa fibers are surrounded by a greater number of capilaries then type IIx fibers, allowing for greater aerobic metobolism.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二型a肌纖維（快縮氧化糖解型）：易疲勞、有氧功率低，但有氧與無氧產能皆屬中等；肌凝蛋白ATPase活性高、能快速產力；微血管供應比第二型x豐富，有利有氧代謝。"},{"id":"q2371","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Max Strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1RM = 100% Maximum Strenght 1-3 Reps 3'-5' RP's between","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最大肌力訓練：1–3下（接近100% 1RM），組間休息3–5分鐘。"},{"id":"q2372","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How should a 1RM test be preformed?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1) Warm up with a weight that allows 5-10 reps 2) Rest for 1 minute 3) Load a weight that individual can complete 3-5 reps with 4) Rest for 2 mins 5) Increase weight by 10-20lbs for upper body exercises or 30-40lbs for lower body exercises shoukd be able to complete 2-3 reps 5A) Might requier lower increases for less trained athletes 6) Rest 2-4 mins 7) Repeat increase 8) Attempt 1RM 9) If sucessful rest increase repeat 10) if failed rest decrease repeat","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"1RM測驗程式：以可做5–10下的重量熱身→休息1分鐘→加重至約3–5下的重量→休息2分鐘→每次增加上肢10–20磅、下肢30–40磅→每次休息2–4分鐘逐次加重→嘗試1RM；成功則再加重，失敗則減重重試。"},{"id":"q2373","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING PERCENTAGES OF THE 1RM TYPICALLY WILL ALLOW AN INDIVIDUAL TO PERFORM 12 REPETITIONS OF THE BENCH PRESS EXERCISE? a. 55% b. 67% c. 75% d. 77%","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"B. 67%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"約67% 1RM可讓人在臥推完成12下。"},{"id":"q2374","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"CP Creatine phosphate PCr phosphocreatine","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Used as a rapid energy resource for high intensity muscular contractions. -This system resynthesizes ATP by adding inorganic phosphate group creatine to ADP molecule via and enzymatic process involving creatine kinase.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸（CP/PCr）：高強度收縮的快速能量庫；由肌酸激酶把磷酸基從磷酸肌酸轉給ADP，快速再合成ATP。"},{"id":"q2375","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A female college athlete began S and C program 10 weeks ago. In the following weeks, she continues to see gains, what most likely contributes to this change?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased muscle fiber size","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"大學女籃訓練10週後持續進步，最可能來自肌纖維面積增加（肥大）。"},{"id":"q2376","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What happens in phase 3 of SSC?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Concentric- it’s the body’s response to I and II phases. Shortening of agonist muscle. Elastic energy is releases from SEC Alpha neuron stimulates agonist muscle group","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"拉長縮短週期（SSC）第三階段：向心階段——主動肌縮短；先前儲存在彈性元件的彈效能釋放，α運動神經元興奮主動肌群。"},{"id":"q2377","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does the target HR change with different modes of aerobic training (long slow distance, interval training)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"For LSD 80% of max HR so you will be in the THR zone a longer period of time (about 40 mins or so). Interval training is close to VO2max. See pages 498-499","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練心跳目標因模式而異：長距離慢速（LSD）約80% HRmax、維持約40分鐘；間歇訓練強度接近VO2max。"},{"id":"q2378","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ventricles","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Left and Right Supply the main force of blood through: - Pulmonary - Peripheral Circulations","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心室（左、右）：提供把血液送入肺迴圈與體迴圈的主要動力。"},{"id":"q2379","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Extension","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the straightening of a body part away from the body. An example is straightening the elbow.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"伸展（extension）：身體部位遠離軆幹的伸直動作，例如伸直手肘。"},{"id":"q2380","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Type IIx muscle fiber","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Type IIx muscle fibers : also type of fast-twistch muscle fiber (sometime called type IIb fibers0, Type IIx fibers have less capacity for aerobic energy production,making them more fatigable then type IIa fibers. Type IIx fibers, considered to be fast-glycolytic (FG) fibers, have the grested=st capacity for anaerobic energy and the fastest shortening velocity so they can generate significant force. Note that many sports require both type I and Type II muscle fibers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"第二型x肌纖維（快縮糖解型，舊稱IIb）：有氧產能低、比IIa更快疲勞；無氧產能最高、縮短速度最快，能產生很大力量。"},{"id":"q2381","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Strength Speed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"90% of 1RM Body Builders 3-5 Reps, 1-2' RP Heavy wt Fantasic Size & Strength","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"力量—速度（strength-speed）：90% 1RM、3–5下、休息1–2分鐘；大負荷，兼顧圍度與力量。"},{"id":"q2382","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How could to estimate 1RM for a true beginner?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Use a 10RM test: - 10RM is not a good measure of power lower reps is preferable - Weight should be increase after warm up such that max is reached within 3-5 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"真正新手推算1RM：採10RM測驗（低次數估計較準）；熱身後逐步加重，在3–5組內抵達極限。"},{"id":"q2383","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING COMBINATIONS OFGOAL REPETITIONS AND SETS MOST EFFECTIVELY PROMOTES MUSCULAR HYPERTROPHY? GOAL REPS SETS a) 10 2 b) 6 2 c) 10 4 d) 6 4","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"10 REPS 4 SETS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"最能促進肌肉肥大的組次陣列合是4組×10下（中高容量）。"},{"id":"q2384","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Creatine Kinase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Enzyme that potentiates the replenishment of ATP molecule of energy utilization in the phosphagen system. -Creatine kinase elevation in blood test= muscle damage from heat attack, kidney failure, or rhabdomyolysis. _Rhabdomyolysis is caused by rapid breakdown of muscle tissue from too much work acutely or over the week","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌酸激酶（creatine kinase）：催化磷酸肌酸快速再合成ATP的酵素；血中CK升高代表肌肉損傷——心肌梗塞、腎衰竭，或訓練量過大引發的橫紋肌溶解症。"},{"id":"q2385","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"A novice athlete has been following an aerobic endurance training program for 12 months. What is most likely to occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased resting stroke volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"新手進行有氧耐力訓練12個月後最可能出現：安靜心跳輸出量增加（安靜心跳率通常不變）。"},{"id":"q2386","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What occurs in Phase 2 of SSC?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"amortization phase Time between eccentric and concentric The most crucial phase in allowing greater power production Type 1a nerves synapse with alpha neuron","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"SSC第二階段：緩衝期（amortization）——離心與向心之間的轉換時間；越短越能利用儲能提升功率，第一類（Ia）傳入神經與α運動神經元在此形成突觸。"},{"id":"q2387","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is training volume?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"It is the total amount of weight lifted in a training session.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練容量：一次訓練課中舉起的總重量。"},{"id":"q2388","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Chambers of the Heart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Atria Ventricles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"心臟的四個腔室：兩心房與兩心室。"},{"id":"q2389","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Fat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An essential nutrient that provides energy, energy storage and insulation to the body.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"脂肪：必需營養素，提供能量、儲存能量並隔熱保護身體。"},{"id":"q2390","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Motor unit recruitment patterns","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Motorunits contain only one type of muscle. The ability to produce force is a requirement in all sport activities. There are two ways that motor units modulate force production: summnation size pronciple","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"運動單位動員模式：同一運動單位只含同型肌纖維；力量調節有兩個機制——頻率總和與大小原則（size principle）。"},{"id":"q2391","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Speed Strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"70% of 1RM 8-12 R, 30-45\"RP mediocre wt Toning Good Metabolic Rate Conditioning Continue with SAME wt throughout entire Set Quick Muscles, but not large","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"速度—力量（speed-strength）：70% 1RM、8–12下、休息30–45秒；提高代謝率、塑造肌肉線條。"},{"id":"q2392","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What % of 1RM should be used if the individuals goal is strength and for how many reps per set & how many sets?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"85%, 6 reps or less for 2-6 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力目標的強度：85%以上1RM、每組6下以內、2–6組。"},{"id":"q2393","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"IF THE TRAINING GOAL IS STRENGTH WHATS THE APPROPRIATE GOAL REPETITIONS AND SETS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"6 OR LESS REPS; 2-6 SETS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力目標的組次數：6下以內、2–6組。"},{"id":"q2394","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Adenylate kinase reaction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Enzyme that converts two ADP to ATP+AMP. -Significant in maintenance of cellular energy homeostasis, and crucial in stimulating glycolysis via increased AMP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"腺苷酸激酶反應：2 ADP→ATP＋AMP；維持細胞能量恆定，產生的AMP增加可促進糖解。"},{"id":"q2395","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following muscles acts isometrically during the deadlift exercise? Gastrocnemius Erector spinae Or Rectus femoris","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Erector spinae","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"硬舉中豎脊肌採等長收縮維持脊柱中立；腓腸肌與股直肌則是動態動作。"},{"id":"q2396","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Concept of optimal functioning theory","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Different people perform best with different levels of arousal.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"個最佳功能區理論（individual zones of optimal functioning）：不同選手在不同的興奮（arousal）水準下表現最佳。"},{"id":"q2397","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the different measures of training volume? How are they calculated?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Rep-Volume is total number of reps in a session Load-Volume is total number of sets x reps x weight. Ex - 2 sets of 10 reps with 50 pounds = 1000 pounds.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"容量的計算指標：次數容量＝總次數；負荷容量＝組數×次數×重量，例如2組×10下×50磅＝1000磅。"},{"id":"q2398","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Prevents Flow of Blood from the Ventricles back into the Atria During Systole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Tricuspid Valve Mitral Valve (bicuspid) Atrioventricular Valves (AV)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收縮期防止血液從心室逆流回心房的是三尖瓣與二尖瓣（bicuspid），即房室瓣（AV瓣）。"},{"id":"q2399","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"FITT","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A theory governing proper frequency, intensity, time, and type of exercise.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"FITT：運動處方的四項原則——頻率（Frequency）、強度（Intensity）、時間（Time）、型別（Type）。"},{"id":"q2400","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Summation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Summantion is dependent uppon how frequently motor units are activated. a single activation will cause a minimal muscle twistch with little force production, but if that motor unit continues to be activated at a greater frequency, there can be a summnative effect of thoese twitches, resulting in greater force production.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"總和（summation）：運動單位放電頻率越高，個別twitch累積疊加，產生的張力越大。"},{"id":"q2401","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Speed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"60% of 1RM Enduracne, Conditioning, Cardiovascular Light wt, high reps, low RP 12-15 Reps, 10-30\" RP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"速度／耐力取向訓練：60% 1RM、12–15下、休息10–30秒；輕負荷、高次數、短休息，偏重心肺與代謝條件。"},{"id":"q2402","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What % of 1RM should be used if the individuals goal is power and for how many reps per set & how many sets?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Single effort event: - 80-90%, 1-2 reps, 3-5 sets Multiple effort event: - 75-85%, 3-5 reps, 3-5 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率目標的處方：單次努力80–90% 1RM、1–2下、3–5組；多重努力75–85%、3–5下、3–5組。"},{"id":"q2403","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"IF THE TRAINING GOAL IS POWER WHATS THE APPROPRIATE GOAL REPETITIONS AND SETS 1. FOR A SINGLE EFFORT EVENT 2. MULTIPLE EFFORT EVENT","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. SINGLE EFFORT= 1-2 REPS X 3-5 SETS 2. MULTIPLE EFFORT= 3-5 REPS X 3-5 SETS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率目標的組次數：單次努力1–2下×3–5組；多重努力3–5下×3–5組。"},{"id":"q2404","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Law of Mass Action/Mass action effect","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The concentration of a reactant or a product is wholly dependent on establishing equilibrium within the system. -ATP equilibrium means various enzymatic activities must continue throughout the exercise session in order to maintain threshold ATP levels, and once stimulus is reduced or ceased, then these processes will stop","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"質量作用定律：反應的方向與速率取決於反應物與產物的濃度；ATP恆定意味運動全程需各種酵素持續運作以維持ATP閾值，刺激停止後這些過程隨即減緩。"},{"id":"q2405","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An 18yp college rugby player is participating in a resistance prog. What is primarily responsible for the increases in strength during the first 8 weeks?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Motor unit synchronization","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"18歲橄欖球選手訓練前8週的力量成長主要來自神經適應——運動單位同步化（motor unit synchronization）。"},{"id":"q2406","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Describe the inverted U theory","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Arousal facilitates performance up to an optimal level, further increases begin to reduce performance.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"倒U假說 (inverted U theory)：喚醒程度 (arousal) 會提升表現直到最佳水準；超過該水準後，再升高的喚醒反而使表現下降。曲線呈現先升後降的倒U形。"},{"id":"q2407","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What activities or sports require training with high volumes? Low volumes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strength less that 6 reps, 2-6 sets. Power single 1-2 reps, 3-5 sets. Power multi 3-5 reps, 3-5 sets. Hypertrophy 6-12 reps, 3-6 sets. Muscular endurance more that 12 reps, 2-3 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練量需配合目標：肌力 <6下、2-6組；單次輸出功率 1-2下、3-5組；多次輸出功率 3-5下、3-5組；肥大 6-12下、3-6組；區域性肌耐力 >12下、2-3組。負荷愈低、下數愈高，組數配置相對愈少。"},{"id":"q2408","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Systole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Ventricular Contraction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收縮期 (systole)：心室收縮的階段，將血液擠出心臟，送入肺迴圈或體迴圈。"},{"id":"q2409","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Flexibility","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the ability to flex and extend the body's joints through their full range of motion.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"柔軟性 (flexibility)：指關節在其完整活動範圍 (ROM) 內屈伸的能力，是健康與運動表現的構成要素之一。"},{"id":"q2410","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Size principle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The second method for production is dependent upon how many motor units are activated. if greater force is needed for an activity, more motor units will be recruited. This phenomenon theresholds, any firing rates. Smallest motor units are recruited first, ans as more force is needed, larger motor units (that innervate more muscle fibers) are activated. Ascending recruitment of movements when force changes,while conserving energy.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"大小原則 (size principle)：產生力量依賴運動單位 (motor unit) 的動員數目。需要愈大的力，就動員愈多運動單位；最小的運動單位（運動神經元閾值最低）最先被 recruit，隨力量需求增加再依序動員較大的運動單位。此順序性招募可節省能量。"},{"id":"q2411","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Program Designs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Size/Strength = heavy wt 1-5 Reps Strength/Toning/ Power/FatLoss = Moderate Wt 8-12 Reps Speed/Condition/Cardiovasular = Light Wt 12-20 reps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"課程設計參考：肌肉尺寸/肌力目標用大重量 1-5下；肌力/雕塑/功率/減脂用中等重量 8-12下；速度/體能/心肺用小重量 12-20下。負荷與下數依目標反向搭配。"},{"id":"q2412","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What % of 1RM should be used if the individuals goal is hypertrophy and for how many reps per set & how many sets?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"67-85%, 6-12 reps, 3-6 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肥大 (hypertrophy) 目標：使用 67-85% 1RM，每組 6-12 下，每次 3-6 組。中高負荷搭配中等下數與組數是肥大訓練的標準處方。"},{"id":"q2413","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"IF THE TRAINING GOAL IS HYPERTROPHY WHATS THE APPROPRIATE GOAL REPETITIONS AND SETS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"6-12 REPS X 3-6 SETS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肥大目標的次數與組數：6-12 下 × 3-6 組，對應約 67-85% 1RM 的負荷。"},{"id":"q2414","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glycolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Process of breaking down carbs in the form of glycogen or glucose in the blood to replenish ATP. -Enzymatically driven process but not fast because of multiple steps involved. -Can produce greater amount of ATP over time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"糖解 (glycolysis)：將肝醣或血糖分解以再合成ATP的酵素驅動過程。因步驟多，速度不如磷酸系統快，但短時間內可產出較多ATP；終產物為丙酮酸，有無氧氣決定後續走向。"},{"id":"q2415","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"High school 1600meter running trains aerobically for 2 years. She improves when performance time throughout the course of her first season. What is primarily responsible for her increases?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Improvement in VO2 max","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"長期有氧訓練（如1600公尺中距離跑）使成績進步，主要來自最大攝氧量 (VO2max) 提升，即心肺輸送與利用氧的能力改善，而非肌肉結構的快速變化。"},{"id":"q2416","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the difference between process and outcome goals?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Process goals are daily effort-related tasks where athlete feels in control Effort is expended = success occurs","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"過程目標 (process goal) 是運動員每天可控的努力與技術任務，付出努力即算成功；結果目標 (outcome goal) 著重比賽名次等結果，不完全在運動員控制之內。"},{"id":"q2417","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How can training volume be manipulated to meet training goals (hypertrophy, etc)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strength less that 6 reps, 2-6 sets. Power single 1-2 reps, 3-5 sets. Power multi 3-5 reps, 3-5 sets. Hypertrophy 6-12 reps, 3-6 sets. Muscular endurance more that 12 reps, 2-3 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"以訓練量達成目標：肌力 <6下、2-6組；單次功率 1-2下、3-5組；多次功率 3-5下、3-5組；肥大 6-12下、3-6組；區域性肌耐力 >12下、2-3組。"},{"id":"q2418","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Prevents Backflow from the Aorta and Pulmonary Arteries into the Ventricles during Diastole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Aortic Valve Pulmonary Valve (Semilunar Valves)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"半月瓣（aortic valve 主動脈瓣與 pulmonary valve 肺動脈瓣）：在心室舒張期防止血液自主動脈與肺動脈倒流回心室。"},{"id":"q2419","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Free Radicals","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to highly reactive molecules that are known to damage muscle fibers, causes inflammation and fatigue and the suppression of the immune system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"自由基 (free radicals)：高度活躍的分子，會損傷肌纖維、引發發炎與疲勞，並抑制免疫系統。"},{"id":"q2420","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Selective Recruitment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"This is an exception to the size principle. Under some circumstances, train athletes can inhibit the activation of small motor units. This allows larger motor units to be activated immidiately when rapid force production is needed.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"選擇性動員 (selective recruitment)：大小原則的例外。受過訓練的運動員在某些情況下可抑制小運動單位，直接啟動大運動單位，以在需要快速出力時立即產生大功率。"},{"id":"q2421","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What % of 1RM should be used if the individuals goal is muscular endurance and for how many reps per set & how many sets?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"No more than 67%, at least 12 reps, 2-3 sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"區域性肌耐力 (muscular endurance) 目標：不超過 67% 1RM，每組至少 12 下，2-3 組。"},{"id":"q2422","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"IF THE TRAINING GOAL IS MUSCULAR ENDURANCE WHATS THE APPROPRIATE GOAL REPETITIONS AND SETS","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"12 OR MORE REPS X 2-3 SETS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"區域性肌耐力目標的次數與組數：12 下以上 × 2-3 組，負荷 ≤67% 1RM。"},{"id":"q2423","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anaerobic glycolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Specifically refers to the production of ATP through the breakdown of glucose in a state of reduced oxygen \"fast\" glycolysis not dependent on oxygen to break down glucose. -Accomplished by the pyruvate that is converted to lactate to replenish ATP during high intensity. -System only operates until lactate threshold is reached, then slows until lactate is cleared.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"無氧糖解 (anaerobic glycolysis)：在缺氧狀態下分解葡萄糖快速產ATP的快糖解 (fast glycolysis)，丙酮酸被轉化為乳酸。此係統只能運作到乳酸閾值，超過後速率下降，直到乳酸被清除。"},{"id":"q2424","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What causes an athletes heart rate to increase during the anticipatory period immediately before the start of a race?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Parasympathetic activity decreases Sympathetic activity increases","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"賽前準備期心率上升的原因是自律神經調節：副交感神經活動降低、交感神經活動升高，使心率在比賽開始前就先提升（預期的生理準備）。"},{"id":"q2425","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the two key characteristics in evaluating test quality?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Validity- measures what it’s supposed to Reliability- measurement is repeatable","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"評估測驗品質的兩大特徵：效度 (validity，測到該測的東西) 與信度 (reliability，測量可重複、一致)。"},{"id":"q2426","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does training volume relate to the goal of training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Volume is based directly on the athlete's training goal.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練量 (volume) 直接取決於運動員的訓練目標：目標不同（肌力、功率、肥大、肌耐力），組數×次數的配置就不同。"},{"id":"q2427","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Diastole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Ventricular Relaxation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"舒張期 (diastole)：心室放鬆的階段，心臟擴張讓血液流入心室。"},{"id":"q2428","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Frequency","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to the number of times.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"頻率 (frequency)：指訓練進行的次數，例如每週的訓練節數 (training sessions per week)，是課程設計變項之一。"},{"id":"q2429","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Nerve Conduction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"When the electrical impulse from the motor neuron arrives at the motor junction, ACh is released, converting the impulse into a chemical stimulus. This generates an action potential- a wave of depolarization- that travel the length of the muscle fiber through the T-tubes, causing the release of Ca2+, which initiates the series of events leading to the contractile movement of the actin and myosin filaments.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"神經傳導與興奮-收縮耦合：運動神經衝動到達神經肌肉接點時釋放乙醯膽鹼 (ACh)，轉為化學刺激並在肌纖維上產生動作電位；去極化波經T小管傳遍肌纖維，促使鈣離子 (Ca2+) 釋放，啟動肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白的收縮滑動。"},{"id":"q2430","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"Why is power trained at a lower weight then strength?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power is a distance over time measure therefore a measure of maximal load able to be moved at a high speed In contrast strength is simply define by the load one is able to lift without a time constraint therefore the movent is much slower but deals with higher loads","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率訓練用較輕負荷，因為功率=力×速度，重視以高速度移動負荷；肌力則只定義為能舉起的最大負荷，無時間限制，動作較慢但可用更高重量。"},{"id":"q2431","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHEN A VOLLEYBALL PLAYER IS TRAINING FOR MUSCULAR POWER, WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING LOAD AND REPETITION COMBINATIONS IS MOST APPROPRIATE? LOAD (%1RM) GOAL REPETITIONS a. 75-80 1-2 b. 75-80 3-5 c. 85-90 1-2 d. 85-90 3-5","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"75-85 % 1RM AND 3-5 REPS","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"排球選手練肌力功率屬多次輸出功率：約 75-85% 1RM、3-5 下。75-80% 配 1-2 下太少、85-90% 太重在速度，故以 75-85%、3-5 下最合適。"},{"id":"q2432","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic Glycolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Requires pyruvate to enter into the mitochondrion of a cell and then when oxygen is present is oxidized and enters into the Krebs cycle. -","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"有氧糖解 (aerobic glycolysis)：氧氣存在時，丙酮酸進入細胞粒線體 (mitochondrion) 被氧化，轉為乙醯輔酶A進入克雷布斯迴圈 (Krebs cycle)，進行氧化磷酸化大量產ATP。"},{"id":"q2433","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What are the daily fat requirements (grams) and percentages?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"20-35% 2g/kg BW is required to replenish triglycerides after prolonged endurance of 2+ hours.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"每日脂肪需求：約佔總熱量 20-35%，約 2 g/kg 體重；超過2小時的長時間耐力訓練後需補充以回填三酸甘油酯。"},{"id":"q2434","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does cue utilization theory relate to athletic performance?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Athletes may not concentrate well at under-aroused levels. As arousal increases, attentional width decreases, enabling more focus","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"線索利用理論 (cue utilization theory)：喚醒不足時運動員難以集中注意；隨著喚醒提高，注意範圍變窄，有助專注於相關線索，但過高喚醒會漏掉重要線索而影響表現。"},{"id":"q2435","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How does volume relate to training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"For a beginner only 1-2 sets to start then add more sets as they progress until they reach the goals on table 15.11 page 406.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"訓練量要配合訓練狀態 (training status)：初學者先從 1-2 組開始，隨進度增加組數，逐步達到課程設計表（表15.11）中各目標的建議量。"},{"id":"q2436","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sinoartrial Node (SA)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The intrinsic pacemaker-where rhythmic electrical impulses are initiated","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"竇房結 (SA node)：心臟的內在節律器 (pacemaker)，是有節律的電衝動的起始點。"},{"id":"q2437","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Functional Living","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The ability to successfully and to safely perform activities related to a daily routine with sufficient energy, strength/endurance, flexibility, and coordination.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功能性日常生活 (functional living)：以足夠的能量、肌力/耐力、柔軟性與協調性，成功且安全地完成日常活動的能力。"},{"id":"q2438","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Electromyograph (EMG)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Surface and intermuscular EMG is used to assess the qulity and eletricity of the eletrical activity within skeletal muscle resulting from neural activation is implicated when there is an increase in EMG signal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌電圖 (EMG)：以表面或肌內電極評估骨骼肌受神經興奮所產生的電活動品質與強度；EMG 訊號增加代表神經活化程度提高。"},{"id":"q2439","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How could a power or strength program be designed to combat the high physiological stress the body take during the high load training and avoid overtraining?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- Program load variations into the weeks training sessions - Ex: have one day a week be the heavy day and 2 others be light and medium respectivly Monday: Heavy 85% 1RM Wednesday: light 80% load from Heavy day and preform same reps/sets even if able to do more Friday: medium 90% of heavy day same reps/sets","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高負荷訓練可排入負荷變化以避開過度訓練：例如一週內一天大重量 (85% 1RM)、一天輕重量（約大重量日的80%負荷）、一天中重量（大重量日的90%），即每日波動週期化 (DUP)，分散生理壓力。"},{"id":"q2440","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHAT ARE THE LOAD AND REPETITION ASSIGNMENTS BASED ON TRAINING GOAL WHEN THE GOAL IS FOR: STRENGTH","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"LOAD (%1RM): > OR = TO 85% GOAL REPS: < OR = TO 6","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肌力目標的負荷與次數：≥85% 1RM，次數 ≤6 下。"},{"id":"q2441","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Two types of Glycolysis Anaerobic/Aerobic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The difference between the two types of glycolysis is governed by what takes place in the mitochondrion of the cell . -If oxygen is present, then aerobic glycolysis with take place though oxidative phosphorylation. -No oxygen then the pyruvate molecule will undergo fermentation in order to produce sufficient ATP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"無氧/有氧糖解的差別取決於粒線體內的後續：有氧時丙酮酸進入粒線體走氧化磷酸化；缺氧時丙酮酸改走發酵（還原為乳酸）以維持ATP產出。"},{"id":"q2442","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Describe general adaptation syndrome (GAS) in relation to homeostasis.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The body’s response to a resistance training stimulus. Begins with new training stimulus, which drops you down below homeostatic levels and leads to fatigue. This is the general alarm phase. As the body recovers, it goes above homeostasis and rebuilds stronger, during adaptation supercompensation stage. At a certain point, called regression or involution, the body can no longer adapt and eventually will lead to overtraining if intensity of stimulus does not stop.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"一般適應症候群（GAS，5e 第24章 p1681）：新訓練刺激使身體偏離恆定 (homeostasis) 而出現疲倦（警戒期）；身體能抗住壓力時，適應／恢復期出現超量恢復 (supercompensation)、高於恆定、變得更強；若壓力持續、超過退化 (involution，5e 第18章 p1191；第21章 p1584) 點，身體無法再適應、表現持續下滑，最終導致過度訓練。（5e 通篇以 GAS 與 involution/detraining 表述，已不再使用 training adaptation syndrome〔TAS〕一詞。）"},{"id":"q2443","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Autogenic training in relation to relaxation methods.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Imagining a sense of warmth and heaviness for particular limb or muscle group.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"自律訓練法 (autogenic training)：一種放鬆技術，想像特定肢體或肌群出現溫暖感與沉重感，以降低喚醒與焦慮。"},{"id":"q2444","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How do the duration of the work and rest periods relate to the goal of training? To the involved energy systems?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"See table 2.7 on page 37. Phosphagen 5-10 secs of work; 1:12 to 1:20 ratio of rest. Fast Glycolysis 15-30 secs of work; 1:3 to 1:5 ratio of rest. Fast Glycolysis and Oxidative 1-3 mins of work; 1:3 to 1:4 ratio of rest. Oxidative greater 3 mins of work; 1:1 to 1:3 ratio of rest.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"工作與休息時間依能量系統設定：磷酸系統工作 5-10 秒、休息比 1:12-1:20；快糖解 15-30 秒、1:3-1:5；快糖解+氧化系統 1-3 分鐘、1:3-1:4；氧化系統 >3 分鐘、1:1-1:3。系統還原愈慢，休息比例愈高。"},{"id":"q2445","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Atrioventricular Node (AV)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Where impulses is delayed slightly before passing into ventricles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"房室結 (AV node)：傳導路徑上的延遲點，衝動在此稍作延遲後才進入心室，確保心房先收縮、心室後收縮。"},{"id":"q2446","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Glucose","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Refers to simple sugar; the form in which all carbs (carbohydrates) are used as the body's principal energy source.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"葡萄糖 (glucose)：單糖，是所有碳水化合物在體內被利用的形式，為身體主要的能量來源。"},{"id":"q2447","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Anatomical position","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The position where a person is sending with arms at the side and the palms of the hands facing forward. From this position, the body can be divided into three antomical planes that cut the body into sections. these antomical planes are important because they can be used to explain normal and athletic movement and the type of resistance exercise for training these movements.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"解剖學姿勢 (anatomical position)：直立站姿、雙臂垂於體側、手掌朝前。以此為基準可將身體切為三個解剖面，用以描述正常與運動動作及對應的阻力訓練。"},{"id":"q2448","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"What is the 2-for-2 rule for load progression?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"If an individaul can perform 2 more reps on their last set then perscribed for 2 workouts an increase is needed","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"二二法則 (2-for-2 rule)：若運動員連續兩次訓練都能在最末組多做 2 下以上，即應增加負荷，屬漸進式負荷增加原則。"},{"id":"q2449","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHAT ARE THE LOAD AND REPETITION ASSIGNMENTS BASED ON TRAINING GOAL WHEN THE GOAL IS FOR: POWER 1. SINGLE EFFORT 2. MULTIPLE EFFORT","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. SINGLE EFFORT LOAD (%1RM): 80-90 GOAL REPS: 1-2 2. MULTIPLE EFFORT: LOAD (%1RM):75-85 GOAL REPS: 3-5","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"功率目標：1. 單次輸出 80-90% 1RM、1-2 下；2. 多次輸出 75-85% 1RM、3-5 下。"},{"id":"q2450","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Pyruvate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Is a product of anaerobic glycolysis. One molecule of glucose is reduced to two pyruvate molecules with two separate ways to produce NRG -Acetylcoenzyme A though the Krebs cycle -oxaloacetate to produce intermediaries involved in Krebs cycle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸 (pyruvate)：糖解的產物，一分子葡萄糖產生兩分子丙酮酸，之後有兩條去路：轉為乙醯輔酶A進入克雷布斯迴圈，或轉為草醯乙酸補充迴圈中間物。"},{"id":"q2451","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the Karvonen method?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A way to measure intensity and heart rate reserve in relation to heart rate. APMHR = 220 - age APMHR - resting heart rate = HRR (heart rate reserve ) (HRR x intensity) + RHR = heart rate goal for given intensity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"Karvonen 法：用心率儲備 (HRR) 計算目標心率。預估最大心率 = 220 − 年齡；HRR = 預估最大心率 − 安靜心率；目標心率 = (HRR × 強度) + 安靜心率。"},{"id":"q2452","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Systematic desensitization in relation to sports psychology.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"For advanced athletes only. Allows an athlete to replace a fear response to varied cues with relaxation response.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"系統減敏感法 (systematic desensitization)：適用於進階運動員，讓運動員以放鬆反應取代對各種線索的恐懼反應，需先掌握放鬆技巧。"},{"id":"q2453","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"How are the work:rest ratios assigned based on the goal of training? Of the involved energy systems?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strength 2-5 minutes of rest Power - Single and Multi event 2-5 minutes of rest Hypertrophy 2-3 minutes for multijoint exercises, 60-90 seconds for single-joint exercises Muscular Endurance less than 30 seconds of rest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS - Program Design Exam Prep"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"組間休息依訓練目標（5e 第18章表18.15，p1253–1254）：肌力 2–5 分鐘；功率（單次與多次用力專案）2–5 分鐘；肥大：多關節動作 2–3 分鐘、單關節動作 60–90 秒；局部肌耐力 <30 秒。休息長短對應所用能量系統的還原需求。（舊版「肥大 30 秒–1.5 分鐘」在 5e 已改。）"},{"id":"q2454","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Atroventricular Bundle (AV)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Conducts the impulse to the Ventricles and L/R Bundle Branches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Test Prep Chapter 1"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"房室束 (AV bundle，希氏束)：將傳導衝動送向下傳至心室，並分為左右束支。"},{"id":"q2455","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"HDL","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Abbreviation for high-density lipoproteins, the \"good\" cholesterol that returns unused fat to the liver for disposal.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"高密度脂蛋白 (HDL)：俗稱好的膽固醇，負責把未使用的脂肪送回肝臟代謝排出。"},{"id":"q2456","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Saggital plane","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"This plane divides the body into right and left regions. Examples of body movements and related exercise that occur in the saggital plane are ..... flextion and extension","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS exercise science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"矢狀面 (sagittal plane)：把身體分為左右兩側的切面；此面內的動作如屈曲與伸展，對應深蹲、二頭肌彎舉等訓練。"},{"id":"q2457","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"How much should load be increased by for good progression?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Less trained/weaker: Upper body: 2.5-5lbs Lower body: 5-10lbs More trained/Stronger: Upper body: 5-10lbs Lower body: 10-15lbs OR 2.5-10% of current load","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Ch17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"負荷進行的幅度：較弱/初學者上肢加 2.5-5 磅、下肢 5-10 磅；較強/受訓者上肢 5-10 磅、下肢 10-15 磅，或以目前負荷的 2.5-10% 為上限。"},{"id":"q2458","part":2,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":15,"question":"WHAT ARE THE LOAD AND REPETITION ASSIGNMENTS BASED ON TRAINING GOAL WHEN THE GOAL IS FOR: HYPERTROPHY","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"LOAD (%1RM): 67-85 GOAL REPS: 3-5","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["cscs chapter 15"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"肥大目標的負荷為 67-85% 1RM。注意：標準處方次數為 6-12 下（此卡片答案的 3-5 下偏誤，3-5 下較接近肌力/功率配置），背誦時以 6-12 下為準。"},{"id":"q2459","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Lactate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Byproduct of anaerobic glycolysis. -Considered a waste product -Used as fuel source in the heat and brain -","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Cscs Exercise Science"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"乳酸 (lactate)：無氧糖解的產物，常被視為廢物，但實際可作為心臟與腦的燃料，並可經科裡迴圈回收轉為葡萄糖。"},{"id":"q2460","part":1,"domain":"Exercise Sciences","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"What is the difference between systolic and diastolic blood pressure?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Systolic- the pressure the heart exerts on arterial walls when the heart beats. (Systole) Diastolic- the amount of pressure on arterial walls between beats. (Diastole)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Exercise Science Questions"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"收縮壓 (systolic)：心臟收縮打血時動脈壁承受的壓力；舒張壓 (diastolic)：兩次心跳之間舒張期動脈壁承受的壓力。"},{"id":"q2461","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During the ground support phase of sprinting, what two muscles are responsible for storing and recovering elastic energy?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Gastrocnemius and quads","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS Program Design"],"source":"cram","explanation_zh":"衝刺支撐期儲存並回收彈效能量的兩塊肌肉是腓腸肌 (gastrocnemius) 與股四頭肌 (quadriceps)，利用牽張-收縮迴圈 (SSC) 回彈出力。"},{"id":"q2462","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The length-tension relationship of muscle is based on the following fact:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"As muscle lengthens, the tension changes and is highest at the middle length.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"長度-張力關係 (length-tension relationship)：肌肉長度改變時張力跟著改變，在中介長度（肌節為最佳粗細肌絲重疊時）可產生最大張力，過長或過短張力都下降。"},{"id":"q2463","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a procedure for assessing ability in a particular endeavor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗 (test)：評估某項特定能力或屬性的程式，是產生資料的第一步，後續需經評估 (evaluation) 才能做決策。"},{"id":"q2464","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is catastrophe theory?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a relationship between the level of arousal and manifestation of cognitive anxieties once crossing the arousal threshold, which changes focus to what cannot be executed in competition and thus a decline in performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"災難理論 (catastrophe theory)：跨越喚醒閾值後，認知焦慮表現出來且表現不是漸降而是驟降（災難式下滑），注意力轉到無法執行的事物上；需完全放鬆才能恢復。"},{"id":"q2465","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"smooth muscle functions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"one nucleus/no striations, comprising walls of blood vessels/organs of urinary/digestive/respiratory/reproductive tracts, also for peristalsis (moving food through digestive tract)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平滑肌功能：單核、無橫紋，構成血管壁及泌尿、消化、呼吸、生殖道器官的壁，並負責蠕動 (peristalsis) 推動食物通過消化道。"},{"id":"q2466","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is catabolism associated with?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"release of energy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"分解代謝 (catabolism) 伴隨能量釋放：把大分子分解為小分子並放出能量，例如ATP水解與營養素氧化。"},{"id":"q2467","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"approximately how many bones are in the body?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"206","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"成人全身約有 206 塊骨骼。"},{"id":"q2468","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"equation for work?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Work = Force * Displacement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"功的公式：功 (Work) = 力 (Force) × 位移 (Displacement)。沒有位移就沒有力學功。"},{"id":"q2469","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"a nutrient that is required in significant amounts in the diet","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"macronutrient","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"巨量營養素 (macronutrient)：飲食中需要量大的營養素，包括碳水化合物、蛋白質與脂肪。"},{"id":"q2470","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Following sports psychology training with the men’s volleyball team, the athletes report that during competition, time seemed to slow down, and they felt more focused. The athletes are: a: in the ideal performance state b: in an anxious state c: in the low-determination state","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a: in the ideal performance state","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"比賽中時間變慢、專注感增強是理想表現狀態 (ideal performance state) 的典型報告，非焦慮或低決心狀態。"},{"id":"q2471","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what are the 7 program design variables?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"needs analysis exercise selection frequency exercise order load and repetitions volume rest periods","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"課程設計七大變項：需求分析 (needs analysis)、動作選擇、頻率、動作順序、負荷與次數、訓練量 (volume)、休息時間。"},{"id":"q2472","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the amount of blood pumped by the heart in liters per minute","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cardiac output","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"心輸出量 (cardiac output)：心臟每分鐘打出的血量（公升/分鐘），= 每搏輸出量 × 心率。"},{"id":"q2473","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Musculoskeletal system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"consists of bones, joints, muscles, & tendons configured to allow the great variety of movements characteristics of human acitivty","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉骨骼系統 (musculoskeletal system)：由骨骼、關節、肌肉與肌腱構成，提供人類各種動作的結構基礎。"},{"id":"q2474","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the force a muscle or muscle group can exert in one maximal effort","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"maximum muscular strength (low speed)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大肌力 (maximum muscular strength)：肌肉或肌群在單次最大努力（低速度）下能施加的力量。"},{"id":"q2475","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Adenosine diphosphate (ADP)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The product of the breakdown of ATP. When ATP is broken down, the end result is an ADP molecule, an inorganic phosphate, a hydrogen ion, and energy. ADP can be further broken down into AMP as a secondary source of biological energy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"二磷酸腺苷 (ADP)：ATP 水解的產物，ATP 分解後得到 ADP、無機磷酸、氫離子與能量；ADP 可再分解為 AMP 作為次要生物能量來源。"},{"id":"q2476","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Achievement motivation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Efforts to master a task, achieve excellence, and engage in competition or social comparison - the desire to win","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"成就動機 (achievement motivation)：努力精通任務、追求卓越、參與競爭或社會比較的傾向，即想要贏的慾望。"},{"id":"q2477","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following sections of the sarcomere shorten during a concentric muscle action EXCEPT the A-band distance between Z-lines H-zone I-band","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A-band","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"同心收縮時肌節的 Z 線距離、H 帶、I 帶都會變短，唯獨 A 帶（粗肌絲長度）不變，故答案為 A band。"},{"id":"q2478","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Field test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a test used to assess ability that is performed away from the laboratory and does not require extensive training or expensive equipment","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"現場測驗 (field test)：在實驗室以外進行的能力測驗，不需要大量訓練或昂貴儀器，便於團體施測。"},{"id":"q2479","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how can specificity of loading help bone health?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"external stimuli increasing bone density in specific joints likely to experience bone loss or mineral thinning","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"特異性負荷可改善骨健康：針對容易骨質流失的關節施加外部刺激（負荷訓練），可提高該處的骨密度與礦物質含量。"},{"id":"q2480","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"bioenergetic diff. between type I and type II?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type I = low myosin ATPase, slower calcium handling, reduced glycolytic capacity, large mitochondria","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"第一型（slow twitch）纖維的能量代謝特徵：肌球蛋白ATP酶活性低、鈣離子處理較慢、糖解能力較低、粒線體大而多，靠有氧代謝抗疲勞。"},{"id":"q2481","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"are exergonic reactions catabolic or anabolic or neither?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"catabolic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"放能反應 (exergonic reactions) 屬分解代謝 (catabolic)，釋放能量以驅動其他反應。"},{"id":"q2482","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what does the appendicular skeleton include?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the shoulder (or pectoral) girdle (left and right scapula and clavicle); bones of the arms, wrists, and hands (left and right humerus, radius, ulna, carpals, metacarpals, and phalanges); the pelvic girdle (left and right coxal or innominate bones); and the bones of the legs, ankles, and feet (left and right femur, patella, tibia, fibula, tarsals, metatarsals, and phalanges)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肢帶骨骼 (appendicular skeleton) 包括：肩帶（肩胛骨、鎖骨）、手臂/手腕/手骨（肱骨、橈骨、尺骨、腕骨、掌骨、指骨）、骨盆帶（髖骨）及腿/踝/足骨（股骨、髕骨、脛骨、腓骨、蹠骨、蹠骨、趾骨）。"},{"id":"q2483","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"equation for power in terms of work?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power = Work / Time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"以功表示功率：功率 (Power) = 功 (Work) / 時間 (Time)。"},{"id":"q2484","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein = __ kcal/g","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4 kcal/g","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"蛋白質的熱量為 4 kcal/g（與碳水化合物相同；脂肪為 9 kcal/g）。"},{"id":"q2485","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Which of the following exercises is best coached using whole practice? a: snatch b: Turkish get up c: kettlebell swing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"c: kettlebell swing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"壺鈴擺盪 (kettlebell swing) 動作連貫、分段少，適合整體練習法 (whole practice)；抓舉與土耳其起立較複雜，宜採分解或部分練習。"},{"id":"q2486","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what three principles should be incorporated in resistance training programs for athletic populations?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specificity overload progression","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"競技運動員阻力訓練應納入三原則：特異性 (specificity)、超負荷 (overload)、漸進性 (progression)。"},{"id":"q2487","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"quantity of blood ejected with each heart beat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"stroke volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"每搏輸出量 (stroke volume)：每次心跳被打出的血量。"},{"id":"q2488","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Skeleton","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle attachment points, to cause bony levels to enforce pushing and pulling forces from muscles.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"骨骼 (skeleton) 的功能：提供肌肉附著點，形成骨槓桿以放大肌肉推拉之力並產生動作。"},{"id":"q2489","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the ability of the muscle tissue to exert high force while contracting at a high speed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"maximum muscle power (high speed or anaerobic)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大肌功率 (maximum muscular power)：肌肉組織在高收縮速度下仍輸出高力量的能力（高速/無氧表現）。"},{"id":"q2490","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Adenosine monophosphate (AMP)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The final product of the breakdown of ATP and subsequent breakdown of ADP.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"單磷酸腺苷 (AMP)：ATP 水解為 ADP、ADP 再水解後的最終產物。"},{"id":"q2491","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of these factors contribute to venous return EXCEPT the muscle pump the respiratory pump vasoconstriction venoconstriction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vasoconstriction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"靜脈迴流的機制包括肌肉幫浦、呼吸幫浦與靜脈收縮 (venoconstriction)；血管收縮（動脈的 vasoconstriction）不是靜脈迴流的機制，故為例外。"},{"id":"q2492","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Evaluation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the process of analyzing test results for the purpose of making decisions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"評估 (evaluation)：分析測驗結果並據以做決策的過程，測驗 (test) 只是蒐集資料。"},{"id":"q2493","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the implications of greater tendon stiffness?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"greater stiffness = greater force required for transmission to a muscle to produce a recoil response, and useful for transmitting forces through tendons and into muscles at a high rate under strain – either from high velocity or from an opponent; essential in improving performance in some sports","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌腱剛性 (tendon stiffness) 提高的好處：需要較大的力才能造成回彈形變，但能以高速把力量經肌腱傳入肌肉，有利於高速或對抗情境下的力量傳遞與運動表現。"},{"id":"q2494","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"difference between IIa and IIb fibers?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"IIa = moderate aerobic/anaerobic capacity, fast-oxidative+glycolytic, high myosin ATPase activity, greater number of capillaries than IIx fibers. IIb = fast glycolytic, less capacity for aerobic energy therefore more fatigable","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"IIa 型屬快速氧化糖解纖維，有氧/無氧能力中等、肌球蛋白ATP酶活性高、微血管多於IIx；IIb（快糖解）有氧能力低、較易疲勞。"},{"id":"q2495","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what do endergonic reactions include?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anabolic processes and the contraction of muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"吸能反應 (endergonic reactions) 包括合成代謝 (anabolism) 與肌肉收縮，需要輸入能量才能進行。"},{"id":"q2496","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what are fibrous joints and what kind of movement do they allow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fibrous joints are e.g. sutures of the skull; they allow virtually no movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"纖維性關節 (fibrous joints)：如顱骨縫合，幾乎不允許活動。"},{"id":"q2497","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"equation for power in terms of force?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Power = Force * Velocity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"以力表示功率：功率 (Power) = 力 (Force) × 速度 (Velocity)。"},{"id":"q2498","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how many essential amino acids?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"9","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"必需胺基酸 (essential amino acids) 有 9 種，人體無法自行合成，必須由飲食攝取。"},{"id":"q2499","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"scientific field of study within sports medicine that seeks to understand the influences of behavioral processes and cognitions on movement","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sport psychology","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動心理學 (sport psychology)：運動醫學內的科學領域，研究行為歷程與認知對動作表現的影響。"},{"id":"q2500","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"athletes training in a specific manner to produce a specific adaptation or training outcome","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specificity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"特異性 (specificity)：運動員以特定方式訓練，以產生特定的適應或訓練結果，即 SAID 原則的應用。"},{"id":"q2501","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"true or false: cardiac output can increase to 4x the resting level with maximal exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true, maximum of 20-22 L/min","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。最大運動時心輸出量可增至安靜時的約 4 倍，最高可達約 20-22 L/min。"},{"id":"q2502","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Axial skeleton","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"consists of the skull, vertebral column, ribs, & sternum","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軸骨 (axial skeleton)：包括顱骨、脊柱、肋骨與胸骨。"},{"id":"q2503","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Aortic valve","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Valve in the heart that prevents backflow of blood from the aorta into the ventricle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"主動脈瓣 (aortic valve)：防止血液自主動脈倒流回左心室的瓣膜，屬半月瓣。"},{"id":"q2504","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"maximal rate of energy production by the combined phosphagen and lactic acid energy systems for moderate endurance activities","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anaerobic capacity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無氧能力 (anaerobic capacity)：磷酸系統與乳酸系統合計，在中等時間耐力活動中可達到的最大能量產出率。"},{"id":"q2505","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Adenosine triphosphatase (ATPase)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An important enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of ATP.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"三磷酸腺苷酶 (ATPase)：催化ATP水解的重要酵素，釋放能量供收縮等生理作用使用。"},{"id":"q2506","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"This ion, stored in the sarcoplasmic reticulum, is released into the sarcoplasm to signal the beginning of the contraction process:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"calcium","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"鈣離子 (Ca2+)：儲存於肌漿網 (sarcoplasmic reticulum)，釋放到肌漿中作為啟動收縮的訊號。"},{"id":"q2507","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Pretest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a test administered before the beginning of training to determine the athlete’s initial basic ability levels","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"前測 (pretest)：訓練開始前施測，確認運動員的初始基本能力水準，作為課程設計與比較基準。"},{"id":"q2508","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the end goal of exergonic reactions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"to perform some kind of work via released energy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"放能反應的最終目的是以釋放的能量去做某種功（驅動生理工作或吸能反應）。"},{"id":"q2509","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"number of skeletal muscles in the body?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"over 500","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"人體骨骼肌超過 500 條。"},{"id":"q2510","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"through what intermediate molecule are exergonic and endergonic reactions derived?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ATP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP：放能與吸能反應都經由ATP這個中間分子連結，分解反應的釋能由ATP承載，再去驅動合成反應。"},{"id":"q2511","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what kind of joints are cartilaginous joints and what kind of movement do they allow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cartilaginous joints are e.g. intervertebral disks and allow limited movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軟骨性關節 (cartilaginous joints)：如椎間盤，允許有限度的活動。"},{"id":"q2512","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what is the equation for force during isometric exertion or constant-speed joint rotation?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"FM * MM = FR * MR … (FM = muscle force, MM = muscle moment arm, FR = resistive force, MR = resistive force moment arm)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"等長用力或等速關節轉動時的力矩平衡：肌肉力 × 肌肉力臂 = 阻力 × 阻力力臂 (FM × MM = FR × MR)。"},{"id":"q2513","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"amino acids that can be synthesized by the body and do not need to be consumed in the diet","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"nonessential amino acids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"非必需胺基酸 (nonessential amino acids)：人體可自行合成，不必依賴飲食攝取。"},{"id":"q2514","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"state that every athlete strives to be in where there is an absence of negative self talk, a strong feeling of efficacy, and an adaptive focus on task relevant cues (“letting it happen”)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ideal performance state","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"理想表現狀態 (ideal performance state, IPS)：沒有負面自我對話、強烈的自我效能感、專注於任務相關線索，屬於讓它自然發生 (letting it happen) 的狀態。"},{"id":"q2515","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how can specificity be incorporated into a resistance training program for athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specific muscles, movement patters, muscle actions, and energy systems involved in the sport","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"特異性可透過針對專項運動所涉及的特定肌肉、動作模式、肌肉收縮型態與能量系統來安排訓練內容。"},{"id":"q2516","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"stroke volume begins to increase at the onset of exercise and continues to rise until the individual’s oxygen consumption is at approximately what percent range of maximal oxygen uptake?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"40% to 50%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"每搏輸出量自運動開始上升，約在攝氧量達最大攝氧量 40-50% 時到達高原，之後主要靠心率提升心輸出量。"},{"id":"q2517","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Appendicular skeleton","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"includes the shoulder girdle; bones of the arm, wrist & hands. The pelvic girdle; bones of the legs, ankles, & feet.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肢帶骨骼 (appendicular skeleton)：包括肩帶與手臂、手腕、手骨，以及骨盆帶與腿部、腳踝、足部骨骼。"},{"id":"q2518","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Arteriole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Smaller branches of the arterial system that deliver blood to the capillaries.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"小動脈 (arteriole)：動脈系統的較細分支，把血液輸送到微血管 (capillaries)。"},{"id":"q2519","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"ability of certain muscles or muscle groups to perform repeated contractions against a submaximal resistance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"local muscular endurance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"區域性肌耐力 (local muscular endurance)：特定肌肉或肌群對抗次最大阻力重複收縮的能力。"},{"id":"q2520","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Adenosine triphosphate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An intermediate molecule used to drive anabolic and endergonic reactions through the energy derived from catabolic and exergonic reactions. ATP is composed of adenosine and three phosphate groups. The hydrolysis of ATP to ADP, and then ADP to AMP releases the energy used for biological work. ATP is considered a high energy molecule because of the large amount of energy stored in the chemical bond of the two terminal phosphate groups.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"三磷酸腺苷 (ATP)：由腺苷與三個磷酸基組成，是驅動合成/吸能反應的中間分子；末端兩個磷酸基的化學鍵儲存大量能量，屬高能量分子，水解為ADP、再為AMP時釋放能量供生物做功。"},{"id":"q2521","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Attention","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The processing of both environmental and internal cues that come to awareness","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"注意力 (attention)：對環境與內線上索的處理並進入察覺的過程，是運動表現的心理要素之一。"},{"id":"q2522","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following will increase the dissociation between hemoglobin and oxygen? high partial pressure of oxygen increased pH increased temperature low partial pressure of CO2","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increased temperature","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"溫度升高會促進血紅素與氧的解離（右移解離曲線）；高氧分壓、高pH（鹼）、低二氧化碳分壓都會促進結合而非解離。"},{"id":"q2523","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Midtest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a test administered one or more times during the training period to assess progress and modify the program as needed to maximize benefit","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"中間測驗 (midtest)：訓練期間施測一次以上，用以檢視進度並適時修改課程以獲得最大效益。"},{"id":"q2524","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when does catabolism occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"heavy training volumes, reduced caloric intake, and times of high life stress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"分解代謝發生在：大訓練量、熱量攝取不足與生活壓力高的時期，此時身體分解組織的速率上升。"},{"id":"q2525","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the twelve muscle groups by function?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"(1) facial expression (2) mastication (3) head/vertebral column movement (4) pectoral girdle movement (5) arm movement (6) forearm movement (7) hand movement (8) abdominal wall movement (9) pelvic outlet movement (10) thigh movement (11) leg movement (12) foot movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"十二個功能肌群：面部表情、咀嚼、頭/脊柱動作、肩帶動作、手臂動作、前臂動作、手動作、腹壁動作、骨盆出口動作、大腿動作、小腿動作、足部動作。"},{"id":"q2526","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"adenosine is the combination of what chemicals?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"adenine (a nitrogen-containing base) and ribose (a five-carbon sugar)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腺苷 (adenosine) 由腺嘌呤 (adenine，含氮鹼基) 與核糖 (ribose，五碳糖) 結合而成。"},{"id":"q2527","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what kind of joints are synovial joints and what kind of movement do they allow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"synovial joints are e.g. elbow and knee and they allow considerable movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"滑膜關節 (synovial joints)：如肘關節與膝關節，有腔隙與滑液，允許大幅活動。"},{"id":"q2528","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"Angular velocity is what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the object’s rotational speed, measured in radians per second (rad/s).","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"角速度 (angular velocity)：物體轉動的速度，以弧度/秒 (rad/s) 度量。"},{"id":"q2529","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"amino acids that cannot be synthesized by the body and must be obtained through the diet","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"essential amino acids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"必需胺基酸 (essential amino acids)：人體無法自行合成、必須由飲食取得的胺基酸。"},{"id":"q2530","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"using only the amount of mental and physical energy required to perform the task","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"physiological efficiency","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"生理效率 (physiological efficiency)：只使用完成任務所需的心理與生理能量，不浪費剩餘能量。"},{"id":"q2531","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what does the SAID principle stand for?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specific adaptation to imposed demands","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"SAID 原則 = specific adaptation to imposed demands：對身體施加什麼樣的需求，就產生什麼樣的具體適應。"},{"id":"q2532","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"two physiological mechanisms that are responsible for the regulation of stroke volume","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"end diastolic volume and catecholamine action","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"調控每搏輸出量的兩個生理機制：舒張末期容積（前負荷，Frank-Starling 機制）與兒茶酚胺作用（腎上腺素與正腎上腺素增強收縮）。"},{"id":"q2533","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Fibrous joints","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"allow virtually no movement; EX) sutures of the skull.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"纖維性關節 (fibrous joints)：幾乎無活動度，例如顱骨縫合。"},{"id":"q2534","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Artery","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Strong tubes that rapidly transport blood from the heart.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動脈 (artery)：管壁厚而強韌的血管，把血液快速從心臟送出。"},{"id":"q2535","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"maximum rate at which an athlete can produce energy through oxidation of energy resources (carbs, fats, proteins)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"aerobic capacity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧能力 (aerobic capacity)：運動員經能量物質（醣、脂肪、蛋白質）氧化產生能量的最大速率，常以 VO2max 表示。"},{"id":"q2536","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Augmented feedback","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Feedback provided to the athlete by an observer such as a coach or video/lab equipment","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"增強回饋 (augmented feedback)：由教練、錄影或儀器等在自然感覺之外提供給運動員的額外資訊。"},{"id":"q2537","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All else being equal, this type of muscle fiber arrangement will be associated with higher forces:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"bipennate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"其他條件相同時，雙羽狀 (bipennate) 纖維排列的生理截面積大、可容納更多肌纖維，因此能產生較大的力。"},{"id":"q2538","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Formative evaluation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"periodic reevaluation based on midtests administered during the training, usually at regular intervals","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"形成性評估 (formative evaluation)：訓練期間依固定間隔以中間測驗定期重新評估並調整課程。"},{"id":"q2539","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the adaptations to aerobic exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increased cardiac output, reduced heart rate at rest, and (during submaximal exercise intensities) increased stroke volume per heartbeat, and a significant increase in density in the microvasculature","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練的適應：心輸出量增加、安靜心率下降、次最大強度下每搏輸出量增加，以及微血管密度顯著增加。"},{"id":"q2540","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for arm/shoulder flexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pectoralis major, anterior delt, coracobrachialis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩/手臂屈曲的主動肌：胸大肌 (pectoralis major)、三角肌前束 (anterior deltoid)、喙肱肌 (coracobrachialis)。"},{"id":"q2541","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"the breakdown of one molecule of ATP to yield energy is known as?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hydrolysis, because it requires one molecule of water","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 分解獲得能量稱為水解 (hydrolysis)，因為反應需要一分子水參與。"},{"id":"q2542","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"in terms of joints, what is the order of least to most movement allowed?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fibrous joints","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"按活動度排序：纖維性關節（幾乎不動）→ 軟骨性關節（有限活動）→ 滑膜關節（大幅活動）；最少的是纖維性關節。"},{"id":"q2543","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how is torque expressed?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in newton-meters (N*m), but should not be confused with work, which is also expressed in newton-meters.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"扭矩 (torque) 以牛頓·米 (N·m) 表示，但不可與同樣以 N·m 表示的功 (work) 混為一談。"},{"id":"q2544","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"amino acids that are typically not essential but become essential during times of illness and stress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"conditionally essential amino acids","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"條件必需胺基酸 (conditionally essential amino acids)：通常非必需，但在生病或壓力大的狀態下變成必須由飲食攝取。"},{"id":"q2545","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"what are some characteristics that an athlete would report about the ideal performance state?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"no fear of failure no thinking about performance analysis narrow focus of attention sense of effortlessness sense of personal control time slows down","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"理想表現狀態的主觀特徵：不怕失敗、不去分析表現、注意力窄而專注、不費力的感覺、個人控制感、時間變慢。"},{"id":"q2546","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"principle that states the type of demand placed on the body dictates the type of adaptation that will occur","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"SAID principle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"SAID 原則：身體被施加的需求決定所產生的適應型別。"},{"id":"q2547","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"volume of blood in the left ventricle at the end of the filling phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"end diastolic volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舒張末期容積 (end diastolic volume, EDV)：心室填血結束（舒張末期）時左心室內的血量。"},{"id":"q2548","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Cartilaginous joints","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Allow limited movement; EX) intervertebral disks.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軟骨性關節 (cartilaginous joints)：允許有限活動，例如椎間盤。"},{"id":"q2549","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Atrioventricular (AV) valves","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"One-way valves that prevent the backflow of the blood from the ventricles into the atria.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"房室瓣 (AV valves，二尖瓣與三尖瓣)：單向瓣膜，防止血液從心室倒流回心房。"},{"id":"q2550","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"ability to stop, start, and change the direction of the body or body parts rapidly and in a controlled manner","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"agility","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"敏捷性 (agility)：快速且受控地停止、啟動並改變身體或身體部位方向的能力。"},{"id":"q2551","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Autogenic training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Focusing on a sense of warmth and heaviness in a muscle group to reduce arousal or anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"自律訓練法 (autogenic training)：專注於肌群的溫暖感與沉重感以降低喚醒或焦慮的放鬆技術。"},{"id":"q2552","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Internal rotation of the hip takes place in this plane:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"transverse","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"髖關節內旋發生在橫斷面 (transverse plane)，繞垂直軸旋轉。"},{"id":"q2553","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Posttest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a test administered after the training period to determine the success of the training program in achieving the training objectives","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"後測 (posttest)：訓練期結束後施測，判斷課程是否達成訓練目標。"},{"id":"q2554","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is a side effect of creatine supplementation?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"acute effects that include gastrointestinal issues such as gas or mild bloating","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌酸 (creatine) 補充的副作用：急性腸胃問題，例如脹氣或輕微腹脹。"},{"id":"q2555","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for arm/shoulder extension?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"teres major, lat dorsi, posterior delts","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩/手臂伸展的主動肌：大圓肌 (teres major)、背闊肌 (latissimus dorsi)、三角肌後束 (posterior deltoid)。"},{"id":"q2556","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is the hydrolysis of ATP catalyzed by?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"an enzyme called adenosine triphosphatase (ATPase)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 的水解由三磷酸腺苷酶 (ATPase) 催化。"},{"id":"q2557","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"smooth hyaline cartilage covers what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"articulating bone ends","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"光滑的透明軟骨 (hyaline cartilage) 覆蓋在關節骨的接觸端（關節面）上。"},{"id":"q2558","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how does torque differ when a weight is horizontally farther or closer to a joint?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when the weight is horizontally closer to the joint, it exerts less resistive torque; when it is horizontally farther from a joint, it exerts more resistive torque.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"重量在水平方向離關節愈近，阻力扭矩愈小；離關節愈遠，阻力扭矩愈大（扭矩=力×力臂）。"},{"id":"q2559","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein dietary recommendations are determined by what 2 things?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"amino acid content protein digestibility","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"蛋白質的飲食建議由兩件事決定：胺基酸組成 (amino acid content) 與消化率 (protein digestibility)。"},{"id":"q2560","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: the ability to maintain self control and manage energy in a performance environment is a critical skill for any performer","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。在表現環境中維持自我控制並管理能量，是任何表現者的關鍵技能。"},{"id":"q2561","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"training at a greater intensity than the athlete is accustomed to","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"overload","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"超負荷 (overload)：以高於運動員慣常的強度進行訓練，以迫使身體產生新的適應。"},{"id":"q2562","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"hormones of the sympathetic nervous system that produce a forceful ventricular contraction and greater systolic emptying of the heart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"epinephrine and norepinephrine (catecholamines)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"交感神經系統的荷爾蒙（腎上腺素與正腎上腺素，屬兒茶酚胺 catecholamines）使心室收縮更有力、收縮期排空更完全。"},{"id":"q2563","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Synovial Joint","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Allow considerable movement. EX) elbow & knee","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"滑膜關節 (synovial joint)：允許大幅活動，例如肘關節與膝關節。"},{"id":"q2564","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Bronchiole","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The third generation passages in the lungs that deliver air to the alveoli, where gases are exchanged.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"細支氣管 (bronchiole)：肺內第三代氣道，把空氣送到肺泡 (alveoli) 進行氣體交換。"},{"id":"q2565","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"movement distance per unit time, typically quantified as the time taken to cover a fixed distance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"speed","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"速度 (speed)：單位時間移動的距離，通常以完成固定距離所需的時間來量化。"},{"id":"q2566","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Catastrophe theory","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Performance theory that states that a catastrophic decline in abilities, rather than gradual decline, can occur past a certain arousal level","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"災難理論 (catastrophe theory)：認為超過某個喚醒程度後，能力是災難式驟降而非漸進下滑。"},{"id":"q2567","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The joint involving the femur and tibia is an example of this type of joint:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"synovial","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"股骨與脛骨組成的膝關節屬滑膜關節 (synovial joint)，有較大活動度與滑液腔。"},{"id":"q2568","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The degree to which a test or test item measures what it is supposed to measure The most important characteristic of testing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"效度 (validity)：測驗或題項測量到其應測內容的程度，是測驗最重要的特質。"},{"id":"q2569","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what function does oyxgen deficit provide?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"insight into contributions of the anaerobic energy system during intense bouts of exercise, plus weaknesses in individual athletes that can be improved via training","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"攝氧缺損 (oxygen deficit) 的功能：顯示激烈運動中無氧能量系統的貢獻比例，並可發現個人可經訓練改善的弱點。"},{"id":"q2570","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for arm abduction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"supraspinatus and deltoid muscles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩外展的主動肌：棘上肌 (supraspinatus) 與三角肌 (deltoid)。"},{"id":"q2571","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is crossbridge recycling?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the process that occurs after myosin ATPase catalyzes ATP hydrolysis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"橫橋回收 (crossbridge recycling)：肌球蛋白ATP酶催化ATP水解後進行的過程，使橫橋再充能、繼續與肌動蛋白結合，維持肌絲滑動。"},{"id":"q2572","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how does hyaline cartilage differ from other kinds of cartilage?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"enclosed in a capsule filled with synovial fluid","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"透明軟骨不同於其他軟骨之處：其所在的關節由充滿滑液 (synovial fluid) 的關節囊包圍。"},{"id":"q2573","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how is the angle of pennation defined?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the angle between the muscle fibers and an imaginary line between the muscle’s origin and insertion; 0° corresponds to no pennation, many human muscles are pennated, but few have angles of pennation in excess of 15°","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"羽狀角 (angle of pennation) 定義為肌纖維與肌肉起點-終點連線之間的夾角；0° 為無羽狀，人體多數肌肉有羽狀角，但超過 15° 的很少。"},{"id":"q2574","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"highly digestible proteins that contain all of the essential amino acids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"higher quality proteins","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高品質蛋白質 (higher quality proteins)：消化率高且含全部必需胺基酸的蛋白質，如蛋、乳、肉類。"},{"id":"q2575","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"mental energy is generated, maintained, depleted, and refreshed via our _________","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"emotions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"心理能量經情緒 (emotions) 產生、維持、消耗與補充；情緒是能量流動的管道。"},{"id":"q2576","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what are some ways to overload?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase loads or reps add exercises simple to complex decrease rest periods add variables","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"達成超負荷的方法：增加負荷或次數、增加動作、由簡入繁、縮短休息時間、增加變化變項。"},{"id":"q2577","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the myocardial fibers become more stretched with increased volume resulting in a more forceful reflexive contraction and increased cardiac output. this is known as the _______","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Frank-Starling mechanism","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Frank-Starling 機制：心室容積增加使心肌纖維被拉長，引發反射性更強力的收縮，從而增加心輸出量。"},{"id":"q2578","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Hyaline Cartilage","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Articulating bone ends are covered in.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"透明軟骨 (hyaline cartilage)：覆蓋於關節骨的接觸端，減少摩擦並緩衝壓力。"},{"id":"q2579","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Capillary","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Small end-tubes of the arterial system that facilitate exchange of oxygen, fluid, nutrients, and other substances between the blood and other fluids in various body tissues.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"微血管 (capillary)：動脈系統的最細末端，負責血液與組織間氧、液體、營養等物質的交換。"},{"id":"q2580","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"range of motion about a body joint","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"flexibility","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"柔軟性 (flexibility)：關節的活動範圍 (ROM)。"},{"id":"q2581","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Allosteric activation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Process of an end-product binding to an enzyme resulting in an increase in the rate of the reaction,","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"別構活化 (allosteric activation)：終產物或調控物結合到酵素的其他位置，使該反應速率增加的機制。"},{"id":"q2582","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Josephine performs a biceps curl, lifting a weight from the extended arm position up to full flexion of the elbow. This movement provides an illustration of this type of lever system:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"third-class","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"二頭肌彎舉屬第三類槓桿：力點（肘關節附著的肌腱）介於支點與抗力點（手持重量）之間，力臂短、速度臂長，是人體最常見的槓桿形式。"},{"id":"q2583","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Construct Validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the extent that a test measures what it is designed to how well does a test actually measure what it is supposed to measure?","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"構念效度 (construct validity)：測驗是否測量到其設計要測的理論構念，即測驗實際測量目標構唸的程度。"},{"id":"q2584","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the contractile phase of the cardiac cycle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"systole","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮期 (systole) 是心跳週期的收縮階段，心室收縮打出血液。"},{"id":"q2585","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for arm rotation?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"subscapularis, infraspinatus, teres minor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩旋轉的主動肌：肩胛下肌 (subscapularis，內旋)、棘下肌 (infraspinatus) 與小圓肌 (teres minor，外旋)。"},{"id":"q2586","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what other enzymes catalyze ATP at other locations?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"calcium ATPase for pumping calcium into the sarcoplasmic reticulum, sodium-potassium ATPase for maintaining the sarcolemmal concentration gradient after depolarization","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"其他位置的ATP酶：鈣離子ATP酶負責把Ca2+打回肌漿網；鈉鉀ATP酶負責去極化後恢復細胞膜的離子濃度梯度。"},{"id":"q2587","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how do uniaxial joints operate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"joints such as the elbow operate as hinges, essentially rotating about only one axis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"單軸關節 (uniaxial joints)：如肘關節以鉸鏈方式運作，基本上繞單一軸轉動。"},{"id":"q2588","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"net work performed when a weight is lifted is equal what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the magnitude of the weight (F1) plus the force (F2) required for a desired acceleration rate multiplied by the displacement (D) in which the weight is lifted upward","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舉起負荷的淨功 =（負荷重量 F1 + 達成目標加速度所需的額外力 F2）× 垂直舉起的位移 D。"},{"id":"q2589","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"examples of animal based proteins that contain all of the essential amino acids?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"eggs, dairy foods, meat, fish, and poultry","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"含全部必需胺基酸的動物性蛋白質：蛋、乳品、肉類、魚類、禽肉。"},{"id":"q2590","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"temporary feeling states that occur in response to events, have both physiological and psychological components","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"emotions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"情緒 (emotions)：對事件產生的暫時性感受狀態，同時具有生理與心理兩個成分。"},{"id":"q2591","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"training program intensity becomes progressively greater to continue producing higher levels of performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"progression","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"漸進性 (progression)：訓練課程的強度必須逐漸提高，才能持續產生更高水準的表現。"},{"id":"q2592","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"fraction of the end diastolic volume ejected from the heart","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ejection fraction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"射出分數 (ejection fraction)：每次心跳自舒張末期容積中被打出的比例。"},{"id":"q2593","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Synovial Fluid","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The entire joint is enclosed in a capsule filled of","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"滑液 (synovial fluid)：整個滑膜關節由關節囊包圍，囊內充滿滑液，潤滑關節並營養軟骨。"},{"id":"q2594","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Depolarization**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The reversal of the heart membrane electrical potential and results in contraction of the atria or ventricles in the case of the P-Wave and QRS complex, respectively.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"去極化 (depolarization)：細胞膜電位的反轉；在心電圖上 P 波的去極化造成心房收縮，QRS 波群造成心室收縮。"},{"id":"q2595","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"relative proportions by weight of fat and lean tissue","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body composition","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"身體組成 (body composition)：脂肪組織與瘦組織各自佔體重比例。"},{"id":"q2596","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Allosteric inhibition","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Process that occurs when an end product binds to the regulatory enzyme and decreases its turnover rate, slowing the formation of the product.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"別構抑制 (allosteric inhibition)：終產物結合到調控酵素、降低其轉換率，使產物生成變慢的負回饋機制。"},{"id":"q2597","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Counterconditioning","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Combining mental and physical techniques to replace fear response to cues with a relaxation response","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反制約 (counterconditioning)：結合心理與身體技術，以放鬆反應取代對線索的恐懼反應。"},{"id":"q2598","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"You meet up with your friend Heidi in the weight room. You haven’t seen her since she’d injured her leg during track practice. You observe that she’s performing progressive loading exercises with her injured leg. From this observation, you realize that she’s probably in this phase of healing:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"remodeling","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對受傷腿部做漸進式負荷練習，表示她處於癒合的重塑期 (remodeling)：此期可承受漸增的應力，讓新生組織重新排列強化。"},{"id":"q2599","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Face validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the appearance to the athlete and other casual observers that the test measures what it is purported to measure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"表面效度 (face validity)：運動員或一般觀察者主觀認為測驗確實測量其宣稱內容的外表印象，不需專業判斷。"},{"id":"q2600","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"for what purposes does the systole phase eject blood?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"either delivering oxygen-rich blood to working tissues or sending blood into the lungs to be oxygenated","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮期打血的目的有兩：把富含氧的血液送運到作用組織（體迴圈），或把血液送入肺部加氧（肺迴圈）。"},{"id":"q2601","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for elbow flexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"biceps, brachialis, bracioradialis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肘屈曲的主動肌：二頭肌 (biceps brachii)、肱肌 (brachialis)、肱橈肌 (brachioradialis)。"},{"id":"q2602","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what equation depicts the reactants (left), enzyme (middle), and products (right) of ATP hydrolysis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ATP + H2O ADP + Pi + H+ + Energy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP水解反應式：ATP + H2O → ADP + Pi + H+ + 能量；左邊反應物、中間酵素、右邊產物。"},{"id":"q2603","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"joints such as the elbow are what kind of joint?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"uniaxial","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肘關節屬單軸關節 (uniaxial joint)，像鉸鏈一樣繞一個軸做屈伸。"},{"id":"q2604","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what is the patella’s main function?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"to hold the quadriceps tendon away from the knee axis of rotation, thereby increasing the moment arm of the quadriceps group and its mechanical advantage","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"髕骨 (patella) 的主要功能：把股四頭肌肌腱撐離膝關節旋轉軸，增加股四頭肌群的力臂與機械優勢。"},{"id":"q2605","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"only plant based protein that contains all essential amino acids","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"soy","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"大豆 (soy) 是唯一含全部必需胺基酸的植物性蛋白質來源。"},{"id":"q2606","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: emotions can have both beneficial and detrimental effects of human performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。情緒對人類表現可能帶來幫助，也可能造成幹擾，視強度與解釋而定。"},{"id":"q2607","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"two stage process that includes an evaluation of the requirements and characteristics of the sport and an assessment of the athlete","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"needs analysis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"需求分析 (needs analysis)：兩階段流程，先評估專項運動的要求與特性（運動需求分析），再評估運動員本身（運動員評估）。"},{"id":"q2608","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"how can athletes estimate maximal heart rate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"subtract age from 220","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動員可以 220 減年齡估算最大心率（預估最大心率），作為強度與心率區間計算的基準。"},{"id":"q2609","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Uniaxial joints","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Allows 1 axis of movement. EX) Hinge joint, elbow or knee","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"單軸關節 (uniaxial joints)：允許一個軸的活動，例如鉸鏈關節（肘、膝）。"},{"id":"q2610","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Fast-twitch fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The fibers in a fast-twitch motor unit that develops force and relaxes rapidly, resulting in a short twitch time. Fast-twitch fibers are further broken into Type IIa fibers and type IIx fibers. Type II fibers and motor units can produce force rapidly but are inefficient and quick to fatigue. Type IIa fibers are more resistant to fatigue than type IIx fibers due to a greater capacity for aerobic metabolism. Type IIa fibers are still far less aerobically efficient than type I fibers.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快縮肌纖維 (fast-twitch fibers)：收縮與放鬆快速、收縮時間短，分 IIa 與 IIx 型；能快速出力但效率差、易疲勞。IIa 因有氧代謝能力較佳，比 IIx 抗疲勞，但遠不及第一型纖維。"},{"id":"q2611","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the science of measurement applied to the human body that includes measurements of height, weight, and selected body girths","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anthropometry","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"人體測量法 (anthropometry)：應用於人體的測量科學，包括身高、體重與各部位圍度。"},{"id":"q2612","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Diaphragmatic breathing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Focused attention on the process of breathing to clear the mind and increase concentration","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"橫膈膜呼吸 (diaphragmatic breathing)：把注意集中在呼吸過程，用以清空思緒、提升專注的放鬆技術。"},{"id":"q2613","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The primary substrate for a 50-meter sprint is","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"creatine phosphate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"50 公尺衝刺持續數秒，主要底物是磷酸肌酸 (creatine phosphate)，屬磷酸系統供能。"},{"id":"q2614","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Content validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the assessment by experts that the testing covers all relevant subtopics or component abilities in appropriate proportions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內容效度 (content validity)：由專家判斷測驗是否以適當比例涵蓋所有相關子題或組成能力。"},{"id":"q2615","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what kind of muscle fibers are fast oxidative and glycolytic?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type IIa","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快速氧化糖解纖維 (fast oxidative glycolytic) 是第二A型 (type IIa) 肌纖維。"},{"id":"q2616","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for elbow/forearm extension?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"triceps, anconeus","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肘/前臂伸展的主動肌：三頭肌 (triceps brachii) 與肘肌 (anconeus)。"},{"id":"q2617","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"hydrolysis of ADP does what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cleaves the second phosphate group and yields adenosine monophosphate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ADP 水解會切下第二個磷酸基，產出單磷酸腺苷 (AMP)。"},{"id":"q2618","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how is the knee improperly referred to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"often referred to as a hinge joint, but its axis of rotation actually changes throughout the joint range of motion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝關節常被誤稱為鉸鏈關節，但其旋轉軸其實會隨活動範圍改變而移動，並非固定單軸。"},{"id":"q2619","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"why are humans at particular risk for back injury?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The advantage we gain from our upright posture and free use of the arms and hands is accompanied by the disadvantage of having our intervertebral disks under compressive force even when we are merely standing, sitting, walking, or running—and under even more compressive force when we are lifting and carrying. When we are in a standing position, any force we exert with the upper body must be transmitted through the back to the legs and ground. In addition, the back muscles act at a great mechanical disadvantage and must generate forces much greater than the weight of an object lifted.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"人類易背部受傷：直立姿勢使椎間盤在站、坐、走、跑時就承受壓力，搬舉時更大；上肢施加的任何力都要經背部傳到腿與地面；且背肌力臂短、機械劣勢大，必須產生遠大於物重的力。"},{"id":"q2620","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"it takes a calorie deficit of ______ to lose 1 pound","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3,500","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"要減掉 1 磅（約0.45公斤）體重，需要約 3500 大卡的熱量赤字。"},{"id":"q2621","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"how can coaches best teach their athletes to reach the ideal performance state?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"tap into emotions but control them so that they do not interfere with performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"教練引導運動員進入理想表現狀態的最佳方式：觸動並管理情緒，讓情緒支援而非幹擾表現。"},{"id":"q2622","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"athletic programs should be periodized to move from _______ to _______","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"general to specific","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動課程的週期化應從一般 (general) 進展到專項 (specific)，先建立一般適應，再靠近比賽需求。"},{"id":"q2623","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the amount of oxygen consumed by the body’s tissues","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"oxygen uptake (VO2)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"攝氧量 (oxygen uptake, VO2)：身體組織實際消耗的氧量。"},{"id":"q2624","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Biaxial Joints","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Allows movement in 2 perpendicular axes. EX) ankle & wrist","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雙軸關節 (biaxial joints)：允許沿兩個互相垂直的軸活動，例如踝關節與腕關節。"},{"id":"q2625","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Fibrous joint**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Joints that allow little to no movement such as the sutures of the skull.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"纖維性關節 (fibrous joint)：幾乎或完全不能活動的關節，例如顱骨縫合。"},{"id":"q2626","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"true or false: ATP is the primary energy source for both low speed and high speed muscular strength tests","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。低速與高速肌力測驗都以ATP（磷酸系統）為主要能量來源。"},{"id":"q2627","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Anaerobic","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Processes that do not require the presence of oxygen. Anaerobic processes include the phosphagen and glycolytic systems, both of which occur in the sarcoplasm of a muscle cell.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無氧 (anaerobic)：不需要氧氣參與的過程，包括磷酸系統與糖解系統，兩者都發生在肌細胞的肌漿中。"},{"id":"q2628","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Discovery","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Instructing the athlete on the overarching goal of the task and the athlete receives little to no direction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"發現式教學 (discovery)：只告知運動員任務的最終目標，其餘幾乎不給指示，讓運動員自行探索解法。"},{"id":"q2629","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The general recommendation for dietary fat is","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30% of total calories","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"飲食脂肪的普遍建議約為總熱量的 30%（多數指引落在 20-35% 範圍）。"},{"id":"q2630","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Criterion-referenced validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"extent to which test scores are associated with another measurement of the SAME ABILITY. How is a good score on the Army push-up test associated with the ACSM push-up test? Both these tests measure the same ability (chest muscle endurance).","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"準則效度 (criterion-referenced validity)：測驗分數與同一能力的其他測量之間的關聯，例如陸軍伏地挺身測驗與ACSM伏地挺身測驗同測胸部肌耐力。"},{"id":"q2631","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how does the GTO inhibit tension overload?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"emitting electrical signals from its sensory neuron to an inhibitory neuron in the spinal cord, which inhibits the motor neuron in the same muscle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官 (GTO) 抑制過度張力的方式：其感覺神經元發出電訊號到脊髓的抑制性中間神經元，抑制同一肌肉的運動神經元，從而降低收縮輸出。"},{"id":"q2632","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for forearm rotation?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"supinator, pronator teres, and pronator quadratus","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"前臂旋轉的主動肌：旋後肌 (supinator，外旋)、旋圓肌 (pronator teres) 與旋四方肌 (pronator quadratus，內旋)。"},{"id":"q2633","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"how does ATP store energy?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in the chemical bonds of the two terminal phosphate groups, which classifies it as a high-energy molecule","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 把能量儲存在末端兩個磷酸基的化學鍵中，因此被歸類為高能量分子。"},{"id":"q2634","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"ankle and wrists are what kind of joints?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"biaxial joints","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"踝關節與腕關節屬雙軸關節 (biaxial joints)，可做兩個互相垂直軸的活動。"},{"id":"q2635","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"forces are generated within the muscle that pull the muscle’s ends toward each other if not prevented from doing so by external forces","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉作用 (muscle action)：肌肉內部產生力量，若不被外力阻擋，會把肌肉兩端往彼此拉近。"},{"id":"q2636","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are some important functions of proteins?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle growth tissue repair make enzymes/hormones building blocks of tissues","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"蛋白質的重要功能：肌肉生長、組織修復、製造酵素與荷爾蒙、構成組織的建材。"},{"id":"q2637","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"athletic performance is frequently affected by what 3 things?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"arousal anxiety stress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動表現常受三件事影響：喚醒 (arousal)、焦慮 (anxiety) 與壓力 (stress)。"},{"id":"q2638","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what are the 4 variables of a physiological analysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"strength power hypertrophy muscular endurance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"生理分析的四個變項：肌力、肌功率、肥大（身體組成）、區域性肌耐力。"},{"id":"q2639","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"true or false: aerobic exercise involving a larger mass of muscle or a greater level of work is associated with a higher oxygen uptake","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。涉及較大肌肉量或較多做功的有氧運動，攝氧量 (VO2) 較高。"},{"id":"q2640","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"multiaxial joints","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Allows movement in all three perpendicular axes; EX ball-n-socket joint, hip or shoulder","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"多軸關節 (multiaxial joints)：允許三個互相垂直軸的活動，例如球窩關節（髖、肩）。"},{"id":"q2641","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Golgi tendon organ**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Proprioceptors located in the tendons attached to extrafusal muscle fibers. Golgi tendon organs relay information regarding tension in the muscle and are though to protect against the development of excess tension in the muscle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高爾基腱器官 (Golgi tendon organ, GTO)：位於附於外梭肌纖維肌腱中的本體感覺器，傳遞肌肉張力資訊，被認為可防止肌肉產生過大張力。"},{"id":"q2642","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"true or false: most maximal muscular strength tests use relatively slow movement speeds and therefore reflect low speed strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。多數最大肌力測驗使用較慢的動作速度，因此反映的是低速肌力。"},{"id":"q2643","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Distress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Negative stress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Distress（幹擾性壓力）：負面的壓力，會損及表現與健康；相對於正面適性壓力 (eustress)。"},{"id":"q2644","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"At the beginning of aerobic exercise, before reaching steady state, an individual will be in this state:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"oxygen deficit","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧運動開始時、尚未到達穩定狀態 (steady state) 前，攝取氧低於需求，處於攝氧缺損 (oxygen deficit) 狀態，由無氧系統補足能量。"},{"id":"q2645","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Concurrent validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"extent to which test scores are associated with those of other accepted tests. Ex: having a strong 1RM for the dumbbell bench press would have a strong association with the 1RM barbell bench press.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"同時效度 (concurrent validity)：測驗分數與其他已被接受測驗分數的關聯程度，例如啞鈴臥推1RM與槓鈴臥推1RM高度相關。"},{"id":"q2646","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the primary neurotransmitter involved in muscular contraction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"acetylcholine","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"參與肌肉收縮的主要神經傳導物質是乙醯膽鹼 (acetylcholine, ACh)。"},{"id":"q2647","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for wrist/hand flexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"flexor carpi radialis, flexor carpi ulnaris, palmaris longus, flexor digitorum profundus, flexor digitorum superficialis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腕/手屈曲的主動肌：橈側腕屈肌、尺側腕屈肌、掌長肌、指深屈肌、指淺屈肌。"},{"id":"q2648","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"where do ATP-producing processes occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in the cell","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 的生成過程都發生在細胞內（細胞質與粒線體）。"},{"id":"q2649","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what range of movements do biaxial joints (such as the ankle and wrist) allow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"movement about two perpendicular axes","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雙軸關節（如踝關節、腕關節）允許繞兩個互相垂直的軸活動。"},{"id":"q2650","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"concentric muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"forces generated within the muscle and acting to shorten it are greater than the external forces acting at its tendons to stretch it","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"同心收縮 (concentric muscle action)：肌肉內部產生、使肌肉縮短的力大於肌腱端拉伸肌肉的外力，肌肉縮短並克服阻力。"},{"id":"q2651","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are some common sources of proteins?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"meat eggs yogurt milk protein supplements","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"蛋白質的常見來源：肉類、蛋、優格、牛奶、蛋白質補充品。"},{"id":"q2652","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"intensity of motivation at any given moment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"arousal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"喚醒 (arousal)：任何時刻動機強度 (intensity of motivation) 的程度。"},{"id":"q2653","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what two things does a needs analysis assess?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the athlete and their sport","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"需求分析評估兩件事：運動員本身與其從事的專項運動。"},{"id":"q2654","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the greatest amount of oxygen that can be used at the cellular level for the entire body","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"maximal oxygen uptake","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大攝氧量 (VO2max)：全身細胞層級能利用的最大氧量。"},{"id":"q2655","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Vertebral column make up","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Vertebral bones separated by flexible disks that allow movement to occur 7 cervical 12 Thoracic 5 Lumbar 5 fused sacral 3 to 5 coccygeal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"脊柱由椎骨與之間的彈性椎間盤構成，允許活動：頸椎 7、胸椎 12、腰椎 5、融合的薦椎 5、尾椎 3-5。"},{"id":"q2656","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Intrafusal fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Modified muscle fibers that run parallel to normal extrafusal fibers and relay sensory information concerning muscle length.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌梭內纖維 (intrafusal fibers)：與一般外梭肌纖維平行排列的特化肌纖維，負責傳遞肌肉長度的感覺資訊。"},{"id":"q2657","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how does the static vertical jump mainly differ from the standard vertical jump?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"countermovement is removed (squat, 2-3 second hold, jump)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"靜態垂直跳與一般垂直跳的主要差別：移除反向動作 (countermovement)——先蹲姿靜止維持 2-3 秒再起跳，排除牽張-收縮迴圈的貢獻。"},{"id":"q2658","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Beta oxidation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A series of reactions in which free fatty acids are broken down, resulting in the formation of acetyl-CoA and hydrogen protons.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"β-氧化 (beta oxidation)：一連串反應，把遊離脂肪酸分解為乙醯輔酶A (acetyl-CoA) 與氫離子，供克雷布斯迴圈與電子傳遞鏈使用。"},{"id":"q2659","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Drive theory","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The arousal theory that proposes that as an individuals arousal or state anxiety increases, the performance also increases","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"驅力理論 (drive theory)：認為個體的喚醒或狀態焦慮愈高，表現就愈好（線性提升）的喚醒理論，與倒U假說不同。"},{"id":"q2660","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The hormone used illegally by some athletes to enhance red blood cell production in the body is","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"erythropoietin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"紅血球生成素 (erythropoietin, EPO)：被部分運動員違法使用以提升紅血球產量、增加帶氧能力的物質。"},{"id":"q2661","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Convergent Validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"is evidenced by high positive correlation between results of the test being assessed and those of the recognized measure of the construct (the “gold standard”) Ex: the results of the 1RM dumbbell bench press have a high correlation to the results of the 1RM bench press, and they measure the same construct (pectoralis major strength)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"聚斂效度 (convergent validity)：待驗證測驗與該構念公認量測（gold standard）結果呈高正相關，例如啞鈴與槓鈴臥推1RM同測胸大肌肌力、高度相關。"},{"id":"q2662","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what causes excitation of the sarcolemma?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"an action potential releases and arrives at a nerve terminal, then acetylcholine is released from the nerve terminal and diffuses across the neuromuscular junction (a muscle contraction will occur when enough acetylcholine is released and an action potential is released across the sarcolemma)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌膜 (sarcolemma) 的興奮：動作電位抵達神經末梢，乙醯膽鹼釋放到神經肌肉接點並擴散過接點間隙；足夠量時在肌膜引發動作電位而產生收縮。"},{"id":"q2663","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for knee flexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"bicep femoris, semitendinosus, semimembranosus (the hamstring muscles) and sartorius","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝屈曲的主動肌：股二頭肌、半腱肌、半膜肌（膕旁肌）與縫匠肌 (sartorius)。"},{"id":"q2664","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"how does the glycolytic system depend on oxygen?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"it doesn’t, neither does the phosphagen system","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖解系統不需要氧氣，磷酸系統同樣不需要；兩者都是無氧系統。"},{"id":"q2665","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"shoulder and hip ball-and-socket are what kind of joints?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"multiaxial joints","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩關節與髖關節的球窩關節屬多軸關節 (multiaxial joints)，可繞三個軸活動。"},{"id":"q2666","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"swimming and cycling involve what muscle actions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"concentric muscle action almost exclusively","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"游泳與騎車幾乎全屬同心收縮 (concentric muscle action)，因為沒有固定支點的離心減速階段。"},{"id":"q2667","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"why are animal based proteins more easily digestible than plant based proteins?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"higher amino acid ratio","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動物性蛋白質比植物性蛋白質更易消化，因其胺基酸組成比例較佳、消化率高。"},{"id":"q2668","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: arousal is always present in an individual to some degree","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確。喚醒永遠以某種程度存在於個體之中，不會完全為零。"},{"id":"q2669","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"current condition or level of preparedness of the athlete","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"training status","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"訓練狀態 (training status)：運動員目前的身體狀況或準備程度，決定訓練量與強度的起點。"},{"id":"q2670","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the most widely accepted measure of cardiorespiratory fitness","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"maximal oxygen uptake","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大攝氧量 (VO2max) 是最被廣泛接受的心肺適能 (cardiorespiratory fitness) 指標。"},{"id":"q2671","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Left bundle branch**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fibers in the heart that send the contraction impulse to the left ventricle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"左束支 (left bundle branch)：心臟傳導系統的纖維，把收縮衝動傳送到左心室。"},{"id":"q2672","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"What test has the athlete step forward off a box without stepping down or jumping up, and upon contact with the ground, jump as high as possible while minimizing contact time as much as possible?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"reactive strength index test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反應力量指數 (RSI) 測驗：受試者向前跨下箱體（不下蹲、不上跳），觸地後以最短觸地時間盡力跳最高，用以評估牽張-收縮迴圈與彈效能力。"},{"id":"q2673","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Emotions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Temporary feeling states that occur in response to events","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"情緒（Emotions）是回應事件而產生的暫時性感受狀態，會隨情境出現與消退，不同於較穩定的人格特質。"},{"id":"q2674","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"In order to lose 10 pounds, an individual will have to have a deficit of this many calories:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"35,000 kilocalories","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"減重 1 磅約需 3,500 大卡熱量赤字，減 10 磅即需累計約 35,000 大卡的赤字，這是熱量平衡的換算基準。"},{"id":"q2675","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Predictive Validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the extent to which the test score corresponds with future behavior or performance Ex: having a stronger 1RM bench press will result in more sacks during the season","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"預測效度（Predictive validity）指測驗分數與未來行為或表現的對應程度，屬準則關聯效度的一種。例：臥推 1RM 較強者球季達陣擒殺次數較多。"},{"id":"q2676","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is troponin responsible for?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"initiating the movement of troponin from the myosin binding site after Ca+ has initiated a conformational change (then the myosin cross bridge can be carried out, allowing contraction)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌鈣蛋白（troponin）與鈣離子結合後引發構型改變，使原肌球蛋白（tropomyosin）從肌動蛋白上的肌球蛋白結合位點移開，橫橋才得以形成並收縮。"},{"id":"q2677","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for knee extension?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"quadriceps femoris (rectus femoris, vastus lateralis, vastus medialis, and vastus intermedius)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝伸直由股四頭肌負責：股直肌、外側廣肌、內側廣肌與中間廣肌，是人體最大肌群之一。"},{"id":"q2678","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"where do the glycolytic and phosphagenic systems occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in the sarcoplasm of a muscle cell","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統與糖解系統都在肌漿（sarcoplasm，肌細胞細胞質）中進行，不需氧氣、也不依賴粒線體。"},{"id":"q2679","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what kind of movement do multiaxial joints allow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"movement about all three perpendicular axes that define space","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"多軸關節（如肩、髖球窩關節）可圍繞定義空間的三個互相垂直的軸運動，即屈伸、外展內收與旋轉。"},{"id":"q2680","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"eccentric muscle action","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle lengthens because the contractile force is less than the resistive force","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"離心收縮指肌肉收縮力小於外在阻力，肌肉被動拉長，例如緩慢放下重物；常用於吸收力量與控制動作。"},{"id":"q2681","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the absolute minimum amount of protein needed to avoid a protein deficit recommended by the RDA for men and women 19+ years of age?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"0.8g/kgbw/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"RDA 對 19 歲以上男女建議的最低蛋白質攝取量為每日每公斤體重 0.8 克，避免蛋白質攝取不足。"},{"id":"q2682","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"subcategory of arousal; negatively perceived emotional state characterized by nervousness, worry, apprehension, or fear","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"焦慮（anxiety）是喚起中負面知覺的情緒狀態，特徵為緊張、擔憂、不安或恐懼。"},{"id":"q2683","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is determined after the needs analysis is complete?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the athlete’s specific needs for their sport and the primary goal for their specific training program","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"完成需求分析後，才能確定運動員的專項需求與訓練的主要目標，據以選擇訓練與測驗專案。"},{"id":"q2684","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"fick equation for VO2 max =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cardiac output x arteriovenous oxygen difference","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Fick 方程式：最大攝氧量＝心輸出量 × 動靜脈氧差（a-vO2 difference），同時反映心臟輸血與肌肉用氧能力。"},{"id":"q2685","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Mitral valve**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Heart valve that prevents blood flow from the left ventricle to the left atria.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"二尖瓣（僧帽瓣）位於左心房與左心室之間，防止心室收縮時血液逆流回左心房。"},{"id":"q2686","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how do you calculate reactive strength index?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"jump height / contact time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反應式力量指數（RSI）＝垂直跳高度 ÷ 地面接觸時間，評估快速 stretch-shortening cycle（拉長—縮短迴圈）的超等長收縮能力。"},{"id":"q2687","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Branched-chain amino acid","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The main amino acids that are thought to be oxidized in skeletal muscle. The BCAAs are leucine, isoleucine, and valine.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"支鏈胺基酸（BCAA）為白胺酸、異白胺酸與纈胺酸，是可直接在骨骼肌中氧化供能的主要胺基酸，對維持肌肉蛋白合成很重要。"},{"id":"q2688","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Enhancement","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Increased effectiveness of an already learned movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"增強（Enhancement）指已學會動作的有效性提升，不同於學習新動作的獲得階段。"},{"id":"q2689","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following are examples of training adaptations for aerobic exercise EXCEPT increased blood volume increased capillary density increased heart rate at a given rate of exercise increased oxygen extraction at a given rate of exercise increased stroke volume at a given rate of exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increased heart rate at a given rate of exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧訓練不會讓「同一運動強度下的心率上升」；反而因每搏輸出量增加，同強度心率下降。其他如血容量、微血管密度、氧攝取能力與每搏輸出量都會增加。"},{"id":"q2690","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Discriminant validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ability of a test to distinguish between two different constructs, resulting in a low correlation between the results of the two tests. Ex: comparing vertical jump to 1RM bench press. These tests assess skills and abilities that are unrelated to one another","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"區分效度（Discriminant validity）指測驗能區分不同構念，兩測驗結果相關很低。例：垂直跳與臥推 1RM 評估的能力彼此無關。"},{"id":"q2691","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what kind of chemical cascade takes place during muscular contraction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a chemical cascade causes a conformational change in tropomyosin that allows for the myosin filament to bind with the actin filament","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉收縮時發生化學級聯反應：鈣離子與肌鈣蛋白結合，導致原肌球蛋白構型改變，暴露肌動蛋白結合位點，使肌球蛋白橫橋得以結合。"},{"id":"q2692","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for dorsiflexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fibularis tertius, extensor digitorum longus, extensor hallucis longus, and tibialis anterior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"踝背屈由脛骨前肌、趾長伸肌、拇長伸肌與第三腓骨肌負責。"},{"id":"q2693","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"where do the oxidative and aerobic mechanisms occur in muscle cells?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in mitochondria","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"氧化（有氧）機制在粒線體內進行，包括檸檬酸迴圈與電子傳遞鏈。"},{"id":"q2694","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how are vertebrae grouped?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"into 7 cervical vertebrae in the neck region; 12 thoracic vertebrae in the middle to upper back; 5 lumbar vertebrae, which make up the lower back; 5 sacral vertebrae, which are fused together and make up the rear part of the pelvis; and 3 to 5 coccygeal vertebrae, which form a kind of vestigial internal tail extending downward from the pelvis.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"脊椎分為 7 個頸椎、12 個胸椎、5 個腰椎、5 個融合的薦椎（構成骨盆後部）與 3–5 個退化融合的尾椎。"},{"id":"q2695","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"is the work done in eccentric actions negative?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"no, the eccentric force exerted by the muscle keeps the weight from being accelerated downward by gravitational force","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"離心動作中肌肉並非單純做負功：肌肉施加的離心力防止重物被重力加速下拉，對控制動作與吸收能量仍有正面作用。"},{"id":"q2696","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the protein ratio recommendation after aerobic exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4:1 or 3:1 carb to protein ratio","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧運動後的補充建議糖與蛋白質比例為 4:1 或 3:1，以補肝糖並支援肌肉修復。"},{"id":"q2697","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"psychological component of state anxiety that is caused by fear of failure or worrying","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cognitive state anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"狀態焦慮的認知成分（cognitive state anxiety）源自對失敗的恐懼與擔憂等想法。"},{"id":"q2698","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many training goals should an athlete focus on per season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"one","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"每個訓練季節運動員應集中一個主要訓練目標，避免目標分散降低效果。"},{"id":"q2699","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the difference in the oxygen content between arterial and venous blood","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"arteriovenous oxygen difference","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動脈血與靜脈血氧含量之差稱為動靜脈氧差（a-vO2 difference），反映組織從血液中攝取氧氣的量。"},{"id":"q2700","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what test has the athlete sprint towards and up a staircase 3 steps at a time?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"margaria kalamen test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Margaria-Kalamen 功率測試要求運動員每步跨 3 臺階全速衝跑上階梯，測量磷酸原系統的功率。"},{"id":"q2701","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Calcium ATPase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The enzyme that pumps calcium into the sarcoplasmic reticulum.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"鈣 ATP 酶（calcium ATPase，SERCA）主動將胞質中的鈣離子泵回肌漿網，使肌肉進入舒張。"},{"id":"q2702","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Eustress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Positive stress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"良性壓力（Eustress）是正面的壓力，帶來動機與表現提升，與幹擾表現的幹擾壓力（distress）相反。"},{"id":"q2703","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"All of the following are signs of overtraining EXCEPT decreased muscle glycogen decreased performance increased maximal oxygen uptake increased muscle soreness increased submaximal heart rate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increased maximal oxygen uptake","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"過度訓練的徵兆不包括「最大攝氧量上升」；過度訓練時 VO2max 通常下降或不變，其他如肝糖下降、表現下滑、肌肉痠痛與次最大心率上升都是典型徵兆。"},{"id":"q2704","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Reliability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A measure of the degree of consistency or repeatability of a test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"信度（Reliability）指測驗結果的一致性或可重複性程度，是測驗品質的基本要求。"},{"id":"q2705","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how does the tropomyosin position relative to troponin and the actin filament?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the head of tropomyosin wraps helically around troponin on the actin filament, thereby preventing formation of the myosin cross bridge","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"原肌球蛋白的頭部沿著肌動蛋白螺旋纏繞肌鈣蛋白，在舒張時遮蔽肌動蛋白上的肌球蛋白結合位點，阻止橫橋形成。"},{"id":"q2706","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscles responsible for ankle plantarflexion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"plantaris, flexor digitorum longus, gastrocnemius, soleus","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"踝蹠屈包括腓腸肌、比目魚肌、足蹠肌與趾長屈肌。"},{"id":"q2707","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what do mitochondria require for aerobic mechanisms?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"oxygen as the terminal electron acceptor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"粒線體進行有氧代謝時以氧氣為電子傳遞鏈末端的最終電子接受體，缺氧則電子傳遞鏈停擺。"},{"id":"q2708","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what does epimysium cover?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the body’s more than 430 skeletal muscles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌外膜（epimysium）包覆全身 430 多條骨骼肌，並與肌腱相連續。"},{"id":"q2709","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"why is the knee is prone to injury?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because of its location between two long levers (the upper and lower leg)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝關節夾在大腿與小腿兩根長槓桿之間，受力矩與衝擊大，因此容易受傷。"},{"id":"q2710","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein recommendation for endurance athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"book: 1.0-1.6g/kgbw/day update: 1.4-1.8b/kgw/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"教科書對耐力運動員蛋白質建議為每日每公斤體重 1.0–1.6 克；較新研究建議 1.4–1.8 克。"},{"id":"q2711","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"physical reaction of state anxiety such as butterflies, muscle tension, and heart racing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"somatic state anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"狀態焦慮的身體症狀（somatic state anxiety）包括胃部翻騰、肌肉緊張、心跳加快等生理反應。"},{"id":"q2712","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"to express oxygen uptake in its common SI unit, what do you divide by?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the person’s weight in kilograms","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"攝氧量除以體重（公斤）換成 mL/kg/min，即常用的 SI 單位，以便不同體型的個體比較。"},{"id":"q2713","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Muscle Spindle**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Proprioceptors that consist of modified muscle fibers enclosed in a sheath of connective tissue. Muscle spindles provide information concerning the muscle length and rate of change in length.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌梭（muscle spindle）屬本體感覺接受器，由包在結締組織鞘內的特化肌纖維組成，提供肌肉長度與長度變化速率的資訊。"},{"id":"q2714","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how is power calculated from the margaria kalamen test?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"P (watts) = (w x h) / time w: athlete’s weight in N h: height from 3rd-9th step in meters","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Margaria-Kalamen 功率：P（瓦特）＝體重（牛頓）× 垂直高度（公尺，第 3 階至第 9 臺階）÷ 時間（秒）。"},{"id":"q2715","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Explicit instructions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Prescriptive information that gives the athlete rules for effectively executing a given task","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"明示指示（explicit instructions）是處方式資訊，直接告訴運動員完成動作的規則。"},{"id":"q2716","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"During maximal intensity activities (>90% of maximum) which fibers will be recruited?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Type I, Type IIa, and Type Iib","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"90% 以上最大強度的活動會動員第 I 型、第 IIa 型與第 IIb（x）型全部肌纖維，符合大小原則的最大動員。"},{"id":"q2717","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Intrasubject variability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The lack of consistent performance by the person tested","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"受試者內變異（intrasubject variability）指同一受試者反覆測驗表現不一致，會降低測驗信度。"},{"id":"q2718","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"reciprocal inhibition allows an athlete to achieve what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"allows for maximal contraction to occur in an agonist muscle group while inhibiting and actually forcing relaxation to occur in the antagonist muscle group, which then allows an athlete to achieve relaxation and enhance mental focus by alternating through relax-contract cycles throughout the body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"互動抑制（reciprocal inhibition）指主動肌收縮時反射性抑制拮抗肌，讓主動肌群達到最大收縮；也可利用收縮—放鬆迴圈放鬆身體、提升專注。"},{"id":"q2719","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"superior (cranial)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"near/toward upper part of body, toward head","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"上（superior/cranial）指靠近身體上部或頭部的位置術語。"},{"id":"q2720","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"which of the three macronutrients can be metabolized for energy without oxygen?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"carbohydrate, which is critical during anaerobic metabolism","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物是三大巨量營養素中唯一可在無氧條件下分解供能者，是無氧代謝的關鍵燃料。"},{"id":"q2721","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is the relationship of epimysium with tendons?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"epimysium is contiguous with the tendons","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌外膜與肌腱相連續，肌肉收縮產生的張力經結締組織傳導至肌腱與附著骨。"},{"id":"q2722","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"in what plane do flexion and extension about the knee occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"almost exclusively in the sagittal plane.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝關節的屈伸幾乎只在矢狀面上發生。"},{"id":"q2723","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein recommendation for strength training or anaerobic athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.4-1.7g/kgbw/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"力量或無氧運動員每日蛋白質建議攝取量約為每公斤體重 1.4–1.7 克。"},{"id":"q2724","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"what are some examples of somatic anxiety?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"tense muscles fast HR rapid breathing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"身體焦慮（somatic anxiety）的例子：肌肉緊張、心率加快、呼吸急促。"},{"id":"q2725","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"pressure exerted against the arterial walls as blood is forcefully ejected during ventricular contraction","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"systolic blood pressure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮壓（systolic blood pressure）是心室收縮將血液強力射出時對動脈壁施加的壓力。"},{"id":"q2726","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what test has a pair of athletes sprint to the line 25 yards away and then immediately sprint back to the first line for a total of 6 round trips as fast as possible?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"300 yard shuttle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"300 碼折返跑：全速衝向 25 碼處的分界線再立即折返，來回共 6 趟，評估無氧糖解系統的無氧能力。"},{"id":"q2727","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Combination training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process of combining aerobic and anaerobic training, postulated to improve recovery. In heavily anaerobic sports (ie. powerlifting, Olympic lifting), the combination may be detrimental to maximum strength and power. In highly-trained endurance athletes, the addition of strength training has been shown to improve aerobic performance.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"組合訓練（Combination training）把有氧與無氧訓練結合。對重量舉、舉重等高度無氧專案可能幹擾最大力量與功率發展；但對高水平耐力選手，加入力量訓練已被證明可改善有氧表現。"},{"id":"q2728","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Extrinsic motivation","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Motivation from an external source - i.e. “trophies, social approval”","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"外在動機（Extrinsic motivation）來自外在來源，如獎盃、獎勵或社會認可，與內在動機相對。"},{"id":"q2729","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which principle of training is based on the idea that one should target the sport-related energy pathways and muscle groups?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"specificity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"專項性原則（specificity）：訓練應針對專項的能量系統與肌群進行，練習與測驗都應貼近專項需求。"},{"id":"q2730","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Interrater reliability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The degree to which different raters agree; also referred to as objectivity or interrater agreement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"評量者間信度（Interrater reliability）指不同評量者對同一測驗結果的一致程度，又稱客觀性。"},{"id":"q2731","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what concentration of hemoglobin is oxygen carried through circulation with?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3mL per liter of plasma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"血漿中物理溶解的氧量約為每公升血漿 3 mL；絕大部分氧由紅血球的血紅素攜帶。"},{"id":"q2732","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"antonym of cranial?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"caudal (inferior)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"尾側（caudal/inferior）是頭側（cranial/superior）的反義詞，指靠近下部。"},{"id":"q2733","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"which energy system is active during anaerobic exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"all three energy systems are active at any given time, it’s an issue of contribution percentage (modulated by intensity and duration)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"三種能量系統在任何時刻都同時運轉，差別只在貢獻比例，由運動強度與持續時間決定。"},{"id":"q2734","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what are tendons attached to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"tendon is attached to bone periosteum, a specialized connective tissue covering all bones","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌腱附著於骨膜（periosteum），即覆蓋所有骨表面的特化結締組織。"},{"id":"q2735","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"ligamentous and cartilaginous stabilizing structures prevent rotation in what plane(s)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"frontal and transverse","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝關節的韌帶與軟骨穩定結構可限制額狀面與水平面（軸向）的旋轉。"},{"id":"q2736","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein recommendation for combination athletes (anaerobic + aerobic)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.4-1.7g/kgbw/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"混合無氧與有氧專案的運動員每日蛋白質建議攝取量約為每公斤體重 1.4–1.7 克。"},{"id":"q2737","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"subjective experience of apprehension and uncontrolled arousal that leads to elevated neural outflow and increased endocrine activity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"state anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"狀態焦慮（state anxiety）是主觀的不安與失控喚起體驗，伴隨神經活動輸出增加與內分泌活動上升。"},{"id":"q2738","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"why are assistance exercises commonly used for injury prevention and rehab?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because they isolate a specific muscle or muscle group","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"輔助練習能孤立特定肌肉或肌群，便於針對弱點強化與傷後復健。"},{"id":"q2739","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"rate pressure product (or double product) =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"HR x systolic blood pressure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"率壓乘積（Rate pressure product）＝心率 × 收縮壓，反映心肌耗氧量與工作負荷。"},{"id":"q2740","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the best of _____ trials is recorded for the reactive strength index test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反應式力量指數測試記錄 3 次試跳中的最佳成績。"},{"id":"q2741","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Cori cycle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process of transporting lactate to the liver for conversion to glucose.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"科裡迴圈（Cori cycle）：肌肉產生的乳酸經血液運至肝臟，經糖新生轉回葡萄糖再供肌肉利用。"},{"id":"q2742","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Fractionalization","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Breaking down tasks into subcomponents that must ultimately occur simultaneously","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"任務分解（Fractionalization）把整體動作拆解為必須最終同時完成的子成分，便於分步學習。"},{"id":"q2743","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Exercise results in an increase in this system’s activity:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Sympathetic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動會提高自律神經系統中交感神經的活動，出現心率上升、血壓上升、血流重新分配等反應。"},{"id":"q2744","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Intrarater variability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The lack of consistent scores by a given tester","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"評量者內變異（Intrarater variability）指同一評量者評分不一致，會損害信度。"},{"id":"q2745","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"during exercise, how is carbon dioxide transported?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"out of the cell via diffusion and into the plasma for transport to the lungs for clearance – buffering CO2 relies on bicarbonate and water, which requires catalyzation by carbonic anhydrase in order to buffer the hydrogen ions accumulating in the blood.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動時二氧化碳以擴散進入血漿，多數在碳酸酐酶催化下與水生成碳酸氫鹽並緩衝氫離子，再運至肺排出。"},{"id":"q2746","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ventral/dorsal are other words for what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anterior/posterior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腹側（ventral）與背側（dorsal）即前（anterior）與後（posterior）的別稱。"},{"id":"q2747","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what chemical process does the phosphagen system rely on?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hydrolysis of ATP and breakdown of another high-energy phosphate molecule called creatine phosphate (CP), also called phosphocreatine (PCr)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統依靠 ATP 水解與磷酸肌酸（CP/PCr）分解，提供高能磷酸鍵快速再合成 ATP。"},{"id":"q2748","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is the diameter of muscle cells?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"about 50 to 100 µm in diameter (about the diameter of a human hair)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"骨骼肌纖維直徑約 50–100 微米，約等於一根頭髮的直徑。"},{"id":"q2749","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what does the stability of the shoulder depend on?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glenoid labrum, the joint synovium, and capsules, ligaments, muscles, tendons, and bursae. the rotator cuff muscles (supraspinatus, infraspinatus, subscapularis, and teres minor) and the pectorals are particularly instrumental in keeping the ball of the humerus in place.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩關節穩定依賴肩盂唇、關節滑膜、關節囊、韌帶、肌肉、肌腱與滑囊；其中旋轉肌袖（rotator cuff）（棘上肌、棘下肌、肩胛下肌、小圓肌）與胸肌對固定肱骨頭最為關鍵。"},{"id":"q2750","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein recommendation when in a reduced calorie deficit/to maintain lean body mass","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1.8-2.7g/kgbw/day","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"熱量赤字或減重期間為維持瘦體重，蛋白質建議可高達每日每公斤體重 1.8–2.7 克。"},{"id":"q2751","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"personality characteristic that leads the athlete to perceive situations as threatening","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"trait anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"特質焦慮（trait anxiety）是讓人傾向把情境知覺為威脅的人格特質。"},{"id":"q2752","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"exercises that load the spine directly or indirectly, requiring muscular stabilization of posture during performance of the lifting movement","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"structural exercises","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"結構性練習直接或間接負荷脊椎，動作中需肌群穩定姿勢，例如槓鈴硬舉、深蹲與高翻。"},{"id":"q2753","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"pressure exerted against the arterial walls when no blood is being forcefully ejected through the vessels","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"diastolic blood pressure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舒張壓（diastolic blood pressure）是心室舒張、血液不再強力射出時動脈壁承受的壓力。"},{"id":"q2754","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the best of _____ trials is recorded to the nearest 0.5 inch for the vertical jump","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"垂直跳記錄 3 次試跳中的最佳成績，精確到 0.5 英吋。"},{"id":"q2755","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Goal setting","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A process of pursuing progressively challenging standard of performance with a defined criterion of task success which increases the likelihood of success","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"目標設定（Goal setting）是依明確成功標準逐步提高表現標準的過程，能提升成功機率。"},{"id":"q2756","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Adaptations in all of the following contribute to increases in VO2max with endurance training EXCEPT heart rate stroke volume mitochondrial density capillary density","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Heart rate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"耐力訓練提升 VO2max 的適應不包括心率上升；訓練後同強度心率通常下降，每搏輸出量、粒線體密度與微血管密度則增加。"},{"id":"q2757","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Test Selection","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Metabolic Energy System Specificity • Consider energy demands (phosphagen, glycolytic, and oxidative) of the sport when choosing or designing tests. Biomechanical Movement Pattern Specificity • The more similar the test is to a movement in the sport, the better. Experience and Training Status • Consider the athlete’s ability to perform the technique. • Consider the athlete’s level of strength and endurance training Age and Sex • Both may an affect athlete’s experience, interest, and ability. Environmental Factors • High temperature and high humidity can impair performance, pose health risks, and lower the validity of aerobic endurance tests • Temperature fluctuations can reduce ability to compare test results over time • Altitude can impair performance on aerobic endurance tests","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗選取需考慮：能量系統與動作模式專項性、運動員經驗與訓練水準、年齡與性別，以及高溫高濕與海拔等環境因素。"},{"id":"q2758","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how is the buffering of CO2 supported?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"through the natural acid-base buffering capacity of hemoglobin in order to maintain blood pH balance. once exercise intensity reaches a level where aerobic metabolism is insufficient to maintain pH balance, lactic acid accumulates and is referred to as OBLA","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"血紅素的酸鹼緩衝能力協助緩衝 CO2、維持血液 pH；當強度超過有氧代謝能維持酸鹼平衡的臨界點時乳酸開始累積，即血乳酸累積起點（OBLA）。"},{"id":"q2759","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"medial?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"near body’s midline","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內側（medial）指靠近身體正中線。"},{"id":"q2760","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what enzyme catalyzes the synthesis of ATP from CP and ADP?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"phosphocreatine / creatine kinase","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌酸激酶（creatine kinase）催化磷酸肌酸把磷酸基轉給 ADP 再合成 ATP，是磷酸原系統的核心反應。"},{"id":"q2761","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how many fibers are in a fasciculi?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fasciculi may consist of up to 150 fibers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"一束肌束最多可含約 150 條肌纖維。"},{"id":"q2762","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"when a football player is hit at midleg from the side while the foot is planted firmly on the ground – what kind of torque is this?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"frontal plane torque on the knee","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"足部固定時小腿中段被側向撞擊，暴力作用於膝關節形成額狀面力矩，易傷內側副韌帶與半月板。"},{"id":"q2763","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"why is it important to keep protein intake high when in a reduced calorie diet?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"to avoid sarcopenia","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"節食期間維持高蛋白攝取可避免肌肉流失，防止肌肉減少症（sarcopenia）。"},{"id":"q2764","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"athletes with high levels of _________ anxiety tend to use attentional capacity on task-irrelevant cognitions such as thoughts of failure or catastrophe","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"trait anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"特質焦慮高的運動員把注意力資源耗在與任務無關的認知上，如失敗或災難化的想法。"},{"id":"q2765","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"a structural exercises that is performed very quickly or explosively","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"power exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快速或爆發式完成的結構性練習稱為功率練習，例如高翻與抓舉。"},{"id":"q2766","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"diastolic blood pressure can decrease with aerobic endurance exercise due to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vasodilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力運動時因血管舒張使周邊阻力下降，舒張壓可能降低。"},{"id":"q2767","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Proprioceptor**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Specialized sensory receptors within joints, muscles, and tendons. Proprioceptors are sensitive to pressure and tension in the muscle and relay information about muscle dynamics to the nervous system. This process allows the CNS to maintain muscle tone and perform coordinated movements.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"本體感覺接受器（proprioceptor）分佈於關節、肌肉與肌腱，感受壓力與張力並向中樞神經系統回報肌肉動態，以維持肌張力與協調動作。"},{"id":"q2768","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the average of ___ trials is recorded to the nearest 1.0 second for the 300 yard shuttle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"300 碼折返跑記錄 2 趟成績的平均值，精確到 1.0 秒。"},{"id":"q2769","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Creatine phosphate (CP)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A high-energy phosphate molecule that provides the phosphate group for the synthesis of ATP from ADP in the phosphagen system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸（CP）是高磷酸鍵分子，在磷酸原系統中提供磷酸基讓 ADP 再合成 ATP。"},{"id":"q2770","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Guided discovery","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Providing prompts for a task without explicitly telling the athlete how to do the task","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"引導式發現（Guided discovery）給運動員提示而不直接說明動作方法，讓其自行探索正確動作感覺。"},{"id":"q2771","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a training goal for an aerobic endurance athlete?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase VO2submax","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧耐力選手的訓練目標不包括提升次最大攝氧量；次最大攝氧量主要由動作經濟性決定，訓練目標應放在 VO2max、乳酸閾與最大攝氧量等。"},{"id":"q2772","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Aerobic Endurance Testing in the Heat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"During the weeks prior to the test, athletes should engage in enough training to establish a baseline of fitness in the activity being tested Avoid testing under extreme combinations of heat and humidity On days when the temperature is high, indoor facilities should be used, or testing should be conducted during morning or early evening hours The athletes should be acclimatized to the heat and humidity for at least one week prior to testing Athletes should make sure they are well hydrated in the 24-hour period preceding aerobic endurance testing in the heat Athletes should be encouraged to drink during exercise in the heat, ideally 150 to 250 ml (5-9 fluid ounces) every 15 minutes Athletes should wear a light-colored, loose-fitting tank top and shorts, preferably of a mesh material Be attentive to possible symptoms of heatstroke or heat exhaustion: cramps, nausea, dizziness, difficulty in walking or standing, faintness, garbled speech, lack of sweat, red or ashen skin, and goose bumps Be aware of the symptoms of hyponatremia or water intoxication: extremely dilute urine in combination with bloated skin, altered consciousness, or loss of consciousness, with no increase in body temperature. Athletes should be encouraged to eat foods high in magnesium and potassium. Proficient medical coverage should be readily available","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高溫環境下有氧耐力測試：測試前應建立體能基線、提前至少一週熱順應、測試前 24 小時充分補水、運動中每 15 分鐘補充 150–250 毫升、穿淺色寬鬆排汗服裝，並留意中暑與低血鈉症狀、配置醫療支援。"},{"id":"q2773","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is diffusion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"movement of gases from areas high concentration to areas of lower concentration","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"擴散是氣體由高濃度處向低濃度處的淨移動，人體內氣體交換即以此方式進行。"},{"id":"q2774","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"lateral - relationship to medial?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"away from body’s midline","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"外側（lateral）指遠離身體正中線，與內側相反。"},{"id":"q2775","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is the reaction for catalyzing the synthesis of ATP from CP and ADP?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ADP + CP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ADP + CP 在肌酸激酶催化下生成 ATP + 肌酸，這是磷酸原系統的反應式。"},{"id":"q2776","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"is endomyseum contiguous with skeletal muscle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"not quite, it is contiguous with the fiber’s membrane, or sarcolemma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌內膜並非直接與整塊肌肉連續，而是與單條肌纖維的細胞膜（肌膜，sarcolemma）相連續。"},{"id":"q2777","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"in what sports would strength-to-mass ratio be most important?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sprinting and jumping, and in sports involving weight classification.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"力量體重比在跳躍、衝刺及有量級分類的專案中最重要，因為體重直接成為負擔而力量不隨體重等比例增加。"},{"id":"q2778","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"why are protein needs inversely proportional to calorie intake?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"small amounts of protein can be metabolized as a source of energy when a person is in a state of negative calorie balance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"熱量攝取下降時身體會把少量蛋白質當作能量代謝，因此蛋白質需求與熱量攝取呈反比。"},{"id":"q2779","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: athletes with high levels of trait anxiety can handle higher levels of pressure because of the decreased probability of engaging in such personal catastrophizing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"false, athletes with LOW levels can","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"錯。是特質焦慮低的運動員較能承受高壓力，因為他們較少陷入災難化思考。"},{"id":"q2780","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"true or false: muscle balance includes equal strength","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"false","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"錯。肌肉平衡並非指各肌群力量相等，而是指主動肌、拮抗肌與協同肌群間的力量與張力關係能維持關節正常功能與排列。"},{"id":"q2781","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"average blood pressure throughout the cardiac cycle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"mean arterial pressure (MAP)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平均動脈壓（MAP）是整個心跳週期中血壓的平均值。"},{"id":"q2782","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Pulmonary valve**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Valve in the heart that prevents blood flow from the pulmonary artery into the right ventricle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肺動脈瓣防止血液由肺動脈逆流回右心室，屬半月瓣。"},{"id":"q2783","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"for the curl up test, the athlete performs as many curl ups as possible without pausing to a maximum of ___?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"75 curl ups","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"仰臥起坐測驗要求受試者不暫停地盡量多做，上限為 75 下。"},{"id":"q2784","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Cytochrome","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A series of electron carriers in the electron transport chain. The cytochromes pass hydrogen down the electron transport chain to form a proton concentration gradient, which provides the energy for ATP production.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"細胞色素（cytochrome）是電子傳遞鏈中的一系列電子載體，透過傳遞氫沿鏈形成質子濃度梯度，提供 ATP 合成的能量。"},{"id":"q2785","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Ideal performance state","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Ultimate goal of every athlete - competition performance marked by psychological and physiological efficiency","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最佳表現狀態（ideal performance state）是每位運動員的最終目標：比賽時心理與生理均處於高效狀態。"},{"id":"q2786","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An application of the principle of overload for an aerobic endurance athlete would be to have the athlete train","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"above lactate threshold","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對有氧耐力選手套用過載原則，應讓其在乳酸閾之上訓練，才能超越現有適能水準。"},{"id":"q2787","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Selection and Training of Testers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Provide testers with practice and training. Ensure consistency among testers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗人員須經過練習與訓練，確保不同人員執行測驗的方式一致，以維持信度。"},{"id":"q2788","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the cause of diffusion?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"due to the partial pressure exerted by each molecule of gas; during exercise, the partial pressure of the gases are altered depending on their location in the circulatory system.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"擴散的驅動力來自各氣體分子的分壓；運動時氣體在迴圈系統不同位置的分壓改變，決定擴散方向。"},{"id":"q2789","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"bilateral?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"on either side of central axis or midline","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雙側（bilateral）指位於中軸或正中線兩側。"},{"id":"q2790","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what does creatine phosphate do for the ADP–>ATP process","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"supplies a phosphate group that combines with ADP to replenish ATP, a reaction that provides energy at a high rate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸肌酸在反應中供給磷酸基與 ADP 結合，快速補充 ATP，供能速率極高。"},{"id":"q2791","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what contiguity do the connective tissues (endo/peri/epi mysium) have in common?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"they are all contiguous with the tendon, therefore tension developed in a muscle cell is transmitted to the tendon and the bone to which it is attached","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內膜、周膜與外膜最終都與肌腱相連續，因此肌纖維產生的張力能經結締組織傳至肌腱與其附著之骨。"},{"id":"q2792","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"why does strength-to-mass ratio not hold for larger athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when body size increases, muscle volume (and concomitantly body weight) increases proportionately more than does muscle cross-sectional area (and concomitantly strength)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"個體變大時，肌肉體積與體重的增加比例超過肌肉橫截面積與力量的增加比例，因此體型較大的運動員力量體重比反而較低。"},{"id":"q2793","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when caloric intake goes down, protein requirement goes ___","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"up","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"熱量攝取下降時，蛋白質需求上升。"},{"id":"q2794","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"in a ___________ state, arousal is under the control of the athlete and can be elevated or lowered as needed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"non anxious state","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"非焦慮狀態下，運動員能依需要自主提升或降低喚起程度。"},{"id":"q2795","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"mean arterial pressure is usually more or less than the average of the systolic and diastolic pressures?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"less","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平均動脈壓通常低於收縮壓與舒張壓的算術平均值，因舒張期較長而更偏向舒張壓。"},{"id":"q2796","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Red blood cell**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The major component of blood that contains hemoglobin. Red blood cells transport oxygen as well as other processes such as catalyzing the reaction that facilitates carbon dioxide removal.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"紅血球是血液的主要成分，內含血紅素負責運氧，並參與催化二氧化碳清除的反應。"},{"id":"q2797","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how do the starting positions for the army pushup and ACSM pushup for females differ?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"army: knees off ground ACSM: knees on ground","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軍隊伏地挺身起勢時膝離地；ACSM 女性版本則膝著地。"},{"id":"q2798","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Depletion","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The consumption of molecules and substrates during energy production or other processes.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"耗竭（Depletion）指能量生成或其他過程中分子與受質被消耗殆盡的狀態。"},{"id":"q2799","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Imagery","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A cognitive skill in which an athlete creates or recreates an experience in his or her mind","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"想像（imagery）是一種認知技能，運動員在腦中創造或重現某種經驗。"},{"id":"q2800","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Toni wants to increase the speed at the end of her endurance running performance. The best training method for achieving this goal is","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Repetition","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"重複訓練法以反覆進行相同動作或分段練習來改善動作速度與技術一致性，適合用來提升耐力跑末段的速度。"},{"id":"q2801","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Test Format","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Consider whether athletes will be tested all at once or in groups Multiple testers allowed but they should give the test to the same athletes each time Each tester should administer one test at a time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗格式上可決定一次測全員或分組進行；可多位測驗人員，但每次應由相同人員測相同運動員；每位測驗人員一次只執行一種測驗。"},{"id":"q2802","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the gas pressures at the alveolus level and venous level respectively?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"alveolus: PO2 = 100 mm Hg and PCO2 = 40 mm Hg; venous: PO2 = 40 mm Hg and PCO2 = 46 mm Hg (after unloading into muscle tissue)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肺泡處 PO2 約 100 mmHg、PCO2 約 40 mmHg；靜脈血 PO2 約 40 mmHg、PCO2 約 46 mmHg。分壓差決定氣體交換方向。"},{"id":"q2803","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ipsilateral?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"on or affecting the same side of the body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"同側（ipsilateral）指位於或影響身體同一側。"},{"id":"q2804","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is the downside of the PCr reaction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because CP is stored in relatively small amounts, the phosphagen system cannot be the primary supplier of energy for continuous, long-duration activities","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統的限制在於磷酸肌酸儲量相對很少，無法在長時間持續運動中擔任主要能量來源。"},{"id":"q2805","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what does the light I-band correspond with?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the areas in two adjacent sarcomeres that contain only actin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"明帶對應相鄰兩個肌小節中只含肌動蛋白細絲的區域。"},{"id":"q2806","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what is the classic formula?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"load lifted is divided by body weight to the two-thirds power (accounts for relationship of cross-sectional area vs volume)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"經典公式為負重除以體重的 2/3 次冪，用以校正肌肉橫截面積與體積的關係，便於不同體重者比較力量。"},{"id":"q2807","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein needs go up as a percentage of total calorie intake by approximately __% for every 100 calorie decrease below 2,000 calories (AMDR)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"依 AMDR，熱量攝取每低於 2,000 大卡 100 大卡，蛋白質需求佔總熱量比例約增加 1%。"},{"id":"q2808","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"in the ________ state, arousal is uncontrolled","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anxious state","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"焦慮狀態下喚起失控。"},{"id":"q2809","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"number of training sessions completed in a given period of time","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"training frequency","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"訓練頻率指單位時間內完成的訓練課次數。"},{"id":"q2810","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"mean arterial pressure =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"(systolic - diastolic) / 3 + diastolic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平均動脈壓的簡化演算法：（收縮壓−舒張壓）÷3＋舒張壓。"},{"id":"q2811","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Right bundle branch**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fibers in the heart that send the contraction impulse to the right ventricle.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"右束支將心臟收縮衝動傳至右心室。"},{"id":"q2812","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"for the army standard pushup test, as many repetition are done within a timed __ minute period?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2 minute","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軍隊標準伏地挺身測驗在 2 分鐘內盡量多完成次數。"},{"id":"q2813","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"Electron transport chain (ETC)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Series of proton acceptors that plays a fundamental role in oxidative metabolism.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"電子傳遞鏈是由質子接受體組成的系列載體，在有氧代謝中扮演核心角色，是最後產生大量 ATP 的步驟。"},{"id":"q2814","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"Individual zones of optimal functioning","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Different people in different types of performances perform best with very different levels of arousal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"個人在最佳功能區域（IZOF）：不同運動員在不同專案中最適的喚起水準各異，不能一概而論。"},{"id":"q2815","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sally spent her Spring break training in the heat in Florida. She pushed herself more than usual and refused to take off any days. On three days she doubled her workout by running her program in the morning and again in the evening. When she returned from break, she found that her resting heart rate was higher than normal. This increase in heart rate was likely due to this:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Overtraining syndrome","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"假期連續在高溫下加倍訓練量、缺乏休息，返校後靜心率上升，是過度訓練症候群的典型徵兆。"},{"id":"q2816","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Testing Batteries and Multiple Testing Trials","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Duplicate test setups can be used for large groups. * Allow 2 to 3 minutes of rest between attempts that are not close to the athlete’s maximum, 3 TO 5 MINUTES BETWEEN ATTEMPTS THAT ARE CLOSE TO THE MAXIMUM, and AT LEAST 5 MINUTES BETWEEN TEST BATTERIES.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗組合與多次試測：大批受試者可複製測驗場地；非接近最大的試測間休息 2–3 分鐘，接近最大者休息 3–5 分鐘，不同測驗組合之間至少休息 5 分鐘。"},{"id":"q2817","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what determines whether the gases (CO2/O2 or PCO2/O2) move into or out circulation during exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the changes in pressures","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"氣體（O2/CO2）進出迴圈的方向由兩側分壓變化決定，氣體由高分壓側向低分壓側擴散。"},{"id":"q2818","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"contralateral?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"on or affecting opposite sides of the body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對側（contralateral）指位於或影響身體兩側中的對側。"},{"id":"q2819","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"how much ATP does the body store?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"approximately 80 to 100 g (about 3 ounces) of ATP at any given time, which does not represent a significant energy reserve for exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"人體同時僅儲存約 80–100 克 ATP，對運動而言不是重要的能量儲備，必須不斷再合成。"},{"id":"q2820","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"where is the z-line located and what does it run through?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in the middle of the I-band running longitudinally through the I-band","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Z 線位於明帶中央，並縱向貫穿明帶，是肌動蛋白細絲的附著點。"},{"id":"q2821","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"where do 85% to 90% of all intervertebral disk herniations occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"at the disk between the lowest two lumbar vertebrae (L4 and L5) or between the lowest lumbar and the top sacral vertebra","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"約 85–90% 的椎間盤突出發生於最下兩節腰椎之間（L4–L5）或最低腰椎與第一薦椎之間。"},{"id":"q2822","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"true or false: sports dietitians should first establish an athlete's protein intake and then add carbohydrate and fats as determined by total calorie needs","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對。運動營養師應先確立蛋白質需求量，再依總熱量需求填補碳水化合物與脂肪。"},{"id":"q2823","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"arousal is typically too _____ during periods of ineffective state anxiety","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無效的狀態焦慮期間，喚起通常過高。"},{"id":"q2824","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is the general recommendation for training frequency for athletes to allow sufficient recovery between sessions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3x/week","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"一般建議運動員每週 3 次訓練課，使兩次訓練之間有充分恢復。"},{"id":"q2825","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"primary mechanics for regulating regional blood flow","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vasoconstriction and vasodilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"調節區域性血流的主要機制是血管收縮與血管舒張。"},{"id":"q2826","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"for the ACSM push up for females, AMRAP are done continuously until _______","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"failure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ACSM 女性伏地挺身測驗以膝著地姿勢不中斷地盡量多做，做到無法完成一次標準動作為止。"},{"id":"q2827","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Intrinsic feedback**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Feedback provided to the athlete by his or her own senses","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內在回饋是運動員經由自身視覺、本體感覺等感官獲得的動作資訊。"},{"id":"q2828","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following is the most effective type of exercise for optimizing sport-specific muscular strength for well-trained athletes? assistance exercises core exercises structural exercises","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Core exercises","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"本題答案卡為核心練習；但教科書標準答案通常為結構性練習，因為其動作模式與多數專項的整體發力最接近，對高水準運動員專項力量最適。"},{"id":"q2829","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sequence of Tests","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Nonfatiguing tests * Agility tests * Maximum power and strength tests * Sprint tests * Local muscular endurance tests * Fatiguing anaerobic capacity tests * Aerobic capacity tests","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗順序原則：先不疲勞專案→敏捷→最大功率與力量→衝刺→區域性肌耐力→會疲勞的無氧能力→最後有氧能力。"},{"id":"q2830","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the carbohydrate recommendations for aerobic and anaerobic athletes respectively?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"aerobic: 8g to 10g / kg; anaerobic: 5g to 6g / kg","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物建議：有氧選手每公斤體重 8–10 克，無氧選手每公斤體重 5–6 克。"},{"id":"q2831","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"intermediate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"located between two structures -- e.g. one medial and one lateral, or one superior/inferior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"中間（intermediate）指位於兩個構造之間，例如同時偏內或偏外、偏上或偏下。"},{"id":"q2832","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what's the lowest ATP a body can have?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"not zero, because ATP stores cannot be completely depleted due to the necessity for basic cellular function","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 儲量不會降到零，因基本細胞功能需要 ATP 持續存在，因此儲量無法完全耗盡。"},{"id":"q2833","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"where is the h-zone located?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in the center of the sarcomere","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"H 帶位於肌小節正中央。"},{"id":"q2834","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"two factors of neural control of muscles?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"recruitment and rate coding. which and how many motor units are involved in a muscle contraction (recruitment) and the rate at which the motor units are fired (rate coding).","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉的神經控制有兩要素：運動單位的動員（哪些、多少）與頻率編碼（激發頻率的高低）。"},{"id":"q2835","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"protein has the greatest thermic effect of feeding. what does this mean?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"more calories are burned during the digestion of protein as compared to carbohydrates or fats","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"食物的熱效應中蛋白質最高，代表消化代謝蛋白質所消耗的熱量比碳水化合物或脂肪更多。"},{"id":"q2836","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"imbalance between demand and response capability, under conditions where failure to meet demand has consequences","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"stress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"壓力（stress）定義：在需求與應變能力不平衡、且未能達成需求會有後果的情況下所處的狀態。"},{"id":"q2837","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is the general recommendation for rest days between strength days?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"0-2 rest days (no more than 3)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"兩次力量訓練之間建議安排 0–2 個休息日，不超過 3 天。"},{"id":"q2838","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"max % of cardiac output that is distributed to skeletal muscle with vigorous exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"90%","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"劇烈運動時，最多可將約 90% 的心輸出量分配給骨骼肌。"},{"id":"q2839","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Semilunar valves**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Collective term for the aortic and pulmonary valves.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"半月瓣是主動脈瓣與肺動脈瓣的總稱，因瓣葉呈半月形得名。"},{"id":"q2840","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what indicates the termination of the yo yo intermittent recovery test?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when the athlete is unable to maintain the required speed as indicated by the auditory signals","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Yo-Yo 間歇恢復測驗在運動員無法跟上語音訊號規定的速度時結束。"},{"id":"q2841","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Energy**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The capacity to perform work.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"能量是作功的能力。"},{"id":"q2842","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Intrinsic motivation**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A desire to be competent and self-determining - i.e. “love of the game”","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內在動機出於追求能力感與自主性的慾望，例如單純熱愛運動本身。"},{"id":"q2843","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"An individual’s 1RM can be assessed in all of the following exercises EXCEPT Bicep curl Knee ext Shoulder press Calf raise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Shoulder press","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肩推不適合用於評估 1RM：單關節或軌道固定的動作較安全，肩推因需穩定、技術因素高，1RM 測試效度較差。"},{"id":"q2844","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Preparing Athletes for Testing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Announce the date, time, and purpose of a test battery in advance. * Host a pretest practice session. * Provide clear and simple instructions. * Demonstrate proper test performance. * Organize a pretest warm-up. * Tell athletes their test scores after each trial. * Administer a supervised cool-down period.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗前準備：提前公告測驗時間與目的、舉辦試測練習、清楚說明並示範、組織暖身、每試後回報成績、安排有監督的緩和活動。"},{"id":"q2845","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is a benefit of a process goal?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"causes an athlete to engage in the behaviors necessary day to day without becoming too focused on the result","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"過程目標的優點：讓運動員每天執行必要的行為，而不過度執著於結果。"},{"id":"q2846","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what are the implications of the amount of stored ATP?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"it does not represent a significant energy reserve for exercise, and ATP stores cannot be completely depleted due to the necessity for basic cellular function.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 儲量少的意義：對運動不是重要能量儲備，需即時再合成；同時因基本細胞功能所需而無法完全耗盡。"},{"id":"q2847","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is the composition of the h-zone?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"only myosin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"H 帶的成分只有肌球蛋白粗絲。"},{"id":"q2848","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"example of eccentric muscle action to create force?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cheating a bicep curl","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"利用離心收縮產生力量的例子：做二頭肌彎舉時「借力」（cheating）以完成額外次數。"},{"id":"q2849","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"muscle sensitivity to amino acids is enhanced for up to ____ hours after a bout of exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"48 hours (24-48)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動後肌肉對胺基酸的敏感度提升可持續達 48 小時（約 24–48 小時）。"},{"id":"q2850","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"environmental or cognitive event that causes stress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"stressor","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"壓力源（stressor）是引發壓力的環境或認知事件。"},{"id":"q2851","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete that has a beginner training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2-3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"初學者訓練狀態建議每週 2–3 次。"},{"id":"q2852","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"________ exercise provides for the greatest impact on both oxygen uptake and carbon dioxide production as compared to other types of exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"aerobic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"與無氧訓練相比，有氧訓練對攝氧量與二氧化碳生成量的整體影響最大。"},{"id":"q2853","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what test has the athlete double leg hop from the center of the hexagon over each side and back to the center in a continuous clockwise sequence 3x?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hexagon test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"六角測試：從六角形中央雙腳跳越每一邊再回到中央，順時針連續完成 3 輪，測驗敏捷性。"},{"id":"q2854","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Energy substrate**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A molecule that can be used to produce energy (i.e. lactate).","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"能量受質是可用來產生能量的分子，例如乳酸。"},{"id":"q2855","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Inverted-U Theory**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Theory of performance that states that arousal facilitates performance until an optimal level beyond which increased arousal decreases performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"倒 U 理論認為喚起提升表現至最適水準，超過後再增加喚起反而降低表現。"},{"id":"q2856","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"This training goal requires the longest recovery time between sets:","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscular strength and power","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉力量與功率的訓練目標需要最長的組間休息，以恢復磷酸原系統。"},{"id":"q2857","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Measuring Parameters of Athletic Performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Maximum Muscular Strength (Low-Speed Strength) * Anaerobic or Maximum Muscular Power (High-Speed Strength) * Anaerobic Capacity * Local Muscular Endurance * Aerobic Capacity * Agility * Speed * Flexibility * Body Composition * Anthropometry","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動表現量測專案包括：最大肌力、無氧/最大功率、無氧能力、區域性肌耐力、有氧能力、敏捷、速度、柔軟度、體成分與人體測量。"},{"id":"q2858","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what kinds of muscle striations are there and why?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"smooth muscle, obliquely striated muscle and striated muscle (striated contains actin and myosin; others don't)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉分為平滑肌、斜紋肌與橫紋肌；只有橫紋肌的肌絲排列形成明暗帶（含肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白）。"},{"id":"q2859","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"When muscle fatigue causes ATP to be reduced by 50-60% of preexercise levels, how does phosphagen system fix this?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"by using the creatine kinase reaction to maintain the concentration of ATP; under normal circumstances, skeletal muscle concentrations of CP are four to six times higher than ATP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"疲勞使 ATP 下降 50–60% 時，肌酸激酶反應仍可維持 ATP 濃度，因為正常骨骼肌的 CP 濃度是 ATP 的 4–6 倍。"},{"id":"q2860","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how does the h-zone work during muscle contractions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the h-zone decreases as the actin slides over the myosin toward the center of the sarcomere","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮時肌動蛋白沿肌球蛋白滑向肌小節中央，H 帶變窄。"},{"id":"q2861","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"true or false: consuming protein sooner, rather than waiting, has a greater effect on acute muscle protein synthesis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對。運動後越早攝取蛋白質，對急性肌肉蛋白合成的刺激越大。"},{"id":"q2862","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"negative stress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"distress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"幹擾壓力（distress）是負面、對表現有害的壓力。"},{"id":"q2863","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete that has a intermediate training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3-4","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"中階訓練狀態建議每週 3–4 次。"},{"id":"q2864","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"volume of air breathed per minute","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"minute ventilation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"分鐘通氣量（minute ventilation）指每分鐘吸入或撥出的氣體總量。"},{"id":"q2865","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"cross-bridge","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"myosin thick head protrudes away from myosin filament & connects to, innervates with, actin thin.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"橫橋是肌球蛋白粗絲的頭部突出並結合到肌動蛋白細絲的結構，是產生收縮力的基礎。"},{"id":"q2866","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Slow-twitch fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Muscle fibers, specifically Type I fibers, with high aerobic efficiency but low maximum force output.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"慢縮肌纖維即第 I 型纖維，有氧效率高但最大輸出力量低、抗疲勞。"},{"id":"q2867","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what is the length of each side of the hexagon when setting up the hexagon test?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"24 inches","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"六角測試配置每邊長 24 英吋。"},{"id":"q2868","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Excess postexercise oxygen consumption (EPOC)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The increase in oxygen uptake following intense exercise.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動後過耗氧量（EPOC）指劇烈運動後攝氧量仍維持升高的現象。"},{"id":"q2869","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Knowledge of performance**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Feedback regarding an athlete’s movement pattern","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"表現知識（KP）是關於動作模式的回饋，告訴運動員動作做得如何。"},{"id":"q2870","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following statements is true about training to optimize muscular hypertrophy? It should be high volume with a moderate-to-low intensity load and short rest periods. It should be moderate volume with a moderate-to-low intensity load and short rest periods. It should be low volume with a high-intensity load and short rest periods. It should be low volume with a high-intensity load and long rest periods.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"It should be high volume with a moderate-to-low intensity load and short rest periods.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉肥大的訓練應為高訓練量、中低強度負荷與短組間休息。"},{"id":"q2871","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Testing Conditions","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* To maximize the reliability of tests, conditions should be as similar as possible for all athletes tested and from test to retest of the same athlete * Temperature and humidity, surface, and type of equipment should be consistent * Athletes should not be tested when fatigued, or when glycogen depleted or overly full from a meal. They should arrive for testing normally hydrated.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"測驗條件應盡量一致：溫度濕度、地面與器材固定；不在疲勞、肝糖耗盡或剛飽食時測驗，受試者應在正常水分狀態下接受測驗。"},{"id":"q2872","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does optimal functioning theory state?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"individuals will have different levels of anxiety and arousal that let them perform at their optimal abilities; there is a standardized mood state evaluation, such as state anxiety inventory, to quantify arousal state and correlate info to the physical performance of the athlete","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"個人最佳功能區域理論認為各有其最適焦慮與喚起水準，可用狀態焦慮問卷等量表量化並與表現關聯。"},{"id":"q2873","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"superficial (external)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"near the outside or surface of an object or body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"淺層（superficial/external）指靠近物體或身體表面。"},{"id":"q2874","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"which type of muscle fibers contain higher concentrations of CP?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type II, therefore individuals with higher percentages of Type II fibers may be able to replenish ATP faster through the phosphagen system","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"第 II 型纖維 CP 濃度較高，因此第 II 型比例高者經磷酸原系統再合成 ATP 可能更快。"},{"id":"q2875","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what does the i-band do during contractions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the I-band also decreases as the Z-lines are pulled toward the center of the sarcomere","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮時 Z 線被拉向肌小節中央，明帶變窄。"},{"id":"q2876","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"function of abdominal muscles during curl-up","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the abdominal muscles act concentrically during raising phase of curl-up and eccentrically during the lowering phase, even though they act isometrically in a sit-up with the trunk held straight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"仰臥起坐（curl-up）中，腹肌在起坐階段做向心收縮、放下階段做離心收縮；而在全身坐起的 sit-up 中軀幹直立階段則接近等長收縮。"},{"id":"q2877","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what happens to excess proteins consumed in the diet?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"broken down to nitrogen which is excreted as urea in urine + remaining ketoacids used for energy or converted to carbs or body fat","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"攝取過多的蛋白質會被分解，含氮部分轉為尿素自尿排出，剩餘碳骨架供能或轉為碳水化合物或體脂。"},{"id":"q2878","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"positive stress","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"eustress","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"良性壓力即 eustress，是正面的壓力。"},{"id":"q2879","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete that has a advanced training status?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4-7","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高階訓練狀態建議每週 4–7 次。"},{"id":"q2880","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"amount of air inhaled and exhaled with each breath","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"tidal volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"潮氣量（tidal volume）是每次呼吸吸入或吐出的空氣量。"},{"id":"q2881","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Synovial joints**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"joints that allow considerable movement with low friction and large ranges of motion (i.e elbow and knee). Sport and exercise movements occur mostly around the synovial joints.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"滑膜關節允許大幅度、低摩擦的運動，如肘、膝；運動動作大多發生在滑膜關節。"},{"id":"q2882","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what test has the athlete sprint 5 yards to the left, 10 yards to the right, and then 5 yards to the spot they started?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pro agility test (5-10-5)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Pro agility（5-10-5）測驗：向左衝 5 碼、向右衝 10 碼、再衝回起始點 5 碼，測驗敏捷與變向能力。"},{"id":"q2883","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Exergonic reaction**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Energy releasing reactions that are generally catabolic.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"放能反應是釋放能量的反應，通常屬分解代謝。"},{"id":"q2884","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Knowledge of results**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Feedback of information about the execution of a task or goal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"結果知識（KR）是關於任務目標達成與否的回饋。"},{"id":"q2885","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Ian is training his quadriceps muscles for muscular endurance. The strength and conditioning coach has prescribed three sets of leg presses. What is the optimum amount of time between sets to help achieve his training goal?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"30 seconds","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"訓練肌肉耐力時組間休息應盡量縮短，30 秒最能符合區域性肌耐力的訓練目標。"},{"id":"q2886","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Vertical Jump","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Wall and Chalk * Commercial Vertec Device * BEST OF 3 TRIALS is recorded to the nearest 0.5 inch","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"垂直跳測驗可用牆壁與粉筆或 Vertec 器材，記錄 3 次試跳最佳成績，精確到 0.5 英吋。"},{"id":"q2887","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does association refer to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"normally refers to connections between different states, but in sport psychology it refers to being aware of the body's physical status during competition or training; maintaining focus on the task","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"聯結（association，專注於身體感受）在運動心理指察覺身體在比賽或訓練中的生理狀態、維持對任務的專注，與分離（dissociation）相對。"},{"id":"q2888","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"deep (internal)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inside, away from surface or body","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"深層（deep/internal）指在內部、遠離身體表面。"},{"id":"q2889","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is the adenylate kinase reaction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2ADP ATP + AMP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腺苷酸激酶（myokinase）反應：2 ADP → ATP + AMP，是 ATP 再合成的輔助途徑。"},{"id":"q2890","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"where are the tubules sarcoplasmic reticulum located?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"parallel to and surrounding each myofibril, and terminates as vesicles in the vicinity of the Z-lines","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌漿網的小管平行於並環繞每條肌原纖維，在 Z 線附近終止膨大為終槽（vesicles）。"},{"id":"q2891","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"the square (second power) of a linear body dimension is related to what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle cross sectional area","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"線性尺寸的平方與橫截面積相關，因此肌肉橫截面積與力量隨橫截面積以平方關係成長。"},{"id":"q2892","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"most easily utilized form of energy","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"carbohydrates/glycogen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物／肝糖是最容易被利用的能量形式。"},{"id":"q2893","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: the more skill an athlete has developed, the better he or she can perform during states of less than or greater than optimal arousal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對。技能越嫻熟的運動員，在非最適喚起（過高或過低）下仍能維持表現的能力越強。"},{"id":"q2894","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete during the off season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4-6","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"休賽季建議每週 4–6 次訓練課。"},{"id":"q2895","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"ratio of minute ventilation to oxygen uptake","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ventilatory equivalent","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"分鐘通氣量與攝氧量之比稱為通氣當量（ventilatory equivalent）。"},{"id":"q2896","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how many total jumps are performed for the hexagon test?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"18 jumps","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"六角測試共跳 18 次（6 邊 × 3 輪）。"},{"id":"q2897","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Fast glycolysis**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Also known as anaerobic glycolysis, fast glycolysis is the process of producing ATP from glucose without the presence of oxygen, ultimately resulting in lactate formation.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快速糖解即無氧糖解：不需氧氣、由葡萄糖產生 ATP，最終生成乳酸。"},{"id":"q2898","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Long-term goals**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Overarching goal or vision of performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"長期目標是整體的表現願景或最終目標，需由中期與短期目標支撐。"},{"id":"q2899","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Have athletes perform this type of recovery between 800 meter sprints for the quickest reduction in lactic acid.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Active recovery","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"800 公尺衝刺間採用積極恢復（低強度活動）能促進血液迴圈、最快地清除乳酸。"},{"id":"q2900","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Static Vertical Jump","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* The test procedures are essentially the same as for the vertical jump, except that the countermovement is removed. * Athlete descends into a squat position (knee angle approximately 110°) and holds this position for 2 to 3 seconds before jumping vertically","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"靜態垂直跳（static vertical jump）與垂直跳程式相同，但移除 counter movement（反擺動作）：下蹲至膝約 110 度並保持 2–3 秒後再垂直跳起。"},{"id":"q2901","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does dissociation refer to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"an athlete disconnecting from the physical tasks in order to block out fatigue, discomfort and pain; leads to decreased physical performance however, in one sense due to increased anxiety about fatigue or pain or task performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"分離（dissociation）指運動員脫離身體感受以隔絕疲勞、不適與疼痛；雖可暫時撐過不適，但可能因對疲勞或任務的焦慮而降低表現。"},{"id":"q2902","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"axial","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"associated with the center of the body (head/neck/trunk = axial skeleton)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軸向（axial）指與身體中軸相關，頭、頸、軀幹構成軸骨。"},{"id":"q2903","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"why is the adenylate kinase reaction important?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because a product of the adenylate kinase (myokinase) reaction is AMP, and AMP is a powerful stimulant of glycolysis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腺苷酸激酶反應重要，因為其產物 AMP 是糖解的強力刺激劑，可加速 ATP 產出。"},{"id":"q2904","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is stored in the vesicles of the sarcoplasmic reticulum?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"calcium ions; regulation of calcium controls muscular contraction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌漿網的終槽儲存鈣離子；鈣離子的釋放與回收調控肌肉收縮與舒張。"},{"id":"q2905","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"the cube (third power) of a linear body dimension is related to what","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle mass proportional to volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"線性尺寸的立方與體積相關，肌肉質量（體積）隨尺寸的立方成長。"},{"id":"q2906","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"carbohydrates = ___ kcal/g","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"4 kcal/g","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"碳水化合物每公克提供 4 大卡熱量。"},{"id":"q2907","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: the optimal arousal point is higher for less skilled athletes than for more advanced players","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"false, LOWER","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"錯。經驗較淺的運動員最適喚起點較低，熟練者能在較高喚起下表現。"},{"id":"q2908","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete during the pre season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"3-4","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"季前建議每週 3–4 次。"},{"id":"q2909","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"areas of the respiratory passages that are not functional for gas exchange","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anatomical dead space","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"解剖無效腔（anatomical dead space）是呼吸道中不進行氣體交換的部分。"},{"id":"q2910","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Tricuspid valve**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Heart valve preventing blood flow from the right ventricle to the right atrium.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"三尖瓣位於右心房與右心室之間，防止心室收縮時血液逆流回右心房。"},{"id":"q2911","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what test has the athlete sprint forward 10m to the first set of timing lights then sprints a further 5m to the turning line where he/she is required to turn and accelerate off the line?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"505 agility test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"505 敏捷測驗：全速跑 10 公尺通過計時光電，再跑 5 公尺至轉線，180 度轉身後加速返回，測驗轉向能力。"},{"id":"q2912","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Flavine adenine dinucleotide (FADH2)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An organic molecule produced from pyruvate during aerobic glycolysis. FADH2, alongside NADH, transport hydrogen atoms to the electron transport chain to produce ATP from ADP via phosphorylation.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"FADH2（黃素腺嘌呤二核苷酸）是有氧代謝中產生的分子，與 NADH 一起把氫帶到電子傳遞鏈，經磷酸化驅動 ATP 合成。"},{"id":"q2913","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Mental imagery**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Mental visualization of a movement or experience related to competition or performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"心智影像（mental imagery）是對比賽或表現相關動作與經驗的腦中視覺化。"},{"id":"q2914","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"To increase the runner’s stride frequency during the maximum speed of sprinting, use this type of training resisted sprinting assisted sprinting inverted sprinting converged sprinting","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Assisted sprinting","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"欲提升最大衝刺時的步頻，使用輔助式衝刺（如拖曳減阻或下坡），迫使神經系統提高步頻。"},{"id":"q2915","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Reactive Strength Index","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"• Boxes of varying heights—for example, 20 cm, 30 cm, and 40 cm • A commercial device able to measure contact time—for example, a jump or contact mat (contact mat systems calculate jump height using flight time.) * Begin with the athlete standing on top of the drop box with the contact mat placed at least 0.2 m in front of the box. * Instruct the athlete to place hands on hips, to step forward off the box without stepping down or jumping up, and, upon contact with the ground, to jump as high as possible while minimizing contact time as much as possible. * From the measuring device, obtain the jump height and contact times * The BEST OF THREE TRIALS is recorded * Calculate the reactive strength index as JUMP HEIGHT DIVIDED BY CONTACT TIME","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"RSI 測驗：由 20–40 公分跳箱向前步下落地後立即盡量跳高並縮短接觸時間，記錄 3 次最佳成績，RSI＝跳躍高度÷接觸時間。"},{"id":"q2916","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is counterconditioning?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the use of somatic and cognitive responses in order to reduce an athlete's performance-related anxiety; this is achieved through systematic desensitization where an athlete visualizes a stressful competitive situation and in order to counter the stress response engages in progressive muscle relaxation; over time application of this to situations causing mild anxiety can be effective in combating anxiety","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反制約（counterconditioning）用身體與認知反應降低比賽焦慮：以系統性減敏感為主，運動員想像壓力情境同時做漸進式肌肉放鬆，反覆練習後可對抗焦慮。"},{"id":"q2917","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"appendicular","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"body's appendages (legs/arms)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"附肢（appendicular）指身體的四肢。"},{"id":"q2918","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what are the reactions of the phosphagen system controlled by?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the law of mass action / mass action effect","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸原系統的反應由質量作用定律控制：產物堆積會減緩反應，移除產物則加速反應。"},{"id":"q2919","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"where are transverse tubules in relation to the sarcoplasmic reticulum?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"perpendicular to the sarcoplasmic reticulum and terminate in the vicinity of the Z-line between two vesicles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"T 小管與肌漿網垂直，在 Z 線附近終止於兩個終槽之間。"},{"id":"q2920","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"the classic formula may favor what kind of athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"athletes of medium weight","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"經典公式（負重÷體重的 2/3 次方）可能對中等體重的運動員較有利。"},{"id":"q2921","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"single sugar molecules","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"monosaccharides","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"單糖是單一糖分子，如葡萄糖、果糖、半乳醣（galactose）。"},{"id":"q2922","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"should coaches increase or decrease the decision making responsibilities of developing athletes?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"decrease","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對發展中的年輕運動員，教練應減少由運動員自行決策的負荷，先建立基本功與結構。"},{"id":"q2923","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete when in season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1-3","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"賽季中建議每週 1–3 次，以維持強度並保留專項訓練能量。"},{"id":"q2924","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"why does the anatomic dead space increase as tidal volume increases?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"respiratory passages stretch with deep breathing","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"深呼吸時呼吸道被拉長擴張，因此解剖無效腔隨潮氣量增加而增大。"},{"id":"q2925","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**T-tubule**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Transverse tubules that run perpendicular to the sarcoplasmic reticulum and terminate in the vicinity of the Z-line between to vesicles. T-tubules run between outlying myofibrils and are contiguous with the sarcolemma at the cell surface. This results in the action potential reaching all depths of the muscle fiber nearly simultaneously.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"T 小管與肌漿網垂直、與肌膜相連續，使動作電位幾乎同時傳達肌纖維各深度，引發協調一致的收縮。"},{"id":"q2926","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"for the 505 agility test, the best time of ___ trials is recorded to the nearest 0.1 second?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"2","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"505 敏捷測驗記錄 2 次試測中的最佳時間，精確到 0.1 秒。"},{"id":"q2927","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Gluconeogenesis**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The formation of glucose from non-carbohydrate sources.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖新生（gluconeogenesis）是由非糖物質（乳酸、生糖胺基酸、甘油）合成葡萄糖。"},{"id":"q2928","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Motivation**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The intensity and direction of effort","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動機的定義：努力的強度與方向。"},{"id":"q2929","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Jake wants to begin a plyometrics training program, but his coach has advised him that in order to begin upper-body plyometric exercises, he must be able to bench press a minimum weight to be considered ready. Based on his personal information (height 6'2\", weight 190 lbs., 22 years of age), what is the minimum weight that Jake must bench press in order to be considered ready for upper-body plyometrics training? 95 lbs. 190 lbs. 285 lbs. 380 lbs.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"285 lbs","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"進行上半身超等長訓練的先決條件是臥推至少達體重等重（190 磅級），但本題官方給定答案為 285 磅，約為體重的 1.5 倍，代表較高門檻的安全標準。"},{"id":"q2930","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Margaria-Kalamen Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* The athlete sprints toward the stairs from a standing start 20 feet (6 m) from the base of the stairs and then up the staircase three steps at a time. * Power in watts is calculated as the athlete’s weight (w) in newtons times height (h) in meters from the 3RD STEP TO THE 9TH STEP divided by the measured time interval (t) in seconds P (watts) = (w × h) / t","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Margaria-Kalamen 測驗：距階梯 6 公尺起跑，每次跨 3 階全速上衝；功率＝體重（牛頓）× 第 3 階至第 9 階垂直高度（公尺）÷ 時間（秒）。"},{"id":"q2931","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does metabolic acidosis refer to?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a condition that occus when the body produces too much acid","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"代謝性酸中毒指身體產生過量酸（如氫離子與乳酸累積）導致體液偏酸的狀態。"},{"id":"q2932","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"abduct","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"movement away from body's midline","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"外展（abduct）指遠離身體正中線的動作。"},{"id":"q2933","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what does the law of mass action / mass action effect control?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the reactions of the phosphagen system","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"質量作用定律控制磷酸原系統的反應方向與速率。"},{"id":"q2934","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"why do action potentials arrive near-simultaneously from the surface to the depths of the muscle fiber?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because the T-tubules run between outlying myofibrils and are contiguous with the sarcolemma at the surface of the cell (when this happens calcium is released throughout the muscle and produces a coordinated contraction)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"因為 T 小管行經肌原纖維之間並與細胞表面的肌膜相連續，動作電位得以同時深入肌纖維各層，鈣離子全面釋放，產生協調一致的收縮。"},{"id":"q2935","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"why might favoring athletes of medium weight be unbiased anyway?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because of the bell-shaped curve describing the normal distribution of anthropometric characteristics among the population, the body weights of a majority of people are clustered close to the mean","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"經典公式偏好中等體重其實偏差有限：人群的人體測量特徵呈常態（鐘形）分佈，多數人體重集中在平均附近。"},{"id":"q2936","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"glucose, fructose, and galactose are examples of what group of carbohydrates?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"monosaccharides","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"葡萄糖、果糖與半乳醣（galactose）都屬單糖。"},{"id":"q2937","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"two things that influence the appropriate level of arousal to achieve optimal performance?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"skill level task complexity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"影響最適喚起水準的兩要素：運動員的技能水準與任務複雜度。"},{"id":"q2938","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"how many sessions per week is recommended for an athlete during the post season?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"0-3 (active rest)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"季後建議每週 0–3 次，以積極休息為主。"},{"id":"q2939","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"true or false: increasing tidal volume makes for more efficient ventilation than increasing frequency of breathing alone","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"對。加深呼吸（增大潮氣量）比單純加快呼吸頻率更有效，因為可減少無效腔通氣的佔比、提高肺泡通氣效率。"},{"id":"q2940","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Type I fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Slow-twitch fibers with high efficiency and the ability for aerobic metabolism. Type I fibers are slower to produce force and have a lower maximum force output, but are incredibly efficient.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"第一型肌纖維（Type I fiber，慢縮肌纖維）：具高效率與有氧代謝能力；收縮產生力量的速度較慢、最大張力也較低，但抗疲勞、非常有效率。"},{"id":"q2941","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"for the 505 agility test, the athlete completes the trials turning off which leg?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"preferred leg","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"505 敏捷性測試中，運動員以慣用腿（preferred leg）蹬地轉向，記錄兩次試測中最佳的一次。"},{"id":"q2942","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Glycogenolysis**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process of breaking down glycogen into glucose.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肝糖分解（Glycogenolysis）：將肝糖分解為葡萄糖的過程，以供應能量。"},{"id":"q2943","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Motive to achieve success (MAS)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The desire to challenge oneself and evaluate one’s abilities","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"追求成功動機（Motive to Achieve Success, MAS）：想要挑戰自己、評估自身能力的內在慾望，並能為成就感到自豪。"},{"id":"q2944","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The ability to perform a quick change in direction of a movement such as that observed during a movement involving the stretch-shortening cycle is called contractility effort distribution reaction time reactive ability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"reactive ability","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"反應能力（reactive ability）：快速改變動作方向的能力，常見於利用伸展縮短迴圈（stretch-shortening cycle, SSC）的動作表現。"},{"id":"q2945","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"300 Yard Shuttle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Pair off athletes of similar ability. * The athletes sprint to the line 25 yards away, then immediately sprint back to the first line. Six such round trips are made as fast as possible without stopping. * The average of two trials is recorded to the nearest 1.0 second.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"300 碼衝刺折返跑（300 Yard Shuttle）：能力相近的運動員兩人一組，衝刺 25 碼後立即折返至起始線，共完成六個來回（共 300 碼），全程不停、盡量快；記錄兩次試測平均，精確到 1.0 秒，用以評估無氧能力。"},{"id":"q2946","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what induces metabolic acidosis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"rapid decrease in blood pH due to increased H+ ions; this response can be used to determine training capacities","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"代謝性酸中毒（metabolic acidosis）：H+ 離子增加導致血液 pH 快速下降的反應；此反應可用來判斷訓練強度區間與訓練容量。"},{"id":"q2947","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"adduct","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"movement toward the body's midline","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內收（adduct）：肢體朝向身體中線移動的動作。"},{"id":"q2948","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is a consequence of the phosphagen system having enzyme-mediated reactions?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the rate of product formation is greatly influenced by the concentrations of the reactants","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"磷酸系統（phosphagen system）的反應由酵素催化，因此產物生成速率深受反應物濃度影響，這即質量作用法則（law of mass action）的表現。"},{"id":"q2949","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how do the actin filaments slide at each end?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inward on myosin filaments, pulling the Z-lines toward the center of the sarcomere and thus shortening the muscle fiber","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌動蛋白（actin）細絲由兩端向內沿肌球蛋白（myosin）粗絲滑動，把 Z 線拉向肌小節（sarcomere）中心，使肌纖維縮短。"},{"id":"q2950","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"most common sources of resistance for strength training exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"gravity, inertia, friction, fluid resistance, and elasticity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"重量訓練最常見的阻力來源：重力、慣性、摩擦力、流體阻力與彈性。"},{"id":"q2951","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"two simple sugar units joined together","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"disaccharide","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雙醣（disaccharide）：由兩個單糖（簡單糖類）單位結合而成的糖。"},{"id":"q2952","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"as an individual's arousal or state anxiety increases, so does performance (theory)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"drive theory","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"驅力理論（drive theory）：個體的覺醒或狀態焦慮越高，表現線性提升；僅適用於簡單、已熟練的動作。"},{"id":"q2953","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"max to near max loads will require _____ recovery times","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"longer","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大到接近最大強度的負荷需要較長（longer）的組間恢復時間。"},{"id":"q2954","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"alveoli with impaired gas exchange due to poor blood flow, poor ventilation, or other problems with the alveolar surface","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"physiological dead space","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"生理性無效腔（physiological dead space）：因血流不佳、通風不佳或肺泡表面問題而氣體交換受損的肺泡。"},{"id":"q2955","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"M-line","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Center of the A band & sarcomere.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"M 線（M-line）：位於 A 帶與肌小節的正中央。"},{"id":"q2956","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Type IIa fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fast-twitch fiber with more endurance than Type IIx, slightly less maximum force production, and less endurance than type I fibers.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"第二型 a 肌纖維（Type IIa fiber）：快縮肌纖維，耐力優於第二型 x 纖維，最大張力產出略低於 IIx，但耐力不如第一型纖維。"},{"id":"q2957","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what are the three central tendency measures?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"mean median mode","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"三個集中趨勢量數：平均數（mean）、中位數（median）、眾數（mode）。"},{"id":"q2958","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Motive to avoid failure (MAF)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The desire to avoid the perception of shame that accompanies failure","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"逃避失敗動機（Motive to Avoid Failure, MAF）：想避免失敗所伴隨的羞恥感，以保護自我形象與自尊。"},{"id":"q2959","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Paula has several years of experience with resistance and plyometric training. Based on her training, what is the suggested plyometric training volume? 80 to 100 100 to 120 120 to 140 140 to 200","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"120 to 140","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Paula 有多年阻力與增強式訓練經驗，屬進階訓練者，建議增強式訓練量為 120～140 次接地（contacts）。"},{"id":"q2960","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Curl Up Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"• Set a metronome to 40 beats per minute -slow, controlled curl-ups to lifting the shoulder blades off the mat in time with the metronome. The upper back must touch the floor before each curl-up. • The athlete performs as many curl-ups as possible without pausing, to a maximum of 75.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"仰臥卷腹測試（Curl Up Test）：節拍器設為每分鐘 40 拍，隨節奏緩慢、有控制地卷腹，肩胛骨抬離墊面即算一次，每次卷腹前上背須回到墊面；不中斷地做到最多 75 次為止。"},{"id":"q2961","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is lactate a byproduct of?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anaerobic glycolysis","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乳酸（lactate）是無氧糖解（anaerobic glycolysis）的副產物。"},{"id":"q2962","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the clavicle in relation to the iliac crest?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"superior to","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"以方向術語而言，鎖骨（clavicle）位於腸骨嵴（iliac crest）的上方（superior）。"},{"id":"q2963","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"as ATP is hydrolyzed to yield the energy necessary for exercise, there is a transient increase in what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ADP concentrations (as well as Pi/phosphorus) in the sarcolemma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 水解釋放運動所需能量時，肌細胞膜（sarcolemma）處的 ADP 與無機磷酸（Pi）濃度會出現暫時性上升。"},{"id":"q2964","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what happens when actin filaments slide over myosin filaments?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"both the H-zone and I-band shrink","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌動蛋白細絲沿肌球蛋白細絲滑動時，H 帶與 I 帶同時縮短，A 帶長度不變。"},{"id":"q2965","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what kind of resistance do high-acceleration (explosive) exercises provide?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"greater resistance to the muscles involved early in the range of motion and less resistance to the muscles involved toward the end of the range of motion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高加速度（爆發性）練習提供的阻力特性：動作範圍早期對相關肌肉阻力較大，越到動作範圍後期阻力越小（慣性效應所致）。"},{"id":"q2966","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"sucrose, lactose, and maltose are examples of what group of carbohydrates?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"disaccharides","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"蔗糖、乳糖、麥芽糖皆屬雙醣類（disaccharides）。"},{"id":"q2967","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"when does drive theory become unproductive or destructive?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when it is applied to complex movements","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"驅力理論用在複雜動作時會失效甚至造成破壞，因為過高的覺醒會幹擾複雜技能的執行。"},{"id":"q2968","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"heavy upper body training may require _____ recovery than heavy lower body training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"less","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"heavy 的上半身訓練所需恢復時間比 heavy 的下半身訓練較少（less），因參與肌群與整體生理需求較小。"},{"id":"q2969","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"certain types of lung disease can significantly reduce alveolar function and increase physiological dead space by as much as ___x the volume of anatomical dead space","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"10x","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"某些肺臟疾病會顯著損害肺泡功能，使生理性無效腔增加至解剖性無效腔體積的 10 倍。"},{"id":"q2970","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Type IIx fiber**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fast-twitch fibers that have the greatest ability to rapidly produce force but are the least efficient and least able to use aerobic metabolism compared to Type I and Type IIa fibers.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"第二型 x 肌纖維（Type IIx fiber）：快縮肌纖維，快速產力能力最強，但效率最差、有氧代謝能力最低（相較第一型與第二型 a 纖維）。"},{"id":"q2971","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the average of scores","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"mean","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平均數（mean）：分數的算術平均值。"},{"id":"q2972","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Glycolytic**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The system of ATP production involving the splitting of glucose to resynthesize ATP. Glycolytic processes can be aerobic or anaerobic depending on exercise intensity, which determines the ultimate destination for the end-products of glycolysis such as pyruvate.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖解系統（glycolytic）：分解葡萄糖以再合成 ATP 的系統；依運動強度可走有氧或無氧路徑，強度決定丙酮酸（pyruvate）等糖解終產物的去向。"},{"id":"q2973","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Negative punishment**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Removal of something valued as a punishment for an undesired behavior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"負性懲罰（negative punishment）：移除重視的事物作為對不良行為的懲罰，使該行為減少。"},{"id":"q2974","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"For most resistance training exercises, the athlete should be instructed to","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Exhale through the sticking point","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"多數阻力訓練動作應指示運動員在轉折點（sticking point，最費力的關卡）時吐氣。"},{"id":"q2975","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Army Push Up","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Beginning position – Knees off ground | * For the Army standard, AMRAP within a timed 2-minute period; chest to fist","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"軍式伏地挺身（Army Push Up）：起始姿勢膝離地；以軍方標準在 2 分鐘內做盡可能多次（AMRAP），胸部必須碰到拳頭。"},{"id":"q2976","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in what organs is lactate used as a fuel source?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"heart and brain","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乳酸可作為燃料被心臟與大腦利用。"},{"id":"q2977","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the talus in relation to the patella?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"talus is inferior to patella","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"距骨（talus）位於髕骨（patella）的下方（inferior）。"},{"id":"q2978","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"transient sarcolemma increases in ADP produces what effect?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increases rate of the creatine kinase and adenylate kinase reaction to replenish the ATP supply","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌細胞膜處 ADP 暫時升高會提高肌酸激酶（creatine kinase）與腺苷酸激酶（adenylate kinase）反應速率，以補充 ATP 供給。"},{"id":"q2979","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"why must rapid, repeated flexions must occur in many crossbridges throughout the entire muscle for measurable movement to occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because only a very small displacement of the actin filament occurs with each flexion of the myosin crossbridge","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"每次肌球蛋白橫橋擺動只能使肌動蛋白細絲位移極小距離，因此必須在整塊肌肉的眾多橫橋上快速、重複地擺動，才產生可測量的動作。"},{"id":"q2980","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what are the implications for weight heaviness in explosive exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because of the addition of inertia, heavier weights can be handled in accelerative exercises than in slow exercises, allowing near-maximal resistance to be attained for all muscles involved in the exercise","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"計入慣性後，加速性（爆發性）練習可以處理比慢速練習更重的重量，讓參與動作的所有肌群都獲得接近最大的阻力。"},{"id":"q2981","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"most common disaccharide","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sucrose","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最常見的雙醣是蔗糖（sucrose）。"},{"id":"q2982","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"arousal facilitates performance up to an optimal level, however further increases in arousal are associated with reduced performance (theory)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inverted U theory","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"倒 U 型理論（inverted U theory）：覺醒可促進表現至最佳點，但再持續升高反而使表現下降。"},{"id":"q2983","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"single joint exercise are _____ taxing than multi joint exercises","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"less","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"單關節動作的消耗（taxing）少於多關節動作。"},{"id":"q2984","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"the movement of oxygen and carbon dioxide across a cell membrane","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"diffusion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"擴散（diffusion）：氧氣與二氧化碳順濃度梯度跨過細胞膜的移動。"},{"id":"q2985","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Vein**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Tubes that transport blood back to the heart.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"靜脈（vein）：把血液運送回心臟的血管。"},{"id":"q2986","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the middlemost score when a set of scores is arranged in order of magnitude","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"median","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"中位數（median）：分數按大小排序後位於最中間的分數。"},{"id":"q2987","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**High-intensity interval training (HIIT)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Brief repeated bouts of high-intensity exercise followed by intermittent recovery periods.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高強度間歇訓練（HIIT）：重複進行短暫的高強度運動，其間安排間歇性的恢復時段。"},{"id":"q2988","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Negative reinforcement**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Removal of something valued as a punishment for an undesired behavior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"負性增強（negative reinforcement）：移除厭惡刺激以提高目標行為出現的頻率（注意：題目答案文字誤寫成負性懲罰的定義「移除重視的事物作為懲罰」；負性增強是拿走不舒服的刺激讓行為增加，負性懲罰才是移除喜愛事物讓行為減少）。"},{"id":"q2989","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"The correct order of the movement phases used in a power clean is beginning position, catch, first pull, scoop, second pull beginning position, first pull, catch, second pull, scoop beginning position, first pull, scoop, second pull, catch beginning position, first pull, second pull, scoop, catch beginning position, scoop, first pull, second pull, catch","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"beginning position, first pull, scoop, second pull, catch","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"power clean 動作階段的正確順序：起始位置→第一拉（first pull）→壺高（scoop）→第二拉（second pull）→接鈴（catch）。"},{"id":"q2990","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"ACSM Push Up for Females","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Beginning position – Knees on ground, legs crossed | * For the ACSM standard, as many repetitions as possible are done continuously until failure.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ACSM 女性伏地挺身：起始姿勢膝蓋著地、雙腿交叉；依 ACSM 標準連續做到力竭，計最多次數。"},{"id":"q2991","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"when does anaerobic glycolysis occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"in a state of reduced oxygen availability","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無氧糖解發生在氧氣可用性降低的狀態下。"},{"id":"q2992","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the sternum in relation to the spine?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sternum is anterior to the spine","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"胸骨（sternum）位於脊柱（spine）的前方（anterior）。"},{"id":"q2993","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"for how long will the ATP hydrolysis to increase the rate of ADP concentrations in sarcolemma continue?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the process will continue until (a) the exercise ceases or (b) the intensity is low enough that it does not deplete CP stores and it allows glycolysis or the oxidative system to become the primary supplier of ATP and rephosphorylate the free creatine","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"ATP 水解使 ADP 持續上升的過程會持續到：(a) 運動停止，或 (b) 強度低到不致耗竭磷酸肌酸（CP）存量，且糖解或有氧系統能成為 ATP 主要來源並再把遊離肌酸再磷酸化。"},{"id":"q2994","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how much calcium is present in the myofibril at rest?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"little calcium is present in the myofibril at rest, most of it is stored in the sarcoplasmic reticulum, therefore few of the myosin crossbridges are bound to actin (becomes strong when the actin binding site is exposed after release of the stored calcium)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"休息時肌原纖維內鈣離子很少，絕大多數儲存在肌漿網（sarcoplasmic reticulum），因此極少數肌球蛋白橫橋與肌動蛋白結合；儲存鈣釋放、暴露肌動蛋白結合位後才會形成強結合。"},{"id":"q2995","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how does the inertia of heavy weight affect the attainable resistance in the power clean?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the strong leg, hip, and back muscles accelerate the bar vertically to a high enough velocity that, even though the weaker upper body muscles cannot exert vertical force equal to the bar's weight, the bar continues to travel upward until the force of gravity decelerates it to zero velocity at the highest bar position","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"power clean 中，強壯的腿、臀、背肌群把桿鈴垂直加速到足夠速度；即使較弱的上半身肌群無法輸出等於桿鈴重量的垂直力，桿鈴仍會因慣性繼續上升，直到重力把它減速至最高點速度為零。"},{"id":"q2996","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"complex carbohydrates containing up to thousands of glucose units","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"polysaccharides","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"多醣類（polysaccharides）：含有高達數千個葡萄糖單位的複合碳水化合物。"},{"id":"q2997","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"athletes in different types of performances perform best with different levels of arousal (theory)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"individual zones of optimal functioning theory","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"個體最佳功能區理論（Individual Zones of Optimal Functioning, IZOF）：不同運動員在不同種類的表現專案中，最佳覺醒水準各異。"},{"id":"q2998","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"sequence of resistance exercises performed during one training session","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"exercise order","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動作順序（exercise order）：一次訓練課中所安排各阻力動作的執行順序。"},{"id":"q2999","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"diffusion results from the movement of gas from ____ concentration to ____ concentrations","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high to low","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"擴散是氣體由高濃度處向低濃度處移動的結果。"},{"id":"q3000","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"SFT; Resting Phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Resting conditions, little calcium is present in the myofibrils (stored in sarcoplasmic reticulum) very few myosin cross-bridges are bound to actin.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮-舒張過程的休息期（resting phase）：休息狀態下肌原纖維內鈣很少（儲於肌漿網），極少數肌球蛋白橫橋與肌動蛋白結合。"},{"id":"q3001","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Venule**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Small tubes that collect blood from the capillaries and converge into the larger veins.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"微靜脈（venule）：收集微血管血液並匯整合較大靜脈的小管。"},{"id":"q3002","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the score that occurs with the greatest frequency","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"mode","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"眾數（mode）：出現次數最多的分數。"},{"id":"q3003","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Observational practice**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Observing a task or skill performed by other novice, intermediate, or expert performers","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"觀察練習（observational practice）：觀看其他初學、中級或專家級示範者執行某項任務或技能。"},{"id":"q3004","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Andrea finds that her athletes’ performance on the push-up test and the YMCA bench press test is not similar, even though both tests are designed to assess muscular endurance of the upper body. These tests appear to lack this type of validity. concurrent validity construct validity content validity convergent validity","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"concurrent validity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"伏地挺身測試與 YMCA 嚥式推舉測試同為評估上半身肌耐力，結果卻不相似，代表兩者缺乏同時效度（concurrent validity）。"},{"id":"q3005","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Yo-Yo Intermittent Recovery Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Measure out a 20 m test course and arrange cones. Place markers 2 m apart at both ends of the test course at the start and turning lines. Also measure out a 5 m distance behind the start line. On an auditory signal, the athletes run forward to the turning line. At the sound of the second signal, athletes arrive at the turning line and then run back to the starting line, arriving in time with the next sound. When the start marker is passed, the athletes jog toward the 5 m mark, and then turn back to the start line. At this point the athletes stop and wait for the next sound. The athletes are required to place one foot on or over the starting or turning line at the sound of each beep. The athletes continue running for as long as they can maintain the increasing speed as indicated by the auditory signals. The termination of the test is indicated by the inability of an athlete to maintain the required pace for two trials. A warning is given the first time the start or turning line is not reached. At the end of the test, record the last level and number of 2 X 20 m intervals performed at that level on a recording sheet. The final Yo-Yo intermittent recovery speed and interval score can be used to calculate the total distance covered by the athlete during the test.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Yo-Yo 間歇恢復測試：在 20 公尺跑道兩端設起點與轉線各向外 2 公尺標記，起點後再量 5 公尺；依音訊訊號衝向轉線、再於下一訊號前回到的起點，通過後慢跑至 5 公尺標記再折回起點等候下一訊號；每次訊號響起須有一隻腳踩過起點或轉線，速度逐級提高，兩次沒跟上即結束；記錄最後等級與該級完成的 2×20 公尺次數，可換算總跑距離。"},{"id":"q3006","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what drives fast glycolysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the conversion of pyruvate into lactate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快速糖解（fast glycolysis）由丙酮酸轉化為乳酸（同時再生 NAD+）所驅動。"},{"id":"q3007","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the spine in relation to the sternum?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"spine is posterior to the sternum","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"脊柱位於胸骨後方（posterior）。"},{"id":"q3008","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"after ATP hydrolysis ends and the exercise ceases or glycolysis/oxidative can become primary supplier of ATP (and rephosphorylate the free creatine), what occurs?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the sarcoplasmic concentration of ATP will remain steady or increase, which will slow down or reverse the directions of the creatine kinase and adenylate kinase reactions. as a result, these reactions/equations are often referred to as near-equilibrium reactions that proceed in a direction dictated by the concentrations of the reactants due to the law of mass action","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動停止或有氧/糖解系統接手供應 ATP 後，肌漿內 ATP 濃度會維持穩定或上升，使肌酸激酶與腺苷酸激酶反應放慢甚至逆向；這類反應稱接近平衡反應，依質量作用法則由反應物濃度決定進行方向。"},{"id":"q3009","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"in the excitation-contraction coupling phase, what must happen before myosin crossbridges can flex?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"they must first attach to the actin filament","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"在興奮-收縮偶聯（excitation-contraction coupling）階段，肌球蛋白橫橋必須先附著到肌動蛋白細絲上，才能進行擺動（power stroke）。"},{"id":"q3010","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how do cam machines with variable radii work?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"changes the length of the moment arm through which the weight stack acts, thereby providing more resistance at points in the range of motion where the muscles could exert greater torque, and less resistance where the muscles could apply less torque","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"可變半徑的凸輪（cam）機器改變配重片力臂（moment arm）長度：在肌肉能輸出較大扭力的關節角度提供較大阻力，在扭力較小處提供較小阻力。"},{"id":"q3011","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"starch, fiber, and glycogen are examples of what group of carbohydrates?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"polysaccharides","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"澱粉、膳食纖維與肝糖皆屬多醣類（polysaccharides）。"},{"id":"q3012","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: any specific emotion can be positively perceived by one athlete but negatively perceived by another","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確：同一種情緒，一名運動員可能正向解讀，另一名卻負向解讀，情緒效應因人而異。"},{"id":"q3013","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is the most common exercise order?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"power > core lifts > assistance lifts","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最常見的動作順序：power（爆發力）動作 → 核心動作（core lifts）→ 輔助動作（assistance lifts）。"},{"id":"q3014","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"2 ways that oxygen is carried in blood","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"transported by hemoglobin dissolved in plasma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"氧氣在血液中有兩種運輸形式：與血紅素（hemoglobin）結合運輸，以及溶解於血漿中運輸。"},{"id":"q3015","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"SFT; Excitation-contraction coupling phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Before myosin cross-bridges can flex, they must first attach to the actin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"興奮-收縮偶聯（excitation-contraction coupling）階段：肌球蛋白橫橋必須先附著肌動蛋白細絲才能擺動。"},{"id":"q3016","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"**Vertebral column**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vertebral bones separated by flexible disks that allow movement to occur. Vertebrae are grouped in the following: Seven cervical vertebrae (C1-C7), the twelve thoracic vertebrae (T1-T12), five lumbar vertebrae (L1-L5), five sacral vertebrae, which are fused together and make up the pelvis, and the three to five coccygeal vertebrae, which form a vestigial internal tail extending downward front the pelvis.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 1 - The Structure and Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"脊柱（vertebral column）：椎骨之間由具彈性之椎間盤隔開以容許動作；計頸椎 7 節（C1-C7）、胸椎 12 節（T1-T12）、腰椎 5 節（L1-L5）、癒合的薦椎 5 節組成骨盆一部分，以及 3～5 節尾椎（退化尾骨，由骨盆向下延伸）。"},{"id":"q3017","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what are the two measures of variability?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"range and standard deviation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"兩個變異量（variability）指標：全距（range）與標準差（standard deviation）。"},{"id":"q3018","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Inorganic phosphate**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Pi, a phosphate molecule not bound to an organic compound. Inorganic phosphate is one of the products of ATP hydrolysis.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無機磷酸（inorganic phosphate, Pi）：未與有機化合物結合的磷酸分子，為 ATP 水解的產物之一。"},{"id":"q3019","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Operant**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The targeted or desired behavior of positive reinforcement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"操縱行為（operant）：正增強所要建立、鎖定的目標（期望）行為。"},{"id":"q3020","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Barbara read a research article that reported the Jackson & Pollock skinfold equation provided body composition estimates that were consistent with results from underwater weighing, a method considered the \"gold standard\" for body composition analysis. What type of validity does the Jackson-Pollock equation have based on this study?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"convergent validity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Jackson-Pollock 皮褶厚度方程式推估的體成分與被視為黃金標準的水中稱重法結果一致，此研究支援該方程式具有聚合效度（convergent validity）。"},{"id":"q3021","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"T-Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Layout: A to B (10 Yds) * C is 5 Yds to the left of B * D is 5 Yds to the right of B The test begins with the athlete standing at point A. The athlete: - Sprints to point B and touches the base of the cone with the right hand. - Shuffles left and touches the base of cone C with the left hand. - Shuffles right and touches the base of cone D with the right hand. - Shuffles left and touches the base of cone B with the left hand. - Runs backward past point A.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"T 測試（T-Test）：A 至 B 為 10 碼，C、D 各在 B 左、右 5 碼；起跑於 A，衝刺至 B 用右手觸錐，左側滑步觸 C（左手），右側滑步觸 D（右手），再左側滑步觸 B（左手），最後倒退跑通過 A；評估直線衝刺、側滑與倒退變向能力。"},{"id":"q3022","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does reaching lactate threshold imply for muscular contraction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"slowing of muscular contractions (possibly until cessation of movement) until lactate can be cleared and homeostasis restored","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"抵達乳酸閾值對肌肉收縮的意義：肌肉收縮變慢（甚至可能停頓），直到乳酸被清除、體內恆定恢復為止。"},{"id":"q3023","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is nose in relation to the ears?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"nose is medial to the ears","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"鼻子位於雙耳的內側（medial）。"},{"id":"q3024","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"why is the ATP resynthesis rate during glycolysis is not as rapid as with the single-step phosphagen system?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because the process of glycolysis involves multiple enzymatically catalyzed reactions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖解過程中 ATP 再合成速率不如磷酸系統快，因為糖解涉及一連串多步驟的酵素催化反應，而磷酸系統只有單一步驟。"},{"id":"q3025","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"how does troponin affect the sarcoplasmic reticulum?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when the sarcoplasmic reticulum is stimulated to release calcium ions, the calcium binds with troponin, a protein that is situated at regular intervals along the actin filament and has a high affinity for calcium ions","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌漿網受刺激釋放鈣離子後，鈣與肌鈣蛋白（troponin）結合；肌鈣蛋白位在海螺旋狀肌動蛋白細絲的固定間隔處，對鈣離子有高親和力。"},{"id":"q3026","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"pitfall of cam-based machines?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"athlete has to move at a constant, slow angular velocity, which is difficult to do consistently, and cam-based machines frequently fail to match normal human torque capability patterns","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"凸輪（cam）機器的缺點：運動員必須以固定、緩慢的角速度動作且難以穩定維持，且凸輪常無法完全吻合人體正常的扭力輸出曲線。"},{"id":"q3027","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are some important functions of fiber?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"increase bulk and water content delay gastric emptying influence feelings of fullness decrease transit time of feces","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膳食纖維的重要功能：增加糞便體積與含水量、延緩胃部排空、影響飽足感、縮短糞便通過腸道的時間。"},{"id":"q3028","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"increases in physiological arousal occur in the presence of cognitive anxiety and a sudden drop in performance occurs, rather than gradual decline (theory)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"catastrophe theory","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"災難理論（catastrophe theory）：在認知焦慮存在下生理覺醒升高時，表現會突然大幅下降，而非緩慢下滑。"},{"id":"q3029","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is circuit training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"performing the exercises with minimal rest periods","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"迴圈訓練（circuit training）：以最少休息時間連續完成各個動作。"},{"id":"q3030","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"70% of carbon dioxide removal occurs through the process of carbon dioxide being delivered to the lungs in the form of _______?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"bicarbonate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"約 70% 的二氧化碳以碳酸氫根（bicarbonate）形式運送至肺部排出。"},{"id":"q3031","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the interval from the lowest to the highest score","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"range","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"全距（range）：最低分到最高分之間的區間。"},{"id":"q3032","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Krebs cycle**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process that occurs when pyruvate enters the mitochondria following glycolysis. The Krebs cycle is a crucial process during oxidative phosphorylation.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"克雷布斯迴圈（Krebs cycle，三羧酸迴圈）：糖解後丙酮酸進入粒線體所進行的一連串反應，是氧化磷酸化的關鍵過程。"},{"id":"q3033","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Part practice**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Separating a skill into a series of subcomponents practice individually","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"部分練習（part practice）：把技能拆成一系列子成分，分別單獨練習。"},{"id":"q3034","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Of the options listed below, which test would be most appropriate to use to test the general strength necessary for a football offensive lineman? the 1 RM leg extension the 1.5-mile run the 1RM bench press skinfold measures","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 RM bench","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"美式足球進攻線球員需要上半身整體最大肌力，最適宜的測驗是 1RM 嚥式推舉（1.5 英里跑測耐力、皮褶測體成分、腿伸機較不具專項參考性）。"},{"id":"q3035","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Hexagon Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The athlete double-leg hops from the center of the hexagon over each side and back to the center. Starting with the side directly in front of the athlete, in a continuous clockwise sequence until all six sides are covered three times (for a total of 18 jumps). LENGTH OF SIDE IS 24 INCHES","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"六角形測試（Hexagon Test）：雙腳跳由六角形中心跳過每一邊再跳回中心，從正前方邊開始順時針連續繞行，六邊各跳 3 輪共 18 跳，每邊長 24 吋；評估敏捷性與連續跳躍爆發力。"},{"id":"q3036","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is required for aerobic glycolysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pyruvate to enter mitochondria, then when oxygen is present the pyruvate is oxidized and enters into the krebs cycle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧糖解的條件：丙酮酸必須進入粒線體，在有氧情況下被氧化並進入克雷斯迴圈（Krebs cycle）。"},{"id":"q3037","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where are the ears in relation to the nose?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"ears are lateral to nose","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雙耳位於鼻子的外側（lateral）。"},{"id":"q3038","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"why is the capacity to produce ATP higher in the glycolytic system than in CP?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"due to a larger supply of glycogen and glucose compared to phosphagenic","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖解系統產生 ATP 的總容量比磷酸肌酸（CP）系統高，因為肝糖與葡萄糖的儲存量遠大於磷酸肌酸存量。"},{"id":"q3039","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"where is tropomyosin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"runs along the length of the actin filament in the groove of the double helix","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"原肌球蛋白（tropomyosin）沿著肌動蛋白細絲長度方向，行於雙螺旋的溝槽中。"},{"id":"q3040","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what are the implications for agonist muscles in the acceleration patterns of exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the agonist muscles receive resistance in excess of bar weight early in the range of motion, but resistance less than bar weight toward the end of the range of motion","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"爆發性動作的加速度特性對主動肌（agonist）的影響：動作範圍早期主動肌承受超過桿鈴重量的阻力，動作範圍後期承受低於桿鈴重量的阻力。"},{"id":"q3041","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how much glycogen is stored in the body?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"15g/kgbw","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"依本卡答案：體內肝糖儲存量約為每公斤體重 15 公克（以成人計約數百公克）。"},{"id":"q3042","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"the athlete's interpretation of arousal and anxiety affect performance, and he or she has the ability to reverse this interpretation (theory)","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"reversal theory","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"翻轉理論（reversal theory）：運動員對覺醒與焦慮的主觀解讀會影響表現，且運動員有能力反轉這種解讀。"},{"id":"q3043","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"with exercise order, why do power lifts need to be performed first?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"power lifts require the highest level of skill/concentration and most affected by fatigue","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"爆發力（power）動作必須最先做，因為它們對技術與專注的要求最高，也最容易受疲勞影響。"},{"id":"q3044","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"why does lactate not accumulate during low to moderate intensity exercise?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sufficient oxygen is available to the working muscles and lactate is removed through the cori cycle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"低到中強度運動時乳酸不堆積，因為工作肌肉氧氣足夠，乳酸透過 Cori 迴圈被持續移走處理。"},{"id":"q3045","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"a measure of the variability of a set of scores about the mean","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"standard deviation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"標準差（standard deviation）：衡量一組分數圍繞平均數變異程度的指標。"},{"id":"q3046","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Physiological efficiency**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Employing only the amount of physical and mental energy to accomplish the task at hand","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"生理效率（physiological efficiency）：只付出完成當前任務所需的體力與心智慧量，不浪費多餘消耗。"},{"id":"q3047","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which of the following tests will provide the most pertinent information about an athlete who is trying out as a spiker on the volleyball team? the 1RM back squat the 1RM bench press the line drill the vertical jump","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Vertical jump","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"排球隊伍攻擊手（spiker）選拔試鏡中最相關的測驗是垂直跳（vertical jump），直接反映攻擊所需的下肢爆發力。"},{"id":"q3048","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Pro Agility Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The athlete sprints 5 yards to the left, Then changes direction and sprints 10 yards to the right Then again changes direction and sprints 5 yards to the spot where they started.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"職業敏捷測試（Pro Agility Test，5-10-5）：先向左衝 5 碼，變向後向右衝 10 碼，再變向衝 5 碼回到起始點。"},{"id":"q3049","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what governs the differentiation between the two types of glycolysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"what takes place in the mitochondrion -- if oxygen is present, aerobic glycolysis will take place through oxidative phosphorylation, but if oxygen isn't available the pyruvate will undergo fermentation to produce sufficient ATP","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"決定糖解走有氧或無氧的關鍵是粒線體內的情況：有氧時丙酮酸經氧化磷酸化處理（有氧糖解）；缺氧時丙酮酸進行發酵生成乳酸以產出足夠 ATP。"},{"id":"q3050","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the body's bilateral structures?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"legs, eyes, lungs","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"身體的雙側（bilateral）構造是左右成對的部位，例如腿、眼睛、肺髒。"},{"id":"q3051","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is the end result of glycolysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pyruvate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"糖解的最終產物是丙酮酸（pyruvate）。"},{"id":"q3052","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what occurs when calcium binds with troponin?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"myosin crossbridge now attaches much more rapidly to the actin filament, allowing force to be produced as the actin filaments are pulled toward the center of the sarcomere","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"鈣與肌鈣蛋白結合後，肌球蛋白橫橋能更快地附著到肌動蛋白細絲，把肌動蛋白拉向肌小節中心而產生力量。"},{"id":"q3053","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"biomechanically, how do athletes decelerate a bar?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"by either (a) reducing upward force on the bar to less than bar weight to let some or all of the bar's weight decelerate it or (b) pushing down against the bar using the antagonist muscles. In either case, the deceleration has the effect of providing less resistance to the agonist muscles late in the range of motion.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"生物力學上運動員減速桿鈴的方式：(a) 把對桿的向上力降到小於桿重，讓桿的重量自行減速；或 (b) 用拮抗肌向下壓桿。兩種做法都會使動作範圍後期主動肌承受的阻力變小。"},{"id":"q3054","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"glycogen storage % in the muscles vs liver","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"75% skeletal muscle 25% liver","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肝糖儲存分佈：約 75% 在骨胳肌、約 25% 在肝髒。"},{"id":"q3055","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"motivation that comes from within the athlete regardless of reward/punishment","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"intrinsic motivation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"內在動機（intrinsic motivation）：來自運動員內部的動力，與外在獎勵或懲罰無關。"},{"id":"q3056","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what are two ways to \"alternate\" exercise order?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"upper body/lower body push/pull","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"交錯安排動作順序的兩種方式：上半身/下半身交錯、推（push）/拉（pull）動作交錯。"},{"id":"q3057","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"cycle where muscle derived lactate is transported via the blood to the liver where it undergoes gluconeogenesis","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cori cycle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Cori 迴圈：肌肉產生的乳酸經血液運送到肝髒，在肝髒經糖新生（gluconeogenesis）轉換回葡萄糖。"},{"id":"q3058","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"SFT; contraction phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when calcium binds to troponin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮期（contraction phase）始於鈣與肌鈣蛋白結合的時刻。"},{"id":"q3059","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the percentage of test takers scoring below an individual","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"percentile rank","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"百分位數（percentile rank）：得分低於某人的受試者所佔百分比。"},{"id":"q3060","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Lactate threshold (LT)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The exercise intensity at which blood lactate begins an abrupt increase above the baseline concentration. The LT begins at approximately 50%-60% of maximal oxygen uptake in untrained individuals and at 70-80% in aerobically trained athletes.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乳酸閾值（lactate threshold, LT）：運動強度達到血液乳酸濃度開始偏離基線急遽上升的點；未受訓者約出現在最大攝氧量（VO2max）的 50%～60%，有氧受訓運動員約在 70%～80%。"},{"id":"q3061","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Positive punishment**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Presentation of an act/object that could decrease an undesired behavior’s occurrence - i.e. pushups after practice do to poor performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正性懲罰（positive punishment）：呈現令人不快的行為或事物以降低不良行為出現率，例如因表現不佳而練習後加做伏地挺身。"},{"id":"q3062","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Which description best fits a test of anaerobic capacity? The movement is at low speed but requires one maximum exertion by the muscle. The movement is fast and requires maximum effort for about 1 second. The movement requires maximal effort for a duration of between 30 and 90 seconds. None of the above.","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The movement requires maximal effort for a duration of between 30 and 90 seconds.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"無氧容量的測驗特徵：動作需維持最大努力約 30～90 秒（此時間域主要由糖解系統供能，能反映無氧容量）。"},{"id":"q3063","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"505 Agility Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* On an auditory signal, the athlete sprints forward 10 m to the first set of timing lights, then sprints a further 5 m to the turning line (one foot must be on or over the line), where he or she is required to turn and accelerate off the line. * The athlete may slow down only after passing through the timing lights for the second time. * THE BEST TIME OF TWO TRIALS is recorded to the nearest 0.1 second. * The athlete completes the trials turning off the preferred leg.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"505 敏捷測試：訊號響起後向前衝刺 10 碼通過第一個計時光電，再衝 5 碼至轉線（一腳須踩過線）蹬地轉向加速跑回，第二次通過光電後才可減速；記錄兩次試測最佳成績，精確到 0.1 秒，以慣用腿蹬地轉向。"},{"id":"q3064","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is an action potential?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"an electrical impulse that is triggered by the rapid depolarization of the cell membrane of a neuron","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動作電位（action potential）：神經元細胞膜快速去極化所觸發的電訊號。"},{"id":"q3065","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the body's isolateral structures?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"hands and feet","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"同側（ipsilateral）構造：指身體同一側的部位配對，例如同側的手與腳。"},{"id":"q3066","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what are the two ways pyruvate may proceed?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1. Pyruvate can be converted to lactate in the sarcoplasm. 2. Pyruvate can be shuttled into the mitochondria.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸的兩種去向：1. 在肌漿中被轉換成乳酸；2. 被送入粒線體進行氧化。"},{"id":"q3067","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is the amount of force produced by a muscle at any instant contingent on?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the number of myosin crossbridges bound to actin filaments cross-sectionally at that instant in time (to reiterate: the number of crossbridges that are formed between actin and myosin at any instant in time dictates the force production of a muscle.)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉在任一瞬間產生的力量取決於該瞬間橫斷面上肌球蛋白橫橋與肌動蛋白細絲結合的數量；橫橋結合數決定產力量。"},{"id":"q3068","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what are some examples of acceleration and deceleration in sport exercises?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sprinting requires the athlete's arms and legs to go through repeated cycles of acceleration and deceleration; throwing a baseball, discus, shot, or javelin all involve sequences of body movements that accelerate the objects to high release speeds","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"專項動作中加速與減速的例子：跑步需要四肢反覆進行加速與減速迴圈；擲棒球、鉄餅、鉛球、標槍都包含一連串把器械加速到高出手速度的身體動作。"},{"id":"q3069","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"the remaining glycogen that is not stored in the skeletal muscle is stored where?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"liver","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"骨骼肌以外的肝糖儲存在肝髒。"},{"id":"q3070","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"motivation that comes from an external source as opposed to internal","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"extrinsic motivation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"外在動機（extrinsic motivation）：來自外部源頭的動力（獎勵、稱讚等），相對於內在動力。"},{"id":"q3071","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"two exercises performed in an alternating fashion that stresses opposing muscles or muscle areas","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"superset","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"超級組（superset）：交錯執行兩個刺激相反肌群或不同肌區的動作。"},{"id":"q3072","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"what occurs when aerobic metabolism is not sufficient to keep up with the formation of lactic acid during higher work intensities and levels begin to rise in the blood?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"OBLA","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"較高工作強度下有氧代謝跟不上乳酸生成、血液乳酸濃度開始上升的現象稱為 OBLA（blood lactate accumulation onset，血乳酸堆積點）。"},{"id":"q3073","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"power stroke","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The energy of pulling action hydrolysis (breakdown) of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to Adenosine diphosphate (ADP) & phosphate (P), catalyzed by enzyme myosin adenosine triphosphate (ATPase).","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動程（power stroke）：橫橋拉動作用所釋放的能量來自 ATP 水解為 ADP 與磷酸，由肌球蛋白三磷酸腺苷三磷酸酶（myosin ATPase）催化。"},{"id":"q3074","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"type of statistics that allows one to draw general conclusions about a population from information collected in a population sample that must be representative","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inferential statistics","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"推論統計（inferential statistics）：可從未自母體抽出之具代表性樣本所得資訊，對母體下一般性結論。"},{"id":"q3075","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Lactic acid**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The acid form of lactate. Often thought to be the product of anaerobic glycolysis, lactic acid is not an end result of anaerobic glycolysis nor is it the cause of rising cytosolic pH associated with fatigue.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乳酸（lactic acid）：lactate 的酸形式；常被誤認為無氧糖解的終產物及胞內 pH 下降與疲勞的原因，兩者皆不正確。"},{"id":"q3076","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Positive reinforcement**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The act of increasing the probability of occurrence of a given targeted behavior by rewarding the behavior","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正性增強（positive reinforcement）：以獎勵提高某目標行為出現的機率。"},{"id":"q3077","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Bundles of Muscle Fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Fasciculi","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌束（fasciculi）：肌纖維的成束集合。"},{"id":"q3078","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Balance Error Scoring System","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"- double-leg stance with feet together - single-leg stance on the non-dominant foot with contralateral leg in approximately 90° of flexion - tandem stance with the dominant foot in front of the non-dominant foot (95). The test is conducted on a firm surface and on a soft surface. * The stances are held for 20 seconds with eyes closed for each condition and hands on hips. * Athletes are told to keep as steady as possible, and if they lose balance, they attempt to regain their initial position as quickly as possible. * Errors include opening eyes; lifting hands from hips; touchdown of non-stance foot; step, hop, or other movement of the stance foot or feet; lifting forefeet or heel; moving hip into more than 30° of hip flexion or abduction; or remaining out of position for more than 5 seconds. * The error scores from the BESS test are summed into a single score.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"平衡錯誤計分系統（BESS）：三種姿勢——雙腳併攏雙腳站、非慣用腳單腳站且對側腳約屈髖 90 度、慣用腳在前的前後腳直線站；分別在硬麵與軟面上雙眼閉合、手叉腰維持 20 秒；錯誤包括睜眼、手離開腰、非支撐腳觸地、支撐腳跨步或跳動、前腳掌或腳跟抬起、髖屈曲或外展超過 30 度、偏離姿勢超過 5 秒等；錯誤分數加總為單一總分，評估平衡功能（常與腦震盪評估相關）。"},{"id":"q3079","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the four segments of sarcomere?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A-band, H-zone, I-band, and Z-line","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌小節（sarcomere）的四個區段：A 帶、H 帶、I 帶與 Z 線。"},{"id":"q3080","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is an example of contralateral action?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a stroke on the right side of the brain may affect the function of the left arm","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"右側腦中風可能影響左臂功能，這是對側（contralateral）控制的例子。"},{"id":"q3081","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"how does ATP resynthesis occur at a faster rate when pyruvate is converted into lactate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"via the rapid regeneration of NAD+","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸轉化為乳酸能快速再生 NAD+，使糖解得以較高速率繼續再合成 ATP。"},{"id":"q3082","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"in the contraction phase of the excitation-contraction coupling phase, where does the energy for the power stroke come from?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"from hydrolysis (breakdown) of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to adenosine diphosphate (ADP) and phosphate, a reaction catalyzed by the enzyme myosin adenosine triphosphatase (ATPase)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"收縮期中，power stroke 的能量來自 ATP 水解為 ADP 與磷酸，此反應由肌球蛋白三磷酸腺苷三磷酸酶（myosin ATPase）催化。"},{"id":"q3083","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"how does the force-velocity relationship of muscle affect a shot-putter who trains with an extra-heavy shot?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"develops greater forces during the accelerative movement than when using the normal shot because the inertia of the heavier implement forces the muscle to contract at relatively low speed, then when a relatively light shot is used, the lower inertia of the shot enables the putter to accelerate the shot more rapidly and to reach a higher speed of release","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"力量-速度關係的應用：用超重鉛球訓練時，較重器械的慣性迫使肌肉以較低速度收縮而產生較大力道；改用較輕的球時慣性較低，能以更快加速把球推出、得到更高出手速度。"},{"id":"q3084","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"system that ranks foods based on how easily carbohydrates are absorbed, resulting in an increase in blood glucose levels","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glycemic index (GI)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"升糖指數（glycemic index, GI）：依碳水化合物食物被吸收後升高血糖的程度與速度為食物分級的系統。"},{"id":"q3085","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"intensity and direction of effort","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"motivation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"動機（motivation）即努力的強度與方向（intensity and direction of effort）。"},{"id":"q3086","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"sequentially performing two different exercises for the same muscle group","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"compound set","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"組集訓練（compound set）：依序連續做兩個針對同一肌群的動作。"},{"id":"q3087","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"increasing maximal _______ uptake is very important for optimal aerobic exercise performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"oxygen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"提升最大攝氧量（oxygen uptake, VO2max）對最佳有氧運動表現非常重要。"},{"id":"q3088","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"SFT; Recharge phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"measurable muscle shortening transpires only when this sequence of events binding of calcium to troponin, coupling of the myosin, cross-bridge with actin, power stroke, dissociation of actin & myosin, & resetting of the myosin head position. Repeated over & over again.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"再充電期（recharge phase）：只有鈣與肌鈣蛋白結合→橫橋與肌動蛋白結合→power stroke→肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白分離→肌球蛋白頭復位，這一連串事件在肌纖維內不斷重複，才會發生可測量的肌肉縮短。"},{"id":"q3089","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"type of statistics that provides a more useful approach for practitioners because it allows for interpretation of the clinical significance of fitness testing","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"magnitude statistics","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"量大統計（magnitude statistics）：對實務工作者更有用的途徑，可據以解讀體適能測驗結果的實務（臨床）重要性。"},{"id":"q3090","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Law of mass action**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Also known as the mass action effect, this principle states that the concentration of the reactants or products in solution will drive the direction of the reactions. In enzyme-mediated reactions such as those of the phosphagen system, the rate of product formation is greatly influenced by the concentrations of reactants.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"質量作用法則（law of mass action）：溶液中反應物或產物的濃度會驅動反應進行方向；磷酸系統等酵素催化反應的產物生成速率深受反應物濃度影響。"},{"id":"q3091","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Progressive muscle relaxation (PMR)**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Self-regulation of physical and psychological arousal through control of skeletal muscle tension","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"漸進式肌肉放鬆（progressive muscle relaxation, PMR）：透過控制骨胳肌張力來自我調節生理與心理覺醒。"},{"id":"q3092","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"outer most layer of connective tissue that encloses the entire muscle","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Epimysium","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌外膜（epimysium）：包圍整塊肌肉最外層的結締組織。"},{"id":"q3093","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Star Excursion Balance Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* The athlete stands in the center of a grid with eight lines (120 cm) extending out at 45° increments * The athlete maintains a single-leg stance facing in one direction while reaching with the contralateral leg as far as possible for each taped line, touching the farthest point possible and then returning to the bilateral position. WITHIN A SINGLE TRIAL, THE ATHLETE REMAINS FACING IN THE BEGINNING DIRECTION AND THE STANCE LEG REMAINS THE SAME, with the other leg doing all of the reaching. * The distance from the center of the star to the touch position is measured. • The starting direction and support leg are chosen randomly. Three trials are performed for each condition and averaged. • Trials are discarded if the athlete does not touch the line, lifts stance foot from the center grid, loses balance, or does not maintain start and return positions for 1 full second.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"星形動態平衡測試（Star Excursion Balance Test）：於中心點單腳站立，地面有八條相隔 45 度、長 120 公分的指示線；用對側腳各方向盡力伸觸最遠點後回到雙腳站位；單次試測中面向與支撐腳固定，隨機決定起始方向與支撐腳，每條件 3 次取平均；未觸線、支撐腳離地、失去平衡或未維持起終點姿勢 1 秒之試測作廢。"},{"id":"q3094","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what does the A-band contain?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"actin and myosin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"A 帶同時含有肌動蛋白（actin）細絲與肌球蛋白（myosin）粗絲（重疊區）。"},{"id":"q3095","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"a stroke on the left side of the brain may affect the movement of the right leg -- this is an example of what?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"contralateral effect","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"左腦中風可能影響右腳活動，是對側效應（contralateral effect）的例子。"},{"id":"q3096","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is a limitation of the ATP resynthesis (during pyruvate-->lactate) due to rapid regeneration of NAD+?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"limited in duration due to the subsequent H+ production and resulting decrease in cytosolic pH; this process is sometimes called anaerobic glycolysis (or fast glycolysis)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"靠快速再生 NAD+ 加速 ATP 再合成（丙酮酸→乳酸，即無氧/快速糖解）的缺點是持續時間有限，因為隨後產生的 H+ 會使胞漿 pH 下降。"},{"id":"q3097","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what must occur for the head to detach from the active actin site and return to its original position?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"another molecule of ATP must replace the ADP on the myosin crossbridge globular head; this allows the contraction process to continue (if calcium is available to bind to troponin) or relaxation to occur (if calcium is not available)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"必須有新的 ATP 分子取代肌球蛋白橫橋球狀頭上的 ADP，橫橋才能從肌動蛋白上脫離並回到原位；若仍有鈣可與肌鈣蛋白結合，收縮繼續；若無鈣，則進入舒張。"},{"id":"q3098","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"downsides of changing the implement loading to a heavy one in throwing or sprinting?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the body needs time to adjust the motor pattern for that particular movement with the new load","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"把擲類或跑步訓練器械改成較重負荷的缺點：身體需要時間重新調整該動作的動作模式（motor pattern）以適應新負荷。"},{"id":"q3099","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"reference food for glycemic index","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glucose (GI = 100)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"升糖指數的參考食物是葡萄糖（定義 GI = 100）。"},{"id":"q3100","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: athletes are rarely completely intrinsically or extrinsically motivation but rather move along a motivation continuum","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確：運動員極少是完全的內在動機或完全的外在動機，多數在動機光譜（continuum）上移動。"},{"id":"q3101","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"compound sets are generally performed for what training goal?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle hypertrophy/fatigue","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"compound set（同肌群連續兩動作）通常以肌肉肥大/製造疲勞為訓練目標。"},{"id":"q3102","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"normal discharge rate of SA node","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"60 to 80 times per minute","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"竇房結（SA node）的正常放電速率為每分鐘 60～80 次。"},{"id":"q3103","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"SFT; Relaxation phase","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Occurs when the stimulation of a motor nerve stops. Calcium is pumped back into the sarcoplasmic reticulum, prevents binding between actin & myosin filaments","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舒張期（relaxation phase）：運動神經刺激停止時發生；鈣被泵回肌漿網，肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白無法結合。"},{"id":"q3104","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"refers to the ability of a test to detect the smallest practically important change in performance","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"smallest worthwhile change","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最小有價值變化（smallest worthwhile change）：測驗能偵測出表現上最小且具實務重要性的變化的能力。"},{"id":"q3105","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Mass action effect**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Also known as the law of mass action, this principle states that the concentration of the reactants or products in solution will drive the direction of the reactions. In enzyme-mediated reactions such as those of the phosphagen system, the rate of product formation is greatly influenced by the concentrations of reactants.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"質量作用效應（mass action effect）：即質量作用法則，反應物或產物濃度決定反應方向；磷酸系統反應的產物生成速率深受反應物濃度影響。"},{"id":"q3106","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Progressive-part training**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Practicing two skill subcomponents individually before combining them then practices the third component and adding it to the first two until the whole skill is mastered","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"漸進式分部訓練（progressive-part training）：先分別練習兩個技能子成分再合併，然後加入第三個子成分與前兩段串接，如此直到熟練整個技能。"},{"id":"q3107","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Tissue covering the outside of fiber bundles","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"perimysium","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌束膜（perimysium）：包圍肌纖維束（fiber bundles）外面的結締組織。"},{"id":"q3108","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Sit and Reach Test","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* Tape yardstick or tape measure to floor * Place a piece of tape about 24 inches long across the yardstick at a right angle to it at the 15 inch mark. * Shoeless athlete sits with yardstick between legs, zero end toward the body, feet 12 inches apart, toes pointed up, heels touching edge of taped line at 15 inch mark. * Athlete slowly reaches forward as with both hands as far as possible on the yardstick, hold position momentarily, ATHLETE SHOULD EXHALE AND DROP HEAD BETWEEN ARMS WHEN REACHING * RECORD BEST OF 3 TRIALS TO THE NEAREST 0.25 INCH","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"坐體前屈測試（Sit and Reach Test）：將量尺貼於地面，在 15 吋處垂直貼一條約 24 吋長的膠帶；赤足坐於量尺兩腿間，零端朝向身體，雙腳間隔 12 吋、腳尖朝上，腳跟貼住 15 吋標線；雙手盡可能緩慢前伸並短暫停留，前伸時應吐氣、低頭於雙臂間；記錄 3 次最佳，精確到 0.25 吋。"},{"id":"q3109","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"where is the H-zone and what does it contain?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"center of sarcomere, contains only myosin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"H 帶位於肌小節中央，只含肌球蛋白（myosin）粗絲。"},{"id":"q3110","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the knee relative to the hip?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"intermediate","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膝蓋相對於髖關節為中間（intermediate）位置。"},{"id":"q3111","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what process is aerobic or slow glycolysis?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when pyruvate is shuttled into the mitochondria to undergo the Krebs cycle, the ATP resynthesis rate is slower because of the numerous reactions, but can occur for a longer duration if the exercise intensity is low enough.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"有氧（慢速）糖解：丙酮酸被送入粒線體進行克雷布斯迴圈時，因反應步驟多，ATP 再合成速率較慢；若運動強度足夠低，可維持較長時間。"},{"id":"q3112","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what other events in skeletal muscle besides contraction does calcium regulate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glycolytic and oxidative energy metabolism, as well as protein synthesis and degradation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"鈣離子在骨胳肌中除了觸發收縮，還調控糖解與有氧能量代謝，以及蛋白質的合成與分解。"},{"id":"q3113","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"exercises using friction as the main source of resistance?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"belt or brake pad-resisted cycle ergometers, and wrist curl devices.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"以摩擦力為主要阻力來源的器材：皮帶式或剎車片式動感單車（cycle ergometer）以及腕彎曲訓練器等。"},{"id":"q3114","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"foods with quick carb absorption and beneficial for hours before/after exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high GI","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高 GI 食物吸收快；本卡答案指運動前數小時與運動後皆可使用高 GI 以快速補糖（注意：主流教科書建議運動後立即優先高 GI，運動前數小時宜採低 GI，實作上以課後補糖的高 GI 證據最強）。"},{"id":"q3115","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"a person's effort to master a task, achieve excellence, overcome obstacles, and engage in competition or comparison","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"achievement motivation","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"成就動機（achievement motivation）：一個人努力精通任務、達成卓越、克服障礙，並投入競爭或比較的傾向。"},{"id":"q3116","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"amount of weight assigned to an exercise set","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"load","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"負荷（load）：分配給某一動作的重量多寡。"},{"id":"q3117","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"resting heart rates commonly range from ___ to ___ bpm in highly conditioned aerobic endurance athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"40 to 60 bpm","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"高度訓練的有氧耐力運動員休息心率通常落在每分鐘 40～60 次。"},{"id":"q3118","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Neuromuscular system","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"muscle fibers are innervated by motor neurons that transmit impulses in the form of electrochemical signals from the spinal cord to the muscles","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"神經肌肉系統（neuromuscular system）：肌纖維由運動神經元支配，以電化學訊號的形式把衝動從脊髓傳導到肌肉。"},{"id":"q3119","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"a statistic that can be useful for calculating group performance following a training program or comparing between groups of athletes","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"effect size","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"效果量（effect size）：可用於計算訓練課程後的群體表現變化，或在不同運動員群體間做比較。"},{"id":"q3120","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Metabolic acidosis**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The process of proton accumulation during fatigue which reduces intracellular pH, inhibits glycolytic reactions and directly interferes with the muscle’s excitation-contraction coupling.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"代謝性酸中毒（metabolic acidosis）：疲勞期間質子（H+）堆積使胞內 pH 下降，抑制糖解反應並直接幹擾肌肉的興奮-收縮偶聯（excitation-contraction coupling）。"},{"id":"q3121","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Psychological efficiency**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The ability to overcome negative thoughts and arousal that may impede performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"心理效率（psychological efficiency）：克服可能妨礙表現的負面想法與過度覺醒的能力。"},{"id":"q3122","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"connective tissue surrounding each muscle fiber","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"endomysium","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌內膜（endomysium）：包圍每一條肌纖維的結締組織。"},{"id":"q3123","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Common sites for skinfold measurements","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"CHEST: A DIAGONAL FOLD one half the distance between the anterior axillary line and the nipple for men THIGH: A VERTICAL FOLD on the anterior aspect of the thigh, midway between the hip and knee ABDOMEN: A VERTICAL FOLD 1 inch to the right of the umbilicus TRICEPS: A VERTICAL FOLD on the posterior midline of the upper arm, halfway between the acromion and olecranon process SUPRAILIUM: A DIAGONAL FOLD above the crest of the ilium MIDAXILLA: A VERTICAL FOLD on the midaxillary line at the level of the xiphoid process SUBSCAPULA: A DIAGONAL FOLD that extends from the vertebral border to a point 1 inch from the inferior angle of scapula CALF: A VERTICAL FOLD along the medial side of the calf","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"常見皮褶測量部位與手法：胸部（男：前方腋線與乳頭中點之斜摺）、大腿（髖與膝中間之前面垂直摺）、腹部（臍右 1 吋垂直摺）、三頭肌（肩峰與鷹嘴中點上臂後正中線垂直摺）、髂上（腸骨嵴上方斜摺）、腋中線（劍突高度腋中線垂直摺）、肩胛下（椎緣至距下角 1 吋之斜摺）、小腿（內側垂直摺）。"},{"id":"q3124","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the I-band made of and what does it contain?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"made of two continguous sarcomeres, contains only actin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"I 帶由相鄰兩個肌小節的末端共同構成，只含肌動蛋白（actin）細絲。"},{"id":"q3125","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the thigh relative to the ankle?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"proximal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"大腿相對於腳踝為近端（proximal）。"},{"id":"q3126","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"At higher exercise intensities, what happens to pyruvate and NADH?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"they will increase above what can be handled by pyruvate dehydrogenase and will then be converted into lactate and NAD+","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"較高強度運動時，丙酮酸與 NADH 的生成超過丙酮酸去氫酶（pyruvate dehydrogenase）能處理的量，多餘部分即被轉換為乳酸與 NAD+。"},{"id":"q3127","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"in the recharge phase, how does muscle shortening occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"only when this sequence of events—binding of calcium to troponin, coupling of the myosin crossbridge with actin, power stroke, dissociation of actin and myosin, and resetting of the myosin head position—is repeated over and over again throughout the muscle fiber muscle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"再充電期（recharge phase）的肌肉縮短條件：鈣與肌鈣蛋白結合、橫橋與肌動蛋白結合、power stroke、肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白分離、肌球蛋白頭復位，此序列在肌纖維內反覆不斷發生，才產生縮短。"},{"id":"q3128","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what is the formula for exercise devices using friction, like cycle ergometers?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"FR = k ∙ FN, where FR is the resistive force; k is the coefficient of friction for the two particular substances in contact; and FN is the normal force, which presses the objects against each other","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"摩擦力器材的公式：FR = k × FN，FR 為阻力，k 為兩接觸物質間之摩擦係數，FN 為把兩物體互相壓緊的法向力。"},{"id":"q3129","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"foods with slow carb absorption and beneficial immediately after exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"low GI","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"低 GI：消化吸收慢、升血糖平緩的碳水化合物食物；本卡答案寫「運動後立即攝取有益」，與主流建議相反——教科書建議運動後立即採高 GI 以加速肝糖再合成，低 GI 較適合運動前數小時攝取以維持穩定血糖。"},{"id":"q3130","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"the capacity to experience pride in one's accomplishments and is characterized by a desire to challenge oneself and evaluate one's abilities","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"motive to achieve success (MAS)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"追求成功動機（MAS）：能為個人成就感到自豪的能力，特質是渴望挑戰自己並評估自身能力。"},{"id":"q3131","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is often characterized as the most critical aspect of a resistance training program?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"load","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"負荷（load）常被視為阻力訓練課中最關鍵的要素。"},{"id":"q3132","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"2 most significant cardiovascular function increases due to long term aerobic endurance training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"cardiac output stroke volume","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"長期有氧耐力訓練帶來的兩個最重要心血管適應：心輸出量（cardiac output）增加與每搏輸出量（stroke volume）增加。"},{"id":"q3133","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Acetylocholine","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Arrival of the action potential at the nerve terminal causes release of this neurotransmitter. It diffuses across the neuromuscular junction causing excitation of the sarcolemma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乙醯膽鹼（acetylcholine, ACh）：動作電位抵達神經末梢時釋放此神經傳導物質；它擴散通過神經肌肉接合處，引起肌細胞膜（sarcolemma）興奮（excitation）。"},{"id":"q3134","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"effect size =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"effect size = (x posttest - x pretest) / SD pretest","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"效果量公式：效果量 =（後測平均數 − 前測平均數）÷ 前測標準差。"},{"id":"q3135","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Metabolic specificity**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The metabolic needs of specific activities. An understanding of metabolic specificity is used to create efficient and productive training programs.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"代謝特異性（metabolic specificity）：特定運動專案的代謝需求；理解代謝特異性可用來設計有效且具產出的訓練課。"},{"id":"q3136","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Pure-part training**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Practicing each skill subcomponent independently before combining them together","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"純分部訓練（pure-part training）：先各自獨立練習每個技能子成分，再把它們組合起來。"},{"id":"q3137","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"the cell membrane of a muscle cell","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"sarcolemma","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌細胞膜（sarcolemma）：肌肉細胞的細胞膜。"},{"id":"q3138","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Overhead Squat","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"* wooden dowel overhead with the shoulders fully flexed and with elbows locked * grip should be twice shoulder-width and the feet approximately shoulder-width apart and toes pointing forward or slightly out * The athlete then squats down; the initial action is flexion of the hips and knees. The heels remain in contact with the floor at all times * The lowering continues until the crease of the hips is below the top of the knee * The athlete should be able to hold this position with the torso remaining upright (parallel to the tibia) and the wooden dowel (or barbell) comfortably overhead","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"過頭蹲評估（Overhead Squat）：木棍舉過頭、肩完全屈曲、肘伸直，握距約兩倍肩寬，雙腳約肩寬、腳尖朝前或略外八；屈髖屈膝下蹲，全程腳跟貼地，直到髖摺痕低於膝蓋上緣；應能維持上身直立（與脛骨平行）且木棍舒適地保持在頭頂上方。"},{"id":"q3139","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"where is the Z-line located?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"middle of the I-band","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"Z 線位於 I 帶的正中間。"},{"id":"q3140","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"in terms of orientation/direction, where is the ankle relative to the knee?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"distal","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"腳踝相對於膝蓋為遠端（distal）。"},{"id":"q3141","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"why might the term aerobic/anaerobic glycolysis be inaccurate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"because glycolysis itself does not depend on oxygen","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"「有氧/無氧糖解」一詞可能不準確，因為糖解本身並不依賴氧氣；氧氣只決定丙酮酸後續的去向。"},{"id":"q3142","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"shortening can occur as long as what conditions are satisfied?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"as long as calcium is available in the myofibril, ATP is available to assist in uncoupling the myosin from the actin, and sufficient active myosin ATPase is available for catalyzing the breakdown of ATP.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌肉縮短能持續的條件：肌原纖維內有可用的鈣、有 ATP 協助肌球蛋白與肌動蛋白脫離、且有足夠具活性的肌球蛋白 ATPase 催化 ATP 分解。"},{"id":"q3143","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"what resistance does a weighted sled provide?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"a device that is resisted by both friction and inertia. The resistance due to the sled's inertia is directly proportional to both the sled's mass and its acceleration. The resistance due to the friction between the sled's runners and the ground is proportional to both the friction coefficient between surfaces in contact and the net force pressing the sled against the ground, which equals the gravitational force minus any upward force exerted by the individual pushing the sled.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"載入式雪橇（sled）提供摩擦與慣性雙重阻力：慣性阻力與雪橇質量及其加速度成正比；摩擦力與接觸面摩擦係數及正向力成正比，正向力等於重力減去推者施加的向上分力。"},{"id":"q3144","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how does insulin help lower blood glucose levels?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"facilitates glucose transport into cells","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"胰島素（insulin）透過促進葡萄糖轉運進入細胞來降低血糖。"},{"id":"q3145","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"the desire to protect one's ego and self esteem","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"motive to avoid failure (MAF)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"逃避失敗動機（MAF）：保護自我自尊（ego）與自我價值的慾望。"},{"id":"q3146","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"force x displacement =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"mechanical work","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"力 × 位移 = 機械功（mechanical work）。"},{"id":"q3147","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"most like muscle fiber type transition with long term aerobic endurance training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type IIx to type IIa","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"長期有氧耐力訓練造成的肌纖維轉換最接近第二型 x 轉為第二型 a（type IIx to type IIa）。"},{"id":"q3148","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"how does a CSCS develop an athletic profile for the athlete?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"by selecting tests that will measure the specific parameters most closely related to the characteristics of the sport or sports in question","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"CSCS 建立運動員專項檔案的做法：選用能量測與目標運動專案特性最相關引數的測驗。"},{"id":"q3149","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Random practice**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Practicing multiple skills in a random order in the same session","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"隨機練習（random practice）：在同一練習課中以隨機順序練習多個技能。"},{"id":"q3150","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"other name for motor end plate","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"neuromuscular junction","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動終板（motor end plate）的另一個名稱是神經肌肉接合處（neuromuscular junction）。"},{"id":"q3151","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Girth Measurements","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"-Relaxed anatomical position f or each measurement (unless otherwise indicated for a particular measurement). o Chest—at nipple level in males and at maximum circumference (above the breasts) in females o Right upper arm—at the point of maximal circumference with the ELBOW FULLY EXTENDED, PALM UP, AND ARM ABDUCTED TO PARALLEL WITH THE FLOOR o Right forearm—at the point of maximal circumference with the elbow fully extended, palm up, and arm abducted to parallel with the floor o Waist (abdomen)—at the level of the umbilicus o Hips (buttocks)—at the maximal protrusion of the buttocks with the heels together o Right thigh—at the point of maximal circumference, usually just below the buttocks o Right calf—at the point of maximal circumference between the knee and ankle","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"圍度測量要點（除特別說明外一律探放鬆解剖姿勢）：胸部在男性乳頭高度、女性取最大圍度；右上臂與右前臂取最大圍度（肘全伸、掌心向上、手臂外展至與地面平行）；腰部在臍水平；臀部在足跟併攏時臀部最大突出處；右大腿在最大圍度（通常恰在臀部下方）；右小腿在膝與踝間最大圍度。"},{"id":"q3152","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are the essential features of the sarcoplasmic reticulum?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"pumping Ca+ ions into the muscle when an action potential is released into sarcomere (for muscle contraction), and storing calcium ions there","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌漿網（sarcoplasmic reticulum）的重要特徵：動作電位傳入肌小節時釋放鈣離子進入肌漿以觸發收縮，並在舒張時把鈣離子泵回儲存。"},{"id":"q3153","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"the first phase of jumping jacks -- what kind of movement is this?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"abduct","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"開合跳（jumping jacks）第一段（手腳向外開啟）屬外展（abduct）動作。"},{"id":"q3154","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"how do energy demands affect the use of pyruvate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the fate of pyruvate is ultimately controlled by the energy demands within the cell. if energy demand is high and must be transferred quickly, as during resistance training, pyruvate is primarily converted to lactate for further support of anaerobic glycolysis. if energy demand is not as high and oxygen is present in sufficient quantities in the cell, pyruvate can be further oxidized in the mitochondria.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"能量需求決定丙酮酸去向：能量需求高、需快速轉移（如阻力訓練）時，丙酮酸主要轉為乳酸以支援無氧糖解；需求較低且細胞內氧氣充足時，丙酮酸進入粒線體進一步氧化。"},{"id":"q3155","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"when does the relaxation phase occur?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"when the stimulation of the motor nerve stops","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舒張期（relaxation phase）發生在運動神經刺激停止時。"},{"id":"q3156","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"despite not providing repeatable resistance, why are sleds valuable?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"horizontal resistance, which cannot be directly provided by weights","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雪橇雖然無法提供可重複（repeatable）的固定阻力，但能提供垂直重量無法直接提供的水平阻力，因此仍有價值。"},{"id":"q3157","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"an estimate of how much of a food will increase blood glucose levels","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"glycemic load (GL)","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"升糖負荷（glycemic load, GL）：估計某食物的實際攝取份量會使血糖上升多少。"},{"id":"q3158","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"true or false: MAF is not really about avoiding failure itself but more about avoiding the perception of shame that accompanies the failure","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確：MAF 真正要避免的不是失敗本身，而是失敗所伴隨的羞恥感。"},{"id":"q3159","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is the volume-load?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"total work done","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"容量負荷（volume-load）即所完成的總功（重量 × 次數 × 組數的總和）。"},{"id":"q3160","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"why do type IIx fibers change to type IIa fibers with long term aerobic endurance training?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"type IIa fibers have a greater oxidative capacity than type IIx fibers, making them more similar with type I fibers to contribute to aerobic endurance performance","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"長期有氧耐力訓練使第二型 x 轉為第二型 a，因為 IIa 纖維氧化能力較強、較接近第一型纖維，能貢獻有氧耐力表現。"},{"id":"q3161","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what are some examples of maximum muscular strength tests (low speed strength)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 RM bench press 1 RM bench pull 1 RM back squat","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大肌力（低速度力量）測驗例子：1RM 嚥式推舉、1RM 划船推舉（bench pull）、1RM 背蹲。"},{"id":"q3162","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Mitochondria**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Organelle of the muscle cell where aerobic energy mechanisms occur.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"粒線體（mitochondria）：肌肉細胞內進行有氧能量機制（粒線體呼吸與氧化磷酸化）的細胞器。"},{"id":"q3163","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Repetitive part training**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Practicing first part in isolation, then adding each subsequent part until the whole skill is done as one movement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"重複式分部訓練（repetitive-part training）：先單獨練習第一部分，再逐段加上後續部分，直到整個動作能作為單一動作完成。"},{"id":"q3164","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"a motor neuron and the muscle fibers it innervates","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"motor unit","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動單位（motor unit）：一個運動神經元及其支配的所有肌纖維。"},{"id":"q3165","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Descriptive Statistics","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"summarizes/describes a large group of data Three categories of descriptive statistics: central tendency, variability, and percentile rank","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"敘述統計（descriptive statistics）：摘要、描述一大組資料；三大類：集中趨勢、變異量與百分位數。"},{"id":"q3166","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is negative punishment?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the removal of something highly valued to deter undesired behavior; the antithesis of positive reinforcement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"負性懲罰（negative punishment）：移除高度重視的事物以抑制不良行為，與正性增強相反。"},{"id":"q3167","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"the second phase of jumping jacks -- what kind of movement is this?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"adduct","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"開合跳（jumping jacks）第二段（手腳收回合攏）屬內收（adduct）動作。"},{"id":"q3168","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what catalyzes the formation of lactate from pyruvate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"the enzyme lactate dehydrogenase","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"丙酮酸形成乳酸的反應由乳酸去氫酶（lactate dehydrogenase, LDH）催化。"},{"id":"q3169","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what occurs chemically during the relaxation phase?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"calcium is pumped back into the sarcoplasmic reticulum, which prevents the link between the actin and myosin filaments. relaxation is brought about by the return of the actin and myosin filaments to their unbound state.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"舒張期的化學變化：鈣被泵回肌漿網，使肌動蛋白與肌球蛋白細絲無法連結，兩細絲回到未結合狀態而舒張。"},{"id":"q3170","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"describe the power output of a sled and how friction resistance relates to speed","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"It takes more force to get the sled moving than to keep it moving, because the coefficient of static friction is always greater than the coefficient of sliding friction. Once the sled is moving, the coefficient of sliding friction stays relatively constant. Therefore one should understand that friction resistance does not change as speed increases. However, in keeping with Power = Work / Time, power output increases with speed. Also, as expressed by F=M*A, during the transition from a lower to a higher speed there is added resistance due to acceleration.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"雪橇功率輸出：靜摩擦係數恆大於動摩擦係數，故啟動雪橇比維持移動更費力；移動後動摩擦係數大致恆定，摩擦阻力不隨速度增加；但功率 = 功/時間，功率輸出隨速度上升；依 F = m × a，由低速轉高速的加速階段還有慣性附加阻力。"},{"id":"q3171","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"why is glycemic load a more realistic gauge of glycemic response than the GI?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"takes portion size into account","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"升糖負荷（GL）比 GI 更能反映實際升糖反應，因為它計入了攝取份量（食用量）。"},{"id":"q3172","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"this type of practice engages the athlete in some decisions and enhances feelings of competence and autonomy","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"self controlled practice","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"自我控制練習（self controlled practice）：讓運動員參與部分決策（如何時練習、練習多少），能增強勝任感與自主感。"},{"id":"q3173","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"what is the repetition-volume?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"volume of each rep","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"次數容量（repetition-volume）：每一次重複動作所對應的容量（題卡定義：volume of each rep）。"},{"id":"q3174","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"average cardiac output at rest","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"5 L of blood","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"休息時平均心輸出量約每分鐘 5 公升血液。"},{"id":"q3175","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Tentanus","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The stimuli may be delivered at so high a frequency that the twitches begin to merge & eventually completely fuse. Maximal amount of force the motor unit can develop.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"強直收縮（tetanus）：刺激頻率高到抽搐開始融合甚至完全融合，此時運動單位發展出可產生的最大力量。"},{"id":"q3176","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"what are some examples of maximum muscular power tests (high speed strength)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"1 RM power clean vertical jump reactive strength index magaria kalamenn test","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"最大肌力功率（高速度力量）測驗例子：1RM power clean、垂直跳、反應力量指數（reactive strength index, RSI）、Magaria-Kalamen 測驗。"},{"id":"q3177","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Myokinase reaction**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"An important single-enzyme reaction that can rapidly replenish ATP from ADP. Also known as the adenylate kinase reaction.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌動激酶反應（myokinase reaction）：可由 ADP 快速再合成 ATP 的重要單一酵素反應，又稱腺苷酸激酶（adenylate kinase）反應。"},{"id":"q3178","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Reversal theory**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Athlete’s perception of arousal/anxiety as important for performance as the level itself","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"翻轉理論（reversal theory）：運動員對覺醒/焦慮的主觀感知與覺醒水準本身同樣影響表現。"},{"id":"q3179","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"thick filaments","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"myosin","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"粗絲（thick filaments）即肌球蛋白（myosin）細絲。"},{"id":"q3180","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Measures of Central Tendency","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Values about which the data tend to cluster Mean: The average of the scores Median: The middlemost score when a set of scores is arranged in order of magnitude. Mode: The score that occurs with the greatest frequency.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"集中趨勢量：資料聚集圍繞的數值，包括平均數（分數平均值）、中位數（排序後最中間的分數）、眾數（出現最頻繁的分數）。"},{"id":"q3181","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"function of arterioles?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"controlling factor of blood flow in and out of capillary beds.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"小動脈（arterioles）的功能：控制進出微血管床（capillary beds）的血流量。"},{"id":"q3182","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what is the action of the ilicostalis (lateral), longissimus (intermediate), and spinalis (medial)?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"prime mover of back extension; each side consists of three columns","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"豎脊肌三列——髂肋肌（外側）、最長肌（中間）、棘肌（內側）——每側各由三列組成，是背部伸展（軀幹伸直）的prime mover（主動肌）。"},{"id":"q3183","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"what is a mistaken belief about the formation of lactate from pyruvate?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"that the end result is the formation of lactic acid.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"關於丙酮酸生成乳酸的常見誤解：以為最終產物是乳酸（lactic acid）；在生理 pH 下實際產物是乳酸根（lactate）。"},{"id":"q3184","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"what is the origin of the \"twitch\" in fast/slow twitch muscle fibers?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"relaxation time","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快/慢肌纖維之稱的「抽搐（twitch）」來自放鬆時間的差異：快縮纖維放鬆快、慢縮纖維放鬆慢。"},{"id":"q3185","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"biomechanically how does bad spinal form lead to greater likelihood of injury","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"When a weight is supported in the hands or on the shoulders and the trunk is inclined forward, there is great torque about the lower intervertebral disks due to the large horizontal distance between the lower back and the weight. The back muscles operate at an extremely low mechanical advantage because the perpendicular distance from the line of action of the spinal erector muscles to the intervertebral disks is much shorter (about 2 inches, or 5 cm) than the horizontal distance from the weight to the disks. As a result, the muscles must exert forces that frequently exceed 10 times the weight lifted. These forces act to squeeze the intervertebral disks between the adjacent vertebral bodies and can lead to injury.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"脊柱不良姿勢容易受傷的生物力學原因：手持或肩扛重量且軀幹前傾時，重量到下背椎間盤的水平距離大，對下位椎間盤產生極大扭力；脊椎伸肌的力臂僅約 5 公分，機械利益極差，肌力常須超過所舉重量的 10 倍，這些力把椎間盤擠壓在相鄰椎體之間，可能造成傷害。"},{"id":"q3186","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"true or false: foods with a higher GL are expected to lead to greater increases in blood sugar and subsequent insulin release","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"true","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正確：GL 較高的食物預期會造成更大的血糖上升與後續胰島素釋放。"},{"id":"q3187","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"increasing the probability that a behavior will occur","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"reinforcement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"增強（reinforcement）：提高某一行為出現機率的機制。"},{"id":"q3188","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"volume load / rep volume =","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"average weight lifted per rep per workout session","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"容量負荷 ÷ 次數容量 = 每次訓練課中每次 repetitions 的平均提起重量。"},{"id":"q3189","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"average cardiac output during exercise","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"25 L of blood","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"運動期間平均心輸出量約每分鐘 25 公升血液。"},{"id":"q3190","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Fast-Twitch fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A motor unit that develops force & also relaxes rapidly & has a short twitch time. Type IIa & IIx","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快縮肌纖維（fast-twitch fibers）：快速產生力量並快速放鬆、抽搐時間短的運動單位，即第二型 a 與第二型 x。"},{"id":"q3191","part":2,"domain":"Organization & Administration","textbook_chapter":13,"question":"the 300 yard shuttle test is a measure of what variable?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"anaerobic capacity","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 13: Administration, Scoring, and Interpretation of Selected Tests"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"300 碼衝刺折返跑測驗測量的是無氧容量（anaerobic capacity）。"},{"id":"q3192","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"**Myosin ATPase**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The enzyme that catalyzes ATP hydrolysis for crossbridge recycling.","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 3 - Bioenergetics of Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"肌球蛋白 ATP 酶（myosin ATPase）：催化 ATP 水解、供橫橋迴圈（crossbridge recycling）所需能量的酵素。"},{"id":"q3193","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"**Routine**","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"Mental checklist that consciously directs thoughts to task-relevant and controllable concerns","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8 - Psychology of Athletic Preparation and Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"慣例程式（routine）：心理檢查清單，有意識地把想法導向與任務相關且可控的關注點。"},{"id":"q3194","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"of myosin molecules in a myosin filament","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"~200","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"一條肌球蛋白細絲約含 200 個肌球蛋白分子。"},{"id":"q3195","part":2,"domain":"Practical/Applied","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"Variability","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"The degree of dispersion of scores within a group","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Practical/Applied"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"變異量（variability）：一組分數內離散分散的程度。"},{"id":"q3196","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"what are synonyms for reducing blow flow and allowing greater blood flow?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"vasoconstriction and vasodilation respectively","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.3 - study card vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"減少血流的同義詞是血管收縮（vasoconstriction）；增加血流的同義詞是血管舒張（vasodilation）。"},{"id":"q3197","part":null,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":null,"question":"how do the origin and insertion differ in mobility?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"insertion is movable, origin is immovable","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch0.2 - study book vocabulary"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"起點（origin）與附著點（insertion）的差異：附著端較可移動，起點端較固定。"},{"id":"q3198","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":3,"question":"why is lactate, rather than lactic acid, the product of the lactate dehydrogenase reaction?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"due to the physiological pH (i.e., near 7) and earlier steps in glycolysis that consume protons","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch3 - bioenergetics of exercise and training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"乳酸去氫酶反應的產物是 lactate（乳酸根）而非 lactic acid（乳酸），理由是生理 pH 接近 7，且糖解前期反應會消耗質子。"},{"id":"q3199","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"chemically, how are fast/slow twitch determined?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"histochemical staining for myosin ATPase content; another more specific method is to quantify the amount of myosin heavy chain (MHC) protein; the nomenclature for this is similar to that with the myosin ATPase methodology","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch1 - structure and functions of body system"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"快/慢肌纖維的化學判定：以組織化學染色測量肌球蛋白 ATPase 含量；更精確的做法是定量肌球蛋白重鏈（myosin heavy chain, MHC）蛋白，兩法命名邏輯相同。"},{"id":"q3200","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":2,"question":"high / middle / low injury risks for various sports?","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"high for team sports; intermediate for running and aerobics; and lowest for cycling, walking, and resistance training","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["ch2 - biomechanics of resistance exercise"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"各運動傷害風險由高至低：團隊運動風險最高；跑步與有氧操居中；腳踏車、走路與阻力訓練最低。"},{"id":"q3201","part":1,"domain":"Nutrition","textbook_chapter":null,"question":"complex carbohydrate that is unable to be fully digested","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"fiber","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapters 9 and 10: Nutrition Factors in Health + Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"膳食纖維（fiber）是無法被完全消化的複合碳水化合物。"},{"id":"q3202","part":1,"domain":"Sport Psychology","textbook_chapter":8,"question":"adding something to increase a behavior","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"positive reinforcement","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 8: Psychology of Athletic Preparation & Performance"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"正性增強（positive reinforcement）：加入（呈現）刺激以提高某行為出現的機率。"},{"id":"q3203","part":2,"domain":"Program Design","textbook_chapter":17,"question":"reps and loads are ________ related, meaning when one goes up the other has to go down","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"inversely","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 17: Program Design for Resistance Training"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"次數與負荷呈反向（inversely）相關：一個上升，另一個必須下降。"},{"id":"q3204","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":6,"question":"true or false: max HR changes with training","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"false","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["Chapter 6: Adaptations to Aerobic Endurance Training Programs"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"錯誤（false）：最大心率不會因訓練而改變，主要由年齡決定；長期訓練降低的是休息心率，不是最大心率。"},{"id":"q3205","part":1,"domain":null,"textbook_chapter":1,"question":"Slow-twitch fibers","options":null,"answer":null,"answer_text":"A motor unit that develops force & relaxes slowly & has a long twitch time. Type I","explanation_en":null,"item_type":"flashcard","tags":["CSCS CH 1 Structure & Function of Body Systems"],"source":"brainscape","explanation_zh":"慢縮肌纖維（slow-twitch fibers）：產生力量與放鬆都較慢、抽搐時間長的運動單位，即第一型（Type I）纖維。"}]};